gy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ba9878a-923a-54ab-93ab-17fe1938fc51', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ba9878a-923a-54ab-93ab-17fe1938fc51'}, {'abstract': 'The evidence suggests that electing a president with a business background is actually a terrible idea.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/05/31/the-wrong-resume/', 'snippet': 'The evidence suggests that electing a president with a business background is actually a terrible idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lost in the exhaust of mendacity left in Las Vegas this week, after Donald Trump brought his birther fantasies to town on behalf of Mitt Romney, was a curious statement by the man who has now cinched the Republican nomination for president. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wrong Résumé', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c0f1a89-c0d1-5a8c-8125-350dee149ca7', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c0f1a89-c0d1-5a8c-8125-350dee149ca7'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers made closing arguments Thursday in the case of Msgr. William J. Lynn, the clergy secretary who is accused of shielding predatory priests and exposing children to sexual abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/us/cases-close-for-msgr-lynn-in-philadelphia-abuse-case.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers made closing arguments Thursday in the case of Msgr. William J. Lynn, the clergy secretary who is accused of shielding predatory priests and exposing children to sexual abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — In an emotional summary after more than two months of testimony, the prosecution in a landmark sexual-abuse trial said here on Thursday that overwhelming evidence showed that a Roman Catholic Church official had shielded predatory priests, lied to parishioners and victims, and exposed innocent children to abuse. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cases Close for Philadelphia Diocese Official', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jury to Get Case of Official At Diocese In Philadelphia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergstrom, Thomas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynn, William J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:02:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd45b132-54dc-5145-8ec4-e9d6a3be830b', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd45b132-54dc-5145