 — A federal judge on Thursday ordered Florida to stop enforcing several “onerous” requirements on voter registration groups that were part of a law passed last year in an effort to tighten election rules.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/us/subFLORIDA/subFLORIDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/us/subFLORIDA/subFLORIDA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1288, 'width': 1932, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Blocks Florida’s Voter Drive Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Blocks Florida&#8217;s Voter Drive Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Civil Liberties Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hinkle, Robert L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'League of Women Voters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rock the Vote', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:28:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d4818d3-1382-5ef4-ae5d-a383d4749011', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d4818d3-1382-5ef4-ae5d-a383d4749011'}, {'abstract': 'Political leaders in Europe need to admit their countries’ complicity in the financial crisis and tell their citizens the hard truths about what it will take to dig out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/opinion/blame-game-european-style.html', 'snippet': 'Political leaders in Europe need to admit their countries’ complicity in the financial crisis and tell their citizens the hard truths about what it will take to dig out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The financial news from Europe keeps getting worse. Spain’s government, its banks foundering, may soon need to be bailed out. The cost of that rescue could strain the new European bailout fund, leaving little behind should investors turn on Italy next. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blame Game, European-Style', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blame Game, European-Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hollande, Francois', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:29:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8935d4c0-8494-5a25-86d9-d7c53ee039ff', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8935d4c0-8494-5a25-86d9-d7c53ee039ff'}, {'abstract': 'Not every effort of the government to restrict religious rights is a step toward the total undermining of religion.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/05/31/do-the-bishops-have-a-case-against-obama/', 'snippet': 'Not every effort of the government to restrict religious rights is a step toward the total undermining of religion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Religion often comes alive in the face of persecution. Recently, Daniel Jenky, the bishop of Peoria, Ill., did not hesitate to play the persecution card in the dispute with the Obama administration over required health insurance coverage of birth control. Evoking the history of “terrible persecution” of the Church, he said: “Hitler and Stalin would not tolerate any competition with the state in education, social services and health care. . . . Barack Obama — with his radical, pro-abortion and extreme secularist agenda — now seems intent on following a similar path.” In an effort to clarify the statement, a diocese spokesperson said, “We certainly have not reached the same level of persecution. However, history teaches us to be cautious once we start down the path of limiting religious liberty.” (She did not explain just what the bishop regarded as the Church’s current “level of persecution” by the administration.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do the Bishops Have a Case Against Obama?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:30:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4efb5abb-b391-5f6f-bda1-623ff9477d11', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4efb5abb-b391-5f6f-bda1-623ff9477d11'}, {'abstract': 'For “Richard’s Wedding” a believable if sarcastic set of 30-ish pals head for a ceremony in Central Park and talk about life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/movies/richards-wedding-written-and-directed-by-onur-tukel.html', 'snippet': 'For “Richard’s Wedding” a believable if sarcastic set of 30-ish pals head for a ceremony in Central Park and talk about life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why not “Richard and Phoebe’s Wedding”? Phoebe’s far more interesting than Richard, and isn’t there something sexist about naming the groom but not the bride?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN/01RDP_RICHARDSWEDDING_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Friends Get Together and Riff', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Richard’s Wedding', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tukel, Onur', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:31:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By David DeWitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeWitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f72c536a-2756-5e5c-a12e-98db6320097a', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f72c536a-2756-5e5c-a12e-98db6320097a'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans in Florida are still trying to keep minorities and poor people, groups that tend to vote Democratic, from the ballot box.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/opinion/floridas-discriminatory-voter-purge.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans in Florida are still trying to keep minorities and poor people, groups that tend to vote Democratic, from the ballot box.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Florida, where a few hundred votes can determine a presidential election, Republicans have never stopped searching for new ways to keep ballots out of the hands of minorities and poor people, groups that tend to vote Democratic. They have cut back on early voting, tried to stamp out registration drives, and imposed onerous identification requirements. (A federal judge reinstated the registration drives on Thursday.) Now, hoping to gain a new edge, Gov. Rick Scott is trying to clear voter rolls of noncitizens, a menace that only he and a few other Republican governors have been able to detect.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida’s Discriminatory Voter Purge', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida’s Discriminatory Voter Purge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Herald', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:35:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/90f088c5-02f8-592a-a9ea-b3a8c961ce37', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90f088c5-02f8-592a-a9ea-b3a8c961ce37'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary “Chely Wright: Wish Me Away” chronicles the steps to Ms. Wright’s announcement of her homosexuality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/movies/chely-wright-wish-me-away-a-documentary.html', 'snippet': 'The documentary “Chely Wright: Wish Me Away” chronicles the steps to Ms. Wright’s announcement of her homosexuality.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I love my fans; I love how much they love me,” the country singer Chely Wright says in “Chely Wright: Wish Me Away,” a documentary about her decision to come out as a lesbian in notoriously conservative Nashville. The comment, with its intimations of narcissism and dependence on the adulation of strangers, is one of several truly heartbreaking moments in a film that, like its subject, feels torn between keeping it all together and letting it all hang out.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_CHELYWRIGHT_SPAN/01RDP_CHELYWRIGHT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 