. game. In 1959-60 he and Wilt Chamberlain became the first players to average more than 30 points a game in a season. He went on to become an analyst for the N.B.A. game of the week on ABC and a food company executive who pocketed more than $3 million when he sold the company in 1996.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/sports/TWYMAN1-obit/TWYMAN1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 792, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/sports/TWYMAN1-obit/TWYMAN1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1584, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/sports/TWYMAN1-obit/TWYMAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/01/sports/TWYMAN1-obit/TWYMAN1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/sports/TWYMAN1-obit/TWYMAN1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jack Twyman, N.B.A. Star Known for Off-Court Assist, Dies at 78', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jack Twyman, N.B.A. Star Known for Off-Court Assist, Dies at 78', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Twyman, Jack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stokes, Maurice', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T01:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/956d1ced-1629-58b3-b33e-1f55e2b4848e', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/956d1ced-1629-58b3-b33e-1f55e2b4848e'}, {'abstract': 'More than two months after Brooklyn voters went to the polls, a hand recount gave David Storobin, a Republican, a slim lead, and his Democratic opponent, Lewis A. Fidler, conceded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/nyregion/david-storobin-poised-to-win-brooklyn-state-senate-seat-after-recount.html', 'snippet': 'More than two months after Brooklyn voters went to the polls, a hand recount gave David Storobin, a Republican, a slim lead, and his Democratic opponent, Lewis A. Fidler, conceded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Storobin’s journey from his birth in the former Soviet Union to his becoming a lawyer in Brooklyn was no easy one. His election to the New York State Senate was not a short trip, either. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/nyregion/BROOKLYN/BROOKLYN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/nyregion/BROOKLYN/BROOKL