': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0aa7e36-16d5-544f-b019-719bccb556fc', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0aa7e36-16d5-544f-b019-719bccb556fc'}, {'abstract': 'Assembly Speaker Sheldon Silver said Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s office should have a smaller role in a proposed state agency for people with disabilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/nyregion/assembly-speaker-presses-cuomo-on-plan-for-disabled-care.html', 'snippet': 'Assembly Speaker Sheldon Silver said Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s office should have a smaller role in a proposed state agency for people with disabilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBANY — The State Assembly speaker, Sheldon Silver, believes that Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo’s office should have a lesser role in a new state agency that the governor has proposed to police the abuse and neglect of people with disabilities. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Silver Presses Governor on Proposal for Disabled', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Silver Presses Governor On Proposal For Disabled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abuse of the Disabled', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Sheldon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T02:08:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1aca3cd2-ac07-5a3b-9be2-1b8dbc657b98', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1aca3cd2-ac07-5a3b-9be2-1b8dbc657b98'}, {'abstract': 'In “Wallander: The Revenge,” Henning Mankell’s detective deals with murder and an army occupation of his town.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/movies/wallander-the-revenge-from-sweden.html', 'snippet': 'In “Wallander: The Revenge,” Henning Mankell’s detective deals with murder and an army occupation of his town.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Wallander: The Revenge” looks and plays like what it is: an episode of a Swedish television series based on Henning Mankell’s crime novels. (It’s Episode 1 of Season 2, which has just been released on DVD, online and through video on demand.) Directed by Charlotte Brandstrom, “The Revenge” is well-made, above-average TV, but it seems small for the big screen. The plot is a bit predictable, and we’re still getting to know the characters when the story ends.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_WALLENDER/FILMROUND5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_WALLENDER/FILMROUND5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/01RDP_WALLENDER/01RDP_WALLENDER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail