ecognize that technological advances have opened the door for unparalleled involvement in public life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Txt 4 Ur Candidate', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maryland', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T02:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Ravel, Jared DeMarinis and Hyla Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ravel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jared', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DeMarinis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Hyla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35b3265e-6e7b-5b5b-812b-3e39ef309c58', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35b3265e-6e7b-5b5b-812b-3e39ef309c58'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook is turning its users into unpaid pitchmen in a type of advertisement known as a sponsored story. We asked Facebook friends who showed up in such ads what they thought of the practice.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/05/31/do-people-like-being-featured-in-facebook-ads/', 'snippet': 'Facebook is turning its users into unpaid pitchmen in a type of advertisement known as a sponsored story. We asked Facebook friends who showed up in such ads what they thought of the practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook is turning its users into unpaid pitchmen in a type of advertisement known as a sponsored story. Companies can pay Facebook to generate automated ads when someone “likes” their brand or product, or references it in some other way. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/technology/bitpix-facebook-likedontlike/bitpix-facebook-likedontlike-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/technology/bitpix-facebook-likedontlike/bitpix-facebook-likedontlike-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do People Like Being Featured in Facebook Ads?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T02:34:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfb5d483-980d-546b-b523-3dcc72540f00', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfb5d483-980d-546b-b523-3dcc72540f00'}, {'abstract': 'Remembering Etta James, Don Cornelius, Whitney Houston, Anthony