e mayor of Milwaukee, sparred over jobs, crime and collective bargaining rights.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/sharp-words-in-final-debate-before-wisconsin-recall-election/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Scott Walker and his challenger, Tom Barrett, the mayor of Milwaukee, sparred over jobs, crime and collective bargaining rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The opposing candidates sat close, side by side, at a round table – the sort of debate setting that says friendly, intimate, low key. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharp Words in Final Debate Before Wisconsin Recall Election', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T04:48:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5111d65d-1765-5b43-bd30-15fb49bbc156', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5111d65d-1765-5b43-bd30-15fb49bbc156'}, {'abstract': 'A state appellate court in Brooklyn has ordered the family to return an ancient artifact to a German museum, turning on its head the familiar scenario of Holocaust survivors suing to reclaim property.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/arts/court-tells-holocaust-survivors-family-to-return-gold-tablet.html', 'snippet': 'A state appellate court in Brooklyn has ordered the family to return an ancient artifact to a German museum, turning on its head the familiar scenario of Holocaust survivors suing to reclaim property.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A state appellate court in Brooklyn has ordered the family of a Holocaust survivor to return an ancient gold tablet to a German museum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nazi Victim’s Family Told to Return Artifact', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nazi Victim’s Family Told to Return Artifact', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations and Restitution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flamenbaum, Riven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vorderasiatisches Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Looting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T05:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2208ca4-cf57-5126-bdf5-1ba990cdd558', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2208ca4-cf57-5126-bdf5-1ba990cdd558'}, {'abstract': 'House Democrats have called for oversight hearings based on reporting in The New York Times that found the rate of sexual assault of Native American women is more than twice the national average.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/us/congressional-hearings-sought-on-abuse-of-native-women.html', 'snippet': 'House Democrats have called for oversight hearings based on reporting in The New York Times that found the rate of sexual assault of Native American women is more than twice the national average.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Democrats on the Natural Resources Committee have called on the committee’s Republican leadership to hold oversight hearings based on reporting in The New York Times in May that found the rate of sexual assault of Native American women is more than twice the national average and even greater in rural Alaskan villages. In a letter, Representatives Edward J. Markey of Massachusetts and Dan Boren of Oklahoma said that they were “extremely concerned that accountability for violent crimes in Indian Country may be decreasing as Native women continue to be victims of sexual assault at alarming rates.” They called on Representative Doc Hastings, Republican of Washington, and chairman of the committee, to “bring this issue to the national spotlight” by convening oversight hearings. Spencer Pederson, a spokesman for the committee, said that Mr. Hastings was reviewing the request. “He certainly shares the goals of ensuring safety on reservations and tribal lands,” Mr. Pederson said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congressional Hearings Sought on Abuse of Native Women', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Congressional Hearings Sought On Abuse of Native Women', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assaults', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boren, Daniel D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name