. The story involves Alan Scott, who longtime readers will know is destined to become Green Lantern. In the issue, fans will meet his boyfriend and witness the beginning of Scott’s journey toward becoming the emerald hero.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before He Was Green Lantern, He Had a Boyfriend', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DC Comics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T07:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cdbb9de-2a8a-5496-8953-b65a8ca37dd1', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cdbb9de-2a8a-5496-8953-b65a8ca37dd1'}, {'abstract': 'A wide range of homes, from condos to Victorians, often more affordable than those in neighboring Essex County communities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/realestate/living-in-verona-new-jersey.html', 'snippet': 'A wide range of homes, from condos to Victorians, often more affordable than those in neighboring Essex County communities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANY of those who end up moving to Verona started house-hunting in surrounding communities: Montclair and Glen Ridge to the east, Cedar Grove and the Caldwells to the north, Roseland to the west. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06