ons/', 'snippet': 'Jack Ewing, European economics correspondent, explores potential runs on banks, the utility of German inflation and how a Greek exit from the euro would work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First of all, thank you for the large number of excellent questions in response to our call for your queries about the euro crisis. I have picked some questions that were most representative of the interest — from all over the world — and most pertinent. And many thanks to readers like “abo” from Paris who did my work for me and supplied replies of their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/blogs/euro-currency-rdv/euro-currency-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/blogs/euro-currency-rdv/euro-currency-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1424, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Future of the Euro: Jack Ewing Answers Readers’ Questions', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date'