ocial media.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/how-i-became-smallbizlady/', 'snippet': 'Introducing Melinda Emerson, who will be blogging about social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Melinda Emerson is founder and chief executive of Quintessence Multimedia, a social media strategy and content development firm. She will be writing regularly about the use of social media in small-business marketing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How I Became @SmallBizLady', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T11:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melinda F. Emerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melinda', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Emerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33f069e6-2350-544c-a7db-5a335a3b18d2', 'word_count': 1040, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33f069e6-2350-544c-a7db-5a335a3b18d2'}, {'abstract': 'A generation of children in Big City India are growing up largely monolingual, although their parents speak many languages.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/indias-new-english-only-generation/', 'snippet': 'A generation of children in Big City India are growing up largely monolingual, although their parents speak many languages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sudhir Nagaraj and his wife, Bidisha, live in the mini-India that is Bangalore. She, a Bengali speaker from a family hailing from India’s east, heads marketing for a social networking start-up. He, fluent in the native Kannada tongue of Bangalore, runs a subsidiary of a multinational telecommunications company. Between them, they speak and understand half a dozen Indian languages. Quite ironic then that their daughter, Ahana, six-and-a-half, growing up in a country with a profusion of tongues, speaks only one language: impeccable English. And English is the common tongue that binds the Nagarajs as a family.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s New ‘English Only’ Generation', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T11:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saritha Rai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saritha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9d883bf-ca4f-5b5c-a999-982c33d31976', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9d883bf-ca4f-5b5c-a999-982c33d31976'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia said outside military intervention was not the solution for Syria but agreed with fears that the 15-month-old conflict is headed toward civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/world/middleeast/new-massacre-reported-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia said outside military intervention was not the solution for Syria but agreed with fears that the 15-month-old conflict is headed toward civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia said Friday that he rejected outside military intervention as an answer to the increasingly horrific bloodshed in Syria, and the Kremlin publicly sided with President Bashar al-Assad of Syria in blaming Mr. Assad’s armed rebel opponents for a massacre there last week that incited world outrage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/syria/syria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/syria/syria-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin Fears Civil War but Rejects Intervention in Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin Rejects Intervention But Fears Civil War in Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T11:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish and Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b69cb0f9-739b-5ca5-b9e2-84c44a81b459', 'word_count': 1254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b69cb0f9-739b-5ca5-b9e2-84c44a81b459'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: A street vendor explains to a customer why what worked for George Burns will not work for him.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/a-warning-about-cigars/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A street vendor explains to a customer why what worked for George Burns will not work for him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary: I was walking north, smoking a cigar on Madison Avenue. On Madison and East 44th Street, an old man was selling counterfeit Montblanc pens from a portable table. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warning About Cigars', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cigars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major'