aragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Sugary Drinks', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T12:09:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62fd3edf-9f89-581f-910e-af9b24b389e5', 'word_count': 79, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62fd3edf-9f89-581f-910e-af9b24b389e5'}, {'abstract': 'Shakil Afridi’s covert work for the C.I.A. as a doctor involved in a bogus vaccination campaign isn’t just hurting U.S.- Pakistani relations. It’s undermining health drives everywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/pakistani-doctors-work-for-the-cia-undermines-vaccinations-campaigns-everywhere/', 'snippet': 'Shakil Afridi’s covert work for the C.I.A. as a doctor involved in a bogus vaccination campaign isn’t just hurting U.S.- Pakistani relations. It’s undermining health drives everywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Shakil Afridi, a doctor who worked with the C.I.A. to collect DNA samples of Osama bin Laden under the guise of a bogus vaccination program, was sentenced last week to 33 years in prison under Pakistan’s tribal justice system. America’s hero is Pakistan’s traitor. And Afridi’s sentence is the latest point of contention in the stalled relations between the United States and Pakistan. Last Friday an affronted U.S. Senate panel cut $33 million in aid — $1 million for every year of Afridi’s sentence.The trial’s many irregularities are attracting a fair bit of attention. Afridi was denied legal representation. He was tried under the Frontier Crimes Regulation, a draconian code governing Pakistan’s tribal areas but not Abbottabad, where he was operating. Even by the standards of that law he was given an excessive sentence. And it remains unclear what exactly he was tried for: “antistate” activities or providing support and medical treatment to members of the Lashkar-e-Islam, a militant group based in Pakistan’s northwestern tribal areas?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Doctor Who Wouldn’t Vaccinate', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afridi, Shakil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T12:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/332d692d-6a3e-5bc8-8715-57ad4e448e9a', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/332d692d-6a3e-5bc8-8715-57ad4e448e9a'}, {'abstract': 'Two fleets, one of them Chinese and the other unidentified, intrude on bluefin tuna zones as the European Union and the United States confer on regulation of illegal fishing.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/as-regulators-meet-fishing-boats-thumb-their-noses/', 'snippet': 'Two fleets, one of them Chinese and the other unidentified, intrude on bluefin tuna zones as the European Union and the United States confer on regulation of illegal fishing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Talk about timing. As American and European fisheries officials met this week in Brussels to talk about, among other things, the problem of illegal and unregulated fishing, Chinese boats were illegally in the Mediterranean, making a mockery of efforts to manage the bluefin tuna fishing season.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Regulators Meet, Fishing Boats Thumb Their Noses', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T12:14:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b887301c-f93e-5ae1-8005-c1a159b9074d', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b887301c-f93e-5ae1-8005-c1a159b9074d'}, {'abstract': 'A report in The New York Times is the latest evidence that Mr. Obama has embraced the use of his predecessor’s national security and anti-terrorism machinery.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/obamas-counterterrorism-actions-complicate-republican-strategy/', 'snippet': 'A report in The New York Times is the latest evidence that Mr. Obama has embraced the use of his predecessor’s national security and anti-terrorism machinery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The revelation that President Obama has been personally and secretly directing a covert cyberwar against Iran could have political implications as the president enters the final stretch of his re-election campaign against Mitt Romney this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Counterterrorism Actions Complicate Republican Strategy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T12:32:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a2dc822-9d52-5ca2-aa08-ce6bd7c984b1', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a2dc822-9d52-5ca2-aa08-ce6bd7c984b1'}, {'abstract': 'A report that showed rising American unemployment in May added to the global pall that has deepened with Europe’s escalating debt crisis and slowing growth in China and India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/business/economy/us-added-69000-jobs-in-may-jobless-rate-at-8-2.html', 'snippet': 'A report that showed rising American unemployment in May added to the global pall that has deepened with Europe’s escalating debt crisis and slowing growth in China and India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a third year, the economic recovery in the United States is floundering, stoking fears of a global slowdown as the Euro