e 12 innovative products are anything but. Summer beauty essentials worth seeking out:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vain Glorious | Summer Beauty Must-Haves', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nails (Body Part)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clarins SA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T13:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lily Nima', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nima', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84196f1c-6787-5fef-9ade-317145370e6f', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84196f1c-6787-5fef-9ade-317145370e6f'}, {'abstract': 'A Facebook ad service has the potential to increase ad revenue, but there are pitfalls. Also, at least three minutes of “Men in Black 3” were censored for Chinese audiences.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/the-breakfast-meeting-turning-likes-to-ads-and-trims-to-men-in-black-3-in-china/', 'snippet': 'A Facebook ad service has the potential to increase ad revenue, but there are pitfalls. Also, at least three minutes of “Men in Black 3” were censored for Chinese audiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook has a service — the “sponsored story” — that converts a user’s idle comment (or “like”) about a product into an ad for that product that appears on friends’ pages, Somini Sengupta writes. The service has the potential to help the company marshal its hundreds of millions users to increase ad revenue, but there are also pitfalls in enlisting your users this way, not least that the service has no sense of humor. (Case in point: the man who posted, wryly, about seeing on Amazon.com a 55-pound container of personal lubricant.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Turning ‘Likes’ to Ads, and Trims to ‘Men in Black 3’ in China', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T13:04:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d75b1ae9-2ee8-575a-a793-4f0ff9ed4ee2', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d75b1ae9-2ee8-575a-a793-4f0ff9ed4ee2'}, {'abstract': 'A new app measures your energy consumption, “likes” become ads on Facebook, the Agriculture Department will increase tests for E. coli in raw beef and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/friday-reading-a-new-app-measures-your-energy-consumption/', 'snippet': 'A new app measures your energy consumption, “likes” become ads on Facebook, the Agriculture Department will increase tests for E. coli in raw beef and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The 