But the immediate reaction from Congressional leaders to the grim jobs report signaled little movement toward breaking the long, partisan deadlock over fiscal policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama, facing some of the worst economic indicators in many months, on Friday urged members of Congress not to “sit on your hands” and to pass the tax breaks and spending programs that he has been pushing for months to increase the pace of job formation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Congress Point Fingers Over Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama and Congress Point Fingers Over Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T14:36:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c54f524b-dd9a-595d-95e8-9bc2941bcfd1', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c54f524b-dd9a-595d-95e8-9bc2941bcfd1'}, {'abstract': 'Reasonably strong private-sector job growth has been offset by government layoffs.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/a-lagging-recovery/', 'snippet': 'Reasonably strong private-sector job growth has been offset by government layoffs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jobs report for May was worse than almost anyone expected. It cries out for action from Washington, but the political pressures point the other way. Just as Europe needs to do something to push growth, so does the United States. But there are powerful forces screaming to cut government spending on both continents. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lagging Recovery', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T14:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee6f306c-ff88-57be-866a-8ae1dd07c31d', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee6f306c-ff88-57be-866a-8ae1dd07c31d'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Shindo, who directed nearly 50 movies, was perhaps best known for films with themes relating to the wartime atomic devastation in his native Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/arts/kaneto-shindo-filmmaker-dies-at-100.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Shindo, who directed nearly 50 movies, was perhaps best known for films with themes relating to the wartime atomic devastation in his native Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kaneto Shindo, a venerable filmmaker whose work was haunted by the wartime devastation of his native Hiroshima, died on Tuesday at his home in Tokyo. He was 100.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'captio