yt://article/9e4d2bc7-636f-5dfe-88fa-6cdea5f4a14e', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e4d2bc7-636f-5dfe-88fa-6cdea5f4a14e'}, {'abstract': '“Green Lantern: Sinestro” hits the hardcover list at No. 4 this week.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/graphic-books-best-sellers-the-latest-green-lantern-series/', 'snippet': '“Green Lantern: Sinestro” hits the hardcover list at No. 4 this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The original Green Lantern, introduced in 1940, has undergone a reboot and is now gay, but the Green Lantern that is more familiar to the general public — from the SuperFriends cartoons, Justice League comics and, perhaps, the Ryan Reynolds film from last year — hits the graphic books hardcover best-seller list at No. 4 this week. “Green Lantern: Sinestro” collects the first six issues of the hero’s latest series, which finds Hal Jordan without his power ring, and his longtime enemy Sinestro on the side of angels. Why does everything have to be so complicated?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: The Latest Green Lantern Series', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T16:12:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed1d66e7-ab1b-542f-bc00-2f0088d9718f', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed1d66e7-ab1b-542f-bc00-2f0088d9718f'}, {'abstract': 'The decision to lump together the leading and supporting actors follows a decision to merge best miniseries with best made-for-TV movie.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/emmys-to-shrink-number-of-acting-awards-for-tv-movies/', 'snippet': 'The decision to lump together the leading and supporting actors follows a decision to merge best miniseries with best made-for-TV movie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The group that hands out the Emmy Awards is making a controversial change to the nominations in its movie and miniseries category. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emmys to Shrink Number of Acting Awards for TV Movies', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T16:17:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35498900-8c0b-5585-a9b9-913d44809efd', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35498900-8c0b-5585-a9b9-913d44809efd'}, {'abstract': 'The two-day Investec Derby Festival began at Epsom Downs Racecourse in Epsom, England, and the French Open tennis tournament continued in Paris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/01/sports/SPTSREPLAY0601.html', 'snippet': 'The two-day Investec Derby Festival began at Epsom Downs Racecourse in Epsom, England, and the French Open tennis tournament continued in Paris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The two-day Investec Derby Festival began at Epsom Downs Racecourse in Epsom, England, and the French Open tennis tournament continued in Paris.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multim