show', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/18f4df6d-a4da-5669-a160-303d2fa3d67e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/18f4df6d-a4da-5669-a160-303d2fa3d67e'}, {'abstract': 'Much more potential than the official line says.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/poor-mouthing-britain/', 'snippet': 'Much more potential than the official line says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote a few days ago about the widespread belief here in the UK that there has somehow been a dramatic collapse in the economy’s potential. Martin Wolf has much more, plus a link to a very important paper by Martin and Rowthorn (pdf) that, as I read it (and Wolf too) very effectively debunks that belief.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poor-Mouthing Britain', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T16:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/648f4c4b-bf05-5330-bd84-9794a26e174f', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/648f4c4b-bf05-5330-bd84-9794a26e174f'}, {'abstract': 'Surveys of manufacturers in many countries appear to indicate that the trade-led recovery of 2010 and 2011 is stalling out or even reversing. The charts reflect the proportion of manufacturers each month who said export orders are increasing. A figure of 50 indicates as many said orders were growing as said they were declining. A figure well above 50 indicates most said orders were rising, while one well below the figure indicates the opposite. They reflect surveys over the past year in the four largest euro zone countries and in four other major exporters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/01/business/Indications-of-a-Trade-Slowdown.html', 'snippet': 'Surveys of manufacturers in many countries appear to indicate that the trade-led recovery of 2010 and 2011 is stalling out or even reversing. The charts reflect the proportion of manufacturers each month who said export orders are increasing. A fi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Surveys of manufacturers in many countries appear to indicate that the trade-led recovery of 2010 and 2011 is stalling out or even reversing. The charts reflect the proportion of manufacturers each month who said export orders are increasing. A figure of 50 indicates as many said orders were growing as said they were declining. A figure well above 50 indicates most said orders were rising, while one well below the figure indicates the opposite. They reflect surveys over the past year in the four largest euro zone countries and in four other major exporters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indications of a Trade Slowdown', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T16:57:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/6825b0da-7fa2-529b-920b-916f125fdd8f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/6825b0da-7fa2-529b-920b-916f125fdd8f'}, {'abstract': 'The queen’s clothes, like those of circus performers and rock stars, are designed for specific functionality, since unlike most commoners, she mainly works standing up.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/fashion/queen-elizabeth-ii-sets-a-style-standard.html', 'snippet': 'The queen’s clothes, like those of circus performers and rock stars, are designed for specific functionality, since unlike most commoners, she mainly works standing up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOUGH it is something the Red Queen might have said, it was actually uttered by Elizabeth II. “I have to be seen to be believed,” the queen of England remarked, according to her most recent biographer, Sally Bedell Smith. Far from being a goofball tautology, that declaration is a shrewd assessment of monarchy management in an era when image rules supreme. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/fashion/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/fashion/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/fashion/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1052, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/fashion/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1993, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/fashion/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/fashion/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N/20120603-QUEEN-slide-5M3N-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw