 the poor May jobs report would imperil President Obama’s re-election chances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economy, and Obama, Mired in Down Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:02:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a50e56-678e-5c98-9935-06658880c8ee', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a50e56-678e-5c98-9935-06658880c8ee'}, {'abstract': 'A. O. Scott gets hot as David Carr (“Whoa!”) criticizes critics and cultural criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/the-sweet-spot-june-1/', 'snippet': 'A. O. Scott gets hot as David Carr (“Whoa!”) criticizes critics and cultural criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s episode, A. O. Scott and David Carr criticize each other’s critical perspectives on cultural criticism. (Just for fun, count how many times Mr. Carr says “Whoa!”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sweet Spot: June 1', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/284ae12f-946e-59d5-911a-9402e86577ff', 'word_count': 29, 'uri': 'nyt://article/284ae12f-946e-59d5-911a-9402e86577ff'}, {'abstract': 'Sotheby’s 10-month lockout of unionized art hand