 Fulton Street, photographed in 1909 when it was new and today, retains some of its fanciful front.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whyte’s restaurant at 145 Fulton Street, photographed in 1909 when it was new and today, retains some of its fanciful front.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before & After: The Way We Were', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Financial District (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:07:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f4afb31b-c5af-5530-8ed7-5d013ebb6f84', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f4afb31b-c5af-5530-8ed7-5d013ebb6f84'}, {'abstract': 'Readers’ questions: The Dakota’s backyard, and Whyte’s restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/realestate/the-dakotas-back-40.html', 'snippet': 'Readers’ questions: The Dakota’s backyard, and Whyte’s restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q We live at 27 West 72nd, and would like to know the history of the huge white brick apartment house next door, the Mayfair, at 15 West 72nd Street. How did it come about, right in the Dakota’s backyard? ... Harvey Kulawitz, New York and Ridgefield, Conn.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03STREET3_SPAN/03STREET3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'image