e-olympians/', 'snippet': 'In 1912, passengers and U.S. Olympians would mingle as they traveled by boat to Sweden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One hundred years ago the Summer Olympics were held in Stockholm. As we count down the days to London 2012, we’ll take a look back at what was happening at the Games a century ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweden 1912: Cruising With the Olympians', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/850cc006-cf5c-56c2-a831-3aa5d3e7b5ed', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/850cc006-cf5c-56c2-a831-3aa5d3e7b5ed'}, {'abstract': 'Millicent Souris’s new cookbook hopes to fulfill the statement, “Easy as pie.” Here, an exclusive recipe from the chef.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/bookshelf-how-to-build-a-better-pie/', 'snippet': 'Millicent Souris’s new cookbook hopes to fulfill the statement, “Easy as pie.” Here, an exclusive recipe from the chef.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been said that simple foods are the most difficult to master. Take, for example, pie. Its familiar, comforting, iconic character comes with countless questions, even for baking hobbyists: How do you make a perfectly flaky crust? What kitchen tools are absolutely essential? How does one thicken a fruit filling? Luckily, just in time for prime summer pie season, comes the chef Millicent Souris’s new cookbook, out today, titled “How to Build a Better Pie.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf | ‘How to Build a Better Pie’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:25:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c27ed2e-0381-56a2-aab1-33c287684ea6', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c27ed2e-0381-56a2-aab1-33c287684ea6'}, {'abstract': 'Check e-mail for co-op news; a long-term guest or a resident; stove replaced by a cheaper model.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/realestate/new-york-real-estate-question-answer.html', 'snippet': 'Check e-mail for co-op news; a long-term guest or a resident; stove replaced by a cheaper model.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Check E-Mail for Co-op News', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q & A', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Q&A', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condominiums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooperatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landlords', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:34