City Room is proud to present this Doughnut Double Feature. Happy National Donut Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a public service to our readers on National Donut Day here in New York City, City Room is proud to present this Doughnut Double Feature. City Room believes that doughnuts, consumed in moderation, are part of a healthy, balanced diet, along with sawdust, bismuth and spider eggs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And Now, a Salute to Doughnuts', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a5729f8-7182-5a60-849c-6bda905f9048', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a5729f8-7182-5a60-849c-6bda905f9048'}, {'abstract': 'Outdoor kitchens seem to be picking up steam again in Westchester. Agents say they can help to sell a house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/realestate/the-kitchens-day-in-the-sun.html', 'snippet': 'Outdoor kitchens seem to be picking up steam again in Westchester. Agents say they can help to sell a house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Dan Amicucci, a builder, visited Tuscany several years ago with his wife, Phyllis, he saw his first Old-World pizza oven and decided he wanted one just like it. A frustrated chef, he envisioned it in the backyard of their Nantucket-style colonial in Armonk.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/03WEZONE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/03WEZONE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/we-zone-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/we-zone-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/03WEZONE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/03WEZONE_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/realestate/03WEZONE_SPAN/03WEZONE_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kitchen’s Day in the Sun', 'kicker': 'In the Region | Westchester', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Kitchen’s Day in the Sun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kitchens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elsa Brenner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elsa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brenner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f6aadea-db5a-5b33-a4a6-52fa0bd05c3a', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f6aadea-db5a-5b33-a4a6-52fa0bd05c3a'}, {'abstract': 'The idea of shippable, long-lasting cheese was easier to conceive than to execute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/magazine/who-made-that-kraft-single.html', 'snippet': 'The idea of shippable, long-lasting cheese was easier to conceive than to execute.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The genius of James L. Kraft, the Canadian-born founder of Kraft Foods, lay not in artisanal cheesemaking but in taking a milk-based product and making it long-lasting, consistent in quality and easy to slice. In 1916, after a series of experiments at his Chicago boardinghouse, the former grocery clerk received a patent for “process cheese”: a sterilized product made by heating Cheddar at 175 degrees for 15 minutes while whisking it continuously. The invention helped turn cheese into a shippable commodity with a longer shelf life — and transform Kraft’s company into a cheese empire. James’s brother Norman, who became Kraft’s head of research, wanted to make things even easier for the consumer by precutting the cheese into slices. The idea was easier to conceive than to execute: process cheese was packaged and sealed while still fluid and hot, and cutting hot cheese was like trying to slice molten lava.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/03wmt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/03wmt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/mag-03WMT-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/mag-03WMT-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1176, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/03wmt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/03wmt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03wmt/03wmt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Kraft Single?', 'kicker': 'Makers', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Kraft Singles)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kraft Foods Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:52:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2337c4f-fdc0-5143-8757-bf910f80a9df', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2337c4f-fdc0-5143-8757-bf910f80a9df'}, {'abstract': 'The former president says that Gov. Scott Walker has split the state, and that division does not work.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/bill-clinton-campaigns-against-walker-in-wisconsin-recall-election/', 'snippet': 'The former president says that Gov. Scott Walker has split the state, and that division does not work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a crowded, chilly park in downtown Milwaukee, former President Bill Clinton on Friday urged Wisconsin residents to remove Gov. Scott Walker from office in the state’s recall election next week, saying that the Republican governor had split the state and that division, as an overarching political philosophy, doesn’t work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Clinton Campaigns Against Walker in Wisconsin Recall Election', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:54:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a0afe5c-dcea-50e8-a0ac-75102361d46e', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a0afe5c-dcea-50e8-a0ac-75102361d46e'}, {'abstract': 'Many children wet the bed because they’re constipated, and their parents and doctors don’t know it.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/when-bedwetting-isnt-an-accident/', 'snippet': 'Many children wet the bed because they’re constipated, and their parents and doctors don’t know it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a pediatric urologist, I know that, as The Times reported recently, the popular laxative Miralax isn’t (gasp!) F.D.A.-approved for children. I still prescribe it daily. I believe Miralax’s active ingredient (polyethylene glycol 3350, or PEG) is safe for kids. The problem isn’t overuse in children; it’s underuse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Bedwetting Isn’t an ‘Accident’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bedwetting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constipation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laxatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:55:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve J. Hodges', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hodges', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356501c0-b06a-5523-827d-b52a9588756e', 'word_count': 742, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356501c0-b06a-5523-827d-b52a9588756e'}, {'abstract': 'After years in a crowded apartment, the Wild Bird Fund is opening a full-fledged rehabilitation center on the Upper West Side of Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/a-wildlife-rescue-center-for-new-york-city/', 'snippet': 'After years in a crowded apartment, the Wild Bird Fund is opening a full-fledged rehabilitation center on the Upper West Side of Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2001, over 7,000 feathered and furry vagrants have passed through a cramped apartment on Manhattan’s Upper West Side, with screaming babies stacked above solemn old-timers and sprightly young fellows whistling aside the gravely ill. But as my colleagues Kelly Slivka and Kate Yandell report in this video, this eclectic menagerie, known as the Wild Bird Fund, has now secured a 1,300-square-foot independent space that opens on Saturday on Columbus Avenue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wildlife Rescue Center for New York City', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:57:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09206f26-d6ed-5a21-aea9-02af19a516d0', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09206f26-d6ed-5a21-aea9-02af19a516d0'}, {'abstract': 'An abridged guide to the many ways that your day is about to get better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/03/magazine/innovations-issue.html', 'snippet': 'An abridged guide to the many ways that your day is about to get better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An abridged guide to the many ways that your day is about to get better.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '32 Innovations That Will Change Your Tomorrow', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T17:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/966e60e1-9e67-5f85-968c-e3eed94fc987', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/966e60e1-9e67-5f85-968c-e3eed94fc987'}, {'abstract': 'Via Verde, an eco-friendly project, evolved from a competition intended to encourage developers to work with architects to use the latest green concepts.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/green-tinted-housing-project-to-open-in-south-bronx-on-monday/', 'snippet': 'Via Verde, an eco-friendly project, evolved from a competition intended to encourage developers to work with architects to use the latest green concepts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Via Verde, the eco-friendly subsidized development in the South Bronx at Brook Avenue and East 156th Street is officially opening on June 18. Designed by the New York office of Grimshaw Architects of London and Dattner Architects from New York, the project was developed by Jonathan Rose, a for-profit developer, and Phipps Houses Group, a nonprofit organization with a history in subsidized housing. \xa0Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg will cut the ribbon, along with Shaun Donovan, the secretary of Housing and Urban Development.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Green-Tinted Housing Project to Open This Month', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank'