'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03magazine-covers-slide-RT6B/03magazine-covers-slide-RT6B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03magazine-covers-slide-RT6B/03magazine-covers-slide-RT6B-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/magazine/03magazine-covers-slide-RT6B/03magazine-covers-slide-RT6B-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Did What to Our Logo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:26:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e0a7f6e6-feca-5c8f-aca8-99b851859032', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e0a7f6e6-feca-5c8f-aca8-99b851859032'}, {'abstract': 'Posters for Clint Eastwood movies, paintings by Bob Dylan, covers rejected by The New Yorker and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/books/review/clint-eastwood-posters-bob-dylan-paintings-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'Posters for Clint Eastwood movies, paintings by Bob Dylan, covers rejected by The New Yorker and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you think of Clint Eastwood, what do you see? The snarling, squinting, cigarillo-chomping, poncho-wearing gunslinger? Or the steely-eyed, angst-ridden, snarling, squinting, Magnum-toting rogue cop? Eastwood has had less menacing roles (“The Bridges of Madison County,” anyone?), but the brooding loner in Sergio Leone’s spaghetti westerns and the hot-tempered detective in the “Dirty Harry” series are indelibly seared on the public’s consciousness, in large part through the posters that defined and sold his stardom. “Perhaps the most striking thing about the early Eastwood poster art,” the film expert Thomas Schatz writes in CLINT EASTWOOD ICON: The Essential Film Art Collection (Insight Editions, $39.95), by David Frangioni, “is the steady clarification of his image — the way his distinctive face and features go from being abstract and unrecognizable in so many of the early posters to being unmistakably those of Clint Eastwood.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/books/review/03eastwood/03eastwood-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/books/review/03eastwood/03eastwood-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 300, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/books/review/03eastwood/03eastwood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/books/review/03eastwood/03eastwood-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/books/review/03eastwood/03eastwood-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Visuals', 'kicker': 'Web Extra', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'valu