ticle/63d430ba-0ce9-54e5-8f90-d949fb11f4bc'}, {'abstract': 'Shares in the online coupon giant tumbled as much as 10 percent on Friday, and by midafternoon remained mired at about $9.65 a share, as a lockup on insider selling expired.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/as-lock-up-expires-groupons-shares-plunge/', 'snippet': 'Shares in the online coupon giant tumbled as much as 10 percent on Friday, and by midafternoon remained mired at about $9.65 a share, as a lockup on insider selling expired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the stock markets have been having a bad day on Friday, Groupon has been having a really bad day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Lockup Expires, Groupon’s Shares Plunge', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Groupon Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:40:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e8a96c6-dee3-5b2e-924c-26d732d7ff3d', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e8a96c6-dee3-5b2e-924c-26d732d7ff3d'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s effort to improve user experience on its search pages while navigating government censorship is being greeted skeptically by some observers in China.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/skepticism-greets-googles-attempt-to-deal-with-censored-terms-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Google’s effort to improve user experience on its search pages while navigating government censorship is being greeted skeptically by some observers in China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As my colleague Michael Wines reports, Google has quietly unveiled a feature on its search pages in China that warns users when they type in terms that could run afoul of the country’s robust censorship network. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Skepticism Greets Google’s Attempt to Deal With Censored Terms in China', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:40:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37256d83-ca67-5b56-9662-01687918d809', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37256d83-ca67-5b56-9662-01687918d809'}, {'abstract': 'Manufacturers in eight countries reported growth in export orders in late 2010 and early 2011, but now those orders are falling or, at best, holding their own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/business/economy/manufacturing-is-losing-its-momentum.html', 'snippet': 'Manufacturers in eight countries reported growth in export orders in late 2010 and early 2011, but now those orders are falling or, at best, holding their own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE end of the credit crisis in 2009 was followed by a sharp rise in world trade. Manufacturing helped lead economic recoveries in the United States and elsewhere. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Manufacturing’s Turn for the Worse', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manufacturing’s Turn for the Worse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:46:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47290780-be08-5428-bbdf-3d7a6f188c55', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47290780-be08-5428-bbdf-3d7a6f188c55'}, {'abstract': 'Stuart Sternberg is a Mets fan, but he is the principal owner of the Tampa Bay Rays. Buying a stake in a sports team means not just investing passionately, but joining a very exclusive club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/your-money/stuart-sternberg-loves-the-mets-owns-the-rays-and-loves-a-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'Stuart Sternberg is a Mets fan, but he is the principal owner of the Tampa Bay Rays. Buying a stake in a sports team means not just investing passionately, but joining a very exclusive club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SITTING at Citi Field this week, I started thinking about whether I would care more about the game, between the New York Mets and the Philadelphia Phillies, if I owned one of the teams. I’m not a fan of either club — a friend had an extra ticket and invited me — but my reverie was prompted by a recent talk I had with Stuart L. Sternberg. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/your-money/02wealth/02wealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buying a Sports Team Takes Heart and Cash, Plenty of It', 'kicker': 'Wealth Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Buying a Sports Team Takes Heart and Cash, Plenty of It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sternberg, Stuart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High Net Worth Individuals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asset Allocation (Personal Finances)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minor Leagues', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:54:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d939d7f-a19c-5de2-8d08-1549a26e2898', 'word_count': 1350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d939d7f-a19c-5de2-8d08-1549a26e2898'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s Summer Reading issue includes a look at the making of “Animal House” and new books about two legendary American musicians.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/book-review-podcast-animal-house-dylan-springsteen-and-other-summer-reading/', 'snippet': 'This year’s Summer Reading issue includes a look at the making of “Animal House” and new books about two legendary American musicians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the Summer Reading issue of the New York Times Book Review, there’s something for everyone. And much more. We lead off with roundups of some of the season’s notable cookbooks, travel books and gardening books. Toni Bentley reviews a new book about the 27-year dancing partnership between Fred Astaire and his sister, Adele. Al Sharpton reviews a biography of James Brown, complete with a picture that will make your week. Jim Bouton looks at two new books about the New York Yankees —\xa0an insider’s history and a collection of essays about loving and hating baseball’s most iconic team. If you prefer the Red Sox, we’ve got them covered, too, with a commemoration of the 100-year anniversary of Fenway Park. In anticipation of Father’s Day, Pamela Paul reviews several picture books that celebrate the energy, imagination and love of dads.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast: ‘Animal House,’ Dylan, Springsteen and Other Summer Reading', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astaire, Fred', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, Robin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keepnews, Peter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tanenhaus, Sam', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8c0c568-9d62-551c-afaf-89c6c71b3cb5', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8c0c568-9d62-551c-afaf-89c6c71b3cb5'}, {'abstract': 'How dealers started a bidding war to drive up prices in the art market.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/is-a-basquiat-painting-really-worth-16-million/', 'snippet': 'How dealers started a bidding war to drive up prices in the art market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in the magazine, Adam Davidson examines what’s really driving some art prices to record highs. In part, it’s because “the value of any artist’s work is determined by an insider world of cultural arbiters who coordinate with one another,” Davidson writes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is a Basquiat Painting Really Worth $16 Million?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:59:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kedmey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kedmey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4541df2e-c31e-5aed-a01a-d67bfe98a6d2', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4541df2e-c31e-5aed-a01a-d67bfe98a6d2'}, {'abstract': 'The Wealth Matters column takes on the subject of owning a professional sports team, and Bucks readers discuss their ownership dreams.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/dreams-of-team-ownership/', 'snippet': 'The Wealth Matters column takes on the subject of owning a professional sports team, and Bucks readers discuss their ownership dreams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan has been writing for the last few weeks about people who follow their passion and invest in areas as varied as films or race horses, restaurants or vineyards. This week, his Wealth Matters column is about investing in sports teams.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreams of Team Ownership', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T18:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3550fa4-4ae5-596b-8284-4beaf12de441', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3550fa4-4ae5-596b-8284-4beaf12de441'}, {'abstract': 'A nine-day tour from Hollywood to Las Vegas accompanied by an expert on the franchise.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/if-theres-no-such-thing-as-too-much-star-trek/', 'snippet': 'A nine-day tour from Hollywood to Las Vegas accompanied by an expert on the franchise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Star Trek fans who find that a convention dedicated to their favorite topic isn’t enough of a journey can book a nine-day tour from Hollywood to Las Vegas, accompanied by an expert on the franchise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If There’s No Such Thing As Too Much ‘Star Trek’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Griffith Observatory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hollywood (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_dat