 exposed. [The Guardian]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Cuts in the Firefighting Budget', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T19:13:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ef7986e-7219-599c-b82a-fa1791bbbf8f', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ef7986e-7219-599c-b82a-fa1791bbbf8f'}, {'abstract': 'For nearly two weeks now, on-site teams have been charting the extent of the damage to historic buildings caused by two strong earthquakes in the Emilia-Romagna region on a disaster map that continues to grow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/world/europe/italy-tries-to-fathom-roster-of-damage.html', 'snippet': 'For nearly two weeks now, on-site teams have been charting the extent of the damage to historic buildings caused by two strong earthquakes in the Emilia-Romagna region on a disaster map that continues to grow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIRANDOLA, ITALY — With every new quiver, something crumbles somewhere or new cracks appear. “It’s like receiving a daily list of war casualties,” said Carla Di Francesco, the supervisor for cultural heritage in this part of northern Italy. “The second major quake compounded the emergency, and we had to start monitoring everything from scratch.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Tries to Fathom Roster of Damage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy Tries to Fathom Roster of Damage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Emilia-Romagna (Italy)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthqua