tract': 'The latest projections by Moody’s Analytics for monthly job growth still point to a close race for the White House. But the odds of a mini-boom that would help the incumbent have faded.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/jobs-forecast-shifts-the-electoral-outlook/', 'snippet': 'The latest projections by Moody’s Analytics for monthly job growth still point to a close race for the White House. But the odds of a mini-boom that would help the incumbent have faded.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The disappointing jobs report released Friday suggests that the economy is weaker than most analysts thought – and that job growth in coming months will be weaker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs Forecast Shifts the Electoral Outlook', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forecasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T19:20:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2dc887b-4d15-5c61-a31c-2c23a7a1766e', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2dc887b-4d15-5c61-a31c-2c23a7a1766e'}, {'abstract': 'The return of the Oprah Book Club will begin with "Wild" by Cheryl Strayed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001582034/oprah-book-club-20.html', 'snippet': 'The return of the Oprah Book Club will begin with "Wild" by Cheryl Strayed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The return of the Oprah Book Club will begin with "Wild" by Cheryl Strayed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/business/video-oprah/video-oprah-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/01/business/video-oprah/video-oprah-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/business/video-oprah/video-oprah-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/01/business/video-oprah/video-oprah-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oprah Book Club 2.0', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T19:20:37+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'OWN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Own', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c86d7959-5636-56f7-a329-77abf95eb7ca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c86d7959-5636-56f7-a329-77abf95eb7ca'}, {'abstract': 'A writer travels all the way to Buenos Aires to taste something heartfelt — and Korean.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/the-case-of-the-argentine-waiter-and-the-korean-supper-club/', 'snippet': 'A writer travels all the way to Buenos Aires to taste something heartfelt — and Korean.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I’ve got one for you,” the waiter said in a stagey whisper and handed me a cafe chit upon which he’d written “casamun.com,” the Web site of the hottest new puerta cerrada, or private supper club, in Buenos Aires. It was the fifth morning in a row that I had had coffee at the elegant Las Violetas cafe. There I earned a warm “Buenos Días” and a courtly half bow from the same distinguished, leonine, white-jacketed waiter I’d had the mornings before. We’d discovered our mutual passion for good food when he saw the French newspaper I’d been reading the first day I came in, right off the plane from Paris. The paper prompted a moist-eyed reminiscence of a trip to France he’d made as a young man; he had told me he hopes to eat a black truffle omelet again before “God drops the curtains.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Case of the Argentine Waiter and the Korean Supper Club', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T19:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2166d1c1-27f2-5b81-a82a-248cacb1e044', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2166d1c1-27f2-5b81-a82a-248cacb1e044'}, {'abstract': 'Luc Petton, a choreographer, brings both swans and dancers together on stage and in everyday life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/dance/100000001582070/dancing-with-swans.html', 'snippet': 'Luc Petton, a choreographer, brings both swans and dancers together on stage and in everyday life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Luc Petton, a choreographer, brings both swans and dancers together on stage and in everyday life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/video-petton-swans/video-petton-swans-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/video-petton-swans/video-petton-swans-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/video-petton-swans/video-petton-swans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/01/arts/video-petton-swans/video-petton-swans-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dancing With Swans', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T19:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Michael Kurcfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurcfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/217551b2-fc90-538a-8614-37316cc31112', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/217551b2-fc90-538a-8614-37316cc31112'}, {'abstract': 'Olympic officials have released a sample menu of food and beverages at the events in London and the high prices have drawn criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/youll-have-to-pony-up-11-for-an-olympic-beer/', 'snippet': 'Olympic officials have released a sample menu of food and beverages at the events in London and the high prices have drawn criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s one advantage of watching the Olympics at home instead of in London: you can crack open a cold one for regular retail prices. Because if you’re at an event at the London Games, a pint of beer will set you back more than $11.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You’ll Have to Pony Up $11 for an Olympic Beer', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heineken NV', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T19:35:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0312224e-c477-5eaa-b919-d309e4b6af81', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0312224e-c477-5eaa-b919-d309e4b6af81'}, {'abstract': 'The Cambodian government will ask the Metropolitan Museum of Art to return twin sandstone figures that were allegedly looted from a jungle temple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/arts/design/cambodia-to-ask-met-to-return-10th-century-statues.html', 'snippet': 'The Cambodian government will ask the Metropolitan Museum of Art to return twin sandstone figures that were allegedly looted from a jungle temple.', 'le