e': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T20:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cathy Horyn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cathy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horyn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d02f3ad9-8693-5568-91bd-6c18e737fd54', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d02f3ad9-8693-5568-91bd-6c18e737fd54'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than use a conventional all-wheel-drive transfer case, Ferrari bolts two transmissions to the FF’s engine, drawing torque from the front and rear of the crankshaft to drive, respectively, the front and rear wheels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/automobiles/2-gearboxes-to-drive-4-wheels.html', 'snippet': 'Rather than use a conventional all-wheel-drive transfer case, Ferrari bolts two transmissions to the FF’s engine, drawing torque from the front and rear of the crankshaft to drive, respectively, the front and rear wheels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RATHER than use a conventional all-wheel-drive transfer case, Ferrari bolts two transmissions to the FF’s V-12 engine, drawing torque from both the front and rear of the crankshaft to drive, respectively, the front and rear wheels. ', 'print_section': 'AU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '2 Gearboxes to Drive 4 Wheels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '2 Gearboxes to Drive 4 Wheels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T20:03:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Automobiles', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': '', '