cker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsberg, Allen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenthal, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T22:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Maurer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maurer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9d76b25-6dee-505c-bb0c-32cbc20b2192', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9d76b25-6dee-505c-bb0c-32cbc20b2192'}, {'abstract': 'Reader suggestions on what, besides large portions of soda, should be prohibited in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/prohibitions-of-the-mundane-and-the-nonsensical/', 'snippet': 'Reader suggestions on what, besides large portions of soda, should be prohibited in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York may be the world’s greatest city, but it abounds with menaces to the public health and well-being. So when Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg proposed banning the sale of large sugary drinks at restaurants and other places, City Room took the opportunity to ask readers to suggest other things that ought not to be allowed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prohibitions of the Mundane and the Nonsensical', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T22:13:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fd57bf4-623f-5720-a657-91d7ace93d83', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fd57bf4-623f-5720-a657-91d7ace93d83'}, {'abstract': 'In “Rowdy Rathore,” a petty thief and a supercop join forces in a film that exemplifies the Bollywood school of More Is More.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/movies/rowdy-rathore-with-akshay-kumar.html', 'snippet': 'In “Rowdy Rathore,” a petty thief and a supercop join forces in a film that exemplifies the Bollywood school of More Is More.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A pumped-up example of the Bollywood school of More Is More, “Rowdy Rathore,” starring Akshay Kumar, has a little of everything, all executed in an exaggerated, playful style by the film’s director, Prabhudheva. There are fights, colorful songs and dances (the stick-in-your-head, drum-driven tunes are by Sajid and Wajid Ali), comedy, romance, a superstar item girl (Kareena Kapoor, who appears in one song) and a plot worthy of the old days of Hindi cinema.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bollywood Plot Thickened With Every Ingredient', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rowdy Rathore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Akshay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T22:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c4c5c40-c18e-52f3-824d-62b12c0b37d9', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c4c5c40-c18e-52f3-824d-62b12c0b37d9'}, {'abstract': 'Florida Republicans keep trying to reduce the participation of minorities and the poor in elections. Now the Justice Department is stepping in.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/the-law-comes-to-florida/', 'snippet': 'Florida Republicans keep trying to reduce the participation of minorities and the poor in elections. Now the Justice Department is stepping in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florida Republicans have gone so far in trying to tilt the voter rolls to their advantage that two higher powers were forced to step in yesterday to right the balance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Law Comes to Florida', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-01T22:18:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f399ca95-a32a-5458-95b9-76e8bf8f3d8f', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f399ca95-a32a-5458-95b9-76e8bf8f3d8f'}, {'abstract': 'Memorial Day weekend was a great preview of summer, with women deciding for themselves what lengths their skirts would be and how high they would wear their shorts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000001582490/bill-cunningham-independents.html', 'snippet': 'Memorial Day weeke