web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/our-servants-do-pretty-much-as-they-please/', 'snippet': 'Slaves in occupied New Orleans didn’t wait for Lincoln: they emancipated themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Touring the United States for the London Times, the war correspondent William Howard Russell reached New Orleans late in May 1861 to find a city ablaze. Confederate flags flew from the public buildings and private homes. Soldiers paraded through the streets in smart columns of dash and pomp. Gentlemen at the St. Charles Hotel pored over the latest papers for news of the dawning war. The police were rounding up suspected abolitionists, and every night mysterious fires flared up around the city – set, it was rumored, by the slaves. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Our Servants Do Pretty Much as They Please’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Butler, Benjamin Franklin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T01:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Rothman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/824d7797-aba2-5917-bcdd-fed336ae041b', 'word_count': 1326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/824d7797-aba2-5917-bcdd-fed336ae041b'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo had made a signature initiative of building the country’s largest convention center and a casino at the Aqueduct racetrack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/nyregion/plan-collapses-for-queens-convention-hall-and-casino.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo had made a signature initiative of building the country’s largest convention center and a casino at the Aqueduct racetrack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $4 billion plan announced by Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo to create the country’s largest convention center and a casino in Queens has fallen apart, the governor acknowledged on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo’s $4 Billion Plan for Project in Queens Falls Apart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proposal To Put Convention Hall In Queens Is Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genting Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T01:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan and Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ad2aa70-d41b-5c47-a884-3e5f0688802e', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ad2aa70-d41b-5c47-a884-3e5f0688802e'}, {'abstract': 'Long Island theaters and day camps offer a variety of programs for theatrically inclined children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/nyregion/for-children-summer-theater-programs-on-long-island.html', 'snippet': 'Long Island theaters and day camps offer a variety of programs for theatrically inclined children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'YOUNGSTERS who thrill to the roar of the crowd at the school play — even if their parents are doing much of the roaring — need not pack away their passion for the summer. Long Island theaters and day camps offer a variety of options during the school break for drama-oriented children, whether they are novices or already dreaming of future residuals. ', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI2_SPAN/03ARTSLI2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI2_SPAN/03ARTSLI2_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI2_SPAN/03ARTSLI2_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI2_SPAN/03ARTSLI2_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1212, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03ARTSLI2_SPAN/03ARTSLI2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 't