 or more grams of crack cocaine with an intent to distribute it because he had previously been convicted of a felony. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jury Draws a Line', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jury Draws a Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurley, Rodney', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, William G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T01:03:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/d26bc397-8f43-50e8-a87c-dbece1ff19dd', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d26bc397-8f43-50e8-a87c-dbece1ff19dd'}, {'abstract': 'It is heartening that after six weeks of silence and spirited discussion, American nuns are pushing back against the Vatican’s unjustified attack on their fidelity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/opinion/when-in-rome-speak-up-for-reality.html', 'snippet': 'It is heartening that after six weeks of silence and spirited discussion, American nuns are pushing back against the Vatican’s unjustified attack on their fidelity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The nation’s Roman Catholic nuns are pushing back against the Vatican’s unjustified attack on their fidelity. The president and the executive director of the Leadership Conference of Women Religious, which represents about 80 percent of the nation’s 57,000 nuns, intend to go to Rome and fully rebut the accusations that the group has “serious doctrinal problems” and a tendency toward “radical feminist themes.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When in Rome, Speak Up for Reality', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When in Rome, Speak Up for Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuns', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leadership Conference of Women Religious', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T01:05:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd809bf8-c34b-5e84-911b-565bfce4161e', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd809bf8-c34b-5e84-911b-565bfce4161e'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Beals, whose youthful voice resulted from a childhood glandular problem, made a long career of playing children and childlike characters on television shows and commercials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/arts/television/dick-beals-85-who-gave-a-voice-to-gumby-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Beals, whose youthful voice resulted from a childhood glandular problem, made a long career of playing children and childlike char