 '_id': 'nyt://article/20320ac6-bae4-52ec-bb47-105c945ceec9', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20320ac6-bae4-52ec-bb47-105c945ceec9'}, {'abstract': 'A book explores the history of the skyline from an engineer’s perspective, and another looks at the story behind the Statue of Liberty.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/nyregion/books-about-the-building-trade-and-the-statue-of-liberty.html', 'snippet': 'A book explores the history of the skyline from an engineer’s perspective, and another looks at the story behind the Statue of Liberty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAMUEL C. FLORMAN’S memoir of life in the construction trade opens with a bang. He recalls overhearing an argument between a contractor working on a six-story apartment building in the Bronx and a city inspector threatening to shut down the job because of a missing permit. Mr. Florman writes: “Suddenly the shouting stopped, and very quietly the inspector said, ‘O.K.’ Pause. ‘It’ll cost you a hundred bucks.’\xa0” ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03BOOK1/03BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/nyregion/03BOOK1/03BOOK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Different Angle on Building in New York', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Different Angle on Building in New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Florman, 