www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/world/europe/turkey-charges-pianist-fazil-say-over-twitter-posts.html', 'snippet': 'Fazil Say, who has said he is an atheist and has criticized Turkey’s pro-Islamic government, is accused of “publicly insulting religious values.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — A court here on Friday charged Fazil Say, a classical and jazz pianist with an international career, with insulting Islamic values in Twitter messages, the latest in a series of legal actions against Turkish artists, writers and intellectuals for statements they have made about religion and Turkish national identity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/Turkey/Turkey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 712, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/Turkey/Turkey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/Turkey/Turkey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/02/world/Turkey/Turkey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/Turkey/Turkey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkish Pianist Is Accused of Insulting Islam', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkish Pianist Is Accused of Insulting Islam', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Say, Fazil', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T02:28:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu and Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ae82f87-eaee-5ea9-9a50-b6bb21413e6f', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ae82f87-eaee-5ea9-9a50-b6bb21413e6f'}, {'abstract': 'Defenseman Marek Zidlicky came to the Devils in a February trade with the Minnesota Wild, making them more consistent and bolstering the power play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/sports/hockey/2012-stanley-cup-marek-zidlicky-has-filled-gap-for-devils-defense.html', 'snippet': 'Defenseman Marek Zidlicky came to the Devils in a February trade with the Minnesota Wild, making them more consistent and bolstering the power play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Marek Zidlicky, the defenseman who seemed to make the Devils complete, says he is finally planning to move into his own place after living for two weeks with Patrik Elias, a fellow Czech, and then in a hotel for almost three months.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Devils Filled Defensive Gap With Zidlicky, and a Hole in His Résumé, Too', 'kicker': 'Stanley Cup Finals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Devils Filled Defensive Gap With Zidlicky, and a Hole in His Résumé, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zidlicky, Marek', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T02:29:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed030d76-ce85-5f13-81cd-fd5324656e89', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed030d76-ce85-5f13-81cd-fd5324656e89'}, {'abstract': 'Share your thoughts on a major moment in the Mets’ 51-season history.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/01/johan-santana-throws-the-mets-first-no-hitter-discuss/', 'snippet': 'Share your thoughts on a major moment in the Mets’ 51-season history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johan Santana threw the first no-hitter in Mets history on Friday night, testing the limits of fate, his pitch count and his surgically repaired shoulder to beat the Cardinals, 8-0. On a night when fans at Citi Field were forced to look back to a quintessentially Mets moment, Santana sent them home with an unforgettable one. Now that it’s over, share your thoughts, your fears as his pitch count rose, and your reaction in the comments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Johan Santana Throws the Mets’ First No-Hitter. Discuss.', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santana, Johan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T02:38:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d29cd4fd-a173-59df-9c2b-399ad7fcbcdc', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d29cd4fd-a173-59df-9c2b-399ad7fcbcdc'}, {'abstract': 'After a string of close calls in their 51-season history, Johan Santana finally finished the job in the Mets’ 8,020nd game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/sports/baseball/in-mets-51st-year-finally-their-first-no-hitter.html', 'snippet': 'After a string of close calls in their 51-season history, Johan Santana finally finished the job in the Mets’ 8,020nd game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 8,019 games, across 51 seasons, it had never happened for the Mets. Not at the Polo Grounds, not at Shea Stadium, not at Citi Field, not on the road. Not for Ryan or Seaver, not for Koosman or Matlack, not for Gooden or Cone, not for Leiter or Glavine. No Mets pitcher had ever thrown a no-hitter. Not until Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/s