ls are saying: It’s O.K. to be a little bit corrupt, when others are so much more corrupt than you.The unusual self-defense by some public servants – corruption is unequivocally a crime in China – is featuring more and more in Chinese media reports, sparking wide debate in a country where the prime minister says corruption is so bad it could one day “terminate” Communist Party rule (see this report by Bloomberg Business News.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/02corruption/02corruption-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/02corruption/02corruption-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1550, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/02corruption/02corruption-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/02/world/02corruption/02corruption-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/world/02corruption/02corruption-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Deciphering the Hidden Rules That Tempt China’s Officials', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T06:22:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf5a3424-eabf-5f87-abc4-f11f21628545', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf5a3424-eabf-5f87-abc4-f11f21628545'}, {'abstract': 'A regional round-up of news from across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/newswallah-bharat-edition-42/', 'snippet': 'A regional round-up of news from across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: Indian cricket team captain Mahendra Singh Dhoni will visit the Baramulla district in north Kashmir on Sunday to cheer for a match in the Kashmir Premier League, or KPL, Kashmir’s own version of the Indian Premier League cricket tournament. The initiative was started by the Indian Army last year to promote cricket among youngsters in the conflict-ridden valley (Hindustan Times).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Andhra Pradesh (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karnataka (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rajasthan (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uttar Pradesh State (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T08:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19057102-db4a-552e-a7af-6209ca8d5185', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19057102-db4a-552e-a7af-6209ca8d5185'}, {'abstract': 'Stable prices are killing us.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/catastrophic-credibility/', 'snippet': 'Stable prices are killing us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little while ago Ben Bernanke responded to suggestions that the Fed needed to do more — in particular, that it should raise the inflation target — by insisting that this would undermine the institution’s “hard-won credibility”. May I say that what recent events in Europe, and to some extent in the US, really suggest is that central banks have too much credibility? Or more accurately, their credibility as inflation-haters is very clear, while their willingness to tolerate even as much inflation as they say they want, let alone take some risks with inflation to rescue the real economy, is very much in doubt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catastrophic Credibility', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T08:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bce98bb3-13cc-5fde-a67c-4e3247958a71', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bce98bb3-13cc-5fde-a67c-4e3247958a71'}, {'abstract': 'An recent queer film festival in the city featured 120 movies from 30 countries and had 7,000 people in attendance.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/mumbai-showcases-gay-and-transgender-films/', 'snippet': 'An recent queer film festival in the city featured 120 movies from 30 countries and had 7,000 people in attendance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A frustrated petitioner arguing her own case before the judge blasts the state for its atrocities and double standards. As the audience in the courtroom erupts into a roar and loud applause, so does the audience sitting in one of the theaters at Cinemax, a popular multiplex in Andheri, Mumbai’s entertainment district.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mumbai Showcases Gay and Transgender Films', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mehta, Deepa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roshan, Hrithik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cinemax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shiv Sena', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T09:04:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mayank Shekhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mayank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shekhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e4ee1f2-1835-59ba-9e7f-9da11648a392', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e4ee1f2-1835-59ba-9e7f-9da11648a392'}, {'abstract': 'Yada yada again.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/my-head-talks-tomorrow/', 'snippet': 'Yada yada again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On ABC’s This Week with George Stephanopoulos, from New York. I assume it will go something like this: ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 