n': 'Aid Workers Who Were Held in Cave Are Rescued From Taliban', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aid Workers Held in Cave Are Rescued From Taliban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hostages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rescues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medair', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnston, Helen', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oirere, Moragwe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T10:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin and John F. Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2f0652b-4ff4-5afd-a73a-db617508d0ee', 'word_count': 602, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2f0652b-4ff4-5afd-a73a-db617508d0ee'}, {'abstract': 'On a recent trip back to the United States, I received a sober reminder of the saddest side of America, in an unexpectedly cheery cover.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/real-life-hunger-games-in-america/', 'snippet': 'On a recent trip back to the United States, I received a sober reminder of the saddest side of America, in an unexpectedly cheery cover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Back in The New York Times newsroom on a recent trip to New York, I came across some children’s literature. The slim pamphlets, in bright colors and featuring beloved cartoon characters, were about subjects like teeth brushing and healthy eating, and I immediately thought I had to pick them up for my kids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/blogs/sesame-st-hunger-books-rdv/sesame-st-hunger-books-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/02/blogs/sesame-st-hunger-books-rdv/sesame-st-hunger-books-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Real-life Hunger Games in America', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Welfare (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eating Well', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T11:00:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcus Mabry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mabry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8feb3ba-efff-5dee-8b22-55ece08dc11e', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8feb3ba-efff-5dee-8b22-55ece08dc11e'}, {'abstract': 'It almost did not happen: Manager Terry Collins had tried to persuade Josh Thole to play one more minor league rehab game.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/a-giddy-catcher-retraces-a-special-night/', 'snippet': 'It almost did not happen: Manager Terry Collins had tried to persuade Josh Thole to play one more minor league rehab game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Josh Thole almost did not get to run to the mound and hug Johan Santana on Friday night, his first night back from the disabled list since May 7, when he sustained a concussion. Never mind how difficult it was for the battery mates Santana and Thole to keep the St. Louis Cardinals guessing and hitless all night, it almost did not happen: Manager Terry Collins had nearly persuaded Thole to play one more minor league rehab game.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Giddy Catcher Retraces a Special Night', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thole, Josh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T13:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0435a944-3f80-59f1-84a7-0407b0e84071', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0435a944-3f80-59f1-84a7-0407b0e84071'}, {'abstract': 'Bailing out America’s Costa del Sol.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/florida-versus-spain/', 'snippet': 'Bailing out America’s Costa del Sol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mainly as a note to myself: What was once Peter Kenen’s big insight about optimum currency areas is now a commonplace: They’re much more likely to be workable if you have fiscal federalism, so that ther