and the foundation creating the National September 11 Memorial Museum have virtually stopped construction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/arts/design/sept-11-memorial-museum-construction-is-frozen-over-financing.html', 'snippet': 'Disagreements between the Port Authority and the foundation creating the National September 11 Memorial Museum have virtually stopped construction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than six months, work on the National September 11 Memorial Museum has been at a virtual standstill because of a multimillion-dollar dispute between the foundation creating it and the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, which is responsible for the construction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Construction Frozen in a Fight Over Financing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Construction Frozen in a Fight Over Financing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National September 11 Memorial and Museum', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building (Construction)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T17:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbdccabc-b20a-5762-ac69-f334ba98757f', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbdccabc-b20a-5762-ac69-f334ba98757f'}, {'abstract': 'After a month of floundering, Elizabeth Warren, the embattled Senate candidate in Massachusetts, gained the Democratic endorsement, avoiding a primary fight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/us/politics/elizabeth-warren-seeks-to-revive-senate-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'After a month of floundering, Elizabeth Warren, the embattled Senate candidate in Massachusetts, gained the Democratic endorsement, avoiding a primary fight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SPRINGFIELD, Mass. — In a display of political muscle, Elizabeth Warren overwhelmingly won the state Democratic Party’s endorsement on Saturday for the United States Senate seat held by Scott P. Brown, a Republican. With the size of her victory, she avoided a party primary in September.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/03massachusetts-span/03massachusetts-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/us/03massachusetts-span/03massachusetts-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 355}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/03massachusetts-span/03massachusetts-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/03massachusetts-span/03massachusetts-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/03massachusetts-span/03massachusetts-span-thumbStandard.jpg