rests in European soccer teams: James in Liverpool and Garnett in A.S. Roma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 30, 1984, Liverpool beat A.S. Roma in a penalty shootout at the Stadio Olimpico in Rome to capture the European Cup, the precursor to soccer’s prestigious Champions League. At the time, Kevin Garnett was an 8-year-old in South Carolina and LeBron James had not been born. But when the same two soccer clubs meet July 28 at Fenway Park as part of their United States summer tours, James and Garnett are likely to be there as minority owners, James for Liverpool and Garnett for Roma.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Rivals May Someday Vie on Distant Field', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Liverpool (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roma (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T18:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Appleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef7c1ca6-917e-5e87-b0fd-8ff8f7bd5024', 'word_count': 830, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef7c1ca6-917e-5e87-b0fd-8ff8f7bd5024'}, {'abstract': 'A kid-judged contest produces a winning explanation of the nature of a flame.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/winning-entry-in-what-is-a-flame-contest/', 'snippet': 'A kid-judged contest produces a winning explanation of the nature of a flame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently wrote about the “Flame Challenge,” a contest organized by the Center for Communicating Science at Stony Brook University. In the competition, more than 800 contestants sought to answer — in everything from poetry to animation — the question, “What is a flame?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Entry in ‘What is a Flame’ Contest', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemistry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALDA, ALAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York at Stony Brook', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T18:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a95795e-b994-53e3-8ffe-f784fc619155', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a95795e-b994-53e3-8ffe-f784fc619155'}, {'abstract': 'The link between obesity and poverty is close and complicated, as leaders in one city learned when they tried to make high-calorie beverages more expensive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/us/richmond-calif-seeks-to-tax-sweetened-beverages.html', 'snippet': 'The link between obesity and poverty is close and complicated, as leaders in one city learned when they tried to make high-calorie beverages more expensive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RICHMOND, Calif. — The California good life — the one of endless varieties of lettuce and tasting rooms nestled in vineyards — does not extend to Richmond’s Iron Triangle, a neighborhood named for the railroad tracks that delineate its borders and historically one of the neediest communities in the Bay Area.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/SODA-2/SODA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/us/SODA-2/SODA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/SODA-2/SODA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/SODA-2/SODA-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan to Tax Soda Gets a Mixed Reception', 'kicker': 'Richmond Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan to Tax Soda Gets a Mixed Reception', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Richmond (Calif)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beverages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T18:11:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Leigh Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2364daae-d6dc-5037-b76b-b904ca206edc', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2364daae-d6dc-5037-b76b-b904ca206edc'}, {'abstract': 'With six killings last week, the number of homicides in just five months in Seattle reached 21, as many as in all of last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/us/wave-of-gun-violence-challenges-seattles-notion-of-security.html', 'snippet': 'With six killings last week, the number of homicides in just five months in Seattle reached 21, as many as in all of last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — The worst surge of gun violence in years, culminating last week in six deaths over the course of an otherwise unremarkable Wednesday morning-into-afternoon, has deeply stressed this city, where many neighborhoods normally feel as safe as living rooms. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/JP-POLICE-2/JP-POLICE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/us/JP-POLICE-2/JP-POLICE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1445, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '