r global panic, they could serve another purpose: to remind investors that the domestic stock market may be the best choice among a tough set of options. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Stock Market Still Looks the Best of a Bad Lot', 'kicker': 'Fundamentally', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Even Now, the U.S. Market Looks the Best of a Bad Lot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T19:44:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul J. Lim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Lim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/605caf57-2e27-5ea3-9ae8-86052ef5c1f8', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/605caf57-2e27-5ea3-9ae8-86052ef5c1f8'}, {'abstract': 'An accelerated program of infrastructure projects, which people in both political parties agree are needed, has potential benefits beyond reducing unemployment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/business/road-repairs-can-end-political-gridlock-economic-view.html', 'snippet': 'An accelerated program of infrastructure projects, which people in both political parties agree are needed, has potential benefits beyond reducing unemployment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEMOCRATS and Republicans share less common ground than at any point in living memory, and they are especially divided about our still-ailing economy. When Democrats propose additional economic stimulus, Republicans call for more cuts in government spending and regulation. And even though the effects of the Great Recession are still with us, political gridlock seems set to continue.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03-VIEW/03-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03-VIEW/03-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1581, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03-VIEW/03-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03-VIEW/03-VIEW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03-VIEW/03-VIEW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Repairing Roads Can End All Kinds of Gridlock', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Repairing Roads Can End All Kinds Of Gridlock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'},