airstrike has increased demand on Afghanistan’s sketchy infrastructure everywhere, and on one tunnel in particular.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALANG PASS, Afghanistan — Nowhere is the impact of Pakistan’s ban on NATO truck traffic more visible than here at the top of the Hindu Kush, on one of the only alternative overland routes for supply convoys to reach Kabul and the rest of the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S.-Pakistan Freeze Chokes Fallback Route in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S.-Pakistan Dispute Chokes an Afghan Supply Route', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delays (Transportation)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:39:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da772c8c-adc8-5892-8293-ea383900dabe', 'word_count': 1053, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da772c8c-adc8-5892-8293-ea383900dabe'}, {'abstract': 'With the European championships starting on Friday, Italy is enmeshed in yet another match-fixing scandal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/sports/soccer/stain-of-scandal-again-taints-italian-soccer.html', 'snippet': 'With the European championships starting on Friday, Italy is enmeshed in yet another match-fixing scandal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soccer in Italy is not unlike driving. Laws are treated merely as suggestions.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YLONGMAN/YLONGMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 570, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YLONGMAN/YLONGMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1140, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YLONGMAN/YLONGMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YLONGMAN/YLONGMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YLONGMAN/YLONGMAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stain of Scandal Again Taints Italian Soccer', 'kicker': 'On Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stain of Scandal Again Taints Italian Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:41:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e3cab49-f8a5-5685-8749-3387c7178f5d', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e3cab49-f8a5-5685-8749-3387c7178f5d'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Williams, the songwriter of “Evergreen,” “We’ve Only Just Begun” and “Rainbow Connection,” talks about a new documentary on his life, the ups and downs of his career and, of course, his long affiliation with the Muppets.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/the-good-guys-and-bad-guys-that-ive-been-paul-williams-on-paul-williams-still-alive/', 'snippet': 'Paul Williams, the songwriter of “Evergreen,” “We’ve Only Just Begun” and “Rainbow Connection,” talks about a new documentary on his life, the ups and downs of his career and, of course, his long affiliation with the Muppets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’d think the life of Paul Williams would provide more than enough material for a documentary: he’s the vintage-1970s songwriter whose work includes “We’ve Only Just Begun,” “Evergreen” (which won him an Academy Award) and “Rainbow Connection” (which didn’t).\xa0 He’s a star of cult films like “Phantom of the Paradise” and “Smokey and the Bandit.” And after badly derailing his career with drug and alcohol abuse, he is now proudly 22 years sober.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Good Guys and Bad Guys That I’ve Been: Paul Williams on ‘Paul Williams Still Alive’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kessler, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Paul (1940- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:43:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8f24748-d721-5024-837a-fd6b17bb11f1', 'word_count': 1716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8f24748-d721-5024-837a-fd6b17bb11f1'}, {'abstract': 'Dread of death, not love of sex, is why the dead keep rising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/opinion/sunday/abraham-lincoln-vampire-hunter.html', 'snippet': 'Dread of death, not love of sex, is why the dead keep rising.', 'lead_paragraph': '“ABRAHAM LINCOLN WAS A WOMAN!” In 2002, a cover story in The Weekly World News reported that a cache of Mathew Brady daguerreotypes of “Babe-raham Lincoln” had been found in the basement of the White House, and hidden among the president’s effects at the Smithsonian was a telltale box of sanitary napkins. Lincoln, it was disclosed, had married a man (“Take a look at a photo of Mary Todd Lincoln and you’ll be convinced”) and given birth to six children. All this, however, is ho-hum compared with the revelations in the coming film “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter,” in which our 16th president is, basically, Buffy in a stovepipe hat.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sunday-review/03LEPORE/03LEPORE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/sunday-review/03LEPORE/03LEPORE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sunday-review/03LEPORE/03LEPORE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sunday-review/03LEPORE/03LEPORE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sunday-review/03LEPORE/03LEPORE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/sunday-review/03LEPORE/03LEPORE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 