reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The horse racing industry should be deeply shamed that extraordinary security measures had to be ordered to guard horses in next Saturday’s Belmont Stakes from the doping abuses engulfing thoroughbred racing. The horses will be kept in an isolated barn with visitors limited, feed and hay bales checked for drugs, and veterinarians and trainers under daily watch to ensure there is no manipulation of food or medication. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s at Stake in the Belmont', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s at Stake in the Belmont', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Steroids', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Racing Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "I'll Have Another (Race Horse)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:46:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d5caa2b-ea08-5846-9b26-c64a5e0dfc26', 'word_count': 373, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d5caa2b-ea08-5846-9b26-c64a5e0dfc26'}, {'abstract': 'The new farm bill, like its predecessors, rewards big farmers of row crops who don’t need help and ignores small ones who do. It also threatens the environment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/opinion/sunday/where-the-trough-is-overflowing.html', 'snippet': 'The new farm bill, like its predecessors, rewards big farmers of row crops who don’t need help and ignores small ones who do. It also threatens the environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every five years or so, Congress promises a new, improved farm bill that will end unnecessary subsidies to big farmers, enhance the environment and actually do something to help small farmers and small towns. But what it usually does is find ways of disguising the old inequities, sending taxpayers dollars to wealthy farmers, accelerating the expansion of industrial farming, inflating land prices and further depopulating rural America.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Trough Is Overflowing', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Deconstruction', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where the Trough Is Overflowing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crop Controls and Subsidies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:46:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert B. Semple Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5313e357-848e-5623-af47-ec09f056d32b', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5313e357-848e-5623-af47-ec09f056d32b'}, {'abstract': 'An appeals court ruled that a federal law excluding same-sex couples from benefits is unconstitutional. But this is unlikely to be the final word.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/opinion/sunday/in-defense-of-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'An appeals court ruled that a federal law excluding same-sex couples from benefits is unconstitutional. But this is unlikely to be the final word.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal appeals court ruling last week that struck down part of the Defense of Marriage Act did not say whether same-sex couples have a constitutional right to marry, but the decision sets the stage for what will almost certainly be a Supreme Court showdown over the unfair treatment of gay people and their families.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Defense of Marriage', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Defense of Marriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2a34fe5-57bc-5596-a096-92ccf28eb516', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2a34fe5-57bc-5596-a096-92ccf28eb516'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of local providers, and even some insurers, are finding ways to improve the American health care system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/opinion/sunday/treating-you-better-for-less.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of local providers, and even some insurers, are finding ways to improve the American health care system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is some good news about the overly costly, underperforming American health care system. A growing number of hospitals, doctors, employers and health insurers are finding ways to reduce the cost of delivering medical care while maintaining or improving quality. If enough providers adopt their already proven techniques, this grass-roots movement could transform the entire system in ways that will benefit all Americans.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Treating You Better for Less', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treating You Better for Less', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virginia Mason Medical Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Premier Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T20:46:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed44bd38-5940-5a96-b7f3-2c1bd7d8eee2', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed44bd38-5940-5a96-b7f3-2c1bd7d8eee2'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney and the Republican base have turned away from their party’s environmental legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/opinion/sunday/friedman-g-reen-op.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney and the Republican base have turned away from their party’s environmental legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MITT ROMNEY certainly has his weaknesses as a candidate, but his biggest challenge in attracting independent swing voters will be overcoming a well-earned reputation for saying whatever the Republican base wants to hear. Having watched him in the primaries, you have to wonder whether there is any issue in which he would turn to the far-right in his party and say: “I’m sorry. You have this wrong. Here’s the hard truth. ...”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', '