, so little outrage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reader Comments on my Nuba Mountains Column', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-02T22:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e269564c-db72-5d66-bb82-5050534fa49b', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e269564c-db72-5d66-bb82-5050534fa49b'}, {'abstract': 'In 2008, major countries managed to come together on a coordinated course that averted a global depression. They seem unwilling to cooperate again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/business/in-economic-deluge-a-world-thats-unable-to-bail-together.html', 'snippet': 'In 2008, major countries managed to come together on a coordinated course that averted a global depression. They seem unwilling to cooperate again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than four years ago, with the world’s financial system in danger of collapsing, major countries managed to come together on a coordinated course that averted a global depression. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03norris-sf-span/03norris-sf-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/business/03norris-sf-span/03norris-sf-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'superJ