al.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/the-wars-of-carl-schurz/', 'snippet': 'How a German revolutionary became a Civil War general.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early months of 1862, Carl Schurz took leave of his post as ambassador to Spain to make a daring step he had been contemplating for months: he wanted a commission in the Army. In a face-to-face meeting with Abraham Lincoln in March, the 33-year-old German immigrant explained that he found the luxurious life of a diplomat “intolerable” while his adopted nation “was fighting for its life.” Lincoln acquiesced, though not without pointing out that Schurz was giving up prestige, comfort, and a “large salary” for a position that paid “little” and would bring “plenty of work,” “discomfort,” and “danger.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wars of Carl Schurz', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schurz, Carl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T01:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andre M. Fleche', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andre', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ce15ab8-aebf-5200-ad46-e0c4101d11d3', 'word_count': 1258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ce15ab8-aebf-5200-ad46-e0c4101d11d3'}, {'abstract': 'Hugo Chavez, the Venezuelan president and a huge baseball fan, left a phone message for fellow Venezuelan Johan Santana after his no-hitter.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/02/venezuelan-president-chavez-sends-congratulatory-wishes-to-santana/', 'snippet': 'Hugo Chavez, the Venezuelan president and a huge baseball fan, left a phone message for fellow Venezuelan Johan Santana after his no-hitter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the people who reached out to congratulate Johan Santana, the Venezuelan left-hander who had just thrown a the first no-hitter in Mets history Friday night, was Hugo Chavez, the Venezuelan president who is a huge baseball fan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chavez, the Venezuelan President, Sends Congratulatory Wishes to Santana', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santana, Johan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T01:33:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c13c208a-9bff-554d-92e6-894e04dc8170', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c13c208a-9bff-554d-92e6-894e04dc8170'}, {'abstract': 'Seeking his first PGA Tour victory, Spencer Levin shot a three-under 69 to move into the lead at the Memorial Tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/sports/golf/spencer-levin-takes-lead-at-memorial.html', 'snippet': 'Seeking his first PGA Tour victory, Spencer Levin shot a three-under 69 to move into the lead at the Memorial Tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN, Ohio — As soon as Spencer Levin struck the putt, he started walking, a sure sign he had misread the line. Levin played his first six holes on Saturday in four under par to take the third-round lead at the Memorial Tournament. But as his par putt rolled toward the hole on the par-3 eighth, Levin was certain he was staring at his second straight bogey. He believed it right up until the ball caught the edge of the hole, rimmed around and, much to his disbelief, dropped. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Between Cigarette Breaks, Player Seeking First Win Takes Lead at Memorial', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Between Cigarette Breaks, Player Seeking First Win Takes Lead at Memorial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levin, Spencer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T01:37:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34fd2439-85d8-5599-8154-d9ef31450165', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34fd2439-85d8-5599-8154-d9ef31450165'}, {'abstract': 'International and American track stars used the Prefontaine Classic in Eugene, Ore., as a proving ground for their Olympic aspirations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/sports/olympics/prefontaine-serves-as-a-tuneup-for-olympic-contenders.html', 'snippet': 'International and American track stars used the Prefontaine Classic in Eugene, Ore., as a proving ground for their Olympic aspirations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — It’s called the Prefontaine Classic, or “the Pre,” but for many Olympic hopefuls, “Pre” doubled as shorthand for preview of their competition leading into the United States track trials, which will take place here at the end of the month.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 539, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1078, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/03/sports/YTRACK/YTRACK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Olympic Contenders, the Prefontaine Serves as a Tuneup and as a Barometer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Olympic Contenders, the Prefontaine Serves as a Tuneup and as a Barometer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Felix, Allyson', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Xiang', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montsho, Amantle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Sanya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pistorius, Oscar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T01:54:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faa73fe8-0cf2-50ae-9164-3a9e06a99b04', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faa73fe8-0cf2-50ae-9164-3a9e06a99b04'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Freeman, a reliever with the Cardinals, made his major league debut on Friday night as Johan Santana was in the midst of a no-hitter for the Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/sports/baseball/cardinals-freeman-reflects-on-debut-in-mets-no-hitter.html', 'snippet': 'Sam Freeman, a reliever with the Cardinals, made his major league debut on Friday night as Johan Santana was in the midst of a no-hitter for the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sam Freeman warmed up the way he always had, taking his time. He has always been a creature of habit, he said Saturday, the day after he made his major league debut with the St. Louis Cardinals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Cardinals Pitcher, It’s Also a Night of Firsts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, '