north of India,” Andrea Thompson writes  in The Sunday Book Review section of The New York Times, Anuradha Roy “describes the crystalline beauty of the peaks in winter, viewed long after the haze of the summer months and the fog of the monsoon, held in secret for those who choose to brave the cold.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Quietly Mesmerizing’ Novel Set in the Himalayas', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roy, Anuradha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Himalayas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hyderabad (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T06:16:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6f7857c-c60f-5f50-9cb9-eca33a1a3772', 'word_count': 196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6f7857c-c60f-5f50-9cb9-eca33a1a3772'}, {'abstract': 'Horsemen and horse welfare advocates need to work together toward their common goals.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/common-goals-need-a-united-approach/', 'snippet': 'Horsemen and horse welfare advocates need to work together toward their common goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been more than a year since I published my first, and last, book, “Greatness and Goodness: Barbaro and His Legacy.” The entire experience has been life-altering, including managing the Web site that provided daily updates on Barbaro; researching the book, which included a two-year stint working for the trainer Steve Asmussen; writing the book; and selling it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedi