ng tech companies in 2012 is still a male game, and so is funding them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawsuit Shakes Man’s World of Tech', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T15:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b93b262-f528-5bae-9607-1404f179da9e', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b93b262-f528-5bae-9607-1404f179da9e'}, {'abstract': 'Adjustable drivers can help golfers, but some teachers said that instruction was still necessary and that the clubs could be overwhelming for some people.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/adjustable-drivers-fix-some-problems-while-posing-others/', 'snippet': 'Adjustable drivers can help golfers, but some teachers said that instruction was still necessary and that the clubs could be overwhelming for some people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the market flooded with adjustable drivers, I wondered if these new tools were affecting golf instruction. Are people no longer asking their pros to fix their driver swings because all their problems are fixable by opening or closing the face with a click of a wrench or by moving some weights in the club head?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Adjustable Drivers Fix Some Problems While Posing Others', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T15:35:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/440583e4-b9f6-5691-9ae8-83a6d8f7b136', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/440583e4-b9f6-5691-9ae8-83a6d8f7b136'}, {'abstract': 'Victoria Azarenka, the top-ranked women’s player, fell Sunday to Dominika Cibulkova, who had twice been on the verge of knocking out Azarenka’s defenses in the past two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/sports/tennis/04iht-tennis04.html', 'snippet': 'Victoria Azarenka, the top-ranked women’s player, fell Sunday to Dominika Cibulkova, who had twice been on the verge of knocking out Azarenka’s defenses in the past two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The weather changed at the French Open, and the top of the tennis pyramid shook.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/04tennis-pic1/04tennis-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/04tennis-pic1/04tennis-pic1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/04tennis-pic1/04tennis-pic1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/04tennis-pic1/04tennis-pic1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/s