ct': 'The Australian opera and musical-theater singer Anthony Warlow will make his Broadway debut as the billionaire industrialist Daddy Warbucks in the coming revival of “Annie.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/a-daddy-for-annie/', 'snippet': 'The Australian opera and musical-theater singer Anthony Warlow will make his Broadway debut as the billionaire industrialist Daddy Warbucks in the coming revival of “Annie.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway-bound “Annie” has found its Daddy. The Australian opera and musical-theater singer Anthony Warlow will make his Broadway debut as the billionaire industrialist Daddy Warbucks in the coming revival of the 1977 musical, the show’s producers announced on Sunday. Mr. Warlow will star opposite the previously announced cast members Katie Finneran as Miss Hannigan and Lilla Crawford as Annie.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Daddy for ‘Annie’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T19:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Piepenburg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Piepenburg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/311f169a-adf4-5892-bfc5-23cc79f65e81', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/311f169a-adf4-5892-bfc5-23cc79f65e81'}, {'abstract': 'Yankees center fielder Curtis Granderson used Saturday night’s ejections of the hitting coach Kevin Long and Manager Joe Girardi by the plate umpire Bob Davidson to call for greater accountability for umpires.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/granderson-calls-for-more-accountability-for-umpires/', 'snippet': 'Yankees center fielder Curtis Granderson used Saturday night’s ejections of the hitting coach Kevin Long and Manager Joe Girardi by the plate umpire Bob Davidson to call for greater accountability for umpires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — Yankees center fielder Curtis Granderson used Saturday night’s ejections of the hitting coach Kevin Long and Manager Joe Girardi by the plate umpire Bob Davidson to call for greater accountability for umpires.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Granderson Calls for More Accountability for Umpires', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Officiating (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granderson, Curtis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Long, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T19:16:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74691074-9622-5332-9b6f-2957f8953c19', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74691074-9622-5332-9b6f-2957f8953c19'}, {'abstract': 'Not an increasing role.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/the-level-of-government-spending/', 'snippet': 'Not an increasing role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A quick note on what has happened to the level of government spending since the economic crisis began.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Level of Government Spending', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T19:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/157235ff-7a66-5a15-8229-73ca2ca9e257', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/157235ff-7a66-5a15-8229-73ca2ca9e257'}, {'abstract': 'Philip Glass, visiting Charleston to attend a festival performance of his opera “Kepler,” takes part in a public interview and is coaxed to the piano to play a bit of “Hydrogen Jukebox,” another work with a Spoleto connection.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/03/philip-glass-at-spoleto-usa-as-speaker-and-spectator-also-performs/', 'snippet': 'Philip Glass, visiting Charleston to attend a festival performance of his opera “Kepler,” takes part in a public interview and is coaxed to the piano to play a bit of “Hydrogen Jukebox,” another work with a Spoleto connection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLESTON, S.C. — Philip Glass was not at the first performances of “Kepler,” his opera about the German mathematician and astronomer that opened here at the Spoleto Festival USA on May 26. But he flew in for the closing performance of the run, on Saturday. And while he was in town, he sat for an hourlong public interview and an impromptu performance at the Dock Street Theater on Saturday afternoon, as part of the festival’s “Music in Time” series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Philip Glass, at Spoleto USA as Speaker and Spectator, Also Performs', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spoleto Festival USA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ginsberg, Allen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glass, Philip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T19:31:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fceb8972-7eed-5d81-a3cf-a7de6ea2aa07', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fceb8972-7eed-5d81-a3cf-a7de6ea2aa07'}, {'abstract': 'Julian Wachner led the Trinity Choir beyond its Wall Street neighborhood to perform a program of contemporary works at Zankel Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/arts/music/julian-wachners-trinity-choir-at-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Julian Wachner led the Trinity Choir beyond its Wall Street neighborhood to perform a program of contemporary works at Zankel Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the conductor and composer Julian Wachner became the director of music and arts at Trinity Wall Street in September 2010 he has pursued at least two distinct agendas. He has increased the amount of contemporary music performed by the church’s admirable Trinity Choir, bolstering that move by inaugurating a new instrumental ensemble, Novus NY. He has also taken steps to make the choir more visible outside its native habitat of Lower Manhattan, like mounting one of its cherished annual performances of Handel’s “Messiah” at Alice Tully Hall last year.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/TRINITY/TRINITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/TRINITY/TRINITY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/TRINITY/TRINITY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/TRINITY/TRINITY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1149, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Forces of Nature and Ecstasy', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Forces Of Nature And Ecstasy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wachner, Julian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Choir (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T19:47:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/21bc22bb-1234-5efe-ad35-4a9b1a1031bc', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21bc22bb-1234-5efe-ad35-4a9b1a1031bc'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Zvi Gotheiner appropriated the dabke, a traditional Middle Eastern line dance, and gave it a modern interpretation in a world premiere in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/arts/dance/zvidance-in-dabke-and-coupling-at-new-york-live-arts.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Zvi Gotheiner appropriated the dabke, a traditional Middle Eastern line dance, and gave it a modern interpretation in a world premiere in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dabke is a line dance of the Levant. At weddings in Jordan, Lebanon and Syria, people link up arm to shoulder or hand in hand and stomp out rhythms and patterns. Israelis, so often at odds with their neighbors, also have a version. Dances are easier to share than territory. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/ZVIDANCE/ZVIDANCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/ZVIDANCE/ZVIDANCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1655, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/ZVIDANCE/ZVIDANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/ZVIDANCE/ZVIDANCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/arts/ZVIDANCE/ZVIDANCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Line Dance Charged With Meaning', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': 