 was wanted in the subway nerve-gas attack that killed 13 commuters and sickened 5,000 more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/world/asia/japan-arrests-fugitive-from-1995-subway-gas-attack.html', 'snippet': 'The police arrested Naoko Kikuchi, a former cult member who was wanted in the subway nerve-gas attack that killed 13 commuters and sickened 5,000 more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The police on Sunday arrested one of the two remaining fugitive suspects from the doomsday cult behind the 1995 nerve-gas attack on the Tokyo subway, Japanese media reported.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Arrests Fugitive Wanted in 1995 Gas Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Arrests Fugitive Wanted In 1995 Tokyo Nerve Gas Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biological and Chemical Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kikuchi, Naoko', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fugitives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aum Shinrikyo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T20:01:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd65b6c5-c57c-53f9-984c-073432536a2f', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd65b6c5-c57c-53f9-984c-073432536a2f'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Bradley’s first competitive match as Egypt’s coach, a World Cup qualifier, was played behind closed doors after a series of tragic events befell soccer after the country’s revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/sports/soccer/for-bob-bradley-and-egypt-a-higher-purpose-after-violence.html', 'snippet': 'Bob Bradley’s first competitive match as Egypt’s coach, a World Cup qualifier, was played behind closed doors after a series of tragic events befell soccer after the country’s revolution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALEXANDRIA, Egypt — Bob Bradley stood at attention as a full military band played the anthem of his adoptive country. In front of him, Egypt’s national soccer team, which he began managing about nine months ago, was lined up on the field at the 80,000-capacity Borg el Arab military stadium, the players singing proudly.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/soccer/04bradley/04bradley-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/soccer/04bradley/04bradley-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/soccer/04bradley/04bradley-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/soccer/04bradley/04bradley-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/sports/soccer/04bradley/04bradley-thumbStandard.jpg',