None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b98440e0-6e03-5f9f-92b7-cc45aa04298d', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b98440e0-6e03-5f9f-92b7-cc45aa04298d'}, {'abstract': 'The Italian designer Valentino Garavani will create costumes for three works by the New York City Ballet, to be performed for one night at its annual fall gala, the company is to announce on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/arts/dance/valentino-to-create-ballet-costumes.html', 'snippet': 'The Italian designer Valentino Garavani will create costumes for three works by the New York City Ballet, to be performed for one night at its annual fall gala, the company is to announce on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Italian designer Valentino Garavani will create costumes for three works by the New York City Ballet, to be performed for one night at its annual fall gala, the company is to announce on Monday. The gala, to be held at Lincoln Center on Sept. 20, will feature a new ballet set to selections from Tchaikovsky’s “Eugene Onegin” and a performance of George Balanchine’s “Rubies” as a tribute to the signature use of red by the designer simply known as Valentino, above. “There is so much beauty in the ballet, the grace, the fluidity,” Valentino said in a news release. He said he was honored to have City Ballet “celebrate my work in this way, and I am very passionate about the design of these very special costumes.” Benefit-priced tickets for the gala are available at (212) 870-5585. Tickets to the performance only go on sale Aug. 6 through (212) 496-0600 or nycballet.com.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valentino to Create Ballet Costumes', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Valentino to Create Ballet Costumes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garavani, Valentino', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T22:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c805558b-d44d-5e56-be68-1b0b009de526', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c805558b-d44d-5e56-be68-1b0b009de526'}, {'abstract': 'Carly Simon is joining the pack of musicians who have gone from writing and performing for the stage to telling all in memoirs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/books/carly-simon-to-share-her-life-story-in-book.html', 'snippet': 'Carly Simon is joining the pack of musicians who have gone from writing and performing for the stage to telling all in memoirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carly Simon is joining the pack of musicians who have gone from writing and performing for the stage to telling all in memoirs. Random House announced on Sunday that it would publish Ms. Simon’s autobiography — the story of her childhood, “the discovery of her life-altering stammer, her meteoric rise and unparalleled career in music, and her loves, including her marriage to James Taylor.” Ms. Simon, above, a daughter of Richard L. Simon, a founder of Simon & Schuster, said she had an early awareness of the publishing industry, writing in a diary even as a child. “After years of keeping journals and writing lyrics for my tunes, I have developed a strong interest in seeing how my life might just string together in a longer form,” she said in a statement. “I know I’ll be looking for a strong chorus, like a repeating dream or theme.” Ms. Simon told Reuters in a recent interview that she was busy writing her book and planned to finish it by year’s end. Susan Kamil, the publisher of Random House, said in an e-mail that Ms. Simon’s “prose on the page is powerful, evocative, narrative driven, and the stories she tells are riveting.” Random House has not announced a publication date.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Carly Simon to Share Her Life Story in Book', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carly Simon to Share Her Life Story in Book', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, Carly', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T22:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman and Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/397c690a-3538-59c5-b3fc-43c63dea9138', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/397c690a-3538-59c5-b3fc-43c63dea9138'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Dawkins, the evolutionary biologist, has moved to a new publisher for his next book, the story of his intellectual evolution and his work as an atheist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/books/a-new-publisher-for-richard-dawkins.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Dawkins, the evolutionary biologist, has moved to a new publisher for his next book, the story of his intellectual evolution and his work as an atheist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Dawkins, the evolutionary biologist, has moved to a new publisher for his next book, the story of his intellectual evolution and his work as an atheist. Ecco, an imprint of HarperCollins, said on Sunday that it had acquired the North American rights to Mr. Dawkins’s book, which is not yet titled. Daniel Halpern, the publisher of Ecco, said in a statement: “We couldn’t be more excited to be working with a thinker and writer as profound and influential as Richard Dawkins. It is truly an honor to have him at Ecco.” An Ecco spokesman said the book was tentatively scheduled for release in the fall of 2014.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Publisher for Richard Dawkins', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Publisher For Richard Dawkins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HarperCollins Publishers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dawkins, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-03T22:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman and Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'org