tps://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/climate-change-threatens-power-output-study-says/', 'snippet': 'As rivers and lakes warm, plants are expected to fall short of the cooling water they need to generate power.', 'lead_paragraph': ' As the climate gets warmer, so do the rivers and lakes that power plants draw their cooling water from. And that is going to make it harder to generate electricity in decades to come, researchers report.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Climate Change Threatens Power Output, Study Says', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shortages', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electric Power Research Institute', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T11:24:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_