stract': 'A Nigerian airliner that crashed in Lagos, killing all 153 on board, was American-built, so the United States will be part of the investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/world/africa/engine-trouble-reported-in-nigerian-crash.html', 'snippet': 'A Nigerian airliner that crashed in Lagos, killing all 153 on board, was American-built, so the United States will be part of the investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAMAKO, Mali — Rescue workers sought to recover corpses and extinguish fires on Monday from a crowded neighborhood in Lagos, Nigeria, where an airliner plummeted from the sky and barreled into the side of a building the day before.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/world/04nigeria2_cnd/04nigeria2_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Engine Trouble Was Reported Before Nigerian Crash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Engine Trouble Was Reported Before Nigerian Crash', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lagos (Nigeria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T12:55:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter and Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8585cb5-cf58-5f65-a6e0-c227b7bcda74', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8585cb5-cf58-5f65-a6e0-c227b7bcda74'}, {'abstract': 'Chesapeake Energy, in an effort to quell an open revolt by shareholders angry about high executive compensation and poor corporate oversight, said it would replace four current board members with new outside directors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/business/chesapeake-agrees-to-new-board.html', 'snippet': 'Chesapeake Energy, in an effort to quell an open revolt by shareholders angry about high executive compensation and poor corporate oversight, said it would replace four current board members with new outside directors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HOUSTON — Chesapeake Energy and its beleaguered chief executive, Aubrey K. McClendon, executed another strategic retreat on Monday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/business/05chesapeake-chief/05chesapeake-chief-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chesapeake Agrees to Revamp Its Board', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chesapeake Agrees To Revamp Its Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chesapeake Energy Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boards of Directors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T12:59:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b7e24bd-c3fb-578c-8d84-eea235282cc5', 'word_count': 1205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b7e24bd-c3fb-578c-8d84-eea235282cc5'}, {'abstract': 'In “First Point,” his new short film, the artist Richard Phillips combines two of his current obsessions: surfing and Lindsay Lohan. Watch the trailer here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/lindsay-lohans-new-wave/', 'snippet': 'In “First Point,” his new short film, the artist Richard Phillips combines two of his current obsessions: surfing and Lindsay Lohan. Watch the trailer here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “First Point,” his new short film, the artist Richard Phillips combines two of his current obsessions: surfing and Lindsay Lohan. Phillips has worked with the actress and tabloid goddess before, on a 90-second video for Neville Wakefield’s “Commercial Break,” which had a very brief run during the 54th Venice Biennale. And his studio is lined with several larger-than-life paintings of Lohan that came directly out of that particular project. But don’t call Lohan his muse. Lohan, Phillips insists, is his collaborator as much as anyone in the stellar cast of people who worked on the film, including the legendary surf filmmaker Taylor Steele; the professional surfer Kassia Meador, who performs mesmerizingly as Lohan’s body double; the editor Jay Rabinowitz; and Thomas Bangalter, one half of the electro duo Daft Punk, who composed the ominously swelling score. As the trailer implies, “First Point” is at once a surf film and a film noir, an exploration of the California dream and the Hollywood nightmare, worlds that Lohan doesn’t have to pretend to straddle on screen. But no doubt the question on everyone’s lips when “First Point” has its premiere next week at Art Unlimited, the curated section of the Art Basel fair, will be: “Is it art?” And that is just fine by Phillips. “It’s just like in my paintings,” he says. “Because of the actor and the popular culture dimensions of the project, it will give people — especially people in the art world — a real sense of instability with regard to my intentions. Is it a film? Is it an art video? It refuses to announce itself as either.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lindsay Lohan’s New Wave', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surfing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lohan, Lindsay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Daft Punk', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T13:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f5f8baf-c0c0-5677-99d3-70395e38e5dd', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5f8baf-c0c0-5677-99d3-70395e38e5dd'}, {'abstract': '“Spartacus: War of the Damned” is set to make its debut in January and will follow the conclusive confrontation between the armies of Spartacus and the Roman general Marcus Crassus.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/starz-announces-final-season-of-spartacus/', 'snippet': '“Spartacus: War of the Damned” is set to make its debut in January and will follow the conclusive confrontation between the armies of Spartacus and the Roman general Marcus Crassus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Historical accounts suggest that the rebellious gladiator Spartacus met his demise in 71 B.C. after his uprising against the Roman republic was defeated. But on cable television, “Spartacus” is coming to an end in 2013: on Monday, the Starz cable channel is expected to announce that the epic action series’s coming season, set to make its debut in January, will be its last.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Starz Announces Final Season of ‘Spartacus’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglas, Kirk', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kubrick, Stanley', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIntyre, Liam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitfield, Andy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T13:01:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2bd73f0-4f91-5e63-97b0-c77a0da43b95', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2bd73f0-4f91-5e63-97b0-c77a0da43b95'}, {'abstract': 'Big Data is moving up a classic modern curve, from discovery to science, and on to engineering and mass use. We are not as far along as a lot of people selling the boom would have you believe, but lots of good businesses are being built that will make a revolution.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/how-big-data-gets-real/', 'snippet': 'Big Data is moving up a classic modern curve, from discovery to science, and on to engineering and mass use. We are not as far along as a lot of people selling the boom would have you believe, but lots of good businesses are being built that will ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The business of Big Data, which involves collecting large amounts of data and then searching it for patterns and new revelations, is the result of cheap storage, abundant sensors and new software. It has become a multibillion-dollar industry in less than a decade. Growing at speed like that, it is easy to miss how much remains to do before the industry has proven standards. Until then, lots of customers are probably wasting much of their money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/technology/04bits-wind/04bits-wind-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/technology/04bits-wind/04bits-wind-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 264, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Big Data Gets Real', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amazon Mechanical Turk', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ClearStory Data', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cloudera', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Factual Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T13:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/434ed08a-eaab-514e-85af-604bd521f778', 'word_count': 799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434ed08a-eaab-514e-85af-604bd521f778'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: New York and its region seem to be in the midst of an apology crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/in-the-news-apologies-all-around/', 'snippet': 'The Day: New York and its region seem to be in the midst of an apology crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': ' This may be a good moment to examine the sorry state of New York and its region. We seem mired in something of an apology crisis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the News, Apologies All Around', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T13:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e132cde-d95a-59ba-9b2f-5b04f7780c1b', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e132cde-d95a-59ba-9b2f-5b04f7780c1b'}, {'abstract': 'Also, sales of the Sunday edition of Rupert Murdoch’s Sun tabloid have yet to match The News of the World’s circulation figures; and Anthony Bourdain moves to CNN.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/the-breakfast-meeting-less-than-daily-newspapers-and-richard-dawsons-kisses/', 'snippet': 'Also, sales of the Sunday edition of Rupert Murdoch’s Sun tabloid have yet to match The News of the World’s circulation figures; and Anthony Bourdain moves to CNN.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The decision to publish The Times-Picayune of New Orleans three times a week, which was quickly echoed by three sister newspapers in Alabama, represents a gamble that other newspapers may feel impelled to take. The idea is to cut costs, guide readers to the newspaper’s Web site for daily news coverage and preserve some print advertising, which remains far more lucrative than digital ads, Christine Haughney reports. There is a danger, she writes:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Less-Than-Daily Newspapers, and Richard Dawson’s Kisses', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T13:15:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}]