h': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' Teaching or Cheating?  Notes From the Tutoring Front Lines', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT SEIDMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SEIDMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b7bfdfd-f442-5c97-9e79-e1a30e96b4fd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b7bfdfd-f442-5c97-9e79-e1a30e96b4fd'}, {'abstract': 'Can you solve the puzzle of the 100 lockers?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/numberplay-100-lockers/', 'snippet': 'Can you solve the puzzle of the 100 lockers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our puzzle this week was suggested by Numberplay participant Volodymyr Ivanchenko, who says the puzzle is fairly easy if taken at the right pace. “Most people move too fast with this one and try to skip steps. That’s where you get into trouble. Just take it a piece at a time and you’ll soon discover the remarkable answer.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: 100 Lockers', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/38b8c077-bef9-533e-bacc-0c237ab46da9', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/38b8c077-bef9-533e-bacc-0c237ab46da9'}, {'abstract': 'In an era of grueling baseline duels, tennis players are adapting — setting up antidotes to would-be poisons and buying back time with fresh ideas, even new shots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/sports/tennis/05iht-shot05.html', 'snippet': 'In an era of grueling baseline duels, tennis players are adapting — setting up antidotes to would-be poisons and buying back time with fresh ideas, even new shots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Tennis is about technique, power, speed, brains, nerves and endurance. It is also about time management, and time is becoming more precious in an era of bigger, stronger, fitter athletes pounding the ball with new-age rackets and new-age strings.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/tennis/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/tennis/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/tennis/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/tennis/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer/05iht-tennis05-roger-federer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1305, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur