an who was arrested after confronting Vice President Dick Cheney in 2006.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Monday unanimously ruled against a protester who said his free speech rights had been violated when Secret Service agents arrested him after he made critical remarks about the Bush administration’s war policies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/us/sub-2-SCOTUS/sub-2-SCOTUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/us/sub-2-SCOTUS/sub-2-SCOTUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1301, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Protester Spurned in Bid To Sue the Secret Service', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protester Spurned in Bid To Sue the Secret Service', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howards, Steven', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Secret Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Dick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:04:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81d910b9-9f12-5cab-a5ab-ea49b223b72f', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81d910b9-9f12-5cab-a5ab-ea49b223b72f'}, {'abstract': 'Rehman Malik, a close aide of the president, said that he had surrendered his British nationality, but that he could not provide the necessary proof on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/world/asia/pakistani-court-suspends-rehman-malik-over-dual-nationality-claim.html', 'snippet': 'Rehman Malik, a close aide of the president, said that he had surrendered his British nationality, but that he could not provide the necessary proof on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — The Supreme Court on Monday suspended the interior minister after he failed to provide proof that he had surrendered his British passport. The order was part of a wider court investigation into lawmakers who hold dual nationality with Western countries, including the United States. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistani Court Bars Interior Minister Over Dual-Nationality Claim', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistani Court Suspends Interior Minister Over Dual-Nationality Claim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malik, Rehman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:12:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood and Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qu