 about an agreement two weeks ago may have been premature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The top United Nations nuclear official announced new talks with Iran on Monday aimed at gaining access to restricted sites, and he expressed concern about satellite images taken last month that showed the Iranians had demolished buildings at one site that inspectors have been especially pressing to visit.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Nuclear Chief Announces New Talks With Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Nuclear Chief Announces New Talks With Iran Over Access to Sites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amano, Yukiya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Tests', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:27:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/427d0e4f-ebeb-5158-a155-3165713d310f', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/427d0e4f-ebeb-5158-a155-3165713d310f'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Sharapova battled her own nerves and a surprisingly difficult opponent, Klara Zakopalova of the Czech Republic, before winning in three sets to reach the French Open quarterfinals.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/sharapova-battles-nerves-but-outlasts-zakopalova/', 'snippet': 'Maria Sharapova battled her own nerves and a surprisingly difficult opponent, Klara Zakopalova of the Czech Republic, before winning in three sets to reach the French Open quarterfinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Shrugging off a series of double faults and unforced errors at key moments, Maria Sharapova defeated unseeded Klara Zakopalova of the Czech Republic, 6-4, 6-7 (5), 6-2, to gain the quarterfinals of the French Open.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharapova Battles Nerves, but Outlasts Zakopalova', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b65760c5-0659-5b8f-828e-52d6cc28d980', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b65760c5-0659-5b8f-828e-52d6cc28d980'}, {'abstract': 'Adam & Eve, London, an independent agency opened in 2008, was acquired by DDB Worldwide, part of the Omnicom Group, which will merge the agency with DDB United Kingdom, London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/business/media/accounts-and-people-of-note-in-the-advertising-industry.html', 'snippet': 'Adam & Eve, London, an independent agency opened in 2008, was acquired by DDB Worldwide, part of the Omnicom Group, which will merge the agency with DDB United Kingdom, London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam & Eve, London, an independent agency opened in 2008, was acquired by DDB Worldwide, part of the Omnicom Group, which will merge the agency with DDB United Kingdom, London, to create Adam & Eve/DDB. Financial terms were not disclosed; the Web site of the British trade publication Campaign estimated the cost of the deal at $92.5 million. James Murphy, a founder of Adam & Eve, becomes chief executive at Adam & Eve/DDB, and Stephen Woodford, chief executive at DDB United Kingdom, becomes chairman at Adam & Eve/DDB. The deal echoed one in 1989 when DDB bought Boase Massimi Pollitt, an independent London agency opened in 1968, and merged it with the DDB London office to form BMP DDB; that name lasted until 2004. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Webdenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T16:32:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9364d6dd-8de8-5c77-be99-f3935c138193', 'word_count': 1389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9364d6dd-8de8-5c77-be99-f3935c138193'}, {'abstract': "The most recent advertisement from the Obama campaign attacks Mitt Romney's tenure as governor of Massachusetts. ", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001585706/weve-heard-it-all