nd-their-favorite-religious-fiction/', 'snippet': 'On Twitter, readers responded to a call for their favorite novels or short stories with religious themes and settings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times staffers and contributors recently shared some of their favorite novels with religious themes, and we put the call out on Twitter for readers to play along using the tag #religiousfiction. Below is a selection from the many responses we received. Special mention goes to Gregory Wolfe, who came up with 16 thoughtful recommendations (by my count), two of which are below. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Readers Recommend Their Favorite Religious Fiction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Godwin, Gail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T17:28:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e134dcb-7417-52b6-8acf-3da64d091485', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e134dcb-7417-52b6-8acf-3da64d091485'}, {'abstract': 'A member of an Afghanistan anticorruption task force tours a rural community, where disputes are resolved the same way they were in the 20th century.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/settling-afghan-disputes-where-custom-holds-sway/', 'snippet': 'A member of an Afghanistan anticorruption task force tours a rural community, where disputes are resolved the same way they were in the 20th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the Chinook helicopter, I saw villages dotting valleys and hugging small brown streams. Every house in Shah Wali Kot district was constructed of mud, until more modern structures emerged on the approach to Kandahar Airfield. Rugged hills and steep passes divided villages. The challenge to Afghanistan’s stability appeared self-evident: How can the state project justice where it can’t reach?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Settling Afghan Disputes, Where Custom Holds Sway', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T17:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Bookman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bookman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4cf0681c-b39a-5c46-ad9e-a21898c8690a', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4cf0681c-b39a-5c46-ad9e-a21898c8690a'}, {'abstract': 'A new campaign seeks recruits for New York State’s volunteer fire departments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/business/media/ads-seek-to-light-a-match-under-would-be-volunteers.html', 'snippet': 'A new campaign seeks recruits for New York State’s volunteer fire departments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The next time a cop asks, “O.K., buddy, where’s the fire?” the answer ought to be, according to a new campaign, “Why, within me, officer.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/business/media/04adnewslettter/04adnewslettter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/04/business/media/04adnewslettter/04adnewslettter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 60