n our Facebook page, or tweet @thecaucus using the hashtag #asknyt. The Times’s Monica Davey and Jeff Zeleny will be answering readers’ questions here on Tuesday and some of your questions may be answered in Tuesday’s special edition of TimesCast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Questions About the Wisconsin Recall', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T17:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f59ce49d-7437-5422-a262-bb255e075305', 'word_count': 92, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f59ce49d-7437-5422-a262-bb255e075305'}, {'abstract': 'How a chance meeting under the High Line led to an adventure on the streets of New York and a poem that “was meant to be.”', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/from-a-familiar-stranger-a-poem-written-on-the-stars/', 'snippet': 'How a chance meeting under the High Line led to an adventure on the streets of New York and a poem that “was meant to be.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'I went for a walk the other night. Someone said it was supposed to rain, but the skies looked clear to me. I headed up Eighth Avenue, crossed over at 23rd Street and at 10th Avenue saw a stairwell going up and took it. I was on the High Line. That much I’d expected. What I had not anticipated was how crowded it would be, like being stuck on a moving sidewalk at an airport. But the night was too nice to begrudge anyone anything, particularly a chance to experience beauty. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From a Familiar Stranger, a Poem Written on the Stars', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venus (Planet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T17:42:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Hayes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hayes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81671cf8-8d56-51e7-bd3a-cb3397a1bb0d', 'word_count': 1230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81671cf8-8d56-51e7-bd3a-cb3397a1bb0d'}, {'abstract': 'Wil S. Hylton, a contributing writer, answers questions about the scientist Craig Venter’s desire for “tons of money, a fancy house” and the ability to save the world.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/behind-the-story-wil-s-hylton-on-craig-venter-and-god-craig-venter-and-dna-graffiti-and-craig-venter-and-piles-of-cash/', 'snippet': 'Wil S. Hylton, a contributing writer, answers questions about the scientist Craig Venter’s desire for “tons of money, a fancy house” and the ability to save the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wil S. Hylton, a contributing writer for the magazine, profiled\xa0the scientist Craig Venter\xa0for this week’s Innovation issue. He last wrote for the magazine about\xa0the state of U.S. biodefense preparations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Story: Wil S. Hylton on Craig Venter and God, Craig Venter and DNA Graffiti and Craig Venter and Piles of Cash', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker