omething to gain.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/in-gupta-case-motive-matters/', 'snippet': 'The government does not have to prove motive for most crimes. But for insider trading cases, the government is required to show that a tipper had something to gain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the prosecution of Rajat Gupta moves into what looks to be its final week, the crucial question for the jury is coming into focus: Why would a wealthy, well-respected business leader reveal confidential corporate information to a hedge fund trader like Raj Rajaratnam?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Gupta Case, Motive Matters', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T18:15:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7c975f1-72cf-5e0a-ad44-de73889b4709', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7c975f1-72cf-5e0a-ad44-de73889b4709'}, {'abstract': 'The Sun began publishing on Sunday, taking the place of The News of the World, which was closed amid the phone-hacking scandal. I', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001585887/the-sun-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'The Sun began publishing on Sunday, taking the place of The News of the World, which was closed amid the phone-hacking scandal. I', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Sun began publishing on Sunday, taking the place of The News of the World, which was closed amid the phone-hacking scandal. I', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/business/video-chozick-sun/video-chozick-sun-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/04/business/video-chozick-sun/video-chozick-sun-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/business/video-chozick-sun/video-chozick-sun-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/04/business/video-chozick-sun/video-chozick-sun-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sun on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T18:16:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'noam cohen', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/7f7a4c06-6fe1-51f8-a441-521833e5b22b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/7f7a4c06-6fe1-51f8-a441-521833e5b22b'}, {'abstract': 'The prestigious artists’ retreat the MacDowell Gallery has awarded the photographer its Edwin MacDowell Medal.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/nan-goldin-given-lifetime-achievement-award/', 'snippet': 'The prestigious artists’ retreat the MacDowell Gallery has awarded the photographer its Edwin MacDowell Medal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The MacDowell Colony, the prestigious artists’ retreat in New Hampshire, has awarded the photographer Nan Goldin its Edwin MacDowell Medal for lifetime achievement in the arts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nan Goldin Given Lifetime Achievement Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldin, Nan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MacDowell Colony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marks, Matthew, Gallery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T18:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8940736d-1964-5451-9cf4-8c3567f9c391', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8940736d-1964-5451-9cf4-8c3567f9c391'}, {'abstract': 'As seen from an Upper East Side balcony, two thick bands of color arc across the sky.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/video-double-rainbow-all-the-way-from-bronx-to-brooklyn/', 'snippet': 'As seen from an Upper East Side balcony, two thick bands of color arc across the sky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times reporter Alan Schwarz snapped the neat video above of Sunday’s double rainbow shortly before 6 p.m. from a 22nd-floor balcony on East 90th Street. From the Bronx at one end to Brooklyn on the other, it’s all in there. No orgiastic voice-over, but it sure is beautiful. Enjoy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Double Rainbow All the Way (From Bronx to Brooklyn)', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T18:19:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1e90c59-b5da-513b-9948-1328949ce445', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1e90c59-b5da-513b-9948-1328949ce445'}, {'abstract': 'A new museum in TriBeCa occupies an abandoned freight elevator.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/is-this-new-yorks-smallest-museum/', 'snippet': 'A new museum in TriBeCa occupies an abandoned freight elevator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Residents of TriBeCa can be forgiven for overlooking the neighborhood’s newest museum, which is built into an abandoned freight elevator and accessible only down a dark alleyway. Simply called Museum, this tiny room officially opened on Cortlandt Alley late last month after a ribbon-cutting ceremony presided over by one Rudolph W. Guliani, a celebrity impostor of the former mayor, Rudolph W. Giuliani. “We wanted a real politician,” said Josh Safdie, one of Museum’s founders, who contacted several local officials before hiring Guliani, a fairly convincing look-alike. “To us, this is about introducing a new institution to the city.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Is this New York’s Smallest Museum?', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T18:23:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09ede013-1cdd-5d81-b9db-04bbb05dd3e5', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09ede013-1cdd-5d81-b9db-04bbb05dd3e5'}, {'abstract': 'Professor Huxley shared the 1963 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine for a breakthrough discovery that helped better understand the electrical stimulation of nerve cells.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/us/andrew-huxley-nobel-winning-physiologist-dies-at-94.html', 'snippet': 'Professor Huxley shared the 1963 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine for a breakthrough discovery that helped better understand the electrical stimulation of nerve cells.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sir Andrew Huxley, a British scientist from an illustrious family whose boyhood mechanical skills led to a career in physiology — “the mechanical engineering of living things,” he called it — and a Nobel Prize for explaining the electrical basis of bodily movement, died on Wednesday. He was 94.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/huxley2/huxley2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/huxley2/huxley2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1595, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/huxley2/huxley2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/huxley2/huxley2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/sports/huxley2/huxley2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Andrew Huxley, Nobel-Winning Physiologist, Dies at 94', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Andrew Huxley, Nobel-Winning Physiologist, Dies at 94', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huxley, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANATOMY AND PHYSIOLOGY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T18:25:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Gellene', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gellene', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecff6202-2d82-5c5f-a1e9-9103796f4b35', 'word_count': 1068, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecff6202-2d82-5c5f-a1e9-9103796f4b35'}, {'abstract': 'Taking another look at Richard Dawson, whose master-of-disguises role on “Hogan’s Heroes” probably made viewers do a double-take when “Family Feud” came on the scene.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/the-many-masks-of-richard-dawson/', 'snippet': 'Taking another look at Richard Dawson, whose master-of-disguises role on “Hogan’s Heroes” probably made viewers do a double-take when “Family Feud” came on the scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Richard Dawson first turned up as host of “Family Feud” in 1976, some people might well have done a double-take. “What is this?” they might have asked. “An actor disguised as a game show host?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Many Masks of Richard Dawson', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'maj