s on the lawn. So sunny, we moved our chairs under the shade of a tree. My husband, my children and I had flown to Washington, D.C., from Los Angeles as my son Ethan Harari is a proud member of the G.W. graduating class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'L.A. P.O.V. | Brian Williams, Walter Cronkite and ‘Girls’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T20:02:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Ephron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ephron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/945e9ebe-97fb-55ce-a35f-523b80132a35', 'word_count': 1285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/945e9ebe-97fb-55ce-a35f-523b80132a35'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama campaign suggests that it is in a better position than at this time in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/new-obama-video-seeks-to-combat-negative-perceptions/', 'snippet': 'The Obama campaign suggests that it is in a better position than at this time in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a challenging week capped by a lackluster jobs report, the Obama campaign released a new Web video Monday that aimed to reassure supporters and asked them not to “lose focus” on the campaign’s “grass-roots organizing efforts.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Obama Video Seeks to Combat Negative Perceptions', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Messina, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'val