ow than decades ago, but self-identified Democrats and Republicans are.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/poll-shows-polarization-limited-to-parties/', 'snippet': 'Americans may not be any more polarized now than decades ago, but self-identified Democrats and Republicans are.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans of different races are no more polarized in their political views than they were 25 years ago. Men and women are no more polarized either. The same goes for people of different education levels, different income groups and different levels of religiosity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poll Shows Polarization Limited to Parties', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kohut, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-04T21:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c41aa5bd-9760-5d11-a280-78809319a0e2', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c41aa5bd-9760-5d11-a280-78809319a0e2'}, {'abstract': 'Dillon Gee gave up three runs in seven innings, but it was nothing like the pitching in the Mets’ three previous games, when the Ca