one Park had hoped a $4 billion convention center and casino would bring jobs to their working-class neighborhood, but state talks with the developer broke down last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/nyregion/in-ozone-park-queens-frustration-at-loss-of-planned-convention-center.html', 'snippet': 'Residents of Ozone Park had hoped a $4 billion convention center and casino would bring jobs to their working-class neighborhood, but state talks with the developer broke down last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ozone Park, a spare, working-class neighborhood in southwestern Queens, has long had a reputation as a place people pass through to get somewhere else. Most visitors are heading to or coming from Kennedy International Airport. Recently, hopes were raised of continuing to transform this neglected area into a destination in its own right by building a convention center and casino: a $4 billion project that promised the area money, jobs and a more central spot in New York’s tourist literature. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dashed Hopes in Queens as Convention Plan Falters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dashed Hopes in Queens As Convention Plan Falters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genting Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ozone Park (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:31:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ccf1e07-a19b-5639-88a1-7bb101d74879', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ccf1e07-a19b-5639-88a1-7bb101d74879'}, {'abstract': 'Sabirhan Hasanoff, formerly of Brooklyn, had helped Al Qaeda since at least November 2007, when he accepted $50,000 from an unidentified co-conspirator, prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/nyregion/sabirhan-hasanoff-pleads-guilty-to-qaeda-support.html', 'snippet': 'Sabirhan Hasanoff, formerly of Brooklyn, had helped Al Qaeda since at least November 2007, when he accepted $50,000 from an unidentified co-conspirator, prosecutors said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former Brooklyn resident pleaded guilty in Federal District Court in Manhattan on Monday to providing material support to Al Qaeda.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guilty Plea to Giving Aid to Al Qaeda Since 2007', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Brooklyn Man Pleads Guilty to Giving Aid to Al Qaeda Since 2007', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hasanoff, Sabirhan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'El-Hanafi, Wesam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Kimba M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:44:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22d9f802-59e5-5f86-88a4-33dc01c810b1', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22d9f802-59e5-5f86-88a4-33dc01c810b1'}, {'abstract': 'A report issued last month by the Environmental Protection Agency suggests that the risks of large-scale mining in the intricate Alaskan ecosystem are too high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/opinion/a-threat-to-bristol-bay.html', 'snippet': 'A report issued last month by the Environmental Protection Agency suggests that the risks of large-scale mining in the intricate Alaskan ecosystem are too high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The possibility that a giant gold-and-copper mine might someday be built near the headwaters that feed Bristol Bay in Alaska, one of the richest salmon fisheries in the world, is cause for alarm. A new report from the Environmental Protection Agency reinforces those fears. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Threat to Bristol Bay', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Threat to Bristol Bay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bristol Bay (Alaska)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copper, Brass and Bronze', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:46:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c460449-0cce-5831-907b-01a92009e4ff', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c460449-0cce-5831-907b-01a92009e4ff'}, {'abstract': 'A militia temporarily shut down Tripoli’s airport in the latest instance of the interim government’s inability to rein in armed groups that emerged in the uprising that ultimately toppled Libya’s dictator, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/armed-group-briefly-seizes-tripoli-airport/', 'snippet': 'A militia temporarily shut down Tripoli’s airport in the latest instance of the interim government’s inability to rein in armed groups that emerged in the uprising that ultimately toppled Libya’s dictator, Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Members of an armed militia briefly shut down Tripoli’s international airport on Monday, swarming the runway and exchanging fire with other armed groups in the latest affront to Libya’s weak interim authorities. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armed Group Briefly Seizes Tripoli Airport', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:47:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9647a0a-500c-5d90-8a6e-d576e42d2fce', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9647a0a-500c-5d90-8a6e-d576e42d2fce'}, {'abstract': 'More Americans than ever suffer from asthma, according to federal health officials. A lot more needs to be done to reduce the triggers and manage this disease.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/opinion/asthma-by-the-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'More Americans than ever suffer from asthma, according to federal health officials. A lot more needs to be done to reduce the triggers and manage this disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal health officials recently issued a gloomy report noting that the percentage of Americans suffering from asthma reached a record high of 8.4 percent in 2010, up from 7.3 percent in 2001. An estimated 25.7 million people had asthma in 2010, including 18.7 million adults and seven million children below the age of 18. It is a frightening disease in which sufferers struggle to breathe. In severe attacks, victims can die.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asthma by the Numbers', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Asthma by the Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asthma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:47:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/36c3c1df-db8d-5829-a41d-e9d115a3090e', 'word_count': 282, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36c3c1df-db8d-5829-a41d-e9d115a3090e'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth II’s achievement is her consistent commitment to multiracialism within the Commonwealth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/opinion/why-the-queen-matters.html', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth II’s achievement is her consistent commitment to multiracialism within the Commonwealth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Queen Matters', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why the Queen Matters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:49:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Watson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1567483c-9121-59d6-ae77-bf4b42800c1a', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1567483c-9121-59d6-ae77-bf4b42800c1a'}, {'abstract': 'The third week of the trial of Rajat K. Gupta, who has been charged with leaking corporate secrets about Goldman Sachs, began with the testimony of the bank’s chief executive.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/goldmans-chief-takes-the-stand-in-an-insider-trading-case/', 'snippet': 'The third week of the trial of Rajat K. Gupta, who has been charged with leaking corporate secrets about Goldman Sachs, began with the testimony of the bank’s chief executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For someone who has not practiced law in 30 years, Lloyd C. Blankfein has been spending quite of bit of time in the courtroom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Blankfein Takes the Stand in an Insider Trading Case', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}