tball/carmelo-anthony-says-hell-help-rebuild-the-knicks.html', 'snippet': 'Looking forward to a full training camp under Coach Mike Woodson, Carmelo Anthony on Monday offered to recruit players if the Knicks ask.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carmelo Anthony has had a few weeks to process the Knicks’ first-round postseason elimination at the hands of the Miami Heat. On Monday afternoon, he made a public appearance on behalf of USA Basketball and watched fans shoot free throws on a makeshift court adjacent to the Flatiron Building in Manhattan. Conditions were not optimal for the shooters, with an unseasonably low temperature, periodic gusts of wind, and cars whizzing by in the background.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Says He’ll Do His Part to Help Rebuild Knicks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anthony Says He’ll Do His Part to Help Rebuild Knicks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:53:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Appleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4acaa0f-0a24-51cf-8221-9b0f56d0274a', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4acaa0f-0a24-51cf-8221-9b0f56d0274a'}, {'abstract': 'Former President Bill Clinton, at a fund-raiser for President Obama on Monday, said having Mitt Romney in the White House would be “calamitous for our country and the world.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/clinton-takes-a-hard-jab-at-romney/', 'snippet': 'Former President Bill Clinton, at a fund-raiser for President Obama on Monday, said having Mitt Romney in the White House would be “calamitous for our country and the world.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former President Bill Clinton, days after lauding Mitt Romney for a “sterling business career” as a private investor, said on Monday that, as president, Mr. Romney “would be, in my opinion, calamitous for our country and the world.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Takes a Hard Jab at Romney', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:54:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44ba2bf8-e719-59be-b466-d260a5a16228', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44ba2bf8-e719-59be-b466-d260a5a16228'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s proposal to curb low-level marijuana arrests is a start, but, for the sake of fairness, the stop-and-frisk program must be reformed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/opinion/no-crime-real-punishment.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s proposal to curb low-level marijuana arrests is a start, but, for the sake of fairness, the stop-and-frisk program must be reformed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State decriminalized the possession of small amounts of marijuana in the late 1970s. But last year, in New York City, 50,000 people — the majority of them, young African-American or Hispanic men — were still arrested for possession because of overzealous policing and a weakness in the law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Crime, Real Punishment', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Crime, Real Punishment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T00:54:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba6aad10-3aee-5f35-97ce-86959d3b2a49', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba6aad10-3aee-5f35-97ce-86959d3b2a49'}, {'abstract': 'A look at the two women’s and two men’s singles matches at the French Open on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/04/preview-of-tuesdays-quarterfinal-matches/', 'snippet': 'A look at the two women’s and two men’s singles matches at the French Open on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at the two women’s and two men’s singles matches at the French Open on Tuesday. Players seeds are in parentheses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Preview of Tuesday’s Quarterfinal Matches', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ''