s the flourishing of harms a well-ordered society ought not permit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Harm in Free Speech', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T01:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Fish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e857ea9e-19c3-5111-9f82-d57e80b476c9', 'word_count': 1819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e857ea9e-19c3-5111-9f82-d57e80b476c9'}, {'abstract': 'The Toronto police on Monday arrested and charged a man with first-degree murder and six counts of attempted murder in connection with a shooting in a downtown Toronto shopping mall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/world/americas/canada-suspect-arrested-in-mall-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'The Toronto police on Monday arrested and charged a man with first-degree murder and six counts of attempted murder in connection with a shooting in a downtown Toronto shopping mall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Toronto police on Monday arrested a man and charged him with first-degree murder and six counts of attempted murder in connection with a shooting that set off a panic in a downtown Toronto shopping mall on Saturday evening. At a news conference, Detective Sgt. Brian Borg said that it appeared that the attack was a gang-related shooting and that the accused man, Christopher Husbands, 23, killed his intended target, Ahmed Hassan, 24. The six people who were wounded by the stray gunfire in the mall’s food court were bystanders. One, a 13-year-old boy who was visiting Toronto with his mother and sister, was in fair condition on Monday after surgery to repair 