'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costas, Bob', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T02:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84f2598e-6a6a-5a42-8db2-f7ca8acd4283', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84f2598e-6a6a-5a42-8db2-f7ca8acd4283'}, {'abstract': 'The influx has raised fears about the tech industry’s growing political clout and its spillover economic effects.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/us/san-francisco-tech-boom-brings-jobs-and-worries.html', 'snippet': 'The influx has raised fears about the tech industry’s growing political clout and its spillover economic effects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — When Twitter moves into its new headquarters in downtown San Francisco this month, it will occupy three floors of an 11-story 1937 Art Deco building that has sat shuttered for five years. Outside, its blue bird logo will replace the former main tenant’s sign, whose analog clocks remain frozen at 9:18, 4:33 and other times past.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/us/jp-Sanfrancisco-2/jp-Sanfrancisco-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/us/jp-Sanfrancisco-2/jp-Sanfrancisco-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit