use officials on Tuesday to announce an agreement to provide incoming students a “shopping sheet” of easy-to-understand terms for financial aid packages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/education/deal-reached-on-student-loans.html', 'snippet': 'College and university presidents will meet with White House officials on Tuesday to announce an agreement to provide incoming students a “shopping sheet” of easy-to-understand terms for financial aid packages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'College and university presidents representing more than one million students will meet with White House officials on Tuesday to announce an agreement to provide incoming students a “shopping sheet” of easy-to-understand terms for financial aid packages, beginning in the 2013-14 school year. The participants promised to clearly detail a student’s net cost after grants and scholarships are taken into account, and estimate the monthly payments a student would have to make after graduation to repay any federal loans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deal Reached on Student Loans', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Deal Reached On Student Loans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Aid (Education)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (Secondary)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T04:11:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': Non