. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1f956c5-71a4-5d57-91e3-d45c458c035b', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1f956c5-71a4-5d57-91e3-d45c458c035b'}, {'abstract': 'Two senior envoys of the Dalai Lama who negotiated with China in nine rounds of talks have resigned, according to the Tibetan government-in-exile in India.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/world/asia/tibet-negotiators-resign.html', 'snippet': 'Two senior envoys of the Dalai Lama who negotiated with China in nine rounds of talks have resigned, according to the Tibetan government-in-exile in India.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two senior envoys of the Dalai Lama who negotiated with China in nine rounds of talks have resigned, according to the Tibetan government-in-exile in India. The envoys, Lodi Gyari and Kelsang Gyaltsen, said in a statement that they were resigning because of the “deteriorating situation inside Tibet,” which, since 2009, has prompted 38 Tibetans to set themselves on fire. The envoys expressed disappointment over China’s rejection of a plan for “genuine autonomy” for Tibet put forward by the Dalai Lama in 2008, and they said current circumstances made substantive dialogue difficult. The last round of talks took place in 2010. The Tibetan exile government said a task force on talks would meet again in December, after China announces its new leadership in the fall, with the aim of renewing negotiations. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tibet: Negotiators Resign', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tibet: Negotiators Resign', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T04:27:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c491f77-32d3-520c-9392-855567adc6af', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c491f77-32d3-520c-9392-855567adc6af'}, {'abstract': 'The lawsuit is against El Salvador for blocking a gold mine, but is not in accordance with the Central America Free Trade Agreement, a World Bank panel ruled Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/world/americas/el-salvador-canadian-lawsuit-over-mine-allowed-to-proceed.html', 'snippet': 'The lawsuit is against El Salvador for blocking a gold mine, but is not in accordance with the Central America Free Trade Agreement, a World Bank panel ruled Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Canadian company’s lawsuit against El Salvador for blocking a gold mine can proceed under the country’s investment law but not under the provisions of the Central America Free Trade Agreement, a World Bank panel ruled Friday. In a case closely watched by environmentalists and the mining industry, the panel, the International Center for Settlement of Investment Disputes, will make a binding decision on whether El Salvador unfairly failed to license the mine proposed by the Pacific Rim Mining Corporation or had the sovereign right to reject it after the company already made investments. Environmentalists had hoped the panel would reject the case outright and slow the spread of mining in Central America. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'El Salvador: Canadian Lawsuit Over Mine Allowed to Proceed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'El Salvador: Canadian Lawsuit Over Mine Allowed to Proceed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Central American Free Trade Agreement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'El Salvador', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Rim Mining Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Treaties', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T04:31:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1246b900-dc56-585b-8fc7-0b4aaa725dc1', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1246b900-dc56-585b-8fc7-0b4aaa725dc1'}, {'abstract': 'His acclaimed film “Kshay” was made by a two man crew, working for four years.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/a-conversation-with-director-karan-gour/', 'snippet': 'His acclaimed film “Kshay” was made by a two man crew, working for four years.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Kshay (Corrode),” written and directed by Karan Gour, is a black-and-white independent feature based on a character’s single-minded obsession with an unfinished statue of the Hindu goddess Lakshmi. The film examines the idea of obsession through the Arvind and Chhaya, a middle-class Indian couple struggling to make ends meet when Chhaya becomes drawn to the statue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation with: Director Karan Gour', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Rupee (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Salman', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T04:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1579f24e-0bb6-5b66-971d-f8e706f0c71c', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1579f24e-0bb6-5b66-971d-f8e706f0c71c'}, {'abstract': 'A Syrian activist group reported that at least 80 soldiers were killedin clashes with rebels, which would be one of the largest losses for government forces since March 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/world/middleeast/syria-heavy-clashes-reported.html', 'snippet': 'A Syrian activist group reported that at least 80 soldiers were killedin clashes with rebels, which would be one of the largest losses for government forces since March 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Syrian activist group reported that at least 80 soldiers were killed over the weekend in clashes with rebels, which would be one of the largest losses for government forces since the uprising began in March 2011. The report, by the Syrian Observatory for Human Rights, could not be independently confirmed. The group also told Reuters that rebels had overrun army checkpoints in the northern town of Ariha, and a photo, right, released by activists was said to show damaged army tanks in the town. The reports cast further doubt on the viability of a truce plan arranged by Kofi Annan, an envoy of the United Nations and the Arab League. He plans to brief the United Nations Security Council this week and will also meet with Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton, who has said President Bashar al-Assad of Syria must resign as part of any solution to the conflict. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Heavy Clashes Reported', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Heavy Clashes Reported', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARAB LEAGUE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANNAN, KOFI', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T04:33:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5deb07aa-9508-5aa3-b72a-89dbafa4b8ee', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5deb07aa-9508-5aa3-b72a-89dbafa4b8ee'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Paar is remembered by many 1950s and ’60s television viewers as the cute, precocious girl whom her father, the late-night talk-show host Jack Paar, introduced to a national audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/arts/television/randy-paar-talk-show-hosts-daughter-and-guest-dies-at-63.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Paar is remembered by many 1950s and ’60s television viewers as the cute, precocious girl whom her father, the late-night talk-show host Jack Paar, introduced to a national audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Randy Paar, who is remembered by many 1950s and ’60s television viewers as the cute, precocious girl whom her father, the late-night talk-show host Jack Paar, introduced to a national audience in his monologues and home movies, died on Saturday after falling off a platform at Grand Central Terminal. A successful lawyer in Manhattan, she was 63.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/arts/PAAR-obit/PAAR-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/arts/PAAR-obit/PAAR-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1688, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype'