e replacement of the commander of United States Special Operations in South Korea after a news media report quoted him as saying that American and South Korean troops had been parachuting into North Korea on spy missions, a statement denied by Washington and the government in Seoul.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. General in South Korea to Be Replaced After Spy Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. General in South Korea Replaced After Spy Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tolley, Neil H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wendt, Eric P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Special Operations Command', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T05:34:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9918079f-0c00-5f6c-9c65-a20d3943171a', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9918079f-0c00-5f6c-9c65-a20d3943171a'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_