es.Soho House’s chief executive, Nick Jones, who founded the club in 1995, currently oversees 10 Soho Houses (six in Britain, three in the United States and one in Berlin).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soho House Expansion Plans Include Mumbai', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burkle, Ronald W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Nick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaPorte, Nicole', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Soho House', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'SoHo (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T08:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62d24336-c7a9-54ad-8cc0-d287f0a6e1a3', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62d24336-c7a9-54ad-8cc0-d287f0a6e1a3'}, {'abstract': 'A small number of independent stores have weathered the luxury blitz in Manhattan’s Greenwich Village. Were they lucky or good?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/magazine/can-mom-and-pop-shops-survive-extreme-gentrification.html', 'snippet': 'A small number of independent stores have weathered the luxury blitz in Manhattan’s Greenwich Village. Were they lucky or good?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was about 6, my dad and I were sitting near Wall Street when I asked him why so many men were wearing suits and ties. It was the 1970s, and we lived in Greenwich Village, a place where you could see men wearing almost anything except a suit and tie. My dad, a theater actor, told me that the people on Wall Street cared about money, and as a result, they had to dress formally. I even remember feeling bad for these poor chumps.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/10economy1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/10economy1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/mag-10economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/mag-10economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/10economy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/10economy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10economy1/10economy1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Mom-and-Pop Shops Survive Extreme Gentrification?', '