obably before — the chattering about the national implications will kick into overdrive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Wisconsin Means — and Doesn’t', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T12:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddb246b9-ad8a-5f5b-a8ad-2770ce51f831', 'word_count': 1286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddb246b9-ad8a-5f5b-a8ad-2770ce51f831'}, {'abstract': 'Louis J. Freeh, the trustee overseeing the bankruptcy of MF Global, estimates that creditors, including banks, big investors and service providers, could have more than $3 billion in claims against the failed brokerage.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/mf-global-trustee-estimates-3-billion-in-claims/', 'snippet': 'Louis J. Freeh, the trustee overseeing the bankruptcy of MF Global, estimates that creditors, including banks, big investors and service providers, could have more than $3 billion in claims against the failed brokerage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trustee overseeing the bankruptcy of MF Global estimates that creditors, including banks, big investors and service providers, could have more than $3 billion in claims against the failed company. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MF Global Trustee Says Claims May Exceed $3 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeh, Louis J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T12:34:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aae721ae-cccd-5ebc-8e8c-c09805c873bb', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aae721ae-cccd-5ebc-8e8c-c09805c873bb'}, {'abstract': 'Arvind Mahankali, a seventh grader at Junior High School 74 in Queens, has placed third in the National Spelling Bee two years in a row. On Monday, Schools Chancellor Dennis M. Walcott visited his school to congratulate him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/05/the-chancellor-pays-tribute-to-a-spelling-bee-finalist/', 'snippet': 'Arvind Mahankali, a seventh grader at Junior High School 74 in Queens, has placed third in the National Spelling Bee two years in a row. On Monday, Schools Chancellor Dennis M. Walcott visited his school to congratulate him.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Chancellor Pays Tribute to a Spelling Bee Finalist', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T12:50:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARIA NEWMAN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'NEWMAN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f625cb5a-5574-587c-b3d1-8dcb12acec66', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f625cb5a-5574-587c-b3d1-8dcb12acec66'}, {'abstract': 'Old people really do have a different smell, airport Wi-Fi may be free but you’ll be charged for higher speeds, colleges will use easy-to-read financial-aid offer forms and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/tuesday-reading-old-people-really-do-have-a-different-smell/', 'snippet': 'Old people really do have a different smell, airport Wi-Fi may be free but you’ll be charged for higher speeds, colleges will use easy-to-read financial-aid offer forms and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Old People Really Do Have a Different Smell', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T12:53:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d65ebff-a0be-5c69-b180-4efa669d6896', 'word_count': 118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d65ebff-a0be-5c69-b180-4efa669d6896'}, {'abstract': 'In Tuesday’s New York Times, Norimitsu Onishi reports on how tech start-ups are moving into San Francisco’s downtown, transforming a neighborhood that has defied development for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/daily-report-a-tech-boom-in-san-franciscos-urban-corepment/', 'snippet': 'In Tuesday’s New York Times, Norimitsu Onishi reports on how tech start-ups are moving into San Francisco’s downtown, transforming a neighborhood that has defied development for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Tuesday’s New York Times, Norimitsu Onishi reports on how tech start-ups are moving into San Francisco’s urban core, transforming a neighborhood that has defied development for decades. Among those making the move is Twitter, which next month will take over three floors of an 11-story 1937 Art Deco building that has sat shuttered for five years. Zynga, Yelp and other social media start-ups also have offices within the city. Meanwhile, workers at the big Silicon Valley companies, like Google and Apple, are becoming attracted to San Francisco’s urban charms, choosing to live in the city while commuting to the valley.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: A Tech Boom in San Francisco’s Urban Core', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T12:56:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75e954be-6565-5afd-8501-6b24a091f7b6', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75e954be-6565-5afd-8501-6b24a091f7b6'}, {'abstract': 'The replica throne is made not from molten steel but from hand-finished, hand-painted fiberglass and fireproof resin and weighs 350 pounds.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/in-game-of-thrones-you-win-or-you-buy-hbo-offering-30000-iron-throne-replicas/', 'snippet': 'The replica throne is made not from molten steel but from hand-finished, hand-painted fiberglass and fireproof resin and weighs 350 pounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One way to obtain the Iron Throne, the ceremonial seat of power in HBO’s “Game of Thrones” that has been made from the swords of hundreds of surrendered lords, is to defeat your rivals in battle and unite the Seven Kingdoms at the cost of thousands of lives and countless treasure. Or if you’re squeamish about the sight of blood and entrails but still have some extra treasure to spare, you could simply buy one for $30,000.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In ‘Game of Thrones,’ You Win or You Buy: HBO Offers $30,000 Iron Throne Replicas', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, George R R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/598a17cb-f56f-5719-b49f-9c773959ef43', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/598a17cb-f56f-5719-b49f-9c773959ef43'}, {'abstract': 'Let chess players use computers during championships: it’ll improve their game, their sense of their limitations and their understanding of the world.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/the-case-for-computers-at-top-chess-tournaments/', 'snippet': 'Let chess players use computers during championships: it’ll improve their game, their sense of their limitations and their understanding of the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — It was Game 8 of the World Chess Championship, and the four-time winner and defending champion, 42-year-old Viswanathan Anand of India, playing white, was a game down to the Israeli Boris Gelfand, 43. Gelfand, perhaps buoyed by his success in Game 7, had chosen an unexpectedly sharp line against Anand, who is renowned for his ability to calculate quickly on the board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chessmate', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:04:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hartosh Singh Bal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hartosh', 'middlename': 'Singh', 'lastname': 'Bal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33289f9f-fa12-5c5a-98ef-d1805efa13d1', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33289f9f-fa12-5c5a-98ef-d1805efa13d1'}, {'abstract': 'I’m against a proposal to make Israel’s Independence Day celebrations less dependent on the Hebrew calendar because it would make this state, well, a little less Jewish.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/making-independence-day-less-dependent-on-the-hebrew-calendar-would-threaten-israels-jewishness/', 'snippet': 'I’m against a proposal to make Israel’s Independence Day celebrations less dependent on the Hebrew calendar because it would make this state, well, a little less Jewish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — The Knesset member Lia Shemtov seems puzzled. Why would anyone oppose her bill proposing a commonsensical fix to an oddity in Israel’s holiday calendar? “Am I missing something?” the Ukrainian-born Israeli told me by phone on Thursday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Independence Days', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calendars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:17:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efc79728-9369-58ca-ab61-a0177b28d0e9', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efc79728-9369-58ca-ab61-a0177b28d0e9'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg has caught grief for his plan to limit serving sizes of sugary drinks and for the ever-growing number of New Yorkers who are stopped by the police.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/at-city-hall-not-seeing-moderation-in-all-things/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg has caught grief for his plan to limit serving sizes of sugary drinks and for the ever-growing number of New Yorkers who are stopped by the police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg would have done well to follow his own advice about food and apply it to policing: everything in moderation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At City Hall, Not Seeing Moderation in All Things', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:18:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/285d0a20-a92a-5821-92d8-c307f45f1af5', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/285d0a20-a92a-5821-92d8-c307f45f1af5'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity firm Thomas H. Lee Partners announced on Tuesday that it would buy a majority stake in the party goods retailer Party City in a deal valued at $2.69 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/thomas-h-lee-takes-majority-stake-in-party-city/', 'snippet': 'The private equity firm Thomas H. Lee Partners announced on Tuesday that it would buy a majority stake in the party goods retailer Party City in a deal valued at $2.69 billion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a private equity party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thomas H. Lee Takes Stake in Party City in $2.69 Billion Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:23:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e23c3701-0b92-50f7-90b6-a5bdbd1d7536', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e23c3701-0b92-50f7-90b6-a5bdbd1d7536'}, {'abstract': 'Apple will go in a different direction from Google Maps, and a D.J.’s comment makes for unhappy Nicki Minaj fans.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/the-breakfast-meeting-disneys-health-push-and-eerie-numbers-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Apple will go in a different direction from Google Maps, and a D.J.’s comment makes for unhappy Nicki Minaj fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a Washington news conference with the first lady, Michelle Obama, the Walt Disney Company on Tuesday plans to announce new nutritional standards for advertisers on its many child-focused outlets, including the Saturday morning cartoons on the ABC stations it owns. The standards would disqualify a wide range of candy, sugared cereal and fast food from advertising, Brooks Barnes writes. Also, Disney will reduce the amount of sodium by 25 percent in the children’s meals served at its theme parks, and create public service announcements to promote exercise and healthy eating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Disney’s Health Push, and Eerie Numbers in China', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:27:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f185ce-d0c0-5a3a-976d-6cd71003b20e', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f185ce-d0c0-5a3a-976d-6cd71003b20e'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles Kings are up, 3-0, and the Devils look lost in the Stanley Cup finals. The Thunder, however, seem to know exactly where they are going; they lead the Spurs, 3-2.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/sports/the-los-angeles-kings-rule-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles Kings are up, 3-0, and the Devils look lost in the Stanley Cup finals. The Thunder, however, seem to know exactly where they are going; they lead the Spurs, 3-2.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a season reaches its final series of the playoffs, with two teams having clawed themselves into position for their sport’s ultimate prize, it’s natural to hunker down and expect something epic. There are going to be ebbs and flows, big gaffes and jaw-dropping feats, swings of momentum that take fans from one extreme to the other. When it’s over, the winning team will celebrate in exhaustion and relief, having taken the opponent’s best shot and persevering.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1460, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/06leadingpic/06leadingpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kings Rule', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harden, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Casey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Driver, Donald', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westbrook, Russell', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Tony', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f1dca32-3551-5412-b997-8e19e1ec01ea', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f1dca32-3551-5412-b997-8e19e1ec01ea'}, {'abstract': 'Sam Grobart, writer of the new tech-help column Tool Kit, answers readers’ questions posted online.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/your-tech-questions-answered-part-4/', 'snippet': 'Sam Grobart, writer of the new tech-help column Tool Kit, answers readers’ questions posted online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this batch of questions, I answer questions about unlockin