Times-Picayune to three days a week would damage the civic and cultural life of the city. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rally and Open Letter Signal Pushback to a Less-Than-Daily Times-Picayune', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Orleans Times-Picayune', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T13:53:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Carr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carr', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc3da243-d0fa-5f6d-8338-184024d18e3f', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc3da243-d0fa-5f6d-8338-184024d18e3f'}, {'abstract': 'Reed Krakoff’s new resort collection is flirtatiously reserved.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/just-one-look-reed-krakoff-2/', 'snippet': 'Reed Krakoff’s new resort collection is flirtatiously reserved.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For prespring (otherwise known as resort), Reed Krakoff presented 31 looks, all of which expressed great reservation and elegance, but with a flirty subtext. Pieces that elongated the body — monochromatic dresses and lean, slit-up-the-side skirts — sent the strongest message about this season’s silhouette: flattery was everything. As in previous collections, Krakoff stuck to a palette of neutrals. Cream and sand colors came accented with hits of coral, orange and bright blue, reminders that minimalism need not be colorless. Here, an example of how effective a bold/barely-there color combination can be.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Reed Krakoff', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T14:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5137b868-5ca9-5e20-911c-18768ffe4d90', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5137b868-5ca9-5e20-911c-18768ffe4d90'}, {'abstract': 'Cisco has “a once in a decade platform.” It is a machine that handles 10 times as much mobile Internet traffic as current devices, and pays attention to different kinds of mobile data – a Facebook app on a phone acts differently from a YouTube video. Just as important is what it says about Cisco’s battle to stay meaningful.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/ciscos-strategic-box/', 'snippet': 'Cisco has “a once in a decade platform.” It is a machine that handles 10 times as much mobile Internet traffic as current devices, and pays attention to different kinds of mobile data – a Facebook app on a phone acts differently from a YouTube vid...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cisco just announced a product that it hopes will give it something it needs just as bad as revenue: relevance in two of the hottest trends in tech, the mobile Internet and software-defined networking, or S.D.N.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/blogs/cisco-asr/cisco-asr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/blogs/cisco-asr/cisco-asr-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cisco’s Strategic Box', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T14:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5933a53c-e0c3-53ec-ac56-adcc46986719', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5933a53c-e0c3-53ec-ac56-adcc46986719'}, {'abstract': 'Photographers are trying to map what remains of the Rwenzori glaciers in Uganda and the Democratic Republic of Congo before they vanish altogether.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/on-our-radar-melting-tropical-glaciers/', 'snippet': 'Photographers are trying to map what remains of the Rwenzori glaciers in Uganda and the Democratic Republic of Congo before they vanish altogether.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scientists rush to map the tropical glaciers in the Rwenzori Mountains, which are expected to disappear in a decade or two from Uganda and the Democratic Republic of Congo. [The Guardian]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Melting Tropical Glaciers', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T14:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d225821e-9d53-569f-a30d-61c570a66aa7', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d225821e-9d53-569f-a30d-61c570a66aa7'}, {'abstract': 'The victory by Gov. Scott Walker ensures that Republicans largely retain control of Wisconsin, and Mr. Walker’s fast-rising political profile is likely to soar among conservatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/us/politics/walker-survives-wisconsin-recall-effort.html', 'snippet': 'The victory by Gov. Scott Walker ensures that Republicans largely retain control of Wisconsin, and Mr. Walker’s fast-rising political profile is likely to soar among conservatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WAUKESHA, Wis. — Gov. Scott Walker, whose decision to cut collective bargaining rights for most public workers set off a firestorm in a state usually known for its political civility, easily held on to his job on Tuesday, becoming the first governor in the country to survive a recall election and dealing a painful blow to Democrats and labor unions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walker Survives Wisconsin Recall Vote', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Governor Wins Wisconsin Vote In Recall Drive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom (1953- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T14:07:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey and Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32736e80-59df-5c95-9e1b-d70c8145a83b', 'word_count': 1339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32736e80-59df-5c95-9e1b-d70c8145a83b'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/what-were-reading-450/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chicago Reader: As a nod to “Ghostbusters,” a green and minty cocktail flavored (and colored) with pickled okra. — Jeff Gordinier ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T14:07:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/162838ba-2906-52b7-a058-6d3c8591265d', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/162838ba-2906-52b7-a058-6d3c8591265d'}, {'abstract': 'The singer Amanda Palmer is one of music’s most productive users of social media, gal