te plans.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/using-smartphones-for-last-minute-indulgences/', 'snippet': 'Cellphones, with their e-mails, to-do lists and calendar appointments, may make you feel as if everything in life is scheduled down to the last minute, leaving little room for, say, an impulsive trip out of town. But an app called HotelTonight is ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can smartphones bring back spontaneity?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/blogs/hotel-app/hotel-app-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/04/blogs/hotel-app/hotel-app-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Using Smartphones for Last-Minute Indulgences', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T15:55:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3e28c02-68f8-596b-988c-0102bde1c3d2', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3e28c02-68f8-596b-988c-0102bde1c3d2'}, {'abstract': 'A daily capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/walkabout-65-wi-fi-while-traveling-and-a-map-of-gas-price-increases/', 'snippet': 'A daily capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wi-Fi for All! More and more airports and hotels are offering Wi-Fi, sometimes in exchange for viewing ads and sometimes for a fee if you want a very good connection. And for those who aren’t satisfied with those options, Sam Grobart, who writes the Took Kit column, explains how to use your own wireless router in a hotel room. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout – 6/5: Wi-Fi While Traveling and a Map of Gas Price Increases', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grobart, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T15:59:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4004f1f1-6040-5a53-88f8-c739b9e1fb7f', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4004f1f1-6040-5a53-88f8-c739b9e1fb7f'}, {'abstract': 'A rag-picker searches for reusable material in Tawi river, Jammu and Kashmir on World Environment Day.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/image-of-the-day-june-5/', 'snippet': 'A rag-picker searches for reusable material in Tawi river, Jammu and Kashmir on World Environment Day.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: June 5', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6dbdfb1-1fac-5390-a7b2-fb712596862a', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6dbdfb1-1fac-5390-a7b2-fb712596862a'}, {'abstract': 'Monica Davey and Jeff Zeleny answer a selection of questions about the Wisconsin recall.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/your-wisconsin-recall-questions-answered/', 'snippet': 'Monica Davey and Jeff Zeleny answer a selection of questions about the Wisconsin recall.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:09 p.m. | Updated  As voters in Wisconsin head to the polls, The Times’s Monica Davey and Jeff Zeleny are answering some of your questions about Tuesday’s recall election. Have a question you don’t see answered here? You can post a question here or on our Facebook page, or send a message via Twitter @thecaucus using the hashtag #asknyt. And be sure to tune back in later on Tuesday night for our live coverage and analysis of the election results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Wisconsin Recall Questions Answered', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom (1953- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:01:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a73aed50-572f-51c2-aea5-9f36df5af302', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a73aed50-572f-51c2-aea5-9f36df5af302'}, {'abstract': 'If Facebook opens up to children under 13, how can it do the job right?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/how-can-facebook-safely-add-under-13s/', 'snippet': 'If Facebook opens up to children under 13, how can it do the job right?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past few weeks, there have been rumors that Facebook is considering expanding its reach to include children under 13. With The Wall Street Journal reporting yesterday that Facebook is actively testing options to create a safe, child-friendly space on the site, those rumors can be officially considered to have reached some sort of critical mass: unnamed sources good enough for The Journal have effectively confirmed them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Can Facebook Safely Add Under-13s?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:11:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b1e3