anley, Civil War soldier and African explorer.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/the-galvanized-yankee/', 'snippet': 'The strange career of Henry Morton Stanley, Civil War soldier and African explorer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is unlikely that Henry Stanley knew, upon joining an Illinois artillery unit on June 4, 1862, that his action validated a central Darwinian principle — namely, that it is not necessarily the biggest and strongest that survive, but the most adaptable. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Galvanized Yankee', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Henry Morton', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Leigh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leigh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3b0686f-9463-55f2-ae16-1fbab9ef7930', 'word_count': 1490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3b0686f-9463-55f2-ae16-1fbab9ef7930'}, {'abstract': 'A call for caution: Let’s not over-interpret the results.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/the-wisconsin-recall/', 'snippet': 'A call for caution: Let’s not over-interpret the results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whatever happens in today’s gubernatorial recall election in Wisconsin, let’s not over-interpret the results.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wisconsin Recall', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name':