alue': 'Williams, Michael Kenneth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FunnyOrDie.com', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:51:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d1d7218-a914-535a-8970-2ae34a53257e', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d1d7218-a914-535a-8970-2ae34a53257e'}, {'abstract': 'A fifth-grade class in Queens offered more marine mascots to aid in the cleanup of the Gowanus Canal.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/kids-draw-the-news-special-edition/', 'snippet': 'A fifth-grade class in Queens offered more marine mascots to aid in the cleanup of the Gowanus Canal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An envelope stuffed with Kids Draw the News submissions landed on City Room’s desk Monday: an entire fifth-grade class’s renderings of Gowanus Canal Cleanup Mascots. We present them all above, as a supplement to last Friday’s slide show.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kids Draw the News: Special Edition', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gowanus Canal (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kolomatsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolomatsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22fdb36e-8284-5e06-aee8-41c5fea08a88', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22fdb36e-8284-5e06-aee8-41c5fea08a88'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway League gives its bi-annual report on the economic impact of Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/broadway-gives-its-regards-to-the-tune-of-11-2-billion-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway League gives its bi-annual report on the economic impact of Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Broadway industry helped generate $11.2 billion in spending by New York City tourists, theater owners and producers during the 2010-11 theater season, a 9 percent increase over the dollar amount in a comparable economic impact study two years earlier, according to the Broadway League trade association of producers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadway Gives Its Regards, to the Tune of $11.2 Billion, to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Broadway League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:56:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0504340d-01a3-5c82-8d02-7dd8b5594f43', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0504340d-01a3-5c82-8d02-7dd8b5594f43'}, {'abstract': 'A high-tech program intended to help reduce traffic congestion in Midtown Manhattan will be expanded to cover 270 blocks, up from 110.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/for-more-of-midtown-traffic-relief-may-be-a-mouse-click-away/', 'snippet': 'A high-tech program intended to help reduce traffic congestion in Midtown Manhattan will be expanded to cover 270 blocks, up from 110.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 4:43 p.m. | A high-tech program introduced last year to help reduce traffic congestion in Midtown Manhattan will be more than doubled in size after initial results indicated that travel speeds had been improved by 10 percent, city transportation officials said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For More of Midtown, Traffic Relief May Be a Mouse Click Away', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City to Widen Effort to Ease Midtown Traffic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T16:59:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric P. Newcomer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Newcomer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ae24733-1396-5c17-81d7-059986e9abef', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ae24733-1396-5c17-81d7-059986e9abef'}, {'abstract': 'Zoe Cassavetes directed a short film to kick off the CDFA Awards, which took place at Alice Tully Hall on Monday. And the winners are…', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/now-playing-fifty-years-of-the-cfda/', 'snippet': 'Zoe Cassavetes directed a short film to kick off the CDFA Awards, which took place at Alice Tully Hall on Monday. And the winners are…', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night the Council of Fashion Designers of America (CFDA) Fashion Awards took place at Lincoln Center’s Alice Tully Hall in New York. There, industry members gathered to commemorate the organization’s 50th anniversary, to recognize the year’s most exciting contributions to fashion design and journalism, and to celebrate the lifetime achievements of some of the business’s biggest creative influences. Kicking off the evening’s ceremony was this short film, “50 Years of the CFDA,” directed by Zoe Cassavetes and inspired by Richard Avedon’s 1969 portraits of Andy Warhol and members of the Factory. “I think it came out as half film, half art collage,” noted Cassavetes about the project. Of her subjects she said: “I was pretty blown away by the talent that came through the studio during those two days [we were shooting]. It was interesting to see which designers are inspired by others and why. It’s not just about the clothes they make … it’s about the universe they create.” Below is a list of this year’s award winners and honorees:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Playing | ‘Fifty Years of the CFDA’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T17:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a34a8c8-a8e4-5877-b143-acffe41b90a3', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a34a8c8-a8e4-5877-b143-acffe41b90a3'}, {'abstract': 'The maker of quirky home furnishings will continue to make some products locally and has found a way to produce in China, too.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/how-jellio-is-solving-its-manufacturing-problems/', 'snippet': 'The maker of quirky home furnishings will continue to make some products locally and has found a way to produce in China, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, we published a case study about Jellio, a company that makes whimsical home furnishings that are hard to manufacture. Demand for Jellio’s products, which include its top-selling Gummi Bear candy-inspired GummiLights, was strong. But to build the business, the owner, Mario Marsicano, knew he had to increase production while reducing costs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Jellio Is Solving Its Manufacturing Problems', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Solutions For Jellio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Production', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T17:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbfdb4ad-1784-5e97-93b7-738950077c0d', 'word_count': 666, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbfdb4ad-1784-5e97-93b7-738950077c0d'}, {'abstract': 'The awards, which were handed out Monday night at Gracie Mansion by the mayor, recognized people and companies for their achievements in “making it” in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/at-made-in-ny-awards-kickstarter-shares-honors-with-streep-and-de-niro/', 'snippet': 'The awards, which were handed out Monday night at Gracie Mansion by the mayor, recognized people and companies for their achievements in “making it” in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The media production company @radical.media and Kickstarter, the crowd-sourced financing Web site, were among the companies and people honored Monday night by the City of New York for their achievements in “making it” in New York, literally and idiomatically.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Made in NY Awards, Kickstarter Shares Honors With Streep and De Niro', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, Perry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'De Niro, Robert', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldberg, Whoopi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meara, Anne', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliver, Katherine', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ripa, Kelly', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stiller, Jerry', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streep, Meryl', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '@radical.media Inc', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kickstarter', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T17:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1919082e-2cee-5850-a875-bb83552519f7', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1919082e-2cee-5850-a875-bb83552519f7'}, {'abstract': 'Some abortion opponents say emergency contraception pills may block fertilized eggs from implanting, but scientists say there is no evidence the pills work that way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/health/research/morning-after-pills-dont-block-implantation-science-suggests.html', 'snippet': 'Some abortion opponents say emergency contraception pills may block fertilized eggs from implanting, but scientists say there is no evidence the pills work that way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Labels inside every box of morning-after pills, drugs widely used to prevent pregnancy after sex, say they may work by blocking fertilized eggs from implanting in a woman’s uterus. Respected medical authorities, including the National Institutes of Health and the Mayo Clinic, have said the same thing on their Web sites.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/06emergency-cnd/06emergency-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/06emergency-cnd/06emergency-cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/06emergency-cnd/06emergency-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/science/06emergency-cnd/06emergency-cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbL