', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee84a813-bc57-5a8f-8ea9-af76bd9c3377', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee84a813-bc57-5a8f-8ea9-af76bd9c3377'}, {'abstract': 'A dreamy vision of a handmade cloak led Sarah Rhodes to explore a nearly lost Aboriginal tradition. Her photographs document the art of possum skin cloaks, whose panels chronicle a lifetime of stories and experiences.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/cloaking-the-aboriginal-past/', 'snippet': 'A dreamy vision of a handmade cloak led Sarah Rhodes to explore a nearly lost Aboriginal tradition. Her photographs document the art of possum skin cloaks, whose panels chronicle a lifetime of stories and experiences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She is backstage at the Sydney Opera House. She is going to perform. A young woman, a photographer, takes her picture. She wears a cloak made from possum pelts stitched together, each individual square adorned with images that contain countless sacred stories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cloaking the Aboriginal Past', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T17:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt McCann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66f4fcf5-e89a-5b4e-a2f1-ccc1972a62da', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66f4fcf5-e89a-5b4e-a2f1-ccc1972a62da'}, {'abstract': 'Catch, in the meatpacking district, has a department store’s dimensions and a nightc