editors during a visit that the Obama administration has not done nearly enough to address the steep dropout rate among college students.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/education-secretary-targets-colleges-with-low-graduation-rates/', 'snippet': 'The Secretary of Education Arne Duncan told New York Times reporters and editors during a visit that the Obama administration has not done nearly enough to address the steep dropout rate among college students.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Secretary of Education Arne Duncan said on Tuesday morning that the Obama administration has not done nearly enough to address the steep dropout rate among college students.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Education Secretary Targets Colleges With Low Graduation Rates', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduation Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Arne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Caldwell and Jacques Steinberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jacques', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83eed840-be98-58bb-9d7b-fadc6019549d', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83eed840-be98-58bb-9d7b-fadc6019549d'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of tweets from the annual fashion awards ceremony, held on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/the-best-tweets-from-the-cfda-awards/', 'snippet': 'A roundup of tweets from the annual fashion awards ceremony, held on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Tweets From the #CFDA Awards', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Depp, Johnny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hilfiger, Tommy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jacobs, Marc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyers, Seth', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Ashley', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Olsen, Mary-Kate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Posen, Zac', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wintour, Anna', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Fashion Designers of America', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:19:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fdaa78e-4e3b-5edd-a1cf-02b614308adb', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fdaa78e-4e3b-5edd-a1cf-02b614308adb'}, {'abstract': 'Debra Winger, whose films include “Terms of Endearment,” “Urban Cowboy” and “An Officer and a Gentleman,” is replacing Laurie Metcalf in David Mamet’s play about a prison inmate with a radical past and the warden from whom she seeks a parole.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/debra-winger-to-make-her-broadway-debut-in-david-mamets-anarchist/', 'snippet': 'Debra Winger, whose films include “Terms of Endearment,” “Urban Cowboy” and “An Officer and a Gentleman,” is replacing Laurie Metcalf in David Mamet’s play about a prison inmate with a radical past and the warden from whom she seeks a parole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a film career that has included “Terms of Endearment,” “Urban Cowboy” and “An Officer and a Gentleman,” it was only a matter of time before someone swept Debra Winger off her feet and carried her over the threshold of Broadway, and the man who’s going to do it (sans naval uniform) is David Mamet. The producers of Mr. Mamet’s coming play, “The Anarchist,” said on Tuesday that Ms. Winger would make her Broadway debut in the production, which is scheduled to begin performances in November. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debra Winger to Make Her Broadway Debut in David Mamet’s ‘Anarchist’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LuPone, Patti', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metcalf, Laurie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winger, Debra', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN REPERTORY THEATER', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22a4707a-9fbc-5c07-8f92-73426ba3354a', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22a4707a-9fbc-5c07-8f92-73426ba3354a'}, {'abstract': 'The front passenger air bag may deploy when a small child is seated there, potentially causing injury, the automaker said.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/kia-recalls-73000-rio-models-for-air-bag-malfunction-hazard/', 'snippet': 'The front passenger air bag may deploy when a small child is seated there, potentially causing injury, the automaker said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kia announced it would recall almost 73,000 of its Rio models from the 2006-8 model years because a passenger air bag could malfunction and deploy when a small child was seated in the front passenger seat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kia Recalls 73,000 Rio Models for Air-Bag Malfunction Hazard', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kia Motors Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d998c4e-0f9b-5a3e-9387-b02543abbd2d', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d998c4e-0f9b-5a3e-9387-b02543abbd2d'}, {'abstract': 'Meg Whitman told 10,000 customers that Hewlett-Packard would be “more than the sum of its parts” in hardware, software and services. The company will deliver secure information and offer insight in a world of cloud computing and a mobile Internet. The one thing she missed: How this will happen.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/meg-whitmans-defining-moment/', 'snippet': 'Meg Whitman told 10,000 customers that Hewlett-Packard would be “more than the sum of its parts” in hardware, software and services. The company will deliver secure information and offer insight in a world of cloud computing and a mobile Internet....', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Meg Whitman spoke Tuesday morning to 10,000 customers and partners at an event in the gambling capital. It was her biggest public performance as the chief executive of Hewlett-Packard. In a sense it was her defining moment: after the turmoil of the last couple of years, she tried to define what H.P. is and does, and why the company still matters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/04/23/technology/bits/bitpix-hp-whitman/bitpix-hp-whitman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meg Whitman’s Defining Moment, Still Undefined', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Margaret C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:42:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da4c317c-adb3-57ae-92fa-4001e9292cdc', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da4c317c-adb3-57ae-92fa-4001e9292cdc'}, {'abstract': 'Apple’s Worldwide Developers Conference, where the company has typically unveiled new iPhones, is just a week away. And as usual, the Web is noisy with tech publications claiming to have the scoop on what’s to come.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/wwdc-round-up-tv-apps/', 'snippet': 'Apple’s Worldwide Developers Conference, where the company has typically unveiled new iPhones, is just a week away. And as usual, the Web is noisy with tech publications claiming to have the scoop on what’s to come.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Apple’s Worldwide Developers Conference, an annual event where the company has typically unveiled new iPhones, will start on Monday. And as usual, the Web is noisy with chatter about what’s to come.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rounding Up Apple Conference Chatter, From Maps to TV Apps', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e73adb3e-976c-5789-8ceb-bc964a3ee910', 'word_count': 558, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e73adb3e-976c-5789-8ceb-bc964a3ee910'}, {'abstract': 'Most teams that fall behind 3-0 in a Stanley Cup finals bow out meekly in a sweep. But once, the fog game spiced things up. Another time, the Red Wings did.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/how-steep-are-the-odds-of-a-3-0-comeback-very/', 'snippet': 'Most teams that fall behind 3-0 in a Stanley Cup finals bow out meekly in a sweep. But once, the fog game spiced things up. Another time, the Red Wings did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Los Angeles taking a 3-0 lead over the Devils in the Stanley Cup finals, television types have repeatedly mentioned that only one N.H.L. team has come from down three-games-to-none to win a Stanley Cup finals: the 1942 Toronto Maple Leafs, who erased the Red Wings’ 3-0 lead to win the Cup. But what happened to all the other teams that fell behind 3-0?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Steep Are the Odds of a 3-0 Comeback? Very', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lumley, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Red Wings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Edmonton Oilers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Minnesota North Stars', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toronto Maple Leafs', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:51:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17aaa046-3d06-5b77-b4b6-648ee22e3ccb', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17aaa046-3d06-5b77-b4b6-648ee22e3ccb'}, {'abstract': 'Rocket Pig, a new shop from Ralf Kuettel, opens on West 24th Street next week and features pork sandwiches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/dining/through-a-courtyard-ambitious-pork.html', 'snippet': 'Rocket Pig, a new shop from Ralf Kuettel, opens on West 24th Street next week and features pork sandwiches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is more than one way to put some pig in a sandwich. Ralf Kuettel (right), the chef and owner of Trestle on Tenth, channels Northern Europe instead of Tennessee or Italy in the sandwich he’ll be serving at his new shop, Rocket Pig, using seasonings like juniper, mustard and bay leaves to flavor hunks of pork neck and shoulder, which he brines, then smokes and roasts. The compact shop, which opens next week, is behind the restaurant, reachable through a rusted gate and a charming little brick courtyard. There are counters for eating, as well as access to the restaurant’s garden. Raw oysters, cheeses, cured meats, potato chips, cookies, brownies and wine and beer round out the menu. Other items, like salads, soups and sausages, may be added in coming months. Everything, except for the alcoholic beverages, can be packed to go. And with the High Line entrance a block away, why not? ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF1__PIG/06STUFF1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF1__PIG/06STUFF1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF1__PIG/06STUFF1__PIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF1__PIG/06STUFF1__PIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF1__PIG/06STUFF1__PIG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Through a Courtyard, Ambitious Pork', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Through A Courtyard, Ambitious Pork', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuettel, Ralf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pork', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rocket Pig (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trestle (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:51:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2851eadb-efaf-572f-a297-0eb83a300133', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2851eadb-efaf-572f-a297-0eb83a300133'}, {'abstract': '“Chariots of Fire”? Sure. But when compiling a list of the best movies about the Summer Olympics, don’t forget “Running Brave” and “American Anthem.”', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/the-best-summer-olympics-movies-with-a-few-asterisks/', 'snippet': '“Chariots of Fire”? Sure. But when compiling a list of the best movies about the Summer Olympics, don’t forget “Running Brave” and “American Anthem.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Summer Olympics always brings two weeks of incredible stories of joy, triumph and heartbreak, mostly involving fit, attractive young people. So it should be a great subject for films, right?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Summer Olympics Movies (With a Few Asterisks)', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crudup, Billy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Coubertin, Pierre', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hemingway, Mariel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lansbury, Angela', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leto, Jared', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neal, Tatum", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prefontaine, Steve', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Chariots of Fire (Movie)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Tokyo Olympiad (Movie)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:52:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/489e353f-adec-5e81-a906-a3b5adafceb4', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/489e353f-adec-5e81-a906-a3b5adafceb4'}, {'abstract': 'From Curtis Stone, cake, loaf and muffin pans with bottoms that can be popped up to release their contents.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/dining/from-a-tv-chef-bottoms-up-in-baking-pans.html', 'snippet': 'From Curtis Stone, cake, loaf and muffin pans with bottoms that can be popped up to release their contents.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest addition to the line of cookware and serving pieces from Curtis Stone, the chef and television personality, is a trio of baking pans that combine heavy-duty steel with silicone liners. The cake, loaf and muffin pans have built-in silicone bottoms that can be popped up, making it easier to release their contents. Mr. Stone said he developed many of the cookware items sold under his name after filming the reality series “Take Home Chef,” in which he randomly finds people in a supermarket and goes to their homes to help them cook a meal. “I got real insight into what people go through in the kitchen and how inadequate their equipment often is,” he said. “My products are not just endorsements. I hope I’m solving problems.” ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF3_PAN/06STUFF3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF3_PAN/06STUFF3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF3_PAN/06STUFF3_PAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF3_PAN/06STUFF3_PAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF3_PAN/06STUFF3_PAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From a TV Chef, Bottoms Up in Baking Pans', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From a TV Chef, Bottoms Up In Baking Pans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Curtis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:53:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2833b029-8f53-55ff-84b4-d25646e7e64f', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2833b029-8f53-55ff-84b4-d25646e7e64f'}, {'abstract': 'Two women partner to make a vegetarian sofrito in verde and spiced varieties.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/dining/a-latino-basic-goes-vegetarian.html', 'snippet': 'Two women partner to make a vegetarian sofrito in verde and spiced varieties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young women embarking on a new artisanal food venture has become a familiar story. Susana Columna and Gloribell Tavera, both of whom lost their jobs in television, now make sofrito, a base for Latino dishes that is as essential as roux in New Orleans or mirepoix in France. (Soffrito is the Italian version.) Though sofrito is often made with pork or pork fat, Chulita’s Famous Sofrito, produced in Long Island City, Queens, is vegetarian. Unlike a mass-market sofrito, it has no added starches, thickeners or other additives. There are two varieties: a verde, with bell peppers, garlic, lemon juice, vinegar and herbs; and a spiced one that is ruddy, dense and less moist, with similar ingredients as well as a good dose of paprika and cumin. Use them to get that bean and pork stew, chicken casserole or paella going; they can also serve as salsa, garnish or embellishment for a bowl of soup.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF2_SOFRITO/06STUFF2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF2_SOFRITO/06STUFF2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF2_SOFRITO/06STUFF2_SOFRITO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF2_SOFRITO/06STUFF2_SOFRITO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06STUFF2_SOFRITO/06STUFF2_SOFRITO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Latino Basic Goes Vegetarian', 'kicker': 'Food Stuff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Latino Basic Goes Vegetarian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Chulita's Famous Sofrito", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spices', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T18:53:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'B