 1}, {'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e662aac-454a-58ed-9659-9c334bd6f6b5', 'word_count': 1302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e662aac-454a-58ed-9659-9c334bd6f6b5'}, {'abstract': 'Kings defenseman Rob Scuderi, who grew up on Long Island, says the Islanders can build a winner in their current arena.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/scuderi-sees-hope-for-his-once-beloved-islanders/', 'snippet': 'Kings defenseman Rob Scuderi, who grew up on Long Island, says the Islanders can build a winner in their current arena.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kings defenseman Rob Scuderi is one game away from having his name engraved on the Stanley Cup for a second time. But he can still remember when that was first a dream, growing up as an Islanders fan on Long Island during the team’s heyday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scuderi Sees Hope for His Once Beloved Islanders', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scuderi, Rob', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Islanders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T19:12:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Luttrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luttrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c02faef5-f982-58f2-847a-e1c891c03abd', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c02faef5-f982-58f2-847a-e1c891c03abd'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney wants to lop off a year from his economic record as governor of Massachusetts — but not from President Obama’s.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/axelrod-accuses-romney-campaign-of-breaktaking-hypocrisy-on-economic-record/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney wants to lop off a year from his economic record as governor of Massachusetts — but not from President Obama’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there’s one thing Mitt Romney cannot stand, it’s when President Obama blames the economic situation he inherited from former president George W. Bush for the country’s current gloomy challenges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Critique of Obama Jobs Record Puts Romney in a Bind', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T19:13:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6024e15b-7199-5a4c-9dc2-04d07666d7e8', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6024e15b-7199-5a4c-9dc2-04d07666d7e8'}, {'abstract': 'In an hourlong conversation with one of her adversaries, the rapper explains her decision to pull out of the Summer Jam concert.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/nicki-minaj-faces-off-with-the-hot-97-d-j-s/', 'snippet': 'In an hourlong conversation with one of her adversaries, the rapper explains her decision to pull out of the Summer Jam concert.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicki Minaj, the Queens rapper, called into Hot 97 on Monday night to explain her decision to pull out of the radio station’s concert the previous day and became embroiled in a heated debate with DJ Funkmaster Flex.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicki Minaj Faces Off With the Hot 97 D.J.’s', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Funkmaster Flex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Wayne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T19:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b4bad7f-c723-5b27-aa83-42a855ed3dce', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b4bad7f-c723-5b27-aa83-42a855ed3dce'}, {'abstract': 'An example of why conservatives see the state as a threat to community.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/big-government-small-families/', 'snippet': 'An example of why conservatives see the state as a threat to community.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week I had the pleasure of joining the Washington Post’s E.J. Dionne on “The Diane Rehm Show” for a discussion of his engaging new book, “Our Divided Political Heart,” which is both a meditation on the individualistic and communitarian strands in American political thought and history, and (as you might expect, given the author) a lament that the contemporary Republican Party has tilted the contemporary balance dangerously toward a radical individualism. My main criticism of his thesis (also perhaps predictably) was to question Dionne’s tendency to equate “community” with “government,” given the way expansions of state power tend to crowd out more personal and/or voluntary forms of common life (civic, religious, familial), replacing human-scale interactions with bureaucratic process and leaving society more atomized than before. To which he responded that while this can happen, it doesn’t have to happen: Government can strengthen local communities as well as weaken them, partner with private groups as well pre-empt them, and fill in the gaps left by purely voluntary effort as well as take those efforts’ place. Conceding that reality, I nonetheless tried to press Dionne a bit more on whether given where we are now, with a large-scale and costly welfare state having become a permanent feature of our national life even as more local and personal forms of community have attenuated, the conservative-communitarian suspicion of state power might not be more relevant than the liberal-communitarian view of the state as an instrument of social solidarity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Government, Small Families', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T19:14:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6dfb860-b7d7-537d-afec-691b6ebc9f09', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6dfb860-b7d7-537d-afec-691b6ebc9f09'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Federer rallied from two sets down to defeat Juan Martín del Potro, and Novak Djokovic saved four match points against Jo-Wilfried Tsonga to advance to the semifinals of the French Open.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/sports/tennis/06iht-mens06.html', 'snippet': 'Roger Federer rallied from two sets down to defeat Juan Martín del Potro, and Novak Djokovic saved four match points against Jo-Wilfried Tsonga to advance to the semifinals of the French Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — In a roundabout sense, Novak Djokovic has the French to thank for helping to make him the armor-plated champion he has become. Djokovic credits leading Serbia’s Davis Cup team to an emotional victory over France in the 2010 final for launching him into the tennis stratosphere, for giving him the confidence to move mountains named Nadal and Federer, for helping him stare down Grand Slam inconveniences like match points.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/tennis/06met-pic2/06met-pic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/tennis/06met-pic2/06met-pic2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/tennis/06met-pic2/06met-pic2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/tennis/06met-pic2/06met-pic2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1270, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/tennis/06met-pic2/06met-pic2-thumbSt