f Neta may be plain, but the sushi served there is not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVEN by the spartan standards of sushi bars, the interior of Neta, on West Eighth Street, is defiantly plain. The walls are covered in a nubby material that makes them look like bulletin boards in a corporate cafeteria. They’re even dotted with pushpin-size holes, as if somebody had taken down the Man With a Van fliers just before unlocking the doors at 5 p.m.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06rest_337/06rest_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 540, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06rest_337/06rest_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 540, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06rest_337/06rest_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06rest_337/06rest_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06rest_337/06rest_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gleaming Sushi That Fills the Eye', 'kicker': 'Restaurant Review ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gleaming Sushi That Fills the Eye', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neta (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'va