tion to take on powerful corporations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Finally, an entity powerful enough to challenge food manufacturing conglomerates takes affirmative action against advertising food to children that we don’t, as a society, actually want them to eat. The Food and Drug Administration? No, not them. The Federal Communications Commission? Not them, either.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disney Limits Junk-Food Ads', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wal-Mart Stores Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T20:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ba4b5a9-4452-5846-b6dd-32ac0bf881fd', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ba4b5a9-4452-5846-b6dd-32ac0bf881fd'}, {'abstract': 'The Knights presented a quirky performance piece at the Stone that recalled some of John Cage’s Happenings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/arts/music/the-knights-echo-john-cages-happenings-at-the-stone.html', 'snippet': 'The Knights presented a quirky performance piece at the Stone that recalled some of John Cage’s Happenings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Random lines from “The Big Lebowski” kept coming up at the Knights’ performance piece at the Stone on Sunday evening. At one point, reading off a card, one of the players said, in effect, “You guys aren’t privy to all the new stuff,” though the language was definitely coarser. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/06knights/06knights-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chamber Players’ Variations in the Key of John Cage', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 