of Vector’s plan to recapitalize the French film equipment maker, rather than a competing proposal by JPMorgan Chase.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the battle to take a big stake in Technicolor, Vector Capital received a prominent supporter in Institutional Shareholder Services.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.S.S. Sides With Vector in Fight Over Technicolor', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Shareholder Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Technicolor SA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vector Capital', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:18:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e627f33-ed3e-5bb5-b412-aea688f26b91', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e627f33-ed3e-5bb5-b412-aea688f26b91'}, {'abstract': 'The outgoing prosecutor at the International Criminal Court recommended to the Security Council that it enforce the arrest warrants on President Omar al-Bashir and three others accused of war crimes in the Darfur conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/world/africa/darfur-war-crimes-prosecutor-urges-action-against-omar-al-bashir.html', 'snippet': 'The outgoing prosecutor at the International Criminal Court recommended to the Security Council that it enforce the arrest warrants on President Omar al-Bashir and three others accused of war crimes in the Darfur conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The outgoing prosecutor at the International Criminal Court, frustrated over his inability to enforce arrest warrants for the Sudanese president and three others accused of war crimes in the Darfur conflict, recommended to the Security Council on Tuesday that it take more severe action against the defendants, including possibly seizing them inside Sudan for trial in The Hague.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Darfur War Crimes Prosecutor Urges Tougher Action Against Sudan President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecutor Urges Tougher Action on Darfur Crimes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Darfur (Sudan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Omar Hassan Al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moreno-Ocampo, Luis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e4c1ef7-be66-50e4-aa5b-b3d684c27866', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e4c1ef7-be66-50e4-aa5b-b3d684c27866'}, {'abstract': 'The Ninth Circuit won’t revisit its ruling on Proposition 8. Now what?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/gay-marriage-inches-towards-the-supreme-court/', 'snippet': 'The Ninth Circuit won’t revisit its ruling on Proposition 8. Now what?', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second week in a row, there is major news on gay rights. Last Thursday, the First Circuit ruled against the Defense of Marriage Act, which prohibits granting federal benefits to same-sex couples. Today, the Ninth Circuit declined to review an earlier decision by a three-judge panel against Proposition 8, which banned same-sex marriage in California.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Marriage Inches Towards the Supreme Court', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:27:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31b924c5-e373-5332-8f2a-20440c0c77ba', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31b924c5-e373-5332-8f2a-20440c0c77ba'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater performs John Cranko’s “Onegin” at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/arts/dance/american-ballet-theater-in-onegin-at-metropolitan-opera-house.html', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater performs John Cranko’s “Onegin” at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are a balletomane, caring more about dancers than choreography, then the casting of John Cranko’s three-act ballet “Onegin” (1965) brings excitements. When I first watched it, in 1978, the Stuttgart Ballet fielded four casts in three days, including two of Cranko’s original cast (Marcia Haydée as Tatiana, Egon Madsen as Lensky); I applauded them all eagerly. In the 1980s, when Natalia Makarova danced Tatiana with the English National Ballet, I thought her more riveting and varied than any previous interpreter. When Lynn Seymour later stepped into the same role, her intensity and naturalism proved yet more astonishing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/ONEGIN/ONEGIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1020, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/ONEGIN/ONEGIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2039, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/ONEGIN/ONEGIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/ONEGIN/ONEGIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/ONEGIN/ONEGIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Savoring Movers Over the Moves', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Savoring Movers Over the Moves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cranko, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Onegin (Ballet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:29:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/92ad30a3-9be8-5f35-8c0b-b2d0e5bcaee2', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92ad30a3-9be8-5f35-8c0b-b2d0e5bcaee2'}, {'abstract': 'The Queen’s Diamond Jubilee may be over but the Victoria and Albert Museum allows visitors to prolong the spirit of celebration and pageantry with “Ballgowns: British Glamour Since 1950.” On display in the museum’s recently renovated fashion galleries through Jan. 6, the show traces the history of royal gowns and evening wear, from debutante balls to red-carpet events.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/gowns-for-belles-of-the-ball-at-the-victoria-and-albert-museum/', 'snippet': 'The Queen’s Diamond Jubilee may be over but the Victoria and Albert Museum allows visitors to prolong the spirit of celebration and pageantry with “Ballgowns: British Glamour Since 1950.” On display in the museum’s recently renovated fashion galle...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Queen’s Diamond Jubilee may be over but the Victoria and\xa0 Albert Museum allows visitors to prolong the spirit of celebration and pageantry by focusing on a garment that encapsulates a sense of occasion: the ballgown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gowns for Belles of the Ball at the Victoria and Albert Museum', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Houssin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Houssin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92e19450-1505-507c-b662-5df9057683b1', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92e19450-1505-507c-b662-5df9057683b1'}, {'abstract': 'Rescue workers continued to recover bodies from the wreckage of the airliner that crashed into a crowded, working-class neighborhood in Lagos on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/world/africa/at-nigeria-crash-site-residents-recount-silent-descent-of-sudden-death.html', 'snippet': 'Rescue workers continued to recover bodies from the wreckage of the airliner that crashed into a crowded, working-class neighborhood in Lagos on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAGOS, Nigeria — A pair of women’s high heels protruding from a charred tan suitcase, a muddied toiletries kit, a change of underwear: rescue workers grimly ferried these possessions of Dana Air Flight 9J 992’s passengers from the airliner’s wreckage here on Tuesday, even as colleagues searched for and found bodies. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/world/NIGERIA/NIGERIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/world/NIGERIA/NIGERIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/world/NIGERIA/NIGERIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo'