y contains some stunning revelations about the American role in using computer warfare to attack Iran’s nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/books/confront-and-conceal-by-david-sanger.html', 'snippet': 'David Sanger’s account of President Obama’s foreign policy contains some stunning revelations about the American role in using computer warfare to attack Iran’s nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is the United States at war with Iran? If David Sanger’s account in his new book, “Confront and Conceal,” on President Obama’s foreign policy, is to be believed — and I find it very believable — we certainly are.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 658, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1316, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 191, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Covert Wars, Waged Virally', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Covert Wars, Waged Virally', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanger, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas E. Ricks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Ricks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/966c62f8-cc43-582e-b117-fae78d71351b', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/966c62f8-cc43-582e-b117-fae78d71351b'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney argued that the economy had stalled under President Obama, and that Mr. Obama did not deserve credit for any improvements that might occur between now and November.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/in-texas-romney-raises-money-and-attacks-obama/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney argued that the economy had stalled under President Obama, and that Mr. Obama did not deserve credit for any improvements that might occur between now and November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT WORTH, Tex. — Mitt Romney headed to Texas on Tuesday, making his way across the state for back-to-back days of fund-raisers. But before he started, he laid out his fundamental campaign message to voters at an office systems warehouse here, arguing that the economy had stalled under President Obama, and that Mr. Obama did not deserve credit for any improvements that might occur between now and November.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Texas, Romney Raises Money and Attacks Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:35:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af920a85-f80d-55a2-8742-7b2d5ca97d47', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af920a85-f80d-55a2-8742-7b2d5ca97d47'}, {'abstract': 'The Times is providing live updates and analysis of the Wisconsin recall election.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/live-updates-of-wisconsin-recall-election/', 'snippet': 'The Times is providing live updates and analysis of the Wisconsin recall election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILWAUKEE — Sixteen months after Wisconsin erupted into one of the fiercest political wars in residents’ memories, voters began streaming into polling places on Tuesday to decide whether to remove Gov. Scott Walker, the Republican whose decision to cut collective bargaining rights for most public workers set off the fight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Updates of Wisconsin Recall Election', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:39:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3272c07e-ee11-52d6-a4a2-5e71556e6e1c', 'word_count': 6460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3272c07e-ee11-52d6-a4a2-5e71556e6e1c'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Clinton again makes remarks that seem at odds with President Obama’s message.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/clinton-in-break-with-obama-urges-tax-cut-extension/', 'snippet': 'Bill Clinton again makes remarks that seem at odds with President Obama’s message.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 9:03 p.m. | Updated  Former President Bill Clinton, voicing a new “antiausterity” line opposed by both parties, suggested Tuesday that all expiring tax cuts be extended temporarily and that short-term budget cutting be put off until the country emerges from what he called a recession.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clinton Suggests Extending Tax Cuts Temporarily', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:49:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbbc12f7-38dd-54ed-96e9-99e0ac281f95', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbbc12f7-38dd-54ed-96e9-99e0ac281f95'}, {'abstract': 'Google has acquired Quickoffice, a start-up that makes a set of applications for iPads and Android tablets that let people open and edit Microsoft Office files. The deal will put additional pressure on Microsoft to release a version of Office for the iPad.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/as-google-bets-on-mobile-office-microsoft-waits/', 'snippet': 'Google has acquired Quickoffice, a start-up that makes a set of applications for iPads and Android tablets that let people open and edit Microsoft Office files. The deal will put additional pressure on Microsoft to release a version of Office for ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Microsoft couldn’t find compelling enough reasons to release its Office applications for the iPad, Google just gave it one.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Google Bets on Mobile Office, Microsoft Waits', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Battle Nears For Office Apps', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quickoffice Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:55:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73cda600-14af-5f2d-ab65-7cfe2a9d928e', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73cda600-14af-5f2d-ab65-7cfe2a9d928e'}, {'abstract': 'The decision, which was due last Saturday, is now expected by the end of next week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/ruling-delayed-on-adding-cancer-to-911-fund-illnesses/', 'snippet': 'The decision, which was due last Saturday, is now expected by the end of next week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An eagerly awaited federal ruling on whether to include cancer among the illnesses that will be treated and result in compensation using money set aside by Congress for victims of the Sept. 11 attack on the World Trade Center has been delayed by several days, federal officials said Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruling Delayed on Adding Cancer to 9/11 Fund Illnesses', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'James Zadroga 9-11 Health and Compensation Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zadroga, James', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf93037-418d-5e23-b359-89a412518424', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf93037-418d-5e23-b359-89a412518424'}, {'abstract': 'Clouds getting in the way of watching Venus make its way across the sun? NASA is streaming live video of the event from Hawaii.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/live-streaming-video-of-venus-transit/', 'snippet': 'Clouds getting in the way of watching Venus make its way across the sun? NASA is streaming live video of the event from Hawaii.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Starting at 6:03 p.m. Eastern, weather permitting, skywatchers around the world can begin looking for Venus to start crossing the face of the sun, a rare event that won’t come around again for 105 years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Live Streaming Video of Venus Transit', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venus (Planet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T21:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/358a4306-dc27-542b-a555-ca848a07e64c', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/358a4306-dc27-542b-a555-ca848a07e64c'}, {'abstract': 'For the 1912 Olympics in Stockholm, tickets were available by mail–and as always, the earlier the request, the better the seat.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/sweden-1912-way-before-stubhub/', 'snippet': 'For the 1912 Olympics in Stockholm, tickets were available by mail–and as always, the earlier the request, the better the seat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One hundred years ago the Summer Olympics were held in Stockholm. As we count down the days to London 2012, we’ll take a look back at what was happening at the Games a century ago. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweden 1912: Way Before Stubhub', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stockholm (Sweden)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T22:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/819f721f-d155-5c5d-bf06-a445898c3a94', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/819f721f-d155-5c5d-bf06-a445898c3a94'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Tuesday’s selection includes a sexist Twitter post from Asus at an electronics conference, a theory that Google Street View photos will be used to train robot cars and a review thread on Yelp about a California jail.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/todays-scuttlebot-jail-on-yelp-and-google-cars/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editor