embership status gives Samsung a seat on the foundation’s board, allowing it to have more of a say in how Linux is developed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Samsung Backs Open Source, Joining Linux Foundation', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Linux (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Open-Source Software', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Linux Foundation, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T22:17:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28674c93-4c99-51cc-bc3d-73148ce2d915', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28674c93-4c99-51cc-bc3d-73148ce2d915'}, {'abstract': 'Appy Couple, a new wedding planning app, replaces the traditional wedding Web site with a stylish app for the tech-savvy, fast-moving and multitasking bride.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/appy-couple-the-wedding-app-for-the-modern-bride/', 'snippet': 'Appy Couple, a new wedding planning app, replaces the traditional wedding Web site with a stylish app for the tech-savvy, fast-moving and multitasking bride.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gone are the days of sending multiple e-mails to your bridal party, calling family members with updates on wedding events, or sending mass texts to guests with directions to venues. Appy Couple, a new wedding app, can replace the traditional wedding planning methods, like building your own Web site, with an app for the tech-savvy, fast-moving and multitasking bride. You can stay in touch with your guests and organize events from your iPhones, iPads and Androids.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Wedding App for the Modern Bride', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T22:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charanna Alexander', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alexander', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ad2d96-06de-5bf0-a1d0-e5427a2605cd', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ad2d96-06de-5bf0-a1d0-e5427a2605cd'}, {'abstract': 'Crossroads GPS releases a new advertisement, part of a $25 million campaign in 10 swing states.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/new-ad-attacks-obama-on-federal-debt/', 'snippet': 'Crossroads GPS releases a new advertisement, part of a $25 million campaign in 10 swing states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crossroads GPS, a conservative advocacy group founded by Karl Rove and other top Republicans, released a new advertisement on Tuesday that hammers President Obama’s handling of the budget and the national debt. The advertisement is the third piece of a $25 million campaign that is running in 10 swing states. Crossroads said it is putting $7 million into the commercial, which uses a ticking clock to drive home the point that the country is piling on more debt every second.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ad Attacks Obama on Federal Debt', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-05T22:29:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b7de1de-e1f0-5a10-9f21-49b174570fea', 'word_count': 80, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b7de1de-e1f0-5a10-9f21-49b174570fea'}, {'abstract': 'The American Heart Association says people uncomfortable with mouth-to-mouth resuscitation can use hands alone to help someone having a heart attack.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/a-lifesaving-lesson-with-a-70s-bee-gees-beat/', 'snippet': 'The American Heart Association says people uncomfortable with mouth-to-mouth resuscitation can use hands alone to help someone having a heart attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It might have been some strange daytime disco event or it might have been a red-carpet movie premiere. It was hard to tell on Tuesday afternoon in Bryant Park. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lifesaving Lesson With a ’70s Bee Gees Beat', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cardiopulmonary Resuscit