’s privacy guidelines, which expressly prohibit app makers from transmitting users’ data without their permission.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/linkedins-leaky-mobile-app-has-access-to-your-meeting-notes/', 'snippet': 'Researchers discovered that LinkedIn’s app for the iPhone had transmitted users’ calendar entries— which may include details about their meeting locations, participants, dial-in information, passwords and sensitive meeting notes — to its servers a...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LinkedIn mobile app subscribers may be surprised to learn that the calendar entries on their iPhones or iPads— which may include details about meeting locations, participants, dial-in information, passwords and sensitive meeting notes — are transmitted back to LinkedIn’s servers without their knowledge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/blogs/linkedin-code/linkedin-code-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/05/blogs/linkedin-code/linkedin-code-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 288}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/blogs/linkedin-code/linkedin-code-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/blogs/linkedin-code/linkedin-code-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 1214, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'LinkedIn’s Leaky Mobile App Has Access to Your Meeting Notes', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LinkedIn Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T00:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dace1d79-2b63-5d0c-9bdc-b513e4dc4dc4', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dace1d79-2b63-5d0c-9bdc-b513e4dc4dc4'}, {'abstract': 'Voters in the Wisconsin recall election would re-elect President Obama, but their antipathy toward government is high.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/wisconsin-exit-poll-highlights/', 'snippet': 'Voters in the Wisconsin recall election would re-elect President Obama, but their antipathy toward government is high.', 'lead_paragraph': '10:03 p.m. | Updated The Times’s polling unit is parsing the exit polls in Wisconsin, looking for clues about the electorate and suggestions of what the recall results might portend for November. This post will be updated as we crunch more numbers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wisconsin Exit Poll Highlights', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T00:04:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Kopicki, Michael D. Shear and Dalia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kopicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29c317ac-ae4c-5ab6-a762-d3f408871f0a', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29c317ac-ae4c-5ab6-a762-d3f408871f0a'}, {'abstract': 'As Tiger Woods prepares for next week’s U.S. Open, his niece Cheyenne Woods will make her professional debut in this week’s L.P.G.A. Championship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/sports/golf/cheyenne-woods-tigers-niece-prepares-for-lpga-major.html', 'snippet': 'As Tiger Woods prepares for next week’s U.S. Open, his niece Cheyenne Woods will make her professional debut in this week’s L.P.G.A. Championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSFORD, N.Y. — When the name Woods moves up leader boards, rapt attention always follows. This week, a Woods most golf fans don’t know — Cheyenne — hopes to make her presence felt after accepting a sponsor’s exemption into the Wegmans L.P.G.A. Championship.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Woods Set for Major. Just Not That Woods. Or That Major.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Woods Set for Major. Not That Woods. Or That Major.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wake Forest University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Cheyenne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T00:09:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa D. Mickey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/765fbaac-60b9-5a6d-af1a-66f93ba6277e', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/765fbaac-60b9-5a6d-af1a-66f93ba6277e'}, {'abstract': 'One thing that the Wisconsin recall is unlikely to do is tell us much about how the presidential contest in the state will evolve in November.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/governors-races-can-be-a-contrary-indicator-for-presidential-elections/', 'snippet': 'One thing that the Wisconsin recall is unlikely to do is tell us much about how the presidential contest in the state will evolve in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The results of the recall election in Wisconsin on Tuesday night may tell us something about the future of the labor movement and the salience of collective bargaining rights as an issue to swing voters. A win by Gov. Scott Walker, who is ahead in the polls, might make other Republican governors who have sought to pare collective bargaining, like John Kasich of Ohio, breathe a little easier when they come up for election again.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Governors’ Races Can Be a Contrary Indicator for Presidential Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T00:10:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aa8189b-daff-5d02-ab55-2d6ed130e55d', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aa8189b-daff-5d02-ab55-2d6ed130e55d'}, {'abstract': 'Senators John McCain and Saxby Chambliss called for the appointment for a special counsel to investigate leaks in wake of recent articles in The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/05/senate-will-investigate-national-security-leaks-about-terrorism-kill-list/', 'snippet': 'Senators John McCain and Saxby Chambliss called for the appointment for a special counsel to investigate leaks in wake of recent articles in The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate will investigate recent national security leaks to the news media in the wake of articles in The New York Times about a “kill list” for terrorists and the use of cyberweapons against Iran, a Senate official said on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Will Investigate National Security Leaks About Terrorism ‘Kill List’', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chambliss, Saxby', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T00:12:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/304db8e7-a571-572b-8d6d-8d5ba0475a45', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/304db8e7-a571-572b-8d6d-8d5ba0475a45'}, {'abstract': 'Evolutionary biol