overnment Accountability Office has found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A yearlong investigation into a federal pension program for low-income veterans has concluded that weak oversight and unclear rules have made the system ripe for abuse, including by financial planners and lawyers who help well-off retirees qualify for benefits by transferring or hiding assets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Veterans Pension Program Is Being Abused, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Veterans Pension Program Is Being Abused, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T01:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e22d8cd2-d44d-5f9a-8e49-69c2a491b64b', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e22d8cd2-d44d-5f9a-8e49-69c2a491b64b'}, {'abstract': 'Efforts to increase and improve regulation of Wall Street have bogged down, and the Systemic Risk Council, formed by the Pew Charitable Trusts, intends to fight for better rules.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/business/new-systemic-risk-council-to-press-for-stricter-financial-regulations.html', 'snippet': 'Efforts to increase and improve regulation of Wall Street have bogged down, and the Systemic Risk Council, formed by the Pew Charitable Trusts, intends to fight for better rules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Efforts to increase and improve regulation of Wall Street have bogged down, according to Sheila C. Bair, the former chairwoman of the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation. On Wednesday, she will announce a new group, the Systemic Risk Council, that will monitor and encourage regulatory reform.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/Regulate/Regulate-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/Regulate/Regulate-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1995, 'width': 1795, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Group Forms to Urge Strict Oversight of Wall Street', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Group Forms To Urge Strict Oversight Of Wall St.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bair, Sheila C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Systemic Risk Council', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Charitable Trusts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T01:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname