-to-play, getting government to work. Nowhere in those books was there a word about casinos. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Governor and the Committee', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Governor and the Committee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genting Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Save New York', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T01:27:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba3c578a-ace3-574e-9616-9de1bb01588e', 'word_count': 569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba3c578a-ace3-574e-9616-9de1bb01588e'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney both governed in periods following economic slumps that weighed down statistics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/us/politics/obama-romney-and-economic-slumps.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama and Mitt Romney both governed in periods following economic slumps that weighed down statistics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Mitt Romney rarely misses an opportunity to chastise President Obama for blaming the country’s gloomy economic challenges on the situation he inherited from President George W. Bus