bject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T02:38:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Berman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/255521db-f33e-569d-bd93-e305498c4ea3', 'word_count': 858, 'uri': 'nyt://article/255521db-f33e-569d-bd93-e305498c4ea3'}, {'abstract': 'The Canadian pornographic actor suspected of dismembering and eating his former lover reveled in Paris and evaded police for days before he was caught in Berlin, authorities said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/world/africa/canada-dismemberment-suspect-will-not-oppose-his-extradition.html', 'snippet': 'The Canadian pornographic actor suspected of dismembering and eating his former lover reveled in Paris and evaded police for days before he was caught in Berlin, authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Police officers in Vancouver, British Columbia, said two parcels, one apparently containing a human hand and the other a human foot, arrived at two schools in the city on Tuesday. They said they had contacted the Montreal police to see if the packages were related to the killing of Jun Lin, a Chinese student. On Monday, the police in Berlin arrested a suspect in the killing, Luka Rocco Magnotta, who left Montreal for Europe over a week ago. Mr. Magnotta has agreed not to contest his extradition to Canada. Parcels containing another hand and foot were sent to the offices of two Canadian political parties last week. Montreal police said earlier on Tuesday that the victim’s head as well as a foot and a hand were still missing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: More Body Parts Turn Up', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: More Body Parts Turn Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magnotta, Luka Rocco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vancouver (British Columbia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Jun', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T02:41:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/877453ac-7945-507a-8602-f7ea6811e233', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/877453ac-7945-507a-8602-f7ea6811e233'}, {'abstract': 'It wasn’t clear if the audience was laughing with him or at him, but the classically trained Mr. Khil enjoyed the Internet acclaim his very sunny rendition of a wordless song brought him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/world/europe/eduard-khil-unlikely-youtube-sensation-dies-at-77.html', 'snippet': 'It wasn’t clear if the audience was laughing with him or at him, but the classically trained Mr. Khil enjoyed the Internet acclaim his very sunny rendition of a wordless song brought him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Eduard Khil, a Brezhnev-era balladeer who experienced an improbable and unwitting YouTube comeback as “Mr. Trololo,” tra-la-lah-ing his way through a song whose lyrics about the American prairie were eliminated because of fears of Soviet censorship, died on Monday in St. Petersburg, Russia. He was 77. ', 