ppy, With a Little Help From His Friends', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Umenyiora, Osi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T03:15:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36737595-e99e-53f2-82c4-44000ed4c8d1', 'word_count': 877, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36737595-e99e-53f2-82c4-44000ed4c8d1'}, {'abstract': 'Using talent and attitude, Tampa Bay has grown from a pushover to a power, leading a division in which all five teams are over .500.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/sports/baseball/tampa-bay-rays-sharp-rise-is-due-to-talent-and-attitude.html', 'snippet': 'Using talent and attitude, Tampa Bay has grown from a pushover to a power, leading a division in which all five teams are over .500.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tampa Bay Rays announced themselves, violently and with purpose, in the ninth inning of an exhibition game against the Yankees in March 2008. The franchise was still an annual loser when Tampa Bay’s Elliot Johnson barreled into catcher Francisco Cervelli at spring training. In so doing, he broke Cervelli’s wrist and broke down the doors of the American League East.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/sports/06kepner-maddon/06kepner-maddon-jumbo.jpg',