teady Approach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T04:01:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24faebb0-c367-5a1e-b2b8-b04aeae76eb8', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24faebb0-c367-5a1e-b2b8-b04aeae76eb8'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in three New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/word-of-the-day-deify/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in three New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'deify •\\ˈde-ə-ˌfi, ˈda-\\• verb ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | deify', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T04:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cbfa60f-e2c5-524e-93e1-ce0c9597f2d1', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cbfa60f-e2c5-524e-93e1-ce0c9597f2d1'}, {'abstract': 'A new survey finds that those without a college degree have dismal job prospects and considerable obstacles blocking improvement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/business/more-young-americans-out-of-high-school-are-also-out-of-work.html', 'snippet': 'A new survey finds that those without a college degree have dismal job prospects and considerable obstacles blocking improvement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For this generation of young people, the future looks bleak. Only one in six is working full time. Three out of five live with their parents or other relatives. A large majority — 73 percent — think they need more education to find a successful career, but only half of those say they will definitely enroll in the next few years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1464, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/business/06YOUTH/06YOUTH-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'More Young Americans Out of High School Are Also Out of Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Young Americans Out of High School Are Also Out of Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center for Workforce Development', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T04:05:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32df3385-a6d8-57c2-a37e-25fad2c6747c', 'word_count': 1012, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32df3385-a6d8-57c2-a37e-25fad2c6747c'}, {'abstract': 'The length of a prison stay increased by more than a third over the past two decades, a period of time in which the prison population doubled, according to a report by the Pew Center on the States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/us/average-prison-stay-grew-36-percent-in-two-decades.html', 'snippet': 'The length of a prison stay increased by more than a third over the past two decades, a period of time in which the prison population doubled, according to a report by the Pew Center on the States.', 'lead_paragraph': ' For petty offenders and violent criminals alike, the length of a prison stay increased by more than a third over the past two decades, a period of time in which the prison population doubled, according to a report by the Pew Center on the States. Inmates released from prison in 2009 spent an average of 2.9 years — or 36 percent — longer behind bars than offenders released in 1990, the report found. The additional time cost taxpayers more than $10 billion. In Florida, the average time served rose by 166 percent; in New York, 2 percent. Eight states showed decreases in the length of prison terms, according to the report, which analyzed data from the federal government’s National Corrections Reporting Program. Adam Gelb, director of the center’s Public Safety Performance Project, noted that the variation among states followed no evident regional pattern, reinforcing the idea that “state policy choices, often driven by particular crimes or circumstances in that state, drive the size and cost of the prison population, rather than data and research about what’s most effective in reducing crime.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Average Prison Stay Grew 36 Percent in Two Decades', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Criminal Justice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Average Prison Stay Grew 36 Percent In Two Decades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Center on the States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T04:13:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica Goode', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goode', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c548906-1da5-5767-8827-79fdc28fcf87', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c548906-1da5-5767-8827-79fdc28fcf87'}, {'abstract': 'Two prominent scientists involved have surrendered more than 3,000 of their private e-mails to BP in response to a subpoena by the United States District Court in New Orleans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/science/earth/louisiana-two-scientists-surrender-e-mail-to-bp.html', 'snippet': 'Two prominent scientists involved have surrendered more than 3,000 of their private e-mails to BP in response to a subpoena by the United States District Court in New Orleans.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two prominent scientists involved in estimating the flow rate from a ruptured oil well during BP’s 2010 oil spill in the Gulf of Mexico have surrendered more than 3,000 of their private e-mails to the company in response to a subpoena by the United States District Court in New Orleans. BP sought the e-mails from the scientists, Chris Reddy and Richard Camilli of the Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution in Massachusetts, to help prepare its defense in a lawsuit brought by the federal government. In an op-ed article in The Boston Globe, the scientists said they had given the company more than 50,000 pages of documents and data before the company also demanded the e-mails. They said they worried that BP would use the e-mails to falsely cast doubt on their conclusions. “Our concern is not simply invasion of privacy, but the erosion of the scientific deliberative process,” the scientists wrote. BP said the subpoena was “in no way an attack on science.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Two Scientists Surrender E-Mail to BP', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Two Scientists Surrender E-Mail To BP', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BP Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gulf of Mexico Oil Spill (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Woods Hole Oceanographic Institution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camilli, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reddy, Chris', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T04:17:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc8f7d76-a450-5a27-a9b7-850a9c98ce58', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc8f7d76-a450-5a27-a9b7-850a9c98ce58'}, {'abstract': 'Just days after word that the College Board would offer an unusual summertime SAT to students enrolled in a preparatory course conducted by the National Society for the Gifted & Talented, the plan has been dropped.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/education/college-board-drops-plans-for-summer-sat.html', 'snippet': 'Just days after word that the College Board would offer an unusual summertime SAT to students enrolled in a preparatory course conducted by the National Society for the Gifted & Talented, the plan has been dropped.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Just days after word that the College Board would offer an unusual summertime SAT to students enrolled in a preparatory course conducted by the National Society for the Gifted & Talented, the plan has been dropped. Critics complained that the Aug. 3 test was unfair, because only students enrolled in the $4,500 course, held on the Amherst College campus, could take it. The next general SAT test date is in October. The College Board initially said the August test was a pilot for summer t