fter Pill?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T09:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Murray and Ariha Setalvad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ariha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setalvad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8aa2d7bd-730a-512c-9494-39536ed9b4f2', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8aa2d7bd-730a-512c-9494-39536ed9b4f2'}, {'abstract': 'Opposition activists said as many as 78 civilians were killed by pro-government militiamen and security forces, as dozens of other countries sought to isolate President Bashar al-Assad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/world/middleeast/amid-reports-of-syria-massacre-nations-press-assad.html', 'snippet': 'Opposition activists said as many as 78 civilians were killed by pro-government militiamen and security forces, as dozens of other countries sought to isolate President Bashar al-Assad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Syrian opposition activists reported a mass killing of villagers by pro-government militiamen and security forces on Wednesday — if verified, the fourth massacre in less than two weeks — threatening to inject a new surge of angry momentum into the growing international effort to isolate President Bashar al-Assad and remove him from power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Reports of New Massacre, Nations Press Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amid Reports of a New Massacre, Nations Seek to Step Up Pressure on Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T09:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone and Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ea7fcb4-33dc-5fc3-b4cd-dc73619920c0', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ea7fcb4-33dc-5fc3-b4cd-dc73619920c0'}, {'abstract': 'A college counselor offers advice to rising seniors, including a summertime suggestion to “get a haircut and get a real job.”', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/counselors-calendar-june-juniors/', 'snippet': 'A college counselor offers advice to rising seniors, including a summertime suggestion to “get a haircut and get a real job.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March, The Choice introduced a series called Counselor’s Calendar, which is intended to keep students on track as they go through the admissions process. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Counselor’s Calendar | June Checklist for Juniors', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, '