'uri': 'nyt://article/7f6ddaee-ca08-5a64-bd44-a81b46b2166a'}, {'abstract': 'What we’re doing to America’s young.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/think-of-the-children-2/', 'snippet': 'What we’re doing to America’s young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time I hear some smug pundit or politician saying that we can’t spend to create jobs because that would be laying too much of a burden on our children, I get angry — because of reports like this:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Think of the Children', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T13:38:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37387ea7-2cca-54a7-b023-eca90e7cd929', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37387ea7-2cca-54a7-b023-eca90e7cd929'}, {'abstract': 'A Federal Reserve official’s remarks stirred hopes for stimulus, and the European Central Bank kept the door open to making a future cut to its main interest rate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'A Federal Reserve official’s remarks stirred hopes for stimulus, and the European Central Bank kept the door open to making a future cut to its main interest rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stocks surged on Wednesday as remarks from a Federal Reserve official stirred stimulus hopes and after stocks in Europe rose when the European Central Bank kept the door open to making a future cut to its benchmark interest rate.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stocks Jump After Central Bank Officials’ Remarks', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Central Banks’ Actions Help Buoy Markets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T13:39:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab8207e8-115a-5255-a1f5-dca4b318ba2b', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab8207e8-115a-5255-a1f5-dca4b318ba2b'}, {'abstract': 'Corning Museum of Glass announces expansion with new North Wing.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/museum-of-glass-to-get-new-wing/', 'snippet': 'Corning Museum of Glass announces expansion with new North Wing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Corning Museum of Glass in upstate New York will create a new north wing with a design by the architect firm Thomas Phifer and Partners that was unveiled on Wednesday. The 100,000-square-foot expansion includes new galleries for the museum’s contemporary glass collection and a large space for glassblowing demonstrations and glass design sessions. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corning Museum to Get New Wing', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corning Museum To Build New Wing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T13:56:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5294fefe-f6e7-5144-9586-dcfbd5cc2b03', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5294fefe-f6e7-5144-9586-dcfbd5cc2b03'}, {'abstract': 'Also, a big deal involving Taylor Swift will finally give labels and performers a cut of radio revenue.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/the-breakfast-meeting-warren-buffett-likes-newspapers-and-barbara-walters-apologizes/', 'snippet': 'Also, a big deal involving Taylor Swift will finally give labels and performers a cut of radio revenue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Taylor Swift and her record label may be reversing decades of music economics with a new deal struck with Clear Channel, the nation’s largest radio operator, writes Ben Sisario. The deal would give the label and performer royalties for traditional radio play — something the music business has long fought for and never received. In return, the label agreed to accept a cut for online radio play (which does award royalties to performers and labels), giving Clear Channel at least some measure of predictability in online payments. Online play is a tiny part of Clear Channel’s business but the company saw an opportunity to preemptively control costs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Warren Buffett Likes Newspapers, and Barbara Walters Apologizes', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buffett, Warren E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgan, Piers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sillerman, Robert F X', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swift, Taylor', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wald, Jonathan', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walters, Barbara', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clear Channel Communications Inc', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Columbia University', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lee Enterprises Inc', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Media General Inc', 'rank': 19, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Omaha World-Herald', 'rank': 20, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Post-Dispatch', 'rank': 21, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2c0f0d2-5643-586c-abba-3c61c85fc316', 'word_count': 529, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2c0f0d2-5643-586c-abba-3c61c85fc316'}, {'abstract': 'Iced coffee season is a time of polarizing debate among java connoisseurs: to brew cold or over ice?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/ristretto-i-dont-know-what-you-did-last-summer/', 'snippet': 'Iced coffee season is a time of polarizing debate among java connoisseurs: to brew cold or over ice?', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s iced coffee season, which in New York means hitting the cold brew.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | I Know What You Did Last Summer', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1842c3fb-9e25-5068-84db-20b01f50e0ca', 'word_count': 981, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1842c3fb-9e25-5068-84db-20b01f50e0ca'}, {'abstract': 'The new version of the Google Translate app is still free and includes new features for language learners.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/tip-of-the-week-translations-on-the-go/', 'snippet': 'The new version of the Google Translate app is still free and includes new features for language learners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you want to brush up your language skills for a European vacation or just take the slower pace of summer to learn something, the free Google Translate mobile app can be a useful tutor. The app, recently updated to match the Ice Cream Sandwich edition of the Android operating system, translates phrases spoken aloud in 17 languages and can translate typed text between 64 languages. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Translations on the Go', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Google Phone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:01:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/366e9a81-b2e2-5507-80fc-caf208d3ad9a', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/366e9a81-b2e2-5507-80fc-caf208d3ad9a'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/what-were-reading-451/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Observer: Why are moms, even after pregnancy, denied the pleasures of a good stiff drink? — Patrick Farrell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:09:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99b93f23-3dc4-5c7f-a926-c7968c03d646', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99b93f23-3dc4-5c7f-a926-c7968c03d646'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of the mismanagement of MF Global provides a damaging look at how the firm was pushed to collapse, but whether prosecutors have enough to pursue criminal charges is a different question.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/assessing-a-case-against-mf-global-executives/', 'snippet': 'An analysis of the mismanagement of MF Global provides a damaging look at how the firm was pushed to collapse, but whether prosecutors have enough to pursue criminal charges is a different question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much as the mythical Icarus plunged to his death after he flew too close to the sun, the trustee’s report on the demise of MF Global shows how the firm pushed the permissible uses of customer money to the edge until the firm collapsed. The question is whether prosecutors can build a criminal case or whether management stayed close enough to the line to avoid being charged.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assessing a Case Against MF Global Executives', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corzine, Jon S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giddens, James W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MF Global', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:12:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed4531d1-6ef4-5cae-9c0c-958c834136d0', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed4531d1-6ef4-5cae-9c0c-958c834136d0'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Baldwin argues that Kevin Costner duped him out of profiting from a lucrative deal to sell cleanup equipment to BP.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/on-our-radar-actors-spar-over-oil-spill-venture/', 'snippet': 'Stephen Baldwin argues that Kevin Costner duped him out of profiting from a lucrative deal to sell cleanup equipment to BP.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for the actors Kevin Costner and Stephen Baldwin face off in court over Mr. Baldwin’s assertion that Mr. Costner cheated him out of his share of a multimillion-dollar deal to sell oil cleanup devices to BP in 2010. [Reuters]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Actors Spar Over Oil Spill Venture', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:15:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/915649ba-0e50-54d2-a2f6-27b5a6f49c47', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/915649ba-0e50-54d2-a2f6-27b5a6f49c47'}, {'abstract': 'Most Americans have never heard of Katie Beckett. But because her mother persuaded Ronald Reagan to waive Medicaid rules on her behalf, my severely disabled son can be raised at home.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/because-of-katie-children-with-severe-disabilities-can-live-at-home/', 'snippet': 'Most Americans have never heard of Katie Beckett. But because her mother persuaded Ronald Reagan to waive Medicaid rules on her behalf, my severely disabled son can be raised at home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Katie Beckett died last month at age 34. Most Americans don’t know who she is. But as a parent of a child with disabilities, her name is as familiar as my own child’s. Because of the legislation that bears her name, hundreds of thousands of children, including my own, are able to be at home with their families instead of being institutionalized.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Because of Katie, Children With Severe Disabilities Can Live at Home', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckett, Katie', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:17:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Myung-Ok Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': 'Myung-ok', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4da95e8c-5014-593c-a34d-fde8fbe6d9a1', 'word_count': 982, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4da95e8c-5014-593c-a34d-fde8fbe6d9a1'}, {'abstract': 'High-speed videography is used to show how mosquitoes are able to fly in the rain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/science/100000001588378/mosquitoes-and-raindrops.html', 'snippet': 'High-speed videography is used to show how mosquitoes are able to fly in the rain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'High-speed videography is used to show how mosquitoes are able to fly in the rain.', 'sourc