TC One series phones might not be showy, but they are as pleasing to use as they are understated.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/two-htc-one-phones-both-pleasing/', 'snippet': 'The HTC One series phones might not be showy, but they are as pleasing to use as they are understated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HTC seems to have taken a page out of the Samsung playbook, with the release of its One Series phones: the One S and the One V.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two HTC One Phones, Both Pleasing', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two New Phones From HTC, Understated and Pleasing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HTC Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25d30ab6-305b-587d-b365-cc7c62001ea5', 'word_count': 642, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25d30ab6-305b-587d-b365-cc7c62001ea5'}, {'abstract': 'For father’s day, ties updated for hip dads, from Park & Bond; new dresses, in time for summer; and Pendleton prints on beach towels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/07/fashion/20120607-BROWSING.html', 'snippet': 'For father’s day, ties updated for hip dads, from Park & Bond; new dresses, in time for summer; and Pendleton prints on beach towels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For father’s day, ties updated for hip dads, from Park & Bond; new dresses, in time for summer; and Pendleton prints on beach towels.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/20120607-BROWSING-slide-MZOH/20120607-BROWSING-slide-MZOH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/20120607-BROWSING-slide-MZOH/20120607-BROWSING-slide-MZOH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping Snapshots: June 7', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Father's Day", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:52:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/26db4ce4-df26-5f70-92f1-199ba9dae894', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/26db4ce4-df26-5f70-92f1-199ba9dae894'}, {'abstract': 'An archaeological dig in London has unearthed remains of the Curtain Theater, which was home to the Lord Chamberlain’s Men from 1597 to 1599 and was the site where plays including “Romeo and Juliet” and possibly “Henry V” were first performed.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/early-theater-of-shakespeares-is-unearthed-in-london/', 'snippet': 'An archaeological dig in London has unearthed remains of the Curtain Theater, which was home to the Lord Chamberlain’s Men from 1597 to 1599 and was the site where plays including “Romeo and Juliet” and possibly “Henry V” were first performed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tomb of William Shakespeare in Stratford-on-Avon may warn the inquisitive (and the morbid) not “to digg the dust encloased heare,” but archaeologists who delved into the dirt in London have found what they say is a momentous site from that playwright’s career: the theater where Shakespeare plays, including “Romeo and Juliet” and possibly “Henry V,” were originally performed. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Early Theater of Shakespeare Is Unearthed in London', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Early Theater of Shakespeare Is Unearthed in London', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Globe Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:55:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/694e8dbe-0287-5d37-a3be-c14695fdaa5f', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/694e8dbe-0287-5d37-a3be-c14695fdaa5f'}, {'abstract': 'That China’s literati can be so blasé about their role in politics is a reminder of the dangers of optimism about the progress of freedom.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/chairman-mao-in-their-own-hand/', 'snippet': 'That China’s literati can be so blasé about their role in politics is a reminder of the dangers of optimism about the progress of freedom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — The past few days have brought some encouragement for observers of grassroots political mobilization in China. As June 4, the 23rd anniversary of the 1989 Tiananmen Square incident rolled around, the sheer variety of words and phrases that online censors have had to block is a heartening indicator of how hard Chinese netizens are pushing for political justice. (The microblogging platform Weibo even removed the candle icon, a common expression of mourning, from its selection of emoticons.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chairman Mao, in Their Own Hand', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Abrahamsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrahamsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac28fcd4-9450-57ae-9e49-a2ea42e21511', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac28fcd4-9450-57ae-9e49-a2ea42e21511'}, {'abstract': 'The Polish team is set to tackle Euro 2012 against historic odds, and with a lineup that has been criticized for not being authentically Polish.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/polands-diverse-euro-2012-team-endures-criticism-aims-high/', 'snippet': 'The Polish team is set to tackle Euro 2012 against historic odds, and with a lineup that has been criticized for not being authentically Polish.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My heart is Polish too,” said Damien Perquis, in French. “Sure, I don’t speak, but I’m a Polish guy too.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poland’s Diverse Euro 2012 Team Endures Criticism, Aims High', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:56:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Marcus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marcus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04b22f6b-e6a0-5937-b623-4db8ab66b945', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b22f6b-e6a0-5937-b623-4db8ab66b945'}, {'abstract': 'Do you need a credit card with a chip? How should you tell your bank you’re traveling? What should you learn before you land? Some money advice for foreign travel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/travel/money-tips-for-globe-trotters.html', 'snippet': 'Do you need a credit card with a chip? How should you tell your bank you’re traveling? What should you learn before you land? Some money advice for foreign travel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CREDIT cards and A.T.M.’s may have eased the challenge of spending and exchanging money on a trip abroad, but that doesn’t mean we don’t occasionally find ourselves in a foreign country, fuming in front of machines that have just rejected our plastic cards. Fortunately, American banks have recently begun issuing credit cards that are more widely accepted around the world. Here are some tips on managing your cards and cash based on my recent trip to Japan and Hong Kong. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10SUBPRAC/10SUBPRAC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 937, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10SUBPRAC/10SUBPRAC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1874, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10SUBPRAC/10SUBPRAC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10SUBPRAC/10SUBPRAC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10SUBPRAC/10SUBPRAC-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Money Tips for Globe-Trotters', 'kicker': 'Practical Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Money Tips for Globe-Trotters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debit Cards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T14:58:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Stellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f99656d1-c9bf-56ee-88fa-82dc34510579', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f99656d1-c9bf-56ee-88fa-82dc34510579'}, {'abstract': 'Sunscreens sprayed from a can, just like hairspray, paints and deodorants, are flammable in the seconds after they have been applied, experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/is-sunscreen-flammable/', 'snippet': 'Sunscreens sprayed from a can, just like hairspray, paints and deodorants, are flammable in the seconds after they have been applied, experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News that a Massachusetts man suffered severe burns while using a backyard grill — just after applying sunscreen spray — has raised new fears about sunscreen products. But dermatologists and burn experts called it a freak occurrence caused not by the sunscreen itself, but by the fact that the man was using an aerosol spray near an open flame.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/05wellsunscreen/05wellsunscreen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 272, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/05wellsunscreen/05wellsunscreen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 545, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/05wellsunscreen/05wellsunscreen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/science/05wellsunscreen/05wellsunscreen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/science/05wellsunscreen/05wellsunscreen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is Sunscreen Flammable?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunscreen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4eb809b1-5dab-501e-8ef6-bf224e5929ad', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4eb809b1-5dab-501e-8ef6-bf224e5929ad'}, {'abstract': 'New picture books about a young girl coping with her military father’s absence and about the rights of children everywhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/books/books-by-jill-biden-and-alain-serres.html', 'snippet': 'New picture books about a young girl coping with her military father’s absence and about the rights of children everywhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of us are more susceptible than others, but it’s not uncommon for picture book illustrations to give almost anyone — grown-ups even more perhaps than children — the goose bumps. And no one’s better at eliciting them than Raúl Colón (“Good-Bye, Havana! Hola, New York!,” “Angela and the Baby Jesus”). In “Don’t Forget, God Bless Our Troops,” his haunting image of a faded soldier standing outside an autumn window, as imagined by the daughter who awaits him at home, is nearly soaked in melancholy.\xa0“Daddy’s not here,”\xa0she thinks, “as she watches a red leaf drift past the window and out of sight.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/books/06childrens-img/06childrens-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/books/06childrens-img/06childrens-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/books/06childrens-img/06childrens-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/books/06childrens-img/06childrens-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/books/06childrens-img/06childrens-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/books/06childrens-img/06childrens-img-thumbStandard.