9a05-63e45bf3886d'}, {'abstract': 'Confusing economic comments — first by Bill Clinton, then by Lawrence Summers — have emboldened Republicans to say they have bipartisan backing for the extension of Bush-era tax cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/summers-comment-adds-to-confusion-over-extending-tax-cuts/', 'snippet': 'Confusing economic comments — first by Bill Clinton, then by Lawrence Summers — have emboldened Republicans to say they have bipartisan backing for the extension of Bush-era tax cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Visit msnbc.com for breaking news, world news, and news about the economy', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summers’s Comment Adds to Confusion Over Extending Tax Cuts', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Summers, Lawrence H', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:06:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0c7c134-283a-50ec-a407-550edf448110', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0c7c134-283a-50ec-a407-550edf448110'}, {'abstract': 'A new tool from NerdWallet lets users compare information about recent graduates from 60 colleges and universities.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/comparing-colleges-by-what-new-graduates-are-doing/', 'snippet': 'A new tool from NerdWallet lets users compare information about recent graduates from 60 colleges and universities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year, many colleges survey their imminent or new graduates about their plans for work or graduate school, and their starting salaries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Colleges by What New Graduates Are Doing', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NerdWallet LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:08:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae3addca-8b64-5574-9f25-66e58841e66b', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae3addca-8b64-5574-9f25-66e58841e66b'}, {'abstract': 'This you call triumph?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/estonian-rhapsdoy/', 'snippet': 'This you call triumph?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since Estonia has suddenly become the poster child for austerity defenders — they’re on the euro and they’re booming! — I thought it might be useful to have a picture of what we’re talking about. Here’s real GDP, from Eurostat:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Estonian Rhapsody', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:19:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d4de005-82f5-55bd-b03f-410818766908', 'word_count': 70, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d4de005-82f5-55bd-b03f-410818766908'}, {'abstract': 'The Boston Celtics have the will to win, and showed it against the Miami Heat on Tuesday. The Los Angeles Kings will have a chance to do the same on Wednesday against the Devils.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/sports/basketball/do-the-heat-have-heart.html', 'snippet': 'The Boston Celtics have the will to win, and showed it against the Miami Heat on Tuesday. The Los Angeles Kings will have a chance to do the same on Wednesday against the Devils.', 'lead_paragraph': "Such is the state of the LeBron James-fixated N.B.A. that now everything — in the Eastern Conference at least — appears to revolve around the axis of the Miami Heat. Whatever happens in any game, it becomes some sort of a reflection on the Heat and their drive for the mythical seven championships. Granted, this is much easier to do when they're in the Eastern Conference finals, so even when the Celtics stage a gritty, for-the-ages victory in Game 5, it was, of course, more about what the Heat did not do. And what the Heat are not. Perhaps what the Heat had for breakfast.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/basketball/07leadpic/07leadpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/basketball/07leadpic/07leadpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/basketball/07leadpic/07leadpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/basketball/07leadpic/07leadpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/basketball/07leadpic/07leadpic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do the Heat Have Heart?', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Herald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'del Potro, Juan Martin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quick, Jonathan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brodeur, Martin', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:21:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_d