bject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philip, Duke of Edinburgh', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:22:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4dbd830-bf93-59da-a7f8-3eaa506510f9', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4dbd830-bf93-59da-a7f8-3eaa506510f9'}, {'abstract': "A scene from Stephen Karam's play at the Laura Pels Theater. (Video courtesy of the Roundabout Theater Company.)", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/theater/100000001588933/excerpt-sons-of-the-prophet.html', 'snippet': "A scene from Stephen Karam's play at the Laura Pels Theater. (Video courtesy of the Roundabout Theater Company.)", 'lead_paragraph': "A scene from Stephen Karam's play at the Laura Pels Theater. (Video courtesy of the Roundabout Theater Company.)", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/arts/video-sons-of-the-prophet/video-sons-of-the-prophet-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/05/arts/video-sons-of-the-prophet/video-sons-of-the-prophet-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/05/arts/video-sons-of-the-prophet/video-sons-of-the-prophet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/05/arts/video-sons-of-the-prophet/video-sons-of-the-prophet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': "Excerpt: 'Sons of the Prophet'", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:25:47+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Roundabout Theater Company', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roundabout', 'middlename': 'Theater', 'lastname': 'Company', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/19c4b32c-3132-5fe4-a415-b5bcdc99b39f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/19c4b32c-3132-5fe4-a415-b5bcdc99b39f'}, {'abstract': 'One look from Ohne Titel’s flattering resort collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/just-one-look-ohne-titel-2/', 'snippet': 'One look from Ohne Titel’s flattering resort collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Ohne Titel yesterday morning, the designers Alexa Adams and Flora Gill showed a collection that seeks to flatter, above all else: the soft, dropped shoulder seams on knits show off pretty collarbones; the roomier skirts, like the one shown here, feature lines on the diagonal, which draw the eye in and against the outward curve of the hips. The color palette, which the designers called “acidic,” include muted mint (on a winning crocodile print cotton sweater with a matching skirt) and coral (the star of a color-blocked shirtdress). The message, which seems to be as much about lines and minimalism as accenting the best parts of a women’s body, is crystal clear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Ohne Titel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c29f7032-60c6-56eb-b246-0055900107ad', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c29f7032-60c6-56eb-b246-0055900107ad'}, {'abstract': 'True Ventures, a firm that focuses on early stage venture capital, has closed a new fund, despite continuing challenges in the broader industry.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/true-ventures-raises-205-million-fund/', 'snippet': 'True Ventures, a firm that focuses on early stage venture capital, has closed a new fund, despite continuing challenges in the broader industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While Facebook’s sagging stock price may have chilled investors’ appetite for rising technology start-ups, some venture capital firms continue to collect new money. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'True Ventures Raises $205 Million Fund', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Andreessen Horowitz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spark Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:40:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b14eef6c-2bd5-5cc3-91f7-6c1498467882', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b14eef6c-2bd5-5cc3-91f7-6c1498467882'}, {'abstract': 'What would Elmo’s best Olympic event be?', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/a-celebritys-drive-for-the-olympics-elmos-o-k/', 'snippet': 'What would Elmo’s best Olympic event be?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the big-name athletes vying for a spot in the London Olympics, perhaps none is bigger than Elmo. He’s got a loyal, young fan base that any N.B.A. player would covet, a Facebook page supporting his quest, and hopefully fireproof fur for his spin in the torch relay. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Celebrity’s Drive for the Olympics: ‘Elmo’s O.K.!’', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:43:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28f22931-405d-5a06-98ea-1acec70fdb7b', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28f22931-405d-5a06-98ea-1acec70fdb7b'}, {'abstract': 'I’ll Have Another drew Post 11 and was installed as the morning-line favorite when post positions were drawn Wednesday morning at Belmont Park for the 144th running of the Belmont Stakes.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/no-surprise-ill-have-another-morning-line-favorite-for-belmont/', 'snippet': 'I’ll Have Another drew Post 11 and was installed as the morning-line favorite when post positions were drawn Wednesday morning at Belmont Park for the 144th running of the Belmont Stakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Triple Crown hopeful I’ll Have Another drew Post 11 and was installed as the morning-line favorite when post positions were drawn Wednesday morning at Belmont Park for the 144th running of the Belmont Stakes. Replays of the draw can be seen on MSG Plus at 2:30 p.m., 6:30 p.m. and 10:00 p.m. Twelve horses are entered for Saturday’s Grade I, $1 million race. Belmont coverage begins at 4:30 p.m. Eastern on NBC; post time is set for 6:40 p.m.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Surprise: I’ll Have Another Is Morning-Line Favorite for Belmont', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85143a9a-dccd-5b9f-a194-83a8a1e9d46a', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85143a9a-dccd-5b9f-a194-83a8a1e9d46a'}, {'abstract': 'The campaign to oust Gov. Scott Walker was heavily aided by President Obama’s party, campaign and labor allies, but fell short against an organized, well-funded Republican apparatus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/us/politics/after-wisconsin-recall-defeat-democrats-assess-their-operation.html', 'snippet': 'The campaign to oust Gov. Scott Walker was heavily aided by President Obama’s party, campaign and labor allies, but fell short against an organized, well-funded Republican apparatus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As a laboratory of democracy, the battle to recall Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin had all of the messy pieces: a clash of armies on the ground, the influence of a vast amount of money and the broader context of an improving but still sagging economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/DEMS/DEMS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/us/DEMS/DEMS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/DEMS/DEMS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/DEMS/DEMS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking at Recall Vote as Drawing Lines for Fall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking at Recall Vote As Drawing Lines for Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T15:46:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a1b6fee-90db-59c2-a272-2a7b9e626159', 'word_count': 1258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a1b6fee-90db-59c2-a272-2a7b9e626159'}, {'abstract': 'New York and Orlando compete for the title of No. 1 tourist destination, International Yarn Bombing Day on Saturday promises, well, yarn, and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/morning-walkabout-66-orlando-vs-new-york-and-international-yarn-bombing-day/', 'snippet': 'New York and Orlando compete for the title of No. 1 tourist destination, International Yarn Bombing Day on Saturday promises, well, yarn, and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who’s No. 1 in Tourism? New York and Orlando were each claiming the crown as the country’s top tourist destination in 2011. But Orlando has released figures showing that it had 55 million visitors last year, while New York had 50.6 million. Still, New York’s tourism agency says that people don’t visit Orlando, they visit three different counties. We’re calling this one a draw. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning  Walkabout — 6/6: Orlando vs. New York, and International Yarn Bombing Day', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major