nippet': 'Noah Rubin of the U.S., who is unseeded, defeated Liam Brady of Britain to advance to the quarterfinals of the French Open junior boys championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Unseeded Noah Rubin of the United States surprised third-seeded Liam Broady of Britain, 6-2, 6-3, to reach the quarterfinals of the French Open junior boys championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In an Upset, Rubin Defeats Broady in Junior Boys Match', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McEnroe, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Townsend, Taylor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e58435d5-1906-5541-9c77-60f9c17aefee', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e58435d5-1906-5541-9c77-60f9c17aefee'}, {'abstract': 'A Gallicized twist on the utilitarian tote.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/the-get-morton-hudsons-tropez-tote/', 'snippet': 'A Gallicized twist on the utilitarian tote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unbleached canvas beach tote with contrast trim is an icon of summer style, a simple yet effective object that designers mess with at their peril. One who’s taken it on and come out ahead is Sydney Weinger of Morton & Hudson, whose linen-lined Tropez tote takes the utilitarian nature of the original and Gallicizes it (hence the reference to the French resort). Diagonal pleats in the canvas give the Tropez texture; leather trim in blue, moss or neon yellow provides a tiny splash of color; and the attached change purse has a practical life beyond towel-and-sunscreen duty. In short, a bag for all summers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Morton & Hudson’s Tropez Tote', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy MacDonell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacDonell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/479dcca3-0205-56a1-b63a-b14b0cdce738', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/479dcca3-0205-56a1-b63a-b14b0cdce738'}, {'abstract': 'Some 1,000 images of Depression-era America that were sent to the New York Public Library in the 1930s and ’40s are not in the Library of Congress. Read more on the Lens blog.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/an-archive-of-depression-era-images-re-emerges/', 'snippet': 'Some 1,000 images of Depression-era America that were sent to the New York Public Library in the 1930s and ’40s are not in the Library of Congress. Read more on the Lens blog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Farm Security Administration’s project to photograph life in Depression-era America yielded a national image archive of incomparable depth and breadth. Most of the images — 175,000 negatives and 1,600 color transparencies — are housed in the Library of Congress. But 41,000 prints were sent in the 1930s and ’40s to the New York Public Library, where they languished largely forgotten and uncataloged. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Archive of Depression-Era Images Re-emerges', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:36:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7bddd32-ba37-53de-9b2a-46b33a7cc414', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7bddd32-ba37-53de-9b2a-46b33a7cc414'}, {'abstract': 'It is a classic move made by the minority party – when things are going badly in a negotiation, tell those who lead to not leave Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/pelosi-to-boehner-dont-leave-town/', 'snippet': 'It is a classic move made by the minority party – when things are going badly in a negotiation, tell those who lead to not leave Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a classic move made by the minority party – when things are going badly in a negotiation, tell those who lead not to leave Washington.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pelosi to Boehner: Don’t Leave Town', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/895d82e9-2615-52e1-9071-17fe9f849347', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/895d82e9-2615-52e1-9071-17fe9f849347'}, {'abstract': 'What to make of Scott Walker’s victory?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/over-interpreting-wisconsin/', 'snippet': 'What to make of Scott Walker’s victory?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yesterday I said we shouldn’t over-interpret the gubernatorial recall election in Wisconsin. If they won, pro-recall forces would be wrong to assume that public sector pensions (and other benefits) are sacrosanct. Scott Walker supporters would be wrong to assume that Wisconsinites necessarily support an anti-union agenda – or more broadly his reckless slashing of government spending.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Over-Interpreting Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom (1953- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:47:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/831d67a3-b13b-5184-a4bd-bd6bd74eafe0', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/831d67a3-b13b-5184-a4bd-bd6bd74eafe0'}, {'abstract': 'This Poetry Pairing, our last one until September, matches Carl Sandburg’s 1914 classic “Chicago” with a 2012 New York Times article about the sprawling freight traffic jams in that city today.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/poetry-pairing-chicago/', 'snippet': 'This Poetry Pairing, our last one until September, matches Carl Sandburg’s 1914 classic “Chicago” with a 2012 New York Times article about the sprawling freight traffic jams in that city today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Poetry Pairing, our last one until September, matches Carl Sandburg’s 1914 classic “Chicago” with a 2012 New York Times article  about the sprawling freight traffic jams in that city today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetry Pairing | ‘Chicago’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:51:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e16ca83a-12ea-50d4-b064-d80d22bc0923', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e16ca83a-12ea-50d4-b064-d80d22bc0923'}, {'abstract': 'Vaughan Mitchell jumped into the Kill Van Kull with some friends and could not swim, the Fire Department said.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/15-year-old-drowns-off-staten-island/', 'snippet': 'Vaughan Mitchell jumped into the Kill Van Kull with some friends and could not swim, the Fire Department said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 15-year-old boy drowned off the north shore of Staten Island in the Kill Van Kull on Tuesday, the authorities said. The boy, Vaughan Mitchell, jumped into the water with some friends off the end of Jersey Street in the New Brighton neighborhood around 5 p.m. and could not swim, the Fire Department said. It took police divers and a fire boat an hour to find him. Vaughan was pronounced dead at Richmond University Medical Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '15-Year-Old Drowns Off Staten Island', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drownings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T16:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rhea Chedid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rhea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chedid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99c368d4-0d60-50c2-b831-f60e11fae482', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99c368d4-0d60-50c2-b831-f60e11fae482'}, {'abstract': '“Every time I feel like we’re in a comfortable position, something happens and we have to stretch even more,” said one of the She Owns It business group owners.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/comparing-notes-on-excess-inventory-and-other-small-business-problems/', 'snippet': '“Every time I feel like we’re in a comfortable position, something happens and we have to stretch even more,” said one of the She Owns It business group owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the last meeting of the She Owns It business group we introduced Deirdre Lord, an owner of The Megawatt Hour, and Beth Shaw, who owns YogaFit. Ms. Lord talked about a marketing opportunity that her company was scrambling to maximize, and Ms. Shaw shared her desire to get out of the apparel business and focus on education, her company’s core competency. Ideally, she would like to license the apparel side of her business. We also caught up with the other members of the group.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Comparing Notes on Excess Inventory (and Other Small-Business Problems)', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Proms Are Over, What About the Unsold Dresses?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adriana Gardella', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adriana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardella', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5ce9433-8bc1-56cf-91b1-8be18734bfbd', 'word_count': 1045, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5ce9433-8bc1-56cf-91b1-8be18734bfbd'}, {'abstract': 'The 17th annual Audie Awards were handed out at the New-York Historical Society on Tuesday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/audie-awards-celebrate-great-voices-not-famous-faces/', 'snippet': 'The 17th annual Audie Awards were handed out at the New-York Historical Society on Tuesday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The audiobook industry honored its best at the 17th annual Audie Awards gala on Tuesday night at the New-York Historical Society. Winners like Tina Fey, William Shatner and Jane Fonda weren’t there, but the stars of the audiobook world — narrators like Katherine Kellgren (seven nominations), Simon Vance and Dion Graham (four each) — were greeted with loud applause.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Audie Awards Celebrate Great Voices, Not Famous Faces', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank':