e', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/nyregion/06casino-span-sub/06casino-span-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/nyregion/06casino-span-sub/06casino-span-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/nyregion/06casino-span-sub/06casino-span-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2019, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gambling Group Lobbied for Convention Center at Cuomo Fund-Raiser', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Convention Project Tied to Cuomo Event', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Genting Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37bdda8b-3a8d-5170-8581-fd8249ac7585', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37bdda8b-3a8d-5170-8581-fd8249ac7585'}, {'abstract': 'The designer opened three stores in Istanbul recently, and it’s there that he went for inspiration for resort.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/just-one-look-michael-kors-3/', 'snippet': 'The designer opened three stores in Istanbul recently, and it’s there that he went for inspiration for resort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Kors opened three stores in Istanbul recently, and it’s there that he went for inspiration for resort. Coats as look changers, legginess (“women are really going for shorts,” Kors said during the presentation) and opulence through fabric (gold ikat shantung, lacquered python, fox fur and cashmere) were the collection’s key points. Most looks were shown with embellished flat sandals — “What makes it resort?” Kors asked the editors in attendance; “what’s on your feet,” he asserted — and small bags decorated with gemstones (“built-in jewelry”). Here, a most elegant panne velvet shift captures the group’s glamorous and easy attitude best.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Michael Kors', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fb9210a-491e-5ec1-9f6b-b55851fe4eab', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fb9210a-491e-5ec1-9f6b-b55851fe4eab'}, {'abstract': 'At the newly expanded Ugg store on Madison Avenue and 58th Street, preparations were underway to introduce what the company, well known for its shearling footwear, was describing as its first freestanding store for men.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/happy-hour-at-ugg/', 'snippet': 'At the newly expanded Ugg store on Madison Avenue and 58th Street, preparations were underway to introduce what the company, well known for its shearling footwear, was describing as its first freestanding store for men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Around 5 p.m. on Tuesday, inside the expanded Ugg store on Madison Avenue and 58th Street, preparations were underway to introduce what the company, well known for its shearling footwear, was describing as its first freestanding store for men. Actually, it’s attached to the two-year-old women’s store, but there’s a separate entrance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Hour at Ugg', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c351232-2d1e-5866-9f51-f435d92228c6', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c351232-2d1e-5866-9f51-f435d92228c6'}, {'abstract': 'Brooks and Collins argue fiercely about Wisconsin, Governor Walker, the Tea Party and President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/recall-of-the-wild/', 'snippet': 'Brooks and Collins argue fiercely about Wisconsin, Governor Walker, the Tea Party and President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: David I’m really sad about the results from Wisconsin. I can’t find a silver lining. You and I totally disagree about what this vote means, and my analysis is much more depressing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Recall of the Wild', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d31de15-2f9b-5e43-b6e4-c4a5e44a11c2', 'word_count': 1441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d31de15-2f9b-5e43-b6e4-c4a5e44a11c2'}, {'abstract': '“Take My Money, HBO!” is a Web page meant to encourage HBO to allow Internet-only subscriptions. Via Twitter, HBO indicated that it was better off keeping with its cable and satellite partners.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/hbo-says-no-for-now-to-fans-who-want-a-web-only-option/', 'snippet': '“Take My Money, HBO!” is a Web page meant to encourage HBO to allow Internet-only subscriptions. Via Twitter, HBO indicated that it was better off keeping with its cable and satellite partners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HBO doesn’t want your money, Web-only television viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HBO Says No, for Now, to Fans Who Want a Web-Only Option', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:37:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2254e92-b9e1-5c02-b6d5-0491876fac7c', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2254e92-b9e1-5c02-b6d5-0491876fac7c'}, {'abstract': 'The police have released the name and a photograph of a man wanted in three cases in Forest Hills in the last few weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/suspect-sought-in-queens-sex-attacks-and-robberies/', 'snippet': 'The police have released the name and a photograph of a man wanted in three cases in Forest Hills in the last few weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young man is wanted in connection with the recent sexual assaults and robberies of several women at knifepoint on the usually safe streets of Forest Hills, Queens, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect Sought in Queens Sex Attacks and Robberies', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Forest Hills (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Palmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Palmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69b16c9e-3b7c-5cd8-bf98-106505ba216b', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69b16c9e-3b7c-5cd8-bf98-106505ba216b'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Sharapova defeated Kaia Kanepi, 6-2, 6-3, in the French Open quarterfinals, and will next face Petra Kvitova.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/sports/tennis/sharapova-and-kvitova-advance-to-semifinals-at-french-open.html', 'snippet': 'Maria Sharapova defeated Kaia Kanepi, 6-2, 6-3, in the French Open quarterfinals, and will next face Petra Kvitova.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — For years, Maria Sharapova struggled on the red clay at the French Open, as if the court itself were a red light screaming at her to stand still. The alternative sometimes proved more embarrassing, at least initially. She ran so awkwardly, so rigidly, that she once compared her ungraceful movements here to that of a cow on ice.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07women/07women-jumbo.jpg'