aid to have begun kicking a ball before he could walk.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07soccer/07soccer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07soccer/07soccer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07soccer/07soccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07soccer/07soccer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07soccer/07soccer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Ukraine Striker, Ending Is Also a Beginning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Star Ukraine Striker Plans to Close One Chapter and Start a New One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Milan (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shevchenko, Andriy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:53:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeré Longman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3adadb8-34f6-57a7-88a9-7d7ed5bac511', 'word_count': 1186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3adadb8-34f6-57a7-88a9-7d7ed5bac511'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Cosey became best known for his work in Miles Davis’s electric band of 1973-75.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/arts/music/pete-cosey-guitarist-with-miles-davis-dies-at-68.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Cosey became best known for his work in Miles Davis’s electric band of 1973-75.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pete Cosey, a guitarist who played on many blues and R&B records in the 1960s but who became best known for his work in Miles Davis’s electric band of 1973-75, contributing a sound drenched in distortion and punctuated by the wah-wah pedal, died on May 30 in Chicago. He was 68.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/cosey/cosey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/cosey/cosey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/cosey/cosey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/cosey/cosey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/arts/cosey/cosey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pete Cosey, Guitarist With Miles Davis, Dies at 68', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pete Cosey, Guitarist With Miles Davis, Dies at 68', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cosey, Pete', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Miles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Ratliff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ratliff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/368ddf2d-9a27-5cb9-8eb0-b82f5ab852b4', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/368ddf2d-9a27-5cb9-8eb0-b82f5ab852b4'}, {'abstract': 'The former Texas-based official, who resigned over controversial remarks about punishing polluters, was expected to face tough questioning.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/former-e-p-a-official-pulls-out-of-house-hearing/', 'snippet': 'The former Texas-based official, who resigned over controversial remarks about punishing polluters, was expected to face tough questioning.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former Environmental Protection Agency official who stepped down this spring over controversial remarks he had made about punishing major polluters has sidestepped a grilling that he was expected to face on Wednesday at a House subcommittee hearing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former E.P.A. Official Pulls Out of House Hearing', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nuwer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nuwer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2eeae5aa-782c-5757-bfb7-94c1f527ebff', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2eeae5aa-782c-5757-bfb7-94c1f527ebff'}, {'abstract': 'Ulysses S. Grant almost quit the Army in June 1862. What made him change his mind?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/grant-on-the-edge/', 'snippet': 'Ulysses S. Grant almost quit the Army in June 1862. What made him change his mind?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early June 1862, a few days after Union forces captured the vital rail lines at Corinth, Miss., William Tecumseh Sherman sat chatting with Henry W. Halleck, his superior and commander of the victorious Yankee army. With elaborate casualness, Halleck mentioned that Ulysses S. Grant, another of his subordinates, was departing the next morning for 30 days’ leave. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grant on the Edge', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Ulysses S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman, William Tecumseh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tennessee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T17:58:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Bassett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bassett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0e1f8e3-a905-5b85-bf08-4a266516ac2e', 'word_count': 1547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0e1f8e3-a905-5b85-bf08-4a266516ac2e'}, {'abstract': 'The singer-songwriter said she went to a doctor after forgetting lyrics to a hit song.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/sheryl-crow-says-brain-tumor-has-affected-her-memory/', 'snippet': 'The singer-songwriter said she went to a doctor after forgetting lyrics to a hit song.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sheryl Crow, the singer and songwriter who has survived breast cancer, disclosed this week that she has a benign brain tumor that has affected her memory.\xa0\xa0 Ms. Crow, 50, mentioned her condition in offhand comments to an audience at a recent concert and her publicist later confirmed that she has a meningioma, a tumor common in middle-aged women that grows in thin layers of tissue around the brain and spinal cord, The Associated Press reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sheryl Crow Says Brain Tumor Has Affected Her Memory', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crow Says Brain Tumor Has Affected Her Memory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tumors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crow, Sheryl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:06:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01137b8f-05dd-5428-9523-f5c2eb2752c4', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01137b8f-05dd-5428-9523-f5c2eb2752c4'}, {'abstract': 'The Nasdaq OMX Group plans to set aside up to $40 million to settle disputes by investors over issues caused by technical glitches in Facebook’s initial public offering.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/nasdaq-sets-aside-40-million-to-settle-facebook-trading-claims/', 'snippet': 'The Nasdaq OMX Group plans to set aside up to $40 million to settle disputes by investors over issues caused by technical glitches in Facebook’s initial public offering.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:28 p.m. | Updated The Nasdaq OMX Group is taking its first step to quell investor anger over the flawed debut of Facebook shares last month — pledging $40 million to cover broker losses — but some customers and competitors quickly raised objections.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nasdaq Sets Aside $40 Million to Settle Facebook Claims', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nasdaq Sets Aside $40 Million for Facebook Claims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:08:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced and Nathaniel Popper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifi