ce their latest venture. | Tumblr’s founder shares his inspiration and mistakes. | Jenna Wortham checks out TaskRabbit, Pocketbooth and Uber.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/technology/100000001590118/timescast-tech-new-xbox-services.html', 'snippet': 'Napster’s founders introduce their latest venture. | Tumblr’s founder shares his inspiration and mistakes. | Jenna Wortham checks out TaskRabbit, Pocketbooth and Uber.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Napster’s founders introduce their latest venture. | Tumblr’s founder shares his inspiration and mistakes. | Jenna Wortham checks out TaskRabbit, Pocketbooth and Uber.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/multimedia/video-tech-120606/video-tech-120606-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/06/multimedia/video-tech-120606/video-tech-120606-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/multimedia/video-tech-120606/video-tech-120606-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/multimedia/video-tech-120606/video-tech-120606-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Tech: New Xbox Services', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airtime Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wortham, Jenna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grobart, Sam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:12:27+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'Jeremy Beiler, Emily B. Hager, Mac William Bishop, Channon Hodge, Pedro Rosado, Erik Olsen and David Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beiler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/61f92f51-61e8-5dd3-845c-7a81ace8287d', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/61f92f51-61e8-5dd3-845c-7a81ace8287d'}, {'abstract': 'Technology that allows the sharing of frequencies is getting new backing as smartphones and tablets put greater demand on available bands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/technology/as-wireless-spectrum-is-squeezed-sharing-is-seen-as-solution.html', 'snippet': 'Technology that allows the sharing of frequencies is getting new backing as smartphones and tablets put greater demand on available bands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cellphone carriers like AT&T and Verizon say they are worried about running out of the radio spectrum that carries wireless calls and data, and they want the government to give them more chunks of it. But a number of companies are developing technology that could change the whole spectrum game by using radio frequencies more efficiently. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 654, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1308, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/07SPECTRUM/07SPECTRUM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Companies Try to Create Room on Radio Spectrum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sharing the Air', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio Spectrum', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'xG Technology Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:12:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44e22314-eafd-5152-9fa7-a701d17cd646', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44e22314-eafd-5152-9fa7-a701d17cd646'}, {'abstract': 'There is something about peace and quiet that is good for the soul – even for a horse named Zenyatta.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/in-zenyattas-transition-a-life-lesson/', 'snippet': 'There is something about peace and quiet that is good for the soul – even for a horse named Zenyatta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I don’t even remember the drive from Louisville to Lexington. I do remember getting up before sunrise to watch the morning workouts at Churchill Downs. It was there I received a message asking if I was available to come to Lane’s End to visit Zenyatta and her colt. The next thing I knew, I was sitting in their reception area crying. When the Lane’s End bloodstock assistant Sarah Campion came in, she took one look at me, patted my arm and said knowingly: “I know; it’s always very emotional to see Zenyatta.” I stumbled on my reply and fled to the bathroom to repair myself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Zenyatta’s Transition, a Life Lesson', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Breeding of Animals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zenyatta (Race Horse)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:16:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie June Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'June', 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6ed03c3-08c5-5eef-9691-86afeaf9c9a1', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6ed03c3-08c5-5eef-9691-86afeaf9c9a1'}, {'abstract': 'Jo-Wilfried Tsonga has been successful when he plays aggressively, but against Novak Djokovic at the French Open, he seemed to abandon his offensive strategy.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/tsonga-played-it-safe-and-paid-a-price/', 'snippet': 'Jo-Wilfried Tsonga has been successful when he plays aggressively, but against Novak Djokovic at the French Open, he seemed to abandon his offensive strategy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jo-Wilfried Tsonga watches a replay of his gripping match with Novak Djokovic he will wince at his lack of aggressive play on his four match points in the fourth set. In much the same way he thwarted Roger Federer in the 2010 United States\xa0 Open semifinals, when he faced double match point at 4-5, 15-40 in the fifth set, Djokovic attacked. Like Federer, who twice chipped backhand returns on second serves, Tsonga elected to play it safe rather than hit out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tsonga Played It Safe, and Paid a Price', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsonga, Jo-Wilfried', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:32:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/247ee7cf-b97e-546f-9d85-e080a98f945f', 'word_count': 870, 'uri': 'nyt://article/247ee7cf-b97e-546f-9d85-e080a98f945f'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists see warning signs that the earth could be approaching a tipping point at which sweeping environmental changes threaten human welfare.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/are-we-nearing-a-planetary-boundary/', 'snippet': 'Scientists see warning signs that the earth could be approaching a tipping point at which sweeping environmental changes threaten human welfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The earth could be nearing a point at which sweeping environmental changes, possibly including mass extinctions, would undermine human welfare, 22 prominent biologists and ecologists warned on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Are We Nearing a Planetary Boundary?', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:39:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8988728-1d06-55b1-a179-ffda6d1d3332', 'word_count': 847, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8988728-1d06-55b1-a179-ffda6d1d3332'}, {'abstract': 'David Karp, Tumblr’s founder, shares his inspiration and mistakes on the inaugural episode of The Times’s weekly technology show. Also, Sam Grobart talks with Yusuf Mehdi, the chief marketing officer for Microsoft’s Interactive Entertainment Business; Napster’s founders introduce their latest venture; and Jenna Wortham checks out TaskRabbit, Pocketbooth and Uber.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/timescast-tech-speaking-with-tumblrs-founder/', 'snippet': 'David Karp, Tumblr’s founder, shares his inspiration and mistakes on the inaugural episode of The Times’s weekly technology show. Also, Sam Grobart talks with Yusuf Mehdi, the chief marketing officer for Microsoft’s Interactive Entertainment Busin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Karp, Tumblr’s founder, shares his inspiration and mistakes on the inaugural episode of The Times’s weekly technology show. Also, Sam Grobart talks with Yusuf Mehdi, the chief marketing officer for Microsoft’s Interactive Entertainment Business; Napster’s founders introduce their latest venture; and Jenna Wortham checks out TaskRabbit, Pocketbooth and Uber. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Tech: Speaking With Tumblr’s Founder', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Xbox (Video Game System)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karp, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tumblr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5f8aa82-6360-5183-a5a2-1a4e1ba88df5', 'word_count': 51, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5f8aa82-6360-5183-a5a2-1a4e1ba88df5'}, {'abstract': 'The new FX series “Legit” stars the Australian comedian Jim Jefferies as a comedian named Jim who hopes to lead a more reputable life.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/fx-orders-new-comedy-series-legit/', 'snippet': 'The new FX series “Legit” stars the Australian comedian Jim Jefferies as a comedian named Jim who hopes to lead a more reputable life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may be the network of spooky houses, lawmen with bad attitudes and bikers with even badder attitudes, but FX also wants to be known as the cable channel that makes you laugh: on Wednesday it added to its roster of scripted comedy series, saying it had picked up a new show called “Legit,” starring the Australian comedian Jim Jefferies. In “Legit,” Mr. Jefferies,\xa0 who created the series with Peter O’Fallon, plays a comedian named Jim who hopes “to become legitimate in life,” according to a release. The series also stars Dan Bakkedahl (of “The Daily Show”) as Jim’s best friend, Steve, and D.J. Qualls (“Hustle & Flow”) as Steve’s brother, Billy. FX is already the home of the comedy series “Louie,” about the life of the comedian Louis C. K., as well as “It’s Always Sunny in Philadelphia” and “Wilfred.” Later this month the channel will introduce the comedy series “Anger Management,” starring Charlie Sheen, and “Brand X,” a late-night series hosted by Russell Brand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'FX Orders New Comedy Series ‘Legit’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brand, Russell', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheen, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ed4cd4b-09f8-5b4e-bd19-5f6deda1d133', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ed4cd4b-09f8-5b4e-bd19-5f6deda1d133'}, {'abstract': 'Digital Domain Media Group has announced that it had entered a deal with Core Media Group to produce images of Elvis for a range of entertainment projects on film, television and at live venues.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/a-comeback-tour-for-a-ghostly-elvis/', 'snippet': 'Digital Domain Media Group has announced that it had entered a deal with Core Media Group to produce images of Elvis for a range of entertainment projects on film, television and at live venues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The special effects company that brought Tupac Shakur back to life in the form of a ghostly image on stage at the Coachella music festival says it has plans for a similar project with images of Elvis Presley, according to The Hollywood Reporter. The company, Digital Domain Media Group, has said it has entered a deal with Core Media Group to produce images of Presley for a range of entertainment projects on film, television and at live events. Core Media owns the rights to Presley’s image. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviving Elvis, Just Like Tupac', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviving Elvis, Just Like Tupac', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Presley, Elvis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakur, Tupac', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Core Media Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Digital Domain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T18:55:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ac8fc85-a000-5fc7-933c-7909045a5f09', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ac8fc85-a000-5fc7-933c-7909045a5f09'}, {'abstract': 'Barneys New York unveils its new window installations, with work by Juergen Teller and Viktor & Rolf.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/clothes-encounters-the-deste-fashion-collection-at-barneys/', 'snippet': 'Barneys New York unveils its new window installations, with work by Juergen Teller and Viktor & Rolf.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Clothes Encounters | The Deste Fashion Collection at Barneys', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/608a0edf-9dc0-515b-a6b8-ce4227bedb36', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/608a0edf-9dc0-515b-a6b8-ce4227bedb36'}, {'abstract': 'Encoded passwords for one out of 25 LinkedIn users were posted to a Russian hacker site. As hackers work to crack those passwords, LinkedIn users would do well to quickly change their log-in credentials. Here is the important thing to note if you are worried about your password being taken. You need to change the password not just for LinkedIn but for any other site where you used the same password.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/linkedin-was-breached-now-what/', 'snippet': 'Encoded passwords for one out of 25 LinkedIn users were posted to a Russian hacker site. As hackers work to crack those passwords, LinkedIn users would do well to quickly change their log-in credentials. Here is the important thing to note if you ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Security researchers have confirmed that a file containing 6.5 million encoded LinkedIn passwords has been posted to a Russian hacker site. LinkedIn has yet to confirm the breach, but it took to its Twitter account Wednesday to tell users it was investigating the matter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'LinkedIn Was Breached. Now What Do You Do?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palin, Sarah', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LinkedIn Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:02:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fff04c8-8f19-5b0a-9849-0dfc674fe0ba', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fff04c8-8f19-5b0a-9849-0dfc674fe0ba'}, {'abstract': 'The next season of “Downton Abbey” won’t be broadcast until January for American audiences, but fans of the show can visit the filming location now. Highclere Castle, a short train ride from London’s city center, has been the setting for the show’s scandal and intrigue since the first episode, and each summer the castle’s owners open the building and grounds to the public.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/downton-abbey-castle-is-open-to-tours/', 'snippet': 'The next season of “Downton Abbey” won’t be broadcast until January for American audiences, but fans of the show can visit the filming location now. Highclere Castle, a short train ride from London’s city center, has been the setting for the show’...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The next season of “Downton Abbey” won’t be broadcast until January for American audiences, but fans of the show can visit the filming location long before then.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Downton Abbey’ Castle Is Open to Tours', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palaces and Castles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Maggie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:05:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Rose Dobson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Dobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/163d9b41-c46f-5eb7-881a-1b7c3493bf3f', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/163d9b41-c46f-5eb7-881a-1b7c3493bf3f'}, {'abstract': 'The cabinet approved a hotly debated bill on Wednesday that gives parents of toddlers an allowance for keeping their children out of state-run day care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/world/europe/german-lawmakers-spar-over-child-care-subsidy.html', 'snippet': 'The cabinet approved a hotly debated bill on Wednesday that gives parents of toddlers an allowance for keeping their children out of state-run day care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Chancellor Angela Merkel’s cabinet approved a bill on Wednesday to provide parents of toddlers with an allowance for keeping their children out of state-run day care, a move that critics say would derail recent efforts to encourage German women to return to work after starting a family. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/world/07GERMANY/07GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/world/07GERMANY/07GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/world/07GERMANY/07GERMANY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/world/07GERMANY/07GERMANY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/world/07GERMANY/07GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/world/07GERMANY/07GERMANY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty