esire to fit in, gearing up for summer camp may now include visits to the \r\nsalon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOTS of tweens and teenagers are gearing up for sleep-away camp, making sure they have stocked up on a season’s worth of bathing suits, sunblock and bug spray. ', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07SKIN_SPAN/07SKIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07SKIN_SPAN/07SKIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07SKIN_SPAN/07zSKIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07SKIN_SPAN/07zSKIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07SKIN_SPAN/07SKIN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07SKIN_SPAN/07SKIN_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Off to Camp, but First ... a Wax?', 'kicker': 'Skin Deep', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Off to Camp, but First ... a Wax?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Felder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a3599ae-a2e3-55d1-a106-7d0616fc76a0', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a3599ae-a2e3-55d1-a106-7d0616fc76a0'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe we were right that Noomi Rapace has the lung capacity of a mermaid.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/how-long-can-you-hold-your-breath/', 'snippet': 'Maybe we were right that Noomi Rapace has the lung capacity of a mermaid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In describing Noomi Rapace’s underwater cover shoot recently, we wrote that the actor “was able to stay submerged for what seemed like minutes at a time.” And it did seem like that — so much so that our original words didn’t even include that “what seemed like.” But then a copy editor here, who obviously has no use for mermaids, raised a skeptical eyebrow at the claim that Rapace held her breath for minutes. So we added the qualifier.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Long Can You Hold Your Breath?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapace, Noomi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:31:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The photo department', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The photo department'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f0f6945-e6e7-525b-b210-f6371ae36d75', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f0f6945-e6e7-525b-b210-f6371ae36d75'}, {'abstract': 'Apple is expected to dump Google Maps from its operating system, in favor of its own product. In response, Google is showing off how much it has done in maps, and how many features it has. The message to Apple is, this will cost more and take longer than you think.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/google-schools-apple-on-maps/', 'snippet': 'Apple is expected to dump Google Maps from its operating system, in favor of its own product. In response, Google is showing off how much it has done in maps, and how many features it has. The message to Apple is, this will cost more and take long...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Google wants Apple, and the rest of us, to know just how expensive and hard it is to make good maps. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/technology/06bits-google/06bits-google-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/technology/06bits-google/06bits-google-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1104, 'width': 1262, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Schools Apple on Maps', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Maps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bedc7929-34cf-5d9d-bcaf-e059f2fa48e2', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bedc7929-34cf-5d9d-bcaf-e059f2fa48e2'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal is always evolving and improving. Against Nicolas Almagro at the French Open, he hit great backhands and won in straight sets.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/nadals-latest-weapon-a-backhand-down-the-line/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal is always evolving and improving. Against Nicolas Almagro at the French Open, he hit great backhands and won in straight sets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rafael Nadal speaks frequently about finding “solutions.” He continues to evolve, adapt, and improve his game, anticipating how his opponents will play him and adding new shots to keep them off balance. On Wednesday in his match against Nicolas Almagro, Nadal knew that Almagro would try to dominate play by ripping his heavy topspin forehand deep into Nadal’s backhand. If Almagro could make the match about his strength against Nadal’s weaker side, he would have his best chance at upsetting Nadal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nadal’s Latest Weapon: A Backhand Down the Line', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almagro, Nicolas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ae9789a-1274-57cc-b624-e022120dce3f', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ae9789a-1274-57cc-b624-e022120dce3f'}, {'abstract': 'Sunscreen manufacturers have tweaked formulas and labels, and have even discontinued products, to comply with a set of the coming Food and Drug Administration regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/fashion/trail-run.html', 'snippet': 'Sunscreen manufacturers have tweaked formulas and labels, and have even discontinued products, to comply with a set of the coming Food and Drug Administration regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EACH summer brings new and supposedly improved sunscreens, but this year’s really are quite different. With a set of the coming Food and Drug Administration regulations in mind, manufacturers have tweaked formulas and labels, and have even discontinued products, to comply. Words like “waterproof” and “sunblock,” which could give a false sense of protection, will be banned. Originally scheduled for this month, these requirements won’t take effect until December, but most new products already abide by them. Here are some possibilities for the sunny days ahead.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07TRIAL1/07zSUBTRIAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07TRIAL1/07zSUBTRIAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07TRIAL1/07TRIAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07TRIAL1/07TRIAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/07TRIAL1/07TRIAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Security Among the SPFs', 'kicker': 'Trial Run', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial Run', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sunscreen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Kiehl's", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:34:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Felder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Felder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e6f832c-d830-56f1-918c-9e3b91e3a2f1', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e6f832c-d830-56f1-918c-9e3b91e3a2f1'}, {'abstract': 'Judge Jed S. Rakoff asked a law student attending the insider trading trial of Rajat K. Gupta to stop sending him letters about the case.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/gupta-trial-judge-reprimands-law-student-spectator/', 'snippet': 'Judge Jed S. Rakoff asked a law student attending the insider trading trial of Rajat K. Gupta to stop sending him letters about the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judge Jed S. Rakoff asked a law student attending the insider trading trial of Rajat K. Gupta to stop sending him letters about the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gupta Trial Judge Reprimands Law Student Spectator', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Procter & Gamble Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:34:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28bd683a-f838-581d-b81b-e765a7b9ee9a', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28bd683a-f838-581d-b81b-e765a7b9ee9a'}, {'abstract': 'The intrusion of valley fever into the career of Conor Jackson now resides somewhere in the background of the struggles of the Mets’ Ike Davis, who has the disease but has not exhibited symptoms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/sports/baseball/slumps-of-conor-jackson-and-ike-davis-have-some-parallels.html', 'snippet': 'The intrusion of valley fever into the career of Conor Jackson now resides somewhere in the background of the struggles of the Mets’ Ike Davis, who has the disease but has not exhibited symptoms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Batting practice for the Class AAA Charlotte Knights had just finished on a steamy, hot afternoon in Fort Mill, S.C., when Conor Jackson emerged from the Knights Stadium clubhouse and took a seat in the dugout. It has been seven years since Jackson, 30, once a fixture in the Arizona Diamondbacks lineup, was a regular in the minor leagues.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07jackson/07jackson-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07jackson/07jackson-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07jackson/07jackson-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07jackson/07jackson-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/07jackson/07jackson-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Profound Slumps, With Some Parallels', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Profound Slumps, With Some Parallels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA DIAMONDBACKS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coccidioidomycosis (Valley Fever)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Conor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Ike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d51d74ac-0d15-5231-becb-f0da4e07bcc6', 'word_count': 1601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d51d74ac-0d15-5231-becb-f0da4e07bcc6'}, {'abstract': 'Sotheby’s files court papers to block a federal effort to seize an ancient statue on behalf of the government of Cambodia.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/auction-house-fights-seizure-of-statue/', 'snippet': 'Sotheby’s files court papers to block a federal effort to seize an ancient statue on behalf of the government of Cambodia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sotheby’s filed papers on Tuesday urging a federal judge to dismiss efforts by prosecutors to repatriate a 10th-century statue to Cambodia, contending that there is no proof that the sculpture had been stolen from its homeland.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Auction House Fights Seizure of Cambodian Statue', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sotheby’s Seeks Dismissal of Cambodian Statue Claim', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations and Restitution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:39:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Mashberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mashberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0064f29-7c82-5672-ac57-00b805311e3f', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0064f29-7c82-5672-ac57-00b805311e3f'}, {'abstract': 'VELObill, a software product that gathers all of the real-time data on your electricity, natural gas and water usage into one smartphone view, took first prize in the people’s choice category of the “Apps for Energy” contest.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/the-peoples-choice-an-all-in-one-mobile-utility-meter/', 'snippet': 'VELObill, a software product that gathers all of the real-time data on your electricity, natural gas and water usage into one smartphone view, took first prize in the people’s choice category of the “Apps for Energy” contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The people have spoken, choosing VELObill as their favorite app among the 50-plus entries in the Energy Department’s Apps for Energy contest. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The People’s Choice: An All-in-One, Mobile Utility Meter', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:40:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Witkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98a9fa3a-482c-56d6-94cf-0ed31c360f36', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98a9fa3a-482c-56d6-94cf-0ed31c360f36'}, {'abstract': 'More on that awful ECB decision.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/the-urge-to-punish/', 'snippet': 'More on that awful ECB decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been hearing various attempts to explain the ECB’s utterly bizarre refusal to cut interest rates despite soaring unemployment, sliding inflation, and on top of all that the special problems of a monetary union that probably can’t survive unless overall demand is strong. The most popular story seems to be that the ECB wants to “hold politicians’ feet to the fire”, letting them know that they won’t get relief unless they do what’s necessary (whatever that is).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Urge to Punish', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:47:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b74d9a56-fceb-54fc-82b9-8dc297ab3115', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b74d9a56-fceb-54fc-82b9-8dc297ab3115'}, {'abstract': 'Twitter’s chubby blue bird, with its playful tuft of feathers and disproportionately small wings, is out. In its place is a sleeker version with an upturned beak.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/as-twitter-matures-a-new-bird-emerges/', 'snippet': 'Twitter’s chubby blue bird, with its playful tuft of feathers and disproportionately small wings, is out. In its place is a sleeker version with an upturned beak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a start-up grows up, it often signals its maturation by hiring a new chief financial officer or filing a prospectus. For Twitter, growing up means a new logo.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Twitter Matures, a New Bird Emerges', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:49:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4ab227a-d607-5384-ae2c-253aebd797f3', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4ab227a-d607-5384-ae2c-253aebd797f3'}, {'abstract': 'From The Lively Morgue: July 4, 1952: Chicago. As part of its coverage of the Republican National Convention, The Times ran a full program and a chart showing the positions that delegates would occupy on the convention floor.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/from-the-lively-morgue-republican-national-convention-chicago-1952/', 'snippet': 'From The Lively Morgue: July 4, 1952: Chicago. As part of its coverage of the Republican National Convention, The Times ran a full program and a chart showing the positions that delegates would occupy on the convention floor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'July 4, 1952: Chicago. As part of its coverage of the Republican National Convention, The Times ran a full program and a chart showing the positions that delegates would occupy on the convention floor. Read more on The Lively Morgue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From The Lively Morgue: Republican National Convention, Chicago, 1952', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Republican National Convention', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:49:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7986803-1794-5994-8e2e-b63478d74bc1', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7986803-1794-5994-8e2e-b63478d74bc1'}, {'abstract': 'For surviving Hawaiian bird species, Hakalau Forest National Wildlife Refuge is both their final redoubt and a laboratory for the audacious possibility of recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/in-hakalau-a-modern-success-story/', 'snippet': 'For surviving Hawaiian bird species, Hakalau Forest National Wildlife Refuge is both their final redoubt and a laboratory for the audacious possibility of recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David J. Flaspohler, an avian ecologist and conservation biologist at Michigan Technological University, writes from Hawaii, where he is studying the influence of human activities on birds and the natural ecosystems that support them. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Hakalau, a Modern Success Story', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii (The Big Island)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By David J. Flaspohler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Flaspohler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a751bba0-503e-5da1-bbfb-f7a48b1b8803', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a751bba0-503e-5da1-bbfb-f7a48b1b8803'}, {'abstract': 'The average cost of a hard drive has risen to $66 from $51 after the flooding in Thailand closed factories late last year. The effects will continue to be felt into next year, says a technology research firm, I.H.S. iSuppli. Demand for the drives is strong, it said, despite an economic slowdown in Europe, India and China.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/after-flooding-stops-hard-drive-costs-continue-to-rise/', 'snippet': 'The average cost of a hard drive has risen to $66 from $51 after the flooding in Thailand closed factories late last year. The effects will continue to be felt into next year, says a technology research firm, I.H.S. iSuppli. Demand for the drives ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report issued by I.H.S. iSuppli, the research firm, found that last year’s extensive flooding in Thailand, where many hard drive components are made, will have a continued impact on the cost of computer drives into 2014.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Flooding Stops, Hard Drive Costs Continue to Rise', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:53:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e693499f-06dd-56c6-aacf-fdaba1c57ec9', 'word_count': 198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e693499f-06dd-56c6-aacf-fdaba1c57ec9'}, {'abstract': 'Alena Smith’s new play, “The Bad Guys,” displays an appreciation of the complicated mixture of honorable and dishonorable impulses in us (well, at least those of us who are guys).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/theater/reviews/the-bad-guys-by-alena-smith-at-mcginn-cazale-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Alena Smith’s new play, “The Bad Guys,” displays an appreciation of the complicated mixture of honorable and dishonorable impulses in us (well, at least those of us who are guys).', 'lead_paragraph': 'As you watch “The Bad Guys,” an absorbing one-act comedy-drama by Alena Smith at the McGinn/Cazale Theater, your opinion of just which characters should be classified as miscreants may shift from scene to scene. The cocky investment banker would seem a natural candidate, right? Hedge funds! Cue the booing and hissing. But then his loyalty to a childhood friend whose life has unraveled earns some sympathy. The drug dealer who freely admits to selling to kids certainly appears to qualify, at least until the moving speech in which he reveals that his illicit trade is the only bulwark between his extended family and abject poverty.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/sub-07bad1/sub-07bad1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boys Being Boys, With Beer and Guns', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boys Being Boys, With Beer and Guns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Alena', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Segal, Tobias', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Braun, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Second Stage Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Hal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T19:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dd3ec38-f41e-5ed3-bd1b-f77119061e0f', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dd3ec38-f41e-5ed3-bd1b-f77119061e0f'}, {'abstract': 'For resort, Max Osterweis and Erin Beatty show a sportier Suno: silk racer-back tank dresses and techy Lucite windbreakers.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/just-one-look-suno/', 'snippet': 'For resort, Max Osterweis and Erin Beatty show a sportier Suno: silk racer-back tank dresses and techy Lucite windbreakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This resort season, the Suno designers Max Osterweis and Erin Beatty expanded their collection to a total of 27 looks. They also showed a sportier Suno: silk racer-back tank dresses (in their signature mixed digital prints), techy Lucite windbreakers in colors like highlighter pink and lavender, and Suno-emblazoned graphic baseball tees. If you look closely at these boyishly boxy trousers and varsity jacket, you’ll see that the print is a basketball court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Suno', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T20:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename':