ek cover, which features a blurry sketch of a serial rapist and murderer, is creepier still. I read “People Who Eat Darkness” over the course of two days and always placed it face down in the kitchen, lest a glimpse of it unnerve the children and animals in the house. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1474, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dark Tale of Tokyo That Only Gets Darker', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dark Tale of Tokyo That Only Gets Darker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackman, Lucie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parry, Richard Lloyd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T20:39:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name'