r has announced the dates and hours of the upcoming New York run of the artist Christian Marclay’s “The Clock,” the popular 24-hour montage of clips from movies and television that depict particular minutes in the day, synchronized wi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April Lincoln Center announced that Christian Marclay’s much-loved “The Clock’’ — a 24-hour montage of clips from movies and television that depict particular minutes in the day, synchronized with the moment they are shown — is coming to Lincoln Center’s David Rubenstein Atrium, on Broadway between 62nd and 63rd Streets, where it will be shown free. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dates and Hours Announced for the Next New York Run of  ‘The Clock’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hours Are Set For ‘The Clock’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T21:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By CAROL VOGEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'VOGEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/960a32de-d75d-571c-ae12-cddb435e11c7', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/960a32de-d75d-571c-ae12-cddb435e11c7'}, {'abstract': 'Pictures from Italy, Bahrain, Afghanistan and Gaza.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/pictures-of-the-day-italy-and-elsewhere-8/', 'snippet': 'Pictures from Italy, Bahrain, Afghanistan and Gaza.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pictures from Italy, Bahrain, Afghanistan and Gaza.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Italy and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'