e': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff30f255-c39d-5bab-9b13-baf625284289', 'word_count': 974, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff30f255-c39d-5bab-9b13-baf625284289'}, {'abstract': 'John Patrick presents a fresh resort collection that included monochromatic nylon uniforms, which he called “not David Bowie ambiguous but pristine, healthy and active.”', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/just-one-look-organic-by-john-patrick-2/', 'snippet': 'John Patrick presents a fresh resort collection that included monochromatic nylon uniforms, which he called “not David Bowie ambiguous but pristine, healthy and active.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I kept thinking about the word ‘throwback’ and realized I don’t want to throw anything back,” said the designer John Patrick of Organic, whose resort collection was inspired by Edit DeAk and Walter Robinson’s 1970s zine Art-Rite. “I’m not watching Nick at Nite anymore. This is fresh.” To get fresh, Patrick showed color-pops of cobalt blue, recycled polyester slip dresses and skirts, classic daisy embroidered tunics in voluminous proportions and — wait for it — men’s wear. Monochromatic nylon uniforms were designed for everyone. “Designing men’s definitely made everything a bit more ambiguous for both,” said Patrick, pointing out this all-white sports-set shown with Roger Vivier kitten heels. “Not David Bowie ambiguous but pristine, healthy and active.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Organic by John Patrick', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T22:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edc95da2-70a3-5b55-8f4b-ff368424b33b', 'word_count': 120, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edc95da2-70a3-5b55-8f4b-ff368424b33b'}, {'abstract': 'The National Black Theater has resolved financial disputes that had threatened its future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/theater/national-black-theater-in-harlem-settles-disputes.html', 'snippet': 'The National Black Theater has resolved financial disputes that had threatened its future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Black Theater, a cultural fixture in Harlem that was in danger of losing its home, has resolved a series of financial disputes that had endangered its future. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/BLACK/BLACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/BLACK/BLACK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/BLACK/BLACK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/BLACK/BLACK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/BLACK/BLACK-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height