Scott Walker succeeded in breaking the political power of public unions and changed politics in a once-reliable blue state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Gov. Scott Walker moved to strip Wisconsin public employees of their collective-bargaining rights last year, a few weeks after taking office, it was clear that he wasn’t doing it to save the state money. If that had been the case, he would have accepted the unions’ agreement to pay far more in health care and pension costs. His real goal was political: to break the unions by demonizing their “bosses,” ending their ability even to collect dues and removing them as a source of money and energy for Democrats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Message From Wisconsin', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Message From Wisconsin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Governors Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barrett, Tom (1953- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T22:06:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_materi