New York Times Magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/ray-bradburys-wants-to-pass-on-a-message-from-jules-verne/', 'snippet': 'Remembrances from a 1955 issue of The New York Times Magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story begins with Ray Bradbury, stepping out of a time machine. From the misty distance emerges a man in a dark suit. It is Jules Verne, who has been dead for 50 years to the day. The conversation between one master of science fiction and another starts with the practical.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ray Bradbury Wants to Pass on a Message From Jules Verne', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradbury, Ray', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T22:07:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Henig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Henig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac3c01ba-b2c1-50d2-915d-a3106c3f4767', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac3c01ba-b2c1-50d2-915d-a3106c3f4767'}, {'abstract': 'Emeli Sandé, whose debut album is “Our Version of Events,” has many influences but a distinct sound of her own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/arts/music/emeli-sandes-our-version-of-events.html', 'snippet': 'Emeli Sandé, whose debut album is “Our Version of Events,” has many influences but a distinct sound of her own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The story of the recent British soul revival is the story of ghosts. Artists like Adele and Amy Winehouse succeeded as much because of the memories they conjured with their reference points as because of their talent. They had the familiarity of yesteryear on their sides. And given that they summoned styles dating back to Motown girl groups and Dusty Springfield, they had a lot of peoples’ yesteryears in their arsenal. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/EMELI/EMELI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/EMELI/EMELI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1819, 'width': 2031, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/EMELI/EMELI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/EMELI/EMELI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/arts/EMELI/EMELI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Singer With Many Influences but a Soul That’s Hers Alone', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Singer With Many Influences But a Soul That’s Hers Alone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sande, Emeli', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-06T22:09:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', '