'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T00:37:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6233eaf2-9170-51df-b971-1c40a2617ccb', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6233eaf2-9170-51df-b971-1c40a2617ccb'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors in the trial of Rajat K. Gupta, a former Goldman Sachs director, focused on a Galleon Group fund of funds that invested in Goldman.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/06/prosecutors-try-to-prove-incentive-for-insider-tips/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors in the trial of Rajat K. Gupta, a former Goldman Sachs director, focused on a Galleon Group fund of funds that invested in Goldman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of 2007, Rajat K. Gupta had an investment in a Galleon Group fund worth $16.4 million. Less than a year later, his stake in the fund was wiped out.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prosecutors Try to Prove Incentive for Insider Tips', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecutors Try to Prove Incentive for Insider Tips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T00:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93812ed9-83a8-5d66-b029-0f1879ccbe0e', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93812ed9-83a8-5d66-b029-0f1879ccbe0e'}, {'abstract': 'The mile-and-a-half distance of the Belmont Stakes, which has stopped 11 horses from winning the Triple Crown since Affirmed won in 1978, will be a daunting task for I’ll Have Another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/sports/belmont-stakes-will-be-a-long-ride-for-ill-have-another.html', 'snippet': 'The mile-and-a-half distance of the Belmont Stakes, which has stopped 11 horses from winning the Triple Crown since Affirmed won in 1978, will be a daunting task for I’ll Have Another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is in years like this one, with a Triple Crown on the line, that the Belmont Stakes truly lives up to its august nickname, the Test of the Champion. In more than a century of American horse racing, only 11 horses have passed this singular exam to earn their place among the sport’s immortals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/BELMONT1/BELMONT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/BELMONT1/BELMONT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1454, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/BELMONT1/BELMONT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/BELMONT1/BELMONT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/sports/BELMONT1/BELMONT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I’ll Have Another’s Long Ride', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’ll Have Another’s Long Ride', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gutierrez, Mario', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "I'll Have Another (Race Horse)", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T00:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa8171bf-cfdb-5282-8474-07d04479de6a', 'word_count': 1225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa8171bf-cfdb-5282-8474-07d04479de6a'}, {'abstract': 'Current and former White House officials have been traveling to Israel to discuss Iran, threatening more sanctions and stressing that the United States is prepared to use force if diplomacy fails.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/world/middleeast/us-continues-to-assure-israel-about-efforts-on-iran.html', 'snippet': 'Current and former White House officials have been traveling to Israel to discuss Iran, threatening more sanctions and stressing that the United States is prepared to use force if diplomacy fails.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama and his senior advisers have said little publicly about Iran since the resumption of negotiations over its nuclear program in April, preferring to let the diplomats hash out the issues in the hope that tensions with Tehran can be managed, at least until the election in November. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Aides in Israel Give Assurances About Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Aides In Israel Give Assurances About Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flournoy, Michele A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T00:57:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4633bd81-e2fd-58ae-8cb1-3c1f9b10a266', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4633bd81-e2fd-58ae-8cb1-3c1f9b10a266'}, {'abstract': 'For readers and writers, the more prizes the better, however they are structured, and let philosophy go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/opinion/prize-or-prejudice.html', 'snippet': 'For readers and writers, the more prizes the better, however they are structured, and let philosophy go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRITAIN’S prestigious Orange Prize, awarded exclusively for fiction by women writing in English without regard to nationality, has just now completed its 17th year. And while the prize is lauded for its international reach and has never been disparaged for choosing to bar translated work, once again the annual clamor erupts: how can such a circumscribed honor be deemed legitimate? Why only women? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prize or Prejudice', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prize or Prejudice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byatt, A S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T00:58:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cynthia Ozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cynthia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e66ffe58-d98d-5cd9-8a97-99d