 'snippet': 'Leaks about drones and cyberattacks, two weapons that by many accounts have devastated Al Qaeda and set back Iran’s nuclear effort, have angered lawmakers in both parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In recent years, the United States has pioneered the use of two innovative weapons, drones and cyberattacks, that by many accounts have devastated Al Qaeda and set back Iran’s nuclear effort.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Attacks, Online and From the Air, Fuel Secrecy Debate', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Renewing a Debate Over Secrecy, and Its Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T01:05:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/f10dd392-47c1-5c2c-a7e2-feaaa624f5db', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f10dd392-47c1-5c2c-a7e2-feaaa624f5db'}, {'abstract': 'The vast majority of candidates in Tuesday’s open, nonpartisan primary who advanced to the fall election were registered Republicans and Democrats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/us/politics/independents-falter-in-california-primary.html', 'snippet': 'The vast majority of candidates in Tuesday’s open, nonpartisan primary who advanced to the fall election were registered Republicans and Democrats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — For those who hoped that an open, nonpartisan primary in California would bring in a new wave of independent candidates and voters, Tuesday’s primary might have felt like a splash of cold water. Turnout remained stubbornly low, and the vast majority of candidates who advanced to the fall election were registered Republicans and Democrats.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/07nonpartisan/07nonpartisan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/07nonpartisan/07nonpartisan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/07nonpartisan/07nonpartisan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/us/07nonpartisan/07nonpartisan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/us/07nonpartisan/07nonpartisan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'California’s Nonpartisan Primary Sh