eduled to be executed Wednesday morning. Mr. Awkal, who was convicted of killing his estranged wife and brother-in-law in 1992, has a long history of severe mental illness and has been found mentally incompetent by three courts in the past 20 years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stay of Execution', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stay of Execution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awkal, Abdul Hamin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kasich, John R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eighth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T01:32:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/18118dbd-3e30-5c11-bd00-c613dcf89c8d', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18118dbd-3e30-5c11-bd00-c613dcf89c8d'}, {'abstract': 'The euro zone’s fourth-largest economy is too big to fail and possibly too big to steamroll, changing the balance of power in bargaining over a deal to rescue Spain’s ailing banks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/world/europe/spain-holds-a-trump-card-in-bank-bailout-talks.html', 'snippet': 'The euro zone’s fourth-largest economy is too big to fail and possibly too big to steamroll, changing the balance of power in bargaining over a deal to rescue Spain’s ailing banks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The bargaining has begun over a d