ject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T03:22:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf9d9b32-c5fc-552c-a8f8-2284588fe65c', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf9d9b32-c5fc-552c-a8f8-2284588fe65c'}, {'abstract': 'With the default rate steadily rising among the nation’s 36 million student loan borrowers, President Obama is seeking to ease the repayment process by streamlining enrollment in the income-based repayment program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/education/obama-seeks-to-clear-loan-repayment-roadblocks.html', 'snippet': 'With the default rate steadily rising among the nation’s 36 million student loan borrowers, President Obama is seeking to ease the repayment process by streamlining enrollment in the income-based repayment program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the default rate steadily rising among the nation’s 36 million student loan borrowers, President Obama is seeking to ease the repayment process by streamlining enrollment in the income-based repayment program, which helps low-income borrowers by capping monthly payments at 15 percent of their discretionary income, and 10 percent in 2014. Fewer than 700,000 borrowers are enrolled in the program, in part because registration is complicated. But beginning Sept. 30, Education Secretary Arne Duncan said Wednesday, most borrowers will be able to electronically import data directly from the Internal Revenue Service onto their application, letting them complete the application at one sitting, without going through their loan servicer. Mr. Duncan said the new process could avert “a significant percentage of defaults.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking to Clear Roadblocks to Loan Repayment', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeking To Clear Roadblocks To Loan Repayment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T03:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/86b32a4c-9f4f-5de3-9394-61317d3d398b', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86b32a4c-9f4f-5de3-9394-61317d3d398b'}, {'abstract': 'The police said Wednesday that they were confident that a hand and a foot mailed to two schools in Vancouver, British Columbia, came from a man who was killed and dismembered in Montreal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/world/americas/canada-police-link-body-parts-to-murder-victim-in-montreal.html', 'snippet': 'The police said Wednesday that they were confident that a hand and a foot mailed to two schools in Vancouver, British Columbia, came from a man who was killed and dismembered in Montreal.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The police said Wednesday that they were confident that a hand and a foot mailed to two schools in Vancouver, British Columbia, came from a man who was killed and dismembered in Montreal. The police in Montreal said the packages were mailed from that city, and other factors indicated that they were some of the remains of Lin Jun, a Chinese student. Luka Rocco Magnotta, a Montreal resident, is in a Berlin jail awaiting extradition to Canada on several charges, including first-degree murder. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Police Link Body Parts to Murder Victim in Montreal', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Police Link Body Parts To Murder Victim in Montreal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montreal (Quebec)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extradition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Magnotta, Luka Rocco', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T03:45:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5796708-d04f-54da-ba87-68ed56cf3bd3', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5796708-d04f-54da-ba87-68ed56cf3bd3'}, {'abstract': 'Several travel agencies in China said Wednesday that foreigners were banned from traveling to the Tibet Autonomous Region, the Chinese name for central Tibet, for at least June.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/world/asia/china-foreigners-barred-in-tibet.html', 'snippet': 'Several travel agencies in China said Wednesday that foreigners were banned from traveling to the Tibet Autonomous Region, the Chinese name for central Tibet, for at least June.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Several travel agencies in China said Wednesday that foreigners were banned from traveling to the Tibet Autonomous Region, the Chinese name for central Tibet, for at least June. The agencies said they had been told of the ban recently. One agency said the ban was expected to last until September, while another said there was a chance the ban could be lifted by July. In late May, two Tibetans set themselves on fire in front of the Jokhang, the holiest temple of Tibetan Buddhism, in the center of Lhasa, the Tibetan capital, to protest Chinese rule. One man died. Those self-immolations were among at least 38 that have taken place in Tibetan regions since 2009. Foreigners were barred from Tibet from late February to early April, a period that coincided with the anniversary of large protests against Chinese rule. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Foreigners Barred in Tibet', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Foreigners Barred in Tibet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel Restrictions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T03:47:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/451018d1-ea50-5502-aaa5-34d637271952', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/451018d1-ea50-5502-aaa5-34d637271952'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Ferkauf was the founder of the E. J. Korvette chain of discount department stores, whose 1950s strategy of low prices, quick turnover and high volume helped shape today’s retail landscape.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/business/eugene-ferkauf-founder-of-e-j-korvette-chain-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ferkauf was the founder of the E. J. Korvette chain of discount department stores, whose 1950s strategy of low prices, quick turnover and high volume helped shape today’s retail landscape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eugene Ferkauf, the founder of the E. J. Korvette chain of discount department stores, whose 1950s strategy of low prices, quick turnover and high volume helped shape today’s retail landscape, died on Tuesday at his home in Manhattan. He was 91. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/FERKAUF1-obit/FERKAUF1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/FERKAUF1-obit/FERKAUF1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1638, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/business/FERKAUF1-obit/FE