22ad5', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76f8443d-294f-5a09-a127-fc273ca22ad5'}, {'abstract': 'After accusations of conflict of interest, Chief Justice Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry said he would leave the panel looking into corruption allegations against his son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/world/asia/pakistans-chief-justice-leaves-panel-investigating-his-son.html', 'snippet': 'After accusations of conflict of interest, Chief Justice Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry said he would leave the panel looking into corruption allegations against his son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Amid accusations of conflict of interest, Pakistan’s chief justice announced on Thursday that he was removing himself from a panel investigating corruption accusations against his son and announced the formation of a two-member bench to look into the claims. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan’s Chief Justice Removes Himself From Panel Investigating His Son', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan’s Chief Justice Removes Himself From Panel Investigating His Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhry, Iftikhar Muhammad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T09:22:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5fb009e-9d85-5899-84c6-acb3dae988