ndy Wasserstein’s “Heidi Chronicles,” though that wasn’t intentional.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE day after my new play, “Rapture, Blister, Burn,” began previews Off Broadway I received a Facebook message from Wendy Wasserstein’s former assistant, a fellow playwright named Jenny Lyn Bader. Jenny had been in our first audience and wanted to tell me how much she had enjoyed the play. She said she wished Wendy were here to see me “taking up where ‘The Heidi Chronicles’ left off.” ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10GINA3/10GINA3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10GINA3/10GINA3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10GINA3/10GINA3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10GINA3/10GINA3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10GINA3/10GINA3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'All Hail ‘Heidi’: Beyond Feminism but Still a Dream', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'All Hail ‘Heidi’: Beyond Feminism But Still a Dream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wasserstein, Wendy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T15:18:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Gionfriddo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gionfriddo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ee92de1-f68c-5305-a85c-4016ce1eca57', 'word_count': 1548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ee92de1-f68c-5305-a85c-4016ce1eca57'}, {'abstract': 'After losing the Western Conference finals on Wednesday, the Spurs praised the Thunder’s incredible playoff run, including victories over Dallas and the Los Angeles Lakers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/sports/basketball/2012-nba-playoffs-spurs-tip-their-hats-to-the-thunder.html', 'snippet': 'After losing the Western Conference finals on Wednesday, the Spurs praised the Thunder’s incredible playoff run, including victories over Dallas and the Los Angeles Lakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OKLAHOMA CITY — The hug came as the clock struck zero and the roars and streamers inside the Chesapeake Energy Arena cascaded from the rafters. A week after they appeared invincible, time had run out on the San Antonio Spurs, and as Tim Duncan embraced Kevin Durant near midcourt, the Thunder’s future had officially begun. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/08spurs/08spurs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 793, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp