'nyt://article/a5c9d605-ba30-5963-87dd-1b4cb31db4f9'}, {'abstract': 'The German automaker is emphasizing plug-in hybrids over the purely electric vehicles with which the E-tron program initially was associated.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/in-audi-e-tron-program-pure-electrics-surrender-some-charge-to-plug-in-hybrids/', 'snippet': 'The German automaker is emphasizing plug-in hybrids over the purely electric vehicles with which the E-tron program initially was associated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reports circulated this week saying that Audi planned to jettison certain vehicles in its E-tron electric-vehicle program because of high development costs and low projected demand, particularly in Europe. The automaker, however, offers an alternative scenario: It couldn’t cancel the cars because their production plans never existed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Audi E-tron Program, Pure Electrics Surrender Some Charge to Plug-in Hybrids', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T15:37:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d1d9c0d-562f-5f34-a592-31ee2c3a24b1', 'word_count': 543, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d1d9c0d-562f-5f34-a592-31ee2c3a24b1'}, {'abstract':