'nyt://article/b1e2b9a1-7c47-5f3c-bf0e-1ff6d710b8be'}, {'abstract': 'A viewer revisits a single painting over a decade: Caravaggio’s “Denial of St. Peter,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/arts/design/caravaggio-denial-of-st-peter-met-museum-of-art.html', 'snippet': 'A viewer revisits a single painting over a decade: Caravaggio’s “Denial of St. Peter,” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years before he died, the Austrian novelist and playwright Thomas Bernhard wrote one of his funniest works, “Old Masters,” a bitter comic tale of a musicologist named Reger who has spent every other day for 30 years visiting the same room at the Kunsthistorisches Museum in Vienna, planting himself on the same settee and looking at the same portrait, “The White-Bearded Man,” by Tintoretto.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08FRAME_SPAN/08FRAME-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 109, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Painting Only You Can See', 'kicker': 'Frame', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Painting Only You Can See', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caravaggio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tintoretto', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernhard, Thomas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T17:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/992a577e-94b2-59d8-aa33-0b41b543eee7', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/992a577e-94b2-59d8-aa33-0b41b543eee7'}, {'abstract': 'The bill would eliminate direct payments to farm landowners, and replace those payments with a crop insurance subsidy, costing $3 billion a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/us/politics/farm-bill-advances-in-senate.html', 'snippet': 'The bill would eliminate direct payments to farm landowners, and replace those payments with a crop insurance subsidy, costing $3 billion a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate on Thursday voted to advance a farm bill that will set the nation’s nutrition and agriculture policy for the next five years. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Advances Farm Bill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senate Advances Farm Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crop Controls and Subsidies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T17:15:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f32cca75-6d8d-5eb3-a89a-6d6b33ea28c5', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f32cca75-6d8d-5eb3-a89a-6d6b33ea28c5'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Rick Scott won’t halt his purge of the Florida voter rolls. The Justice Department should go ahead and sue.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/so-sue-them/', 'snippet': 'Gov. Rick Scott won’t halt his purge of the Florida voter rolls. The Justice Department should go ahead and sue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Florida’s governor, Rick Scott, is itching for a fight with the Justice Department. As The Miami Herald reported on Wednesday, he’s refusing a federal demand to stop purging his state’s voter rolls. His office sent a defiant letter that, as the Herald put it, “all but dares the Justice Department to sue Florida.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'So Sue Them', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T17:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e2a6256-7ffd-5338-8768-5718362e3277', 'word_count': 471, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e2a6256-7ffd-5338-8768-5718362e3277'}, {'abstract': 'At an annual dinner on Thursday night, the Japan Society will formally announce that Miwako Tezuka, the associate curator at the Asia Society, has been named the new director of organization’s gallery, making her its first Japanese chief.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/japan-society-names-new-gallery-director/', 'snippet': 'At an annual dinner on Thursday night, the Japan Society will formally announce that Miwako Tezuka, the associate curator at the Asia Society, has been named the new director of organization’s gallery, making her its first Japanese chief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At an annual dinner on Thursday night the Japan Society will formally announce that Miwako Tezuka, the associate curator at the Asia Society, has been named the new director of the organization’s gallery, making her its first Japanese chief. The current director, Joe Earle, is retiring in September. “I am honored to join Japan Society and to work with its dedicated staff to create exciting exhibitions and related programming that stir the imaginations of the New York audience and people the world over,” Dr. Tezuka said in a statement. Motoatsu Sakurai, the president of the society, said, “Miwako is a well-regarded curator, who has an intimate knowledge of the New York art scene and a broad perspective of Japanese art in the global sphere.” The nonprofit Japan Society was set up to encourage mutual understanding between the United States and Japan, and its gallery has been mounting exhibitions since 1971.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Society Names New Gallery Director', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Society Names New Gallery Director', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sakurai, Motoatsu', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Japan Society', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T17:24:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13aa71df-076a-5fb5-a492-89c88ced6982', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13aa71df-076a-5fb5-a492-89c88ced6982'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors in New Jersey say the singer and actress failed to file tax returns in 2005, 2006 and 2007 when she earned more than $1.6 million.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/lauryn-hill-charged-with-tax-evasion/', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors in New Jersey say the singer and actress failed to file tax returns in 2005, 2006 and 2007 when she earned more than $1.6 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal prosecutors have charged the singer and actress Lauryn Hill with failing to file income tax returns for three years during which she earned more than $1.6 million.\xa0 Prosecutors in New Jersey said in a court document that Ms. Hill, an eight-time Grammy Award winner, did not file tax returns in 2005, 2006, and 2007, even though she owns and operates four corporations, tours as a musician and earns royalties from recordings and films she has made.\xa0 She is scheduled to appear before a magistrate in federal court in Newark on June 29 to answer the charges. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lauryn Hill Charged With Tax Evasion', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lauryn Hill Faces Tax Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hill, Lauryn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fugees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T17:25:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdcdb9f3-3740-5205-a990-f7c160eb2721', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdcdb9f3-3740-5205-a990-f7c160eb2721'}, {'abstract': 'United Nations observers say that they were prevented from entering the site of another reported massacre in Syria, and that government forces shot at them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/middleeast/100000001592374/un-observers-blocked-from-site.html', 'snippet': 'United Nations observers say that they were prevented from entering the site of another reported massacre in Syria, and that government forces shot at them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'United Nations observers say that they were prevented from entering the site of another reported massacre in Syria, and that government forces shot at them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/multimedia/video-tc-120607-syria/video-tc-120607-syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/07/multimedia/video-tc-120607-syria/video-tc-120607-syria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/multimedia/video-tc-120607-syria/video-tc-120607-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/07/multimedia/video-tc-120607-syria/video-tc-120607-syria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast | U.N. Observers Blocked', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ban Ki-moon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'maj