e': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bryans Reach Doubles Final', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T18:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4599ee-171f-5947-9078-1a54d6fe49ba', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4599ee-171f-5947-9078-1a54d6fe49ba'}, {'abstract': 'CW has become the first of the five big English-language broadcast television networks to complete the bulk of its advertising sales ahead of the 2012-13 season.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/the-cw-is-first-to-finish-upfront-sales/', 'snippet': 'CW has become the first of the five big English-language broadcast television networks to complete the bulk of its advertising sales ahead of the 2012-13 season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CW has become the first of the five big English-language broadcast television networks to complete the bulk of its advertising sales ahead of the 2012-13 season in what is known as the upfront market.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The CW Is the First to Finish ‘Upfront’ Sales', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Television Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T18:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e521fb2-3395-5eb3-9e81-ab5490f70ad3', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e521fb2-3395-5eb3-9e81-ab5490f70ad3'}, {'abstract': 'When Greeks return to the polls, the future of their participation in the euro — and perhaps the nature of the currency union itself — will hang in the balance. Niki Kitsantonis takes readers’ questions.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/ask-about-the-greek-elections/', 'snippet': 'When Greeks return to the polls, the future of their participation in the euro — and perhaps the nature of the currency union itself — will hang in the balance. Niki Kitsantonis takes readers’ questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greeks will return to the polls on Sunday, June 17, amid growing doubts about the euro’s viability in its current form, worries that Greece won’t be able pay its bills next month, and rising speculation about how the country would go about leaving the euro and starting to print its own currency. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ask About the Greek Elections', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden Dawn (Greece)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T18:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'bylin