over the long term, Spain will have trouble meeting its substantial financial requirements until foreign investors inject new money.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — While the Spanish government was able to sell all the bonds it wanted to on Thursday, it mostly sold to the usual buyers: Spain’s increasingly fragile banks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/business/08SPAINBOND/08SPAINBOND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/business/08SPAINBOND/08SPAINBOND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1586, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/business/08SPAINBOND/08SPAINBOND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/business/08SPAINBOND/08SPAINBOND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/business/08SPAINBOND/08SPAINBOND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Madrid Leans on Its Troubled Banks to Buy Its Bonds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grappling Globally With the Economy: In Spain, a Vicious Circle of Risky Bond Sales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g