ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b0877d8-7e59-5dae-a4f1-38404e728b40', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b0877d8-7e59-5dae-a4f1-38404e728b40'}, {'abstract': 'The brand’s new resort collection features wearable fashions with a mix of tweed, tie-dye and denim.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/just-one-look-proenza-schouler-2/', 'snippet': 'The brand’s new resort collection features wearable fashions with a mix of tweed, tie-dye and denim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Proenza Schouler designers Jack McCollough and Lazaro Hernandez ask themselves, which they often do, “How would our girl wear this?” 9 out of 10 times the answer is, “with jeans.” Proenza Schouler will open its first store this July on Madison Avenue, designed by the architect David Adjaye, who also did the showroom and offices. Resort finds McCollough and Hernandez not with their heads in the clouds on some fantasy surfing safari but thinking on their feet. In other words: “How are we going to keep our store filled?” The answer: wearable pieces steeped in the DNA of the brand, including tweeds (like the coat pictured here), tie-dyes, lace and, yes, an entire range of denim pieces “their girl” will definitely want to snatch up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Proenza Schouler', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T19:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30358233-5792-5fdf-8040-dd82852e03fa', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30358233-5792-5fdf-8040-dd82852e03fa'}, {'abstract': 'Sam the Bugler is as much a part of New York’s racetracks as the horses and jockeys.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/the-man-with-the-lips-that-call-fans-to-life/', 'snippet': 'Sam the Bugler is as much a part of New York’s racetracks as the horses and jockeys.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you have watched horse racing at Aqueduct, Belmont or Saratoga racetracks in the past 20 years, chances are good that you have heard Sam Grossman playing the flourish announcing each race on his three-foot-long trumpet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Man With the Lips That Call Race Fans to Life', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Racing Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T19:14:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab2f8acc-7d40-5eae-9595-4adf118d672b', 'word_count': 448, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab2f8acc-7d40-5eae-9595-4adf118d672b'}, {'abstract': 'The city announced the winners of a poetry and art competition related to water conservation.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/thoughts-on-water-from-young-new-yorkers/', 'snippet': 'The city announced the winners of a poetry and art competition related to water conservation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York City has announced the latest winner