own (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:06:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ef7fd2a-9b39-57c2-bb60-df6b7629b5d5', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ef7fd2a-9b39-57c2-bb60-df6b7629b5d5'}, {'abstract': 'The rules, known as Basel III, are intended to ensure that banks can survive financial shocks like the crisis in 2008, mostly by requiring them to raise more capital.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/the-fed-proposes-stronger-buffers-for-banks/', 'snippet': 'The rules, known as Basel III, are intended to ensure that banks can survive financial shocks like the crisis in 2008, mostly by requiring them to raise more capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Federal Reserve proposed on Thursday that the country’s banks adopt a broad package of international regulations aimed at making the global financial system more resilient to shocks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fed Wants U.S. Banks to Adhere to Stiffer International Rules', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fed Wants Stiffer Global Rules for Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Basel Committee on Banking Supervision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:08:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98bbc010-571a-5f9d-a088-0dbb1cf99a79', 'word_count': 525, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98bbc010-571a-5f9d-a088-0dbb1cf99a79'}, {'abstract': 'Charles Isherwood on some of his favorite YouTube clips of Tony Awards past.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/theater-talkback-numbers-that-stopped-the-show-on-tony-night/', 'snippet': 'Charles Isherwood on some of his favorite YouTube clips of Tony Awards past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tony Awards have promised us more live performances than ever this year, with even musicals that were shown little affection in the nominations, like “Godspell” and “Ghost,” getting their moment before the television audience. (The television audience that isn’t watching the finale of “Mad Men,” that is.) The long-since-shuttered “Hairspray” is reportedly being resurrected via cruise ship, so seasick-prone viewers should remember to take their Dramamine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Numbers That Stopped the Show on Tony Night', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isherwood, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27767a35-4dce-52c8-8ef6-c7a06fc3e898', 'word_count': 828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27767a35-4dce-52c8-8ef6-c7a06fc3e898'}, {'abstract': 'Joe Scarborough attacked The Times for running a story on Mitt Romney’s house in La Jolla.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/mitt-romney-his-money-and-identity-politics/', 'snippet': 'Joe Scarborough attacked The Times for running a story on Mitt Romney’s house in La Jolla.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier today, Joe Scarborough railed against a Times spread on Mitt Romney’s $12 million house in La Jolla, Calif. His particular gripe was that we didn’t give comparable coverage to John Kerry’s personal wealth in 2004. “Did The New York Times ever dispatch reporters to John Kerry’s homes, because John Kerry is worth a lot more money, obviously, than Mitt Romney?” Actually, we did. Here’s one. Here’s another. And another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mitt Romney, His Money and Identity Politics', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scarborough, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:11:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/683fbe81-0380-5a69-b457-2fd10dba9d42', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/683fbe81-0380-5a69-b457-2fd10dba9d42'}, {'abstract': 'The Dia Foundation, which maintains “The Lightning Field,” an outdoor installation in New Mexico, is getting help from a campaign to sustain the work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/arts/design/lightning-field-restoration-campaign-is-set.html', 'snippet': 'The Dia Foundation, which maintains “The Lightning Field,” an outdoor installation in New Mexico, is getting help from a campaign to sustain the work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Walter De Maria’s magical “Lightning Field,” in the remote desert of western New Mexico, is showing its age. Years of rough weather have damaged the work, which was commissioned by the Dia Foundation and completed in 1977.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08VOGEL1/08VOGEL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1189, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08VOGEL1/08VOGEL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1763, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08VOGEL1/08VOGEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08VOGEL1/08VOGEL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08VOGEL1/08VOGEL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 174, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaign Aims to Restore Weather-Abused ‘Lightning Field’', 'kicker': 'Inside Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Campaign A