lse pretenses to obtain internal documents from an institute that challenges climate science.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The water and climate expert Peter Gleick, a scientist who masqueraded as a board member of a conservative organization to gain access to its confidential financial information, has been reinstated as president of the Pacific Institute, the environmentally minded think tank that he founded. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Gleick Reinstated at Pacific Institute', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleick, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heartland Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:31:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcf28b9c-233b-5ed6-9700-6fd1f7b2a80c', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcf28b9c-233b-5ed6-9700-6fd1f7b2a80c'}, {'abstract': 'The State Department announced that it had authorized $33 million in rewards for information on the location of seven leaders of the Shabab militants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/world/africa/33-million-offered-in-search-for-shabab-in-somalia.html', 'snippet': 'The State Department announced that it had authorized $33 million in rewards for information on the location of seven leaders of the Shabab militants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NAIROBI, Kenya — The United States government announced on Thursday $33 million in rewards for in