, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfb4b27d-1621-58db-b013-75a8f2bc856e'}, {'abstract': 'The Boston Celtics were among the most turnover-prone teams in the N.B.A’s regular season, but have reinvented their offense through more careful playmaking and ball-handling.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/boston-redefines-its-offense-through-ball-control/', 'snippet': 'The Boston Celtics were among the most turnover-prone teams in the N.B.A’s regular season, but have reinvented their offense through more careful playmaking and ball-handling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Boston Celtics haven’t merely veered off script in the Eastern Conference finals, they’ve set its pages ablaze and scattered the ashes on South Beach. What looked to be a brief formality of a series has turned out to be anything but; not only have the mighty Miami Heat tumbled into a legitimate crisis, but the Celtics -– once a team far too lopsided to be considered a serious title contender -– have somehow created a stable, efficient offense out of thin air.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Redefines Its Offense Through Ball Control', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rondo, Rajon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:41:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2753af2c-a4c1-5a4e-9f5e-dc6a937a7ec9', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2753af2c-a4c1-5a4e-9f5e-dc6a937a7ec9'}, {'abstract': 'Should a former cleaning woman be confronted about jewelry that cannot be found?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/fashion/missing-jewelry-and-other-sticky-situations-social-qs.html', 'snippet': 'Should a former cleaning woman be confronted about jewelry that cannot be found?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my husband lost his job, I fired our once-a-week cleaning woman to streamline expenses. Since then, I’ve noticed that several pieces of expensive, irreplaceable jewelry belonging to my parents are missing. This woman continues to work for my neighbor, and I am tempted to cross the street and confront her. But I worry that I may be making a mistake, and the jewelry is hiding in an attic trunk or basement. Any suggestions?Barbara, Rockville Centre, N.Y. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im