r’s last stand before it cedes the smartphone battle to Apple and Google. But how are the phones selling? One estimate suggests that shipments so far are relatively small...', 'lead_paragraph': '6:44 p.m. | Updated\xa0 Adding clarification that the Lumia 900 began shipping last quarter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/03/26/technology/bitpix-nokia-lumia900/bitpix-nokia-lumia900-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'IDC Says Nokia Shipped 2.2 Million Lumia Phones Last Quarter', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nokia Oyj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:51:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9638a21-ebcc-520d-9443-49c149d99e72', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9638a21-ebcc-520d-9443-49c149d99e72'}, {'abstract': 'If the neighborhood kids are crashing your parties, it’s fine (and right) to speak up.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/when-its-time-for-the-neighborhood-children-to-go-home/', 'snippet': 'If the neighborhood kids are crashing your parties, it’s fine (and right) to speak up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just say it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When It’s Time for the Neighborhood Children to Go Home', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:54:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/538b2cf3-2223-5c8a-a29e-ae784ba02958', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/538b2cf3-2223-5c8a-a29e-ae784ba02958'}, {'abstract': 'The chef of fine-dining shrines like Marea and Ai Fiori is opening a pizzeria next week in the East Village.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/nicoletta-a-lower-crust-option-from-michael-white/', 'snippet': 'The chef of fine-dining shrines like Marea and Ai Fiori is opening a pizzeria next week in the East Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chef Michael White’s attachment to Wisconsin pizza goes back to his childhood. He said his first restaurant job was at a pizzeria in his hometown, Beloit, Wis., when he was 16. But his father, Gerry White, who is in New York this week from Beloit, said he recalled that his son, who is now 40, hung around the place when he was maybe just 6. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nicoletta, a Lower-Crust Option from Michael White', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T20:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5cce040-bd5d-54b9-9806-cd33e11903f4', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5cce040-bd5d-54b9-9806-cd33e11903f4'}, {'abstract': 'The brand’s new resort collection is filled with clever reinterpretations of its principle staple, the Trialmaster racing jacket.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/just-one-look-belstaff-2/', 'snippet': 'The brand’s new resort collection is filled with clever reinterpretations of its principle staple, the Trialmaster racing jacket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is Belstaff the next Burberry? That seems to be the driving ambition at the English company whose heritage rests on the shoulders of a single piece of outerwear, the Trialmaster racing jacket. But the designer Martin Cooper (who happens to be a Burberry alum) has already gone a considerable distance with the brand in a short time. Using the crosshatch pattern on the original jacket’s hardware as a leitmotif, Cooper turned out a resort collection full of clever riffs on the Trialmaster — as a snappy linen jacket, say, or a fitted dress — that will get fashion motors running without any trouble at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Belstaff', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76212558-cfa3-5bc6-80e8-39d0f316069d', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76212558-cfa3-5bc6-80e8-39d0f316069d'}, {'abstract': 'Fans lined up early and often for signed books at this year’s publishing industry convention.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/among-the-autograph-hounds-at-bea/', 'snippet': 'Fans lined up early and often for signed books at this year’s publishing industry convention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thursday, the last day of BookExpo America, the publishing industry’s annual convention, is a relatively light day for author appearances, but the autograph area this morning still looked like a LaGuardia departure lounge during a blizzard. More than half of those in the long, snaking line to meet Kristin Cashore, the author of “Bitterblue,” were seated on the floor, biding their time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Among the Autograph Hounds at BEA', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'BookExpo America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27c3e7c7-3cc3-5b09-84a7-28cdd5f494d3', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27c3e7c7-3cc3-5b09-84a7-28cdd5f494d3'}, {'abstract': 'With Reagan-Obama comparisons.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/real-government-spending-per-capita/', 'snippet': 'With Reagan-Obama comparisons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A followup, for the purposes of a project I’m working on, on this post about falling government spending recently. Here are two figures, both in natural logs: overall real government spending per capita, and state and local real government spending per capita, this time in levels rather than changes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Real Government Spending Per Capita', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:08:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f820ef58-6d4e-5ba9-892b-481090223a94', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f820ef58-6d4e-5ba9-892b-481090223a94'}, {'abstract': 'In “Bel Ami,” an adaptation of the Guy de Maupassant novel, Robert Pattinson plays a manipulative journalist who rises through Belle Époque Paris by exploiting a series of women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/movies/bel-ami-from-maupassant-novel-with-robert-pattinson.html', 'snippet': 'In “Bel Ami,” an adaptation of the Guy de Maupassant novel, Robert Pattinson plays a manipulative journalist who rises through Belle Époque Paris by exploiting a series of women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Georges Duroy, the coldblooded social climber who seduces his way to the top of Gallic society in Guy de Maupassant’s 1885 novel, “Bel Ami,” is one of the nastiest pieces of work in French literature. But Robert Pattinson, who plays Georges in the novel’s latest English-language adaptation, seems stuck in the land of “Twilight.” Lowering your gaze and flashing a vampirish glare is not acting, it’s making faces. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08BELAMI_SPAN/08BELAMI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08BELAMI_SPAN/08BELAMI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08BELAMI_SPAN/08BELAMI_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08BELAMI_SPAN/08BELAMI_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08BELAMI_SPAN/08BELAMI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08BELAMI_SPAN/08BELAMI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Parisian Journalist’s Ruthless Liaisons', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Parisian Journalist’s Ruthless Liaisons', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pattinson, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott Thomas, Kristin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ricci, Christina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thurman, Uma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bel Ami (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donnellan, Declan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ormerod, Nick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a46a8d16-2608-59d6-b08d-67d7142b0fc2', 'word_count': 664, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a46a8d16-2608-59d6-b08d-67d7142b0fc2'}, {'abstract': 'Resort 2013', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/07/fashion/ReedKrakoffResort2013.html', 'snippet': 'Resort 2013', 'lead_paragraph': 'Resort 2013', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/ReedKrakoffResort2013-slide-6ZYW/ReedKrakoffResort2013-slide-6ZYW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/07/fashion/ReedKrakoffResort2013-slide-6ZYW/ReedKrakoffResort2013-slide-6ZYW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reed Krakoff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krakoff, Reed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:14:44+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/31119bba-6b70-5a9f-b0cc-ae0ab52b9547', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/31119bba-6b70-5a9f-b0cc-ae0ab52b9547'}, {'abstract': 'After snacking on fried octopus balls, go shopping and wind up floating high above the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/10/travel/10OSAKA.html', 'snippet': 'After snacking on fried octopus balls, go shopping and wind up floating high above the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After snacking on fried octopus balls, go shopping and wind up floating high above the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T/10OSAKA-slide-DX5T-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spin Around Osaka, Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Osaka (Japan)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/95478cee-07ce-574e-a355-22b84dc22e52', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/95478cee-07ce-574e-a355-22b84dc22e52'}, {'abstract': 'In Japan’s third-largest city, you can view noodles in a museum, see Tigers play baseball, gaze at aquatic creatures (real and fake) and grab a drink at Beer Belly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/travel/36-hours-in-osaka-japan.html', 'snippet': 'In Japan’s third-largest city, you can view noodles in a museum, see Tigers play baseball, gaze at aquatic creatures (real and fake) and grab a drink at Beer Belly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OSAKA’S concrete canyons and elevated freeways will never win the city any urban beauty contests. But when the ethos of a place is kuidaore — the concept of eating oneself bankrupt — aesthetics don’t much matter. Fittingly, Japan’s third-largest city has no shortage of fine-dining establishments (the city now boasts 108 total Michelin stars, including five three-star restaurants); but the convivial, freewheeling local food culture can just as easily be tapped into at the inexpensive food stalls that line the recently renovated banks of the Dotonbori canal. And when the belly-busting glut becomes too much, Osaka’s top-notch museums and urban parks provide welcome, necessary respite.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10HOURS_SPAN/10HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 495, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10HOURS_SPAN/10HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 495}}, {'rank': 0, 'su