'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a80a0d20-efa3-5e5f-9961-0cb7f4635cb9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a80a0d20-efa3-5e5f-9961-0cb7f4635cb9'}, {'abstract': 'The budgets for each public school that arrive each spring, dictating the degree of austerity for the following year, are almost never seen by parents. They are not pretty, most principals would agree, and they have grown increasingly complicated in the last few years.  Yet parents, as well as their children, soon feel the consequences, as schools turn to the families for everything from donations of toilet paper and hand sanitizers to money, which can total thousands of dollars, to fill gaps in staffing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/07/a-complex-budget-picture-feeds-reliance-on-parent-donations/', 'snippet': 'The budgets for each public school that arrive each spring, dictating the degree of austerity for the following year, are almost never seen by parents. They are not pretty, most principals would agree, and they have grown increasingly complicated ...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Complex Budget Picture Feeds Reliance on Parent Donations', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:20:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By ANNA M. PHILLIPS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee42f17c-461d-5e7d-9ae6-fbc5a5bb17a8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee42f17c-461d-5e7d-9ae6-fbc5a5bb17a8'}, {'abstract': 'Young performers take the spotlight in the annual workshop performances of the School of American Ballet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/arts/dance/school-of-american-ballet-at-peter-jay-sharp-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Young performers take the spotlight in the annual workshop performances of the School of American Ballet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the School of American Ballet Workshop Performances on Tuesday evening the sight of young dancers eating up the stage made a strong case for ballet as the province of their age. Still, the annual performances aren’t only about spotlighting the next generation of talent; they also allow audiences to see repertory with new eyes. At the school, affiliated with New York City Ballet, performances of Balanchine works usually come with a little extra snap and crackle.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08WORKSHOP/WORKSHOP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 808, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08WORKSHOP/WORKSHOP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1617, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08WORKSHOP/08WORKSHOP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08WORKSHOP/08WORKSHOP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08WORKSHOP/08WORKSHOP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Youthful Training Gets a Payoff Moment', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Youthful Training Gets a Payoff Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'School of American Ballet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:20:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/259e10bb-5767-5b70-8cce-112fdc6d9d0d', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/259e10bb-5767-5b70-8cce-112fdc6d9d0d'}, {'abstract': 'Several works in an exhibition organized by the Public Art Fund in City Hall Park, near Zuccotti Park where Occupy Wall Street encamped, address issues of free speech and protest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/arts/design/common-ground-at-city-hall-park.html', 'snippet': 'Several works in an exhibition organized by the Public Art Fund in City Hall Park, near Zuccotti Park where Occupy Wall Street encamped, address issues of free speech and protest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve been living out of town for the last year — perhaps on a different planet — you might need some back story before heading down to see “Common Ground,” an exhibition of outdoor sculpture and performance by 10 international artists in City Hall Park.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ