olition of Medicare and Medicaid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Washington Doesn’t Get Us’', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T21:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0576311-6e15-5b2c-9333-e2ffa1658505', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0576311-6e15-5b2c-9333-e2ffa1658505'}, {'abstract': 'Claudia Beqaj hoped to buy an alcove studio or a one-bedroom below 23rd Street for about $400,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/realestate/a-place-of-her-own-no-strings-attached.html', 'snippet': 'Claudia Beqaj hoped to buy an alcove studio or a one-bedroom below 23rd Street for about $400,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SINCE her graduation from Rutgers University in 2000, Claudia Beqaj has lived in Manhattan, first sharing apartments with roommates and then sub-subletting from a friend. ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/realestate/10HUNT4_395/10HUNT4_395-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1048, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/realestate/10HUNT4_395/10HUNT4_395-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2001, 'subType': 'superJ