 at the Belmont Stakes, preventing Big Brown and jockey Kent Desormeaux from winning the Triple Crown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/sports/100000001593404/spoiling-history.html', 'snippet': 'In 2008, Da’Tara, ridden by Alan Garcia, pulled off a huge upset at the Belmont Stakes, preventing Big Brown and jockey Kent Desormeaux from winning the Triple Crown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2008, Da’Tara, ridden by Alan Garcia, pulled off a huge upset at the Belmont Stakes, preventing Big Brown and jockey Kent Desormeaux from winning the Triple Crown.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/video-jockey/video-jockey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spoiling History at Belmont', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T23:49:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'Justin Sablich and Jim Luttrell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sablich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Luttrell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/85114baa-9424-5262-a45a-fdad2d9eb239', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/85114baa-9424-5262-a45a-fdad2d9eb239'}, {'abstract': 'A 68-year-old fuel vendor from the southern Puglia region was arrested on suspicion of attempted multiple homicides with the intent of terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/world/europe/italy-man-arrested-in-school-bombing.html', 'snippet': 'A 68-year-old fuel vendor from the southern Puglia region was arrested on suspicion of attempted multiple homicides with the intent of terrorism.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Investigators in the southern Puglia region said Thursday that they had detained a suspect in a bombing that killed one student and wounded five at a Brindisi school three weeks ago. After hours of interrogation that started on Wednesday, officials said, a 68-year-old fuel vendor from the area was arrested on suspicion of attempted multiple homicides with the intent of terrorism. The authorities later identified the man as Giovanni Vantaggiato. Because the school was dedicated to Francesca Morvillo, who was killed with her husband, Giovanni Falcone, a prosecutor, by a Mafia bomb 20 years ago, investigators had initially investigated links to organized crime. The prosecutor Cataldo Motta said the suspect had admitted to having “economic problems,” but could not explain how that might have prompted him to carry out what Mr. Motta called a terrorist act. “He did not explain, he did not give justifications,” he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy: Man Arrested in School Bombing', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italy: Man Arrested in School Bombing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T23:52:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d25e025f-1097-5386-bba0-f43a82258bf3', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d25e025f-1097-5386-bba0-f43a82258bf3'}, {'abstract': 'Pakistan’s chief justice, Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry, removed himself from a panel investigating corruption accusations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/world/asia/pakistan-judge-quits-his-sons-case.html', 'snippet': 'Pakistan’s chief justice, Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry, removed himself from a panel investigating corruption accusations.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Amid accusations of conflict of interest, Pakistan’s chief justice, Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry, removed himself from a panel investigating corruption accusations against his son and announced the formation of a two-member bench to look into the claims. The day before, the son, Arsalan Chaudhry, testified before his father that rumors that he had accepted bribes worth $3 million to $4 million from a powerful and well-connected real estate developer were untrue. Justice Chaudhry had insisted he could rule fairly in the case, but he stepped aside after mounting criticism that he was hurting the court’s credibility. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan: Judge Quits His Son’s Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: Judge Quits His Son’s Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhry, Iftikhar Muhammad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-07T23:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b723cc56-2bf9-55e2-a901-1e8b339698c8', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b723cc56-2bf9-55e2-a901-1e8b339698c8'}, {'abstract': 'The unveiling of the Tejano Monument in Austin underscored the lack of a Juneteenth statue, after years of controversy led to the project’s cancellation in favor of a memorial for African-American Texans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/us/juneteenth-project-stalls-but-replacement-emerges.html', 'snippet': 'The unveiling of the Tejano Monument in Austin underscored the lack of a Juneteenth statue, after years of controversy led to the project’s cancellation in favor of a memorial for African-American Texans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tejano Monument, unveiled in March on the Texas Capitol’s south lawn, stands to honor the state’s early Spanish and Mexican settlers. But for some Texans, it is a reminder of the failed Juneteenth monument project, approved two years before the Tejano Monument.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/us/ttjuneteenth/ttjuneteenth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/us/ttjuneteenth/ttjuneteenth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/us/ttjuneteenth/ttjuneteenth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/us/ttjuneteenth/ttjuneteenth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/us/ttjuneteenth/ttjuneteenth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/us/ttjuneteenth/ttjuneteenth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'