 'byline': {'original': 'By James Montague', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Montague', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7614174-98b2-5666-a14d-e6f1fb43ecc1', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7614174-98b2-5666-a14d-e6f1fb43ecc1'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators concluded that a blaze that killed a family in Carmel, N.Y., was started by ash that was flicked unintentionally into a bed of mulch in front of the house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/nyregion/sons-cigarette-caused-fatal-carmel-fire-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'Investigators concluded that a blaze that killed a family in Carmel, N.Y., was started by ash that was flicked unintentionally into a bed of mulch in front of the house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARMEL, N.Y. (AP) — A man’s flicked cigarette ash probably caused the house fire in this Putnam County town last month that killed his parents and two sisters, the police said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Son’s Cigarette Caused Fatal Fire in Putnam County, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Son’s Cigarette Caused Fire, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Carmel (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Larchmont (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:06:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4468433b-6332-5e96-8695-3f4db71a8008', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4468433b-6332-5e96-8695-3f4db71a8008'}, {'abstract': 'A credible vote this month in Egypt is desperately needed. The courts, the media and the bureaucracy are conspiring to make sure that doesn’t happen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/opinion/egypt-struggles-toward-a-president.html', 'snippet': 'A credible vote this month in Egypt is desperately needed. The courts, the media and the bureaucracy are conspiring to make sure that doesn’t happen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month’s first round of presidential voting in Egypt produced two flawed, polarizing candidates: Ahmed Shafik, former President Hosni Mubarak’s last prime minister; and Mohamed Morsi, a functionary of the Muslim Brotherhood. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Struggles Toward a President', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Struggles Toward a President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shafik, Ahmed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7f74476-febe-53f0-b0ce-4f6d22da90c9', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7f74476-febe-53f0-b0ce-4f6d22da90c9'}, {'abstract': 'A writer of prose distinguished by deep research and powerful narrative force, Mr. Unsworth won a Booker Prize in 1992 for “Sacred Hunger.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/books/barry-unsworth-historical-novelist-dies-at-81.html', 'snippet': 'A writer of prose distinguished by deep research and powerful narrative force, Mr. Unsworth won a Booker Prize in 1992 for “Sacred Hunger.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barry Unsworth, considered one of the foremost historical novelists in English, who was known for rich, densely textured fiction that conjured lost worlds — those of the Trojan War, medieval Europe and the Napoleonic age, among many others — died on June 4 in Perugia, Italy. He was 81 and had lived in the Umbria region of Italy for many years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/UNSWORTH-obit/UNSWORTH-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/UNSWORTH-obit/UNSWORTH-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2022, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/UNSWORTH-obit/UNSWORTH-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/UNSWORTH-obit/UNSWORTH-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/UNSWORTH-obit/UNSWORTH-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Barry Unsworth, Writer of Historical Fiction, Dies at 81', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Barry Unsworth, Writer of Historical Fiction, Dies at 81', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Unsworth, Barry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Perugia (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:12:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/18071506-f04d-5629-ac10-b7835f893f43', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18071506-f04d-5629-ac10-b7835f893f43'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s proposal to decriminalize public possession of small amounts of marijuana is sound and has wide support from law enforcement. The State Senate majority leader should drop his opposition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/opinion/common-sense-on-marijuana.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s proposal to decriminalize public possession of small amounts of marijuana is sound and has wide support from law enforcement. The State Senate majority leader should drop his opposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Skelos, the majority leader of the New York State Senate, shows a serious lack of good sense in opposing Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s plan to decriminalize possession of small amounts of marijuana in public view. Mr. Skelos’s flippant remark — that the proposal would allow people to “walk around with 10 joints in each ear” — trivializes a serious problem and misrepresents a sound proposal that has broad support from law enforcement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Common Sense on Marijuana', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Common Sense on Marijuana', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skelos, Dean G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:13:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/29edd499-ca8f-50d3-97d6-0df2f26525f0', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29edd499-ca8f-50d3-97d6-0df2f26525f0'}, {'abstract': 'Doodnauth Shivmangal, the owner and trainer of the horse Guyana Star Dweej, has managed to stir some excitement in an immigrant community ahead of the Belmont Stakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/nyregion/guyana-star-dweej-is-a-long-shot-in-the-belmont-stakes.html', 'snippet': 'Doodnauth Shivmangal, the owner and trainer of the horse Guyana Star Dweej, has managed to stir some excitement in an immigrant community ahead of the Belmont Stakes.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dood!” cried the former jockey Jerry Bailey, shaking the hand of Doodnauth Shivmangal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/nyregion/TRAINER1/TRAINER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind Belmont Long Shot, a Quirky and Bold Trainer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Behind a Belmont Long Shot: A Bold, Quirky Owner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guyana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shivmangal, Doodnauth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:17:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c9ae338-78ae-5774-b8e0-30dde372d12e', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c9ae338-78ae-5774-b8e0-30dde372d12e'}, {'abstract': 'Maybe it doesn’t matter whether we want to hang out with the president.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/07/youre-likable-enough-mitt/', 'snippet': 'Maybe it doesn’t matter whether we want to hang out with the president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recent political commentary contrasts Mitt Romney’s negative personal image with President Obama’s positive one. Polls report that Obama is more “likable” than Romney, and that his “favorable to unfavorable” ratio is more positive.\xa0Other things being equal, it is no doubt better for a candidate to be liked than disliked, but when other things are not equal, historical data suggest that a candidate’s likability is a relatively minor factor in deciding modern presidential elections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘You’re Likable Enough, Mitt.’', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Jimmy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldwater, Barry M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam