 investigating the operations of the company, which was buoyed by financial support from the state. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Pitcher’s Video Game Company Goes Bankrupt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Pitcher’s Video Game Company Goes Bankrupt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schilling, Curt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhode Island', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '38 Studios', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:25:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9121789a-0d05-59b5-9dbf-f9e7eb9c3553', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9121789a-0d05-59b5-9dbf-f9e7eb9c3553'}, {'abstract': 'Since Republicans love to contrast President Obama’s record with that of Ronald Reagan, let’s look at government spending in each man’s administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/opinion/krugman-reagan-was-a-keynesian.html', 'snippet': 'Since Republicans love to contrast President Obama’s record with that of Ronald Reagan, let’s look at government spending in each man’s administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s no question that America’s recovery from the financial crisis has been disappointing. In fact, I’ve been arguing that the era since 2007 is best viewed as a “depression,” an extended period of economic weakness and high unemployment that, like the Great Depression of the 1930s, persists despite episodes during which the economy grows. And Republicans are, of course, trying — with considerable success — to turn this dismal state of affairs to their political advantage. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reagan Was a Keynesian', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reagan Was A Keynesian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keynes, John Maynard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/28a75b05-0b2a-5148-bfac-db25b3edda41', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a75b05-0b2a-5148-bfac-db25b3edda41'}, {'abstract': 'The House wastes time passing legislation designed to satisfy the ideological desires of conservative voters while the bills that need to become law get blocked.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/opinion/the-bills-to-nowhere.html', 'snippet': 'The House wastes time passing legislation designed to satisfy the ideological desires of conservative voters while the bills that need to become law get blocked.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is now the pattern of business in the House of Representatives: Spend most of the time passing bills designed not to become law but to satisfy the ideological desires of conservative voters. And block laws that actually need to get passed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bills to Nowhere', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bills to Nowhere', 'name': No