e': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Should Teach Our Children?', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T01:33:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Gutting', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gutting', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225b4dd3-78a3-54c7-959c-0dc061e12794', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225b4dd3-78a3-54c7-959c-0dc061e12794'}, {'abstract': 'Jiffy Lube’s new campaign seeks to set itself apart from shady mechanics and their thwarted attempts to make expensive and unnecessary repairs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/business/media/jiffy-lube-seeks-to-distance-itself-from-the-upsell.html', 'snippet': 'Jiffy Lube’s new campaign seeks to set itself apart from shady mechanics and their thwarted attempts to make expensive and unnecessary repairs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A NEW commercial for Jiffy Lube, the oil-change chain, opens on a quiet road, where a mechanic working underneath a car at a repair shop spots a woman driving by in an S.U.V. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/business/Adco1/Adco1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/business/Adco1/Adco1-articleLarge