cks off, here are slimmed-down versions of five teams to watch:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bite-Size Previews of Five Euro 2012 Contenders', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T02:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/789fa6c4-4a6d-5c66-ac5d-985f0fdb8639', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/789fa6c4-4a6d-5c66-ac5d-985f0fdb8639'}, {'abstract': '“Corpo Celeste” is a coming-of-age story that is also a kind of metaphor for the Roman Catholic Church, which is portrayed as having lost its way and its faithful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/movies/corpo-celeste-from-alice-rohrwacher.html', 'snippet': '“Corpo Celeste” is a coming-of-age story that is also a kind of metaphor for the Roman Catholic Church, which is portrayed as having lost its way and its faithful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An image, at once arresting and overly symbolic, sums up what’s good and bad about “Corpo Celeste,” the writer-director Alice Rohrwacher’s feature debut: Blindfolded almost-teenagers grope their way around a spartan church sanctuary in Reggio Calabria, Italy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08RDP_CORPO_SPAN/08RDP_CORPO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/08/arts/08RDP_CO