, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:06:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31a850de-3c72-51a3-b5c9-f02c95b4738f', 'word_count': 1246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31a850de-3c72-51a3-b5c9-f02c95b4738f'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 195 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/word-of-the-day-gaunt/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 195 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'gaunt •\\ˈgȯnt, ˈgänt\\• adjective ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | gaunt', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:08:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f0ac419-be22-501c-945b-ba67094d95af', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f0ac419-be22-501c-945b-ba67094d95af'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. begins its official push to qualify for the 2014 World Cup with a match against Antigua and Barbuda. It will probably get tougher from there.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/qualifying-for-the-cup-starts-now/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. begins its official push to qualify for the 2014 World Cup with a match against Antigua and Barbuda. It will probably get tougher from there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago this month, the United States was eliminated from the World Cup in South Africa. Its road to the next tournament, which kicks off two years from Tuesday in Brazil, starts Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Qualifying for the Cup Starts Now', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donovan, Landon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Tim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTIGUA (GUATEMALA)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0b651da-00aa-5ff4-9886-4b2e50bb1acc', 'word_count': 606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0b651da-00aa-5ff4-9886-4b2e50bb1acc'}, {'abstract': 'More than half the grain distributed by the state never reaches the people it is intended for.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/indias-failed-food-system/', 'snippet': 'More than half the grain distributed by the state never reaches the people it is intended for.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Spurred by agricultural innovation and generous farm subsidies, India now grows so much food that it has a bigger grain stockpile than any country except China, and it exports some of it to countries like Saudi Arabia and Australia,” Vikas Bajaj writes in The New York TImes. “Yet one-fifth of its people are malnourished — double the rate of other developing countries like Vietnam and China — because of pervasive corruption, mismanagement and waste in the programs that are supposed to distribute food to the poor. ”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s Failed Food System', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b4b6605-a7a5-5208-b57e-0a9bbda01db8', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b4b6605-a7a5-5208-b57e-0a9bbda01db8'}, {'abstract': 'A scientist who posed as a board member of a conservative organization to gain access to its confidential information has been reinstated as president of the Pacific Institute.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/science/earth/scientist-peter-gleick-is-reinstated-after-deceit.html', 'snippet': 'A scientist who posed as a board member of a conservative organization to gain access to its confidential information has been reinstated as president of the Pacific Institute.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A scientist who posed as a board member of a conservative organization to gain access to its confidential information has been reinstated as president of the Pacific Institute, the environmental research organization that he founded in California. The institute said Wednesday in a statement that an independent inquiry had confirmed the account offered by the scientist, Peter Gleick, of the false pretenses under which he obtained documents of the Heartland Institute in February. The documents contained details about the budget, strategy and donors to the institute, which disputes that global warming is under way. The statement said the Pacific Institute’s board of directors had accepted Dr. Gleick’s apology. By saying that its investigation confirmed Dr. Gleick’s account, the institute implicitly backed his assertion that he was not responsible for creating a document labeled a fake by Heartland that was disseminated along with other genuine ones. Heartland, based in Chicago, assailed the announcement as a “whitewash.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scientist Is Reinstated After Deceit', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Environment', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scientist Is Reinstated After Deceit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heartland Institute', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleick, Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Institute for Studies in Development, Environment and Security', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b39b712-592e-5a8d-95d5-e44598fe78db', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b39b712-592e-5a8d-95d5-e44598fe78db'}, {'abstract': 'Coleman Scott defeated Shawn Bunch in a wrestle-off in Times Square Thursday night to earn the final spot on the United States Olympic freestyle wrestling team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/sports/olympics/wrestle-off-in-times-square-decides-final-olympic-roster-spot.html', 'snippet': 'Coleman Scott defeated Shawn Bunch in a wrestle-off in Times Square Thursday night to earn the final spot on the United States Olympic freestyle wrestling team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Thursday began, of the three men who had a shot at the last spot on the Olympic freestyle wrestling team, Shawn Bunch was most confident in Shawn Bunch.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/wrestle/wrestle-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/wrestle/wrestle-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/wrestle/wrestle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/08/sports/wrestle/wrestle-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank'