Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Issa, Darrell E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0510082d-2b8e-58c4-8f2c-f938e170a564', 'word_count': 552, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0510082d-2b8e-58c4-8f2c-f938e170a564'}, {'abstract': 'The board of trustees of Florida A&M University voted 8 to 4 on Thursday that it did not have confidence in the leadership of the university president, James Ammons.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/us/florida-am-university-president-loses-vote.html', 'snippet': 'The board of trustees of Florida A&M University voted 8 to 4 on Thursday that it did not have confidence in the leadership of the university president, James Ammons.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The board of trustees of Florida A&M University voted 8 to 4 on Thursday that it did not have confidence in the leadership of the university president, James Ammons. The trustees who voted against Dr. Ammons said they did not believe he could steer them out of a crisis that followed the hazing death of a drum major, Robert Champion, in November. More than a dozen people, mostly students, have been charged in the death. The university also remains embroiled in an inquiry into financial irregularities. Dr. Ammons, whose contract runs through June 2016, vowed to do better. “You have my commitment to fix them and get this job done,” Dr. Ammons said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: School President Loses Vote', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: School President Loses Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ammons, James H', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Champion, Robert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida A&M University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T04:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7feabac-00ac-5bc3-af63-887b7775e008', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7feabac-00ac-5bc3-af63-887b7775e008'}, {'abstract': 'Aaron Cook, ranked No. 1 in the world in his weight class, was left off the team in favor of Lutalo Muhammad, who is No. 59 in the same weight class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/sports/olympics/olympic-games-british-take-issue-with-tae-kwon-do-pick.html', 'snippet': 'Aaron Cook, ranked No. 1 in the world in his weight class, was left off the team in favor of Lutalo Muhammad, who is No. 59 in the same weight class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some critics of this