curity Administration colleagues, Louise Rosskam produced images from Puerto Rico that found the inner strength and dignity of her subjects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As socially conscious photographers in the Depression-era United States, Edwin and Louise Rosskam thought they knew the face of need. But their stateside experiences hardly prepared them for what they encountered in Puerto Rico in late 1937.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peaks and Valleys on a Small Island', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puerto Ricans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Delano, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shahn, Ben', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Farm Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Standard Oil Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2638af7b-ecac-55f8-91f4-6a06c14c4047', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2638af7b-ecac-55f8-91f4-6a06c14c4047'}, {'abstract': 'What criminal offense justifies a convicted juvenile receiving a life sentence without parole?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/when-should-juvenile-offenders-receive-life-sentences/', 'snippet': 'What criminal offense justifies a convicted juvenile receiving a life sentence without parole?', 'lead_paragraph': 'After two arguments heard in March, the Supreme Court is expected to rule in the next few weeks on when it is appropriate to sentence juvenile offenders to life without parole. When do you think harsh sentencing is appropriate for minors, if ever? Should young inmates be housed with adults? What would you propose as an alternative sentence if a youth has committed a serious, violent crime?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Should Juvenile Offenders Receive Life Sentences?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T09:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5628faa5-acf3-5839-9dd0-909ebf6a96df', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5628faa5-acf3-5839-9dd0-909ebf6a96df'}, {'abstract': 'Discussions aimed at securing access to restricted sites — where the United Nations believes scientists may have tested explosives that could be used on nuclear warheads — stalled on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/world/middleeast/nuclear-agency-resumes-talks-with-iran-on-site-access.html', 'snippet': 'Discussions aimed at securing access to restricted sites — where the United Nations believes scientists may have tested explosives that could be used on nuclear warheads — stalled on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — After a brief spurt of optimism, impetus toward resolving the nuclear dispute with Iran slowed further on Friday as senior inspectors from the United Nations nuclear watchdog said they had made “no progress” toward gaining access to restricted sites they suspect of being used to test potential triggers for nuclear warheads.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘No Progress’ in Iran Nuclear Talks, U.N. Inspectors Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nuclear Talks Stall as Iran Bars Access To Inspectors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T09:15:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e6abaf0-1674-5eda-81be-4851b3efec60', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e6abaf0-1674-5eda-81be-4851b3efec60'}, {'abstract': 'Legacy, a nonprofit organization that has long sought to discourage younger Americans from smoking, is hoping a Web series on My Damn Channel will reach a younger audience of smokers.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/comic-web-series-comes-with-a-quit-smoking-sponsor/', 'snippet': 'Legacy, a nonprofit organization that has long sought to discourage younger Americans from smoking, is hoping a Web series on My Damn Channel will reach a younger audience of smokers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another example of the growing interest in online video, particularly to reach younger consumers, the American Legacy Foundation is sponsoring 