1-5468-9908-d140bb8983f1'}, {'abstract': 'Within a decade, there could be a drug that staves off brain destruction and death, some experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/a-new-front-in-the-battle-against-alzheimers/', 'snippet': 'Within a decade, there could be a drug that staves off brain destruction and death, some experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the New York Times Magazine on Sunday, Gina Kolata reports on new efforts to discover a treatment for Alzheimer’s disease.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Front in the Battle Against Alzheimer’s', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T10:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4ce2841-7f80-5e87-a39a-4685cd31ba61', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4ce2841-7f80-5e87-a39a-4685cd31ba61'}, {'abstract': 'An interview with defender Oguchi Onyewu, who talks about playing for his country and for Sporting Lisbon, his motivation to appear in a third World Cup in 2014 and why his family likes to joke about his soccer career.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/q-and-a-with-oguchi-onyewu/', 'snippet': 'An interview with defender Oguchi Onyewu, who talks about playing for his country and for Sporting Lisbon, his motivation to appear in a third World Cup in 2014 and why his family likes to joke about his soccer career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oguchi Onyewu is one of the few players on the United States national team who can say they have worked in as many countries as the squad’s coach, Jurgen Klinsmann. In a decade in Europe, Onyewu, an imposing central defender who turned 30 last month, has played for clubs in France, Belgium, England, Italy, the Netherlands and now Portugal, where he recently finished a strong first season with Sporting Club of Lisbon. He has played 65 times for the U.S., including appearances in the 2006 and 2010 World Cups, and is a member of the team that will open qualifying for the 2014 tournament this weekend. Onyewu spoke with the Goal blog on Tuesday about playing in Europe, his place on the national team, racism in the sport and why his family gets a good laugh about his soccer career. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A. with U.S. National Team Defender Oguchi Onyewu', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onyewu, Oguchi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sporting Lisbon (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T10:00:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67a44fd9-d007-5d8f-80fd-4bfda2cc569f', 'word_count': 2154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67a44fd9-d007-5d8f-80fd-4bfda2cc569f'}, {'abstract': 'So far this year, the combined value of takeovers in Europe has fallen 23 percent as market volatility and a reduction in financing continue to thwart efforts across the Continent to complete deals.', 'web_ur