vent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — What was that about sports promoting international harmony and understanding?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/blogs/rdv-ukraine/rdv-ukraine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/08/blogs/rdv-ukraine/rdv-ukraine-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sports, Racism and Disharmony at Euro 2012', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tymoshenko, Yulia V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T11:55:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb58e9ba-da81-52ed-b7ad-ea70ec3e1582', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb58e9ba-da81-52ed-b7ad-ea70ec3e1582'}, {'abstract': 'The judicial inquiry investigating ethics in the British press said in a statement Friday that prime ministers past and present would testify next week about their ties with the media.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/world/europe/top-british-politicians-to-appear-at-hacking-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The judicial inquiry investigating ethics in the British press said in a statement Friday that prime ministers past and present would testify next week about their ties with the media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The judicial inquiry investigating the ethics and behavior of the British press following the phone hacking scandal unveiled an A-list of politicians on Friday — including prime ministers past and present — to testify over four days next week about their ties with the media, particularly the Murdoch empire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top British Politicians to Appear at Hacking Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: Hacking Panel’s Big Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News International Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T11:55:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ef59f4a-bd58-5dfa-af12-456985ad2694', 'word_count': 926, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ef59f4a-bd58-5dfa-af12-456985ad2694'}, {'abstract': 'Members of Guns N’ Roses, Poison and Skid Row reminisce about their days working and playing hard on the Sunset Strip in the ’80s, the setting for the movie “Rock of Ages.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/movies/bret-michaels-duff-mckagan-and-sebastian-bach-reminisce.html', 'snippet': 'Members of Guns N’ Roses, Poison and Skid Row reminisce about their days working and playing hard on the Sunset Strip in the ’80s, the setting for the movie “Rock of Ages.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN the 1980s the Sunset Strip — a stretch of Sunset Boulevard in West Hollywood packed with bars and clubs — was the center of the hard-rock and hair-metal scene, spawning bands like Guns N’ Roses, Mötley Crüe and Poison. Based on the Broadway musical, the film “Rock of Ages,” which opens on Friday, starring a leather-pantsed Tom Cruise (at left and right) as the self-destructive, baboon-owning sex god Stacee Jaxx, fondly spoofs the era. It’s 1987, and the boys look like girls, the groupies look like strippers, and the hair is highly flammable. Meanwhile, as a small-town blonde named Sherrie (Julianne Hough) and her aspiring rocker boyfriend, Drew (Diego Boneta), try to succeed amid the sleaze, church-lady protesters are fighting to shut down a club called the Bourbon Room.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/arts/10MICHAELS_SPAN/10MICHAELS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guitars, Groupies and Lots and Lots of Hair', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guitars, Groupies and Lots and Lots of Hair', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rock of Ages (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hough, Julianne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McKagan, Duff', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bach, Sebastian', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michaels, Bret', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cruise, Tom', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T12:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sia Michel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Michel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af0be64a-3f3a-5442-98ce-f3883316d82d', 'word_count': 1714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af0be64a-3f3a-5442-98ce-f3883316d82d'}, {'abstract': 'A Japanese artist has joined up with Hermès to create limited-edition silk scarves decorated with abstract color studies.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/hes-a-rainbow-hiroshi-sugimoto-for-hermes/', 'snippet': 'A Japanese artist has joined up with Hermès to create limited-edition silk scarves decorated with abstract color studies.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Light is my medium to be investigated,” says the Japanese artist Hiroshi Sugimoto, who spent years chasing bands of prismatic color around his studio in Tokyo and capturing them, with what was for him rapid-fire succession, using a Polaroid camera. In collaboration with Hermès, 20 of the artist’s abstract color studies have been translated into silk scarves in signed, limited editions of seven each. “Couleurs de L’Ombre” (Colors of Shadow), as the collection is called, is a moving tribute to the lowly Polaroid, which faces imminent extinction. (Sugimoto in fact exhausted his last batch of the film to make the images.) Hermès, on the other hand, developed new inkjet technology in order to faithfully recreate the subtle gradations of intense color. Where the original Polaroids are small and precious, the scarves are large — just over 55 inches square — and dynamic, playing with light in ways the artist had never anticipated. Though at around $10,000, you might think twice about actually wearing one. “It’s serious art for me,” Sugimoto says, with a nod to Hermès. “And if it’s serious art, for me, it’s also very reasonably priced.” Available at hermes-editeur.com.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s a Rainbow | Hiroshi Sugimoto for Hermès', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T12:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/924d444d-cd89-5d59-b15d-6d3dc1a6403b', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/924d444d-cd89-5d59-b15d-6d3dc1a6403b'}, {'abstract': 'China’s women’s gymnastics team won a gold medal in the 2008 Beijing Olympics, but competitors questioned whether the competitors were too young.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/flashback-friday-age-controversy-follows-chinese-gymnasts/', 'snippet': 'China’s women’s gymnastics team won a gold medal in the 2008 Beijing Olympics, but competitors questioned whether the competitors were too young.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most Olympic gymnasts, especially female ones, look young. They are teenagers to start with, and are much smaller than most their age.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flashback Friday: Age Controversy Follows Chinese Gymnasts', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2008)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'He Kexin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Gymnastics Federation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)'