 'lead_paragraph': 'Qualifications for rappers at Bonnaroo 2012: technique, inclusiveness, vocal bite, stage presence. Thursday night brought three in a row to the This Tent for a deluge of multiply rhymed lines and polysyllabic precision: Danny Brown, Yelawolf and Kendrick Lamar. (More are due in the next days, both well-qualified on those fronts: GZA and Ludacris.) But their shticks were different, and in my earnest way I prefer Kendrick Lamar, who equally earnestly presents pleasures–booze and sex–as ways to “ease the pain” of a deprived upbringing and a competitive adult life. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonnaroo: Kendrick Lamar and Rappers With Vocal Bite', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamar, Kendrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yauch, Adam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T17:28:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdfd9bd9-7c6c-5b17-8296-0a1917e7d803', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdfd9bd9-7c6c-5b17-8296-0a1917e7d803'}, {'abstract': 'Slide Show: The 2012 Bonnaroo Music and Arts Festival got underway in Manchester, Tenn., on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/scenes-from-bonnaroo/', 'snippet': 'Slide Show: The 2012 Bonnaroo Music and Arts Festival got underway in Manchester, Tenn., on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' More Photographs', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scenes from Bonnaroo', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T17:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cf48788-fcfc-5652-890d-316e8f491673', 'word_count': 16, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cf48788-fcfc-5652-890d-316e8f491673'}, {'abstract': 'Take a day — or two — to wrestle with your undone fiscal tasks and clean up as many of them as possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/your-money/untangle-your-financial-woes-with-a-tuneup.html', 'snippet': 'Take a day — or two — to wrestle with your undone fiscal tasks and clean up as many of them as possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There comes a point in most people’s lives when the pile of undone financial tasks — the un-automated bills, the out-of-balance retirement accounts, the out-of-date budget, the under-optimized rewards programs — becomes large enough to provoke a sort of low-grade anxiety.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/your-money/09money-illo/09money-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/09/your-money/09money-illo/09money-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/your-money/09money-illo/09money-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,