: 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4be3252-4cef-55d4-b81d-7fa599f1e83d'}, {'abstract': 'The Bob Marshall Wilderness Complex is home to elk, moose and wolves. But, on this adventure, smaller creatures provided the most action.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/travel/searching-for-wildlife-in-montanas-bob-marshall-wilderness-complex.html', 'snippet': 'The Bob Marshall Wilderness Complex is home to elk, moose and wolves. But, on this adventure, smaller creatures provided the most action.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS we crept out of camp, the morning sky was slowly turning pink. Smoke billowed from the kitchen tent where we had just filled our mugs with wood-fired coffee. A Smith & Wesson pistol hung awkwardly on my hip. The tops of the surrounding Swan Range began to glow orange with the sunrise. Our guide, Jack Rich, scoped the grassy patches below the closest ridgeline, looking for movement. After spying a small cluster of animals from a distance, Jack led my friend Marie and me even deeper into the Bob Marshall Wilderness Complex, a tranquil pocket of Montana backcountry commonly referred to as the Bob.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10EXPLORER2/10EXPLORER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10EXPLORER2/10EXPLORER2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10EXPLORER2/10EXPLORER2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10EXPLORER2/10EXPLORER2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 10