he indie-pop singer Madeline Follin gives an insider’s view of the festival circuit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADELINE FOLLIN, 23, a singer in the indie-pop duo Cults, grew up going to music festivals around San Diego, her hometown. Now she knows her way around them as a performer.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10QNA/10QNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 730, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10QNA/10QNA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1459, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10QNA/10QNA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10QNA/10QNA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10QNA/10QNA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rocking Summer Music Festivals', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rocking Summer Music Festivals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cults (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T18:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4535632-971c-5114-9645-2bce060bc936', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4535632-971c-5114-9645-2bce060bc936'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond to an article about Dresden, Germany.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/travel/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond to an article about Dresden, Germany.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: Re “36 Hours in Dresden, Germany” (May 27): We’ve been to Dresden many times and have always loved it. The collections in the Zwinger Palace can easily take a day, and the VW plant tour is fascinating. Did I miss a reference to the Green Vault? It’s an amazing collection of decorative arts, some of which were shown at the Metropolitan Museum of Art. Rob HouckMount Kisco, N.Y.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Stops in Dresden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T18:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/92950b96-a690-5696-a8eb-a8bfeb5a5963', 'word_count': 241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92950b96-a690-5696-a8eb-a8bfeb5a5963'}, {'abstract': 'For tourists, this small South Korean city used to be virtually off the map. Then, Yeosu landed the 2012 World Expo — and things changed dramatically.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/travel/in-south-korea-all-roads-lead-to-yeosu-host-of-the-world-expo.html', 'snippet': 'For tourists, this small South Korean city used to be virtually off the map. Then, Yeosu landed the 2012 World Expo — and things changed dramatically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNTIL five years ago, Yeosu was an unremarkable, out-of-the-way city on the southern coast of South Korea. Despite a temperate climate, scenic islands and a spicy local cuisine, the city was, among tourists, virtually off the map. A largely rural municipality spread out over a peninsula and 317 islands, it has three commercial and residential hubs that used to be the only places to find anything resembling bustle. Then fate smiled on the city. Yeosu (pronounced YUH-sue) was chosen to host the 2012 World Expo, the smallest city in a generation to have the honor. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10KOREA3/10KOREA3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10KOREA3/10KOREA3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10KOREA3/10KOREA3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/travel/10KOREA3/10KOREA3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images