jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T18:38:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba2996b5-8082-5c49-a997-f9ff24ac31b7', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba2996b5-8082-5c49-a997-f9ff24ac31b7'}, {'abstract': 'A 12-room ninth-floor co-op where Leon Hess, the oil magnate and Jets owners, lived until his death.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/big-ticket-sold-for-17-25-million/', 'snippet': 'A 12-room ninth-floor co-op where Leon Hess, the oil magnate and Jets owners, lived until his death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The apartment on Park Avenue whereLeon Hess, the oil magnate and New York Jets owner, lived until his death in 1999 sold for $17.25 million, the biggest sale of the week, according to city records.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $17.25 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hess, Leon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Park Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T18:40:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ab52343-a27c-555b-8f55-baa107726452', 'word_count': 376, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ab52343-a27c-555b-8f55-baa107726452'}, {'abstract': 'While the LeBron James narrative churns onward, we stop to pause and consider the most recent of James’s dominant performances.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/jamess-brilliance-considered-on-its-own-merits/', 'snippet': 'While the LeBron James narrative churns onward, we stop to pause and consider the most recent of James’s dominant performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most instinctive response to the play of LeBron James is a wide-eyed stare. The relentless loathing directed toward him may provide a constant white noise, but when LeBron is LeBron, all else is mute; there’s no delight or celebration, but an awe that what we’ve witnessed should not be possible. James is often portrayed as both a hyper-flawed mortal and a peerless physical specimen, but at his most astounding, James is merely a transcendent basketball form. He doesn’t steal our attentions with some uncharacteristic seriousness. He captures us in his raw gravity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'James’s Brilliance, Considered on Its Own Merits', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T18:45:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59568be6-1f6e-55df-8643-fa5b1fe291c3', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59568be6-1f6e-55df-8643-fa5b1fe291c3'}, {'abstract': 'The designer tackles every side of what is known as a rather schizophrenic season: resort.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/just-one-look-derek-lam/', 'snippet': 'The designer tackles every side of what is known as a rather schizophrenic season: resort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a lot going on in the Derek Lam resort collection: leather pieces and safari/military jackets; stripes and animal spots; some swim, some chunky knits. Together it addressed every side of what is known as a rather schizophrenic season. (In November, when these clothes arrive in stores, are women shopping for the coming winter in New York or a holiday vacation in St. Barts? Or both?) The favorite, which three T editors each gravitated toward separately, was this belted handkerchief dress with buttons on the diagonal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Derek Lam', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T18:45:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e90d4228-9345-5825-b357-c104addfa9bc', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e90d4228-9345-5825-b357-c104addfa9bc'}, {'abstract': 'A four-bedroom lakefront contemporary in Wayne, N.J., and a five-bedroom colonial in Riverdale.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/10/realestate/20120610-OTMREGION.html', 'snippet': 'A four-bedroom lakefront contemporary in Wayne, N.