ations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T19:57:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaf0ccff-a029-57af-bfba-fedb8261b6d0', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaf0ccff-a029-57af-bfba-fedb8261b6d0'}, {'abstract': 'Friday’s exchange between President Obama and Mitt Romney was eerily similar to one between Mr. Obama and Senator John McCain of Arizona in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/republicans-take-aim-at-obamas-doing-fine-comments/', 'snippet': 'Friday’s exchange between President Obama and Mitt Romney was eerily similar to one between Mr. Obama and Senator John McCain of Arizona in 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years ago, President Obama eagerly seized on Senator John McCain’s comment that the “fundamentals of the economy are strong” to paint his Republican rival as out of touch with a plummeting reality.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republicans Take Aim at Obama’s ‘Doing Fine’ Comments', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T19:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77c27725-e4a8-56be-816f-41aacd626516', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77c27725-e4a8-56be-816f-41aacd626516'}, {'abstract': 'The designer has never been one to shy away from color, and resort has her seeing red — and lots of it.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/just-one-look-roksanda-ilincic/', 'snippet': 'The designer has never been one to shy away from color, and resort has her seeing red — and lots of it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roksanda Illincic has never been one to shy away from color, and resort has her seeing red — and lots of it. At the heart of the collection is a lacquered cotton that the designer cut into a simple car coat (which she showed cinched with a sliver of a white belt), a high-waisted dress and a pair of skinny trousers. The pants served as the underpinning for a series of lean, almost tuniclike dresses, whose graphic, asymmetrical color blocking, she said, was inspired by the work of Ellsworth Kelly and Kazimir Malevich.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Roksanda Ilincic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85271b73-8899-5f71-a549-78342efd6103', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85271b73-8899-5f71-a549-78342efd6103'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama on Friday afternoon backed away from his earlier comments that the “private sector is doing fine,” telling reporters that he does not believe that the economy is doing fine.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/obama-backs-away-from-fine-comment/', 'snippet': 'President Obama on Friday afternoon backed away from his earlier comments that the “private sector is doing fine,” telling reporters that he does not believe that the economy is doing fine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama on Friday afternoon backed away from his earlier comments that the “private sector is doing fine,” telling reporters that he does not believe the economy is doing fine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Backs Away From ‘Fine’ Comment', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7aa44f28-93ae-5644-8a73-8710e099772e', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7aa44f28-93ae-5644-8a73-8710e099772e'}, {'abstract': 'HomeAway joins with Priceline to allow customers to book plane tickets and car rentals in addition to homes.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytim