ils surfaced purporting to show that Mr. McGurk had a relationship with an Iraq correspondent for The Wall Street Journal while he was the Bush White House’s top Iraq adviser.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Raises Questions About Nominee for Iraq Ambassador', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senator Raises Questions About Envoy Nominee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bebb2e9e-d11a-584a-b22c-f8c7688b7134', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bebb2e9e-d11a-584a-b22c-f8c7688b7134'}, {'abstract': 'Spain appears poised to seek help for its ailing banks, a long-anticipated acknowledgment of the depth of its economic crisis. The only questions might be when, and how much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/business/global/madrid-seeks-more-information-on-banks-needs.html', 'snippet': 'Spain appears poised to seek help for its ailing banks, a long-anticipated acknowledgment of the depth of its economic crisis. The only questions might be when, and how much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Spain appears poised to seek a bailout of its ailing banks, a long-anticipated acknowledgment by the government of Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy of the depths of Spain’s economic crisis.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/business/Eurojp/Eurojp-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/09/business/Eurojp/Eurojp-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/business/Eurojp/Eurojp-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 672, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/business/Eurojp/Eurojp-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressed to Take Bailout, Spain Tries to Measure Its Need', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pressed to Seek a Bailout, Spain Assesses the Needs of Its Banks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajoy, Mariano', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:12:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder and Paul Geitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Geitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0236157d-b3f8-50d4-979e-1109df7f756f', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0236157d-b3f8-50d4-979e-1109df7f756f'}, {'abstract': 'A federal health official’s decision came as a vindication for people who have claimed that their cancers were caused by exposure to the dust cloud and debris at ground zero.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/nyregion/ruling-to-allow-9-11-health-fund-to-cover-cancers.html', 'snippet': 'A federal health official’s decision came as a vindication for people who have claimed that their cancers were caused by exposure to the dust cloud and debris at ground zero.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal health official’s ruling has cleared the way for 50 different types of cancer to be added to the list of sicknesses covered by a $4.3 billion fund set up to compensate and treat people exposed to the toxic smoke, dust and fumes in the months after the Sept. 11, 2001, terrorist attacks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sept. 11 Health Fund Given Clearance to Cover Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '9/11 Health Fund Given Clearance To Cover Cancer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'James Zadroga 9-11 Health and Compensation Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute for Occupational Safety and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, John M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:16:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anemona Hartocollis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anemona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartocollis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/605eb7ab-a75a-523f-a202-36626a745797', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/605eb7ab-a75a-523f-a202-36626a745797'}, {'abstract': 'Marco Reus, Mario Gotze, and Andre Schurrle of the German team could have an impact in the European Championship.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/for-euro-2012-germany-has-impressive-depth/', 'snippet': 'Marco Reus, Mario Gotze, and Andre Schurrle of the German team could have an impact in the European Championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soccer, like most sports, is a team game which, in the vaguest definition, revolves around 11 players who must work together in a series of carved out positions and tactics to enable the most efficient means of obtaining and exploiting a small leather ball to allow them to win a game. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Euro 2012, Germany Has Impressive Depth', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stefan Bienkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stefan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bienkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35a5a907-e223-5198-892b-7539dac3a572', 'word_count': 914, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35a5a907-e223-5198-892b-7539dac3a572'}, {'abstract': 'A scientist who used deceit to combat a group fighting action on global warming gets his job back.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/peter-gleicks-pacific-institute-return/', 'snippet': 'A scientist who used deceit to combat a group fighting action on global warming gets his job back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After an internal investigation, Peter Gleick has been reinstated as president of the Pacific Institute, the environmental group largely focused on water and climate that he founded in 1987. The career of this seasoned and lauded scientist and policy analyst ran off the rails when Gleick masqueraded as a member of the board of the anti-regulatory Heartland Institute to obtain internal documents on budgets and strategies. (He undertook this deception even as he was heading a task force on scientific ethics for the American Geophysical Union.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Gleick’s Pacific Institute Return', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gleick, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Michael E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heartland Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Institute for Studies in Development, Environment and Security', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:19:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6365360-4205-536e-bf43-dbff93f0a2b9', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6365360-4205-536e-bf43-dbff93f0a2b9'}, {'abstract': 'The man who created “Live From Lincoln Center” is stepping down as executive producer of the show after more than 30 years in the role.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/live-from-lincoln-center-creator-to-depart/', 'snippet': 'The man who created “Live From Lincoln Center” is stepping down as executive producer of the show after more than 30 years in the role.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Goberman, who created PBS’s much-honored series “Live From Lincoln Center” more than three decades ago, is leaving as the show’s executive producer at the end of the month, Lincoln Center said Friday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Live From Lincoln Center’ Creator to Depart', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Live From Lincoln Center’ Creator to Depart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:22:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b61efa94-9ceb-5125-941c-ab5598d6c3f5', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b61efa94-9ceb-5125-941c-ab5598d6c3f5'}, {'abstract': 'Institutional investors joined a “bumper crop of proxy fights,” a JPMorgan regulator faced tough questions, Nasdaq’s plan to settle Facebook claims met investor anger and tensions grew between MF Global trustees. A look back on the past week’s highs and lows.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/dealbooks-week-in-review-nobody-is-happy/', 'snippet': 'Institutional investors joined a “bumper crop of proxy fights,” a JPMorgan regulator faced tough questions, Nasdaq’s plan to settle Facebook claims met investor anger and tensions grew between MF Global trustees. A look back on the past week’s hig...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Institutional investors joined in on proxy fights, JPMorgan’s front-line regulator faced a fiery round of questioning, Nasdaq’s plan to settle Facebook claims met investor anger and the turf war between MF Global trustees grew increasingly tense. A look back on our reporting of the past week’s highs and lows in ferocious finance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DealBook’s Week in Review: Nobody Is Happy', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Owles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Owles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b554d1be-7359-5bb1-b25f-11913e9530cb', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b554d1be-7359-5bb1-b25f-11913e9530cb'}, {'abstract': 'A small-town bar band removes any doubts that it can scale up with rip-roaring rock and roll that had the crowd yelling along.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/bonnaroo-alabama-shakes-commands-the-big-stage/', 'snippet': 'A small-town bar band removes any doubts that it can scale up with rip-roaring rock and roll that had the crowd yelling along.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Alabama Shakes have had a wild year: a transformation from small-town bar band to national and international exposure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonnaroo: Alabama Shakes Commands the Big Stage', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tharpe, Rosetta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alabama Shakes (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:25:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ac7b07b-1e57-58b1-ab85-e3ddd4052743', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ac7b07b-1e57-58b1-ab85-e3ddd4052743'}, {'abstract': 'A new book gathers the legendary food writer’s best essays on drink, most of which have been out of print for decades.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/vintage-m-f-k-fisher/', 'snippet': 'A new book gathers the legendary food writer’s best essays on drink, most of which have been out of print for decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inextricably bound up with M.F.K. Fisher’s lifelong passion for food was the pleasure she took from sipping and serving a simple house wine, a crisp aperitif or a prickly, delicious glass of Champagne. In “M.F.K. Fisher: Musings on Wine and other Libations” (Sterling Epicure; $19), Fisher’s biographer, Anne Zimmerman, gathers all of the eminent food writer’s essays on drink under one beautifully designed cover. Some of these gems have been plucked from well-known collections, like “The Art of Eating” and “Long Ago in France,” but many others — the entertaining “a Vintage Spat,” for example, and the rousing “Wine is Life” — have been out of print for decades. For Fisher fans, coming across these is like reading an as-yet-unopened letter from a dear old friend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vintage M.F.K. Fisher', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, M F K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, Anne', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Wallace', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wallace', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2afa06a-d70f-54df-831b-c571b777120d', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2afa06a-d70f-54df-831b-c571b777120d'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Pakistan, Russia, West Bank and Egypt.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/pictures-of-the-day-pakistan-and-elsewhere-28/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Pakistan, Russia, West Bank and Egypt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Pakistan, Bahrain, West Bank and Egypt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pictures of the Day: Pakistan and Elsewhere', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:33:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ffc779c-85ed-5c73-b818-41d9b2dd1732', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ffc779c-85ed-5c73-b818-41d9b2dd1732'}, {'abstract': 'Badgley Mischka has gotten into the social media mix by previewing their resort collection via Pinterest.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/badgley-mischka-previews-resort-collection-via-pinterest/', 'snippet': 'Badgley Mischka has gotten into the social media mix by previewing their resort collection via Pinterest.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:15 p.m. | Updated Every day another brand tries exercising its digital muscles, from starting a Tumblr to live-streaming its runway shows. The bridal and resort seasons seem to be an opportune time for designers to experiment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Badgley Mischka Previews Resort Collection via Pinterest', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mischka, Badgley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pinterest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:33:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica C. Andrews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Andrews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de7fbe7b-1d18-5474-8e2d-6807b52676be', 'wor