United States of America brings “The Golden Veil,” a celebration of ideas about stories, to the stage at the Kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/theater/reviews/the-golden-veil-by-normandy-raven-sherwood-at-the-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'The National Theater of the United States of America brings “The Golden Veil,” a celebration of ideas about stories, to the stage at the Kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Odd and original but not quite satisfying, “The Golden Veil,” a production of the National Theater of the United States of America at the Kitchen, is like a cabinet of curiosities, stuffed with bits and pieces of European and American culture: myths and pastoral legends; gothic don’t-go-into-the-woods stories; songs that wouldn’t be out of place on Harry Smith’s “Anthology of American Folk Music”; dances, courtly and otherwise.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1437, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/GOLDEN/GOLDEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shepherdess in All Her Glory', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Shepherdess in All Her Glory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kitchen, The (Manhattan, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Theater of the United States of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherwood, Normandy Raven', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:52:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Saltz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saltz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f373c397-dca9-51be-831b-0af5c7ce2125', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f373c397-dca9-51be-831b-0af5c7ce2125'}, {'abstract': 'An outside counsel said that inappropriate actions by some committee staff members did not prevent Representative Maxine Waters of California from receiving a fair hearing.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/08/house-ethics-panel-wont-release-waters-report-on-misconduct-investigation/', 'snippet': 'An outside counsel said that inappropriate actions by some committee staff members did not prevent Representative Maxine Waters of California from receiving a fair hearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The House Ethics Committee refused to release on Friday the internal material it used for its decision earlier this week to move ahead with charges against Representative Maxine Waters of California.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Ethics Panel Won’t Release Waters Report on Misconduct Investigation', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T20:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lichtblau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6dbce5c-8aba-5ff3-91c0-6fee894a3cd5', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6dbce5c-8aba-5ff3-91c0-6fee894a3cd5'}, {'abstract': 'John Luther Adams’s monumental percussion work, “Inuksuit,” was given its West Coast premiere at the Ojai Music Festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/arts/music/john-luther-adamss-inuksuit-at-ojai-music-festival.html', 'snippet': 'John Luther Adams’s monumental percussion work, “Inuksuit,” was given its West Coast premiere at the Ojai Music Festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OJAI, Calif. — The superb Norwegian pianist Leif Ove Andsnes was a natural choice to be music director of this summer’s Ojai Music Festival, which opened on Thursday evening here in California’s beautiful Ojai Valley. Mr. Andsnes has long felt strongly about the culture and environment of his homeland. For years he was a co-director of the Risor Chamber Music Festival in a small coastal town in southeastern Norway, where distinguished musicians young and old gather each summer for six busy days of concerts and camaraderie, and the music-making takes inspiration from the place itself: a charming, rustic fishing village.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/OPENING/OPENING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/OPENING/OPENING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1706, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/OPENING/OPENING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/OPENING/OPENING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/09/arts/OPENING/OPENING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At a Concert, Even the Birds Chime In', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Concert, Even the Birds Chime In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schick, Steven', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adams, John Luther', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ojai (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-08T21:06:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'sub