: 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e26ba089-0a5d-5679-a08e-e5bbc84eb2b8', 'word_count': 971, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e26ba089-0a5d-5679-a08e-e5bbc84eb2b8'}, {'abstract': 'The top priority for the flagging euro zone is to fix the disastrous design flaw in which the 17 members agreed to a common monetary policy without coordinating their budgets and regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/opinion/the-euros-11th-hour.html', 'snippet': 'The top priority for the flagging euro zone is to fix the disastrous design flaw in which the 17 members agreed to a common monetary policy without coordinating their budgets and regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WITH each passing day, the noose around the neck of the euro zone grows tighter, with no indication that European leaders share any coherent vision for avoiding the hangman.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cr