aecde-daa8-502e-8e28-b0c0de15fdfd', 'word_count': 352, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7acaecde-daa8-502e-8e28-b0c0de15fdfd'}, {'abstract': 'Friday at Bonnaroo was full of smart female singers and songwriters: gentle and raucous, poppy and strange, open-hearted and enigmatic, sometimes all at once.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/bonnaroo-an-afternoon-of-smart-female-singers-and-songwriters/', 'snippet': 'Friday at Bonnaroo was full of smart female singers and songwriters: gentle and raucous, poppy and strange, open-hearted and enigmatic, sometimes all at once.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This one’s for the ladies. Actually that was Ludacris’s line as he introduced one of his many celebrations of lust and intoxication, setting off squeals, fist pumps and shout-alongs in a wildly appreciative arena-size crowd that swarmed well beyond This Tent. He had a backup band with him, not that I could get close enough to see it onstage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonnaroo: An Afternoon of Smart Female Singers and Songwriters', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T10:10:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d26c4e4c-a9bf-5b7d-b646-81fcb7c7b30c', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d26c4e4c-a9bf-5b7d-b646-81fcb7c7b30c'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Tanier blogged and tweeted at events and locations throughout New York on Saturday. Re-live his day here.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/live-updates-a-sports-day-like-no-other/', 'snippet': 'Mike Tanier blogged and tweeted at events and locations throughout New York on Saturday. Re-live his day here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many world-class sporting events are scheduled for today, and several of them are in the New York metropolitan area. Mike Tanier is blogging and tweeting at events and locations throughout the region, including the Mets-Yankees game in the Bronx, Game 5 of the Kings-Devils Stanley Cup finals in Newark and the Adidas Grand Prix on Randalls Island. Follow his progress here and on Twitter @FO_MTanier with the hashtag #fanathon. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Reporter’s Marathon Day in Sports', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Relishing a Glut of Sports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T10:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tanier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3b20284-c638-5c72-a9a1-77428d716abb', 'word_count': 5627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3b20284-c638-5c72-a9a1-77428d716abb'}, {'abstract': 'The Afghan president’s spokesman said Saturday that last week’s civilian casualties during a raid on Taliban fighters in eastern Afghanistan were unacceptable.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/world/asia/france-says-4-troops-killed-in-eastern-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Afghan president’s spokesman said Saturday that last week’s civilian casualties during a raid on Taliban fighters in eastern Afghanistan were unacceptable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The Afghan president’s spokesman sternly rebuked American officials on Saturday, saying that the civilian casualties last week during an NATO-Afghan raid on Taliban fighters in eastern Afghanistan were unacceptable, not only because of the loss of innocent life but also because Afghan forces were not involved in the decision to call in an airstrike. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Official Rebukes NATO for Civilian Deaths', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Official Rebukes NATO for Civilian Deaths', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T10:36:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sangar Rahimi and Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sangar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rahimi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbe7f0c3-55ca-5fba-b80c-240ed9e0f6dd', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbe7f0c3-55ca-5fba-b80c-240ed9e0f6dd'}, {'abstract': 'European finance ministers promised up to $125 billion in aid, which they hope will quell rising financial turmoil ahead of elections in Greece next week that could roil world markets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/business/global/spain-moves-closer-to-bailout-of-banks.html', 'snippet': 'European finance ministers promised up to $125 billion in aid, which they hope will quell rising financial turmoil ahead of elections in Greece next week that could roil world markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Responding to increasingly urgent calls from across Europe and the United States, Spain on Saturday agreed to accept a bailout for its cash-starved banks as European finance ministers offered an aid package of up to $125 billion.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/10SPAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/10SPAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/10SPAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/10SPAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/10SPAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/10SPAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/world/10SPAIN/1