Roland Garros on Sunday in a match guaranteed to make history. A Djokovic win would be his fourth straight major title. While technically not a Grand Slam (which must occur in the same calendar year), it would nonetheless be an astonishing accomplishment. For Nadal, a victory on Sunday would give him a record seventh French Open title, eclipsing Bjorn Borg’s total and further cementing his reputation as the best clay-court player ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Djokovic and Nadal, It’s a Chess Match', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7db24c75-b9f8-59e4-8fa7-f93827683fea', 'word_count': 744, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7db24c75-b9f8-59e4-8fa7-f93827683fea'}, {'abstract': 'Every year when a Triple Crown is on the line, three women usually gather at Belmont Park, each wearing a corsage — they form an exclusive club of Triple Crown horse owners.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/an-exclusive-club-garlands-and-corsages/', 'snippet': 'Every year when a Triple Crown is on the line, three women usually gather at Belmont Park, each wearing a corsage — they form an exclusive club of Triple Crown horse owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year when a Triple Crown is on the line, three women usually gather at Belmont Park, each wearing a corsage: one blue and white, one yellow and black, one pink and black.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Exclusive Club: Garlands and Corsages', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T16:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4837111c-ae53-5968-ba0c-598bf1b3d982', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4837111c-ae53-5968-ba0c-598bf1b3d982'}, {'abstract': 'Maria Sharapova defeated Sara Errani 6-3, 6-2, to win the French Open and become the 10th woman to win a career Grand Slam.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/sports/tennis/maria-sharapova-wins-french-open.html', 'snippet': 'Maria Sharapova defeated Sara Errani 6-3, 6-2, to win the French Open and become the 10th woman to win a career Grand Slam.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Ever since shoulder surgery nearly forced Maria Sharapova into early retirement, she occupied an odd, conflicted space in both tennis and the wider world of sports. She remained among the most marketable female athletes on the planet, tall and blond and famous, a superstar in every sense except the most important one.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10women-2/10women-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10women-2/10women-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1425, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10women-2/10women-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10women-2/10women-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10women-2/10women-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A French Open Title and a Career Grand Slam for Sharapova', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Final Pieces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Errani, Sara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T16:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/058ff649-d9a1-5c1d-b139-734b57fcd969', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/058ff649-d9a1-5c1d-b139-734b57fcd969'}, {'abstract': 'Some say three bank robbers made a great escape from prison in the San Francisco Bay in 1962, while others say they could not have survived.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/us/anniversary-of-a-mystery-at-alcatraz.html', 'snippet': 'Some say three bank robbers made a great escape from prison in the San Francisco Bay in 1962, while others say they could not have survived.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago, on the night of June 11, 1962, the three convicts were locked down as usual. Guards walking the tier outside their cells saw them at 9:30 and checked on them periodically all night, looking in at the sleeping faces, hearing nothing strange. But by morning, the inmates had vanished, Houdini-like. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1351, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/0alcatraz/0alcatraz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tale of 3 Inmates Who Vanished From Alcatraz Maintains Intrigue 50 Years Later', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fate of 3 Inmates Who Vanished From Alcatraz Remains a Mystery 50 Years Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Frank Lee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anglin, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALCATRAZ (SAN FRANCISCO)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anglin, Clarence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T16:19:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert D. McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de936735-a5fa-563a-b66e-627108430f56', 'word_count': 1315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de936735-a5fa-563a-b66e-627108430f56'}, {'abstract': 'Deady delusions in Deutschland.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/wolkenkuckucksheim/', 'snippet': 'Deady delusions in Deutschland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Martin Wolf reports on a letter he has received from the Director General of the German Finance Ministry; taken in context with the speech just given in Riga by Germany’s man at the ECB, what we get is a terrifying picture. Basically, it seems that even as the euro approaches a critical juncture, senior German officials are living in Wolkenkuckucksheim — cloud-cuckoo land.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wolkenkuckucksheim', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T16:24:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2efc334c-5c73-5fb5-83b6-febe7a9d5fd9', 'word_count': 307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2efc334c-5c73-5fb5-83b6-febe7a9d5fd9'}, {'abstract': 'Among the big names who have fallen in the United States Open at Olympic Club: Ben Hogan, Arnold Palmer, Tom Watson and Payne Stewart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/sports/golf/us-open-olympic-club-has-been-unkind-to-favorites.html', 'snippet': 'Among the big names who have fallen in the United States Open at Olympic Club: Ben Hogan, Arnold Palmer, Tom Watson and Payne Stewart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the United States Open championship, the charm and the challenge for the world’s best golfers is coping with a course many of them have not played for more than a decade, if at all. This year’s site is the Lake Course of Olympic Club in San Francisco, a little bit of heaven with mostly sidehill fairways that drift down from the sandy cliffs above the Pacific Ocean through sentries of cypress trees and sloping target greens to the shore of Lake Merced. The club’s name calls to mind Mount Olympus, the home of the mythical Greek gods, but at its four previous Opens over more than half a century, Olympic has treated human golf gods rudely. And what glorious gods they were.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1209, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/anderson1/anderson1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Favorites Have Way of Fading When Open Is Played at Olympic', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Favorites Have Way of Fading When Open Is Played at Olympic', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olymp