gnition and scanned the scraps of his recent weeks. Crinkled chip bags on the dashboard. Soda cups at his feet. And on the passenger seat, a rumpled SAT practice book whose owner had been told since fourth grade he was headed to the Ivy League. Pencils up in 20 minutes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-span-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/us/10stimulants1-span/10stimulants1-span-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Risky Rise of the Good-Grade Pill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Risky Rise of the Good-Grade Pill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'SAT (College Admission Test)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T17:48:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Schwarz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwarz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/283b71b7-0080-5590-b400-2d197af8bbd2', 'word_count': 3474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/283b71b7-0080-5590-b400-2d197af8bbd2'}, {'abstract': 'The former jockey Donna Barton Brothers interviews winning riders in the Triple Crown races on horseback in her role as analyst for NBC.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/riding-a-horse-and-carrying-a-microphone/', 'snippet': 'The former jockey Donna Barton Brothers interviews winning riders in the Triple Crown races on horseback in her role as analyst for NBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Mario Gutierrez came from virtually nowhere to ride I’ll Have Another to victory in the Kentucky Derby, Donna Barton Brothers was waiting just beyond the finish line to interview him in her role as analyst for NBC — on horseback. For Brothers, being on a horse comes more naturally than holding a microphone. Her mother, Patti Barton, was a trailblazer for women jockeys, and Brothers, her sister and her brother followed in her footsteps. When Brothers retired in 1998, she was the second-winningest female rider in the United States by money earned. But she never strayed too far away from the sport she loved. She is married to a horse trainer, Frank Brothers, and works as an analyst for NBC Sports and TVG.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riding a Horse and Carrying a Microphone', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '30 Seconds With Donna Barton Brothers: Waiting Past the Finish Line for the Winner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T17:57:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Hoppert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoppert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8839ebd-15b6-5fc1-937e-a055b269b42f', 'word_count': 2895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8839ebd-15b6-5fc1-937e-a055b269b42f'}, {'abstract': 'Novak Djokovic used constant pressure to defeat Roger Federer at the French Open.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/breaking-it-down-djokovic-vs-federer/', 'snippet': 'Novak Djokovic used constant pressure to defeat Roger Federer at the French Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is an intense pressure that Novak Djokovic, the world No. 1, brings to a match that you just can’t find on a stat sheet – or can you?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking It Down: Djokovic vs. Federer', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T18:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O'Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shannessy", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ea7dc22-a52d-5b1c-856c-7dac83fbd15a', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ea7dc22-a52d-5b1c-856c-7dac83fbd15a'}, {'abstract': 'Refocused on his career as a Giant, the former Yankees outfielder Melky Cabrera has the highest batting average in the National League.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/sports/baseball/melky-cabrera-reaches-new-heights-with-giants.html', 'snippet': 'Refocused on his career as a Giant, the former Yankees outfielder Melky Cabrera has the highest batting average in the National League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Several San Francisco Giants veterans, including Barry Zito, Aubrey Huff and Ryan Theriot, were sitting by their lockers at AT&T Park last weekend discussing how the team would muddle through if their closer, Santiago Casilla, could not pitch because of a knee injury.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/melky/melky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}