pe_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/456376e0-0374-5903-b495-bfda82e9d459', 'word_count': 1403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/456376e0-0374-5903-b495-bfda82e9d459'}, {'abstract': 'Long before Carlos Correa became the first Puerto Rican player to be picked first in baseball’s draft, even before Roberto Clemente made his debut for the Pittsburgh Pirates, Hiram Bithorn was a major league pitching star. In the years since, the island has struggled to produce other top-notch pitchers.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/keeping-score-hope-that-puerto-rico-can-end-its-major-league-slump/', 'snippet': 'Long before Carlos Correa became the first Puerto Rican player to be picked first in baseball’s draft, even before Roberto Clemente made his debut for the Pittsburgh Pirates, Hiram Bithorn was a major league pitching star. In the years since, the ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April 1942, five years before Jackie Robinson broke baseball’s color line, Hiram Bithorn made his debut for the Chicago Cubs. By 1943, he was one of the game’s earliest Hispanic stars, winning 18 games, tossing 7 shutouts and compiling a 2.60 earned-run average.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping Score: Hope That Puerto Rico Can End Its Major League Slump', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puerto Ricans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Carlos (1994- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vazquez, Javier', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T18:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4468398e-374f-57c0-a391-e43b837d36e7', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4468398e-374f-57c0-a391-e43b837d36e7'}, {'abstract': 'Friday night at Bonnaroo, Radiohead was a rhythm band, hitting groove after groove and riding them to darkly kinetic places.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/bonnaroo-radioheads-festival-evolution/', 'snippet': 'Friday night at Bonnaroo, Radiohead was a rhythm band, hitting groove after groove and riding them to darkly kinetic places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time Radiohead played at Bonnaroo, in 2006, it seemed to metamorphose on the spot: from a cerebral, futuristic, anxiety-driven band playing its arcane songs to earnest theater audiences to a cerebral, futuristic band that could make tens of thousands of people dance like crazy. Friday night at Bonnaroo was the follow-through: Radiohead the rhythm band, hitting groove after groove and riding them to darkly kinetic places. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bonnaroo: Radiohead’s Festival Evolution', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonnaroo Festival (Manchester, Tenn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radiohead', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T18:19:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiz