 the last 70 years in professional baseball, but he has not been on the winning side of a no-hitter since Don Larsen’s perfect game in the 1956 World Series. Coleman was an infielder for the Yankees.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Padres History Missing Chapter on No-Hitters', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Extra Bases: Padres’ History Missing Chapter On No-Hitters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Padres', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T20:21:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fe4d9de-3b9c-52f1-b45d-abaac27d5584', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fe4d9de-3b9c-52f1-b45d-abaac27d5584'}, {'abstract': 'When it comes to Triple Crown tradition, the Belmont Stakes seems a little off-key in its post-parade musical choices.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/they-got-the-song-right-here/', 'snippet': 'When it comes to Triple Crown tradition, the Belmont Stakes seems a little off-key in its post-parade musical choices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most thrilling parts of the Kentucky Derby and Preakness pomp and circumstance comes when 100,000 voices rise for the singing of “My Old Kentucky Home” and “Maryland, My Maryland.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Got the Song Right Here', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub