}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1aa63e0-4b8c-531f-8b20-d289bcdf9be1', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1aa63e0-4b8c-531f-8b20-d289bcdf9be1'}, {'abstract': 'For some gay celebrities, there is a new normal that avoids the choreographed tap dance out of the closet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/sunday-review/how-celebrities-come-out-now.html', 'snippet': 'For some gay celebrities, there is a new normal that avoids the choreographed tap dance out of the closet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTENDED or not, President Obama’s declaration of support for gay marriage had some of the classic hallmarks of a celebrity coming out of the closet and identifying himself or herself as gay. It was a carefully orchestrated revelation, designed to try to maximize acceptance and minimize any negative consequences from, say, the Christian ministers whom Mr. Obama mollified by phone. It was not unlike how openly gay actors used to worry about the reaction within Hollywood.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sunday-review/10celebrities-thumb/10celebrities-thumb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sunday-review/10celebrities-thumb/10celebrities-thumb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sunday-review/10celebrities-thumb/10celebrities-thumb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/sunday-review/10celebrities-thumb/10celebrities-thumb