earch that compares the use of racially charged search terms with voting patterns suggests that Barack Obama’s race lowers his chance of re-election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Obama won 52.9 percent of the popular vote in 2008 and 365 electoral votes, 95 more than he needed. Many naturally concluded that prejudice was not a major factor against a black presidential candidate in modern America. My research, a comparison of Americans’ Google searches and their voting patterns, found otherwise. If my results are correct, racial animus cost Mr. Obama many more votes than we may have realized.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Racist Are We? Ask Google', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2008', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-09T21:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Stephens-Davidowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens-Davidowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab26730-fa9e-5234-9eef-158eaca641e2', 'word_count': 887, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab26730-fa9e-5234-9eef-158eaca641e2'}, {'abstract': 'The recession and its aftermath have forced many older people who are out of work to draw Social Security earlier than they had planned.', 'web_url':