ial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0edc844d-e054-5988-aa30-99388884178e', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0edc844d-e054-5988-aa30-99388884178e'}, {'abstract': 'A brash French immigrant finds his fate in an obscure Virginia battle.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/death-on-virginias-sacre-soil/', 'snippet': 'A brash French immigrant finds his fate in an obscure Virginia battle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wheat fields played famous host to some of the bloodiest carnage at the landmark battles of Antietam and Gettysburg. They also marked a number of lesser-known engagements, including a forgotten battle waged in the Shenandoah Valley on June 9, 1862, when Union and Confederate forces clashed near Port Republic, a bucolic village located in the heart of the valley along the south fork of the Shenandoah River. For one Southern patriot, the battle in this wheat field was where a sentimental vow he made to leave his bones on the sacred soil of Virginia was tragically fulfilled. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death on Virginia’s ‘Sacré’ Soil', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T01:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1fc9d8f-3b6b-5be1-b9d2-a63500f26a97', 'word_count': 1337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1fc9d8f-3b6b-5be1-b9d2-a63500f26a97'}, {'abstract': 'Wondering about the possibilities for Germany with Mario Gomez scoring and its manager making all the right moves with his lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/09/germans-win-and-dutch-stumble-in-group-of-death/', 'snippet': 'Wondering about the possibilities for Germany with Mario Gomez scoring and its manager making all the right moves with his lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeré Longman of The Times was in Lviv, Ukraine, on Saturday to see Germany’s 1-0 victory over Portugal in Euro 2012, and writes about the possibilities for the Germans with Mario Gomez scoring and Joachim Löw making all the right moves with his lineup. Things did not go nearly as well for the Netherlands in Kharkiv, where Denmark stole a goal — and a 1-0 victory — on a counterattack in a game in which they might have lost by three or four. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germans Win and Dutch Stumble in Group of Death', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T01:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a58a9587-6d94-5938-a07c-e4219030975e', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a