 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c6d4b08-6729-5524-b1b9-dd9159506e8f'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal and Novak Djokovic meet in the men’s French Open final, both with an eye on the record books.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/live-analysis-mens-french-open-final/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal and Novak Djokovic meet in the men’s French Open final, both with an eye on the record books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Play was halted in the 2012 French Open men’s singles final between Novak Djokovic and Rafael Nadal with Djokovic to serve in the fourth set at 4-6, 3-6, 6-2, 2-1. It was the first men’s final at the tournament since 1973 to be postponed to another day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Men’s Final of French Open Postponed Until Monday', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T13:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0d586a2-4072-583c-89b8-4be11227d0fe', 'word_count': 3090, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0d586a2-4072-583c-89b8-4be11227d0fe'}, {'abstract': 'A daily prayer call is helping to bring together a dozen Ghanaian health aides who live in the Bronx but are scattered throughout the region while working.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/uniting-through-a-prayer-call/', 'snippet': 'A daily prayer call is helping to bring together a dozen Ghanaian health aides who live in the Bronx but are scattered throughout the region while working.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent Tuesday at noon, a dozen live-in home health aides — all from the Bronx — dialed a conference-call number. They phoned from their elderly patients’ small apartments in Queens and from spacious houses in New Jersey and Connecticut. Within seconds, they were connected to their pastor, Benjamin Boakye, of Ebenezer Assembly of God Church on Jerome Avenue in the Bronx.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uniting Through a Prayer Call', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heisler, Todd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T13:17:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72d89d98-70c8-5eb9-8457-9282f18404ff', 'word_count': 325, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72d89d98-70c8-5eb9-8457-9282f18404ff'}, {'abstract': 'SC Johnson Gallery in Racine, Wis., offers another attraction for aficionados of Frank Lloyd Wright.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/wright-gallery-opens/', 'snippet': 'SC Johnson Gallery in Racine, Wis., offers another attraction for aficionados of Frank Lloyd Wright.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For aficionados of Frank Lloyd Wright, the new SC Johnson Gallery in Racine, Wis., offers another attraction on the fan circuit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wright Gallery Opens', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Frank Lloyd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T14:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Glusac', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glusac', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41fc81c2-c68d-5fc2-a2f8-0aef1b700289', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41fc81c2-c68d-5fc2-a2f8-0aef1b700289'}, {'abstract': 'Students pressured to succeed in high school turn to Adderall for tunnel focus.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/snorting-the-good-grade-drug/', 'snippet': 'Students pressured to succeed in high school turn to Adderall for tunnel focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Students feeling pressure to succeed aren’t snorting cocaine or heroin, but Adderall, an amphetamine prescribed for attention deficit hyperactivity disorder. One student told a New York Times reporter that “he and his friends routinely shared to study late into the night, focus during tests and ultimately get the grades worthy of their prestigious high school in an affluent suburb of New York City. The drug did more than just jolt them awake for the 8 a.m. SAT; it gave them a tunnel focus tailor-made for the marathon of tests long known to make or break college applications.” Read the full story here, and follow more stories from high school students here—or share your own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snorting the Good Grade Drug', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T14:31:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53870a0b-3c34-518c-b24b-3b6bd6afa981', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53870a0b-3c34-518c-b24b-3b6bd6afa981'}, {'abstract': 'Despite the popularity of TV shows like “Game of Thrones,” HBO doesn’t offer a standalone service that allows fans to stream episodes.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/disruptions-for-hbo-still-beholden-to-a-cable-company/', 'snippet': 'Despite the popularity of TV shows like “Game of Thrones,” HBO doesn’t offer a standalone service that allows fans to stream episodes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After cutting the cable TV cord two years ago, I’m often a bit late to the conversations about hot new shows. So last week, after hearing friends rave incessantly about “Game of Thrones,” I gave it a try.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/business/10disrupt-pic/10disrupt-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/business/10disrupt-pic/10disrupt-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disruptions: For HBO, Still Beholden to a Cable Company', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disruptions: For HBO, Still Beholden To a Cable Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T15:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5de06aa1-e4ba-58e0-add6-4926cdf9a4e9', 'word_count': 665, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5de06aa1-e4ba-58e0-add6-4926cdf9a4e9'}, {'abstract': '‘The Duchess of Malfi,’ a Jacobean tragedy that just ended its run at Old Vic in London, was written when memories of the first Queen Elizabeth were fresh. Now it provokes Ben Brantley’s reflections on the present queen.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/london-theater-journal-another-prisoner-of-noble-title/', 'snippet': '‘The Duchess of Malfi,’ a Jacobean tragedy that just ended its run at Old Vic in London, was written when memories of the first Queen Elizabeth were fresh. Now it provokes Ben Brantley’s reflections on the present queen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — What do you suppose she’s really thinking beneath the mask of majesty? All that nonstop pomp and pageantry must feel like a straitjacket. And surely she has disturbing things on her mind at the moment — worries about her husband, for one — as her reveling subjects pay such ostentatious tribute to her. Wouldn’t you just love to know what’s going on inside that serene head of hers?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Another Prisoner of Noble Title', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Best, Eve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Old Vic Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T15:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13096ccf-9c6e-58e9-829d-4b1a26a2458d', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13096ccf-9c6e-58e9-829d-4b1a26a2458d'}, {'abstract': 'It’s all happening in Gdansk! Live coverage of Spain and Italy in the Euro 2012 soccer tournament.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/italy-spain-live/', 'snippet': 'It’s all happening in Gdansk! Live coverage of Spain and Italy in the Euro 2012 soccer tournament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s how The Times called the action from Gdansk as tournament favorites Spain battled Italy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012: Italy-Spain As it Happened', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gdansk (Poland)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T15:05:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'f