frantic chromatic babble of Clifford Brown and Jon Hendricks’s “Joy Spring” is quite a leap for any singer. But Karrin Allyson made it look easy on Thursday evening at Birdland. Her show, whose selections change with every set, is a celebration of a 13-album career that is one of the most stable in jazz. She has an easy mastery of bebop, bossa nova, chanson and soft rock, to name four of the many styles in which she is comfortable.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/arts/SUBBIRDLAND/SUBBIRDLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 989, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/arts/SUBBIRDLAND/SUBBIRDLAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 989, 'width': 727, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweet Core, Steely Edge', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sweet Core, Steely Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLYSON, KARRIN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barth, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T21:49:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9082273-5ef2-5997-ac1d-41c24d3c0c44', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9082273-5ef2-5997-ac1d-41c24d3c0c44'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn Philharmonic has its revival under a new artistic director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/arts/music/brooklyn-philharmonic-sets-out-on-ambitious-new-programs.html', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn Philharmonic has its revival under a new artistic director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This season the Brooklyn Philharmonic, revived from the dead, traveled to three of the borough’s communities with tailor-made concert series. In October the orchestra took Russian cartoon music to Brighton Beach and in March, an ambitious program full of premieres to Downtown Brooklyn, a new-music epicenter as of late.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/arts/11bedstuy-web/11bedstuy-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/arts/11bedstuy-web/11bedstuy-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bridging Past, Present and Future', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Resurrected to Bridge Past, Present and Future', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierson, Alan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mos Def', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bedford-Stuyvesant (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank':