': 1202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73ecab7e-3778-55b6-b492-67dfafbc974c'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal, seeking a record seventh title at Roland Garros, won the first two sets against Novak Djokovic but then came apart and must wait until Monday to play again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/sports/tennis/french-open-final-suspended-with-nadal-ahead.html', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal, seeking a record seventh title at Roland Garros, won the first two sets against Novak Djokovic but then came apart and must wait until Monday to play again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The Rafael Nadal on court late Sunday afternoon at Roland Garros seemed more like an impostor, so unlike Nadal, on his favorite surface, at his favorite tournament, getting bullied around on clay. The snarl was still there, the face all twisted and contorted; however, it came not from the usual dominance but from anger over circumstance.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 623, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1247, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/sports/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2/10frenchopen_men_337-slide-0JE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Nadal Ahead but Out of Sorts, Final Is Suspended', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Nadal Ahead But Out of Sorts, Final Is Suspended', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T22:09:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/500e5fdd-a233-5b37-91d0-87aed390c7c5', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/500e5fdd-a233-5b37-91d0-87aed390c7c5'}, {'abstract': 'Data will include retail sales and import prices for May, Kroger and Smithfield Foods will report earnings and Apple will hold its annual conference.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/business/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-june-11.html', 'snippet': 'Data will include retail sales and import prices for May, Kroger and Smithfield Foods will report earnings and Apple will hold its annual conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ECONOMIC REPORTS Data to be reported this week will include import prices for May (Tuesday); retail sales for May, the Producer Price Index for May and business inventories for April (Wednesday); weekly jobless claims, the Consumer Price Index for May and the current account deficit for the first quarter (Thursday); and industrial production for May and the Thomson Reuters/University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for June (Friday).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week Ahead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looking Ahead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T22:11:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b3e68f7-64ba-5487-8d35-8983f2fd2f0f', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b3e68f7-64ba-5487-8d35-8983f2fd2f0f'}, {'abstract': 'Apps have become vital in marketing mobile technologies to consumers, and the allegiance of app developers to Apple has helped propel the success of its devices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/technology/apple-keeps-loyalty-of-mobile-app-developers.html', 'snippet': 'Apps have become vital in marketing mobile technologies to consumers, and the allegiance of app developers to Apple has helped propel the success of its devices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Smartphones running Google’s Android operating system outsell iPhones more than two to one. And yet, even as Google’s system has gobbled up market share, Apple has held onto one critical advantage — the loyalty of mobile app developers. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1287, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/Apple/Apple-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Outsells, but Apple Cultivates Loyalty of App Developers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Android Outsells, but Apple Cultivates Loyalty of App Developers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':