country last week that Afghan officials say killed 18 civilians. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Allies Restrict Airstrikes on Taliban in Civilian Homes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Allies Restrict Airstrikes Against Taliban in Homes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petraeus, David H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, John R', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T23:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02264ded-d86c-5698-b974-b15c6db6c37f', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02264ded-d86c-5698-b974-b15c6db6c37f'}, {'abstract': 'Shawn Johnson, a gold medalist at the 2008 Olympics, attended the national gymnastics championships this weekend, but only as a spectator. She retired from the sport last week.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/a-fan-at-an-event-she-once-dominated/', 'snippet': 'Shawn Johnson, a gold medalist at the 2008 Olympics, attended the national gymnastics championships this weekend, but only as a spectator. She retired from the sport last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. LOUIS — Shawn Johnson, a gold medalist at the 2008 Olympics, walked into the arena to watch the United States gymnastics national championships on Sunday and felt her stomach flutter and her body start to shake.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fan at an Event She Once Dominated', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2008)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Shawn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T23:18:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6517ed0-7b10-504c-9fb4-850f782328a7', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6517ed0-7b10-504c-9fb4-850f782328a7'}, {'abstract': 'A groundbreaking deal between Clear Channel Communications and the Big Machine record label raised the possibility of a solution over compensation for broadcasting music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/business/media/radio-royalty-deal-offers-hope-for-industrywide-pact.html', 'snippet': 'A groundbreaking deal between Clear Channel Communications and the Big Machine record label raised the possibility of a solution over compensation for broadcasting music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the recording industry has lobbied Congress to change how radio stations pay royalties. The broadcasters have lobbied just as hard to preserve the status quo, making an agreement look all but impossible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/altRadio-1/altRadio-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/business/altRadio-1/altRadio-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Radio Royalty Deal Offers Hope for Industrywide Pact', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Radio Royalty Deal Offers Hope for Industrywide Pact', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royalties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clear Channel Communications Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Academy of Recording Arts and Sciences', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Recording Industry Assn of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Machine Records', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pandora Media Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lobbying and Lobbyists', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T23:26:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f2a2908-8353-5f66-9e1d-c474eff9f210', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f2a2908-8353-5f66-9e1d-c474eff9f210'}, {'abstract': 'One of the great mysteries of the 2012 playoffs is how the Kings suddenly transformed from a mediocre team that barely made the playoffs to the juggernaut they have been in the postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/10/luck-and-shooting-accuracy-in-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'One of the great mysteries of the 2012 playoffs is how the Kings suddenly transformed from a mediocre team that barely made the playoffs to the juggernaut they have been in the postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — One of the great mysteries of the 2012 playoffs is how the Kings suddenly transformed from a mediocre team that barely made the playoffs to the juggernaut they have been in the postseason. Even after losing two straight games for the first time this spring, courtesy of the revivified Devils in the Stanley Cup finals, they are still 15-4 in the postseason.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Luck and Shooting Accuracy in Los Angeles', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-10T23:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20bce324-16b1-5b0d-bcfe-38fd17feaa7d', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20bce324-16b1-5b0d-bcfe-38fd17feaa7d'}, {'abstract': 'Central to any solution to the European debt crisis will be the role of Spain’s prime minister, Mariano Rajoy, although he is known for playing both sides of an issue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/world/europe/mariano-rajoy-of-spain-steps-up-in-debt-crisis.html', 'snippet': 'Central to any solution to the European debt crisis will be the role of Spain’s prime minister, Mariano Rajoy, although he is known for playing both sides of an issue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Spain’s agreement to take a European bank bailout pushes the country into a pivotal role in determining how — and if — the euro zone can survive its debt crisis. Central to any solution will be Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy, who spent his first six months in power denying that a bailout would be necessary. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/world/RAJOY/RAJOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/11/world/RAJOY/RAJOY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/world/RAJOY/RAJOY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 751, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/world/RAJOY/RAJOY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1502, 'width': 20