paragraph': 'For more than five decades, the Chinatown Fair arcade attracted a steady stream of visitors, some drawn to its dim, dank and narrow battlefield of wall-to-wall Japanese street-fighter games, and others lured by a more peculiar attraction: a succession of chickens that took on all comers at tick-tack-toe, a few quarters at a time. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinatown Fair Is Back, Without Chickens Playing Tick-Tack-Toe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinatown Fair Is Back, Without Chickens Playing Tick-Tack-Toe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCADES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chickens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T00:41:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kia Gregory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gregory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ef23fbc-73c5-5f71-8a97-776ebdf7632b', 'word_count': 1239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ef23fbc-73c5-5f71-8a97-776ebdf7632b'}, {'abstract': 'After an article on sexual abuse at a Bronx private school appeared in The New York Times Magazine, former students volunteered new recollections of mistreatment by teachers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/nyregion/horace-mann-alumni-gathering-online-share-accounts-of-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'After an article on sexual abuse at a Bronx private school appeared in The New York Times Magazine, former students volunteered new recollections of mistreatment by teachers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One said a teacher had compelled her to have sex with him if she wanted a passing grade. Another said he had been sexually assaulted by a teacher after having a private dinner at his house. Others spoke of having been groped by faculty members while they were students. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10horacemann_ss-slide-3V5E-thumb/10horacemann_ss-slide-3V5E-thumb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/10/magazine/10horacemann_ss-slide-3V5E-thumb/10horacemann_ss-slide-3V5E-thumb-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gathering Online, Alumni of an Elite School Share Their Accounts of Abuse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gathering Online, Alumni of an Elite School Share Their Accounts of Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kamil, Amos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bennahum, David S', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Horace Mann School', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T00:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'las