he law in a federal appeals court, two federal district courts and a bankruptcy court. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Defense of Marriage Act, Exposed', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Defense of Marriage Act, Exposed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense of Marriage Act (1996)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T02:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bcc1618-2142-5790-bfd9-2572840b11d5', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bcc1618-2142-5790-bfd9-2572840b11d5'}, {'abstract': 'Intraparty disputes are not new in Texas, but rarely have the divisions become as heated as they have between supporters of Republican Senate candidates David Dewhurst and Ted Cruz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/us/politics/texas-runoff-between-cruz-and-dewhurst-fiercely-contested.html', 'snippet': 'Intraparty disputes are not new in Texas, but rarely have the divisions become as heated as they have between supporters of Republican Senate candidates David Dewhurst and Ted Cruz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT WORTH —