me': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auburn University', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christian, Edward', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Auburn (Ala)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillips, Ladarious K', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T02:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Tierney and Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tierney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c93bc9c2-c3d6-5048-8ee4-8f66dee384da', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c93bc9c2-c3d6-5048-8ee4-8f66dee384da'}, {'abstract': 'A new study shows that consumers are still being kept in the dark about overdraft fees. These costly games will continue until regulators require banks to provide clear, concise pricing information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/opinion/more-debit-card-follies-and-abuses.html', 'snippet': 'A new study shows that consumers are still being kept in the dark about overdraft fees. These costly games will continue until regulators require banks to provide clear, concise pricing information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal Consumer Financial Protection Bureau needs to bring transparency to debit card banking. The Federal Reserve made a good regulatory start in 2010, when it required banks to get account holders’ consent before enrolling them in overdraft “protection” programs that could cost them $35 each time they used a debit card and overdrew their account — the cards provide no warning of insufficient funds. Customers who did not opt in would have their purchases declined. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Debit Card Follies and Abuses', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Debit Card Follies and Abuses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T02:12:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6e9fa6b-5efd-5648-8b67-9e6542cfbf08', 'word_count': 258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6e9fa6b-5efd-5648-8b67-9e6542cfbf08'}, {'abstract': 'After the Kings’ Game 5 loss to the Devils in the Stanley Cup finals, team captain Dustin Brown said that “it’s been a long, long playoffs.” The Kings have no choice but to play through it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/sports/hockey/2012-stanley-cup-finals-kings-fighting-fatigue-as-well-as-devils.html', 'snippet': 'After the Kings’ Game 5 loss to the Devils in the Stanley Cup finals, team captain Dustin Brown said that “it’s been a long, long playoffs.” The Kings have no choice but to play through it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL SEGUNDO, Calif. — As the miles in the air and on the ice accumulate, as the hits become unrelenting, the temptation to sit on the beach and feel the soft breeze can become more pronounced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kings Fighting Fatigue, as Well as Devils', 'kicker': 'Stanley Cup Finals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Dustin (Ice Hockey)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T02:15:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': "By Joseph D'Hippolito", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "D'Hippolito", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ef013b8-92d5-52f6-9ae9-3f330fada4da', 'word_count': 589, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ef013b8-92d5-52f6-9ae9-3f330fada4da'}, {'abstract': 'Barry Obama smoked a lot of pot as a teenager. This doesn’t make him a reprobate; it makes him a product of his place and times. He came into his hobby as Hawaii’s marijuana culture hit its high point.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/opinion/pakalolo-and-the-president.html', 'snippet': 'Barry Obama smoked a lot of pot as a teenager. This doesn’t make him a reprobate; it makes him a product of his place and times. He came into his hobby as Hawaii’s marijuana culture hit its high point.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People with Hawaiian roots, like me, like to look for signs of true Hawaiianness in our president. Usually they’re subtle; these days Mr. Obama seems far more a product of the South Side of Chicago than the south shore of Oahu. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakalolo and the President', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakalolo and the President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorial Observer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T02:19:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bff77efd-ff90-550c-b221-2b6a0b9c6eab', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bff77efd-ff90-550c-b221-2b6a0b9c6eab'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney spoke to supporters at a campaign event in Des Moines, Iowa. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001592538/mitt-romney-in-des-moines-iowa.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney spoke to supporters at a campaign event in Des Moines, Iowa. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney spoke to supporters at a campaign event in Des Moines, Iowa. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xla