://article/d97815d4-4fff-5dee-b87e-72692e1cc924'}, {'abstract': 'A college counselor gives expert advice to maximize campus visits, including a tip to pretend you’re lost to get a sense of how students treat strangers.', 'web_url': 'https://thechoice.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/college-visit/', 'snippet': 'A college counselor gives expert advice to maximize campus visits, including a tip to pretend you’re lost to get a sense of how students treat strangers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brennan Barnard is the director of college counseling at The Derryfield School in Manchester, N.H. He recently wrote our June college checklist for rising seniors, which details what the members of the class of 2013 should be doing as they prepare for college. In this essay, Mr. Barnard provides more in-depth advice about visiting college campuses this summer. — Tanya Caldwell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Make the Most of a College Visit', 'kicker': 'The Choice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T09:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brennan Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brennan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50cee629-6443-5c71-bafb-08982d390543', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50cee629-6443-5c71-bafb-08982d390543'}, {'abstract': 'O.K., the Avian flu pandemic was a bust. But does that really mean the stockpiled food in my basement was overkill?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/we-the-survivors/', 'snippet': 'O.K., the Avian flu pandemic was a bust. But does that really mean the stockpiled food in my basement was overkill?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The other day, I came across a tin of powdered butter that I’d stored in my basement five years ago as part of an emergency cache. All I needed to do was add 27 cups of water and — voila! — I’d have a huge amount of peculiar-tasting buttery substance with which to adorn my bread and Kraft Dinner while I waited out an influenza pandemic in a pristine state of self-quarantine. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Survivors', 'kicker': 'A J Aiséirithe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Influenza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stockpiling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Pearson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pearson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c822af6-84a8-58af-9102-53afb5b7bf2f', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c822af6-84a8-58af-9102-53afb5b7bf2f'}, {'abstract': 'Why is the recovery from the most recent recession different? Local government employment has fallen by 3 percent from its peak, and is still falling, two economists note.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/americas-hidden-austerity-program/', 'snippet': 'Why is the recovery from the most recent recession different? Local government employment has fallen by 3 percent from its peak, and is still falling, two economists note.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Polak is the chairman of the economics department at Yale University. Peter K. Schott is a professor of economics at the Yale School of Management.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Hidden Austerity Program', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Local Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T10:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Polak and Peter K. Schott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Polak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Schott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/945d50d6-fdf3-5b9b-bdcf-49fbc4287a74', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/945d50d6-fdf3-5b9b-bdcf-49fbc4287a74'}, {'abstract': 'The European telecommunications operator has agreed to sell back more than one billion shares to China Unicom, as the European financial crisis continues to hurt earnings in Telefónica’s main markets.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/telefonica-to-sell-stake-in-china-unicom-for-1-4-billion/', 'snippet': 'The European telecommunications operator has agreed to sell back more than one billion shares to China Unicom, as the European financial crisis continues to hurt earnings in Telefónica’s main markets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Telefónica, the largest European telecommunications operator by revenue, has agreed to sell back a 4.56 percent stake in China Unicom, part of an effort by Telefónica to reduce debt as the European financial crisis continues to hurt earnings in its main markets in Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Telefonica to Sell Shares Back to China Unicom for $1.4 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Unicom (Hong Kong) Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Telefonica S.A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T10:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15aa3b1d-20ac-5479-af43-f0fdf9faadeb', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15aa3b1d-20ac-5479-af43-f0fdf9faadeb'}, {'abstract': 'Despite a series of initial offerings being withdrawn recently in Asia, the Malaysian palm oil giant Felda Global Venture Holdings appears to be filling order books ahead of pricing its I.P.O. on Wednesday, in what would be the world’s second-biggest offering this year, after Facebook.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/felda-moving-ahead-with-3-2-billion-i-p-o-in-malaysia/', 'snippet': 'Despite a series of initial offerings being withdrawn recently in Asia, the Malaysian palm oil giant Felda Global Venture Holdings appears to be filling order books ahead of pricing its I.P.O. on Wednesday, in what would be the world’s second-bigg...', 'lead_paragraph':