ather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e717d02-96f6-5428-9cc7-5bbec2b53981', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e717d02-96f6-5428-9cc7-5bbec2b53981'}, {'abstract': 'A recipe for home-style Finnish food.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/ravenous-fried-baltic-herring-at-home/', 'snippet': 'A recipe for home-style Finnish food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My kitchen in Helsinki is a repository for toy-size appliances: a half fridge that freezes all the vegetables that I’ve placed inside except for the palm-size, gold-flesh rutabagas that are as durable as they are delicious; two small burners that offer heat along with the unappetizing smell of an electrical fire; and a microwave that’s useless for cooking, so I’ve converted it into a storage cabinet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ravenous | Fried Baltic Herring, at Home', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T12:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monique Truong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Truong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/438fbf9a-4d25-59db-85e4-5d2e1550ceec', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/438fbf9a-4d25-59db-85e4-5d2e1550ceec'}, {'abstract': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/opinion-report-obamas-pakalolo-habit/', 'snippet': 'A summary of what’s on today’s editorial page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the editorial page', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Opinion Report: Obama’s Pakalolo Habit', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T12:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fddf573d-1465-564d-a1c0-8e6f37f530e2', 'word_count': 50, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fddf573d-1465-564d-a1c0-8e6f37f530e2'}, {'abstract': 'The outgoing leader of the Department of Energy’s ARPA-E research program reflects on the interconnectedness of technology, finance, business, markets and policies.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/q-and-a-a-panoramic-view-of-energy-innovation/', 'snippet': 'The outgoing leader of the Department of Energy’s ARPA-E research program reflects on the interconnectedness of technology, finance, business, markets and policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a busy two and a half years for Arun Majumdar, who is stepping down from his post as director of the Department of Energy’s Advanced Research Projects Agency for Energy. As the founding director, voice and face of the agency, better known as ARPA-E, Dr. Majumdar has been on the front lines of the Obama administration’s investments in experimental energy projects, many of which focus on improving efficiency, reducing pollution or devising plant-based alternatives to fossil fuels. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: A Panoramic View of Energy Innovation', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biofuels', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Synthetic Biology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advanced Research Projects Agency-Energy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berkeley (Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T12:09:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josie Garthwaite', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garthwaite', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93546aab-656a-527d-a0c5-7a8d7df09ec2', 'word_count': 1639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93546aab-656a-527d-a0c5-7a8d7df09ec2'}, {'abstract': 'Commerce Secretary John Bryson was hospitalized overnight after being involved in two hit-and-run accidents in Southern California.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/u-s-secretary-of-commerce-linked-to-hit-and-run/', 'snippet': 'Commerce Secretary John Bryson was hospitalized overnight after being involved in two hit-and-run accidents in Southern California.', 'l