d and Brian X. Chen report in Monday’s New York Times, Apple has held onto one critical advantage even as Google’s system has surged: the loyalty of mobile app developers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: App Developers Stick With Apple', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T12:36:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb3d1b65-7e75-5a3c-9a3c-8a187efe6d52', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb3d1b65-7e75-5a3c-9a3c-8a187efe6d52'}, {'abstract': 'The markets seem strangely unimpressed.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/things-you-really-dont-want-to-see-the-morning-after-a-bailout/', 'snippet': 'The markets seem strangely unimpressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a commonplace that the half-life of euro rescue plans has been steadily falling — that is, the time between the initial euphoria over the latest bailout loan or whatever and the realization that the fundamentals have not been addressed keeps getting shorter. Apparently that half-life is now down to a few hours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Things You Really Don’t Want To See The Morning After A Bailout', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T12:41:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96c9b93b-00bd-5fe9-ba71-f4161afe3596', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96c9b93b-00bd-5fe9-ba71-f4161afe3596'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney spoke at the Americans for Prosperity conference in Washington. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/multimedia/100000001593335/mitt-romney-in-washington.html', 'snippet': 'Mitt R