were related to drunken driving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Diehl, a longtime offensive lineman for the New York Giants, was arrested and charged with drunken driving after crashing his BMW into a row of parked cars in Astoria, Queens on Sunday night. Mr. Diehl was alone in the car, and no injuries were reported. The crash occurred around 8:45 p.m. near 31-31 35th Street. He was taken to the 114th Precinct station house. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Lineman Charged With Drunken Driving After Crashing Car', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diehl, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50c0598f-8d24-5a2b-97a3-0ef0c5fe52e7', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50c0598f-8d24-5a2b-97a3-0ef0c5fe52e7'}, {'abstract': 'What’s it like to write a young adult novel with your mother, when your mother is Jodi Picoult?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/video-whats-it-like-to-write-a-book-with-jodi-picoult/', 'snippet': 'What’s it like to write a young adult novel with your mother, when your mother is Jodi Picoult?', 'lead_paragraph': 'That’s my first question for Samantha van Leer, who just finished writing the young adult novel “Between the Lines” with her mother — who happens to be Jodi Picoult (it’s an unusual way to spend your sophomore and junior years of high school, if nothing else).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'VIDEO: What’s It Like to Write a Book With Jodi Picoult?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picoult, Jodi', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:04:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd00a0e1-9aee-5312-be5b-7b1be6de8f28', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd00a0e1-9aee-5312-be5b-7b1be6de8f28'}, {'abstract': 'Supporting a structure of kleptocracy.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/financial-repression-chinese-style/', 'snippet': 'Supporting a structure of kleptocracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have no idea whether this John Hempton piece on China is at all right, but it’s a terrific read, and provides food for thought.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Financial Repression, Chinese Style', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/825ea611-38af-5385-adb4-45e5bf156c1d', 'word_count': 192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/825ea611-38af-5385-adb4-45e5bf156c1d'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian government has rushed through a chilling anti-protest law, raising the tensions with an already restive protest movement.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/law-and-disorder/', 'snippet': 'The Russian government has rushed through a chilling anti-protest law, raising the tensions with an already restive protest movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The magic number in Moscow is now 12. At 12 noon on June 12 Muscovites plan to come out for another massive anti-government protest. Over the last few days, 12 people have been arrested on charges stemming from the last large-scale demonstration, which ended in violence on May 6.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Law and Disorder', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei N', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b479730-63ff-5d43-b589-b3b924515f5f', 'word_count': 823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b479730-63ff-5d43-b589-b3b924515f5f'}, {'abstract': 'The acquisition of Paradigm, a software company focused on the oil and natural gas industry, will allow Apax Partners and JMI Equity to take advantage of a push by energy companies to find new resources.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/apax-led-group-to-buy-paradigm-for-1-billion/', 'snippet': 'The acquisition of Paradigm, a software company focused on the oil and natural gas industry, will allow Apax Partners and JMI Equity to take advantage of a push by energy companies to find new resources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The private equity firms Apax Partners and JMI Equity agreed on Monday to buy Paradigm, a software company focused on the oil and natural gas industry, for $1 billion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apax and JMI Equity to Buy Paradigm for $1 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APAX PARTNERS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:18:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e67ecbc9-2637-54fb-a892-1930de97b522', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e67ecbc9-2637-54fb-a892-1930de97b522'}, {'abstract': 'She learned of her condition, she said Monday morning, during a time of personal high points — including improved ratings for her show, and an interview with President Obama.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/on-good-morning-america-robin-roberts-reveals-she-has-bone-marrow-disorder/', 'snippet': 'She learned of her condition, she said Monday morning, during a time of personal high points — including improved ratings for her show, and an interview with President Obama.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:15 p.m. | Updated  Robin Roberts, the co-host of “Good Morning America,” told viewers on Monday that she had been diagnosed with a rare blood and bone marrow disorder called M.D.S.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On ‘Good Morning America,’ Robin Roberts Reveals Bone Marrow Disorder', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, Robin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4282198b-aa42-570a-b246-f1352f0deed0', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4282198b-aa42-570a-b246-f1352f0deed0'}, {'abstract': 'Also, no afternoon TV program has broken out of the pack since the end of Oprah Winfrey’s show, and Gordon Brown contradicts earlier testimony in Britain’s inquiry into press ethics.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/the-breakfast-meeting-spinning-in-syria-and-a-no-fuss-coming-out-for-gay-actor/', 'snippet': 'Also, no afternoon TV program has broken out of the pack since the end of Oprah Winfrey’s show, and Gordon Brown contradicts earlier testimony in Britain’s inquiry into press ethics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the government of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria has used high-priced public relations advisers — veterans of the Clinton, Bush and Thatcher administrations — to portray themselves in the Western media as accessible, progressive and even glamorous, Bill Carter and Amy Chozick write. Until recently, the Assad government had a couple of obvious things working in its favor, in the words of a Middle East expert who once worked for a charity sponsored by Mr. Assad’s wife, Asma: “He speaks English, and his wife is hot.” The violent crackdown against the political opposition there has changed that friendly calculus — something the longtime ABC News correspondent Barbara Walters found out this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Spinning in Syria, and a ‘No Fuss’ Coming Out for Gay Actor', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:20:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/245e55a4-7ce4-54e4-8eeb-48bed836382e', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/245e55a4-7ce4-54e4-8eeb-48bed836382e'}, {'abstract': 'This Father’s Day, empower dad with a book about all that mom’s gone through to give him kids.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/bookshelf-body-back/', 'snippet': 'This Father’s Day, empower dad with a book about all that mom’s gone through to give him kids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s an audacious gift idea for Father’s Day: after he’s opened those Beach Boys tickets, slip him a copy of “Body Back” (Clementine, $30), a new book by Heather Porter. Its cover is red, with a nude by Natasha Law, but it’s not exactly that kind of title. When Daddy looks a little more closely, he’ll see that he’s holding “the mother’s handbook to medical, physical and emotional well-being.” Yes, you’re bestowing upon him the gift of knowledge about everything you’ve been through after you’ve given him and nurtured the greatest gifts of all — his children. Of course, it’s really a present for you, too (payback for all those surprises that were really for him, like cooking lessons and lingerie).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bookshelf | ‘Body Back’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:30:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Kane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c32ffca-5b16-5510-b889-2bc8cf1ff153', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c32ffca-5b16-5510-b889-2bc8cf1ff153'}, {'abstract': 'Two groups dropped lawsuits in which they contended that Google’s book-scanning in France violated copyright, and said they would offer digital versions of their works for Google to sell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/technology/french-publisher-group-strikes-deal-with-google-over-e-books.html', 'snippet': 'Two groups dropped lawsuits in which they contended that Google’s book-scanning in France violated copyright, and said they would offer digital versions of their works for Google to sell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Even as a dispute over Google’s digital book project deepens in the United States, the company said Monday that it had reached an agreement in France that could bring back to life thousands of out-of-print works. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'French Publisher Group Strikes Deal With Google Over E-Books', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Has Deal in France For Book-Scanning Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'French Publishers Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Societe des Gens de Lettres', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T13:34:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bffa262d-14b2-5bef-8105-df2705a0f9d7', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bffa262d-14b2-5bef-8105-df2705a0f9d7'}, {'abstract': 'A hat trick for Messi. Game 7 in the N.B.A. A split decision in the Bradley-Pacquiao fight. And a six-pitcher no-hitter. Those are three days worth replaying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/sports/a-weekend-long-on-memorable-sports-moments-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'A hat trick for Messi. Game 7 in the N.B.A. A split decision in the Bradley-Pacquiao fight. And a six-pitcher no-hitter. Those are three days worth replaying.', 'lead_paragraph': "As it turns out, the weekend was not big enough to contain all of the sporting events the gods — or the television executives — tried to cram in it. Something, apparently, had to give. So it rained in Paris and Rafael Nadal's victory in the men's French Open final leaked into Monday. Which means a Game 7 in the N.B.A., a Stanley Cup finals that will not die, the Belmont (deflated as it was), Euro 2012 openers, a Lionel Messi hat trick in a Brazil-Argentina friendly and a boxing match that turned into the sport's latest mess, a six-pitcher no-hitter by the Mariners, well, all of that was going to have to keep you occupied.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/basketball/12leadingpic/12leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/basketball/12leadingpic/12leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/basketball/12leadingpic/12leadingpic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'su