th who? Tune in to the first episode on TNT this Wednesday, June 13, at 9 p.m. Me? I’m anxious to know what Brewster has in her makeup bag and what she’s using to keep herself looking so luminous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Face Time | Jordana Brewster', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T14:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Turnbow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turnbow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a881f145-b4ce-523f-b8c7-30a58087b737', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a881f145-b4ce-523f-b8c7-30a58087b737'}, {'abstract': 'Buy good things and stay in them a long time. Investing success is as simple as that – and ignoring all of the noise around you.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/the-two-keys-to-investing-pickiness-and-persistence/', 'snippet': 'Buy good things and stay in them a long time. Investing success is as simple as that – and ignoring all of the noise around you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl Richards is a certified financial planner in Park City, Utah, and is the director of investor education at BAM Advisor Services. His book, “The Behavior Gap,” was published earlier this year. His sketches are archived here on the Bucks blog. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Two Keys to Investing: Pickiness and Persistence', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vanguard Group Inc', 'rank': 2, '