.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/really-quitting-smoking-is-harder-for-women/', 'snippet': 'Conventional wisdom says it is harder to quit for women, but the largest study of the claim to date finds that there is little difference in successful cessation rates among men and women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Really? Quitting Smoking Is Harder for Women', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Claim: Quitting smoking is harder for women.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T15:25:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a01c5352-d944-52ab-b76d-e5ce7684b002', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a01c5352-d944-52ab-b76d-e5ce7684b002'}, {'abstract': 'New experiments have found success in reducing congestion not by assessing fees but by offering discounts or cash to get drivers to change their habits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/science/experimental-campaigns-pay-drivers-to-avoid-rush-hour-traffic.html', 'snippet': 'New experiments have found success in reducing congestion not by assessing fees but by offering discounts or cash to get drivers to change their habits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PALO ALTO, Calif. — London, Singapore, Stockholm and a few other cities around the world battle heavy traffic with a “congestion charge,” a stiff fee for driving in crowded areas at peak hours. But drivers generally hate the idea, and efforts to impose it in this country have failed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12TRAF/12TRAF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 629, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12TRAF/12TRAF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1258, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12TRAF/12TRAF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12TRAF/12TRAF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12TRAF/12TRAF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Incentives for Drivers Who Avoid Traffic Jams', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Incentives For 