ooklike claws. Scientists are trying to copy that agility in a robot.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/science/cockroaches-split-second-escape-trick.html', 'snippet': 'In milliseconds, a roach can flip under a ledge by swinging its body around like a pendulum and hanging on underneath with hooklike claws. Scientists are trying to copy that agility in a robot.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cockroaches are not just insidious home invaders, a new study finds; they are also brilliant escape artists. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1469, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/science/12OBCOCKROACH2_SPAN/12OBOX2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Now You See It, Now It’s Swung Out of Sight', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Now You See It, Now It’s Swung Out of Sight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PLoS One', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cockroaches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T16:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96798416-5ce3-5e05-8e31-630941f35c86', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96798416-5ce3-5e05-8e31-630941f35c86'}, {'abstract': 'What babies remember; what birds know; and what humans eat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2012/06/12/science/12science_pod.html', 'snippet': 'What babies remember; what birds know; and what humans eat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What babies remember; what birds know; and what humans eat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What babies remember; what birds know; and what humans eat.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T16:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/be665eda-cc65-5886-970e-ee9bad74b0fa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/be665eda-cc65-5886-970e-ee9bad74b0fa'}, {'abstract': 'Any plan must raise more revenue, contribute to deficit reduction and address the growing nation’s growing disparity between rich and poor, Senator Max Baucus said.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/baucus-says-tax-overhaul-that-raises-revenue-is-moving-forward/', 'snippet': 'Any plan must raise more revenue, contribute to deficit reduction and address the growing nation’s growing disparity between rich and poor, Senator Max Baucus said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Max Baucus of Montana, the chairman of the Senate Finance Committee, said on Monday that an overhaul of the tax code was moving forward, but that any plan must raise more revenue, help reduce the deficit and address the nation’s growing disparity between rich and poor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Baucus Says Tax Overhaul That Raises Revenues Is Moving Forward', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baucus, Max', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bipartisan Policy Center Debt Reduction Task Force', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T16:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96294b30-4489-5e6e-8761-c50e8530ba3c', 'word_count': 557, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96294b30-4489-5e6e-8761-c50e8530ba3c'}, {'abstract': 'With a super PAC, friends can give the gift that keeps on giving: A seat in Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/buy-a-candidate/', 'snippet': 'With a super PAC, friends can give the gift that keeps on giving: A seat in Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Citizens United, the Supreme Court dismissed the idea that unlimited independent political expenditures from corporations or unions would lead “to corruption or the appearance of corruption” and held that “the appearance of influence or access will not cause the electorate to lose faith in this democracy.” This startlingly naïve decision, as well as lower court rulings and F.E.C. policies that rely on it, has given rise to a campaign system that’s best described as a Hobbesian state of nature.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Buy a Candidate', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T16:48:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2d3c78f-94b6-528c-af04-8d1eb78b0eb3', 'word_count': 447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2d3c78f-94b6-528c-af04-8d1eb78b0eb3'}, {'abstract': 'The author of the magazine’s cover article explains why it was finally time for this complicated story to be told.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/behind-the-cover-story-amos-kamil-on-sexual-abuse-at-horace-mann/', '