{'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84b289cc-553f-548e-815d-87c69c670d43', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84b289cc-553f-548e-815d-87c69c670d43'}, {'abstract': 'The dashing young Turk was one of the more compelling singers to perform for the Eurovision Song Contest last month.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/asked-answered-cam-bonomo/', 'snippet': 'The dashing young Turk was one of the more compelling singers to perform for the Eurovision Song Contest last month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ah, to be 25, dressed like a Left Bank buccaneer and belting out irresistible Anatolian pop before a televised audience of 125 million kitsch-craving European fans. Such was Can Bonomo’s perch at the Eurovision Song Contest last month. The dashing young Turk, from a Sephardic Jewish family in Izmir, represented Turkey in Eurovision. Though he did not win — the prize went to Swedish-Moroccan singer Loreen —\xa0Bonomo was one of the more compelling singers to take the enormous and purpose-built stage in Baku, Azerbaijan. His song “Love Me Back” was performed as a jaunty set piece, variously channeling Pirates of the Caribbean (the ride), Show Boat and Ali Baba. A spicy summer mix, you might say. Bonomo stopped whirling for a moment to talk to us about “Istanbul music” and more.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asked & Answered | Can Bonomo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T17:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Grant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a9d1c59-068d-508a-b2d3-05e14dafc0d4', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a9d1c59-068d-508a-b2d3-05e14dafc0d4'}, {'abstract': 'Hunter Kemper bounced back from a broken elbow to make the United States triathlon team, making London his fourth Olympic Games.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/kempers-fourth-olympics-was-no-sure-thing/', 'snippet': 'Hunter Kemper bounced back from a broken elbow to make the United States triathlon team, making London his fourth Olympic Games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When triathlete Hunter Kemper realized he had qualified for his fourth Olympic Games, the triumph wasn’t over his teammates. It was over his elbow. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kemper’s Fourth Olympics Was No Sure Thing', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemper, Hunter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T17:33:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6675e237-ce39-56c8-a645-e8f1f12a754c', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6675e237-ce39-56c8-a645-e8f1f12a754c'}, {'abstract': 'The United States has withdrawn a negotiating team from Pakistan in the latest sign that talks to reopen NATO supply routes into Afghanistan remain stalemated, American officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/world/asia/us-withdraws-team-from-pakistan-talks-on-nato-supply-routes.html', 'snippet': 'The United States has withdrawn a negotiating team from Pakistan in the latest sign that talks to reopen NATO supply routes into Afghanistan remain stalemated, American officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The United States has withdrawn a low-level negotiating team from Pakistan in the latest sign that talks to reopen NATO supply routes into neighboring Afghanistan remain stalemated, American officials said Monday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/global-home/12pakistan-image/12pakistan-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/global-home/12pakistan-image/12pakistan-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Takes Step Toward Exit in Pakistan Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan: U.S. Pulls Negotiators', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T17:48:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt and Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/453581f4-6039-5807-b89f-9dd229ec7dce', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/453581f4-6039-5807-b89f-9dd229ec7dce'}, {'abstract': 'The Enterprise remains visible from a pier in Manhattan. Once it is enclosed, it will not be open to the public until the museum opens an exhibition, scheduled for July 19.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/still-time-to-get-a-free-glimpse-of-space-shuttle/', 'snippet': 'The Enterprise remains visible from a pier in Manhattan. Once it is enclosed, it will not be open to the public until the museum opens an exhibition, scheduled for July 19.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The weather continues to interfere with plans for the space shuttle Enterprise, even after its oft-delayed arrival in Manhattan last week. But its new owners’ frustration is extending the opportunity for New Yorkers to get a good look at Enterprise free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Time to Get a Free Glimpse of the Space Shuttle', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T17:48:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fcda39d-a02a-5376-98e4-9361b2336781', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fcda39d-a02a-5376-98e4-9361b2336781'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal, the defending champion at Roland Garros, defeated Novak Djokovic on Monday to become the first man to win seven French Open singles titles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/sports/tennis/nadal-finishes-off-djokovic-for-seventh-french-open-title.html', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal, the defending champion at Roland Garros, defeated Novak Djokovic on Monday to become the first man to win seven French Open singles titles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Knees covered in clay, eyes wide and mouth agape, Rafael Nadal scaled the railing at Roland Garros and sprinted up the stands. His family stood waiting for him, and Nadal hugged them, one after another, until he came to his coach, his uncle Toni, who lifted his nephew off the ground.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/12tennis/12tennis-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/12tennis/12tennis-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/12tennis/12tennis-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/12tennis/12tennis-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/12tennis/12tennis-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width