ubstitute', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What We Eat: Doubts by the Teaspoonful', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Sweeteners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aspartame', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sucralose (Artificial Sweetener)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sugar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T18:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2486f24a-29de-56d3-880c-bb4930bc2bc2', 'word_count': 1559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2486f24a-29de-56d3-880c-bb4930bc2bc2'}, {'abstract': 'Times readers react to the Top 10 list of best Summer Olympics movies.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/readers-react-best-summer-olympics-movies/', 'snippet': 'Times readers react to the Top 10 list of best Summer Olympics movies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, The Times’s Victor Mather presented his list of the 10 best Summer Olympics movies of all time.  Readers expressed their thoughts on this topic on Twitter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers React: Best Summer Olympics Movies', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T18:12:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84013a7f-9e46-5827-99dc-f82bef0744f1', 'word_count': 58, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84013a7f-9e46-5827-99dc-f82bef0744f1'}, {'abstract': 'Human rights groups said the detainees’ cases presented questions about whether an earlier ruling giving detainees a right to challenge their imprisonment was being followed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/us/politics/justices-decline-to-hear-appeals-by-guantanamo-detainees.html', 'snippet': 'Human rights groups said the detainees’ cases presented questions about whether an earlier ruling giving detainees a right to challenge their imprisonment was being followed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Monday refused to hear appeals from seven men held at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, passing up an opportunity to clarify its last Guantánamo decision, in 2008. That ruling, in Boumediene v. Bush, gave prisoners at Guantánamo a “meaningful opportunity” to challenge their detentions in court.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1202, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Reject Detainees’ Appeal, Leaving Cloud Over Earlier Guantánamo Ruling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Justices Reject Detainees’ Appeal, Leaving Cloud Over Earlier Guantánamo Ruling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T18:16:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db0a7b5e-e075-5c12-9548-1d1705210201', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db0a7b5e-e075-5c12-9548-1d1705210201'}, {'abstract': 'Under an agreement with 11 states that sued over delays, the agency is expected to announce proposed rules on fine particulates on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/e-p-a-soot-rules-expected-this-week/', 'snippet': 'Under an agreement with 11 states that sued over delays, the agency is expected to announce proposed rules on fine particulates on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal Environmental Protection Agency plans to propose new air quality standards for soot by Thursday and issue final standards by Dec. 14 under a tentative agreement with 11 states that sued the agency earlier this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Soot Rules Expected This Week', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Air Act', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'ma