lass, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/136871f7-7907-52b9-b159-73312a8d8bd3', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/136871f7-7907-52b9-b159-73312a8d8bd3'}, {'abstract': 'Interviews with fans of England and France attending their Euro 2012 match in Donetsk, Ukraine, said they had generally been treated well so far in the host countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/sports/soccer/france-ties-england-amid-heavy-security-and-concerns-of-racist-behavior.html', 'snippet': 'Interviews with fans of England and France attending their Euro 2012 match in Donetsk, Ukraine, said they had generally been treated well so far in the host countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DONETSK, Ukraine — On a day of blistering heat and searing chances from France, England desperately held on for a 1-1 tie in the opening match for both teams at the European Championships.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/ENGLAND1/ENGLAND1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/ENGLAND1/ENGLAND1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/ENGLAND1/ENGLAND1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/ENGLAND1/ENGLAND1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'super