 version of our e-mail conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drilling Down: Does the ‘Freemium’ Model Really Work?', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDERSON, CHRIS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Fred', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T19:30:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/457c5541-1c13-5031-9350-24f3fa2c2b73', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/457c5541-1c13-5031-9350-24f3fa2c2b73'}, {'abstract': 'Our summer reading contest begins on Friday and lasts all summer. If you’re still not convinced you should participate, you should read what this New Jersey high school teacher has to say.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/guest-blog-taking-a-dip-in-the-nonfiction-pool-with-our-summer-reading-contest/', 'snippet': 'Our summer reading contest begins on Friday and lasts all summer. If you’re still not convinced you should participate, you should read what this New Jersey high school teacher has to say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you were among the thousands who posted about #summerreading on Twitter last Thursday, thank you again. The hashtag has been going strong ever since, and we expect readers to keep posting thoughts and recommendations all season long. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guest Blog | ‘Taking a Dip in the Nonfiction Pool’ With Our Summer Reading Contest', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T19:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ade1b9e7-3575-5386-9e3d-3ee52fe2e942', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ade1b9e7-3575-5386-9e3d-3ee52fe2e942'}, {'abstract': 'Emigrate expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/latvia-and-the-romney-record/', 'snippet': 'Emigrate expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, not a connection you expected anyone to make. But there’s something there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latvia and the Romney Record', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T19:32:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f722659-628b-5c8a-9b09-b13a6f6887ec', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f722659-628b-5c8a-9b09-b13a6f6887ec'}, {'abstract': 'Autonomous Research, a London-based boutique research firm, has hired Guy Moszkowski from Bank of America Merrill Lynch as the chief executive of its United States operations.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/bank-of-americas-moszkowski-to-join-a-research-boutique/', 'snippet': 'Autonomous Research, a London-based boutique research firm, has hired Guy Moszkowski from Bank of America Merrill Lynch as the chief executive of its United States operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Autonomous Research, a London-based boutique research firm, has decided to expand in the United States in a big way — by hiring one of the top banking analysts around.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bank of America’s Moszkowski to Join a Research Boutique', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moszkowski, Guy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Autonomous Research LLP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T19:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca55f24-9780-5bee-a7a8-f8d4e971eb5e', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca55f24-9780-5bee-a7a8-f8d4e971eb5e'}, {'abstract': 'In a report to Group of 20 leaders, regulators and central bankers found that the United States, the European Union and Japan are behind schedule on measures that w