ne the other day. “I see lethargy and leisure time as my enemy. I’m not a guy who should have a lot of free time. It’s bad for me.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Bourdain Is All Over the Media Menu', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T19:59:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7bdbbdf-6dbd-5c0c-b3d6-fdbbc83bf468', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7bdbbdf-6dbd-5c0c-b3d6-fdbbc83bf468'}, {'abstract': 'This flirty pop-over mixes parachute silk with the blue jean basic beautifully.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/just-one-look-nina-ricci-2/', 'snippet': 'This flirty pop-over mixes parachute silk with the blue jean basic beautifully.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There are slightly more casual references this season,” said Nina Ricci’s Peter Copping at this morning’s resort presentation. “This is the first time we’ve done denim.” (So easily did this denim fit into Copping’s equation for resort, one would never have known it was a novelty unless told.) Showed in the company of quintessential skirt suits, butterfly-themed pieces (a printed romper being the Parisian house’s idea of beachwear) and looks that matched dress to trench, this flirty pop-over mixes parachute silk with the blue jean basic beautifully.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Nina Ricci', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ricci, Nina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T20:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d206e831-9e3f-556b-aa0c-eebcf3a80ea3', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d206e831-9e3f-556b-aa0c-eebcf3a80ea3'}, {'abstract': 'A popular class of drugs used to treat Type 2 diabetes may increase the risk of vision problems, a new study suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/popular-diabetes-drugs-carry-vision-risks/', 'snippet': 'A popular class of drugs used to treat Type 2 diabetes may increase the risk of vision problems, a new study suggests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A popular class of drugs used to treat Type 2 diabetes may increase the risk of vision problems, a new study suggests, underlining the importance of regular eye exams for anyone with diabetes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diabetes Drugs Carry Vision Risks', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diabetes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T20:00:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23e18ec3-bb9e-55bc-b0ea-8161d95f5208', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23e18ec3-bb9e-55bc-b0ea-8161d95f5208'}, {'abstract': 'The Fed’s latest figures on wealth show the middle class sustaining the biggest decline since the housing boom ended. And they show an odd finding on a group whose income rose.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/where-wealth-declined-most-and-an-income-riddle/', 'snippet': 'The Fed’s latest figures on wealth show the middle class sustaining the biggest decline since the housing boom ended. And they show an odd finding on a group whose income rose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The bleak portrait of the financial health of American families that the Federal Reserve published Monday shows that the impact of the economic crisis has fallen with disproportionate weight on the middle class.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Wealth Declined Most (and an Income Riddle)', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T20:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aa1dd2e-a371-5315-abaf-593d0116ec68', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aa1dd2e-a371-5315-abaf-593d0116ec68'}, {'abstract': 'Here are the results from the New Yorker’s contest asking readers to imagine corporate/literary mashups.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/little-dorito-and-more-suggestions-for-literary-product-placement/', 'snippet': 'Here are the results from the New Yorker’s contest asking readers to imagine corporate/literary mashups.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A blogger’s recent discovery that a 99-cent e-book version of “War and Peace” sold in Barnes and Noble’s Nook Store had replaced every instance of the ordinary English word “kindle” with the word “Nook” prompted much online tittering about the wisdom of outsourcing book digitization to a company named Superior Formatting Publishing as well as reminders of the deep roots of literary product placement. (When Jules Verne began serializing “Around the World in 80 Days” in 1872 shipping companies lobbied to be name-checked in the text.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Little Dorito’ and More: Suggestions for Literary Product Placement', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Product Placement', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenman, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T20:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a8667de-20a0-5b83-8c7e-c402dca3fdde', 'word_count': 320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a8667de-20a0-5b83-8c7e-c402dca3fdde'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Haste, a New York police officer, is expected to surrender on Wednesday on charges of first- and second-degree manslaughter in the shooting of 18-year-old Ramarley Graham.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/nyregion/officer-to-face-manslaughter-charges-in-bronx-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Haste, a New York police officer, is expected to surrender on Wednesday on charges of first- and second-degree manslaughter in the shooting of 18-year-old Ramarley Graham.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A police officer will be prosecuted on manslaughter charges in the shooting death of Ramarley Graham, an 18-year-old who was killed by a single police bullet in his bathroom after a team of narcotics officers broke into his Bronx home, three people briefed on the charges said Monday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/GRAHAM/GRAHAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/GRAHAM/GRAHAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/GRAHAM/GRAHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/GRAHAM/GRAHAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/GRAHAM/GRAHAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Faces Manslaughter Charges in a Bronx Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officer Faces Manslaughter Charges in a Bronx Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haste, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Ramarley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T20:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein and Wendy Ruderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'la