ns', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T20:43:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5e9141-9fd5-5e37-9c00-b3112dbfa328', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5e9141-9fd5-5e37-9c00-b3112dbfa328'}, {'abstract': 'Some reports have “air rage” incidents rising sharply, while others seem to indicate that Americans are the world’s best-behaved airline passengers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/business/air-rage-might-or-might-not-be-increasing-on-the-road.html', 'snippet': 'Some reports have “air rage” incidents rising sharply, while others seem to indicate that Americans are the world’s best-behaved airline passengers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EVERY time I watch the television news, somebody is urgently talking about some new threat to become alarmed about. I’m thinking, in particular, about the scary report on CNN recently — widely cited in the media — that “air rage” incidents are up sharply.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/Road/Road-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/Road/Road-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1740, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/Road/Road-thumbStandard.jpg