il (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:24:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a53ba7aa-4a51-56ee-8ebe-536947e440de', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a53ba7aa-4a51-56ee-8ebe-536947e440de'}, {'abstract': 'Wu created an insect-inspired palette rich in tropical greens and corals.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/just-one-look-jason-wu-2/', 'snippet': 'Wu created an insect-inspired palette rich in tropical greens and corals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jason Wu focused on nature and its interaction with man for resort. Taking cues from the artist Mike Libby, who is best known for making bugs and beetles from old watch parts, Wu created an insect-inspired palette rich in tropical greens and corals. An oversize botanical print tee bloomed over a pair of pin-thin white trousers with a black waistband — ideal for gardening with the C.Z. Guest crowd. Contrasting the prim and pretty pieces Wu is known for were electric blue leather separates: a motorcycle jacket, a pencil skirt with an exposed zipper. Flourishing alongside these were a bevy of evening looks, including a black crystal embroidered dress and a peekaboo black and cream jersey top over a navy sheer skirt. This sporty crochet striped bikini with matching boy shorts and color-blocked backpack is destined for a trip to Turks and Caicos, where Wu is headed as soon as the season closes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Jason Wu', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:25:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2adf3d6f-e239-5fc4-9752-4a2e8ac2abd5', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2adf3d6f-e239-5fc4-9752-4a2e8ac2abd5'}, {'abstract': 'Letters to the editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/science/does-doctor-know-best-4-letters.html', 'snippet': 'Letters to the editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Doctor Know Best? (4 Letters)', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Does Doctor Know Best?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ae66244-4b10-5b5b-ade8-e1bf880f19e7', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ae66244-4b10-5b5b-ade8-e1bf880f19e7'}, {'abstract': 'The two chefs behind a Boston tapas restaurant plan to open in Chelsea in the fall.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/bostons-toro-to-bring-tapas-to-new-york/', 'snippet': 'The two chefs behind a Boston tapas restaurant plan to open in Chelsea in the fall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Boston chefs, Ken Oringer (right) and Jamie Bissonnette, are planning to open a New York outpost of Toro, the Spanish tapas restaurant they founded in that city in 2005. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston’s Toro to Bring Tapas to New York', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:27:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7402d19-4731-5810-8a87-57babec35299', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7402d19-4731-5810-8a87-57babec35299'}, {'abstract': 'A new feature on the iPhone moves Apple closer to the mobile wallet business by storing digital payment options and loyalty cards in one handy application.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/apple-empties-your-wallet-and-puts-it-in-the-iphone/', 'snippet': 'A new feature on the iPhone moves Apple closer to the mobile wallet business by storing digital payment options and loyalty cards in one handy application.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Passbook that Apple announced on Monday is not quite a wallet, but it nudges us one step closer to turning our phones into pocketbooks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Puts Your Wallet in the iPhone', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77fa07c5-3c99-5f02-ba68-f02f16b7ed55', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77fa07c5-3c99-5f02-ba68-f02f16b7ed55'}, {'abstract': 'Apple’s new releases are usually sold for their effect on consumers and educators. With iPhones and iPads increasingly making their way into offices, however, and cloud computing blurring the line between work and home, Apple is becoming an enterprise device company, too. Some of the new features show how.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/apple-steps-further-into-the-enterprise/', 'snippet': 'Apple’s new releases are usually sold for their effect on consumers and educators. With iPhones and iPads increasingly making their way into offices, however, and cloud computing blurring the line between work and home, Apple is becoming an enterp...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Apple’s new product announcements on Monday got a lot of attention as consumer purchases. Hello, sports score-reciting Siri. Goodbye, 17-inch laptop. Several of the features on display, however, show that Apple is also interested in stepping up its presence in products for organizations. It amounts to a new series of challenges to Microsoft as it prepares to release its Windows 8 operating system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple Steps Further Into the Business Market', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Enterprise Computing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cisco Systems Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Skype Technologies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9140ef8d-4a07-5ca2-ae4e-ead88d8d4df5', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9140ef8d-4a07-5ca2-ae4e-ead88d8d4df5'}, {'abstract': 'Two years after being forced to return the piano and resign, the former administrator has settled his case with the city’s conflicts board and agreed to a $1,000 fine.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/lesson-for-principal-dont-walk-off-with-schools-grand-piano/', 'snippet': 'Two years after being forced to return the piano and resign, the former administrator has settled his case with the city’s conflicts board and agreed to a $1,000 fine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People take all sorts of things from the workplace: pens, paper, maybe a stapler now and again, but what about a grand piano?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lesson for Principal:  Don’t Walk Off With School’s Grand Piano', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Piano Was Meant for School, But Principal Took It Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pianos', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Principals (School)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest Board (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:33:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric P. Newcomer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Newcomer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2262f22-b13d-505d-8fd4-85c4630bbc53', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2262f22-b13d-505d-8fd4-85c4630bbc53'}, {'abstract': 'The Indian dancer Ramya Ramnarayan performed Bharatanatyam pieces at the Ailey Citigroup Theater on Saturday evening.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/arts/dance/ramya-ramnarayan-at-ailey-citigroup-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The Indian dancer Ramya Ramnarayan performed Bharatanatyam pieces at the Ailey Citigroup Theater on Saturday evening.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a particular feature of traditional Indian dance that a solo performer, with musicians, can hold the attention of an audience for an evening’s entire recital. In ballet few ballerina solos last longer than two minutes. On Saturday evening Ramya Ramnarayan danced for two hours, leaving the stage only briefly in the pauses between her five numbers. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/ramya1/ramya1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/ramya1/ramya1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/ramya1/ramya1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/ramya1/ramya1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/ramya1/ramya1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Slowly, Subtly, Invoking the Divine', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Slowly, Subtly, Invoking the Divine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:36:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a3685e6-1087-5cd7-a86f-67a06936e967', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a3685e6-1087-5cd7-a86f-67a06936e967'}, {'abstract': 'A rise in temperatures speeds the release of carbon dioxide from soil in forests, which in turn could accelerate global warming, researchers report.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/warming-will-unlock-carbon-in-forests-study-warns/', 'snippet': 'A rise in temperatures speeds the release of carbon dioxide from soil in forests, which in turn could accelerate global warming, researchers report.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Climate scientists have long been concerned about the possibility that warming temperatures will speed changes on the earth’s surface that will in turn accelerate global warming. The best illustration of such a feedback loop involves the melting of sea ice in the Arctic. The ice reflects solar radiation back into space rather than absorbing it. When it melts, it leaves open water that absorbs the heat rather than reflecting it. The more warm water there is, the more ice melts, and so on. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Warming Will Unlock Carbon in Forests, Study Warns', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carbon Dioxide', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soil', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Irvine', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:36:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicity Barringer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barringer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42982a19-8312-53a5-b4f4-00d88347e76c', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42982a19-8312-53a5-b4f4-00d88347e76c'}, {'abstract': 'Apps can now deliver information like blood glucose levels, the location of a stent or the name of the nearest specialty hospital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/business/apps-for-the-traveler-with-medical-issues.html', 'snippet': 'Apps can now deliver information like blood glucose levels, the location of a stent or the name of the nearest specialty hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Travelers with chronic ailments like diabetes or high blood pressure have long struggled to remember when to take their pills as they cross time zones. Or they may have had a hard time finding emergency care in a foreign country or communicating about complicated health conditions. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/Medical1/Medical1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/Medical1/Medical1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1217, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The App as Health Aide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The App as Health Aide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:41:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Weed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/005e7db1-c430-54c8-a629-0763c800fda9', 'word_count': 1118, 'uri': 'nyt://article/005e7db1-c430-54c8-a629-0763c800fda9'}, {'abstract': 'The study found more psychological and social problems among young adults from broken homes who had a gay parent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/health/study-examines-effect-of-having-a-gay-parent.html', 'snippet': 'The study found more psychological and social problems among young adults from broken homes who had a gay parent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young adults from broken homes in which a parent had had a same-sex relationship reported modestly more psychological and social problems in their current lives than peers from other families that had experienced divorce and other disruptions, a new study has found, stirring bitter debate among partisans on gay marriage.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debate on a Study Examining Gay Parents', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Debate On a Study Examining Gay Parents', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:41:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benedict Carey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benedict', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a1da4c9-18b8-5ef3-bc3e-7826b85e4ac0', 'word_count': 743, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a1da4c9-18b8-5ef3-bc3e-7826b85e4ac0'}, {'abstract': 'It can take a long for abused children to come forward. We need more lenient statutes of limitation.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/humiliation-shame-and-fear/', 'snippet': 'It can take a long for abused children to come forward. We need more lenient statutes of limitation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On this first day of the Jerry Sandusky child sex abuse trial, the prosecutor, Joseph McGettigan, put the following words up on a screen: humiliation, shame and fear. Those are the reasons it almost always takes a long time for abused children to come forward, if they ever do, perhaps especially boys raped by older men.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Humiliation, Shame and Fear', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statutes of Limitations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d928d08-ce50-5b59-accb-3cd826fe732f', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d928d08-ce50-5b59-accb-3cd826fe732f'}, {'abstract': 'Apple now has 400 million active accounts in iTunes with credit cards. That means that all of Apple’s iOS devices are linked to those credit cards, too, challenging Google Wallet and others in the race to become a smartphone payment method.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/apples-stash-of-credit-card-numbers-is-its-secret-weapon/', 'snippet': 'Apple now has 400 million active accounts in iTunes with credit cards. That means that all of Apple’s iOS devices are linked to those credit cards, too, challenging Google Wallet and others in the race to become a smartphone payment method.', 'lead_paragraph': 'screenshot via Apple', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Stash of Credit Card Numbers Is Its Secret Weapon', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:45:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/154be31e-70b2-5e67-b343-d4884b7dbce8', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/154be31e-70b2-5e67-b343-d4884b7dbce8'}, {'abstract': 'After years on the margins, the blaring, pulsating sound of electronic dance music is ascendant, and Las Vegas has embraced the trend the only way it knows how: by going all in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/arts/music/djs-and-dance-music-are-the-new-stars-in-las-vegas.html', 'snippet': 'After years on the margins, the blaring, pulsating sound of electronic dance music is ascendant, and Las Vegas has embraced the trend the only way it knows how: by going all in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Steve Wynn, the 70-year-old casino magnate, stood before an invitation-only crowd at the opening of a Japanese restaurant here last week, promising good food and even better music.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/MUSIC/MUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/MUSIC/MUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/MUSIC/MUSIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/MUSIC/MUSIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/MUSIC/MUSIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/MUSIC/MUSIC-t