ing that the social network’s shares will struggle for some time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Drumbeat of Bad News, Investors Bet Against Facebook', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:48:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ca02604-e4bb-5dc8-a79c-3d6cee9c611d', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ca02604-e4bb-5dc8-a79c-3d6cee9c611d'}, {'abstract': 'A $150 million building devoted to artifacts from the American Revolution is to be constructed in Independence National Historic Park in Philadelphia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/arts/design/revolution-museum-unveils-design-by-robert-a-m-stern.html', 'snippet': 'A $150 million building devoted to artifacts from the American Revolution is to be constructed in Independence National Historic Park in Philadelphia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'George Washington’s tent. His camp cups. The gun used by the minuteman commander who faced the British on the North Bridge in Concord. These are a few of the artifacts that will be on display when the American Revolution Center, a nonprofit educational organization, builds and moves into its new home, the Museum of the American Revolution, steps from Independence Hall and the Liberty Bell in Philadelphia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 545, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1090, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/museum/museum-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Design Shown for Museum of American Revolution', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Design Shown for Museum Of American Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Revolutionary War, American (1775-83)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the American Revolution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Robert A M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:54:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/722fc9ad-26a2-5713-9d2b-58ca0f862b0a', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/722fc9ad-26a2-5713-9d2b-58ca0f862b0a'}, {'abstract': 'Jake Ballard is focused on recovering from an A.C.L. injury and returning to play for the Giants in 2013, assuming he clears waivers.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/ballard-is-waived-but-hopes-to-be-back/', 'snippet': 'Jake Ballard is focused on recovering from an A.C.L. injury and returning to play for the Giants in 2013, assuming he clears waivers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Giants tight end Jake Ballard was lifting weights at the team’s training facility Monday when he received a phone call from his agent, Blake Baratz, who told him that he was going to be waived. Baratz then explained that the move was mostly procedural — the team was going to waive him, then re-sign him Tuesday afternoon, assuming he cleared waivers, at which point he could be placed on the physically-unable-to-perform list as he continues to rehabilitate his injured knee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ballard Is Waived but Hopes to Be Back', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ballard, Jake', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T21:56:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e05d9b18-e0a0-5eed-b390-d3625c0747c4', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e05d9b18-e0a0-5eed-b390-d3625c0747c4'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Monday’s selection includes artists scanning sculptures in the Metropolitan Museum of Art for reproduction with 3-D printers and what the chief executive of Nasdaq did during the Facebook stock offering.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/todays-scuttlebot-star-trails-and-sculpture-scans/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Monday’s selection includes artists scanning sculptures in the Metropolitan Museum of Art for reproduction with 3-D printers and what the ch...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web on Monday. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna