/06/12/us/louisiana-execution-vacated-in-linked-cases.html', 'snippet': 'A judge vacated the death sentence of a man, five months after the Supreme Court tossed out his conviction in a different case because prosecutors did not turn over key evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge in New Orleans on Monday vacated the death sentence of a Louisiana man, five months after the United States Supreme Court tossed out his conviction in a different case because prosecutors did not turn over key evidence. The conviction of the man, Juan Smith, that was vacated by the Supreme Court was for his role in a 1995 mass murder. The conviction that led to Mr. Smith’s death sentence arose from another multiple murder that year. Lawyers for Mr. Smith had argued that his death sentence in the latter case was obtained largely on the basis of the previous conviction and should be vacated because of the Supreme Court’s ruling. The Orleans Parish District Attorney’s office plans a retrial in the case the court addressed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Louisiana: Execution Vacated in Linked Cases', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Louisiana: Execution Vacated In Linked Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Juan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-11T23:45:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'sectio