ument_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a34ded2-eba9-5245-a3e5-1b3c8d805e32', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a34ded2-eba9-5245-a3e5-1b3c8d805e32'}, {'abstract': 'The delayed arrival of the Boeing 787 Dreamliner and a dispute between pilots has hurt India in its newest effort to shine on the international stage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/world/asia/at-air-india-a-nations-latest-stumble-in-the-spotlight.html', 'snippet': 'The delayed arrival of the Boeing 787 Dreamliner and a dispute between pilots has hurt India in its newest effort to shine on the international stage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Like China, India has long been eager to showcase the best features of its fast-growing economy on the international stage. But whenever it gets a chance to shine, something almost invariably goes wrong.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/AIRINDIA/AIRINDIA-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Time to Shine, India Can’t Get Off the Ground', 'kicker': 'Memo From New Delhi', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Time to Shine, India Can’t Get Off the Ground', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR INDIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T01:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5329f995-0951-5d92-83d4-66c7254847a9', 'word_count': 945, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5329f995-0951-5d92-83d4-66c7254847a9'}, {'abstract': 'A visit three years ago provided the occasion for a strong message from General Manager Brian Cashman, en route to the Yankees’ 27th World Series title.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/back-in-atlanta-yanks-recalling-2009/', 'snippet': 'A visit three years ago provided the occasion for a strong message from General Manager Brian Cashman, en route to the Yankees’ 27th World Series title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — The last time the Yankees came to Atlanta during interleague play was in 2009, the year they went on to win their 27th World Series. But at the time of their visit here the Yankees were underachieving. They had lost four of their previous six games and two straight and General Manager Brian Cashman was concerned.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Back in Atlanta, Yanks Recalling 2009', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cashman, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T01:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecfaf2e2-dc95-55a6-a77c-a78cc044c4f8', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecfaf2e2-dc95-55a6-a77c-a78cc044c4f8'}, {'abstract': '“Explosive” growth among deeply religious groups has fueled the population rise, a study says, challenging the entrenched image of New York Jews as liberal, affluent and well educated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/nyregion/new-yorks-jewish-population-is-growing-again.html', 'snippet': '“Explosive” growth among deeply religious groups has fueled the population rise, a study says, challenging the entrenched image of New York Jews as liberal, affluent and well educated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After decades of decline, the Jewish population of New York City is growing again, increasing to nearly 1.1 million, fueled by the “explosive” growth of the Hasidic and other Orthodox communities, a new study has found. It is a trend that is challenging long-held notions about the group’s cultural identity and revealing widening gaps on politics, education, wealth and religious observance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/CENSUS1/CENSUS1-thumbL