reak and the memory of Joshua Chamberlain may affect the shape of the Senate next year.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/the-colonel-and-the-governor/', 'snippet': 'How Angus King, Maine’s fierce independent streak and the memory of Joshua Chamberlain may affect the shape of the Senate next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had last seen Angus King standing on the shores of Maine’s Casco Bay, reading from the autobiography of Col. Joshua Lawrence Chamberlain.\xa0This was at a benefit for Maine writers and publishers back in 2009.\xa0Chamberlain, a revered figure in Maine, was the Bowdoin College professor who prevented the flanking of Federal lines on the second day of the Battle of Gettysburg, and who might, as a result, have single-handedly saved the Union.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Colonel and the Governor', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chamberlain, Joshua', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Angus Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Margaret Chase', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowe, Olympia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T01:52:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Finney Boylan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Finney', 'lastname': 'Boylan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7679c21-3957-5a78-ad87-437a3039e76f', 'word_count': 1512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7679c21-3957-5a78-ad87-437a3039e76f'}, {'abstract': 'President Hugo Chávez, battling cancer as he runs for re-election, has not declared an heir apparent, raising speculation about who could take his place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/world/americas/hugo-chavez-forces-venezuela-to-contemplate-a-void.html', 'snippet': 'President Hugo Chávez, battling cancer as he runs for re-election, has not declared an heir apparent, raising speculation about who could take his place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — President Hugo Chávez is the undisputed, 24-7, one-man show of Venezuelan politics, its be-all and end-all. He makes laws on his own, with the stroke of a pen. He expropriates buildings and businesses with the wave of a hand. His face smiles from billboards and posters. He posts his thoughts on Twitter. He talks on television for hours on end. He even sings and dances.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/VENEZUELA/VENEZUELA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/world/VENEZUELA/VENEZUELA-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/VENEZUELA/VENEZUELA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/world/VENEZUELA/VENEZUELA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 