stions about data and the authors’ industry ties have surrounded a study about hydrofracking in Pennsylvania that was done by a new research arm at the State University at Buffalo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report from a new institute at the State University at Buffalo asserting that state oversight has made natural gas drilling safer is causing tumult on campus and beyond, with critics arguing that the institute is biased toward industry and could undercut the university’s reputation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/BUFFALO/BUFFALO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/nyregion/BUFFALO/BUFFALO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Institute’s Gas Drilling Report Leads to Claims of Bias and Concern for a University’s Image', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Institute’s Gas Drilling Report Leads to Claims of Bias and Concern for a University’s Image', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York at Buffalo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T01:59:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57295c6f-8017-56b0-8ed9-1d150916c1db', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57295c6f-8017-56b0-8ed9-1d150916c1db'}, {'abstract': 'Join me as we float through Peter A. Collins’s puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/ice-cream/', 'snippet': 'Join me as we float through Peter A. Collins’s puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TUESDAY’S PUZZLE — Well, we are just awash in water images today, aren’t we? Man your canoes and strap on those life jackets, my friends; we are riding some rapids through Peter A. Collins’s puzzle. We’ve got MOON RIVER, RED RIVER, WILD RIVER and even THE BRIDGE OVER THE RIVER KWAI running through the grid. Oh, yes, and there’s the RIO BRAVO there in the southeast. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ice Cream or Candy', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea9e8daa-c06e-5883-adab-b523446da2a5', 'word_count': 341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea9e8daa-c06e-5883-adab-b523446da2a5'}, {'abstract': 'Burdens are just about equally distributed among the eclectic characters in “Storefront Church,” John Patrick Shanley’s unwieldy but affecting new play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/theater/reviews/storefront-church-by-john-patrick-shanley.html', 'snippet': 'Burdens are just about equally distributed among the eclectic characters in “Storefront Church,” John Patrick Shanley’s unwieldy but affecting new play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Burdens are just about equally distributed among the eclectic characters in “Storefront Church,” John Patrick Shanley’s unwieldy but affecting new play about a handful of Bronx dwellers whose lives become tangled in unexpected ways when a mortgage goes sour. With the exception of one willfully oblivious bank executive, the men and women who find themselves gathering for a church service at the play’s conclusion all feel a measure of sorrow from the hard compromises life demands — but perhaps also a sense that burdens are lightened when shared.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/store/store-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/store/store-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/store/store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/arts/store/store-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url