r wins in 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — He is a multiple champion this year who won one of his titles in a playoff at the expense of the three-time major champion Ernie Els. And he is not Jason Dufner. The South African Branden Grace comes into this week’s United States Open — his first — with three European Tour victories in 2012, including one in sudden death against Els and Retief Goosen, a two-time United States Open champion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Outsider Arrives at the United States Open', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:20:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db996819-bab5-562c-956f-ccd33dcb85e7', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db996819-bab5-562c-956f-ccd33dcb85e7'}, {'abstract': 'David Diehl, a longtime offensive lineman for the Giants, was arrested and charged with drunken driving after crashing his BMW into a row of parked cars in Astoria, Queens, on Sunday night.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/sports/football/giants-david-diehl-charged-with-dwi-after-crash-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'David Diehl, a longtime offensive lineman for the Giants, was arrested and charged with drunken driving after crashing his BMW into a row of parked cars in Astoria, Queens, on Sunday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Diehl, a longtime offensive lineman for the Giants, was arrested and charged with drunken driving after crashing his BMW into a row of parked cars in Astoria, Queens, on Sunday night, the police said. Diehl was alone in the car. No injuries were reported. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giants Lineman Charged With D.W.I. After Crash in Queens', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Football ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giants Lineman Arrested', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diehl, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:23:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer and Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dff6e3c3-74d4-51c6-8a88-bd3c76300ed7', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dff6e3c3-74d4-51c6-8a88-bd3c76300ed7'}, {'abstract': 'The 2012 presidential race isn’t about how to soar but how not to slide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/opinion/bruni-an-election-half-empty.html', 'snippet': 'The 2012 presidential race isn’t about how to soar but how not to slide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a statement of such unqualified certainty that Jeb Bush made it pretty much in passing, as if it required no elaboration, accommodated no dissent and was the obvious starting point from which all political discussion should flow.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/frank-bruni/frank-bruni-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Election Half Empty', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Election Half Empty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:24:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/be5864c1-23d8-572c-99c0-99681136eb35', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be5864c1-23d8-572c-99c0-99681136eb35'}, {'abstract': 'Eight people were injured in a small fire on a trolley car on Monday in the city of Dnipropetrovsk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/world/europe/ukraine-gunpowder-accident.html', 'snippet': 'Eight people were injured in a small fire on a trolley car on Monday in the city of Dnipropetrovsk.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Eight people were injured in a small fire on a trolley car on Monday in the city of Dnipropetrovsk. Local prosecutors said the accidental fire occurred when a passenger dropped a bag of gunpowder, causing it to ignite. The accident renewed fears of terrorist attacks in the city, where four explosive devices detonated in late April, wounding 38. “This was not an explosion — this was an ignition of gunpowder that is not a terrorist action,” a prosecutor, Natalya Marchuk, told the Interfax news agency, adding that an investigation would be conducted. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine: Gunpowder Accident', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine: Gunpowder Accident', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroad Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:25:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1087dec-3d16-547b-9058-18ce89714cdb', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1087dec-3d16-547b-9058-18ce89714cdb'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets have been victimized by defensive lapses in losing six of their last seven games. The latest blunders came Sunday afternoon, when the Yankees stormed to a 5-4 victory and swept the Mets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/sports/baseball/mets-solid-season-being-undercut-by-shaky-defense.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets have been victimized by defensive lapses in losing six of their last seven games. The latest blunders came Sunday afternoon, when the Yankees stormed to a 5-4 victory and swept the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'First, there was the optimism engendered by the Mets’ surprising start to the season. Then came the euphoric afterglow from Johan Santana’s historic no-hitter. But now all the good feelings have been pushed aside by a week of deflating losses in which the Mets were continually victimized by their own defensive lapses. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/sports/METS/METS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 