ation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc26312a-bc84-5423-8cea-c3d4bfa2a975', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc26312a-bc84-5423-8cea-c3d4bfa2a975'}, {'abstract': 'UnitedHealthcare’s commitment to keep elements of the health care reform is welcome, but it is not a substitute for the broader mandatory changes under the law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/opinion/health-reforms-consumers-want.html', 'snippet': 'UnitedHealthcare’s commitment to keep elements of the health care reform is welcome, but it is not a substitute for the broader mandatory changes under the law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UnitedHealthcare, one of the nation’s largest health insurers, announced this week that it would keep some of the popular benefits and consumer protections required by the federal health care law even if the Supreme Court strikes down all or part of it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Reforms Consumers Want', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Health Reforms Consumers Want', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UnitedHealth Group Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Healthcare Insurance Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:30:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebdcc56e-7ce1-5980-af9e-00d84c4919e9', 'word_count': 336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebdcc56e-7ce1-5980-af9e-00d84c4919e9'}, {'abstract': 'Vandals spray-painted graffiti Monday on the walls of Yad Vashem, Israel’s official Holocaust memorial, with messages attacking Zionism and blaming Zionists for the Holocaust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/world/middleeast/israel-memorial-vandalized.html', 'snippet': 'Vandals spray-painted graffiti Monday on the walls of Yad Vashem, Israel’s official Holocaust memorial, with messages attacking Zionism and blaming Zionists for the Holocaust.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Vandals spray-painted graffiti overnight Monday on the walls of Yad Vashem, Israel’s official Holocaust memorial, with messages attacking Zionism and blaming Zionists for the Holocaust. Nearly a dozen messages were scrawled around the Warsaw Ghetto Square monument and other parts of the campus. One said, “If Hitler hadn’t existed, the Zionists would have invented him,” and another said, “The Zionists wanted the Holocaust.” One message was signed “Global Haredi Judaism,” fueling suspicions that those behind the act were ultra-Orthodox Jewish extremists who reject the modern state of Israel. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel: Memorial Vandalized', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Memorial Vandalized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yad Vashem Holocaust Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graffiti', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:32:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/81508f46-48d6-531c-9ae5-5b52a3419064', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81508f46-48d6-531c-9ae5-5b52a3419064'}, {'abstract': 'Just a few miles from the Olympic Club, the 36-unit El Camino Inn has a connection to two United States Open winners.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/11/san-francisco-hotel-has-ties-to-champions/', 'snippet': 'Just a few miles from the Olympic Club, the 36-unit El Camino Inn has a connection to two United States Open winners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO\xa0— In the city billed as the gateway to San Francisco there sits a hotel that can claim to being a portal to the United States Open championship. The El Camino Inn on Mission Street has ties to two of the four United States Open golf champions crowned a few miles away at the Olympic Club.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco Hotel Has Ties to Champions', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T02:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name':