com/2012/06/12/sports/baseball/cubs-outbid-rivals-to-sign-cuban-slugger-jorge-soler.html', 'snippet': 'The Chicago Cubs won the bidding for the Jorge Soler, agreeing to a nine-year, $30 million contract. The 20-year-old Cuban outfielder is expected to beef up Chicago’s minor league system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago Cubs won the bidding for the Cuban outfielder Jorge Soler, agreeing to a nine-year, $30 million contract, according to two executives in Major League Baseball who had been apprised of the deal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cubs Outbid Rivals to Sign Cuban Slugger', 'kicker': 'Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cubs Are Said To Win Rights To Cuban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soler, Jorge (1992- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soler, Jorge', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clemens, Roger', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T03:13:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36d05d7c-a23b-5b6e-8341-0b70bac27fcd', 'word_count': 443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36d05d7c-a23b-5b6e-8341-0b70bac27fcd'}, {'abstract': 'With a 3-0 victory over the Braves in Atlanta, the Yankees reclaimed a piece of first place in the American League East for the first time since April 24.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/sports/baseball/yankees-return-to-first-place-in-al-east.html', 'snippet': 'With a 3-0 victory over the Braves in Atlanta, the Yankees reclaimed a piece of first place in the American League East for the first time since April 24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a 3-0 victory over the Braves in Atlanta, the Yankees reclaimed a piece of first place in the American League East for the first time since April 24. They had fallen as far as last place on May 21. Since then, they have won 14 of 18 and climbed 10 games over .500, a season high, to catch the idle Tampa Bay Rays. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Return to First Place in A.L. East', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Pro Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Return to First', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T03:23:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e70ae7-e750-563a-9b5c-fdf612edcb31', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e70ae7-e750-563a-9b5c-fdf612edcb31'}, {'abstract': 'As president, Mitt Romney said, he would seek to overhaul the federal government’s largest school programs into a voucherlike system, replacing top-down Washington mandates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/us/politics/in-romneys-voucher-education-policy-a-return-to-gop-roots.html', 'snippet': 'As president, Mitt Romney said, he would seek to overhaul the federal government’s largest school programs into a voucherlike system, replacing top-down Washington mandates.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Voucher” is a fighting word in education, so it may be understandable that when Mitt Romney speaks about improving the nation’s schools, he never uses that term.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/us/12educ1/12educ1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vouchers Unspoken, Romney Hails School Choice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vouchers Unspoken, Romney Hails School Choice', 'name':