l': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faa3f791-6f95-59eb-9097-8cb5d76da3bf', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faa3f791-6f95-59eb-9097-8cb5d76da3bf'}, {'abstract': 'Although riot police fired rubber bullets in at least one instance, the disturbances after the Kings’ Stanley Cup win were far less serious than those that followed the Los Angeles Lakers’ most recent N.B.A. titles, or the riot that engulfed downtown Vancouver after last year’s Cup finals.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/disturbances-are-few-in-a-city-prepared-to-keep-title-celebration-calm/', 'snippet': 'Although riot police fired rubber bullets in at least one instance, the disturbances after the Kings’ Stanley Cup win were far less serious than those that followed the Los Angeles Lakers’ most recent N.B.A. titles, or the riot that engulfed downt...', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Minor disturbances broke out around Staples Center on Monday night after the Los Angeles Kings beat the Devils, 6-1, in Game 6 of the Stanley Cup finals to capture their first championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disturbances Are Few in a City Prepared to Keep Title Celebration Calm', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T06:28:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fee3db9-db96-5bb7-abf2-efef37ab9f84', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fee3db9-db96-5bb7-abf2-efef37ab9f84'}, {'abstract': 'Much of India lacks emergency services, but a new program brings ambulances to the remotest parts of this southern state.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/dial-108-for-ambulance-in-tamil-nadu/', 'snippet': 'Much of India lacks emergency services, but a new program brings ambulances to the remotest parts of this southern state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The village of Kottaiyur is about a three-hour drive southeast from Bangalore, in the Krishnagiri district of Tamil Nadu. Kottaiyur is inhabited by 4,000 Irulars, who are classified by the state government as a tribal community. Although the village is connected with the nearest town, Denkanikottai, which is 30 kilometers (19 miles) away, by a concrete road, the bus service linking the village with the outside world is sporadic and unreliable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dial 108 for Ambulance in Tamil Nadu', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T06:37:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charukesi Ramadurai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charukesi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramadurai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7747dbf-695b-5e18-9c01-65e625cdd1c1', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7747dbf-695b-5e18-9c01-65e625cdd1c1'}, {'abstract': 'In some Gulf states, schools have a surprising problem: To fight against the ubiquity of English while teaching Arab students high-quality Arabic. A university in Milan is going in the other direction, changing its curriculum to teach all its graduate-level courses in English and doing away with instruction in the local students’ native Italian.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-push-and-pull-of-teaching-in-english/', 'snippet': 'In some Gulf states, schools have a surprising problem: To fight against the ubiquity of English while teaching Arab students high-quality Arabic. A university in Milan is going in the other direction, changing its curriculum to teach all its grad...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In some Gulf states, schools have a surprising problem: To fight against the ubiquity of English while teaching Arab students high-quality Arabic, of the sort that could be used at a professional broadcaster like Al Jazeera. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Push and Pull of Teaching in English', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL JAZEERA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T06:53:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4da7258-1b3c-574c-8aef-c9acde44205e', 'word_count': 85, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4da7258-1b3c-574c-8aef-c9acde44205e'}, {'abstract': 'Facts and figures of the Kings’ championship run that highlights just how good they were this postseason.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-kings-cup-victory-and-the-measure-of-greatness/', 'snippet': 'Facts and figures of the Kings’ championship run that highlights just how good they were this postseason.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES – The N.H.L. released a list of notes and numbers surrounding the Kings’ Stanley Cup run. Taken together, they form an impressive portrait of just how good the Kings were this postseason. A look at some of those facts and figures:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Kings’ Cup Victory and the Measure of Greatness', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T07:18:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf872d7-b2a9-54ae-b5e9-3292033c9a80', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf872d7-b2a9-54ae-b5e9-3292033c9a80'}, {'abstract': 'The corruption allegations against his son were a serious blow for the chief justice, Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry, who until now has been virtually venerated by many Pakistanis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/world/asia/pakistans-husain-haqqani-said-to-seek-help-from-us.html', 'snippet': 'The corruption allegations against his son were a serious blow for the chief justice, Iftikhar Muhammad Chaudhry, who until now has been virtually venerated by many Pakistanis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Pakistan’s chief justice has wielded his court as a whip against the status quo, the country’s rich and powerful, calling top government officials and military spymasters to account and asserting himself as a political force in his own right. But on Tuesday he found himself at the center of a new political firestorm when a well-connected property baron stood up in court and accused his family of corrupt dealing, detailing $3.7 million in kickbacks and cash payments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1658, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/13/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/world/PAKISTAN/PAKISTAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trial of Son Taints Pakistan’s Venerated Chief Justice', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trial of Son Taints Pakistan’s Venerated Chief Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussain, Malik Riaz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhry, Iftikhar Muhammad', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Extortion and Blackmail', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T07:51:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh and Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d994081b-8f00-52eb-a141-20143a45b739', 'word_count': 1207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d994081b-8f00-52eb-a141-20143a45b739'}, {'abstract': 'Every team at Euro 2012 has played one game, so what do we know?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/euro-2012-a-quick-take-on-4-days-8-games-and-16-teams/', 'snippet': 'Every team at Euro 2012 has played one game, so what do we know?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every team at Euro 2012 has played one game, so what do we know? In a tournament with some of the most expensive talent from some of the most expensive leagues in the world, Alan Dzagoev (CSKA Moscow), Mario Mandzukic (Wolfsburg) and Andriy Shevchenko (Dynamo Kyiv) are the unlikely leaders in the race for the Golden Boot; Carlos Velasco Carballo — the Spanish referee who flashed four yellow cards and the tournament’s only two reds in the event’s first game — has a future as a blackjack dealer; and the only Dutchman on track for the quarterfinals is Russia’s coach, Dick Advocaat. Let’s recap briefly the standings after the first four days:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012: A Quick Take on 4 Days, 8 Games and 16 Teams', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T08:02:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44d4a604-655b-54d3-89c1-9ba761754902', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44d4a604-655b-54d3-89c1-9ba761754902'}, {'abstract': 'Former Prime Minister John Major testified on Tuesday about a long run of Conservative rule that ended in painful defeat when Tony Blair came to power with Rupert Murdoch’s endorsement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/world/europe/british-hacking-inquiry-sharpens-political-divide.html', 'snippet': 'Former Prime Minister John Major testified on Tuesday about a long run of Conservative rule that ended in painful defeat when Tony Blair came to power with Rupert Murdoch’s endorsement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — As the judicial inquiry into the British press sifts painstakingly through competing claims about the influence of Rupert Murdoch’s newspapers, former Prime Minister John Major disclosed on Tuesday, for what he said was the first time, that Mr. Murdoch withdrew his newspapers’ support for the Conservatives after Mr. Major refused a demand for changes in his policies on Europe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Ex-Premier Says Murdoch Press ‘Lowered Tone’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Premier Tells of Pressure by Murdoch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labour Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Gordon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Major, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborne, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Party (Great Britain)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blair, Tony', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T08:24:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9299bbff-e64d-585d-998a-f5a0e601accb', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9299bbff-e64d-585d-998a-f5a0e601accb'}, {'abstract': 'Can you choose the best synonym for “demeanor” as it is used in the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/test-yourself-english-june-12-2012/', 'snippet': 'Can you choose the best synonym for “demeanor” as it is used in the article?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the article “The Making of an Olympic Sex Symbol.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, June 12, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T08:32:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ec29704-e2f0-56ce-a2f2-2fcd9682a49f', 'word_count': 46, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ec29704-e2f0-56ce-a2f2-2fcd9682a49f'}, {'abstract': 'Seven countries including India can import Iranian oil, but not China, the U.S. administration said.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/india-gets-waiver-for-oil-trade-with-iran/', 'snippet': 'Seven countries including India can import Iranian oil, but not China, the U.S. administration said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Less than three weeks before stringent American sanctions intended to reduce Iran’s oil exports take effect, “the Obama administration announced on Monday that it would exempt seven major importers of Iranian oil — but not China — from the measures because these countries had ‘significantly reduced’ their oil purchases from Iran,” Mark Landler writes in The New York Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India Gets Waiver for Oil Trade With Iran', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T08:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2ada20b-72e2-5698-a738-42e177246d24', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2ada20b-72e2-5698-a738-42e177246d24'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of Americans need to change careers. Why are we making it so hard?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/magazine/so-you-think-you-can-be-a-hair-braider.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of Americans need to change careers. Why are we making it so hard?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jestina Clayton grew up in a village in Sierra Leone where every girl learns traditional African hair-braiding. Then, when she was 22, she moved to Centerville, Utah, a place where no one learns traditional African hair-braiding. So Clayton was pleasantly surprised to find a niche in the market among a small group of Utah parents who had adopted African children but didn’t know how to style their hair.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17economy2/17economy2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17economy2/17economy2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17economy2/17economy2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'widt