'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1157ccf9-6d01-5c9b-84cc-aec777b0636a', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1157ccf9-6d01-5c9b-84cc-aec777b0636a'}, {'abstract': 'They’re not the closers now, but it may not be long.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/fantasy-focus-sleeper-relievers/', 'snippet': 'They’re not the closers now, but it may not be long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As someone who rarely chooses to pay the prevailing rate at auction for top-tier closers, I’m often left spending the next six months chasing anyone on my waiver wire(s) who may be even remotely in the mix for saves. This year is no exception, as we’ve seen guys like Mariano Rivera, Sergio Santos, and Andrew Bailey get hurt. Others such as Jordan Walden and Javy Guerra lost their jobs, so we’ve seen quite an influx of new closers already.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Focus: Sleeper Relievers', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grilli, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Padilla, Vicente', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Regan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Regan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67d4d7de-8c97-561f-bf7d-fc4f81ef017e', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67d4d7de-8c97-561f-bf7d-fc4f81ef017e'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times, plus a look at