utomobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petersen Automotive Museum', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swiss Federal Institute of Technology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phil Patton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Patton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/154ee374-bb95-5463-bc3d-929715c593a4', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/154ee374-bb95-5463-bc3d-929715c593a4'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans’ insistence that tax cuts are stimulative and that tax increases never reduce the deficit are unsupported by the facts, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-fiscal-legacy-of-george-w-bush/', 'snippet': 'Republicans’ insistence that tax cuts are stimulative and that tax increases never reduce the deficit are unsupported by the facts, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform – Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fiscal Legacy of George W. Bush', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/766eee3e-cfad-5627-9f64-7aad9950541d', 'word_count': 1037, 'uri': 'nyt://article/766eee3e-cfad-5627-9f64-7aad9950541d'}, {'abstract': 'Today’s thoroughbreds are genetically engineered for speed and aggression, not the soundness and stamina it takes to win three Grade I races in five weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/a-different-era-and-a-different-animal/', 'snippet': 'Today’s thoroughbreds are genetically engineered for speed and aggression, not the soundness and stamina it takes to win three Grade I races in five weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite Union Rags’s stirring rally in Saturday’s Belmont (for which I congratulate him and his connections heartily), I missed the hoopla and anticipation of seeing I’ll Have Another take a crack at the Triple Crown.Then again, is it that surprising that a racehorse that went all out to win the Derby and the Preakness came up injured before the last dance? Just another argument that today’s thoroughbreds are genetically engineered for speed and aggression, not the soundness and stamina it takes to win three Grade I races in five weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Different Era, and a Different Animal', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calumet Farm', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:03:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Deitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07b4f343-4872-5d20-8988-af1c63382c69', 'word_count': 1700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07b4f343-4872-5d20-8988-af1c63382c69'}, {'abstract': 'A Standford professor’s system to reduce traffic congestion at peak hours, first attempted on an Infosys campus.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/an-inspiration-from-bangalore-reduces-traffic-jams/', 'snippet': 'A Standford professor’s system to reduce traffic congestion at peak hours, first attempted on an Infosys campus.', 'lead_paragraph': '“London, Singapore, Stockholm and a few other cities around the world battle heavy traffic with a ‘congestion charge,’ a stiff fee for driving in crowded areas at peak hours,” John Markoff writes in The New York Times. “But drivers generally hate the idea, and efforts to impose it in this country have failed,” he wrote, referring to the United States. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Inspiration From Bangalore Reduces Traffic Jams', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Infosys Technologies Ltd', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Department (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stockholm (Sweden)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:11:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ee484cb-bb32-51c2-96a6-9c117a12b1a8', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ee484cb-bb32-51c2-96a6-9c117a12b1a8'}, {'abstract': 'David Axelrod says that if President Obama wins a second term, the administration would consider ways to undo the effects of the Supreme Court’s Citizens United ruling, which allows unlimited campaign spending by corporations and unions.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/axelrod-floats-amendment-to-stem-campaign-spending/', 'snippet': 'David Axelrod says that if President Obama wins a second term, the administration would consider ways to undo the effects of the Supreme Court’s Citizens United ruling, which allows unlimited campaign spending by corporations and unions.', 'lead_paragraph': '1:09 p.m. | Updated On David Axelrod’s New York City itinerary for Monday: to meet privately with potential donors to a “super PAC” supporting President Obama’s re-election, then publicly declare that if that re-election happens, Mr. Obama will stop at almost nothing to undo the ruling that made super PACs possible.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Axelrod Floats Amendment to Stem Campaign Spending', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Speaking Out Against ‘Super PACs’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Action Committees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Axelrod, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Priorities USA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:24:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85c65b70-00d3-52b6-98d5-1c6329cf60ae', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85c65b70-00d3-52b6-98d5-1c6329cf60ae'}, {'abstract': 'After forecasting a pretax loss of more than 450 million Australian dollars from its international unit and with its shares at a 17-year low, Qantas Airways has hired Macquarie to help the company defend itself against potential hostile takeover bids.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/wary-of-a-takeover-qantas-hires-macquarie/', 'snippet': 'After forecasting a pretax loss of more than 450 million Australian dollars from its international unit and with its shares at a 17-year low, Qantas Airways has hired Macquarie to help the company defend itself against potential hostile takeover b...', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Qantas Airways of Australia has hired the investment bank Macquarie to provide advice on fending off potential hostile takeover bids after its shares plunged to their lowest levels since the company was privatized in 1995. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wary of a Takeover, Qantas Hires Macquarie', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:26:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89383928-a0ca-5501-8602-07f7991e35a5', 'word_count': 783, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89383928-a0ca-5501-8602-07f7991e35a5'}, {'abstract': 'The Mexican telephone operator América Móvil has acquired six million shares in the Dutch telecommunications company KPN as it continues to build up ownership in the European business.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/america-movil-increases-stake-in-kpn/', 'snippet': 'The Mexican telephone operator América Móvil has acquired six million shares in the Dutch telecommunications company KPN as it continues to build up ownership in the European business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlos Slim Helú is not taking no for an answer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'America Movil Lifts Stake in KPN', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6751ce0d-0d40-56f3-9dd2-ac1a2e979727', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6751ce0d-0d40-56f3-9dd2-ac1a2e979727'}, {'abstract': 'Raising the age of consent to 18 makes little sense when nearly half of all women are married by then.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/indias-new-child-sex-abuse-bill-unrealistic-critics-say/', 'snippet': 'Raising the age of consent to 18 makes little sense when nearly half of all women are married by then.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Protection of Children from Sexual Offenses Bill was hailed as a landmark legislation, one that will strengthen the fight against child abuse in India, when it was passed by the upper house of Parliament in May. President Pratibha Patil is expected to sign it in coming weeks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India’s New Child Sexual Abuse Bill Draws Critics', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patil, Pratibha', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:51:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikhila Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikhila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd28211-d417-5183-8a55-4f8de143f339', 'word_count': 833, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd28211-d417-5183-8a55-4f8de143f339'}, {'abstract': 'We’ll be updating our forecasting model at least four or five times a week. What should you look for? Here’s a quick guide.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/a-guide-to-forecast-model-updates/', 'snippet': 'We’ll be updating our forecasting model at least four or five times a week. What should you look for? Here’s a quick guide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that our presidential forecast model has been released, we’re looking forward to obsessing over every detail and seeing how the forecast changes as new polls and economic data are released. I hope our readers will feel the same way, so here’s a quick guide on what to look for in our model updates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Guide to Forecast Model Updates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T10:59:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78bf90b4-537d-5f7c-940b-184be955f73b', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78bf90b4-537d-5f7c-940b-184be955f73b'}, {'abstract': 'Discussing the best ways to get working capital to small businesses at the Clinton Global Initiative conference.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/why-the-s-b-a-s-partnership-with-ibm-isnt-enough/', 'snippet': 'Discussing the best ways to get working capital to small businesses at the Clinton Global Initiative conference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week, I posted about my first day at the Clinton Global Initiative in Chicago, a gathering of about 900 leaders from across the country. I participated in the small-business working group, and the team I was on focused on developing new ways for Main Street businesses to get access to capital – a topic near and dear to my heart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the S.B.A.’s Partnership With I.B.M. Isn’t Enough', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mills, Karen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clinton Global Initiative', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Business Machines Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Small Business Administration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T11:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd2dd3dc-f448-57c7-b5a9-da33025eec5a', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd2dd3dc-f448-57c7-b5a9-da33025eec5a'}, {'abstract': 'Explaining India’s new child sexual abuse bill.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/a-conversation-with-neela-gangadharan-ministry-of-women-and-child-development/', 'snippet': 'Explaining India’s new child sexual abuse bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'India Ink sent questions to the Ministry of Women and Child Development about the Protection of Children Against Sexual Offenses Bill, which was made into law on May 10. Here is the ministry’s response.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Ministry of Women and Child Development on the Child Sexual Abuse Bill', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T11:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikhila Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikhila', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7774a034-0911-5ba1-ab7e-05e3cbf7f457', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7774a034-0911-5ba1-ab7e-05e3cbf7f457'}, {'abstract': 'Most observers think the Spanish bailout amounts to a preview of more trouble ahead.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/is-the-spanish-bailout-a-bad-sign-of-things-to-come/', 'snippet': 'Most observers think the Spanish bailout amounts to a preview of more trouble ahead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the weekend Spain agreed to accept as much as $125 billion in aid from euro zone partners to rescue its banks, becoming the largest European country to get financial assistance in the region’s debt crisis. Although some observers were eager to declare that the size of the bailout showed that leaders are finally coming to terms with Europe’s economic woes, most seem to believe it amounts to a preview of more trouble ahead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Containment', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T11:49:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09ce49c2-fcc9-5b21-a6db-971b11cdf1e0', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09ce49c2-fcc9-5b21-a6db-971b11cdf1e0'}, {'abstract': 'Both the Obama and Romney campaigns are complaining about their candidate’s words being taken out of context, while using the words of the rival candidate in attack ads.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/campaigns-use-opponents-words-and-cry-foul/', 'snippet': 'Both the Obama and Romney campaigns are complaining about their candidate’s words being taken out of context, while using the words of the rival candidate in attack ads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s White House advisers have never been enamored of the press. But even by that measure, their reaction to coverage of the president’s news conference last week has been particularly testy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Campaigns Use Opponent’s Words, and Cry Foul', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carney, Jay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodhouse, Brad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T11:52:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3c88547-70d5-5f14-a261-1ce166bff20b', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3c88547-70d5-5f14-a261-1ce166bff20b'}, {'abstract': 'Let’s acknowledge the Syrian conflict for what it is: a civil war. If there’s no global appetite for action then we should take responsibility for inaction.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/call-the-syrian-conflict-a-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'Let’s acknowledge the Syrian conflict for what it is: a civil war. If there’s no global appetite for action then we should take responsibility for inaction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT — On Saturday, after yet another massacre in Syria, I sat down for tea with Maan Abdul Salam, a Syrian activist decamped to Beirut. I’d hoped to lighten the mood with a game of backgammon, but we struggled through each roll of the dice. Maan’s literary cafe in Damascus, once a haven for bright minds and dissident intellectuals, shuttered months ago. Now he wore the exhaustion of a drawn-out struggle. Without adding to his anguish, I wanted his take on one question: has Syria passed a mark, into a state of civil war?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It Is What It Is', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War and Guerrilla Warfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T11:54:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lara Setrakian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setrakian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea00d55a-9d12-502d-afd1-4ccba920e237', 'word_count': 595, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea00d55a-9d12-502d-afd1-4ccba920e237'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/morning-take-out-503/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why the Bailout in Spain Won’t Work \xa0|\xa0 The euro zone’s offer of $125 billion to bail out Spanish banks over the weekend was hailed by finance ministers and officials across Europe as a masterstroke. But by now, it should be apparent that the bailout has failed — or is at least on its way to failing, Andrew Ross Sorkin writes in his DealBook column.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T11:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/043ced5b-082c-57c4-b129-ac93a2fa5dea', 'word_count': 2008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/043ced5b-082c-57c4-b129-ac93a2fa5dea'}, {'abstract': 'Research by comScore is being highlighted by Facebook to show that ads there offer a “return on investment.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/facebook-tries-to-prove-ads-work/', 'snippet': 'Research by comScore is being highlighted by Facebook to show that ads there offer a “return on investment.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'After taking a beating during its initial public offering over questions about whether its ad-focused business model is solid enough for the company to succeed on a $100 billion scale, Facebook is in a hurry to offer up new data to prove that its ads do, in fact, work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Tries to Prove Ads Work', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'comScore Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T12:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename':