ldman Sachs director Rajat K. Gupta says phone recordings show that David Loeb, a senior Goldman salesman, passed on tips to a hedge fund manager. The judge has ruled that the recording are not admissible as evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/judge-in-gupta-trial-bars-2-wiretapped-calls-as-hearsay/', 'snippet': 'A defense lawyer for the former Goldman Sachs director Rajat K. Gupta says phone recordings show that David Loeb, a senior Goldman salesman, passed on tips to a hedge fund manager. The judge has ruled that the recording are not admissible as evide...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the trial of Rajat K. Gupta, a former Goldman director accused of leaking secrets about the bank to Raj Rajaratnam, jurors have heard a lot about David Loeb, a Goldman Sachs executive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge in Gupta Trial Bars 2 Wiretapped Calls as Hearsay', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T12:56:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c049161-e3a2-510c-8ec2-a1c76b16b1f0', 'word_count': 368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c049161-e3a2-510c-8ec2-a1c76b16b1f0'}, {'abstract': 'Two prepaid carriers, Cricket and Virgin Mobile, are offering the iPhone. Which is the better deal?', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/pre-paid-iphone-shoot-out-cricket-vs-virgin/', 'snippet': 'Two prepaid carriers, Cricket and Virgin Mobile, are offering the iPhone. Which is the better deal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just a week after writing about the prepaid no-contract iPhone deal from\xa0mobile provider Cricket, Virgin Mobile announced it would also offer the iPhone 4 and 4S on a prepaid no-contract deal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prepaid iPhone Shootout: Cricket vs. Virgin', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Which Phone Deal Is Better? As Always, It Depends', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cellular Telephones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cricket Communications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Virgin Mobile', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T12:59:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/796ed83d-3900-5165-b119-8a229478b56d', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/796ed83d-3900-5165-b119-8a229478b56d'}, {'abstract': 'A classic ladylike purse, made new in a novel itsy-bitsy size.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-get-perrins-attelage-minaudiere/', 'snippet': 'A classic ladylike purse, made new in a novel itsy-bitsy size.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The specialty leather-goods brand Perrin Paris is probably foreign territory to even the most seasoned Madison Avenue shopper. But there’s nothing low profile about Perrin. After nearly 12 decades of being available\xa0exclusively in France, and more recently in Beverly Hills, Calif., the Parisian fashion house has opened shop in New York City’s Carlyle Hotel (987 Madison Avenue). The house is known for glove making, sunglasses and handbags, and is a favorite among high-profilers like Beyoncé (a fan of the Menotte Clutch), P. Diddy (Cabriolet driving gloves) and Martha Stewart (who helped design the company’s jet-set travel pouch). “Often, American women look for practicality in a bag whereas les Francaises understand it is more about the image and the completion of a look,” says Sally Perrin, the creative director of the fourth-generation-run business. “We bridge the past with the present by creating witty and unique designs.” The Attelage Minaudière is a perfect example: a classic ladylike purse by all accounts but made new in a novel itsy-bitsy size. “It’s a wrist ornament,” Perrin says, noting that the bag is available in goatskin, crocodile, lambskin, shagreen and, come fall, lacquered wood. “It’s an accessory in every sense of the word.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Perrin’s Attelage Minaudière', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T13:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f5900b-f100-5550-9bee-c4c52cca3b0a', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f5900b-f100-5550-9bee-c4c52cca3b0a'}, {'abstract': 'White Light, Lincoln Center’s fall festival dedicated to humanity’s spiritual side, announces a new season anchored by Esa-Pekka Salonen conducting Mahler’s Symphony No. 9 with the Philharmonia Orchestra of London.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-white-light-festival-turns-to-dark-hued-mahler/', 'snippet': 'White Light, Lincoln Center’s fall festival dedicated to humanity’s spiritual side, announces a new season anchored by Esa-Pekka Salonen conducting Mahler’s Symphony No. 9 with the Philharmonia Orchestra of London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'White Light, Lincoln Center’s fall festival dedicated to humanity’s spiritual side, will present Esa-Pekka Salonen conducting Mahler’s Symphony No. 9 with the Philharmonia Orchestra of London next season, the center said on Tuesday. The festival will feature the jaw-harp virtuoso Wang Li; the organist Cameron Carpenter playing Bach in Alice Tully Hall; and a Stockhausen program. The announcement of the new season, to run for a month starting on Oct. 18, said the series would also include the United States debut of the Latvian Radio Choir; a Charpentier program by William Christie and Les Arts Florissants; a music-theater work by Heiner Goebbels called “I went to the house but did not enter,” with the Hilliard Ensemble; and an appearance by the singer Mary Chapin Carpenter.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The White Light Festival Turns to Dark-Hued Mahler', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'White Light Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White Light Festival (Lincoln Center, NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salonen, Esa-Pekka', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T13:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel J. Wakin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Wakin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9816b6b3-a3f9-57f7-a496-121c52b88192', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9816b6b3-a3f9-57f7-a496-121c52b88192'}, {'abstract': 'The British government is headed for a bruising showdown presaging what some clerics called the most serious rift between church and state in centuries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/world/europe/churches-challenge-uk-government-over-same-sex-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'The British government is headed for a bruising showdown presaging what some clerics called the most serious rift between church and state in centuries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British government was headed for a bruising showdown on Tuesday with Anglican and Roman Catholic Church leaders over Prime Minister David Cameron’s contentious plan to legalize same-sex marriage, presaging what some clerics called the most serious rift between church and state in centuries.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Churches Challenge British Government Over Same-Sex Marriage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gay Marriage Creating Rift In Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGLICAN CHURCHES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T13:13:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3068a2de-f009-584b-9840-793347495f8f', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3068a2de-f009-584b-9840-793347495f8f'}, {'abstract': '“Masters of Sex” stars Michael Sheen and Lizzy Caplan as the sex researchers William Masters and Virginia Johnson, while “Ray Donovan” stars Liev Schreiber as a professional trouble-shooter in Los Angeles.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/showtime-adds-new-series-masters-of-sex-and-ray-donovan/', 'snippet': '“Masters of Sex” stars Michael Sheen and Lizzy Caplan as the sex researchers William Masters and Virginia Johnson, while “Ray Donovan” stars Liev Schreiber as a professional trouble-shooter in Los Angeles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Showtime’s family of original programming has grown by two, with a little help from Masters and Johnson. The cable channel, already home to series including “Homeland,” “Dexter” and “Shameless,” announced that it was picking up two new shows including “Masters of Sex,” which dramatizes the lives of the sex researchers William Masters and Virginia Johnson. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Showtime Adds New Series: ‘Masters of Sex’ and ‘Ray Donovan’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Showtime Adds 2 Series', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons