: 'Yoga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T14:39:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/6a87513f-0e29-590a-969c-e51590ba66f3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/6a87513f-0e29-590a-969c-e51590ba66f3'}, {'abstract': 'When the Kings won the Stanley Cup on Monday night, Los Angeles and its fans acted very much like a real hockey town.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/leading-off-the-new-kings/', 'snippet': 'When the Kings won the Stanley Cup on Monday night, Los Angeles and its fans acted very much like a real hockey town.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end, Los Angeles threw hockey a proper party Monday night. The silver streamers were a classy touc,h and the Kings fans were more than appropriately raucous for a Stanley Cup-clinching victory over the Devils. The Kings who skated with the Cup over their heads were nothing but completely deserving after a 6-1 scorching, proving all the necessary grit and resilience, proudly representing underdogs everywhere by having accomplished this as a No. 8 seed. The only glitch came when the crowd failed to follow hockey etiquette and boo Commissioner Gary Bettman, at which point you might have noticed Canada collectively rolling its eyes. Amateurs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leading Off: The New Kings', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durant, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 