acific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d363e7a-5d6f-5c0d-a489-efaaf9504c59', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d363e7a-5d6f-5c0d-a489-efaaf9504c59'}, {'abstract': 'Major automakers have committed to integrating a button onto their vehicles’ steering wheels to summon Siri, Apple’s voice-command program.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/wheelies-the-eyes-free-edition/', 'snippet': 'Major automakers have committed to integrating a button onto their vehicles’ steering wheels to summon Siri, Apple’s voice-command program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Eyes-Free Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buick Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Siri Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3415f9c-c9fd-5980-887e-7db726ee43f3', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3415f9c-c9fd-5980-887e-7db726ee43f3'}, {'abstract': 'Lena Dunham’s show deserves attention for a reason beyond its current role as cultural Rorschach.', 'web_url': 'https://bruni.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/a-new-comedys-enduring-appeal/', 'snippet': 'Lena Dunham’s show deserves attention for a reason beyond its current role as cultural Rorschach.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Girls,” “Girls,” “Girls.” The HBO show arrived about two months ago on a wave of curiosity and anticipation and has only increased its hold on the chattering class’s attention since, providing departure points for debates about minorities on screen, about women’s body types on screen, about the disillusionments of people in their 20s, about the entitlement of people in their 20s, about urban arrogance, about urban drift.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Comedy’s Enduring Appeal', 'kicker': 'Frank Bruni', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:05:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By FRANK BRUNI', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BRUNI', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6d4ca80-6742-5284-968f-470fa0c97359', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6d4ca80-6742-5284-968f-470fa0c97359'}, {'abstract': 'A report released on Tuesday showed that median total pay for executives at companies in the FTSE 100 rose 10 percent, to £3.7 million, even as the index fell 5 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/executive-pay-rises-10-in-britain-adding-to-debate/', 'snippet': 'A report released on Tuesday showed that median total pay for executives at companies in the FTSE 100 rose 10 percent, to £3.7 million, even as the index fell 5 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Pay for top managers in Britain rose 10 percent last year, a report released on Tuesday showed, providing fresh ammunition for critics who argue that executive pay has become excessive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Executive Pay Rises 10% in Britain, Adding to Debate', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamond, Robert E Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorrell, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lloyds Banking Group Plc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WPP', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:09:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83d99504-9157-5d32-ba5a-9078cddfcf95', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83d99504-9157-5d32-ba5a-9078cddfcf95'}, {'abstract': 'For creatures of comfort, Phoebe Philo offered new pieces that work seamlessly into a wardrobe of old ones.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/just-one-look-celine-2/', 'snippet': 'For creatures of comfort, Phoebe Philo offered new pieces that work seamlessly into a wardrobe of old ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were plenty of familiar elements at Céline yesterday — wide-leg slacks, car coats, color blocking and scarves wrapped tightly around the neck, to start — but the familiar felt desirable, still. Loyalists, a k a the creatures of comfort who have the luxury of getting very comfortable with wearing Céline, appreciate designer Phoebe Philo’s consistency, and the fact that she builds collections upon collections and offers new pieces that work seamlessly into a wardrobe of old ones. Come November, you might layer in this animal spot, for example, but you need not buy a brand new white pant or scarf to achieve the look.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Céline', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:14:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Herman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/244443f9-3d37-593c-abf8-82410fcc2e00', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/244443f9-3d37-593c-abf8-82410fcc2e00'}, {'abstract': 'Seagate’s new line of consumer hard drives, Backup Plus, is slim, attractive and easy to use.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/seagate-emphasizes-backups-in-new-hard-drive-line/', 'snippet': 'Seagate’s new line of consumer hard drives, Backup Plus, is slim, attractive and easy to use.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seagate, the hard drive maker, is redoing its consumer line-up with a new product that should make its mission crystal clear to shoppers. Named Backup Plus, the slim (14.5 millimeters) hard drive moves data from a computer for safe keeping. But it also will pull down photos from Facebook or Flickr too.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seagate Emphasizes Backups in New Hard Drive Line', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seagate’s Latest Hard Drives Strive for Style and Simplicity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data Storage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seagate Technology PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damon Darlin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Darlin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8e3fa9-24fc-51a2-9370-b3d18ce25e09', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8e3fa9-24fc-51a2-9370-b3d18ce25e09'}, {'abstract': 'The Borsa, the cafe district of Cairo, Egyptian soccer fans had a tough choice Sunday night — what a Euro 2012 match or the Pharoah’s World Cup qualifier in Guinea.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/euro-2012-the-view-from-egypt/', 'snippet': 'The Borsa, the cafe district of Cairo, Egyptian soccer fans had a tough choice Sunday night — what a Euro 2012 match or the Pharoah’s World Cup qualifier in Guinea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — At 7 p.m. Sunday evening, an identical argument broke out in front of more than a dozen television screens in Borsa, the outdoor café-lined haven of downtown Cairo. At issue: whether to watch the second half of Spain versus Italy in the European Championship or switch to the start of Egypt’s 2014 World Cup qualifier against Guinea.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012: The View From Egypt', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2014 (Soccer)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:15:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Ross', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ross', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d2f1677-89a0-52eb-b2e6-b7150abe6a37', 'word_count': 1073, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d2f1677-89a0-52eb-b2e6-b7150abe6a37'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Brantley on “The Witness” by Vivienne Franzmann at the Royal Court Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/london-theater-journal-part-of-the-family/', 'snippet': 'Ben Brantley on “The Witness” by Vivienne Franzmann at the Royal Court Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All domestic dramas more or less plop us down into other people’s homes. But watching “The Witness,” Vivienne Franzmann’s absorbing new play at the Royal Court Theater, I really felt like part of the family, as if I might be allowed to lean over and nibble off a character’s sandwich or change the television channel. And when the insults and accusations started flying, my first instinct was to run to my bedroom and slam the door.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Part of the Family', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brantley, Ben', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Court Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:16:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70427269-70b5-55a7-995a-44ad128d734b', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70427269-70b5-55a7-995a-44ad128d734b'}, {'abstract': 'Quinoa lends bulk to the classic pairing of spinach and mushrooms, and walnuts add richness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/health/nutrition/quinoa-spinach-and-mushroom-salad-recipes-for-health.html', 'snippet': 'Quinoa lends bulk to the classic pairing of spinach and mushrooms, and walnuts add richness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is almost a classic spinach and mushroom salad, but it’s bulked up by the quinoa, which goes very well with the mix and is nicely complemented by the walnuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/health/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/health/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/health/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 758, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/health/13recipehealth/13recipehealth-s