'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/reimagined-side-show-musical-has-dates-on-two-coasts/', 'snippet': 'Bill Condon (“Dreamgirls”) will direct the musical about Siamese twins, slated for runs at La Jolla Playhouse and the Kennedy Center.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Side Show,” the Henry Krieger/Bill Russell musical about Siamese twins who became circus stars during the Depression, ran only 91 performances on Broadway in 1997, despite some critical acclaim. Now La Jolla Playhouse in California and the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts in Washington, D.C., are producing what they call a “re-imagining” of the show that is scheduled to open on the West Coast in 2013 and on the East Coast in 2014. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reimagined ‘Side Show’ Musical Has Dates on Two Coasts', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Condon, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, John F, Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Jolla Playhouse', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:37:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1206572-48f8-57eb-b2fc-1ad6fa924e92', 'word_count': 209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1206572-48f8-57eb-b2fc-1ad6fa924e92'}, {'abstract': 'What was once the stuff of jokes — the idea that members of Egypt’s old regime would try to shift blame for killing protesters during last year’s revolution from themselves to the Islamists who took part in the uprising — has now become fact.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/egyptian-candidate-embraces-conspiracy-theory-to-explain-killing-of-protesters/', 'snippet': 'What was once the stuff of jokes — the idea that members of Egypt’s old regime would try to shift blame for killing protesters during last year’s revolution from themselves to the Islamists who took part in the uprising — has now become fact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Three weeks ago, after the first round of Egypt’s presidential election set up a final runoff between a leader of the Islamist Muslim Brotherhood and a former general who served as Hosni Mubarak’s prime minister during last year’s revolution, the activist blogger Mahmoud Salem joked that the candidate of the old regime might be forced to embrace some sort of wild conspiracy theory to deflect responsibility for the killing of hundreds of protesters during the uprising.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Candidate Embraces Conspiracy Theory to Explain Killing of Protesters', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shafik, Ahmed', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Suleiman, Omar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'April 6 Youth Movement', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76df2e59-e0c7-5b7b-8f26-5e86de484d4a', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76df2e59-e0c7-5b7b-8f26-5e86de484d4a'}, {'abstract': 'Dublin is not just for drinking. The food is good, too.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/an-eaters-sequel-to-a-drinkers-guide-to-dublin-cheese-toasties-edition/', 'snippet': 'Dublin is not just for drinking. The food is good, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My latest Drink column is, essentially, an updated Dublin pub crawl, culminating at the charming L. Mulligan Grocer in Stoneybatter. My friend and I enjoyed our dinner there as much as our drinks: he had chicken stuffed with black pudding and beets, and I had one of the best steaks I’ve had in recent memory. There were no false notes: this was delicious and honest food featuring Irish ingredients, thoughtful but not overthought. (And the menus are a treat, too: beautifully written and fitted inside vintage books. It was this attention to detail that impressed us most on our visit to Mulligan’s.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Eater’s Sequel to a Drinker’s Guide to Dublin, Cheese Toasties Edition', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/674f2921-a73b-5cd4-acc1-6216f4307ac0', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/674f2921-a73b-5cd4-acc1-6216f4307ac0'}, {'abstract': 'For the fifth day in a row, the Romney campaign assailed President Obama for remarks that he said revealed the president’s disconnect from economic reality.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/now-whos-out-of-touch-romney-tries-to-turn-the-tables-on-obama/', 'snippet': 'For the fifth day in a row, the Romney campaign assailed President Obama for remarks that he said revealed the president’s disconnect from economic reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — Mitt Romney understands the power of the verbal gaffe, real or perceived. During the Republican primaries, he offered up an all-you-can-eat buffet of them: his wife’s “Cadillacs,” his friends’ Nascar teams, how he liked being able to fire people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Who’s Out of Touch? Romney Tries to Turn the Tables on Obama', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Uses Obama’s Words Against Him, Calling Him ‘Out of Touch’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/22a83ff3-eb2f-5133-83f0-816662741aa2', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/22a83ff3-eb2f-5133-83f0-816662741aa2'}, {'abstract': 'Sabra Dipping Company opened a plant in Mexico to make dips tailored for the Latin American market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/business/foreign-cuisine-branded-in-america-sells-to-global-market.html', 'snippet': 'Sabra Dipping Company opened a plant in Mexico to make dips tailored for the Latin American market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an effort to become a global player in the sale of internationally inspired dips and side dishes, Sabra dips, a joint venture of PepsiCo and the Strauss Group, officially opened a $10 million plant in Mexico on Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/HUMMUS-1/HUMMUS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/business/HUMMUS-1/HUMMUS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/HUMMUS-1/HUMMUS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/HUMMUS-1/HUMMUS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/HUMMUS-1/HUMMUS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'heig