 women who say they provide financial support to their baby-boomer parents is increasing, according to research from Ameriprise Financial.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daughters of Boomers Giving More Financial Help to Parents, Study Finds', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ameriprise Financial Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0188a15-43f6-50bc-82d0-77f8aefcce66', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0188a15-43f6-50bc-82d0-77f8aefcce66'}, {'abstract': 'Barbara Lippert, formerly from Adweek, is joining Bob Garfield, formerly of Ad Age; both will be editors at large for MediaPost. Their first assignment is to file video reports from the annual advertising awards in Cannes, France.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/once-dueling-ad-critics-are-teaming-up-at-mediapost/', 'snippet': 'Barbara Lippert, formerly from Adweek, is joining Bob Garfield, formerly of Ad Age; both will be editors at large for MediaPost. Their first assignment is to file video reports from the annual advertising awards in Cannes, France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the trade publications Advertising Age and Adweek have fought as fiercely as any of the pairs of marketing rivals they cover — Coke and Pepsi, Kellogg and General Mills,\xa0 PC and Mac. Their competition was typified for many years by their dueling ad critics, Bob Garfield for Ad Age and Barbara Lippert for Adweek.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Once-Dueling Ad Critics Are Teaming Up at MediaPost', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garfield, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:57:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a5d24dc-b326-57b7-9c4f-1c152559a210', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a5d24dc-b326-57b7-9c4f-1c152559a210'}, {'abstract': 'A study finds fewer fires likely in the tropics and more in temperate zones in a warming world.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/fire-and-warming-different-forecasts-for-tropics-and-temperate-zones/', 'snippet': 'A study finds fewer fires likely in the tropics and more in temperate zones in a warming world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Researchers using a decade of satellite data on fires and a suite of climate models have produced the first thorough global estimate of changes in the frequency of fires in the world’s forests under greenhouse-driven global warming. There’s ample uncertainty but the study, published today in the peer-reviewed online journal Ecosphere, points to a variety of outcomes, with fires likely becoming more frequent in zones you might expect — like temperate North America and particularly the western United States — but rarer in the tropics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fire and Warming – Different Forecasts for Tropics and Temperate Zones', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Geography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North America', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ce11e55-e48b-5ae3-aab7-fd5c9c382729', 'word_count': 872, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ce11e55-e48b-5ae3-aab7-fd5c9c382729'}, {'abstract': 'Overfishing of striped bass and other predators reduces the number that feed on Sesarma crabs, causing a population explosion of these grass-eating animals.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/pressures-on-predators-lead-to-marshland-die-offs/', 'snippet': 'Overfishing of striped bass and other predators reduces the number that feed on Sesarma crabs, causing a population explosion of these grass-eating animals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Swaths of Cape Cod’s salt marshes are slowly disintegrating. For the human observer, the most notable sign of their decline might be the increase in night herons. They crouch like low, dark smudges on the salt marshes at dawn after feeding on the surfeit of Sesarma crabs through the night. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pressures on Predators Lead to Marshland Die-Offs', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bass (Fish)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crabs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grass', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ecology (Journal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cape Cod (Mass)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T15:58:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Slivka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slivka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41e258d1-1e49-57de-9771-c11371c0b111', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41e258d1-1e49-57de-9771-c11371c0b111'}, {'abstract': 'We’re happy to announce that the Styles desk of The Times is now on Pinterest at pinterest.com/nytimes.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/were-on-pinterest/', 'snippet': 'We’re happy to announce that the Styles desk of The Times is now on Pinterest at pinterest.com/nytimes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re happy to announce that the Styles desk of The New York Times is now on Pinterest, at pinterest.com/nytimes. We’ve posted our first fashion and beauty boards — Hair, Beach Bliss, Color Riot and Materials and Textures — alongside food- and interior design-themed boards created by our colleagues on the Dining and Home desks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re on Pinterest!', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T16:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simone S. Oliver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simone', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Oliver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18b5998e-61b3-57c0-9225-278075688fda', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18b5998e-61b3-57c0-9225-278075688fda'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks might be the best fit for Ray Allen, and vice versa.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/schlosser-ray-allen-post/', 'snippet': 'The Knicks might be the best fit for Ray Allen, and vice versa.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following their Eastern Conference finals loss to the Heat, the Celtics are already facing questions regarding what they’ll do next.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Ray Allen Be a Knick?', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, RAY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fields, Landry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garnett, Kevin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lin, Jeremy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Novak, Steve', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Paul', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shumpert, Iman', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Celtics', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T16:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Schlosser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schlosser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de067cea-e29e-5933-a86e-dfd58efb2691', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de067cea-e29e-5933-a86e-dfd58efb2691'}, {'abstract': 'I makes them.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/zingers/', 'snippet': 'I makes them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Politico collects what they say were my best.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zingers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T16:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2ca14bc-cb13-5bcb-ae05-a1614546a8fb', 'word_count': 8, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2ca14bc-cb13-5bcb-ae05-a1614546a8fb'}, {'abstract': 'Al Pacino, who played Ricky Roma in the film version, would play Shelly Levene in the revival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/glengarry-glen-ross-with-al-pacino-aiming-for-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Al Pacino, who played Ricky Roma in the film version, would play Shelly Levene in the revival.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A new Broadway revival of David Mamet’s Pulitzer Prize-winning play, “Glengarry Glen Ross,” is in the works for the 2012-13 season with Al Pacino in line to play the desperate salesman Shelly “The Machine” Levene, according to two Broadway producers with knowledge of the plans.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Glengarry Glen Ross,’ With Al Pacino, Aiming for Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Glengarry’, With Pacino, Aiming for Broadway', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tony Awards (Theater Awards)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mamet, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pacino, Al', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Jeffrey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Daniel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T16:02:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d2f1842-2d05-57a4-a083-a1028b3a7484', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d2f1842-2d05-57a4-a083-a1028b3a7484'}, {'abstract': 'Gurung applied geometry and his own quirky vision to similar silhouettes this season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/just-one-look-prabal-gurung-2/', 'snippet': 'Gurung applied geometry and his own quirky vision to similar silhouettes this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prabal Gurung’s second resort collection felt like an extension of his pre-fall presentation — he showed similar silhouettes (short suit, sheath and shirt dress), all with his own quirky vision. He evolved from psychedelic pop prints to geometry this season. The dominating print is all about numbers. “It’s very mathematical,” Gurung says, “the way the pattern is fragmented.” He is referring to the looks, like this one, inspired by the 26-year-old artist Aaron Moran, whose reclaimed and rough-edged wood sculptures always have a smooth finish (sort of like Gurung’s work). Here, a cubist silk and cotton mikado blazer and tuxedo short would be fun even without the red waistband and bright blue collar.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Prabal Gurung', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurung, Prabal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T16:03:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814e5adc-3bdb-5b07-b7d4-627b08460737', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814e5adc-3bdb-5b07-b7d4-627b08460737'}, {'abstract': 'Hector Negroni, the head of municipal bond trading at Goldman Sachs, is leaving the firm to set up a new investment fund at Fundamental Advisors, the private equity firm said on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/goldmans-muni-chief-heads-to-fundamental-advisors/', 'snippet': 'Hector Negroni, the head of municipal bond trading at Goldman Sachs, is leaving the firm to set up a new investment fund