tep of roasting it (see variation below).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/health/15recipehealth/15recipehealth-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Red Quinoa, Cauliflower and Fava Bean Salad With Buttermilk Curry Dressing', 'kicker': 'Recipes for Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T16:48:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Fitness & Nutrition', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Rose Shulman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': 'Rose', 'lastname': 'Shulman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'recipe', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6986ed4-8dee-5300-9f95-34386db86444', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6986ed4-8dee-5300-9f95-34386db86444'}, {'abstract': 'A book that enables you to comprehend the cocktail long before you reach for a shaker, and primes you to mix a fine drink once you do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/dining/a-sensible-guide-to-cocktails-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'A book that enables you to comprehend the cocktail long before you reach for a shaker, and primes you to mix a fine drink once you do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They call themselves the Jellymongers, but Sam Bompas and Harry Parr, who have created models of St. Paul’s Cathedral and other landmarks in gelatin, do not include Jell-O shots in their new book, “Cocktails With Bompas & Parr.” Instead, they have written an exceptionally sensible if somewhat cheeky treatise on the cocktail, with recipes. It will make you smart, able to comprehend the cocktail long before you reach for a shaker, and primed to mix a fine drink once you do.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFF_COCKTAILS1/13STUFF_COCKTAILS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1214, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '