34'}, {'abstract': 'The managers of Flatiron Wines & Spirits, a new no-frills shop, look for wines that are true to their terroir, and to the history and culture of their region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/dining/a-new-wine-shop-in-the-flatiron-district-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'The managers of Flatiron Wines & Spirits, a new no-frills shop, look for wines that are true to their terroir, and to the history and culture of their region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wines that are true to their terroir, and to the history and culture of their region, line the light wood shelves of Flatiron Wines & Spirits, a new no-frills shop. If they are natural, organic or biodynamic, so much the better. That’s the wine philosophy of its managers, Beau Rapier and Dan Weber, who worked at Uva in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. Regions they like include Burgundy, the Loire Valley, Piedmont, the Rhone Valley, the Mosel, Champagne and Northern California. They also regularly curate three tables of 100 wines each (red, white and rosé), all for less than $15 a bottle, from the 1,500 or so wines in the store. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFFSHOP_SPAN/13STUFFSHOP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFFSHOP_SPAN/13STUFFSHOP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFFSHOP_SPAN/13STUFF5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFFSHOP_SPAN/13STUFF5-superJumbo.jpg', 'h