'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d31ff0d-ab97-5790-bbcb-846a397bba7d', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d31ff0d-ab97-5790-bbcb-846a397bba7d'}, {'abstract': 'The selections include chocolate truffles with rye whiskey, Scotch, bourbon or chocolate stout ganache inside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/dining/vosges-chocolates-with-liquor-for-dad-food-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'The selections include chocolate truffles with rye whiskey, Scotch, bourbon or chocolate stout ganache inside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mom is the one who usually gets the fancy chocolates; for Dad, it’s a bottle. But Vosges Haut-Chocolat has come up with a gift that has both, putting the booze in the bonbons. The company has packed an assortment in a handsome vintage-style cigar box. There are two sleek dark chocolate bars with a thin filling of gooey caramel flavored with stout; a box of nine chocolate truffles with rye whiskey, Scotch, bourbon or chocolate stout ganache inside (the Scotch, a smoky Islay, is the most assertive); some nonalcoholic peanut butter bonbons; and caramels with and without bacon. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFF_CHOCOLATE/13STUFF_CHOCOLATE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1193, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13STUFF_CHOCOLATE/13STUFF_CHOCOLATE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1759, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's