uinnipiac University survey shows President Obama with a 6-point lead over Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama is viewed more favorably in Pennsylvania than Mitt Romney, and most voters there say the president would do a better job on foreign policy. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Stays Ahead in Pennsylvania Poll', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, Robert P Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T17:03:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dalia Sussman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dalia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f512615-8dbe-55d0-81cb-8f9418532119', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f512615-8dbe-55d0-81cb-8f9418532119'}, {'abstract': 'Backstage at Stella McCartney’s fairground-themed resort presentation, held on Monday at a cemetery in the East Village.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/resort-report-stella-mccartney/', 'snippet': 'Backstage at Stella McCartney’s fairground-themed resort presentation, held on Monday at a cemetery in the East Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function j