rl': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06PIMMS1_SPAN/06PIMMS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06PIMMS1_SPAN/06PIMMS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/06/dining/06PIMMS1_SPAN/06PIMMS1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From That Tropical-Drink Paradise, England', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From That Tropical-Drink Paradise, England', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T17:51:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Simonson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simonson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05c1d669-7161-5627-8152-1ad59be4ce85', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05c1d669-7161-5627-8152-1ad59be4ce85'}, {'abstract': 'The Times’s restaurant critic laments the departure of three top chefs.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/requiem-for-the-oddities-of-isa/', 'snippet': 'The Times’s restaurant critic laments the departure of three top chefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One time a food critic from another city asked me what kind of food Prune served. I had a hard time answering, because the restaurant seemed uncategorizable to me; the place looked like a bistro, but the menu didn’t look like a bistro menu, or like any other menu in town. Finally I resorted to telling him about the dishes: They serve canned sardines with Triscuits, I said. There’s bone marrow, and a dish that has an octopus tentacle next to a beef tongue. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Requiem for the Oddities of Isa', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Somer, Taavo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Isa (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T17:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fbd0e90-71b2-54b8-9346-dec2a12a3d7f', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fbd0e90-71b2-54b8-9346-dec2a12a3d7f'}, {'abstract': 'From Hawaii, David J. Flaspohler, an avian ecologist and conservation biologist, examines the question of how life begins after it has been extinguished from a patch of the earth.', 'web_url': 'https://scientistatwork.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/a-delicate-web-of-life-that-started-with-lava/', 'snippet': 'From Hawaii, David J. Flaspohler, an avian ecologist and conservation biologist, examines the question of how life begins after it has been extinguished from a patch of the earth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David J. Flaspohler, an avian ecologist and conservation biologist at Michigan Technological University, writes from Hawaii, where he is studying the influence of human activities on birds and the natural ecosystems that support them. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Delicate Web of Life That Started With Lava', 'kicker': 'Scientist at Work', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biodiversity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii (The Big Island)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T17:55:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By David J. Flaspohler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Flaspohler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e2fa662-f945-58c2-aa46-1bcb4fd1c399', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e2fa662-f945-58c2-aa46-1bcb4fd1c399'}, {'abstract': 'Catherine Greig, longtime mistress of James (Whitey) Bulger, admitted to helping him elude the police for years, but it is not clear whether she will be made to testify against him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/us/girlfriend-of-whitey-bulger-gets-8-year-prison-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'Catherine Greig, longtime mistress of James (Whitey) Bulger, admitted to helping him elude the police for years, but it is not clear whether she will be made to testify against him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Catherine E. Greig, the longtime girlfriend of the crime boss James (Whitey) Bulger, was sentenced on Tuesday to eight years in prison for her role in helping him elude the authorities during the 16 years the two spent in hidi