person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/297671c4-d41e-52b6-915f-7af509c0f7e4', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/297671c4-d41e-52b6-915f-7af509c0f7e4'}, {'abstract': 'An emergency room physician and Wikipedia editor noticed the similarities between an H.I.V. article and a book on pediatrics.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/book-that-plagiarized-from-wikipedia-is-pulled-from-market/', 'snippet': 'An emergency room physician and Wikipedia editor noticed the similarities between an H.I.V. article and a book on pediatrics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Indian publisher, Jaypee Brothers Medical Publishers, said on Tuesday that it had withdrawn a medical textbook after an editor of Wikipedia wrote to say that a section had been plagiarized from the Wikipedia article on H.I.V.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book That Plagiarized From Wikipedia Is Pulled From Market', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daef62fd-8ec4-53bb-b777-11ddafc7896f', 'word_count': 390, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daef62fd-8ec4-53bb-b777-11ddafc7896f'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans on the Senate Judiciary Committee on Tuesday strongly criticized Attorney General Eric Holder’s decision to appoint two United States attorneys to investigate recent disclosures of classified national security information.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/republican-lawmakers-and-holder-spar-over-leak-investigation/', 'snippet': 'Republicans on the Senate Judiciary Committee on Tuesday strongly criticized Attorney General Eric Holder’s decision to appoint two United States attorneys to investigate recent disclosures of classified national security information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republican members of the Senate Judiciary Committee on Tuesday strongly criticized Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr.’s recent decision to appoint two United States attorneys to investigate recent disclosures of classified national security information, saying the move was not enough and that he should appoint a special prosecutor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Republican Lawmakers and Holder Spar Over Leak Investigation', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:27:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael S. Schmidt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Schmidt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54e7cf5f-742a-53fe-bf20-b37fa1d8ac15', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54e7cf5f-742a-53fe-bf20-b37fa1d8ac15'}, {'abstract': 'The Treasury Department reached the settlement over accusations of noncompliance with United States sanctions against Iran, Cuba and other countries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/business/ing-bank-to-pay-619-million-over-sanctions-violations.html', 'snippet': 'The Treasury Department reached the settlement over accusations of noncompliance with United States sanctions against Iran, Cuba and other countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Treasury Department announced on Tuesday that it had reached a $619 million settlement with ING Bank to settle an investigation into compliance with United States sanctions against Iran, Cuba and other countries. It is the largest fine a bank has paid to settle accusations of sanctions violations. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ING Bank to Pay $619 Million to Settle Inquiry Into Sanctions Violations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ING Bank to Pay $619 Million to Settle Inquiry Into Sanctions Violations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ING Groep N.V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:33:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Lowrey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowrey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afa55118-910c-506f-a604-77dd9773f23c', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afa55118-910c-506f-a604-77dd9773f23c'}, {'abstract': 'The man who greened dry regions through efficient irrigation gets a big prize.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/food-prize-for-pioneer-in-drip-by-drip-farming-efficiency/', 'snippet': 'The man who greened dry regions through efficient irrigation gets a big prize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve intersected a few times with Daniel Hillel, a pioneering agricultural innovator from Israel, and each time I’ve come away with new insights, often about subjects far broader than the efficient irrigation methods he devised and refined, which have helped dry regions around the world feed themselves. It’s great to see him named this year’s recipient of the World Food Prize, an award created in 1987 by another agricultural leader, Norman Borlaug (read Justin Gillis’s fine obituary of Borlaug here). ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Prize for Pioneer in Drip-by-Drip Farming Efficiency', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drought', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Irrigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0e1f5ba-05aa-58fc-ad9a-fac649bc348e', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0e1f5ba-05aa-58fc-ad9a-fac649bc348e'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney suggested we have too many firefighters, teachers and policemen.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/we-dont-need-no-teachers/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney suggested we have too many firefighters, teachers and policemen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a squabble in the presidential campaign over whether Mitt Romney said the country needs fewer police officers, firefighters and teachers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Don’t Need No Teachers!', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75868880-1cd9-5b7c-b434-5662c7ac65c6', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75868880-1cd9-5b7c-b434-5662c7ac65c6'}, {'abstract': 'The object as an art form and design solution, courtesy of the London-based architect.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/mirror-mirror-david-adjaye/', 'snippet': 'The object as an art form and design solution, courtesy of the London-based architect.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A mirror, to me, reflects life,” said David Adjaye of his most recent creations. “They create luminosity and brightness, and you can see the brightness more the less it acts like a mirror and the more it behaves like a reflecting plane.” The London-based architect, who was the 2011 Designer of the Year at Design Miami (and who is designing Proenza Schouler’s soon-to-open first store, on Madison Avenue) had been thinking about mirrors following a conversation he had “about a year ago” with his friend, the fashion designer Duro Olowu, about the act of gazing. “That’s what inspired the thinking, that a mirror is more than an object to look at yourself in,” Adjaye recalled. Olowu included Adjaye’s mirrors in “Material,” a group show he curated at Salon 94 Freemans earlier this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mirror, Mirror | David Adjaye', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:40:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rima Suqi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rima', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Suqi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7245a283-d0ef-5c76-89d3-e3fc29fae56e', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7245a283-d0ef-5c76-89d3-e3fc29fae56e'}, {'abstract': "June 12, 2012 - Hopes for job creation, in Ohio's pottery industry.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001601706/pottery-makes-a-comeback-in-ohio.html', 'snippet': "June 12, 2012 - Hopes for job creation, in Ohio's pottery industry.", 'lead_paragraph': "June 12, 2012 - Hopes for job creation, in Ohio's pottery industry.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/video-bdl-120612-pottery/video-bdl-120612-pottery-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/12/business/video-bdl-120612-pottery/video-bdl-120612-pottery-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/12/business/video-bdl-120612-pottery/video-bdl-120612-pottery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/12/business/video-bdl-120612-pottery/video-bdl-120612-pottery-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pottery Makes a Comeback in Ohio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop, Nadia Sussman, Pedro Rosado and Channon Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nadia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/18240cff-0342-55f4-a476-1e81d0078325', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/18240cff-0342-55f4-a476-1e81d0078325'}, {'abstract': 'Pair a modifier like Campari with a base spirit and a mixer, and you have a number of classic drinks at hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/12/dining/summer-drinks-generator.html', 'snippet': 'Pair a modifier like Campari with a base spirit and a mixer, and you have a number of classic drinks at hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pair a modifier like Campari with a base spirit and a mixer, and you have a number of classic drinks at hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Drinks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:42:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Food', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/89d0719d-1e85-5dfd-9e23-f2a542f1bb9f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/89d0719d-1e85-5dfd-9e23-f2a542f1bb9f'}, {'abstract': 'Oil-based emollients can help protect hair throughout summer, as well as facilitating the wet look that was seen on many spring runways.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/oil-slick-serums-for-sleek-summer-hair/', 'snippet': 'Oil-based emollients can help protect hair throughout summer, as well as facilitating the wet look that was seen on many spring runways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many people don’t realize that the sun can wreak as much havoc on their hair as their skin.“The UV light damages your hair,” said Dr. Debra Jaliman, a New York dermatologist and author of “Skin Rules.” “It breaks the chemical bonds, which causes split ends and makes hair more susceptible to breakage.”David Lopez, a hairstylist in New York who has worked with many celebrities, said that sun exposure can also lead to “dryness, frizz and even cause hair color to fade if you dye it.”Perhaps counterintuitively given that hot, humid weather can result in lank strands, oil-based emollients can help protect hair throughout summer, as well as facilitating the wet look that was seen on many spring runways. Here are some hair oils currently on the market. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oil Slick: Serums for Sleek Summer Strands', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrea Artebery', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Artebery', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6be70ae-4971-5846-aec2-b8a2b704ddca', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6be70ae-4971-5846-aec2-b8a2b704ddca'}, {'abstract': 'For a standout cocktail party, don’t settle for what’s around the house. Look to modifiers like liqueurs, bitters, vermouths and fortified wines to give mixed drinks a professional look and flavor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/dining/how-bartenders-use-liqueurs-and-bitters.html', 'snippet': 'For a standout cocktail party, don’t settle for what’s around the house. Look to modifiers like liqueurs, bitters, vermouths and fortified wines to give mixed drinks a professional look and flavor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A COCKTAIL party shouldn’t start with the first brandish of a shaker; it should start with a menu. Curating a short list of drinks, instead of casting around for something novel to mix with that gin, allows you to serve drinks that will please even your most discerning guests, and to be a more nimble host.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN/13SUBMEEHAN_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Embellish Like Bartenders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Embellish Like Bartenders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T18:45:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk