used to allow his work to be sold in e-book format.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Long Resistance, Pynchon Allows Novels to Be Sold as E-Books', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Godoff, Ann', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pynchon, Thomas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Penguin Group', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T20:11:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14e83221-1665-5e92-a65c-c74e00f1fb8c', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e83221-1665-5e92-a65c-c74e00f1fb8c'}, {'abstract': 'The use of advanced diagnostic imaging like CT and PET scans has soared in recent years, even when doctors do not stand to profit, a study of H.M.O. data has found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/health/as-medical-imaging-rises-radiation-concerns-follow.html', 'snippet': 'The use of advanced diagnostic imaging like CT and PET scans has soared in recent years, even when doctors do not stand to profit, a study of H.M.O. data has found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in health care systems in which doctors do not bill for each test they administer, the use of diagnostic imaging like CT and PET scans has soared, as has patients’ radiation exposure, a new study has found.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Radiation Concerns Rise With Patients’ Exposure', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Radiation Concerns Rise With Patients’ Exposure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the American Medical Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computerized Axial Tomography (CAT Scans)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T20:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Gee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af1c155a-888b-535c-b0f6-1b4419d64317', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af1c155a-888b-535c-b0f6-1b4419d64317'}, {'abstract': 'Gina Chon agreed to resign after she admitted violating company policy by showing articles before publication to Brett McGurk, then on the National Security Council staff.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/journal-reporter-quits-over-e-mails-to-iraqi-envoy-nominee/', 'snippet': 'Gina Chon agreed to resign after she admitted violating company policy by showing articles before publication to Brett McGurk, then on the National Security Council staff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Wall Street Journal reporter who traded steamy e-mails with Brett McGurk, the Obama ad