ost concerts are performed in the 1,000-seat open-air Libbey Bowl, adjacent to this charming town’s park. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/13jpfestival/13jpfestival-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/13jpfestival/13jpfestival-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ojai Savors a Scandinavian Import: Long Musical Nights', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ojai Savors a Scandinavian Import: Long Musical Nights', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANDSNES, LEIF OVE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ojai (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T21:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f299d0-c9ec-5eee-ac06-58d646d37d58', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f299d0-c9ec-5eee-ac06-58d646d37d58'}, {'abstract': 'A new generation of good and bad Ewings butts heads at Southfork in the resurrected “Dallas” on TNT.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/arts/television/dallas-is-updated-in-new-tnt-series.html', 'snippet': 'A new generation of good and bad Ewings butts heads at Southfork in the resurrected “Dallas” on TNT.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were brewery assembly line workers, pioneers on the prairie and plenty of detectives in the spring of 1978, but it was hard to find a rich person in prime time. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/television/13dallas4/13dallas4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fossil Fuels and New Energy', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fossil Fuels and New Energy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henderson, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duffy, Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagman, Larry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Turner Network Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gray, Linda', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dallas (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metcalfe, Jesse', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T21:57:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba8757d-9f6b-53a1-9995-d6b036d335b6', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba8757d-9f6b-53a1-9995-d6b036d335b6'}, {'abstract': 'Lost for four decades, a 1936 Mercedes roadster may set price records when it’s auctioned off in August.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-baroness-and-her-lost-mercedes/', 'snippet': 'Lost for four decades, a 1936 Mercedes roadster may set price records when it’s auctioned off in August.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1992, when David Gooding worked in the car department at Christie’s, he received a telephone call from a lawyer charged with settling the estate of an elderly woman who had died alone in Vevey, Switzerland. For a time this woman summered at a hotel in Greenwich, Conn., and among her possessions there was a dusty old Mercedes that had been languishing in a warehouse, surrounded by old carnival equipment. “It’s black,” Gooding recalled the lawyer saying. “It’s a convertible, and it’s old.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Baroness and Her Lost Mercedes', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T22:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56613c9b-74a6-5ae3-804a-09dd7ea7e234', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56613c9b-74a6-5ae3-804a-09dd7ea7e234'}, {'abstract': 'The spirits panel tasted 20 bottles of gin, mostly made by young distilleries. The lesson was clear: making gin is not for amateurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/dining/gin-leads-summers-fight.html', 'snippet': 'The spirits panel tasted 20 bottles of gin, mostly made by young distilleries. The lesson was clear: making gin is not for amateurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GROW your own, brew your own, butcher your own, ferment your own. This has been the mantra of the do-it-yourself ethos in pursuit of authentic flavors and pleasures uncorrupted by corporate or other intrusive interests. Distill your own was never far behind.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SPIRITS_SPAN/13SPIRITS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/dining/13SPIRITS_SPAN/13SPIRITS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 3