T22:11:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b77ec3d5-b179-55b4-99ae-c1fcee93d781', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b77ec3d5-b179-55b4-99ae-c1fcee93d781'}, {'abstract': 'In a city that’s home to the world’s top-ranked restaurant, what can the Frugal Traveler find to eat?', 'web_url': 'https://frugaltraveler.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/eating-frugally-in-copenhagen/', 'snippet': 'In a city that’s home to the world’s top-ranked restaurant, what can the Frugal Traveler find to eat?', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s become really hip to eat old-fashioned Danish food,” Nina A.S. Geist told me as we shared a kartoffelmad — an open-faced potato sandwich loaded with crispy fried onions — at Dyrehaven, a local cafe in the fun Vesterbro neighborhood of Copenhagen. It was great to hear this from a Dane, because from abroad what appears most hip about Danish cuisine is Noma, the world’s top-ranked restaurant for the second year running, according to Restaurant Magazine’s much-blabbed-about list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eating Frugally in Copenhagen', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T22:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By SETH KUGEL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KUGEL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75762eb5-3991-52a7-9e71-3c1941c78950', 'word_count': 1690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75762eb5-3991-52a7-9e71-3c1941c78950'}, {'abstract': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s new choreography for “Firebird” has its New York premiere with American Ballet Theater at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/arts/dance/ratmanskys-firebird-for-american-ballet-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Alexei Ratmansky’s new choreography for “Firebird” has its New York premiere with American Ballet Theater at the Metropolitan Opera House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Parts of Alexei Ratmansky’s “Firebird” make me wish that I were a child again, with him as a parent or godfather telling old stories with new twists and dimensions. At its best, his “Firebird,” which had its New York premiere with American Ballet Theater on Monday night at the Metropolitan Opera House, feels timeless and modern, an ancient myth for the children, with sexual and psychological layers that appeal to adult intelligence today.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1/SUB-FIREBIRD-JP-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,