rk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82ab8f53-f541-54f9-aa2e-3de400c888a6', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82ab8f53-f541-54f9-aa2e-3de400c888a6'}, {'abstract': 'The six new landmarks were all erected within a few decades after New York City’s five boroughs consolidated in 1898.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/3-firehouses-among-6-buildings-now-designated-city-landmarks/', 'snippet': 'The six new landmarks were all erected within a few decades after New York City’s five boroughs consolidated in 1898.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each has a distinct architectural style. One, a narrow three-story building with a bold red door, features a recessed stone eagle overlooking an ashlar limestone entrance. The second, completed in neo-Classical style, is one of the first of its kind in the city to feature two truck-size doors instead of just one. The third, a churchlike Neo-Medieval brick fortress, has steep gables and a hose-drying tower.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '3 Firehouses Among 6 Buildings Now Designated City Landmarks', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Landmarks Preservation Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mansfield Hotel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T22:43:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric P. Newcomer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Newcomer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organ