nator Olympia J. Snowe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update 12:15 a.m.: Charles Summers, the Secretary of State, emerged the winner Tuesday night of the six-way primary on the Republican side for the Senate seat being vacated by Olympia J. Snowe. On the Democratic side, state Senator Cynthia Dill won the four-way primary. The two will face each other — and Angus King, the independent and former two-term governor — in November, along with some lesser known independent candidates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maine Begins to Pick a Senate Successor to Snowe', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-12T22:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95f197c4-b22f-5149-a972-c958213a8e22', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95f197c4-b22f-5149-a972-c958213a8e22'}, {'abstract': '“UFO in Her Eyes,” a satire directed by Xiaolu Guo, is now showing at MoMA.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/movies/ufo-in-her-eyes-a-chinese-satire-at-moma.html', 'snippet': '“UFO in Her Eyes,” a satire directed by Xiaolu Guo, is now showing at MoMA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three-Headed Bird Village — the setting for Xiaolu Guo’s stingingly funny satire, “UFO in Her Eyes” — is a quiet agricultural hamlet in the Guangxi province of southern China that is uprooted by instant globalization. The catalyst is a sighting by Kwok Yun (Shi Ke), an unmarried peasant in her 30s, of what she believes is a U.F.O. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia