-walshs-opponent/', 'snippet': 'Joe Walsh, the singer and guitarist for The Eagles, endorsed Tammy Duckworth in her race against the rocker’s namesake, Rep. Joe Walsh, a first-term Republican running for re-election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Type the name Joe Walsh into any search engine, and two very different people pop up. The first, Representative Joe Walsh of Illinois, is a first-term Republican running for re-election. The second is a Rock and Roll Hall of Famer who endorsed the congressman’s Democratic opponent on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Endorsing Joe Walsh’s Opponent', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disambiguation: Endorsing Joe Walsh’s Opponent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duckworth, L Tammy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T00:49:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Yaccino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yaccino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1857ea96-833c-5a43-9888-1067352ff552', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1857ea96-833c-5a43-9888-1067352ff552'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Rutherford, a Hollywood actress cast in innocent parts, also played Scarlett O’Hara’s sister in “Gone With the Wind.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/movies/ann-rutherford-andy-hardys-screen-sweetheart-dies-at-94.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Rutherford, a Hollywood actress cast in innocent parts, also played Scarlett O’Hara’s sister in “Gone With the Wind.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ann Rutherford, an actress who became famous in the late 1930s as Mickey Rooney’s sweetheart in the hugely successful Andy Hardy series and earned a role in one of the biggest movies in Hollywood history, as Scarlett O’Hara’s sister in “Gone With the Wind,” died on Monday at her home in Beverly Hills, Calif. She was 94. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1529, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/RUTHERFORD1-obit/RUTHERFORD1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': '