nytimes.com/2012/06/13/technology/google-street-view-case-brought-employee-denials.html', 'snippet': 'Google insiders said they were not aware of the data collection in the Street View project either because it was not part of their job or they did not review the project documentation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google has long prided itself on not being a conventional company. But there is one characteristic it apparently shares with the most sclerotic bureaucracy: the willingness of its employees to say, “Not my job.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1526, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/13/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/GOOGLE/GOOGLE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Denials Over Google Street View', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Denials Over Google Street View', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Street View', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T02:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9154097-676c-5de0-96b0-13d9572ba006', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9154097-676c-5de0-96b0-13d9572ba006'}, {'abstract': 'After the median family’s net worth plummeted after the Great Recession, Americans deserve a robust debate in the presidential campaign on ways to recover.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/opinion/the-beleaguered-middle-class-wealth-erased.html', 'snippet': 'After the median family’s net worth plummeted after the Great Recession, Americans deserve a robust debate in the presidential campaign on ways to recover.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans know, all too well, the pain unleashed by the Great Recession of 2007-9. Still the numbers on the loss of personal wealth during those years are staggering and say a lot about why the economic recovery has been so sluggish — and why the government will need to do a lot more to turn things around. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wealth Erased', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Beleaguered Middle Class: The crisis has erased nearly two decades of wealth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T02:22:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ff64d3e-a4d4-5b16-82a2-d96585ef7c6a', 'word_count': 394, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ff64d3e-a4d4-5b16-82a2-d96585ef7c6a'}, {'abstract': 'Since former President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt received a life sentence, a torrent of leaks has sprung suggesting that he may be nearing his end.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/world/middleeast/once-illegal-health-rumors-now-have-mubarak-die-daily.html', 'snippet': 'Since former President Hosni Mubarak of Egypt received a life sentence, a torrent of leaks has sprung suggesting that he may be nearing his end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Former President Hosni Mubarak uses a wheelchair, is able to eat little more than Jell-O, and has his two grown sons by his bedside. He suffers from sore joints in his feet, high blood pressure, shortness of breath and, according to rumors widely circulated in the Egyptian and foreign press, he required artificial respiration and heart defibrillation within the space of just 24 hours last weekend. Twice, doctors could not find his pulse, the reports said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/world/middleeast/MUBARAK/MUBARAK-articleLarge.jpg', 'heigh