CO — Rory McIlroy was spotted on the Olympic Club driving range throwing a golf ball at his bag. He was practicing — not for his United States Open defense, beginning Thursday, but for his appearance Tuesday night at the Giants’ home game against the Houston Astros. It was Irish Heritage Night and McIlroy, who is from Northern Ireland, was asked to throw out the first pitch. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McIlroy Tries His Hand as a Pitcher', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:04:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c242fd6-ba08-542d-b602-682f667220e8', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c242fd6-ba08-542d-b602-682f667220e8'}, {'abstract': 'In New Orleans and in Alabama on Tuesday, scores of newspaper employees walked into one-on-one meetings and walked out 10 minutes later with severance packages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/us/new-orleans-struggles-with-latest-storm-newspaper-layoffs.html', 'snippet': 'In New Orleans and in Alabama on Tuesday, scores of newspaper employees walked into one-on-one meetings and walked out 10 minutes later with severance packages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW ORLEANS — Brett Anderson kept his face out of the paper and gave fake names when making reservations, as dining critics customarily do, but in a town like New Orleans he was not fooling many people. They know Mr. Anderson by sight, just as they knew that a reporter named Katy Reckdahl had had a baby in New Orleans 24 hours before Hurricane Katrina hit — she wrote a big article about it in the paper five years later, but people knew.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/us/PICAYUNE/PICAYUNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/us/PICAYUNE/PICAYUNE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/us/PICAYUNE/PICAYUNE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/us/PICAYUNE/PICAYUNE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Orleans Struggles With Latest Storm, Newspaper Layoffs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Orleans Struggles With Latest Storm, Newspaper Layoffs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times-Picayune (New Orleans)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advance Publications Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birmingham News', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:11:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68514957-80bc-5f22-a272-2021e10066b1', 'word_count': 1280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68514957-80bc-5f22-a272-2021e10066b1'}, {'abstract': 'The Los Angeles Kings’ victory on Monday to win the Stanley Cup was seen by an average of 4.9 million viewers, down 10 percent from the comparable game last year between the Bruins and Canucks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/sports/hockey/stanley-cup-viewership-down-from-last-year.html', 'snippet': 'The Los Angeles Kings’ victory on Monday to win the Stanley Cup was seen by an average of 4.9 million viewers, down 10 percent from the comparable game last year between the Bruins and Canucks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Los Angeles Kings’ 6-1 throttling of the Devils on Monday night to win the Stanley Cup was seen by an average of 4.9 million viewers, down 10 percent from the nearly 5.5 million who watched the comparable game last year between the Boston Bruins and Vancouver Canucks. NBC carried the last four games of the Stanley Cup finals, averaging 3.5 million viewers, down 34 percent from the five games the network showed last year, when the Bruins won. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stanley Cup Viewership Down From Last Year', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Hockey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cup Viewership Down From ’11', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Kings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/83a974f0-af3f-5164-b2ca-c41e7f38decc', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83a974f0-af3f-5164-b2ca-c41e7f38decc'}, {'abstract': 'There are populists in both parties whose hostility to illegal immigration will make any agreement much harder to reach than elites on both sides realize.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/12/the-great-immigration-reform-mirage/', 'snippet': 'There are populists in both parties whose hostility to illegal immigration will make any agreement much harder to reach than elites on both sides realize.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a breakfast interview with Bloomberg View on Monday, Jeb Bush, the former governor of Florida, expressed general disappointment with the Republican Party’s rightward drift since his brother left the White House in 2009. He also cited a specific place where his party needs to return to the center: The issue of immigration reform. According to Bush, Mitt Romney’s focus on border enforcement has placed him “in a box” and limited his appeal to Hispanic voters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Immigration Reform Mirage', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 