able to meeting with him. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fleck Had Suggestions  for Woods, but Not a Way to Reach Him', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleck, Jack', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Tiger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Golf Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42c14114-c4c4-54d5-aead-85147d23095a', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42c14114-c4c4-54d5-aead-85147d23095a'}, {'abstract': 'The health care law, now under review by the Supreme Court, requires states to have health insurance exchanges by January 2014. Some states have made extensive plans, while others have done little.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/12/us/states-progress-on-health-insurance-exchanges.html', 'snippet': 'The health care law, now under review by the Supreme Court, requires states to have health insurance exchanges by January 2014. Some states have made extensive plans, while others have done little.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The health care law, now under review by the Supreme Court, requires states to have health insurance exchanges by January 2014. Some states have made extensive plans, while others have done little.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'States’ Progress on Exchanges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:36:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/498612c7-b7ec-5d2c-9059-d784c8bae0b0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/498612c7-b7ec-5d2c-9059-d784c8bae0b0'}, {'abstract': 'An Iranian naval commander announced the project Tuesday, according to the Fars news agency. Some fear Iran could use the submarine to justify enriching uranium to higher levels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/world/middleeast/iran-says-it-is-building-a-nuclear-powered-submarine.html', 'snippet': 'An Iranian naval commander announced the project Tuesday, according to the Fars news agency. Some fear Iran could use the submarine to justify enriching uranium to higher levels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An Iranian naval commander said Tuesday that Iran had begun work on its first nuclear-powered submarine. “We have taken the first steps in the direction of building nuclear-powered submarines,” Deputy Navy Cmdr. Abbas Zamini said, according to the Fars news agency. Some analysts fear Iran could use the submarine project to justify enriching uranium to higher levels. Mark Hibbs, a nuclear proliferation expert at the Carnegie Endowment for International Peace, was cited by Reuters as saying that many nuclear-powered submarines use uranium fuel enriched to levels that could also be suitable for atomic bombs. Iran is scheduled to meet next week with international negotiators over its nuclear program. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Says It Is Building a Nuclear-Powered Submarine', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Says It Is Building a Nuclear-Powered Submarine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Submarines and Submersibles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:37:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Artin Afkhami', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Artin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Afkhami', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5f0d2dd-94fd-5a7d-b069-4e4102e59d32', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5f0d2dd-94fd-5a7d-b069-4e4102e59d32'}, {'abstract': 'Debate over the health law has centered on the individual mandate, but the focus could shift to insurance exchanges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/us/navigating-the-health-care-maze.html', 'snippet': 'Debate over the health law has centered on the individual mandate, but the focus could shift to insurance exchanges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Even a self-described data nerd like Peter Kim was nearly undone by his hunt for health insurance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/us/EXCHANGE-1/EXCHANGE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/us/EXCHANGE-1/EXCHANGE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 6