people and leading to more than 120 arrests. Riot police used water cannons, tear-gas and rubber bullets to contain the street fighting that broke out hours before Russia and Poland played to a draw in the European soccer championship, an event that Polish officials hoped would showcase the country’s recent strides. But enmity between Russia and Poland runs centuries deep and a march by Russian fans in honor of their national holiday, Russia Day, brought out Polish fans and clashes erupted. Polish soccer hooligans chanted, “Hit the red trash with a hammer, with a sickle” and “Instead of leaves, there’ll be communists hanging from the trees.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poland: For Russia-Poland Pre-Game, a Street Fight', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poland: For Russia-Poland Pre-Game, A Street Fight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T03:58:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b140c1e7-4d3c-532a-8096-f10969bd0a7d', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b140c1e7-4d3c-532a-8096-f10969bd0a7d'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 161 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https: