tps://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/after-liposuction-exercise-keeps-the-fat-off/', 'snippet': 'Liposuction, generally considered the most popular form of cosmetic surgery, removes fat from just beneath the skin, but to avoid regaining fat of an even more harmful variety, a new study suggests, people need to exercise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Liposuction, generally considered the most popular cosmetic surgical procedure in the United States and worldwide, involves suctioning out subcutaneous fat cells, those that accumulate just beneath the skin. But to gain lasting benefits, a new study suggests, people need to exercise. Otherwise they risk regaining the fat lost during surgery and redistributing that fat to their midsections, an outcome that has the potential to make them less healthy than before the operation. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Liposuction, Exercise Keeps the Fat Off', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liposuction', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastic Surgery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T04:01:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97a3bccb-9446-5158-8f19-18eb35f142e9', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97a3bccb-9446-5158-8f19-18eb35f142e9'}, {'abstract': 'The arrangement expands on an existing content-sharing relationship between the two sites and will include co-productions of online video shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/business/media/cnbc-and-yahoo-finance-expand-partnership-to-online-video.html', 'snippet': 'The arrangement expands on an existing content-sharing relationship between the two sites and will include co-productions of online video shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Seeking to improve its standing among business news Web sites, CNBC will announce a new partnership on Wednesday with Yahoo Finance, the largest such Web site in the United States.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/CNBC/CNBC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/business/CNBC/CNBC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1843, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Bolster Web Reach, CNBC Joins With Yahoo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Bolster Web Reach, CNBC Joins With Yahoo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNBC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T04:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiz