vered with disheveled blankets, three more children lie bandaged; plastic sheeting covers a window and a bookshelf, as if the room was quarantined, or as if its owner were clinging to normalcy by protecting the furniture. In another picture (Slide 13), wounded men, one in camouflage fatigues, lie cheek by jowl on floral print couches.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rare View of Conflict in Syria', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Homs (Syria)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lebanon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T09:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b19926f-4e87-5d36-8894-f4e105351a5e', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b19926f-4e87-5d36-8894-f4e105351a5e'}, {'abstract': 'Selective disclosures of sensitive information can be a form of currency to reward or punish news organizations, and ultimately are a disservice to media independence, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/leaks-and-press-freedoms/', 'snippet': 'Selective disclosures of sensitive information can be a form of currency to reward or punish news organizations, and ultimately are a disservice to media independence, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaks and Press Freedoms', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc176182-59ef-5cd4-a89b-b63f34ce4bce', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc176182-59ef-5cd4-a89b-b63f34ce4bce'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/the-early-word-dialing-for-dollars/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today’s Times', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Dialing for Dollars', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T10:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b8bf411-2bb9-5c0d-ae33-2118069b2538', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b8bf411-2bb9-5c0d-ae33-2118069b2538'}, {'abstract': 'Pitchers who were once highly regarded, and who seem to be rebounding from woeful stretches, may represent bargains in the fantasy marketplace.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/fantasy-focus-buy-good-pitchers-running-bad/', 'snippet': 'Pitchers who were once highly regarded, and who seem to be rebounding from woeful stretches, may represent bargains in the fantasy marketplace.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An odd thing has happened this year, though perhaps it happens every year: pitchers who were former (or prospective) aces, but recently left for dead, have recaptured their form for stretches of varying lengths. Consider Jake Peavy and Johan Santana, two former Cy Young Award winners you could have drafted in the later rounds. Santana, even after being shelled by the Yankees, has a 73:22 strikeout/walk ratio in 73 innings and an earned run average of 2.96. Peavy has fallen off of late but still has a 72:20 K/BB ratio in 82 2/3 innings, a 3.05 E.R.A. and an 0.968 WHIP.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Focus: Buy Good Pitchers Running Bad', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buchholz, Clay', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hughes, Phil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jimenez, Ubaldo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liriano, Francisco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matusz, Brian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T10:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Liss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb569a64-7419-514a-82dc-c406584e7529', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb569a64-7419-514a-82dc-c406584e7529'}, {'abstract': 'UEFA’s plan to expand the European Championships to 24 teams will most likely mean the end of the so-called Group of Death.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/the-impending-death-of-the-group-of-death/', 'snippet': 'UEFA’s plan to expand the European Championships to 24 teams will most likely mean the end of the so-called Group of Death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Along with predictions of German triumph, supermarket beer promotions, organized Oranje invasions and metatarsal injuries, the Group of Death has become a time-honored element of major tournament culture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Impending Death of the Group of Death', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T10:02:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Ruthven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruthven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a2b1d15-b775-5058-9277-776a41abe39c', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a2b1d15-b775-5058-9277-776a41abe39c'}, {'abstract': 'The Syrian government announced that Al Heffa, a village where a massacre had been feared, was now open to United Nations inspectors because it had been “cleansed.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/world/middleeast/new-weapons-push-syrian-crisis-toward-civil-war.html', 'snippet': 'The Syrian government announced that Al Heffa, a village where a massacre had been feared, was now open to United Nations inspectors because it had been “cleansed.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — Syria announced on Wednesday that the village of Al Heffa in its Mediterranean hinterland, which United Nations monitors had been physically blocked from visiting to check on fears of a massacre there, had been “cleansed” of armed terrorist gangs, the government’s blanket term for the opposition.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Kept Out of a Town That Syria Says It ‘Cleansed’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Kept Out of a Town That Syria Says It ‘Cleansed’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian National Council', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arms Trade', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T10:31:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil MacFarquhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MacFarquhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e425d275-68d8-5887-aec9-2c730371e574', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e425d275-68d8-5887-aec9-2c730371e574'}, {'abstract': 'Philipp M. Hildebrand, who will oversee BlackRock’s institutional client relationships outside the United States, stepped down from the Swiss National Bank in January after doubts were raised about currency trades he and his wife made in 2011.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/blackrock-hires-former-swiss-central-bank-chief/', 'snippet': 'Philipp M. Hildebrand, who will oversee BlackRock’s institutional client relationships outside the United States, stepped down from the Swiss National Bank in January after doubts were raised about currency trades he and his wife made in 2011.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The money manager BlackRock has hired Philipp M. Hildebrand, who resigned under a cloud from the Swiss National Bank in January, to oversee institutional client relationships outside the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BlackRock Hires Former Swiss Central Bank Chief', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hildebrand, Philipp M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackRock Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swiss National Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T10:37:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c1ee39a-467d-5673-bdbe-cf1753bd57b8', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c1ee39a-467d-5673-bdbe-cf1753bd57b8'}, {'abstract': 'The famous provocateur is fed up with MoMA and the state of her love life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/magazine/the-devil-in-marina-abramovic.html', 'snippet': 'The famous provocateur is fed up with MoMA and the state of her love life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching the new documentary about you, “The Artist Is Present,” got me curious about the economics of performance art. In 2010, you did a show at the Museum of Modern Art, where you sat for 700 hours, staring at visitors. It was seen by as many as 750,000 people, and during that time the museum collected millions in receipts. Did you get a cut of the door, like a musician? I got so little I don’t even want to tell. I was paid an honorarium of exactly $100,000. It covered one year of my work, plus how much I pay for assistants and office rent.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17talk/mag-17talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17talk/mag-17talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17talk/mag-17talk-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'