tament to short memories, a willingness to forgive and the potent desire to win.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/for-a-virginia-republican-a-comeback-and-a-tough-fight-ahead/', 'snippet': 'The Republican Party’s willingness to once again embrace George Allen as its Senate candidate for Virginia stands as a testament to short memories, a willingness to forgive and the potent desire to win.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Political redemption, it seems, is almost never completely out of reach.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Virginia Republican, a Comeback and a Tough Fight Ahead', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Political Memo: A Comeback in Virginia, Shadowed by a Stumble', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, GEORGE F', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor, Eric', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaine, Timothy M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Webb, James H Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T12:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2e84a14-79ea-5916-8405-b6d7a30d9409', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2e84a14-79ea-5916-8405-b6d7a30d9409'}, {'abstract': 'Metropolitan Diary: Relying on free street samples for lunch can be unsatisfying, especially if one doesn’t examine the merchandise closely.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/grabbing-a-quick-and-unpleasant-bite/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: Relying on free street samples for lunch can be unsatisfying, especially if one doesn’t examine the merchandise closely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dear Diary: I am walking down Lexington Avenue on the Upper East Side. I have missed lunch and am late for a meeting when I pass a store handing out free samples. I grab three pieces, say a quick thank you, thrust the nourishment into my mouth and keeping moving.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grabbing a Quick, and Unpleasant, Bite', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Awaking to a Masked Visitor, and Other Reader Tales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cleansers, Detergents and Soaps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T12:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winton J.  Tolles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winton', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Tolles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2db5696-8fc9-5780-8a86-b635d886fc66', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2db5696-8fc9-5780-8a86-b635d886fc66'}, {'abstract': 'Charlie Sheen discusses gambling, Alcoholics Anonymous, his relationship with “Two and a Half Men” and the creation of his new FX series, “Anger Management.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/charlie-sheen-talks-about-anger-management-and-anger-management/', 'snippet': 'Charlie Sheen discusses gambling, Alcoholics Anonymous, his relationship with “Two and a Half Men” and the creation of his new FX series, “Anger Management.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Hey, remember that Charlie Sheen fellow? Used to be the star of a sitcom, “Two and a Half Men,” until he got into a war of words with its co-creator Chuck Lorre and was fired from the show? Taught us some lessons about tiger blood, warlocks and winning? Went on a cross-country live tour that didn’t get such hot reviews? What ever happened to that guy?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charlie Sheen Talks About ‘Anger Management’ and Anger Management', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lorre, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheen, Charlie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lions Gate Entertainment Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T13:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b23d0d1a-7874-5022-bc1c-fe04d6f65318', 'word_count': 1845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b23d0d1a-7874-5022-bc1c-fe04d6f65318'}, {'abstract': 'Workers at Google said they were not aware of the data collection in the Street View project either because it was not part of their job or they did not review the project documentation.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/daily-report-google-employees-know-nothing/', 'snippet': 'Workers at Google said they were not aware of the data collection in the Street View project either because it was not part of their job or they did not review the project documentation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Google has long prided itself on not being a conventional company, Edward Wyatt, a New York Times reporter notes. But he writes there is one characteristic it apparently shares with the most sclerotic bureaucracy: the willingness of its employees to say, “Not my job.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': N