, 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Advance Publications Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Birmingham News', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting  Group (BSkyB)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huffington Post', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times-Picayune (New Orleans)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T13:22:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec1d259f-3184-5365-ba7a-0eb4ca7dff24', 'word_count': 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec1d259f-3184-5365-ba7a-0eb4ca7dff24'}, {'abstract': 'Eating frugally in Copenhagen, a flirting app bans minors after rape cases, Verizon wireless plan to cover several devices and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/wednesday-reading-eating-frugally-in-copenhagen/', 'snippet': 'Eating frugally in Copenhagen, a flirting app bans minors after rape cases, Verizon wireless plan to cover several devices and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wednesday Reading: Eating Frugally in Copenhagen', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T13:29:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27f6831d-f9e7-53e4-ac88-96ac40c1918b', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27f6831d-f9e7-53e4-ac88-96ac40c1918b'}, {'abstract': 'Patrick Kwan recalls how, years ago, he rescued Lily the chicken from the dancing chicken booth at the Chinatown Fair arcade', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/a-chickens-journey-from-chinatown-to-a-private-sanctuary/', 'snippet': 'Patrick Kwan recalls how, years ago, he rescued Lily the chicken from the dancing chicken booth at the Chinatown Fair arcade', 'lead_paragraph': 'For those who have entered the newly reopened Chinatown Fair arcade in years past, most have distinct memories about the place: the street-fighting games, the old-school games, but more often than not, the chicken that played tick-tack-toe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chicken’s Journey From Chinatown to a Private Sanctuary', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T13:37:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kia Gregory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gregory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/801b2737-183e-5f8e-9bcc-da1355e318be', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/801b2737-183e-5f8e-9bcc-da1355e318be'}, {'abstract': 'The Broadway revival of “Godspell,” Stephen Schwartz and John-Michael Tebelak’s musical loosely based on parables from the New Testament, will play its final performance on June 24.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/the-bad-news-broadway-revival-of-godspell-to-close/', 'snippet': 'The Broadway revival of “Godspell,” Stephen Schwartz and John-Michael Tebelak’s musical loosely based on parables from the New Testament, will play its final performance on June 24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annals of Broadway may have plenty of room for musicals with religious themes and stories inspired by the Gospels, but the summer season does not. The producers of the Broadway revival of “Godspell,” the pop musical loosely based on parables from the New Testament, said late Tuesday evening that the production will play its final performance at the Circle in the Square Theater on June 24.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bad News: Broadway Revival of ‘Godspell’ to Close', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bad News: ‘Godspell’ to Close', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bleu, Corbin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parrish, Hunter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Stephen', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tebelak, John-Michael', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Circle in the Square Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6eca2d5-d191-5718-a2b7-9558868e1c07', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6eca2d5-d191-5718-a2b7-9558868e1c07'}, {'abstract': 'Maps developed by Climate Central show that the warming trend in the United States intensified after 1970.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/a-state-by-state-climate-map/', 'snippet': 'Maps developed by Climate Central show that the warming trend in the United States intensified after 1970.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If those New England seasons feel far warmer these days than they were 20 years ago, it’s because they are. So are Florida’s, Arizona’s, and Washington State’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A State-by-State Climate Map', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:05:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kelly Slivka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kelly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Slivka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f46a2254-a45a-5a34-930f-a5231fefe6a3', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f46a2254-a45a-5a34-930f-a5231fefe6a3'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/what-were-reading-456/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NPR: At last, someone has the courage to come out against bananas in fruit salad. And more solid advice on composition and creativity. — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:06:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70468a34-24a2-5a37-b9e5-1be27ae3815e', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70468a34-24a2-5a37-b9e5-1be27ae3815e'}, {'abstract': 'Saunders’s head-to-toe bamboo print: very chic and not in the least over the top.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/just-one-look-jonathan-saunders/', 'snippet': 'Saunders’s head-to-toe bamboo print: very chic and not in the least over the top.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Separates allow me to do what I love to do with color,” Jonathan Saunders\xa0said as the sun beamed down through the skylight at Industria studios, highlighting the vibrant greens, blues and reds of his resort collection. “But I’m loving a total, head-to-toe print look.” Saunders pulled out a pair of fluid palazzo pants in a bamboo print, one of several late-’70s-inspired motifs he designed for resort, including a graphic floral and a multicolored dot pattern that brought the artist Victor Vasarely to mind. The bamboo palazzo pants can be worn with a simple black top, of course, but paired with one in the matching bamboo print, the look could have easily passed for an evening dress — very chic and not in the least over the top.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Jonathan Saunders', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vasarely, Victor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a254f7c-af3a-58a3-8129-5dfd1164a184', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a254f7c-af3a-58a3-8129-5dfd1164a184'}, {'abstract': 'The Flyover feature of Apple’s mapping app for its phones and tablets inspires a reader to extol its virtues.', 'web_url': 'https://pogue.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/apples-mapping-feature-wins-raves/', 'snippet': 'The Flyover feature of Apple’s mapping app for its phones and tablets inspires a reader to extol its virtues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can’t possibly write today’s blog post any better than the person who submitted it — reader Adam Ornstein. Adam, take it away!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Mapping Feature Wins Raves', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:15:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b90d657b-8d74-54d7-a173-a6b58c7a3eed', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b90d657b-8d74-54d7-a173-a6b58c7a3eed'}, {'abstract': 'Rafael Nadal won the men’s title at the French Open, but a run by opponent Novak Djokovic was notable in its own right.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/breaking-it-down-nadal-vs-djokovic/', 'snippet': 'Rafael Nadal won the men’s title at the French Open, but a run by opponent Novak Djokovic was notable in its own right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For world No. 1, Novak Djokovic, the best defense has proven to be more offense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking It Down: Nadal vs. Djokovic', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsonga, Jo-Wilfried', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': "By Craig O' Shannessy", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': "O'", 'lastname': 'Shannessy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a10bcc4-56be-5756-ad57-291fe246e7de', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a10bcc4-56be-5756-ad57-291fe246e7de'}, {'abstract': 'Richard D. Parsons, former chairman of Citigroup and former chief executive of Time Warner, is joining the board of the investment bank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/parsons-joins-lazard-board/', 'snippet': 'Richard D. Parsons, former chairman of Citigroup and former chief executive of Time Warner, is joining the board of the investment bank.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One might have thought that after 16 years on the board of Citigroup — and one terrifying financial crisis — Richard D. Parsons would have had his fill of financial firms. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parsons Joins Lazard Board', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parsons, Richard D', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lazard LLC', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T14:21:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f80bb613-8a06-545b-a72a-c4fa108f7b80', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f80bb613-8a06-545b-a72a-c4fa108f7b80'}, {'abstract': 'Guillaume Henry presented his collection on June 12.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/13/fashion/resort2013carven.html', 'snippet': 'Guillaume Henry presented his collection on June 12.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guillaume Henry presented his collection on June 12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/fashion/resort2013carven-slide-C5OB/resort2013carven-slide-C5OB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1434, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ra