'2012-06-13T14:52:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5630dd88-94d2-5f3f-b887-1109333747dc', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5630dd88-94d2-5f3f-b887-1109333747dc'}, {'abstract': 'Government employees in Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, demand better terms of employment.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/image-of-the-day-june-13/', 'snippet': 'Government employees in Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir, demand better terms of employment.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: June 13', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b561b66-d09e-5f31-b7df-9d356a37c5d9', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b561b66-d09e-5f31-b7df-9d356a37c5d9'}, {'abstract': 'Diesel fumes are “on the same order of magnitude as passive smoking,” an official with the World Health Organization’s cancer agency said.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/on-our-radar-diesel-fumes-cause-cancer-w-h-o-says/', 'snippet': 'Diesel fumes are “on the same order of magnitude as passive smoking,” an official with the World Health Organization’s cancer agency said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Health Organization declares that diesel fumes cause cancer, suggesting that the exhaust is a public health threat rivaling secondhand smoke. The United States rates it only as a “likely” carcinogen. [Associated Press]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Diesel Fumes Cause Cancer, W.H.O. Says', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:08:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f17537d2-b71a-566c-8d61-58d712afa6c4', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f17537d2-b71a-566c-8d61-58d712afa6c4'}, {'abstract': 'The former head of the Chinese national soccer association and 10 former national team players and executives were sentenced Wednesday for accepting bribes and fixing matches.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/sports/soccer/lengthy-prison-terms-in-chinese-soccer-corruption-case.html', 'snippet': 'The former head of the Chinese national soccer association and 10 former national team players and executives were sentenced Wednesday for accepting bribes and fixing matches.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — The former head of the Chinese soccer association and 10 other former national team players and executives were sentenced by Chinese courts Wednesday to lengthy prison terms for accepting bribes and fixing matches, according to Xinhua, the state-run news agency.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Soccer Officials Sentenced in China', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Officials Sent to Prison', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xie Yalong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:09:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d7b3923-51a9-584b-bdba-642dc54345e1', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d7b3923-51a9-584b-bdba-642dc54345e1'}, {'abstract': 'Whether or not Doug O’ Neill and Paul Reddam scratched I’ll Have Another out of concern for his well-being or concern for his stud value doesn’t matter because the horse has benefited from the decision.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/the-business-of-good-horsemanship/', 'snippet': 'Whether or not Doug O’ Neill and Paul Reddam scratched I’ll Have Another out of concern for his well-being or concern for his stud value doesn’t matter because the horse has benefited from the decision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fans of thoroughbred racing, once again, will have to go another year without a Triple Crown winner and many of them have expressed their frustration as paranoia, accusing Doug O’Neill, the trainer of I’ll Have Another, of a host of different motives: he was afraid of a drug test, he was afraid of losing, he was afraid that, like Big Brown, an abysmal showing in the Belmont would have cast doubt on his horse’s triumphs in the Preakness and the Kentucky Derby. The subsequent announcement that he was retiring the Flower Alley colt has led some to observe that I’ll Have Another’s value as a breeding animal has trumped his value as an athlete. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Business of Good Horsemanship', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "I'll Have Another (Race Horse)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reddam, J Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:11:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Nusser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nusser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3201cd5-5426-57dd-88e6-7b04f290b425', 'word_count': 661, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3201cd5-5426-57dd-88e6-7b04f290b425'}, {'abstract': 'The miraculous non-disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/guess-whos-emerging-from-the-crisis/', 'snippet': 'The miraculous non-disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FT Alphaville:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Guess Who’s Emerging From the Crisis?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:12:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e85a0835-4a5d-53f1-94da-89f96e327903', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e85a0835-4a5d-53f1-94da-89f96e327903'}, {'abstract': 'The Menier Chocolate Factory revives Harvey Fierstein’s Tony-winning play, directed by Douglas Hodge.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/london-theater-journal-a-flickering-torch-song/', 'snippet': 'The Menier Chocolate Factory revives Harvey Fierstein’s Tony-winning play, directed by Douglas Hodge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Long before America cuddled up with those wholesome gay pixies on “Will and Grace” and “Modern Family,” there was “Torch Song Trilogy,” a play that scratched the surface of a fierce drag queen to discover a lovable Jewish mother with good family values beneath. Arnold was this comforting creature’s reassuringly plain name. The man who created him on the page and the stage, Harvey Fierstein, won Tony Awards for both Best Play and Best Actor in 1983, giving daring and triumphant new breadth to the notion of theater queen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: A Flickering ‘Torch Song’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Torch Song Trilogy (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bedella, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fierstein, Harvey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hodge, Douglas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Menier Chocolate Factory', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1da0594-bc5f-59a5-850f-9c441ce6c88a', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1da0594-bc5f-59a5-850f-9c441ce6c88a'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Haste faces charges of charges of first- and second-degree manslaughter in the shooting death of Ramarley Graham, an unarmed 18-year-old.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/nyregion/officer-pleads-not-guilty-in-ramarley-graham-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Haste faces charges of charges of first- and second-degree manslaughter in the shooting death of Ramarley Graham, an unarmed 18-year-old.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An officer charged with manslaughter in the shooting death of an unarmed 18-year-old man who was followed by the police to his home in the Bronx and then killed by a single police bullet in his bathroom had “no choice” but to shoot him, the officer’s lawyer said at his arraignment on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/nyregion/GRAHAM1/GRAHAM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/nyregion/GRAHAM1/GRAHAM1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/nyregion/GRAHAM1/GRAHAM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/nyregion/GRAHAM1/GRAHAM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/nyregion/GRAHAM1/GRAHAM1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Officer Had ‘No Choice’ in Bronx Man’s Shooting, His Lawyer Says in Court', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officer Had ‘No Choice’ in Bronx Man’s Shooting, His Lawyer Says in Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haste, Richard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Ramarley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:27:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By ZENA BARAKAT and RANDY LEONARD', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'BARAKAT', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LEONARD', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31e34951-48a7-502f-8586-591aec91c9f8', 'word_count': 792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31e34951-48a7-502f-8586-591aec91c9f8'}, {'abstract': 'The collection, titled Propaganda, is inspired by poster art from World War I and World War II.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/just-one-look-lwren-scott/', 'snippet': 'The collection, titled Propaganda, is inspired by poster art from World War I and World War II.', 'lead_paragraph': 'L’Wren Scott’s first resort collection began innocently enough. “I was sitting in my office one day with all of my crayons and started coloring,” she said. Scott created nine prints, which she then produced in nine silhouettes. The collection, titled Propaganda, is inspired by poster art from World War I and World War II. The bright prints include “The Bomb” (exploding grenades), “Bromance” (American and British flags) and “Why Knot” (Chinese peace knots). Many of the looks are topped off with a cap, some done in a print, appropriately named “Hats Off,” riffed from a rendering of Queen Elizabeth by Cecil Beaton. But our favorite print spells out “L’Wren Scott don’t fake it” —\xa0in Morse code.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | L’Wren Scott', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:30:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3a9ad61-9b14-5eaa-b1bf-155d2970eb39', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3a9ad61-9b14-5eaa-b1bf-155d2970eb39'}, {'abstract': 'Opposition to Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s plan to restrict sales of big sugary beverages was strongest among older voters, white voters and voters on Staten Island.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/slim-majority-of-new-yorkers-oppose-soda-ban/', 'snippet': 'Opposition to Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s plan to restrict sales of big sugary beverages was strongest among older voters, white voters and voters on Staten Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A narrow majority of New York City voters oppose Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg’s plan to restrict sales of big sugary beverages in city restaurants, movie theaters and street carts, according to a poll released on Wednesday. Opponents of the plan edged out supporters, 51 percent to 46 percent; opposition was strongest among older voters, white voters and voters on Staten Island.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Slight Majority of New Yorkers Oppose Soda Ban', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Narrow Majority of City Voters Oppose Mayor’s Soda Plan, Poll Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T15:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4672415d-21c0-5b43-bfd3-8f50fa71ef27', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4672415d-21c0-5b43-bfd3-8f50fa71ef27'}, {'abstract': 'The program’s failure to pick up a devoted audience reflects CNN’s problems in general as it struggles to attract viewers during quiet news periods.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/cnn-is-ending-john-kings-political-show/', 'snippet': 'The program’s failure to pick up a devoted audience