imes.com/2012/06/14/world/middleeast/russia-and-iran-accuse-the-us-of-arming-syrian-rebels.html', 'snippet': 'Russia and Iran castigated the United States on Wednesday for its support of opposition forces battling President Bashar al-Assad and his military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Russia and Iran, Syria’s staunchest allies, castigated the United States on Wednesday for its support of opposition forces battling President Bashar al-Assad and his military, and the Iranians accused the Americans and their allies of sending weapons and troops into Syria.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia and Iran Criticize the United States on Syria', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia and Iran Criticize the United States on Syria', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:16:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0db3d821-9404-5bbe-a869-e6ed1bb77a63', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0db3d821-9404-5bbe-a869-e6ed1bb77a63'}, {'abstract': 'The resort collections are an opportunity for designers to test new or nutty ideas before they incorporate them into their bigger spring runway shows, beginning in September.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/fashion/resort-collections-offer-peek-at-september-shows.html', 'snippet': 'The resort collections are an opportunity for designers to test new or nutty ideas before they incorporate them into their bigger spring runway shows, beginning in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THIS week in fashion, we celebrate a fairly new tradition in which dozens of designers unveil their intra-season resort collections during informal presentations by saying things like, “Color, for me, is like food,” or “I like the idea of beach to evening,” or “In the middle of this collection, I watched the movie ‘Marley,’ so there’s a bit of Rasta in there.”', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1375, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14zROW/14zROW-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Just Vacation Flings', 'kicker': 'Front Row', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Just Vacation Flings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chloe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCartney, Stella', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ricci, Nina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Altuzarra, Joseph', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Givenchy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Celine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tisci, Riccardo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pucci, Emilio', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:22:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9b20775-14e7-5952-9d53-4a465602c6eb', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9b20775-14e7-5952-9d53-4a465602c6eb'}, {'abstract': 'John Lanchester’s new novel is a sprawling chronicle of several characters living and working on one street.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/a-microcosm-of-london-john-lanchester-talks-about-capital/', 'snippet': 'John Lanchester’s new novel is a sprawling chronicle of several characters living and working on one street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his new novel, “Capital,” John Lanchester tracks the lives of several characters living and working on one London street: a banker and his wife; a Polish house builder; a Muslim family running a shop; a teenage West African soccer star; and a political refugee who works illegally as a traffic warden, to name a few. The street’s residents have been receiving notes in the mail with pictures of their own houses and the cryptic message: “We Want What You Have.” In a recent interview via e-mail, Mr. Lanchester discussed fiction and nonfiction, Dickens and Tolstoy, immigration, the changing behavior of the English, and more. Below are excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Microcosm of London: John Lanchester Talks About ‘Capital’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lanchester, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:28:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/575dd921-14d5-5d61-a289-02310bdb0be8', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/575dd921-14d5-5d61-a289-02310bdb0be8'}, {'abstract': 'An investigation into the death of an Estonian explosive ordnance disposal technician found that he was killed at a site in Libya where groups were fighting over access to Qaddafi-era munitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/world/middleeast/death-illustrates-issues-with-libyas-stockpiles-of-arms.html', 'snippet': 'An investigation into the death of an Estonian explosive ordnance disposal technician found that he was killed at a site in Libya where groups were fighting over access to Qaddafi-era munitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The death of an Estonian explosive ordnance disposal technician in Libya this spring illustrates the continuing problem of loose weapons stockpiles almost a year after Col. Muammar el-Qaddafi was driven from power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/world/middleeast/14libya/14libya-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/world/middleeast/14libya/14libya-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Illustrates Issues With Loose Weapons Stockpiles in Libya', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death Illustrates Problems of Weapons Stockpiles in Libya', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines, Explosive', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keerdo, Kaido', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qaddafi, Muammar el-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Chivers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chivers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08f1360f-4906-5d74-bbef-e80b0c8c843a', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08f1360f-4906-5d74-bbef-e80b0c8c843a'}, {'abstract': 'Small businesses are easy prey for hackers bent on raiding bank accounts because many lack firewalls and monitoring systems, but these businesses can protect themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/protecting-business-accounts-from-hackers.html', 'snippet': 'Small businesses are easy prey for hackers bent on raiding bank accounts because many lack firewalls and monitoring systems, but these businesses can protect themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May 2010, Golden State Bridge, an engineering and construction company based in Martinez, Calif., was robbed of more than $125,000 when cybercriminals hacked into its bank account. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/smallbusiness/14sbiz/14sbiz-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Owners May Not Be Covered When Hackers Wipe Out A Business Bank Account', 'kicker': 'Small-Business Guide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Owners May Not Be Covered When Hackers Wipe Out A Business Bank Account', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bank Robberies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Ryckman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryckman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79d32d90-a352-5150-9acb-3da62c1716f9', 'word_count': 1235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79d32d90-a352-5150-9acb-3da62c1716f9'}, {'abstract': 'The Tampa Bay Rays are legally obligated to play in St. Petersburg, Fla., for another 15 years, and it will not let the team leave without a fight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/sports/baseball/st-petersburg-clings-to-tampa-bay-rays-as-others-clamor-for-a-move.html', 'snippet': 'The Tampa Bay Rays are legally obligated to play in St. Petersburg, Fla., for another 15 years, and it will not let the team leave without a fight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. — Mayor Bill Foster scoffs at critics who accuse him of holding the Tampa Bay Rays prisoner in their stadium. Yes, attendance has generally been weak at Tropicana Field, an unattractive venue that lacks many of the amenities found at newer stadiums and, yes, people who live on the other side of the bay, in Tampa, are clamoring for the team to move there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14rays/14rays-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14rays/14rays-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14rays/14rays-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14rays/14rays-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14rays/14rays-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'City Clings to Rays as Others Clamor for a Move', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Clings to Rays as Others Clamor for a Move', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tampa Bay Rays', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tropicana Field (St Petersburg, Fla)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:29:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c42dea4-6916-50ec-9a69-b8b1146ec813', 'word_count': 1362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c42dea4-6916-50ec-9a69-b8b1146ec813'}, {'abstract': 'A brash young general embarrasses the Union Army with one of the Civil War’s boldest cavalry maneuvers.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/jeb-stuarts-wild-ride/', 'snippet': 'A brash young general embarrasses the Union Army with one of the Civil War’s boldest cavalry maneuvers.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Gentlemen, in ten minutes everyone must be in the saddle.” It was 2 a.m. on June 12, 1862, and a 29-year-old Confederate brigadier general named James Ewell Brown Stuart — Jeb to his intimates and posterity — was about to write history with his famous “Ride Around McClellan.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jeb Stuart’s Wild Ride', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Robert E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Army of the Potomac', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Cleary', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cleary', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d4f95e5-e86b-5110-ba7f-d07b1c78b09b', 'word_count': 1306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d4f95e5-e86b-5110-ba7f-d07b1c78b09b'}, {'abstract': 'Fanciful colors and patterns were applied to classic Herrera pieces for this collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/just-one-look-carolina-herrera-2/', 'snippet': 'Fanciful colors and patterns were applied to classic Herrera pieces for this collection.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The ‘Lovers’ and the ‘Rabbits’ go very well,” Herrera said, referring to resort’s two standout prints. The “Lovers” is a watercolor with renderings of men and women in fanciful colors, applied to classic Herrera pieces: peplum blouse and cotton skirt and dress. “It’s very easy,” Herrera noted, “and feminine.” As for “Rabbit,” it’s here on a silk collared blouse and pleated skirt. Hippity hoppity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Carolina Herrera', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T16:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a5c79c3-0a21-52b3-a529-15fab05bc9db', 'word_count': 67, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a5c79c3-0a21-52b3-a529-15fab05bc9db'}, {'abstract': '“Rev.,” about an Anglican church in London, and “The Yard,” about Toronto schoolchildren, provide satire whose bite is cushioned by gentleness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/arts/television/rev-and-the-yard-two-short-series-on-hulu.html', 'snippet': '“Rev.,” about an Anglican church in London, and “The Yard,” about Toronto schoolchildren, provide satire whose bite is cushioned by gentleness.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Rev.” is a British series about a country priest who moves to London, and “The Yard” is a Canadian mini-series about the tribal relationships among the children in a Toronto elementary school. What unites them, apart from their both making their American debuts online at Hulu, is the comedy of transgression: lasciviousness and foul language springing from what would seem to be the unlikeliest mouths.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/hulu1/hulu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/hulu1/hulu1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/hulu1/hulu1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/hulu1/hulu1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/13/arts/hulu1/hulu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_