a', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9ac3761-4ae1-5226-885f-51e3f05ad0ee', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9ac3761-4ae1-5226-885f-51e3f05ad0ee'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: President Obama is scheduled to visit the One World Trade Center construction site on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/barclay-street-1142-a-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: President Obama is scheduled to visit the One World Trade Center construction site on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Barclay Street, 11:42 a.m.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '1 World Trade Center (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afe6ef27-6c58-5004-b05a-531def845b17', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afe6ef27-6c58-5004-b05a-531def845b17'}, {'abstract': '“Bullet for Adolf,” by Woody Harrelson and Frankie Hyman, is scheduled to start performances at New World Stages next month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/woody-harrelson-as-director-and-co-writer-coming-to-off-broadway/', 'snippet': '“Bullet for Adolf,” by Woody Harrelson and Frankie Hyman, is scheduled to start performances at New World Stages next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the summer of 1983, when an acting career was still just a dream, Woody Harrelson worked construction in Houston and met a play’s worth of colorful characters, including an aspiring writer from Harlem named Frankie Hyman who became his best buddy on the scaffolding. That fall Mr. Harrelson headed for New York to try to break into theater, only to hit dead ends. As with many struggling actors, his thoughts turned to writing his own scripts, and he found himself thinking back to that summer in Houston – though it would take more than 25 years, and a collaboration with Mr. Hyman, to finish the play he had in mind.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Woody Harrelson, as Director and Co-Writer, Coming to Off Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Harrelson to Direct Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotton, Shamika', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harrelson, Woody', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New World Stages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Houston (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:29:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fafb8127-e10f-5aaa-a1b2-2e5cfd873635', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fafb8127-e10f-5aaa-a1b2-2e5cfd873635'}, {'abstract': 'New York appears to be closing in on a plan to extract gas while protecting its environment.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/cuomos-wise-move-on-new-yorks-gas-resource/', 'snippet': 'New York appears to be closing in on a plan to extract gas while protecting its environment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York Governor Andrew M. Cuomo (@nygovcuomo) appears to be closing in on a plan for extracting natural gas while limiting environmental risks in the state, as reported today by Danny Hakim for The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuomo’s Wise Move on New York’s Gas Resource', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:29:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ae4f0cb-489f-5bf8-a27c-2db43493abd0', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ae4f0cb-489f-5bf8-a27c-2db43493abd0'}, {'abstract': 'A government watchdog issued a report Wednesday harshly criticizing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s handling of a raid on a Gaza-bound Turkish ship in 2010, which left nine activists dead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/world/middleeast/israeli-watchdog-criticizes-government-over-gaza-flotilla-raid.html', 'snippet': 'A government watchdog issued a report Wednesday harshly criticizing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s handling of a raid on a Gaza-bound Turkish ship in 2010, which left nine activists dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — Israel’s state comptroller, the government’s watchdog, issued a report on Wednesday harshly criticizing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu over his handling of a commando raid on a Gaza-bound Turkish ship in 2010. The raid, meant to halt a flotilla challenging Israel’s naval blockade of the territory, turned deadly, with severe diplomatic consequences for Israel.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israeli Watchdog Criticizes Government Over Gaza Flotilla Raid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel’s Official Watchdog Criticizes Gaza Flotilla Raid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Gaza Movement', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gaza Strip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:33:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/386b0d6f-0fb5-5d95-b67a-9bc33d76dcab', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/386b0d6f-0fb5-5d95-b67a-9bc33d76dcab'}, {'abstract': 'This season, table dressing calls for a perfectly unmatchy batch of colorful and boldly printed linen.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/table-toppings/', 'snippet': 'This season, table dressing calls for a perfectly unmatchy batch of colorful and boldly printed linen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Table Toppings', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:36:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3219b755-5cc4-5211-871c-1ad77c4e4fd5', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3219b755-5cc4-5211-871c-1ad77c4e4fd5'}, {'abstract': 'Ackeem Green, a member of the Harlem Youth Marines, a group that uses military tradition and rules to help youngsters avoid trouble, was shot and killed on June 3.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/in-harlem-youth-marines-mourn-the-death-of-a-member/', 'snippet': 'Ackeem Green, a member of the Harlem Youth Marines, a group that uses military tradition and rules to help youngsters avoid trouble, was shot and killed on June 3.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The young people, all wearing green camouflage uniforms and standing attentively in two perfect lines, were reciting the Pledge of Allegiance with gusto and aplomb. But they were not in complete unison, and that made the tall man leaning against a wall unhappy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young Cadets Mourn a Comrade, Felled by Gunfire in Harlem', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young Cadets Mourn a Comrade, Felled by Gunfire in Harlem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:51:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3aa54df-3c94-5bd5-9b42-43d3eaa4ed27', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3aa54df-3c94-5bd5-9b42-43d3eaa4ed27'}, {'abstract': 'In testimony before the Senate Banking Committee, Jamie Dimon assured lawmakers that the bank’s board was investigating the trading losses. Once the investigation is complete, he said, the bank will decide whose paychecks to pursue.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/jpmorgans-chief-says-clawback-attempts-are-likely/', 'snippet': 'In testimony before the Senate Banking Committee, Jamie Dimon assured lawmakers that the bank’s board was investigating the trading losses. Once the investigation is complete, he said, the bank will decide whose paychecks to pursue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — JPMorgan Chase is “likely” to try to recover compensation from executives responsible for a recent multibillion-dollar trading blowup, according to Jamie Dimon, the bank’s chief executive.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'JPMorgan’s Chief Says Clawback Efforts Are ‘Likely’', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Proud’ JPMorgan Chief Apologizes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99dfbe63-c643-5bb8-aeab-99572f52abdc', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99dfbe63-c643-5bb8-aeab-99572f52abdc'}, {'abstract': 'A researcher from Amnesty International describes a pattern of violence in which Syria’s government uses overwhelming force to subdue restive areas of the country.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/human-rights-group-documents-violence-from-inside-syria/', 'snippet': 'A researcher from Amnesty International describes a pattern of violence in which Syria’s government uses overwhelming force to subdue restive areas of the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Syria’s state news agency said that after days of heavy shelling and intense fighting in the northwestern Latakia Province, government forces had retaken the rebellious village of Al Heffa, driving antigovernment fighters out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Human Rights Group Documents Violence From Inside Syria', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:58:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66395680-f2ac-5f9e-ad20-ba7cf5575dcf', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66395680-f2ac-5f9e-ad20-ba7cf5575dcf'}, {'abstract': 'ABC has completed its sale of commercial time before the start of the 2012-13 season as the so-called upfront market proceeds to a close.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/abc-holds-steady-in-upfront-ad-sales/', 'snippet': 'ABC has completed its sale of commercial time before the start of the 2012-13 season as the so-called upfront market proceeds to a close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A third English-language broadcast television network, ABC, has completed its sale of commercial time before the start of the 2012-13 season as the so-called upfront market proceeds to a placid close.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Holds Steady in ‘Upfront’ Ad Sales', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T17:58:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Elliott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Elliott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb5c2e3-b77b-5fe2-990e-a09ed9843d8a', 'word_count': 436, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb5c2e3-b77b-5fe2-990e-a09ed9843d8a'}, {'abstract': 'Lawrence Ulrich takes a brief spin in the purely electric hatchback, which is undergoing an internal field test in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/driving-the-audi-a3-e-tron/', 'snippet': 'Lawrence Ulrich takes a brief spin in the purely electric hatchback, which is undergoing an internal field test in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of all the Leafs, Volts, Teslas and Karmas, Audi’s E-tron moniker is most redolent of sci-fi films and the utopian promise of a brave, new, petrol-free world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Driving the Audi A3 E-tron', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:04:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Ulrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ulrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c83be5d7-d55b-5877-a15f-a100c8054ff5', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c83be5d7-d55b-5877-a15f-a100c8054ff5'}, {'abstract': 'Lena Dunham, photographed here as a high-school student, told the magazine in November 2001 about her favorite New York location: Under the Bridge.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/lena-dunhams-secret-girls-spot/', 'snippet': 'Lena Dunham, photographed here as a high-school student, told the magazine in November 2001 about her favorite New York location: Under the Bridge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last weekend’s magazine, Andrew Goldman asked Lena Dunham, who\xa0 lived with her parents while creating “Girls” for HBO, whether, now that she’s moving out, she’s moving to “cool, young Williamsburg or established, family-oriented Brooklyn Heights.” The latter, she said: “We lived there all through my high-school career, so I have an intense attachment to it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lena Dunham’s Secret Girls’ Spot', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:08:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e05e1b2f-f118-5627-bf0b-e9811e8d6b8e', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e05e1b2f-f118-5627-bf0b-e9811e8d6b8e'}, {'abstract': 'Tyra Banks, who is focusing her business plans on ventures aimed at empowering young women, was greeted by a group of girls near the site of a new building that will eventually house the Lower Eastside Girls Club.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/tyra-banks-sets-an-example/', 'snippet': 'Tyra Banks, who is focusing her business plans on ventures aimed at empowering young women, was greeted by a group of girls near the site of a new building that will eventually house the Lower Eastside Girls Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Standing in the rain near the site of a new building on Avenue D that will eventually house the Lower Eastside Girls Club, a group of young girls on Tuesday afternoon greeted Tyra Banks by practicing one of her signature moves, the “smize.” As anyone who has watched “America’s Next Top Model” knows, that is smiling with your eyes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tyra Banks Sets an Example', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banks, Tyra', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lower Eastside Girls Club', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:11:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d8ddddf-c23d-52d0-99e6-42cc05e94e06', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d8ddddf-c23d-52d0-99e6-42cc05e94e06'}, {'abstract': 'Phony Twitter users like @NotBillWalton and @NotWaltFrazier are in playoff form as the N.B.A. season reaches its climax.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/sports/basketball/impostors-on-twitter-post-up-during-nba-finals.html', 'snippet': 'Phony Twitter users like @NotBillWalton and @NotWaltFrazier are in playoff form as the N.B.A. season reaches its climax.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oklahoma City had scarcely gained control of the opening tip in Game 1 of the N.B.A. finals Tuesday night when @NotWaltFrazier, who recently surpassed 10,000 followers on Twitter, complimented Thunder Coach Scott Brooks on his hair: “Scotty Brooks with the fresh cut for the Finals. Follicle cleanin’ and national TV preenin’! #JustForMen”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14twitter/14twitter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 274, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14twitter/14twitter-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 274, 'width': 568, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14twitter/14twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14twitter/14twitter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14twitter/14twitter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Impostors Post Up in N.B.A. Finals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Twitter, Impostors Post Up in the Finals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frazier, Walt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walton, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Gervino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gervino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/75da6f4d-3079-5cfe-a4cf-bd72a4d64226', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75da6f4d-3079-5cfe-a4cf-bd72a4d64226'}, {'abstract': 'An impasse over Syria and fractious domestic politics in both countries have underscored the limits of President Obama’s ability to “reset” ties between the nations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/world/europe/putins-return-brings-rapid-chill-to-us-russia-ties.html', 'snippet': 'An impasse over Syria and fractious domestic politics in both countries have underscored the limits of President Obama’s ability to “reset” ties between the nations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Sitting beside President Obama this spring, the president of Russia gushed that “these were perhaps the best three years of relations between Russia and the United States over the last decade.” Two and a half months later, those halcyon days of friendship look like a distant memory.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/world/diplo/diplo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/world/diplo/diplo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Crisis and Putin’s Return Chill U.S. Ties With Russia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Putin Returns and Syria Boils, U.S.-Russia Ties Sour', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:13:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bcf696b-ef11-5387-8b53-ca08e1b40c21', 'word_count': 1174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bcf696b-ef11-5387-8b53-ca08e1b40c21'}, {'abstract': 'A single-shoulder tunic with a snakeskin belt and over-the-knee boots seems destined for a stroll along the Amalfi Coast.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/just-one-look-salvatore-ferragamo-2/', 'snippet': 'A single-shoulder tunic with a snakeskin belt and over-the-knee boots seems destined for a stroll along the Amalfi Coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Salvatore Ferragamo’s creative director, Massimiliano Giornetti, presented resort at the Louvre Museum in Paris yesterday while simultaneously live streaming the show internationally. (T editors huddled together around a computer in the fashion department to watch.) The collection evoked la dolce vita in a big way with exotic skins (crocodile minidresses; python to-the-knee boots), over-the-top accessories (giant hobo bags and look-changing belts) and swinging fringe trim on skirts, tops and coats. Here, a barely there single-shoulder tunic nipped at the waist with a snakeskin belt and over-the-knee boots seems destined for a stroll along the Amalfi Coast. All that’s missing are the Jackie O. shades, maybe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Salvatore Ferragamo', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:15:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/357f0ba9-465a-55d6-b689-0ad00b287fde', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/357f0ba9-465a-55d6-b689-0ad00b287fde'}, {'abstract': 'My wife was never more needed by our son than on that first day, but as a new dad, I’m needed more all the time.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/becoming-a-new-father-slowly/', 'snippet': 'My wife was never more needed by our son than on that first day, but as a new dad, I’m needed more all the time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my wife was pregnant, my son would kick and cough, change her body, tastes, routines. She had a visceral, constant reminder of his presence. For me, it was completely different. My son was a notion. I looked the same, felt the same and could easily forget he was on his way. If I didn’t actively remember to think about him, I didn’t. Instead I focused on tangible things: cribs, strollers, memorizing songs to sing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Becoming a New Father, Slowly', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Father's Day", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T18:17:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Novotny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Novotny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c017a56b-9faa-5c53-ad92-1eb99602934a', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c017a56b-9faa-5c53-ad92-1eb99602934a'}, {'abstract': 'After coming to seem outdated to some in the cosmetics industry, the rose is enjoying a renaissance of sorts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/fashion/skin-deep-the-rose-is-making-a-comeback.html', 'snippet': 'After coming to seem outdated to some in the cosmetics industry, the rose is enjoying a renaissance of sorts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR at least a century, the rose has been entwined in our notions of beauty and desire. A key accessory for prom queens and figure skaters (not to mention Queen Elizabeth II’s diamond jubilee), it has figured in cold cream, Chanel No. 5 and the classic Smith’s Rosebud Salve.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14SKIN_SPAN/14SKIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/14/fashion/14SKIN_SPAN/14SKIN_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 210}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'typ