eographer Wayne McGregor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/arts/dance/australian-ballet-at-the-koch-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The Australian Ballet opened its week at Lincoln Center with a retrospective and an impeccably modern centerpiece by the choreographer Wayne McGregor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Celebrating its 50th year, the Australian Ballet opened its week on Tuesday night at the David H. Koch Theater with the first of two performances of a triple bill with the ambiguous title “Infinity.” Its first third, “Luminous,” was a retrospective of repertory highlights and dancer showcases, interspersed with video; its centerpiece, “Dyad 1929,” choreographed by Wayne McGregor, was impeccably modern; and the finale, “Warumuk — in the dark night,” by the choreographer Stephen Page and including performers from Bangarra Dance Theater, was a mythic evocation of Australia’s aboriginal past.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/arts/australian1/australian1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1021, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/arts/australian1/australian1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2021, 'width': 2015, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/arts/australian1/australian1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/arts/australian1/australian1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/arts/austra