ame': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14devils-1/14devils-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/14devils-1/14devils-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Run to Finals, Devils and Parise Consider Their Futures', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Run to Finals, Devils and Parise Consider Their Futures', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parise, Zach', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Free Agents (Sports)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:31:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Caldwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caldwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c855cb67-094b-5581-a0e5-b36add98f7c5', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c855cb67-094b-5581-a0e5-b36add98f7c5'}, {'abstract': 'Few of the people who were abused by teachers at Horace Mann decades ago have legal recourse because of New York State’s statute of limitations, but there is at least the possibility of legislative redress.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/the-law-and-sex-abuse-at-horace-mann/', 'snippet': 'Few of the people who were abused by teachers at Horace Mann decades ago have legal recourse because of New York State’s statute of limitations, but there is at least the possibility of legislative redress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague William Glaberson has\xa0an article in today’s New York Times\xa0about the legal implications of the abuses detailed in “Prep-School Predators,” which appeared in the magazine this past Sunday. They are few. Because of New York State’s statute of limitations — one of the most restrictive in the nation – it seems pretty clear that no one who spoke about the experiences described in the magazine has any legal recourse.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Law and Sex Abuse at Horace Mann', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mann, Horace', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:36:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariel Kaminer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaminer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/160d02a9-98f4-5851-a09c-2cd7fb2fe385', 'word_count': 212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/160d02a9-98f4-5851-a09c-2cd7fb2fe385'}, {'abstract': 'Many players think that squeezes are executed only by experts. But some just “play themselves.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/crosswords/bridge/bridge-senior-trial-final-for-the-world-mind-sports-games.html', 'snippet': 'Many players think that squeezes are executed only by experts. But some just “play themselves.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many players think that squeezes are executed only by experts. But some just “play themselves.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima