, 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conventions, Fairs and Trade Shows', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:44:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d21a188-dbee-5dfb-97a9-3bea5bb7f5f8', 'word_count': 1123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d21a188-dbee-5dfb-97a9-3bea5bb7f5f8'}, {'abstract': 'You can make the number of apps on your phone manageable by putting them in folders and regularly reviewing their usefulness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/technology/personaltech/six-steps-to-decluttering-your-smartphones-apps.html', 'snippet': 'You can make the number of apps on your phone manageable by putting them in folders and regularly reviewing their usefulness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was a little boy, my mother used to scare me into cleaning my room with tales of the Collyer brothers. You know about the Collyers, right? Two brothers. Lived together. Hoarded everything. Everything. Like, whole rooms filled to the ceiling with stuff. One brother died when a stack of ephemera collapsed on him. The other brother, already paralyzed and blind, died of starvation days later.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/14-TOOLKIT-SUB/14-TOOLKIT-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/14-TOOLKIT-SUB/14-TOOLKIT-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/14-TOOLKIT-SUB/14-TOOLKIT-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/business/14-TOOLKIT-SUB/14-TOOLKIT-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/business/14-TOOLKIT-SUB/14-TOOLKIT-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Steps to Decluttering Your Smartphone', 'kicker': 'Tool Kit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Six Steps to Decluttering Your Smartphone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:45:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e035a1a3-92da-5c96-80e9-4ff09a74f892', 'word_count': 1084, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e035a1a3-92da-5c96-80e9-4ff09a74f892'}, {'abstract': 'Yayoi Kusama’s exhibit opens at the Whitney Museum today.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/an-infinity-of-lights-photos-from-the-new-yayoi-kusama-exhibit/', 'snippet': 'Yayoi Kusama’s exhibit opens at the Whitney Museum today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The adorable, polka-dot-obsessed Japanese artist Yayoi Kusama is having her first United States retrospective at the Whitney Museum in July, but today the first part of the show opens. The installation, “Fireflies on the Water,” consists of a small room with mirrored walls, two inches of water on the floor, a raised platform for a viewer to stand on and 150 colored lights dangling from the ceiling.\xa0Only one person is allowed in the room at a time. Once the door closes behind you, it’s like you’re suspended in outer space. An infinity of lights surrounds you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Infinity of Lights: Photos From the New Yayoi Kusama Exhibit', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kusama, Yayoi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Kellner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kellner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3bb87578-4068-5fe1-97cd-830c87684a1a', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3bb87578-4068-5fe1-97cd-830c87684a1a'}, {'abstract': 'The question of who should control the .music suffix is the latest example of the music world’s struggle over the Internet, as industry groups and technology giants compete.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/digital-notes-plans-for-a-new-music-suffix-but-who-will-own-it/', 'snippet': 'The question of who should control the .music suffix is the latest example of the music world’s struggle over the Internet, as industry groups and technology giants compete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As part of changes planned by the organization that oversees Web addresses, music fans might soon be typing “JustinBieber.music” or “BruceSpringsteen.music” instead of more familiar addresses that end in .com or .net.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Notes: Plans for a New .Music Suffix, but Who Will Own It?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Internet Corp for Assigned Names and Numbers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Recording Industry Assn of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d7f0e14-41cf-5645-b8c2-6a894740a816', 'word_count': 815, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d7f0e14-41cf-5645-b8c2-6a894740a816'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama presents the Presidential Medal of Freedom to Shimon Peres, calling him “the essence of Israel.”', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/obama-honors-israels-president/', 'snippet': 'President Obama presents the Presidential Medal of Freedom to Shimon Peres, calling him “the essence of Israel.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON —President Obama presented Israel’s president,Shimon Peres, with America’s highest civilian honor, the Presidential Medal of Freedom, calling Mr. Peres “the essence of Israel itself — an indomitable spirit that will not be denied.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Honors Israel’s President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bestowing Honor, Obama Lauds Israel’s Peres', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Medal of Freedom', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peres, Shimon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-13T22:49:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/756aea86-44e9-5a48-849d-7611b3e1a101', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/756aea86-44e9-5a48-849d-7611b3e1a101'}, {'abstract': 'After moving constantly while growing up, Stuart Emmrich finds himself left with a somewhat complicated relationship with possessions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/garden/stuart-emmrich-the-unencumbered-life.html', 'snippet': 'After moving constantly while growing up, Stuart Emmrich finds himself left with a somewhat complicated relationship with possessions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN I was in sixth grade, and living in the town of Cape Coral, Fla., with my mother and stepfather, a real estate developer who was helping to turn this former Gulf Coast swampland into a planned community, our family car — a steel-gray Ford Torino I longed to drive one day — kept getting stolen.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': 