iving to the president.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/for-donors-40000-a-plate-and-dont-be-late/', 'snippet': 'Fashion industry leaders are opening up their wallets for President Obama, filling a crucial void in New York fund-raising circles left by Wall Street donors who remain leery of giving to the president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The garment district is the new financial district.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Donors, $40,000 a Plate, and Don’t Be Late', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Donors, $40,000 a Plate, and Don’t Be Late', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Sarah Jessica', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wintour, Anna', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:14:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/022fcbf7-d1aa-56ff-a1a9-74c242821bd4', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/022fcbf7-d1aa-56ff-a1a9-74c242821bd4'}, {'abstract': 'Governor Cuomo’s preliminary blueprint for hydraulic fracturing appears to be on the right track. But many important issues must still be addressed and tough, detailed regulations issued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/opinion/drilling-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Governor Cuomo’s preliminary blueprint for hydraulic fracturing appears to be on the right track. But many important issues must still be addressed and tough, detailed regulations issued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Andrew Cuomo’s preliminary blueprint for hydraulic fracturing in New York State strikes a sensible balance between the need for economic development and the need to protect the environment and human health. Many important issues must still be addressed — and tough, detailed regulations issued — before Mr. Cuomo can think of greenlighting drilling. But he appears to be on the right track.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Drilling in New York', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drilling in New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:15:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fb8b16d-aa62-5192-966e-33962a1f0e35', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fb8b16d-aa62-5192-966e-33962a1f0e35'}, {'abstract': 'Even as Mr. Dimon admits to the greed and hubris of big banks, he is still resisting needed regulations, and lawmakers are still giving him a pass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/opinion/jamie-dimon-on-the-hill.html', 'snippet': 'Even as Mr. Dimon admits to the greed and hubris of big banks, he is still resisting needed regulations, and lawmakers are still giving him a pass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jamie Dimon, the head of JPMorgan Chase, told the Senate Banking Committee on Wednesday that he had been “dead wrong” to dismiss early news reports of his bank’s reckless trading and that he was “sorry” for the resulting losses, variously estimated at $2 billion to $5 billion, and counting. He even ventured that too-big-to-fail banks have “negatives,” including “you know, greed, arrogance, hubris, lack of attention to detail.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Dimon on the Hill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Dimon on the Hill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:17:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dff8067f-afa2-551f-95c5-a552f49cb55a', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dff8067f-afa2-551f-95c5-a552f49cb55a'}, {'abstract': 'The response of the venture firm Kleiner Perkins to charges of sex discrimination can be summed up in five words: None of this is true. In a seven-page response filed in San Francisco Superior Court late Wednesday, the firm took an aggressive stance to charges that it retaliated against a female partner.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/venture-firm-fires-back-in-discrimination-case/', 'snippet': 'The response of the venture firm Kleiner Perkins to charges of sex discrimination can be summed up in five words: None of this is true. In a seven-page response filed in San Francisco Superior Court late Wednesday, the firm took an aggressive stan...', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers, the Silicon Valley venture capital firm, filed its legal response Wednesday to the sex discrimination charges made last month by a junior partner, Ellen Pao, sweepingly and specifically denying all the claims.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venture Firm Fires Back in Discrimination Case', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kleiner Perkins Denies Sex Bias in Response to a Lawsuit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexual Harassment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doerr, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nazre, Ajit', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pao, Ellen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Streitfeld', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Streitfeld', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83cf49d1-fbfd-5c9a-94b4-aee3d5bded9b', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83cf49d1-fbfd-5c9a-94b4-aee3d5bded9b'}, {'abstract': 'It is easy to feel how tangible a generation really is after it is gone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/opinion/we-who-are-left-when-a-generation-passes.html', 'snippet': 'It is easy to feel how tangible a generation really is after it is gone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime in 1931, my dad and his four siblings, farm kids all, posed for a formal photograph. The boys are wearing suits, and the girl, my aunt Janelle, is wearing an infant’s white dress. The oldest boy, Everon, is perhaps 12 years old, and my dad is 5. And now they are all gone. Everon and Janelle, the last of them, died six days apart in early June.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'We Who Are Left When a Generation Passes', 'kicker': 'Editorial Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'We Who Are Left When a Generation Passes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minnesota', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:21:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': N