7c-8192db63f682', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11d05e8c-1ca6-5c74-be7c-8192db63f682'}, {'abstract': 'In rejecting the appeals of Guantánamo detainees that challenge the legality of their imprisonment, the justices are denying the prisoners a basic right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/opinion/the-supreme-court-retreats-on-habeas.html', 'snippet': 'In rejecting the appeals of Guantánamo detainees that challenge the legality of their imprisonment, the justices are denying the prisoners a basic right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Supreme Court ruled in 2008 that Congress could not strip federal courts of jurisdiction to hear habeas corpus petitions from non-American prisoners at Guantánamo Bay, the 5-to-4 majority opinion written by Justice Anthony Kennedy appeared to be a landmark victory for the rights of detainees. “The laws and Constitution are designed to survive, and remain in force, in extraordinary times,” Justice Kennedy wrote in Boumediene v. Bush, and “the framers decided that habeas corpus, a right of first importance,” must be part of the American legal framework. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Court Retreats on Habeas', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Court Retreats on Habeas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tatel, David S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boumediene, Lakhdar', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6dfaa05-5378-52cb-afcc-34d6e22281eb', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6dfaa05-5378-52cb-afcc-34d6e22281eb'}, {'abstract': 'A judge on Wednesday ended a showdown that had threatened to leave the city unable to pay its bills as early as Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/us/michigan-judge-dismisses-lawsuit-challenging-detroit-solvency-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A judge on Wednesday ended a showdown that had threatened to leave the city unable to pay its bills as early as Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A judge on Wednesday threw out a legal challenge to an agreement intended to spare Detroit from financial ruin, ending a showdown that had threatened to leave the city unable to pay its bills as early as Friday. The judge, William Collette, of Ingham County Circuit Court, dismissed a suit that had been brought by Detroit’s corporation counsel, though opposed by its mayor, Dave Bing. The suit said that Detroit, which in April agreed to a deal with the state to steady its finances, could not enter into the contract because, the suit asserted, the state owes Detroit hundreds of millions of dollars from past debts. Mr. Bing said the city could now move forward in its effort to recover. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Michigan: Judge Dismisses Lawsuit Challenging Detroit Solvency Deal ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Michigan: Judge Dismisses Lawsuit Challenging Detroit Solvency Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value'