dding, which allows advertisers to place bids on ad space for specific groups of users at specific times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its quest to bolster the growth of its digital advertising, Facebook is slowly breaking down its walled garden for advertisers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Begins Ad Bidding System', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T01:45:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c3912110-73c5-564c-8de3-7935be81dd6a', 'word_count': 237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c3912110-73c5-564c-8de3-7935be81dd6a'}, {'abstract': 'The Kentucky Horse Racing Commission approved a limited ban on the race-day medication furosemide, also known as Lasix or Salix, in an effort to restore public confidence in the sport.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/sports/kentucky-commission-bars-lasix-in-top-races.html', 'snippet': 'The Kentucky Horse Racing Commission approved a limited ban on the race-day medication furosemide, also known as Lasix or Salix, in an effort to restore public confidence in the sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Kentucky Horse Racing Commission approved a limited ban on the race-day medication furosemide Wednesday in an effort to restore public confidence that horses are running without what many veterinarians say is a performance-enhancing drug. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Tim