e': 'persons', 'value': 'Vinson, Roger', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Broccoli', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chemerinsky, Erwin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eastman, John C', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeffrey, Terence P', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T02:44:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By James B. Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ea7eeee-492c-544d-9f26-3ee6b3166c42', 'word_count': 2302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ea7eeee-492c-544d-9f26-3ee6b3166c42'}, {'abstract': 'As the U.S. Catholic bishops gather for their annual spring meeting, protesters want them to intervene on behalf of the nation’s nuns, who have been sharply criticized by the Vatican for “serious doctrinal problems.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/protesters-for-nuns-ask-u-s-bishops-to-help-them-out/', 'snippet': 'As the U.S. Catholic bishops gather for their annual spring meeting, protesters want them to intervene on behalf of the nation’s nuns, who have been sharply criticized by the Vatican for “serious doctrinal problems.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Protesting the Vatican’s criticism of the United States’ largest organization of Roman Catholic nuns, a group of people gathered outside the annual spring meeting of U.S. bishops in Atlanta on Wednesday and delivered a petition asking the bishops to intervene on the nuns’ behalf.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protesters for Nuns Ask U.S. Bishops to Help Them Out', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Priests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leadership Conference of Women Religious', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vatican City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T02:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9a7270a-d9d6-5c25-be4f-59adc8a23c62', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9a7270a-d9d6-5c25-be4f-59adc8a23c62'}, {'abstract': 'A graduate of The Citadel who went on to work with children there and at other schools and served as a foster parent pleaded guilty to 22 counts of child sexual abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/us/south-carolina-man-gets-50-years-for-molesting-over-20-children.html', 'snippet': 'A graduate of The Citadel who went on to work with children there and at other schools and served as a foster parent pleaded guilty to 22 counts of child sexual abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A graduate of The Citadel who went on to work with children there and at other schools and served as a foster parent pleaded guilty to 22 counts of child sexual abuse and was sentenced to 50 years in prison on Wednesday. The man, Louis ReVille, 32, who was arrested in October after an investigation revealed he molested more than 20 children he taught and coached in the Charleston area, apologized to his victims. Some are suing the institutions that hired him, including The Citadel, a military college. Victims have claimed that The Citadel knew Mr. ReVille molested teenagers at a camp in 2002, luring boys into his room with the promise of pizza and Chinese food and then showing them pornography and encouraging group masturbation sessions. The college, which investigated the complaint but did not report it to police, apologized. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'South Carolina: Man Gets 50 Years for Molesting Over 20 Children', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'South Carolina: Man Gets 50 Years For Molesting Over 20 Children', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T02:51:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d912900-5fb2-589e-8744-12433474ea86', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d912900-5fb2-589e-8744-12433474ea86'}, {'abstract': 'U.S. lawmakers said Jorge Luis García Pérez, who testified last Thursday on the short-term detention of dissidents, was released Wednesday, four days after he was beaten and arrested by authorities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/world/americas/cuba-senators-condemn-treatment-of-cuban-dissident.html', 'snippet': 'U.S. lawmakers said Jorge Luis García Pérez, who testified last Thursday on the short-term detention of dissidents, was released Wednesday, four days after he was beaten and arrested by authorities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several United States senators are condemning the arrest and abuse they say a Cuban dissident endured after he testified by video conference before a Senate subcommittee looking into repression on the island. Lawmakers said Jorge Luis García Pérez, known as Antúnez, was released Wednesday, four days after he was beaten and arrested by authorities. He had testified last Thursday from the United States Interest Section in Havana on the short-term detention of dissidents. Mr. García Pérez still faces charges, including “spreading false information,” senators Robert Menendez of New Jersey and Marco Rubio of Florida, both Cuban-Americans, said in a statement. The Cuban government has not responded, but generally treats dissidents as common criminals in the pay of the American government and exile groups.\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuba: Senators Condemn Treatment of Cuban Dissident', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T02:51:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/736b60da-7f4b-5c9b-ad39-9d6947e5aecf', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/736b60da-7f4b-5c9b-ad39-9d6947e5aecf'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print for June 14, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/pageoneplus/corrections-june-14.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print for June 14, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 14', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T03:01:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c2e68eb-95a8-5176-b22a-affb8bd53da8', 'word_count': 663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c2e68eb-95a8-5176-b22a-affb8bd53da8'}, {'abstract': 'What can Mormons Building Bridges, who marched in solidarity at the Salt Lake City gay pride parade earlier this month, learn from the history of Mormons for E.R.A.?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/equal-rights-gay-rights-and-the-mormon-church/', 'snippet': 'What can Mormons Building Bridges, who marched in solidarity at the Salt Lake City gay pride parade earlier this month, learn from the history of Mormons for E.R.A.?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, gay and lesbian Americans celebrate gay pride. There has in fact been a lot to celebrate recently: the end of the military’s Don’t Ask, Don’t Tell policy; President Obama’s endorsement of gay marriage; and the recent ruling by a federal appeals court that declared the Defense of Marriage Act unconstitutional. For the most part, these political breakthroughs have been backed by an American public that is increasingly supportive of gay rights.\xa0Such a monumental and rapid transformation on the question of homosexuality has led many observers to deem gay rights the fastest-moving civil rights movement in our nation’s history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Equal Rights, Gay Rights and the Mormon Church', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Equal Rights Amendment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bayh, Birch Evan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salt Lake City (Utah)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T03:05:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil J. Young', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Young', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a5e86e2-d1eb-5b03-9889-4cec61cca6cc', 'word_count': 2447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a5e86e2-d1eb-5b03-9889-4cec61cca6cc'}, {'abstract': 'Sheldon Adelson, a billionaire casino owner, and his wife, Dr. Miriam Adelson, are by far the most prolific campaign donors in the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/us/politics/sheldon-adelson-sets-new-standard-as-campaign-aid-surges-into-8-figures.html', 'sni