ia, and mostly worried about final exams that would test his perfect 4.0 grade average.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/Y-GOLFERS/Y-GOLFERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/Y-GOLFERS/Y-GOLFERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/Y-GOLFERS/Y-GOLFERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/Y-GOLFERS/Y-GOLFERS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/sports/Y-GOLFERS/Y-GOLFERS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Everyman Qualifiers Offer Inspiration', 'kicker': 'U.S. Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Three Everyman Qualifiers Offer Inspiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympic Club (San Francisco, Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCormick, Mark', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hossler, Beau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MILLER, DENNIS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T03:13:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9880f64-bf09-5e71-a868-1c780496565e', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9880f64-bf09-5e71-a868-1c780496565e'}, {'abstract': 'Many of us want to keep our children engaged over the summer. But how much is too much to prevent “summer slide”?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/13/summer-learning-fun-via-e-mail-and-download/', 'snippet': 'Many of us want to keep our children engaged over the summer. But how much is too much to prevent “summer slide”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As with many things, some parents worry disproportionately about “summer slide.” Do children forget everything they’ve learned over the long summer break? It depends on how and where they spend it. If you’re reading my words, it’s likely that your children have access to reading materials at home. Children who don’t read over the summer lose two to three months of reading development while children who do gain a month — but research shows that children surrounded by reading material don’t appear to be at much risk. Summer reading is as effective as summer school, and it doesn’t matter what children read, as long as the reading is happening. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Learning Fun, Via E-mail and Download', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 