84 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'rationalize •\\ˈrash-nə-ˌliz, ˈra-shə-nə-ˌliz\\• verb ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | rationalize', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T04:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad81d14-75ac-587f-a931-8f5816fcacbd', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad81d14-75ac-587f-a931-8f5816fcacbd'}, {'abstract': 'Under pressure to perform and failing to execute, Cristiano Ronaldo can hardly enjoy a Portugal victory, while Russia’s Andrey Arshavin is exhausting himself while driving Russia through Euro 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/a-victory-for-portugal-but-a-disappointment-for-ronaldo/', 'snippet': 'Under pressure to perform and failing to execute, Cristiano Ronaldo can hardly enjoy a Portugal victory, while Russia’s Andrey Arshavin is exhausting himself while driving Russia through Euro 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Joao Moutinho and his teammates ran to the corner of the field to embrace Silvestre Valera after the substitute put Portugal ahead of Denmark, 3-2, in the closing minutes of their Group B match Wednesday at Euro 2012, Cristiano Ronaldo fell to the grass and lay on the ground in the middle of the penalty box, alone, several yards away from the celebration.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Victory for Portugal, but a Disappointment for Ronaldo', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '