le/3b52c0c3-0029-5eee-8253-0efb35e23949', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b52c0c3-0029-5eee-8253-0efb35e23949'}, {'abstract': 'Why do social networking sites find it hard to control who uses their services?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/when-safeguards-arent-safe-enough/', 'snippet': 'Why do social networking sites find it hard to control who uses their services?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT mobile app was used by three men to meet young children, whom they are accused of raping?WHAT technology, which many mobile apps use, has prompted new fears about the safety such apps?WHAT safeguards did Skout have in its app for children? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Safeguards Aren’t Safe Enough', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T08:43:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Murray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d297817f-d533-5c1f-82a4-448bda3eeb18', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d297817f-d533-5c1f-82a4-448bda3eeb18'}, {'abstract': 'After a friend’s death, making a trip to Fair Grounds Race Course in New Orleans to bet on horses with names that reminded us of him.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/paying-tribute-at-the-track/', 'snippet': 'After a friend’s death, making a trip to Fair Grounds Race Course in New Orleans to bet on horses with names that reminded us of him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Leap Day, my best friend and artist extraordinaire, Gregory Paul Frank, died after nine days in hospice. The next day, his daughter, son-in-law and I went to Fair Grounds Race Course in New Orleans and bet on horses with names that reminded us of Greg.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Paying Tribute at the Track', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fair Grounds Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T09:29:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Dunau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c1e1d45-16a8-5eb9-8ac4-04b2bf35a0d7', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c1e1d45-16a8-5eb9-8ac4-04b2bf35a0d7'}, {'abstract': 'The author of a recent Human Rights Watch report blames the weak regulatory mechanism for rampant illegal mining in India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/a-conversation-with-christopher-albin-lackey/', 'snippet': 'The author of a recent Human Rights Watch report blames the weak regulatory mechanism for rampant illegal mining in India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the past several years, India’s mining industry has been rocked by a series of scandals in Karnataka and Goa, among other states. The Supreme Court has banned iron ore mining in Bellary, northern Karnataka, after an ombudsman released a detailed report describing what it called the industry’s “mafia-type operations.” In the coastal state of Goa, a mining scandal helped swing an election decisively in favor of an opposition political party.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Conversation With: Christopher Albin-Lackey', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mines and Mining', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Albin-Lackey, Christopher', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Goa (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karnataka (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T09:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68558f33-6b79-5d0d-8b7a-6ddc69ef24b7', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68558f33-6b79-5d0d-8b7a-6ddc69ef24b7'}, {'abstract': 'The Lede is following developments in the day-long testimony on Thursday of Prime Minister David Cameron at a British judicial inquiry into the media standards and the behavior of the press.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/live-updates-on-cameron-testimony-to-british-inquiry/', 'snippet': 'The Lede is following developments in the day-long testimony on Thursday of Prime Minister David Cameron at a British judicial inquiry into the media standards and the behavior of the press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lede followed developments in the daylong testimony of Prime Minister David Cameron on Thursday to a British judicial inquiry on media standards and the behavior of the press. Mr. Cameron’s appearance, which lasted about six hours and included questions about the nature of his relationship to Rupert Murdoch’s media empire, followed three days of testimony by British political leaders past and present. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Updates on Cameron Testimony to British Inquiry', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cameron, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T09:54:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b0f0664-c5f3-5af9-beb1-9efd9841c051', 'word_count': 4837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b0f0664-c5f3-5af9-beb1-9efd9841c051'}, {'abstract': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/the-early-word-delineation/', 'snippet': 'Political news from today’s Times and around the Web, plus a look at what’s happening in Washington.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Delineation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, '