_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/406bb081-3be1-58a1-974c-81324960c33f', 'word_count': 604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/406bb081-3be1-58a1-974c-81324960c33f'}, {'abstract': 'There was a lot to like about the first part of this pitch, including a socially conscious solution to a serious problem.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/a-pitch-for-a-pollution-solution-goes-off-the-deep-end/', 'snippet': 'There was a lot to like about the first part of this pitch, including a socially conscious solution to a serious problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For our last pitch, I reviewed a Web 2.0 company that wants to help you manage your digital experience. This week, I review a pitch for a company that wants to solve our energy problems and clean up the Mississippi River at the same time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pitch for a Pollution Solution Goes Off the Deep End', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/764ae8e3-e7bd-5681-9b8f-f30b8a4f9688', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/764ae8e3-e7bd-5681-9b8f-f30b8a4f9688'}, {'abstract': 'Graduated from Juilliard. Married Meryl Streep’s daughter. Hopes to be the next Dick Van Dyke. But first he has some vampires to kill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/magazine/benjamin-walker-sexypants-vampire-hunter.html', 'snippet': 'Graduated from Juilliard. Married Meryl Streep’s daughter. Hopes to be the next Dick Van Dyke. But first he has some vampires to kill.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What I’m trying to do,” Benjamin Walker announced with mock solemnity from the stage at Joe’s Pub, the nightclub arm of the Public Theater, “is something I’ve never done before.” He made this admission on a mild evening in early April to an attentive audience of mostly young women. Walker, 29, was hosting an installment of “Find the Funny,” his charmingly slack monthly comedy show, and dressed in a fitted gray hoodie, charcoal pants and brown work boots, he surveyed the tightly packed room and ran a hand through his floppy brown hair. Then he started to play the ringing intro to Kings of Leon’s swooning hit “Use Somebody.” With his foot, he tapped a device on the floor to loop his guitar line so he could play in harmony with himself. This is not an easy trick to pull off. There’s a reason Kings of Leon has two guitar players.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17walker1/17walker1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17walker1/17walker1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17walker1/17walker1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1018, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17walker1/17walker1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1491, 'sub