e paid off.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/for-the-thunder-a-coach-who-made-the-pieces-and-plays-fit/', 'snippet': 'The Oklahoma City Coach Scott Brooks was criticized after the Thunder lost to Dallas last season. This year, his players work well together, and his adjustments have paid off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since becoming the coach of the Oklahoma City Thunder in 2008, Scott Brooks has led the team to higher winning percentages, and deeper playoff runs, in each of the last three seasons. After a disappointing conference finals loss to eventual champs Dallas last spring, the Thunder dethroned the Mavericks – along with past impediments Los Angeles and San Antonio – en route to the franchise’s first- ever N.B.A. finals against the Heat and a Game 1 victory on Tuesday night. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Thunder, a Coach Who Made the Pieces (and Plays) Fit', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Derek', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sefolosha, Thabo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westbrook, Russell', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T11:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Cavan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f4a86f5-b317-5054-8a5d-6bbd444aa297', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f4a86f5-b317-5054-8a5d-6bbd444aa297'}, {'abstract': 'The Finnish company, struggling to restart its mobile phone business with Microsoft, also said it would post a wider loss in the second quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/technology/nokia-to-cut-10000-jobs-and-close-3-facilities.html', 'snippet': 'The Finnish company, struggling to restart its mobile phone business with Microsoft, also said it would post a wider loss in the second quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Nokia said Thursday it would slash 10,000 jobs, or 19 percent of its work force, by the end of 2013 as part of an emergency overhaul that includes closing research centers and a factory in Germany, Canada and Finland, and the departures of three senior executives.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/business/Nokia/Nokia-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 298, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/business/Nokia/Nokia-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 298}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/business/Nokia/Nokia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/business/Nokia/Nokia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/business/No