llying a separate crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/14/students-report-cyberbullying-is-pervasive/', 'snippet': 'Nearly 70 percent of some 10,000 students statewide told legislators they were victims of cyberbullying or knew someone who had been attacked on the Web. A legislator sees this as support for his bill to make cyberbullying a separate crime.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Students Report Cyberbullying Is Pervasive', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T11:42:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44738fc8-073e-5b86-9eef-398091a8a161', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44738fc8-073e-5b86-9eef-398091a8a161'}, {'abstract': 'HBO has apologized for a scene in its hit fantasy series “Game of Thrones” that showed the decapitated head of former President George W. Bush on a pike and said the scene will be removed from future DVD releases.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/hbo-apologizes-for-bush-head-in-game-of-thrones-dvd/', 'snippet': 'HBO has apologized for a scene in its hit fantasy series “Game of Thrones” that showed the decapitated head of former President George W. Bush on a pike and said the scene will be removed from future DVD releases.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:45 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'HBO Apologizes for Bush Head in ‘Game of Thrones’ DVD', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'HBO Apologizes For Bush Scenes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DVD (Digital Versatile Disc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benioff, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T11:53:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63b68cd7-dd5f-5c07-83fe-f6a1a8a9c834', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63b68cd7-dd5f-5c07-83fe-f6a1a8a9c834'}, {'abstract': 'In Justin Bieber’s new album, “Believe,” he branches out musically while hewing to the persona he created.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/arts/music/justin-biebers-album-believe-comes-out-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'In Justin Bieber’s new album, “Believe,” he branches out musically while hewing to the persona he created.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just how fast is Justin Bieber allowed to grow up? And how much? Mr. Bieber, the defining teen star of recent years, turned 18 in March and has been in the public eye for almost four years, long enough to begin chafing. His desire to move in the world as an adult is palpable, but the very scale of his celebrity exacts its own sort of toll. Mr. Bieber can be his own man, sure, so long as he continues to belong to everyone else too. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17BIEBER_SPAN/17BIEBER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pop’s Good Boy Tries Growing Up', 'kicker': 'Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop’s Good Boy Tries Growing Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T12:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cfff10c-9551-5f5c-bbfa-8533366f0a7b', 'word_count': 1566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cfff10c-9551-5f5c-bbfa-8533366f0a7b'}, {'abstract': 'Pop Warner football acts to reduce youth concussion risk, a review of the MacBook Pro, the possible end of the summer job and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/thursday-reading-youth-football-acts-to-reduce-concussion-risk/', 'snippet': 'Pop Warner football acts to reduce youth concussion risk, a review of the MacBook Pro, the possible end of the summer job and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Thursday Reading: Youth Football Acts to Reduce Concussion Risk', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T12:02:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/347320b3-f2af-5d06-aa08-9eeb7bb1ea21', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/347320b3-f2af-5d06-aa08-9eeb7bb1ea21'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/morning-take-out-505/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘Proud’ JPMorgan Chief Apologizes \xa0|\xa0 Jamie Dimon, the outspoken chief executive of JPMorgan Chase under scrutiny for a multibillion-dollar trading loss at his firm, apologized for the problems on Wednesday even as he mounted a fierce defense of his bank.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T12:03:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77887f24-a617-5ea9-bbcf-dc8d6acc64bb', 'word_count': 2336, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77887f24-a617-5ea9-bbcf-dc8d6acc64bb'}, {'abstract': 'Despite partisan sniping, President Obama’s choice to lead the commission and a nominee seeking a second term seem to be headed toward confirmation.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/two-nuclear-nominees-get-a-hearing/', 'snippet': 'Despite partisan sniping, President Obama’s choice to lead the commission and a nominee seeking a second term seem to be headed toward confirmation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s nominee to lead the Nuclear Regulatory Commission said at a Senate confirmation hearing on Wednesday that the nuclear industry’s share of American electricity production, steady at 20 percent for the last decade, could decline in coming years. Nonetheless, a diverse electricity supply requires continued use of nuclear power, she said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Nuclear Nominees Get a Hearing', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and E