'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lautenberg, Frank R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nestle, Marion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taubes, Gary', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corn Refiners Assn', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taco Bell Corp', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T13:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Bittman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bittman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e82a7425-3bb9-505d-a65d-7c70114b7a09', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e82a7425-3bb9-505d-a65d-7c70114b7a09'}, {'abstract': 'Charlie Sheen, who returns to television in a new FX series, “Anger Management,” talks about his Twitter account, the unexpected places it has taken him, and making things right with his ex-wives and his fans.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/another-installment-of-civilized-conversation-with-charlie-sheen/', 'snippet': 'Charlie Sheen, who returns to television in a new FX series, “Anger Management,” talks about his Twitter account, the unexpected places it has taken him, and making things right with his ex-wives and his fans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — In a previous polite chat with Charlie Sheen, he discussed the creation of his new FX series, “Anger Management.” In these final excerpts from that conversation, at his base camp at the studio where the show is produced, Mr. Sheen (who is the subject of an article this week) talks about his Twitter account, which he operates with the help of his social-media manager, Bob Maron; the unexpected places it has taken him; and making things right with his ex-wives and his fans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Installment of Civilized Conversation With Charlie Sheen', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheen, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T13:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d8266e7-a2bc-5680-99a3-6aa32e86302c', 'word_count': 1331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d8266e7-a2bc-5680-99a3-6aa32e86302c'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Weber’s memorable images, set near his Long Island home, go on display on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/bruces-bellport/', 'snippet': 'Bruce Weber’s memorable images, set near his Long Island home, go on display on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The celebrated photographer Bruce Weber has always used his home bases — in Montana, the Adirondacks, Montauk, and Miami — as settings for his distinctly American fashion shoots. Tomorrow, the Bellport-Brookhaven Historical Society on Long Island will unveil “A Bellport Tale,” a new exhibit of photos that Weber took when he resided in Bellport in the 1970s and ’80s. “Everyone knew each other,” Weber said of the quaint bayside village. “You could knock on any door and just invite a neighbor over to be part of a photography sitting. It was as easy as borrowing a cup of sugar.” The images in the exhibit come from a shoot that appeared in British Vogue in 1982 called “Under Weston Eyes.” Starring Talisa Soto and the male model of the moment, Bruce Hulse, that story was styled by Grace Coddington and inspired by the work of another photographer, Edward Weston. “He took things that were very personal to him and let us see into that world,” Weber said. “I thought it would be interesting to do a series of pictures of my own imaginary family, living together in the dysfunctional, neurotic, beautiful way that families do.” The exhibit (on view through Sept. 3) includes many memorable images, but perhaps none is more evocative of a quiet life on the bay than that of a shirtless Hulse, sitting on the stern of a boat, cigarette in hand, wearing calf-revealing baggy trousers, rumpled socks and dress shoes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruce’s Bellport', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coddington, Grace', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Bruce (1946- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weston, Edward', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vogue', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bellport (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T13:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Pask', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pask', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8334103b-c839-5dde-ab63-61506ce46efb', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8334103b-c839-5dde-ab63-61506ce46efb'}, {'abstract': 'If you don’t have a bad feeling, you’re not paying attention.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/historical-echoes/', 'snippet': 'If you don’t have a bad feeling, you’re not paying attention.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin O’Rourke:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Historical Echoes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T13:02:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb6c59a-beb1-5915-b412-a6f25ac11d9a', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb6c59a-beb1-5915-b412-a6f25ac11d9a'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama laid out his re-election bid as a stark choice between strong government action to lift the middle class and Republican policies he said had led to a deep recession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/us/politics/obama-speech-seeks-to-assert-stark-choice-for-voters.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama laid out his re-election bid as a stark choice between strong government action to lift the middle class and Republican policies he said had led to a deep recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CLEVELAND — Framing his re-election bid as a stark choice between government action to lift the middle class and a return to Republican economic policies that he said had caused a deep recession, President Obama on Thursday called the presidential decision facing Americans a clear-cut one that will determine the long-term trajectory of the economy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 700, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15obama_337/15obama_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Says Election Offers a Clear Choice on the Economy’s Long-Term Path', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Says Election Offers a Clear Choice on the Economy’s Long-Term Path', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T13:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper and Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98fc0f52-0c37-5bfe-8c86-93a47871bdc6', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98fc0f52-0c37-5bfe-8c86-93a47871bdc6'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain testifies about the relationship between the British press and government, subscriptions to Time Inc. magazines will be available via Apple’s newsstand, and the inspiration of the Martin Scorsese film “Goodfellas” died on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/the-breakfast-meeting-questions-for-prime-minister-and-can-bieber-ever-grow-up/', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister David Cameron of Britain testifies about the relationship between the British press and government, subscriptions to Time Inc. magazines will be available via Apple’s newsstand, and the inspiration of the Martin Scorsese film “Goodf...', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British prime minister, David Cameron, is spending all of Thursday testifying before the Leveson commission as it investigates the relationship between the British press and recent governments. Mr. Cameron seemed confident during the early questions, Alan Cowell and John F. Burns write, but his tone sharpened when Robert Jay, the lead counsel for inquiry, inferred that Mr. Cameron shaped Conservative Party media policy to please Rupert Murdoch and his newspapers. Those polices “weren’t dictated by anyone else,” Mr. Cameron said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Questions for Prime Minister, and Can Bieber Ever Grow Up?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T13:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea0594c2-e91b-5214-ae97-39aeb3dac4fe', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea0594c2-e91b-5214-ae97-39aeb3dac4fe'}, {'abstract': 'The geographic terrain of the 2012 presidential campaign will narrow on Thursday to a 250-mile stretch between Cleveland and Cincinnati, two cities that will hold dueling events by President Obama and Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/obama-and-romney-campaigns-face-off-in-ohio/', 'snippet': 'The geographic terrain of the 2012 presidential campaign will narrow on Thursday to a 250-mile stretch between Cleveland and Cincinnati, two cities that will hold dueling events by President Obama and Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The geographic terrain of the 2012 presidential campaign will narrow on Thursday to a 250-mile stretch in Ohio between Cleveland and Cincinnati, the two cities that will play host to dueling events by President Obama and Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama and Romney Campaigns Face Off