ub_date': '2012-06-14T14:34:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Haley Sweetland Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Haley', 'middlename': 'Sweetland', 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ac1e948-8e01-5913-b86b-7620684bf77c', 'word_count': 591, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ac1e948-8e01-5913-b86b-7620684bf77c'}, {'abstract': 'A small-scale replica of a World War II concentration camp erected in Prague commemorates the assassination of the notorious Nazi general Reinhard Heydrich and celebrates those who were part of the resistance movement.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/in-prague-revisiting-an-assassination-and-the-resistance-movement/', 'snippet': 'A small-scale replica of a World War II concentration camp erected in Prague commemorates the assassination of the notorious Nazi general Reinhard Heydrich and celebrates those who were part of the resistance movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A small-scale replica of a World War II concentration camp was erected in Prague to commemorate the assassination of the notorious Nazi general Reinhard Heydrich, 70 years ago in the Czech capital. The exhibition, “Assassination of Heydrich,”\xa0 opened last month on Karlovo namesti (Charles Square) and will run until June 18.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Prague, Revisiting an Assassination and the Resistance Movement', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heydrich, Reinhard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Prague (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T14:37:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': "By Julie O'Shea", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Shea", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd1a1ee-d863-5b49-9e75-9a1b8d9f37c5', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd1a1ee-d863-5b49-9e75-9a1b8d9f37c5'}, {'abstract': 'From the Cairo bureau of The New York Times, The Lede is following the reaction in Egypt to twin rulings by the country’s highest court on Thursday, which threw the country’s post-revolutionary political transition into disarray.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/latest-updates-on-electoral-turmoil-in-egypt/', 'snippet': 'From the Cairo bureau of The New York Times, The Lede is following the reaction in Egypt to twin rulings by the country’s highest court on Thursday, which threw the country’s post-revolutionary political transition into disarray.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reporting from the Cairo bureau of The New York Times, The Lede is following the reaction in Egypt to twin rulings by the country’s highest court on Thursday, which threw the country’s post-revolutionary political transition into disarray. Two days before Egyptians go to the polls to elect a new president, the court dissolved the country’s recently elected Parliament and struck down a law passed by that body that would have barred Hosni Mubarak’s last prime minister from this weekend’s presidential election. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Latest Updates on Electoral Turmoil in Egypt', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T14:40:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7102480-3a0c-5938-8ccf-08144ee08513', 'word_count': 3353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7102480-3a0c-5938-8ccf-08144ee08513'}, {'abstract': 'A panel of judges also blessed the presidential bid of Hosni Mubarak’s last prime minister, putting Egypt’s troubled move to democracy in grave doubt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/world/middleeast/new-political-showdown-in-egypt-as-court-invalidates-parliament.html', 'snippet': 'A panel of judges also blessed the presidential bid of Hosni Mubarak’s last prime minister, putting Egypt’s troubled move to democracy in grave doubt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A panel of judges appointed by Egypt’s ousted president, Hosni Mubarak, threw the nation’s troubled transition to democracy into grave doubt Thursday with rulings that dissolved the popularly elected Parliament and allowed the toppled government’s last prime minister to run for president, escalating a struggle by remnants of the old elite to block Islamists from coming to power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/15egyptspan/15egyptspan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 