 SCHOOLBOOK', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Schoolbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fcc9a59-501b-5ada-9283-58cf3e37dde3', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fcc9a59-501b-5ada-9283-58cf3e37dde3'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes the very best travel guides aren’t traditional guidebooks at all.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/now-reading-offbeat-city-guides/', 'snippet': 'Sometimes the very best travel guides aren’t traditional guidebooks at all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite the glut of travel guides available, it’s sometimes hard to find ones that are actually instructive, that get at the heart of what’s going on in a given city and spare us the travel-writing clichés. That’s why it’s a welcome treat to discover Marc Santo and Scott Newman’s scrappy little Revel in New York series, the third edition of which went on sale last week. The pocket-size Revel isn’t a typical guidebook — half of its pages are devoted to freewheeling interviews with chefs, artists and architects about their work. But each of these subjects, New Yorkers either by birth or disposition, also shares a dozen or so deeply idiosyncratic recommendations. Taken together, their tips offer a unique way of exploring the city, even for its current residents.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Reading | Offbeat City Guides', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Heyman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heyman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f1e083-fbe4-5787-b746-f8f1837d7cae', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f1e083-fbe4-5787-b746-f8f1837d7cae'}, {'abstract': 'A man protests the alleged targeting of Muslims as terror suspects in India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/image-of-the-day-june-14/', 'snippet': 'A man protests the alleged targeting of Muslims as terror suspects in India.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: June 14', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1262f006-1dc3-5c9f-b733-73dc4099c29e', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1262f006-1dc3-5c9f-b733-73dc4099c29e'}, {'abstract': 'The musician Michael Arenella not only plays the music of the Jazz Age, but he also tries to live in its style.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/design/living-in-the-past-is-a-full-time-gig.html', 'snippet': 'The musician Michael Arenella not only plays the music of the Jazz Age, but he also tries to live in its style.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MICHAEL ARENELLA is at an open-air flea market in Lambertville, N.J., his fedora-topped head leaning over a gramophone. He winds the crank, lifts the arm and places the needle on a 78. Out of the old oak box comes a voice from the past: Arthur Fields singing “In My Tippy Canoe” in 1921. Mr. Arenella stands silently, hands in his pockets, taking in every crackly note.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living in the Past Is a Full-Time Gig', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Living in the Past Is a Full-Time Gig', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dreamland Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arenella, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Twenties', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:01:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Stapinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stapinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c09352e-c394-5700-8c2a-a237d402acdc', 'word_count': 1636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c09352e-c394-5700-8c2a-a237d402acdc'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Arenella, a musician from Brooklyn, escapes the reality of modern life through replicating the style of the Jazz Age. For him, living retro is a way to find happiness in ordinary things.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/design/100000001604782/living-retro.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Arenella, a musician from Brooklyn, escapes the reality of modern life through replicating the style of the Jazz Age. For him, living retro is a way to find happiness in ordinary things.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Arenella, a musician from Brooklyn, escapes the reality of modern life through replicating the style of the Jazz Age. For him, living retro is a way to find happiness in ordinary things.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/video-living-retro/video-living-retro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/video-living-retro/video-living-retro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/video-living-retro/video-living-retro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/video-living-retro/video-living-retro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Living Retro', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:02:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'Natalia V. Osipova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalia', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Osipova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/9569b356-06d9-5bbf-8a60-79fe1306ec01', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/9569b356-06d9-5bbf-8a60-79fe1306ec01'}, {'abstract': 'By taking the time to write a manual, I am demonstrating to my workers that I intend to take a rational approach to the boss/employee relationship.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/the-balance-of-power-between-bosses-and-workers/', 'snippet': 'By taking the time to write a manual, I am demonstrating to my workers that I intend to take a rational approach to the boss/employee relationship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were lots of comments to my post on how I fire people, and I’d like to address some of the points. Commenters raised two main issues: First, that the policies I outlined in my employee manual are written for the benefit of the company as opposed to the employee and, second, that I seemed to be favoring firing people instead of training them. Both of these are complex issues that are handled differently by different companies. I can only comment on my own thoughts and experiences. Please don’t blame me for the many, many bad bosses and companies out there. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Balance of Power Between Bosses and Workers', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment Insurance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65f739ec-a867-5ca1-a649-f2cd7f03909b', 'word_count': 1623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65f739ec-a867-5ca1-a649-f2cd7f03909b'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Bormann, an ecologist who taught at Dartmouth and Yale, spotted the new environmental danger with a team of scientists while doing research in a New Hampshire forest in 1971.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/us/f-herbert-bormann-ecologist-dies-at-90.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Bormann, an ecologist who taught at Dartmouth and Yale, spotted the new environmental danger with a team of scientists while doing research in a New Hampshire forest in 1971.', 'lead_paragraph': 'F. Herbert Bormann, a plant ecologist whose research with colleagues on a swath of New Hampshire forest in 1971 documented a new environmental horror in the United States — acid rain — died on June 7 at his home in North Branford, Conn. He was 90. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Bormann1/Bormann1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Bormann1/Bormann1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Bormann1/Bormann1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Bormann1/Bormann1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1413, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Bormann1/Bormann1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Bormann1/Bormann1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/sports/Borman