N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:32:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1401499-3968-5caa-8026-43848db0487a', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1401499-3968-5caa-8026-43848db0487a'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Walker, who has emerged as a leading voice in the Republican Party after becoming the nation’s first governor to survive a recall, said Mr. Romney needed to broaden his appeal beyond Republicans to carry Wisconsin in November.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/romney-should-hone-economic-message-walker-says/', 'snippet': 'Scott Walker, who has emerged as a leading voice in the Republican Party after becoming the nation’s first governor to survive a recall, said Mr. Romney needed to broaden his appeal beyond Republicans to carry Wisconsin in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin, who became a champion to conservatives after fending off a recall effort last week, offered a bit of advice to Mitt Romney: Refine your economic message and give people a reason to vote for you, rather than simply against President Obama.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Should Hone Economic Message, Walker Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:33:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2555ddd7-0999-5895-97fd-79fd2845daac', 'word_count': 470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2555ddd7-0999-5895-97fd-79fd2845daac'}, {'abstract': 'The lack of indoor toilets in India not only poses health and sanitation problems, but also exposes a double standard that works against women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/world/asia/in-mumbai-a-campaign-against-restroom-injustice.html', 'snippet': 'The lack of indoor toilets in India not only poses health and sanitation problems, but also exposes a double standard that works against women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI, India — Men and women here in India’s largest city, a congested, humanity-soaked metropolis of roughly 20 million residents, would seem bound by at least one common misery: far too many people sharing far too few toilets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/asia/15india-photo/15india-photo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Mumbai, a Campaign Against Restroom Injustice', 'kicker': 'Mumbai Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In India, a Fight Against Restroom Injustice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bathrooms and Toilets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:33:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e24cd96b-19a2-5371-9c7d-6f33e83750ef', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e24cd96b-19a2-5371-9c7d-6f33e83750ef'}, {'abstract': 'The selection and duties of board members of the Fed’s regional banks leave too much room for the appearance, if not reality, of conflicts of interest, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/an-institutional-flaw-at-the-heart-of-the-federal-reserve/', 'snippet': 'The selection and duties of board members of the Fed’s regional banks leave too much room for the appearance, if not reality, of conflicts of interest, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson is the Ronald A. Kurtz Professor of Entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Institutional Flaw at the Heart of the Federal Reserve', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bollinger, Lee C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geithner, Timothy F', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve Bank of New York', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T15:37:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/612dec7a-c724-5910-b7c6-bf00d306fca4', 'word_count': 2368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/612dec7a-c724-5910-b7c6-bf00d306fca4'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Cruise stars in “Rock of Ages,” a musical, based on the Broadway show, set in the 1980s and featuring rock songs of the time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/movies/review-rock-of-ages-a-musical-starring-tom-cruise.html', 'snippet': 'Tom Cruise stars in “Rock of Ages,” a musical, based on the Broadway show, set in the 1980s and featuring rock songs of the time.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Rock of Ages,” a jukebox musical turned junky big-screen attraction about making it in the music biz back when it still existed, is just entertaining enough to keep you from dark thoughts about the state of Hollywood. The movie is too insipid for such hand wringing, in any event, and the attention-grabbing turns by Alec Baldwin, Russell Brand and especially Tom Cruise as a rock-star crazy help enliven its overlong two hours. All singing, some dancing, the movie brings to mind “Glee,” but its truer, superior progenitor is that 1933 Cinderella story, “42nd Street,” the one in which the producer tells the chorine, “You’re going out a youngster, but you’ve got to come back a star!” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/movies/15rock-span/15rock-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/movies/15rock-span/15rock-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight':