ure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ffd4782-22c2-556e-80ac-12976edd06dd', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ffd4782-22c2-556e-80ac-12976edd06dd'}, {'abstract': 'Newt Gingrich wants to help middle-class candidates by getting rid of the $2500 cap on direct donations.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/let-them-give-millions/', 'snippet': 'Newt Gingrich wants to help middle-class candidates by getting rid of the $2500 cap on direct donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Newt Gingrich has long been a font of bad ideas, and ideas that don’t make any sense. Lately he’s been churning out bad ideas that, simultaneously, don’t make any sense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Let Them Give Millions', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T16:50:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0896286e-23f5-5c19-bbe7-80c51cb74f2e', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0896286e-23f5-5c19-bbe7-80c51cb74f2e'}, {'abstract': 'New York chefs, restaurateurs, food suppliers and industry executives have joined the effort to lobby state leaders to ban a process known as hydraulic fracking.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/restaurant-industry-moves-against-gas-drilling/', 'snippet': 'New York chefs, restaurateurs, food suppliers and industry executives have joined the effort to lobby state leaders to ban a process known as hydraulic fracking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Restaurant industry opposition to the controversial gas-drilling method known as hydraulic fracturing is growing as increasing numbers of high-profile New York chefs, restaurateurs, food suppliers and industry executives have joined the effort to lobby Gov. Andrew M. Cuomo, the State Legislature and the State Department of Environmental Conservation to ban the process. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Industry Moves Against Gas Drilling', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T16:50:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85ec890d-db45-59b6-8b56-b6d19226a68b', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85ec890d-db45-59b6-8b56-b6d19226a68b'}, {'abstract': 'Nathan Lane, now in “The Iceman Cometh” in Chicago, and Laurie Metcalf, in “Long Day’s Journey Into Night” in London, exchange e-mails about performing O’Neill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/theater/nathan-lane-and-laurie-metcalf-on-acting-in-oneill.html', 'snippet': 'Nathan Lane, now in “The Iceman Cometh” in Chicago, and Laurie Metcalf, in “Long Day’s Journey Into Night” in London, exchange e-mails about performing O’Neill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN two time zones on two continents, the actors Nathan Lane and Laurie Metcalf have been taking on formidable roles that sit at the center of the American theatrical canon. Mr. Lane, a two-time Tony winner and beloved musical-comedy star, was Theodore Hickman, known as Hickey, the hardware salesman who strips away the illusions that sustain the seedy New York bar dwellers in Eugene O’Neill’s “Iceman Cometh” at the Goodman Theater in Chicago. Ms. Metcalf, who earned some of the best reviews of her career in “The Other Place” last year Off Broadway, is the morphine-addicted matriarch Mary Tyrone in O’Neill’s “Long Day’s Journey into Night” at the Apollo Theater in London. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 615, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17ONEILL_SPAN/17ONEILL_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 90, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Journeys Into O’Neill, via E-Mail', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Journeys Into O’Neill, Via E-Mail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Iceman Cometh (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lane, Nathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Metcalf, Laurie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Long Day's Journey Into Night (Play)", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Eugene", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T16:52:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4caae6df-be95-5746-b56a-99120ddfa982', 'word_count': 2059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4caae6df-be95-5746-b56a-99120ddfa982'}, {'abstract': 'The prisonlike conditions on Kabul bases often drive service members to extremes to escape the pressure and keep up their spirits. Sometimes that escape is a plate of French cheese.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/the-best-and-worst-in-kabul-military-dining/', 'snippet': 'The prisonlike conditions on Kabul bases often drive service members to extremes to escape the pressure and keep up their spirits. Sometimes that escape is a plate of French cheese.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve risked my life in Afghanistan for a plate of French cheese. While not as arduous as serving in rural Afghanistan, the prisonlike conditions on Kabul bases — no family, long hours, repetitive food and confined spaces — often drive service members to extremes to escape the pressure and keep up their spirits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best, and Worst, in Kabul Military Dining', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Bases and Installations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Security Assistance Force', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T16:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Sand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a5c805a-b290-52ed-9fbe-8ef121fe43e2', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a5c805a-b290-52ed-9fbe-8ef121fe43e2'}, {'abstract': 'The designers Peter Pilotto and Christopher De Vos told a strong story through embellishments and exquisite fabrics this season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/just-one-look-peter-pilotto/', 'snippet': 'The designers Peter Pilotto and Christopher De Vos told a strong story through embellishments and exquisite fabrics this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having found inspiration in the medieval prints of 16th-century illuminated manuscripts, designers Peter Pilotto and Christopher De Vos told a strong story through embellishments (beadwork and 3-D embroidery) and exquisite fabrics (polyamide mesh, silk cloque and mikados) this season. Here, a tailored jacket with a multicolor geometric print builds upon the shapes and silhouette of the electric blue sheath dress beneath, making dressing by numbers infinitely more fun.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Peter Pilotto', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T17:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a92693b9-1998-5d6c-a1b5-d8708dd03f29', 'word_count': 71, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a92693b9-1998-5d6c-a1b5-d8708dd03f29'}, {'abstract': 'Although a guest of a tenant is accused of setting a 2010 fire in Bensonhurst, the landlords knew that the building had been illegally subdivided and shared blame for the deaths, prosecutors said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/nyregion/manslaughter-charges-for-landlords-in-brooklyn-fire-that-killed-5.html', 'snippet': 'Although a guest of a tenant is accused of setting a 2010 fire in Bensonhurst, the landlords knew that the building had been illegally subdivided and shared blame for the deaths, prosecutors said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The landlords of an illegally subdivided apartment building in Brooklyn, where five Guatemalan immigrants died in a 2010 fire, were arraigned Thursday on manslaughter charges. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source