de Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Universal Music Group', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T17:36:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c822a49e-3322-5023-9df3-1f28b20ec5fb', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c822a49e-3322-5023-9df3-1f28b20ec5fb'}, {'abstract': 'Eva Moskowitz has written a book based on her experiences with the Success Academy Charter schools that is part polemic on school choice, part how-to guide and part personal memoir. It includes the tenets of what Ms. Moskowitz terms "joyful rigor."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/14/in-book-success-academy-operator-promotes-charter-schools-and-offers-advice/', 'snippet': 'Eva Moskowitz has written a book based on her experiences with the Success Academy Charter schools that is part polemic on school choice, part how-to guide and part personal memoir. It includes the tenets of what Ms. Moskowitz terms "joyful rigor....', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In New Book, Success Academy Operator Promotes Charter Schools and Offers Advice', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T17:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By KYLE SPENCER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kyle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SPENCER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/267c3212-dca7-514d-a3cd-f13a71e7f7a1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/267c3212-dca7-514d-a3cd-f13a71e7f7a1'}, {'abstract': 'Julian Assange, the WikiLeaks founder, lost his last chance in Britain to appeal a ruling ordering his extradition to Sweden to face allegations of sexual abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/world/europe/british-court-rejects-assange-appeal-to-block-extradition.html', 'snippet': 'Julian Assange, the WikiLeaks founder, lost his last chance in Britain to appeal a ruling ordering his extradition to Sweden to face allegations of sexual abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Britain’s Supreme Court on Thursday rejected a final move by the founder of WikiLeaks, Julian Assange, to reopen his appeal of a ruling ordering him extradited to Sweden to face allegations of sexual abuse and rape. In a statement, the court also ruled that he must be extradited by midnight on July 7, barring further legal intervention. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/europe/15assange/15assange-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/world/europe/15assange/15assange-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/europe/15assange/15assange-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/europe/15assange/15assange-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail',