atrix,” 30-foot-long work by Keith Haring that is part of an exhibition of his art at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/arts/design/keith-harings-work-at-the-brooklyn-museum.html', 'snippet': 'A closer look at “Matrix,” 30-foot-long work by Keith Haring that is part of an exhibition of his art at the Brooklyn Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KEITH HARING’S ebullient, graffiti-based work epitomized an entire strain of 1980s art. His inspiration came from the street and from comic books, not from museums, and it burst onto the scene alongside that of similarly minded peers like Kenny Scharf and Jean-Michel Basquiat.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17HARING1_SPAN/17HARING1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17HARING1_SPAN/17HARING1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17HARING1_SPAN/17HARING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17HARING1_SPAN/17HARING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17HARING1_SPAN/17HARING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17HARING1_SPAN/17HARING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}