l that would allow restaurants to start serving diners at sidewalk tables at 10 a.m., two hours earlier than the law permits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making New York Safe for Brunch', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T18:26:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e8ad97a-7c2a-586c-9d70-53d88ab0a655', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e8ad97a-7c2a-586c-9d70-53d88ab0a655'}, {'abstract': 'Ellen Pao’s lawyer says she wants to wage her sex discrimination case against the venerable Silicon Valley venture capital firm Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers in a “public forum” and opposes an arbitration.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/lawyers-for-discrimination-plaintiff-vow-to-fight-venture-firm-in-public-forum/', 'snippet': 'Ellen Pao’s lawyer says she wants to wage her sex discrimination case against the venerable Silicon Valley venture capital firm Kleiner Perkins Caufield & Byers in a “public forum” and opposes an arbitration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re not going away quietly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/22/technology/22bits-pao/22bits-pao-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/22/technology/22bits-pao/22bits-pao-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyers for Discrimination Plaintiff Vow to