 cities around the globe over time. The result is an interesting historical atlas of the rise ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can learn a lot about the world from Wikipedia, sometimes without reading the articles.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/technology/14bits-wikipedia/14bits-wikipedia-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/14/technology/14bits-wikipedia/14bits-wikipedia-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 118, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Big Data Sees Wikipedia', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mapping The World Via Wikipedia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crowdsourcing (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T18:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2d3a12a-1267-5c37-9850-87417c46b883', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2d3a12a-1267-5c37-9850-87417c46b883'}, {'abstract': 'Stores were looted and homes abandoned in Al Heffa, besieged for days by Syrian forces, and the smell of death hung in the air, said United Nations monitors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/world/middleeast/monitors-report-vast-devastation-in-syrian-village.html', 'snipp