79-b6b4-00d4af011e4e'}, {'abstract': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Thursday’s selection includes Amazon Publishing selling e-books in other digital bookstores, an excerpt from a book about the hacker group Anonymous and a drawing game that uses face tracking.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/todays-scuttlebot-anonymous-attack-and-facebook-decisions/', 'snippet': 'The technology reporters and editors of The New York Times scour the Web for important and peculiar items. Thursday’s selection includes Amazon Publishing selling e-books in other digital bookstores, an excerpt from a book about the hacker group A...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some interesting items that the tech reporters and editors of The New York Times found on the Web on Thursday. See more here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: Anonymous Attack and Facebook Decisions', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T20:59:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11827ba9-428d-50e8-8d6e-826c8c910251', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11827ba9-428d-50e8-8d6e-826c8c910251'}, {'abstract': 'Broad porcelain-blue brush strokes, ceramic-colored prints and, for diversity’s sake, polka dots — took center stage this season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/just-one-look-missoni-2/', 'snippet': 'Broad porcelain-blue brush strokes, ceramic-colored prints and, for diversity’s sake, polka dots — took center stage this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Angela Missoni looked to Chinese and British pottery for this resort season, leaving the Italian brand’s famous zigzags in the back seat (except on swimwear). Broad porcelain-blue brush strokes, ceramic-colored prints and, for diversity’s sake, polka dots — took center stage instead. Missoni also dipped its feet in more feminine silhouettes: busy printed pieces cut in A-line skirts like this one, paired with a fitted tee, got a cinch at the waistline with a wide (also printed) belt. The wedge bootie ends the sentence affirmatively.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Missoni', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Missoni, Angela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/161d5923-f4ce-5b04-8b5d-c6f1797709fd', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/161d5923-f4ce-5b04-8b5d-c6f1797709fd'}, {'abstract': 'In the Never-Never Land that is the international art world, there is a conspicuous display of disposable income.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/design/large-works-and-big-changes-at-art-basel.html', 'snippet': 'In the Never-Never Land that is the international art world, there is a conspicuous display of disposable income.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BASEL, Switzerland — The day before the invitation-only opening of Art Basel, scores of collectors and dealers gathered in the cavernous building that houses Art Unlimited, the annual show of super-size artworks. Word had spread quickly about an extraordinary photo-realist painting by the Italian-born artist Rudolf Stingel. Based on a 1980s photograph of the New York dealer Paula Cooper looking glamorous with sultry eyes and a cigarette in one hand, the large canvas (it measures 11 by 15 feet) was hung dramatically in a space by itself. Its price was around $3 million, and it was bought by François Pinault, the French luxury goods magnate and owner of Christie’s, before the fair even opened.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15VOGEL_SPAN/15VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15VOGEL_SPAN/15VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'super