complish all of this without being especially interesting. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15YOURSISTER_SPAN/15YOURSISTER_SPAN-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Solitary Retreat to a Remote Island Leads to Many Mix-Ups', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Solitary Retreat to a Remote Island Leads to Many Mix-Ups', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shelton, Lynn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeWitt, Rosemarie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blunt, Emily', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duplass, Mark', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:07:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e4c6d66-8d42-544b-af1f-ed688737fbcc', 'word_count': 678, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e4c6d66-8d42-544b-af1f-ed688737fbcc'}, {'abstract': 'The Iranians have managed to steadily increase their enrichment of uranium and are now producing a concentrated form close to bomb grade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/sunday-review/irans-high-card-at-the-nuclear-negotiation-table.html', 'snippet': 'The Iranians have managed to steadily increase their enrichment of uranium and are now producing a concentrated form close to bomb grade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE rising hostilities against Iran and its atomic complex — assassinations and cyberattacks, trade bans and oil embargoes, frozen assets and banking prohibitions, among other acts open and covert — have clearly done much to bring Tehran back to negotiations, which are to resume Monday. But the drama has also tended to overshadow a central fact: the Iranians have managed to steadily increase their enrichment of uranium and are now raising their production of a concentrated form close to bomb grade.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s High Card at the Nuclear Table', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran’s High Card at the Nuclear Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uranium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:08:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By William J. Broad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Broad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d46fb07-8cae-5814-b72c-e82899cdb420', 'word_count': 1089, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d46fb07-8cae-5814-b72c-e82899cdb420'}, {'abstract': 'One of the earliest churches in the Roman Forum has been partially restored and is scheduled to reopen for tour groups in September.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/design/roman-forum-church-santa-maria-antiqua.html', 'snippet': 'One of the earliest churches in the Roman Forum has been partially restored and is scheduled to reopen for tour groups in September.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — By the eighth century one of the earliest churches in Rome was considered quaint enough to be called Santa Maria Antiqua. The Latin name is still painted amid tiers of haloed saints in murals in the cavernous brick church, which has been largely inaccessible since 1980 on a dusty side path in the Forum.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN/15ANTIQUES1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ancient Church in Rome, Restored and Imagined', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ancient Church in Rome, Restored and Imagined', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bethel Woods Center for the Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Posters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:10:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59d277c9-21f1-5db1-80f5-397fd8fa84e0', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59d277c9-21f1-5db1-80f5-397fd8fa84e0'}, {'abstract': 'David Maraniss’s book minutely traces Barack Obama’s African and American lineages back for more than a century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/books/review/barack-obama-by-david-maraniss.html', 'snippet': 'David Maraniss’s book minutely traces Barack Obama’s African and American lineages back for more than a century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his 2008 campaign, Barack Obama so often stressed the improbability of his story that we have grown inured to how unlikely it really is. Everyone knows that his name, along with his inexperience, was an electoral handicap; that his mixed-race background made his victory historic; and that his transformation within five years from local Illinois politician to the most famous person on earth (and first incumbent president since Woodrow Wilson to win the Nobel Peace Prize) has no obvious parallel. The great virtue of David Maraniss’s huge and absorbing new biography is to demonstrate that Obama’s saga in its full and previously unexplored detail is more surprising and gripping than the version the world is familiar with.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1613, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17Fallows/17Fallows-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Making of the President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Families', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Barack Obama: The Story (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maraniss, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:13:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk':