bstract': 'With its banks heavily exposed to Greek debt, the country is nervously watching Greece’s crisis unfold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/business/global/cyprus-weighs-european-bailout-or-loan-from-russia.html', 'snippet': 'With its banks heavily exposed to Greek debt, the country is nervously watching Greece’s crisis unfold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senior officials of Cyprus said Thursday that the government could seek a European Union bailout to support its struggling banks in the coming days and at the latest by the end of the month, even as they indicated the country was continuing to pursue other options, including a possible bilateral loan from Russia. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cyprus Weighs Russian Loan or a Bailout From Europe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cyprus Weighs Russian Loan Or a Bailout From Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cyprus Popular Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cyprus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:14:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bda7469c-4908-5cef-9e08-b7a6ea64e14f', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bda7469c-4908-5cef-9e08-b7a6ea64e14f'}, {'abstract': 'When a child’s absorbed by a gadget during a family visit, there’s nothing wrong with asking the parent to help her turn it off.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/when-friends-visit-the-ipod-goes-off/', 'snippet': 'When a child’s absorbed by a gadget during a family visit, there’s nothing wrong with asking the parent to help her turn it off.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s quandary: “Yesterday,” R. wrote, “my 6-year-old child and the rest of our family visited another family with a child (also 6) who spent the whole time on an iPod Touch.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Friends Visit, the iPod Goes Off', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d1d62b2-0706-5914-86d3-b4f124e8e637', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d1d62b2-0706-5914-86d3-b4f124e8e637'}, {'abstract': '“Orient-Occident: A Dialogue of Souls” explored interactions among 14th- and 15th-century musicians of Arab cultures, including Sephardic Jews, and those of Christian Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/music/jordi-savalls-orient-occident-at-metropolitan-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Orient-Occident: A Dialogue of Souls” explored interactions among 14th- and 15th-century musicians of Arab cultures, including Sephardic Jews, and those of Christian Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Demonstrating the ways music has created connections among disparate cultures has become a minor industry within the classical concert world. Yo-Yo Ma’s Silk Road Project has ranged freely through musical history, reviving ancient works and commissioning new ones. Early-music specialists like Joel Cohen and Jordi Savall have taken a more scholarly but equally lively approach, and Mr. Savall’s offerings have been particularly ambitious. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/15JORDI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/15JORDI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/SUBJORDI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/SUBJORDI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/15JORDI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/15JORDI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15JORDI_SPAN/15JORDI_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 99, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Building East-West Bridges in Tune', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Building East-West Bridges in Tune', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Museum of Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savall, Jordi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:18:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4effeddf-0619-5308-ad09-eaebac0807c3', 'word_count': 514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4effeddf-0619-5308-ad09-eaebac0807c3'}, {'abstract': 'The young performer Alex Getlin sang on Monday night about ambition, determination and big dreams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/music/alex-getlin-18-performs-at-feinsteins-at-loews-regency.html', 'snippet': 'The young performer Alex Getlin sang on Monday night about ambition, determination and big dreams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It always gives me pause when great expectations are heaped on a teenage performer, no matter how talented. The temptation for the singer is to swallow the hype and breathlessly await the imminent glory predicted by pundits. But it should be remembered that over the last 50 years scores of baby Barbra Streisands have been promised show business conquests that haven’t materialized. And as 18-year-old Alex Getlin, a confident, engaging young Broadway-style singer with a big voice performed her show, “You’re Gonna Hear From Me,” on Monday evening at Feinstein’s at Loews Regency, I worried.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Songs of Innocence and Aspiration', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Songs of Innocence and Aspiration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/528d693f-5d3f-5943-a74d-64340efce624', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/528d693f-5d3f-5943-a74d-64340efce624'}, {'abstract': '“The Chaperone,” by Laura Moriarty, is a fictionalized account of Louise Brooks’s teenage summer in New York with a woman Ms. Moriarty has named Cora Carlisle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/books/the-chaperone-by-laura-moriarty.html', 'snippet': '“The Chaperone,” by Laura Moriarty, is a fictionalized account of Louise Brooks’s teenage summer in New York with a woman Ms. Moriarty has named Cora Carlisle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Louise Brooks, the queen of silent-movie flappers, was a wicked little minx of 15, she traveled from Wichita, Kan., to New York City to study modern dance. It was the summer of 1922, and she was accompanied by Alice Mills, who Louise would later describe as “a stocky, bespectacled housewife of 36.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15BOOK/JPBOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 732, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15BOOK/JPBOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1463, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15BOOK/15BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15BOOK/15BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15BOOK/15BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guiding a Future Star, but Finding Her Own Shine', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Guiding a Future Star, but Finding Her Own Shine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Louise', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moriarty, Laura', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:20:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0262b6d-3569-51a6-be2e-548c2cdfc736', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0262b6d-3569-51a6-be2e-548c2cdfc736'}, {'abstract': 'A concert on Wednesday evening featuring Philip Glass, who celebrated his 75th birthday in January, opened a three-evening benefit, with Mr. Glass playing three of his piano études.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/music/philip-glass-at-issue-project-room.html', 'snippet': 'A concert on Wednesday evening featuring Philip Glass, who celebrated his 75th birthday in January, opened a three-evening benefit, with Mr. Glass playing three of his piano études.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thematic tightness is the name of the game in classical music these days. The onus is on artists to organize events that are as satisfying for the mind as for the ear.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/15GLASS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/15GLASS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/GLASS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/GLASS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/15GLASS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/15GLASS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15GLASS_SPAN/15GLASS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Birthday Concert in Three Parts', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Birthday Concert In Three Parts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Issue Project Room', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glass, Philip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:26:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b442c53-e707-51c2-b3fa-f282cbc13081', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b442c53-e707-51c2-b3fa-f282cbc13081'}, {'abstract': 'The outlook for employment growth between now and the election is unchanged this week, Moody’s Analytics says, but next week’s data could force a revision downward.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/jobs-forecast-is-steady-but-stay-tuned/', 'snippet': 'The outlook for employment growth between now and the election is unchanged this week, Moody’s Analytics says, but next week’s data could force a revision downward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The economic data of the past week has been close enough to expectations that Moody’s Analytics, a research firm, has not changed its forecast for job growth in coming months. As it did last week, the firm forecasts an average of 157,000 net new jobs a month in the six months leading up to Election Day. But the data has been weak enough to make the Moody’s economists nervous.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jobs Forecast Is Steady, but Stay Tuned', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:27:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2b57617-f4a8-5fb3-a093-d3d45cbfb6b1', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2b57617-f4a8-5fb3-a093-d3d45cbfb6b1'}, {'abstract': 'Mathieu Demy, the son of the French filmmakers Agnès Varda and Jacques Demy, makes his feature directing debut with “Americano.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/movies/americano-by-mathieu-demy.html', 'snippet': 'Mathieu Demy, the son of the French filmmakers Agnès Varda and Jacques Demy, makes his feature directing debut with “Americano.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It would be quite possible, based on its first 10 minutes or so, to dismiss — or perhaps to celebrate — “Americano” as an exercise in cinematic nepotism. The main character, Martin, is played by Mathieu Demy, who also directed (this is his first feature) and who is the son of two great French filmmakers: Agnès Varda, the lioness of the Nouvelle Vague, and Jacques Demy, beloved by discerning romantics around the world for “The Umbrellas of Cherbourg.” Martin’s girlfriend, Claire, is played by Chiara Mastroianni, daughter of the “Umbrellas” star Catherine Deneuve and Marcello Mastroianni. When a family emergency summons Martin to Los Angeles, the first person he meets is a woman named Linda, played by Geraldine Chaplin, whose pedigree hardly needs elaboration.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/15AMERICANO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/15AMERICANO_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/americano-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/americano-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/15AMERICANO_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/15AMERICANO_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15AMERICANO_SPAN/15AMERICANO_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 107, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Slow Unraveling of Family Secrets', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Slow Unraveling of Family Secrets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Americano (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Demy, Mathieu', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayek, Salma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaplin, Geraldine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mastroianni, Chiara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:27:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/052bf1e3-c3ff-53bf-988d-35c3dd75ea8e', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/052bf1e3-c3ff-53bf-988d-35c3dd75ea8e'}, {'abstract': 'Documenta 13, the latest edition of the festival at Kassel, Germany, features a staggering array of invention and creativity, quite a bit of it art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/design/documenta-13-in-kassel-germany.html', 'snippet': 'Documenta 13, the latest edition of the festival at Kassel, Germany, features a staggering array of invention and creativity, quite a bit of it art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KASSEL, Germany — The longtime curator Carolyn Christov-Bakargiev has a lot on her mind, and she has managed to wedge