seems to be stirring in Indiana: a Senate race.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ads in Indiana Frame a Stirring Senate Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Ad Campaign: Indiana Senate Race Heats Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourdock, Richard E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:30:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/257c30a1-779c-585c-aea3-bbfba02a2ef3', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/257c30a1-779c-585c-aea3-bbfba02a2ef3'}, {'abstract': 'Burch creates the perfect look for a trip to the boulangerie in the south of France.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/just-one-look-tory-burch/', 'snippet': 'Burch creates the perfect look for a trip to the boulangerie in the south of France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tory Burch showed her resort collection in her Madison Avenue townhouse shop (near her Upper East Side home), befitting the designer’s reputation for dressing the leisure set. Burch explained that she focused on “down-to-earth fabrics, mixing brocade with a military jacket.” There were tile-print jersey dresses, traditional sun dresses in white with pintuck pleats and to-the-knee skirts (khaki with silver embellishments, brocades). “It’s how I hope I personally dress,” Burch said. Mosaic prints in sea blues were shown alongside youthful striped pencil trousers. Here, Burch pairs a brocade bandeau top in mint and gold with a military shirt and textural heavy silk skirt — the perfect look for a trip to the boulangerie in the south of France.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Tory Burch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:35:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb8aa218-97d5-57ef-8267-b5ab3a9934c6', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb8aa218-97d5-57ef-8267-b5ab3a9934c6'}, {'abstract': 'In his Cleveland speech, the president said his rival wants to move the country backwards.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/painting-romney-with-the-bush-brush/', 'snippet': 'In his Cleveland speech, the president said his rival wants to move the country backwards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mr. Obama gave a major speech in Cleveland today, by which I mean it was really long (6,607 words) and dreary. Mr. Romney spoke the day before, delivering what is now called “a prebuttal,” which is sort of like a Star Wars prequel, but just not as interesting or well-acted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Painting Romney With the Bush Brush', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:36:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b28ebc94-23c3-5671-ba4f-4f94eda08718', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b28ebc94-23c3-5671-ba4f-4f94eda08718'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Kiwanuka, who played the Highline Ballroom on Wednesday, offered doubt, prayers and pilgrimages, all within a gentle vamp.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/music/michael-kiwanuka-at-the-highline-ballroom.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Kiwanuka, who played the Highline Ballroom on Wednesday, offered doubt, prayers and pilgrimages, all within a gentle vamp.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soothing, swaying tunes hold despair and a quest for faith in the songs of Michael Kiwanuka, who performed at the Highline Ballroom on Wednesday night.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15HIGHLINE1_SPAN/15HIGHLINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15HIGHLINE1_SPAN/15HIGHLINE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, '