ea8-50cc55ea93ea', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60f27c23-b03c-5fb2-aea8-50cc55ea93ea'}, {'abstract': 'The choral ensemble Blue Heron performed Spanish Renaissance settings of the text of the “Song of Songs.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/arts/music/blue-heron-at-st-ignatius-of-antioch.html', 'snippet': 'The choral ensemble Blue Heron performed Spanish Renaissance settings of the text of the “Song of Songs.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ancient Hebrew love poem called the “Song of Songs” has long been interpreted as a religious allegory and incorporated by Jews and Christians into scripture. In the program notes that accompanied Blue Heron’s concert on Sunday afternoon, Scott Metcalfe, the music director of this excellent Renaissance choral ensemble based in Boston, writes that for those who read the poem from a secular viewpoint, it is clearly about an amorous young couple.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15HERONALT_SPAN/15HERONALT_ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15HERONALT_SPAN/15HERONALT_ALT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15HERONALT_SPAN/HERONALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15HERONALT_SPAN/HERONALT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15H