'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weems, Carrie Mae', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALLEN, GERI', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97e68fe9-5cb8-5e8a-8afc-8c9ad7d6c4ca', 'word_count': 1479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97e68fe9-5cb8-5e8a-8afc-8c9ad7d6c4ca'}, {'abstract': 'The absence of a roof on Arthur Ashe Stadium has been a pressing topic for the past few years as rain delays have created havoc in the United States Open schedule.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/response-to-u-s-t-a-renovations-wheres-the-roof/', 'snippet': 'The absence of a roof on Arthur Ashe Stadium has been a pressing topic for the past few years as rain delays have created havoc in the United States Open schedule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After the United States Tennis Association revealed a renovation plan to the Billie Jean King National Tennis Center that will include a new Louis Armstrong Stadium, a new Grandstand court, improved pedestrian walkways and a two-story viewing platform that will make it easier to watch players practice, the reaction focused on what the project does not include: a roof.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Response to U.S.T.A. Renovations: Where’s the Roof?', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ashe, Arthur, Stadium', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Tennis Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Tennis Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:54:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naila-Jean Meyers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naila-jean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meyers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/191eb139-8973-5c61-a30d-9dabee751862', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/191eb139-8973-5c61-a30d-9dabee751862'}, {'abstract': 'The Tony-winning revival will begin a national tour in October.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/anything-goes-will-be-gone-from-broadway-on-aug-5/', 'snippet': 'The Tony-winning revival will begin a national tour in October.', 'lead_paragraph': '6:34 p.m. | Updated  The Tony-winning revival of “Anything Goes” will close on August 5, five weeks earlier than planned but after a 565-performance run that was extended three times. And “The Lyons,” Nicky Silver’s caustic comedy of family dysfunction, will close at the Cort Theater on July 1.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Anything Goes’ and ‘The Lyons’ to Close', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Footnote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Anything Goes (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roundabout Theater Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T21:56:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Heller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de43c31d-1156-5048-9e91-d785d0a6078e', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de43c31d-1156-5048-9e91-d785d0a6078e'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of illustrations from The One-Page Magazine, at a size larger than you can see them in print.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/the-rented-guinea-pig-and-other-snippets-from-the-one-page-magazine/', 'snippet': 'A selection of illustrations from The One-Page Magazine, at a size larger than you can see them in print.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week, we commission several spot illustrations for\xa0The One-Page Magazine. Because it has\xa0so much going on, the images usually end up being quite small. To commemorate the six-month anniversary of the page (which was last month), here is a belated look back at some of the more compelling illustrations, at sizes larger than you get to see in print.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Rented Guinea Pig and Other Snippets From The One-Page Magazine', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T22:08:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Drea Zlanabitnig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Drea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zlanabitnig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63075d72-fee8-5ca9-ad38-d799eb6493c9', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63075d72-fee8-5ca9-ad38-d799eb6493c9'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel L. Swarns tells the story of several generations of Michelle Obama’s family in a book that reads like a panorama of black life in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/books/review/american-tapestry-by-rachel-l-swarns.html', 'snippet': 'Rachel L. Swarns tells the story of several generations of Michelle Obama’s family in a book that reads like a panorama of black life in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twelve presidents were slaveholders, and perhaps another dozen (including the two named George Bush) came from families that once upon a time owned slaves. In common with many of our most venerable institutions, the presidency has ample connection to “slavery time”: the White House is like an Internet link that, if you click on it, bounces you to the lawn of a plantation.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17ball-img/17ball-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17ball-img/17ball-img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 843, 'width': 964, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17ball-img/17ball-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17ball-img/17ball-img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/books/review/17ball-img/17ball-img-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The First Lady’s Family', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Families', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swarns, Rachel L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T22:11:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Ball', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ball', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb80667f-f276-59ea-b8de-6751807c326b', 'word_count': 1353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb80667f-f276-59ea-b8de-6751807c326b'}, {'abstract': 'Susan Mosakowski’s “Escape” follows three pairs of people in an apartment building, with everyone looking for a measure of liberation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/theater/reviews/escape-by-susan-mosakowski-at-la-mama.html', 'snippet': 'Susan Mosakowski’s “Escape” follows three pairs of people in an apartment building, with everyone looking for a measure of liberation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Escape,” a new play by Susan Mosakowski, follows three eccentric pairs of neighbors, all of whom are seeking some form of liberation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/15STAGEROUNDUP4_SPAN/15STAGEROUNDUP4_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':