ling pharmacies into Medicaid managed care.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/us/texas-medicaid-overhaul-means-pain-for-some-pharmacists.html', 'snippet': 'Independent drugstores are raising questions about the state’s effort to save tens of millions of dollars by rolling pharmacies into Medicaid managed care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long after the state rolled pharmacies into Medicaid managed care in March — an effort to save tens of millions of dollars a year — Ronald Barrett noticed something unusual at his store, Oak Cliff Pharmacy in southern Dallas. When he entered a child’s prescription into his computer to see how much he would be reimbursed by CVS Caremark, the managed care plan’s pharmacy benefit manager, he got an error message. A phone call indicated that the prescription had already been filled, at a CVS pharmacy down the road. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/us/15TTMedicaid1/15TTMedicaid1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Some Druggists, Medicaid Changes Mean Pain', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune | Bitter Pills', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Some Druggists, Medicaid Changes Mean Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CVS Caremark Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugstores', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T23:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Becca Aaronson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Becca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aaronson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dd72b8d-1a89-5c96-962d-e73a97ea301e', 'word_count': 1111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dd72b8d-1a89-5c96-962d-e73a97ea301e'}, {'abstract': 'The author, a native of Mumbai studying at New York University, writes that her dreams of unlimited freedom were brought to earth by the realization that “real life isn’t set to music.”', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/14/the-heady-rush-of-freedom-in-college-and-how-to-manage-it/', 'snippet': 'The author, a native of Mumbai studying at New York University, writes that her dreams of unlimited freedom were brought to earth by the realization that “real life isn’t set to music.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ariha Setalvad, who is studying journalism and psychology as an undergraduate at New York University, was raised in India and graduated from B.D. Somani International School in Mumbai. She is a summer intern on The Choice blog.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Heady Rush’ of Freedom in College, and How to Manage It', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T23:30:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ariha Setalvad', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ariha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Setalvad', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf2f857c-17e5-513e-a47b-fe932a43e8e5', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf2f857c-17e5-513e-a47b-fe932a43e8e5'}, {'abstract': 'In theory and practice, the system for disciplining teachers and administrators for sexual misconduct is a recipe for disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/opinion/give-new-york-citys-public-schools-the-power-to-punish.html', 'snippet': 'In theory and practice, the system for disciplining teachers and administrators for sexual misconduct is a recipe for disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SINCE November, when the investigation into sexual abuse at Penn State University dominated the news, the nation’s attention has repeatedly turned to such abuse in schools. Similar allegations followed at Syracuse University and in many athletic programs in schools across the United States.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Give Schools the Power to Punish', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Give Schools the Power to Punish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARBITRATION, CONCILIATION AND MEDIATION', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-14T23:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dennis M. Walcott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dennis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d210e11c-e10e-5a1f-b7bd-a96fcd95c820', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d210e11c-e10e-5a1f-b7bd-a96fcd95c820'}, {'abstract': 'When a gay candidate and a candidate who favors decriminalizing marijuana won primaries last month, some took it as a sign that El Paso was turning progressive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/us/wins-by-orourke-and-gonzalez-provide-test-for-el-paso.html', 'snippet': 'When a gay candidate and a candidate who favors decriminalizing marijuana won primaries last month, some took it as a sign that El Paso was turning progressive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ahead of the state’s May 29 primary, Beto O’Rourke, a Democratic candidate in Congressional District 16, wanted to talk about something other 