urist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece to Tourists: Keep Coming', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T10:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86ebf0eb-0c6c-5360-8162-a03873bc2eb3', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86ebf0eb-0c6c-5360-8162-a03873bc2eb3'}, {'abstract': 'How the world’s most powerful drug traffickers run their billion-dollar business.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/magazine/how-a-mexican-drug-cartel-makes-its-billions.html', 'snippet': 'How the world’s most powerful drug traffickers run their billion-dollar business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One afternoon last August, at a hospital on the outskirts of Los Angeles, a former beauty queen named Emma Coronel gave birth to a pair of heiresses. The twins, who were delivered at 3:50 and 3:51, respectively, stand to inherit some share of a fortune that Forbes estimates is worth a billion dollars. Coronel’s husband, who was not present for the birth, is a legendary tycoon who overcame a penurious rural childhood to establish a wildly successful multinational business. If Coronel elected to leave the entry for “Father” on the birth certificates blank, it was not because of any dispute over patrimony. More likely, she was just skittish about the fact that her husband, Joaquín Guzmán, is the C.E.O. of Mexico’s Sinaloa cartel, a man the Treasury Department recently described as the world’s most powerful drug trafficker. Guzmán’s organization is responsible for as much as half of the illegal narcotics imported into the United States from Mexico each year; he may well be the most-wanted criminal in this post-Bin Laden world. But his bride is a U.S. citizen with no charges against her. So authorities could only watch as she bundled up her daughters and slipped back across the border to introduce them to their dad.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '36', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 564, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 564}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/magazine/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0/17cartel_ss-slide-PJX0-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cocaine Incorporated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Snow Kings of Mexico', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Customs and Border Protection (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guzman Loera, Joaquin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinaloa Cartel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smuggling', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zetas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Radden Keefe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': 'Radden', 'lastname': 'Keefe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32ccbfb2-3646-5160-8dc1-e16055d83b13', 'word_count': 7641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32ccbfb2-3646-5160-8dc1-e16055d83b13'}, {'abstract': 'Urbane Apartments’ rental fees are among the highest per square foot in the Detroit area.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/how-a-detroit-landlord-made-his-properties-hot/', 'snippet': 'Urbane Apartments’ rental fees are among the highest per square foot in the Detroit area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As we all know, Detroit has taken some hits during the economic downturn. But residents like Eric Brown, a real estate developer, are fighting back. The president of Urbane Apartments, Mr. Brown used his social media savvy to turn his Motor City apartment complexes into attractive locations for young professionals. He has built an online community and made Urbane Apartments a hub for all things cool and fun in Detroit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Detroit Landlord Made His Properties Hot', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T11:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melinda F. Emerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melinda', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Emerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69094318-482a-598a-ae9d-1dc29a344eec', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69094318-482a-598a-ae9d-1dc29a344eec'}, {'abstract': 'People in the developed world are more likely to say that China is the world’s leading economic power, whereas people in the developing world — and the Chinese — are more likely to say the United States is.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/putting-chinas-economic-power-in-perspective/', 'snippet': 'People in the developed world are more likely to say that China is the world’s leading economic power, whereas people in the developing world — and the Chinese — are more likely to say the United States is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In January, David Leonhardt noted a finding that more Americans said China was the world’s leading superpower than said the United States was. New global survey data from Pew Research Center suggests this view is becoming more widespread around the world — although, tellingly, not in China itself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting China’s Economic Power in Perspective', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T11:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89754cdf-9a6b-5d07-8f4c-87b90daf9fc5', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89754cdf-9a6b-5d07-8f4c-87b90daf9fc5'}, {'abstract': 'As the nation’s economy settles into a slump, the campaign speeches have, too.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/singular-focus-on-the-economy-leads-to-one-note-campaigns/', 'snippet': 'As the nation’s economy settles into a slump, the campaign speeches have, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWS FLASH! Mitt Romney thinks President Obama has failed to deliver the economic recovery Americans deserve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Singular Focus on the Economy Leads to One-Note Campaigns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T11:32:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5e6712e-1ec2-573a-86b2-76d0fd6f0b6d', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5e6712e-1ec2-573a-86b2-76d0fd6f0b6d'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/morning-take-out-506/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': No