 was wearing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shirt Off His Back', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Awaking to a Masked Visitor, and Other Reader Tales', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Madison Square Park (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T12:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert H. Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93838339-9475-58c0-b2ae-26f01586244b', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93838339-9475-58c0-b2ae-26f01586244b'}, {'abstract': 'The jailing of a Venezuelan judge has further undermined the Chávez government’s claim to democratic legitimacy.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/chavez-does-not-let-the-law-get-in-his-way/', 'snippet': 'The jailing of a Venezuelan judge has further undermined the Chávez government’s claim to democratic legitimacy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' MONTREAL — The right to be present at your own trial is a core civil right. Certainly, article 125 of Venezuela’s criminal procedure code bans in-absentia trials. Which is why, when faced with an attempt to sentence one of his clients who was not in the courtroom, the Venezuelan defense attorney José Amalio Graterol objected forcefully and refused to participate in an obviously illegal procedure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Pantomime of Justice', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Afiuni, Maria Lourdes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T12:31:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8f54cae-e858-592c-8976-6949f244bd8e', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8f54cae-e858-592c-8976-6949f244bd8e'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese officials, bending to public pressure, have announced an investigation into the death of dissident Li Wangyang, whose body was found hanging from a hospital window this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/world/asia/china-to-investigate-death-of-labor-activist.html', 'snippet': 'Chinese officials, bending to public pressure, have announced an investigation into the death of dissident Li Wangyang, whose body was found hanging from a hospital window this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Chinese officials, bending to public pressure, have announced an investigation into the death of a veteran labor activist whose body was found hanging from a hospital window this month, days after he gave a series of interviews in which he vowed to continue fighting to end the Communist Party’s monopoly on power.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China to Investigate Death of Labor Activist', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Activist’s Death to Be Examined', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Wangyang', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T12:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99b28e9c-c555-53aa-966f-4f7dd4d76630', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99b28e9c-c555-53aa-966f-4f7dd4d76630'}, {'abstract': 'Windows 7 has more than one way to open a Jump List.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/tip-of-the-week-jumping-to-the-jump-list/', 'snippet': 'Windows 7 has more than one way to open a Jump List.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jump lists — those pop-up windows that list recently used Web sites, actions, files and folders for programs in the Windows 7 Start menu and taskbar — are easy to see with a quick right-click of the mouse on a program button. For a faster and more fluid way to open the jump list from a taskbar icon, you can also press the mouse’s left button and quickly drag the cursor in an upward motion to reveal the items on that particular jump list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Jumping to the Jump List', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wi