/cc5217c6-cd1a-5185-aeb8-71942b32c21c'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Rachel Swarns talks about Michelle Obama’s family history; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Dexter Filkins discusses Syria; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2012/06/14/books/review/17books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Rachel Swarns talks about Michelle Obama’s family history; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Dexter Filkins discusses Syria; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Rachel Swarns talks about Michelle Obama’s family history; Julie Bosman has notes from the field; Dexter Filkins discusses Syria; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Sam Tanenhaus is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Book Review Podcast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/8dcbc789-a0e7-51f2-9d3a-73eb07558056', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/8dcbc789-a0e7-51f2-9d3a-73eb07558056'}, {'abstract': 'An American group aligned with the fossil fuels industry plans counterdemonstrations on a wind-power appreciation day.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/on-our-radar-a-global-wind-day/', 'snippet': 'An American group aligned with the fossil fuels industry plans counterdemonstrations on a wind-power appreciation day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s Global Wind Day, an annual celebration coordinated by the wind industry that includes events like a photo competition, the inauguration of new wind farms and many festivals, mostly in Europe. In the United States, a group aligned with the fossil fuels industry plans counterdemonstrations to denounce the “push for expensive, inefficient and job-destroying offshore wind energy.” [Global Wind Day, Americans for Prosperity]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Global Wind Day', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ddd092cd-aa12-5135-9d68-61cdac33452d', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ddd092cd-aa12-5135-9d68-61cdac33452d'}, {'abstract': 'The party led by the jailed member of Parliament, Jagan Mohan Reddy, swept the by-polls in the southern state.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/congress-suffers-electoral-defeat-in-andhra-pradesh/', 'snippet': 'The party led by the jailed member of Parliament, Jagan Mohan Reddy, swept the by-polls in the southern state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Indian National Congress, which leads the governing coalition in New Delhi, suffered a significant electoral setback in a large southern state, Andhra Pradesh, on Friday at the hands of a breakaway political faction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Congress Suffers Electoral Defeat in Andhra Pradesh', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukherjee, Pranab', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reddy, Y S Rajasekhara', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 3, 'maj