: 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:41:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Brian', 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/0aabb767-8316-5982-9e3a-1e1a8d3938f4', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0aabb767-8316-5982-9e3a-1e1a8d3938f4'}, {'abstract': 'The second round of the United States Open was on Friday at the Olympic Club in San Francisco, and several Times contributors live blogged the day’s play, which included the exit of top-ranked golfer Luke Donald.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/live-blog-follow-second-round-action-at-the-u-s-open/', 'snippet': 'The second round of the United States Open was on Friday at the Olympic Club in San Francisco, and several Times contributors live blogged the day’s play, which included the exit of top-ranked golfer Luke Donald.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years since capturing his last major championship, Tiger Woods will enter the weekend at the Olympic Club sharing the lead at the United States Open with two other former major winners, Jim Furyk (2003 U.S. Open) and David Toms (2001 P.G.A.). The three are the only players in the field in red numbers, each at one under.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Second-Round Recap: Highlights From the U.S. Open', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fowler, Rickie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Furyk, Jim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Sergio', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ishikawa, Ryo', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Dennis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McDowell, Graeme', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McIlroy, Rory', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westwood, Lee', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Olympic Club (San Francisco, Calif)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:42:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f32262ed-d87f-5035-bed8-d88346f269db', 'word_count': 3391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f32262ed-d87f-5035-bed8-d88346f269db'}, {'abstract': 'Three New York restaurants are taking orders out front.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/summers-new-destination-the-walk-up-window/', 'snippet': 'Three New York restaurants are taking orders out front.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a suburban twist in the most urban of settings: the walk-up (or drive-up) window. At Sauce, a restaurant that opened last fall on the Lower East Side, you can saunter up and order a meal in a container after midnight, or for breakfast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer’s New Destination: The Walk-Up Window', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56650278-ce7e-5331-aaee-8d7547fae229', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56650278-ce7e-5331-aaee-8d7547fae229'}, {'abstract': 'Helen K. Kim and Noah S. Leavitt, who married after meeting in graduate school, share a scholarly interest in marriages like theirs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/us/studying-and-living-jewish-asian-intermarriage.html', 'snippet': 'Helen K. Kim and Noah S. Leavitt, who married after meeting in graduate school, share a scholarly interest in marriages like theirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One weekend night 15 years ago, a group of graduate students at the University of Chicago decided to interrupt their research long enough for a dinner party. Helen K. Kim made a chocolate tart with ginger cream filling. Her classmate Noah S. Leavitt regarded it and scoffed, “Nice use of your time, making a fancy dessert with all the homework we have.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/RELIGION/RELIGION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/RELIGION/RELIGION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/RELIGION/RELIGION-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jewish-Asian Couple’s Union Leads to a Scholarly Interest in Intermarriage', 'kicker': 'On Religion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jewish-Asian Couple’s Union Leads to a Scholarly Interest in Intermarriage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:47:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samuel G. Freedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samuel', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Freedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9790f4a7-1359-5784-b550-4220d4022434', 'word_count': 1051, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9790f4a7-1359-5784-b550-4220d4022434'}, {'abstract': 'Every week my severely overweight father would rotate to a new fad diet, and my family ended up eating whatever freeze-dried, saccharin-loaded concoction he was trying at that moment.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/growing-up-with-a-fat-dad/', 'snippet': 'Every week my severely overweight father would rotate to a new fad diet, and my family ended up eating whatever freeze-dried, saccharin-loaded concoction he was trying at that moment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up with a fat dad — 450 pounds at his heaviest. Every week he would rotate to a new fad diet, and my family ended up eating whatever freeze-dried, saccharin-loaded concoction he was trying at that moment. By the time I was 9, I was an expert on Atkins, Pritikin and Weight Watchers, just to name a few. Did I mention spending four weeks at Duke University’s “fat farm” consuming only minuscule bowls of white rice, while my 10-year-old peers were home eating ice cream cones?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Growing Up With a Fat Dad', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dad Was the Dieter, but I Was the Hungry One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:47:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dawn Lerman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dawn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lerman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/142f2fee-df9a-5f7a-8122-0fbf41fea529', 'word_count': 977, 'uri': 'nyt://article/142f2fee-df9a-5f7a-8122-0fbf41fea529'}, {'abstract': 'Muneer A. Satter, Hughes Lepic and Gerald J. Cardinale are all retiring from Goldman Sachs, according to a memo to employees.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/more-goldman-partners-head-for-the-exit/', 'snippet': 'Muneer A. Satter, Hughes Lepic and Gerald J. Cardinale are all retiring from Goldman Sachs, according to a memo to employees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Goldman Sachs employees were greeted Friday morning by a number of senior level departures. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Goldman Partners Head for the Exit', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T14:47:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e115523-5e2c-5d48-906a-7272101246cf', 'word_count': 1651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e115523-5e2c-5d48-906a-7272101246cf'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama outlined a new immigration policy under which young illegal immigrants who came to the country as children can obtain work permits and will not face deportation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/us/us-to-stop-deporting-some-illegal-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama outlined a new immigration policy under which young illegal immigrants who came to the country as children can obtain work permits and will not face deportation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of thousands of illegal immigrants who came to the United States as children will be allowed to remain in the country without fear of deportation and able to work, under an executive action the Obama administration announced on Friday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/us/politics/16obama4-span/16obama4-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 6