in Oklahoma City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/sports/basketball/in-duel-of-stars-heats-lebron-james-gains-an-early-edge.html', 'snippet': 'LeBron James and Kevin Durant have played to a virtual statistical tie in the first two games of the N.B.A. finals, but the Heat got the split they wanted in Oklahoma City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OKLAHOMA CITY — Their statistics were nearly identical, mirror images of dueling superstars in search of the slightest of edges. But as LeBron James and Kevin Durant spoke late Thursday night, it was clear that the psychology of the N.B.A. finals had been flipped in favor of the Miami Heat. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/sports/16duel1/16duel1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 861, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/sports/16duel1/16duel1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1721, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/sports/16duel1/16duel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/16/sports/16duel1/16duel1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/sports/16duel1/16duel1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Duel of Stars, Heat’s James Gains Early Edge', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Duel of Stars, Heat’s James Gains an Early Edge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durant, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:25:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Spousta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spousta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7094618-7edc-53f6-b932-0b78d4033bd6', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7094618-7edc-53f6-b932-0b78d4033bd6'}, {'abstract': 'The assignment to depict Nik Wallenda’s plan to cross high above Niagara Falls on a tightrope tonight drew many lovely submissions.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/kids-draw-the-news-nik-wallendas-big-night/', 'snippet': 'The assignment to depict Nik Wallenda’s plan to cross high above Niagara Falls on a tightrope tonight drew many lovely submissions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update: This assignment is closed. The more results can be seen here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kids Draw the News | Nik Wallenda’s Big Night', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallenda, Nik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niagara Falls (NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fb75bee-7a45-55cb-bbc4-ec6e0b855810', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fb75bee-7a45-55cb-bbc4-ec6e0b855810'}, {'abstract': 'As he begins his bus tour Friday, Mr. Romney, who has lain low and focused much of his time on fund-raising since winning the Republican nomination, now will likely be forced to wade into an issue that he had steered clear of for most of the campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/immigration-announcement-may-overshadow-romney-bus-tour/', 'snippet': 'As he begins his bus tour Friday, Mr. Romney, who has lain low and focused much of his time on fund-raising since winning the Republican nomination, now will likely be forced to wade into an issue that he had steered clear of for most of the campa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — Mitt Romney begins a five-day bus tour on Friday, during which he had hoped to make his case to small-town voters that President Obama’s economic policies are failing everyday Americans. But the Romney campaign may find it more difficult to stay on message in the wake of the Obama administration’s announcement that it would stop deporting younger immigrants who came to the United States as children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Immigration Announcement May Overshadow Romney Bus Tour', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ayotte, Kelly A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:33:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Wheaton and Michael Barbaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wheaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barbaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a12d3ed-c55f-53f4-bcf5-307069e44af2', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a12d3ed-c55f-53f4-bcf5-307069e44af2'}, {'abstract': 'Squabbling children can create a driver distraction that rivals anything a cellphone can offer. Here’s my solution; what’s yours?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/siblings-squabbling-in-the-car/', 'snippet': 'Squabbling children can create a driver distraction that rivals anything a cellphone can offer. Here’s my solution; what’s yours?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s parental quandary is mine again — or rather, one I’ve solved, at least temporarily, but one on which I thought we could all use a little good crowd-sourced advice. The problem? Children squabbling madly away in the car.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Siblings, Squabbling in the Car', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:33:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/556dfd5c-0557-5719-b0e8-05f18c3647fb', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/556dfd5c-0557-5719-b0e8-05f18c3647fb'}, {'abstract': 'London’s attempt to start a new men’s event was also unusual in that it was introduced with a party given by Prince Charles.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/prince-charles-kicks-off-london-mens-fashion-week/', 'snippet': 'London’s attempt to start a new men’s event was also unusual in that it was introduced with a party given by Prince Charles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The season of international men’s-wear fashion shows kicked off in London on Thursday, which was unusual in that London, apart from its Savile Row traditions, has more recently treated men’s wear as an afterthought when it comes to the runway. London’s attempt to start a new men’s event was also unusual in that it was introduced with a party given by Prince Charles in the State Apartments of St. James’s Palace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prince Charles Kicks Off London Men’s Fashion Week', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank