e Republican nominee, may have provided a conduit for foreign money to enter the presidential race.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McCain Says Adelson is Putting ‘Foreign Money’ Into Campaign', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing Door for Foreign Cash in Election', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:51:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcdef810-34af-509f-b0d9-ca1e91584fd7', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcdef810-34af-509f-b0d9-ca1e91584fd7'}, {'abstract': 'A collapse of the euro could derail America’s fragile recovery and doom Mr. Obama’s re-election hopes. He may be running out of time to sway the German chancellor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/world/europe/in-euro-crisis-obama-tries-to-sway-merkel.html', 'snippet': 'A collapse of the euro could derail America’s fragile recovery and doom Mr. Obama’s re-election hopes. He may be running out of time to sway the German chancellor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — At the end of a summit meeting at Camp David last month, as the other world leaders were heading for their helicopters, President Obama did what has become a habit during his years in the White House: he made time for an informal but deadly serious talk with Chancellor Angela Merkel of Germany.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/world/germany/germany-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Euro Crisis, Obama Looks to Merkel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Euro Crisis, Obama Looks to Merkel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:52:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Landler and Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Landler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/668e845a-3c99-55b1-ac68-c7fb3508e780', 'word_count': 1305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/668e845a-3c99-55b1-ac68-c7fb3508e780'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Stolz, who had retired from the agency in 1981 after failing to get a deputy director post, was called back to help repair its image.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/us/richard-f-stolz-dies-at-86-headed-cia-spy-operations-after-iran-contra.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Stolz, who had retired from the agency in 1981 after failing to get a deputy director post, was called back to help repair its image.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard F. Stolz, a career intelligence officer who was called out of retirement in 1987 to run the Central Intelligence Agency’s spying operations and cleanse its image after the Iran-contra scandal, died on June 9 in Williamsburg, Va. He was 86.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/us/16stolz1/16stolz1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/us/16stolz1/16stolz1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/us/16stolz1/16stolz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/16/us/16stolz1/16stolz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/us/16stolz1/16stolz1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Richard F. Stolz Dies at 86; Headed C.I.A. Spy Operations After Iran-Contra', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Richard F. Stolz, 86, Chief Of C.I.A. Spy Operations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stolz, Richard F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iran-Contra Affair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:55:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Denise Grady', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Denise', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grady', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbbc5c36-9812-53ab-9196-79c8a91e5a02', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbbc5c36-9812-53ab-9196-79c8a91e5a02'}, {'abstract': 'Their resort collection included reworked favorites like silk and satin midnight-blue track pants, dark knit sweaters and leather minidresses.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/just-one-look-rag-bone-2/', 'snippet': 'Their resort collection included reworked favorites like silk and satin midnight-blue track pants, dark knit sweaters and leather minidresses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Rag and Bone’s David Neville and Marcus Wainwright expand their line to include women’s bags, they’re stepping back and revisiting the essence of the brand with their clothing. In the designers’ resort collection you’ll find reworked favorites like silk and satin midnight-blue track pants, dark knit sweaters and leather minidresses. Pops of color came in floral printed pieces and gold sequined dresses and blouses. Their signature Newbury ankle boots came in perennial black, blue and brown. If you have the classic colors covered, check out the new shiny gold leather version.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Rag & Bone', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T15:57:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8add1d84-d7d0-56e2-ae7a-9a181de4c350', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8add1d84-d7d0-56e2-ae7a-9a181de4c350'}, {'abstract': 'The members of LMFAO — both descended from Berry Gordy of Motown royalty — speak of their other influences, which include (surprise) Fred Astaire, Eddie Murphy and “The Secret.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/arts/music/lmfao-speaks-about-influences.html', 'snippet': 'The members of LMFAO — both descended from Berry Gordy of Motown royalty — speak of their other influences, which include (surprise) Fred Astaire, Eddie Murphy and “The Secret.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE fun-loving pop-rock duo LMFAO have been a major presence on the Billboard charts since last year, when they released their sophomore album, “Sorry for Party Rocking” (Interscope). Spoiler: They weren’t sorry. Their single “Party Rock Anthem” was just that: an inescapably addictive soundtrack for clubs, parties, barbecues, street fairs, anywhere people gathered to have a good time. Hits like “Sexy and I Know It” became remixed staples for nightlife-worshiping fans, not least because LMFAO created dance moves along with them.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1378, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN/17PLAYLIST1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Loves DeBarge. And Fred Astaire.', 'kicker': 'Playlist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loves DeBarge. And Fred Astaire.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LMFAO', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/03212325-1af3-5b6c-a148-86c707fc7121', 'word_count': 1039, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03212325-1af3-5b6c-a148-86c707fc7121'}, {'abstract': 'The Japandroids, a Canadian garage-rock duo, have released a new album, “Celebration Rock.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/arts/music/japandroids-new-album-is-celebration-rock.html', 'snippet': 'The Japandroids, a Canadian garage-rock duo, have released a new album, “Celebration Rock.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF everything had gone according to the plan drawn up by Japandroids, they would already be long forgotten. Formed in Vancouver in 2006, this garage-rock duo had decided to call it quits in late 2008 after failing to break out of the British Columbia music scene, but not before commemorating their departure with “Post-Nothing,” a debut — and farewell — album. But after their song “Young Hearts Spark Fire” was posted by the online music publication Pitchfork in March 2009, “Post-Nothing” went from a would-be posthumous release to an industry calling card, leading to a record deal and two years of relentless touring.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/arts/17SNAPSHOT/17SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Loud Enough to Be Heard in Another Country', 'kicker': 'Snapshots | Japandroids', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loud Enough To Be Heard In Another Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music'