en-vs-england/', 'snippet': 'Live blogging the first-round match in Kiev, Ukraine, between England and Sweden in the European soccer championships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The distance between England and a European championship is vast — in real and psychic terms. But maybe, just maybe, those hurdles are not quite as high after England took the lead, lost the lead, tied the game and roared back to defeat Sweden in a Group D game in Kyiv, Ukraine, at the European Championships.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012 Highlights: Sweden (2) vs. England (3)', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hodgson, Roy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahimovic, Zlatan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rooney, Wayne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/957063a6-b028-5662-821e-0f6e3e20d5fb', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/957063a6-b028-5662-821e-0f6e3e20d5fb'}, {'abstract': 'Airport makeovers, a Niagara Falls high-wire act and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/morning-walkabout-615-airport-makeovers-and-a-niagara-falls-high-wire-act/', 'snippet': 'Airport makeovers, a Niagara Falls high-wire act and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bigger, Better Airports The biggest airports in the country —\xa0Los Angeles, Dallas, Atlanta, Chicago and the three that serve New York City have been undergoing major renovations and expansions. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Walkabout — 6/15: Airport Makeovers and a Niagara Falls High-Wire Act', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bdbe0376-612b-5eb5-9bbb-d33ae5f2bcb3', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bdbe0376-612b-5eb5-9bbb-d33ae5f2bcb3'}, {'abstract': 'Rajat K. Gupta, the retired head of the consulting firm McKinsey & Company and a former Goldman Sachs board member, is the most prominent executive convicted in the government’s sweeping investigation into insider trading on Wall Street.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/rajat-gupta-convicted-of-insider-trading/', 'snippet': 'Rajat K. Gupta, the retired head of the consulting firm McKinsey & Company and a former Goldman Sachs board member, is the most prominent executive convicted in the government’s sweeping investigation into insider trading on Wall Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rajat K. Gupta, the retired head of the consulting firm McKinsey & Company and a former Goldman Sachs board member, was found guilty on Friday of conspiracy and securities fraud for leaking boardroom secrets to a billionaire hedge fund manager.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rajat Gupta Convicted of Insider Trading', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_