ooks', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0c48a6f-2a04-5df8-acb4-d11ff227fbd2', 'word_count': 1291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0c48a6f-2a04-5df8-acb4-d11ff227fbd2'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers share their tales of following their passion for a collectible and their plans for what will happen to the collection in the future.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/keeping-a-cool-head-about-a-passion-investment/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers share their tales of following their passion for a collectible and their plans for what will happen to the collection in the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan has been writing for the last few weeks about various people who have followed their hearts and invested in everything from vineyards to baseball teams to racehorses. He raises the question in this week’s Wealth Matters column about whether decisions by these people on when to buy sell or how much to pay are any better than the decisions by people who put their money into stocks and bonds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Keeping a Cool Head About a Passion Investment', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:16:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/150e7a1f-0a00-5832-9c1c-446b8bf8fa00', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/150e7a1f-0a00-5832-9c1c-446b8bf8fa00'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/weekend-fare-97/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recognition of National Lobster Day, which is Friday, Ed’s Lobster Bar Annex, 25 Clinton Street (between East Houston and Stanton Streets), on the Lower East Side, will hold a lobster fest starting at 4:30 p.m. For $60 a person, you can taste everything from half a chilled lobster and lobster rolls to lobster-filled ravioli and tacos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:17:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d3d0715-e7f3-5e87-9273-418d17e9792b', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d3d0715-e7f3-5e87-9273-418d17e9792b'}, {'abstract': 'Some couples are opting to replace the traditional cake with another sweet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/fashion/weddings/replacing-the-cake-field-notes.html', 'snippet': 'Some couples are opting to replace the traditional cake with another sweet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KELLIE CICCONI has always been a picky eater. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xl