logs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/image-of-the-day-june-15/', 'snippet': 'Anchored fishing boats at a seashore in a village in Maharashtra.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: June 15', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boats and Boating', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monsoons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca0a9de2-b099-558b-a627-04663e98a93a', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca0a9de2-b099-558b-a627-04663e98a93a'}, {'abstract': 'Metdist, based in London and set up by Raj Bagri in 1970, could earn about £130 million, or $202 million, in the sale of London Metal Exchange to Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/little-known-firm-to-reap-millions-in-exchanges-sale/', 'snippet': 'Metdist, based in London and set up by Raj Bagri in 1970, could earn about £130 million, or $202 million, in the sale of London Metal Exchange to Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – A little-known metals trading company owned by an Indian family stands to become one of the biggest winners in London Metal Exchange’s sale to Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little-Known Firm to Reap Millions in Exchange’s Sale', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T16:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ff1e34c-5011-563f-82bf-c8676f1ba3ce', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ff1e34c-5011-563f-82bf-c8676f1ba3ce'}, {'abstract': 'Compared with the economies of other industrialized countries, the United States economy has done rather well since the depths of 2008. Only the Canadian economy has done better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/business/economy/a-slow-recovery-but-its-all-relative.html', 'snippet': 'Compared with the economies of other industrialized countries, the United States economy has done rather well since the depths of 2008. Only the Canadian economy has done better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE slow pace of the American economic recovery seems likely to be a major issue in this year’s presidential election. But by the standards of other developed countries, the United States has done rather well since the credit crisis blossomed in 2008 and sent the world into recession.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Slow Recovery in the United States, but It’s All Relative', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Slow Recovery in the United States, but It’s All Relative', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5,