attracting, like Jude Law and Judi Dench, but also its plan to keep ticket prices low.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/big-names-flock-to-michael-grandages-new-theater-company/', 'snippet': 'The new venture is notable for not only the talent it’s attracting, like Jude Law and Judi Dench, but also its plan to keep ticket prices low.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Judi Dench, Jude Law and Daniel Radcliffe will play major characters in the inaugural season of London theater from a new producing company formed by the Tony Award-wining director Michael Grandage (“Red”) and his business partner, James Bierman, who together ran the Donmar Warehouse from 2006 to 2011, according to an announcement from the two men on Thursday night. The season will include a new play, “Peter and Alice” by John Logan, the Tony-winning author of “Red,” with Ms. Dench and the actor Ben Whishaw playing the two real-life figures who inspired “Alice in Wonderland” and “Peter Pan.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Names Flock to Michael Grandage’s New Theater Company', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Names Flock To New Theater Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bierman, James', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dench, Judi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grandage, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Law, Jude', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Radcliffe, Daniel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T17:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e672ad2-2ecf-54f1-9e98-838292df6cf9', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e672ad2-2ecf-54f1-9e98-838292df6cf9'}, {'abstract': 'Wang’s collection was filled with mock croc designs, transparency and bras galore.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/just-one-look-alexander-wang-2/', 'snippet': 'Wang’s collection was filled with mock croc designs, transparency and bras galore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All you need to know about Alexander Wang’s resort collection is: mock croc (on everything from bags to puffer jackets!), transparency (in flowing paneled dresses and sturdy gossamer heeled shoes) and bras galore. This look features faux-croc track shorts and a classic knit tank, which from the front is a halter top but from the back is more of a bodysuit, with classic bra straps. Undergarments as outerwear also came in cropped corsets, spongy lime-colored compact knit tubes and new neoprene bibbed dresses. The response was supportive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Alexander Wang', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Knitting and Knit Goods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Alexander (1983- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T17:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a523ab4-5202-5ea2-8f2e-3a53782fc53b', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a523ab4-5202-5ea2-8f2e-3a53782fc53b'}, {'abstract': 'On the 17th-century Dutch craze for dollhouses.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/an-earlier-housing-bubble/', 'snippet': 'On the 17th-century Dutch craze for dollhouses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bloomberg View’s excellent economic history blog tells of an earlier housing bubble, from the same country and era that brought us tulip-mania.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Earlier Housing Bubble', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T17:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4ffd9f4-c709-507b-951e-0ed061d6d704', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4ffd9f4-c709-507b-951e-0ed061d6d704'}, {'abstract': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott debate the relative merits of museums and memorials and discuss how to best make sense of Sept. 11.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000001606862/the-sweet-spot-june-15-2012.html', 'snippet': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott debate the relative merits of museums and memorials and discuss how to best make sense of Sept. 11.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott debate the relative merits of museums and memorials and discuss how to best make sense of Sept. 11.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/15/arts/video-sweetspot-06152012/vi