hop that sat near the Guerneville 5 & 10, whose metal marquee and wooden sign made the place look like a relic from the 40s, which, in fact, it is.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17OVER3/17OVER3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Free Spirits in a Sonoma Hamlet', 'kicker': 'Overnighter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Free Spirits in a Sonoma Hamlet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sonoma County (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:41:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Marsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d4c648e-1dab-5727-9f40-9ee083e0971f', 'word_count': 1751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d4c648e-1dab-5727-9f40-9ee083e0971f'}, {'abstract': 'A formerly forlorn area of Asbury Park has emerged as a hip extension of the city’s robust cultural and culinary scene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/travel/a-jersey-shore-rebound.html', 'snippet': 'A formerly forlorn area of Asbury Park has emerged as a hip extension of the city’s robust cultural and culinary scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHILE towns along the Jersey Shore reinvented themselves during the boom of the aughts, sprouting boutique hotels and upscale restaurants, Asbury Park retained a refreshing, rare Americana charm. Restaurants — and boutique hotels — arrived, but they have had to share the Boardwalk with nostalgic attractions like a pinball museum and a psychic. And a majestic urban ghost presides over it all: the Boardwalk ends at the magnificent shell of a 1920s-era casino and carousel house. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17HEADSUP_SPAN/17HEADSUP_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jersey Shore Rebound', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Jersey Shore Rebound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Asbury Park (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:42:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Washburn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Washburn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1e183d5-a12a-530f-a512-e18dfdadee51', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1e183d5-a12a-530f-a512-e18dfdadee51'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/arts/june-17-23.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT seems that New York City abounds with free summer outdoor movie screenings nowadays, but perhaps the daddy of them all is the HBO BRYANT PARK SUMMER FILM FESTIVAL, which celebrates its 20th anniversary this year with some of its biggest hits from the past. It starts Monday with “Psycho” and concludes Aug. 20 with “Raiders of the Lost Ark,” and on Mondays in between are heavyweights like “On the Waterfront” (July 9), “All About Eve” (Aug. 13) and “The Wizard of Oz” (July 2), which, weather permitting, may well generate the season’s biggest turnout. (I remember when “Casablanca” closed the festival a few years back. Some viewers reverently whispered famous lines a moment before they were uttered on screen.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'June 17 — 23', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:42:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90a7c950-f66e-5ad4-a37e-d8a6b85c3812', 'word_count': 1604, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90a7c950-f66e-5ad4-a37e-d8a6b85c3812'}, {'abstract': 'Best known for a newly renovated architectural marvel, Brno is home to hundreds of modernist buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/travel/exploring-czech-functionalism-in-brno.html', 'snippet': 'Best known for a newly renovated architectural marvel, Brno is home to hundreds of modernist buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLAT-FACED, devoid of frills and anonymous, the synagogue stood at the end of a narrow street in the Czech city of Brno, not far from a railroad trestle where trains could be heard building speed for points farther east. Beyond the two slightly angled gray walls at either side of its four glass entry doors, the synagogue appeared remarkably plain, standing out among the neighboring buildings with an unwelcoming facade, and showing no sign of life.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/travel/17CULTURED1/17CULTURED1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Czech Trove of Minimalist Design', 'kicker': 'Cultured Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Czech Trove of Minimalist Design', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czech Republic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brno (Czech Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:42:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evan Rail', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rail', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/523e77bf-3d81-5ce9-b48c-4fa801f68438', 'word_count': 1670, 'uri': 'nyt://article/523e77bf-3d81-5ce9-b48c-4fa801f68438'}, {'abstract': 'The quail gets top billing at this new Bay Area restaurant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/travel/restaurant-report-state-bird-provisions-in-san-francisco.html', 'snippet': 'The quail gets top billing at this new Bay Area restaurant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2003, after dining at Tapawingo, in Ellsworth, Mich., the Times reporter R. W. Apple Jr. observed that it “may be the best restaurant anywhere in the country that’s a four-hour drive from the closest major city.” Mr. Apple took note of Tapawingo’s chef, Stuart Brioza, then 28, predicting that “he will be one of the best chefs in America, full stop, in just a few years.” He also lauded Tapawingo’s pastry chef, Nicole Krasinski, as an adroit match for Mr. Brioza’s “restless spontaneity.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{