cker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chicago: Radisson Blu Aqua Chicago', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'HOTELS AND MOTELS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Illinois', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:44:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven McElroy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McElroy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec31d969-ed73-5c66-9db7-1cce3c8876b6', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec31d969-ed73-5c66-9db7-1cce3c8876b6'}, {'abstract': 'A 10,882-square-foot condo overlooking Central Park with the second-highest sale price ever for a New York City apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/big-ticket-sold-for-70-million/', 'snippet': 'A 10,882-square-foot condo overlooking Central Park with the second-highest sale price ever for a New York City apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 14-room duplex penthouse apartment above the Ritz-Carlton that sold for $70 million to the casino magnate Steve Wynn was the biggest sale of the week, according to city records. It was also the second-highest price ever paid for an apartment in New York City. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | Sold for $70 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wynn, Stephen A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4891035b-8ae4-5667-9563-86412f5e7f7d', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4891035b-8ae4-5667-9563-86412f5e7f7d'}, {'abstract': 'The kitchen will close on Sunday for its first updating in 27 years.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/gracie-mansion-to-get-a-new-kitchen/', 'snippet': 'The kitchen will close on Sunday for its first updating in 27 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The kitchen at Gracie Mansion is about to be renovated for the first time in 27 years, City Room reports. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gracie Mansion to Get a New Kitchen', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:45:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6eb4637-1639-593b-bf4c-738902ce0703', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6eb4637-1639-593b-bf4c-738902ce0703'}, {'abstract': 'Theyskens shows the softer side of cool, in the form of an all-white palette.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/just-one-look-theyskens-theory-2/', 'snippet': 'Theyskens shows the softer side of cool, in the form of an all-white palette.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Come this resort season, the Theyskens’ Theory girl (who’s either a downtown model or someone working a downtown-model-off-duty look) will have to shelve her black leather motorcycle pants and tattered tees. Because the designer Olivier Theyskens is showing the softer side of cool, in the form of an all-white palette. Jumpsuits, trousers, cropped jackets — everything you already have in black, you’ll now want in white. Even those velour hot shorts now come in a white (and more covered) version. Denim vests and overall shorts are washed in light blue, and there’s an even brighter side: rainbow jeweled crop tops and threaded mini dresses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Just One Look | Theyskens’ Theory', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06d093be-85ea-5dc2-b555-fd14bfa0a961', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06d093be-85ea-5dc2-b555-fd14bfa0a961'}, {'abstract': 'The device, running a new version of the Windows operating system, would be the first computer of the company’s own design, and would be aimed squarely at Apple’s iPad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/technology/microsoft-expected-to-introduce-tablet.html', 'snippet': 'The device, running a new version of the Windows operating system, would be the first computer of the company’s own design, and would be aimed squarely at Apple’s iPad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, Microsoft has made the software that runs a majority of the world’s personal computers, leaving a gang of outside hardware companies to design the machines. Apple, its rival, makes it all.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/technology/16tablet-pic/16tablet-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/technology/16tablet-pic/16tablet-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft Is Expected to Introduce a Tablet', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Microsoft Is Expected To Introduce a Tablet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T18:46:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7c102c9-da11-5730-a8ec-6215b3014dcf', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7c102c9-da11-5730-a8ec-6215b3014dcf'}, {'abstract': 'A famous pâtissier creates a dessert menu for the Japanese airlines All Nippon Airways.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/flights-of-fancy-indeed-french-patissier-onboard/', 'snippet': 'A famous pâtissier creates a dessert menu for the Japanese airlines All Nippon Airways.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The innovative French pastry chef Pierre Hermé, one of the world’s most famous pâtissiers, has enjoyed a long love affair with Japan. In 1998, he introduced the first outpost of his Pierre Hermé Paris pastry boutique in Tokyo, three years before opening one in Paris.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Flights of Fancy, Indeed: French Pâtissier Onboard', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALL NIPPON AIRWAYS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ratha Tep', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ratha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tep', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34275bce-6b59-5b98-ade6-aa8691c0a2c4', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34275bce-6b59-5b98-ade6-aa8691c0a2c4'}, {'abstract': 'Estrangement gets complicated when parents can watch children’s lives going on without them on Facebook, Twitter or other social media.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/advice-for-the-estranged-online-and-off/', 'snippet': 'Estrangement gets complicated when parents can watch children’s lives going on without them on Facebook, Twitter or other social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who are estranged from family members often don’t speak about it — out of shame, embarrassment or to avoid the judgment of acquaintances. Elizabeth Vagnoni, a documentary filmmaker, whose two sons no longer speak to her, said: “They think, ‘What did you do? What kind of mother must you be?’” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Advice for the Estranged, Online and Off', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:02:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6bc7d696-4471-5d2b-bd9f-dbf5eb0b25f2', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6bc7d696-4471-5d2b-bd9f-dbf5eb0b25f2'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Brooks’s reluctance to change his starting lineup has given the Miami Heat the upper hand in the N.B.A. finals.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/why-the-thunders-starting-lineup-isnt-working/', 'snippet': 'Scott Brooks’s reluctance to change his starting lineup has given the Miami Heat the upper hand in the N.B.A. finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For evidence of the power of lineup manipulation in basketball, one need look no further than the intriguing circumstances that have forced Serge Ibaka to (rather unsuccessfully) check Shane Battier. An incredibly athletic defensive player of the year candidate has been humbled in his attempts to defend an aging spot-up shooter, largely due to Scott Brooks’s reluctance to make what could be the N.B.A. finals’ most crucial adjustment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the Thunder’s Starting Lineup Isn’t Working', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battier, Shane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Scott', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haslem, Udonis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibaka, Serge', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perkins, Kendrick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City (Okla)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:03:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfdfa08c-fb0f-53ec-bd05-c5a73e0f81d9', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfdfa08c-fb0f-53ec-bd05-c5a73e0f81d9'}, {'abstract': 'A public outcry ensued when graphic photos of a 23-year-old woman and her dead fetus were posted online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/world/asia/china-suspends-family-planning-workers-after-forced-abortion.html', 'snippet': 'A public outcry ensued when graphic photos of a 23-year-old woman and her dead fetus were posted online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — China suspended three local family planning officials in northwest China this week following a public outcry over reports that they had forced a young woman to undergo an abortion seven months into her pregnancy, according to Xinhua, the official Chinese news agency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Suspends Family Planning Workers After Forced Abortion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Suspends Family Planning Workers After Forced Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:04:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63f7614d-527c-5fb1-b2c4-bb338b3fa759', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63f7614d-527c-5fb1-b2c4-bb338b3fa759'}, {'abstract': 'In David Foster Wallace’s “Infinite Jest” and other novels, made-up movies are a big part of the fun.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/movies-that-flicker-only-on-the-page/', 'snippet': 'In David Foster Wallace’s “Infinite Jest” and other novels, made-up movies are a big part of the fun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Janet Maslin recently reviewed two novels that each featured fictional movies. Jess Walter’s “Beautiful Ruins” includes the idea for a movie called “Donner!” about the Donner party, which, Ms. Maslin writes, “might just be the worst screenplay idea Hollywood has ever known.” And in Alan Furst’s new novel, “Mission to Paris,” an actor stars in a movie about World War I called “Après la Guerre,” or “After the War,” which begins filming at the dawn of World War II.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Movies That Flicker Only on the Page', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Movies That Flicker Only on the Page', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMIS, MARTIN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARONOFSKY, DARREN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wagner, Bruce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallace, David Foster', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:06:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2e31815-f155-5254-b30a-68806d4021b8', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2e31815-f155-5254-b30a-68806d4021b8'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook, in a motion that seeks to consolidate several shareholder lawsuits, provided the first glimpse of the social network’s defense of its bungled I.P.O. It is a defense built, in part, on Nasdaq’s missteps.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/in-motion-facebook-lays-out-defense-and-highlights-nasdaqs-missteps/', 'snippet': 'Facebook, in a motion that seeks to consolidate several shareholder lawsuits, provided the first glimpse of the social network’s defense of its bungled I.P.O. It is a defense built, in part, on Nasdaq’s missteps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly one month after its bungled initial public offering, Facebook is breaking its silence.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Motion, Facebook Lays Out Defense and Highlights Nasdaq’s Missteps', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Facebook Asks Court To Consolidate I.P.O. Lawsuits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:07:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Evelyn M. Rusli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dcefc1c-0bca-53c9-9b7b-e5014eeacc73', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dcefc1c-0bca-53c9-9b7b-e5014eeacc73'}, {'abstract': 'Neil Munro of The Daily Caller interrupted the president as he was making his statement from the Rose Garden. “It’s not time for questions, sir,” Mr. Obama said. “Not while I’m speaking.”', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/reporter-interrupts-obama-during-statement-on-immigration/', 'snippet': 'Neil Munro of The Daily Caller interrupted the president as he was making his statement from the Rose Garden. “It’s not time for questions, sir,” Mr. Obama said. “Not while I’m speaking.”', 'lead_paragraph': '4:40 p.m. | Updated The interruption stunned White House correspondents and television viewers. And it clearly surprised President Obama, too.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reporter Interrupts Obama During Statement on Immigration', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reporter Interrupts Obama’s Statement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e80664d6-9e49-5f05-8ca1-1e6b40dbfaea', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e80664d6-9e49-5f05-8ca1-1e6b40dbfaea'}, {'abstract': 'The day in sports included swimming in Rome, the European soccer championships and badminton in Jakarta, Indonesia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/15/sports/20120615photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'The day in sports included swimming in Rome, the European soccer championships and badminton in Jakarta, Indonesia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The day in sports included swimming i