None, 'lastname': 'Considine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d10f96a-eacc-58ab-9cc9-1c0123ee26d7', 'word_count': 468, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d10f96a-eacc-58ab-9cc9-1c0123ee26d7'}, {'abstract': 'The economic package would include the sale of state assets and the abolition of some state agencies, but would also offer incentives to companies that hire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/business/global/italy-makes-plans-to-cut-debt-and-revive-growth.html', 'snippet': 'The economic package would include the sale of state assets and the abolition of some state agencies, but would also offer incentives to companies that hire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The Italian government moved forward on Friday with a wide-ranging package of economic measures worth about 80 billion euros, or $101 billion, that were meant both to spur economic growth and make a dent in the country’s unsustainably large public debt.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italy Makes Plans to Cut Debt and Revive Growth', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Measures Worth $101 Billion, Italy Aims to Spur Growth and Trim Its Debt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monti, Mario', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:28:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a70f35e-cdba-5ab9-861a-309d95fcda19', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a70f35e-cdba-5ab9-861a-309d95fcda19'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than be disappointed that the Devils lost in the Stanley Cup final, a longtime fan celebrates how an unexpected hockey-watching companion was found: his son.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/for-fathers-day-the-gift-of-a-fellow-fan/', 'snippet': 'Rather than be disappointed that the Devils lost in the Stanley Cup final, a longtime fan celebrates how an unexpected hockey-watching companion was found: his son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Devils came within two games of winning the Stanley Cup, the biggest prize in hockey. As a longtime fan, I should have been bitterly disappointed. But I wasn’t, because while I followed their two-month playoff run, an unexpected hockey-watching companion developed: my six-year-old son, Nicholas. The boy who was once more interested in watching the Zamboni than the hockey game turned into a sports-page-reading fanatic. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Father’s Day, the Gift of a Fellow Fan', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Father's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stanley Cup', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:29:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Harder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a80cd1b-c29f-5c5a-b7ee-4a32bd3dcc8b', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a80cd1b-c29f-5c5a-b7ee-4a32bd3dcc8b'}, {'abstract': 'What is the new “normal” in Hollande’s France?', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/lumiere-the-new-normal-chic/', 'snippet': 'What is the new “normal” in Hollande’s France?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The French like their leaders to be regal, so François Hollande’s pledge to be a “normal” president will take some getting used to. Not that Hollande seems ready to surrender any of the powers of his office or abandon Charles de Gaulle’s “certain idea of France” as an exceptional nation. For now, the changes are a matter of style. Less spending, less glamour, less Versailles. More caution, more prudence, more modest living. So what is the new “normal” in Hollande’s France?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lumière | The New Normal Chic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/392ca9dd-c4a6-582a-ba98-5557dcdbe0ad', 'word_count': 970, 'uri': 'nyt://article/392ca9dd-c4a6-582a-ba98-5557dcdbe0ad'}, {'abstract': 'On the first day of the inaugural edition of London Collections: Men, as this city got used to the idea of having its very own Fashion Week for men, the look for spring 2013 was black dress socks worn with shorts', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/in-london-men-look-toward-spring/', 'snippet': 'On the first day of the inaugural edition of London Collections: Men, as this city got used to the idea of having its very own Fashion Week for men, the look for spring 2013 was black dress socks worn with shorts', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the first day of the inaugural edition of London Collections: Men, as this city got used to the idea of having its very own Fashion Week for men, the look for spring 2013 was black dress socks worn with shorts. Both Lou Dalton, an up-and-comer, and the designers at Topman, the premium men’s division of Topshop, styled their models in black socks, which did not exactly suggest the sort of directionality for which London designers are supposedly known. That middle-aged look for lawn-mowing has been all over Brooklyn already.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Shows Open With Up-and-Comers', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Socks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Topshop', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T19:33:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_i