an insider trading case based largely on circumstantial evidence. But his lawyers have several issues they may bring up on appeal.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/for-gupta-what-lies-ahead/', 'snippet': 'Rajat K. Gupta’s conviction shows that federal prosecutors can still win an insider trading case based largely on circumstantial evidence. But his lawyers have several issues they may bring up on appeal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rajat K. Gupta’s conviction on four of six counts shows that federal prosecutors can still win an insider trading case based largely on circumstantial evidence. In the end, it appears that the jury was quite persuaded by wiretaps. For the two charges that he was acquitted on, the government did not present overheard conversations of Raj Rajaratnam describing his source of inside information. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Gupta, What Lies Ahead', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insider Trading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rajaratnam, Raj', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rakoff, Jed S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Galleon Group', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T20:19:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a0786e6-38ee-5ac2-b60b-c4c5db30932f', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a0786e6-38ee-5ac2-b60b-c4c5db30932f'}, {'abstract': 'Major League Baseball upheld a scorer’s decision in the Mets game Wednesday night, meaning R.A. Dickey’s one-hitter will not become a no-hitter.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/still-a-one-hitter-baseball-says/', 'snippet': 'Major League Baseball upheld a scorer’s decision in the Mets game Wednesday night, meaning R.A. Dickey’s one-hitter will not become a no-hitter.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:34 p.m. | Updated R.A. Dickey will have to keep working to get a no-hitter. As expected, Major League Baseball on Friday upheld the ruling made Wednesday, when the official scorer decided that B. J. Upton’s chopper to third base in the first inning was indeed a hit and not an error by David Wright, who grabbed at the ball with his bare hand but never gained control.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still a One-Hitter, Baseball Says', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T20:23:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d6a49bf-b54f-5b8e-b2b3-09e165bfbf87', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d6a49bf-b54f-5b8e-b2b3-09e165bfbf87'}, {'abstract': 'Lively ho