ess Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir and Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5fe6a5f-39a1-576a-bf7a-26298ebadb6e', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5fe6a5f-39a1-576a-bf7a-26298ebadb6e'}, {'abstract': 'The Barcelona collective known as por instantes brings pedestrian encounters to fleeting life in “La Travesía.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/arts/dance/por-instantes-at-baryshnikov-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Barcelona collective known as por instantes brings pedestrian encounters to fleeting life in “La Travesía.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Barcelona collective known as por instantesisn’t as exotic as it sounds. Led by the German-born choreographer Julia Koch and the American director Daniel Zippi, the group named itself after the phrase “by moments,” which seems to mirror the way its collaborators bring pedestrian encounters to fleeting life. A woman sways seductively while caressing her shoulder. A couple’s lips brush slowly for a kiss, then draw apart. Another woman speaks incessantly to anyone who will listen. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/arts/TRAVESIA1/TRAVESIA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/16/arts/TRAVESIA1/TRAVESIA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N