count': 1168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afc52eda-da97-5c44-9f46-55bbc226a2bc'}, {'abstract': 'A reader responds to an article about Wi-Fi on Amtrak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/travel/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'A reader responds to an article about Wi-Fi on Amtrak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor: “Wi-Fi and Amtrak: Missed Connections (June 3): Beside issues with Internet connection, there’s no corporate accountability at Amtrak. I’m on Amtrak regularly and often find the Wi-Fi is entirely shut off, not just spotty. When asked to fix it, conductors invariably say, “Service needs to be switched on from a central office.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Letters to the Editor', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'View From The Tracks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMTRAK', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T21:31:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/660d9e51-030e-5175-a131-d9f439ad7695', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/660d9e51-030e-5175-a131-d9f439ad7695'}, {'abstract': 'By 2020, the agency estimates, only six counties in the nation are expected to be out of compliance.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/e-p-a-casts-new-soot-standard-as-easily-met/', 'snippet': 'By 2020, the agency estimates, only six counties in the nation are expected to be out of compliance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As anticipated, the Environmental Protection Agency announced on Friday that it was proposing to update and tighten national air quality standards for fine-particle soot.Somewhat surprisingly, however, the agency said that by the time these new standards were fully in force in 2020, all but six counties in the United States would be in compliance with them as a result of steps taken to abide by other tightened rules. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.P.A. Casts New Soot Standard as Easily Met', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Clean Air Agencies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T21:35:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leslie Kaufman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leslie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaufman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfba812a-009f-576b-aa8a-c74d6b88110f', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfba812a-009f-576b-aa8a-c74d6b88110f'}, {'abstract': 'The Up, a cute-as-a-Bug Volkswagen, is perfect for the parking-starved city, but won’t be trolling for spaces in America. It’s not coming here.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/17/automobiles/autoreviews/17wheel-slides.html', 'snippet': 'The Up, a cute-as-a-Bug Volkswagen, is perfect for the parking-starved city, but won’t be trolling for spaces in America. It’s not coming here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Up, a cute-as-a-Bug Volkswagen, is perfect for the parking-starved city, but won’t be trolling for spaces in America. It’s not coming here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'sub