ading', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gupta, Rajat K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T21:41:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden and Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf94dec0-0d13-5d1c-801d-1cb7aab4fea3', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf94dec0-0d13-5d1c-801d-1cb7aab4fea3'}, {'abstract': 'Readers debate the merits of the target-date mutual funds that their employers have picked to put in their 401(k) or other workplace retirement plans.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/picking-the-best-target-date-mutual-fund/', 'snippet': 'Readers debate the merits of the target-date mutual funds that their employers have picked to put in their 401(k) or other workplace retirement plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before we get to the business of target-date fund selection, which is the subject of this weekend’s Your Money column, a quick word on the basic merits of target-date mutual funds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Picking The Best Target-Date Mutual Fund', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mutual Funds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T Rowe Price Group Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T21:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bbb75987-c418-5499-88c1-119dae2214d0', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bbb75987-c418-5499-88c1-119dae2214d0'}, {'abstract': 'How will you celebrate Bloomsday? What will you drink? And who are your favorite Irish writers, past and present?', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/celebrating-bloomsday-with-james-joyce-and-other-irish-writers/', 'snippet': 'How will you celebrate Bloomsday? What will you drink? And who are your favorite Irish writers, past and present?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers picked up on the not-so-subtle nod to James Joyce’s “Ulysses” at the end of my June “Drink” column. Hey, it was hard to resist: for those who love the book, any walk around Dublin in some way evokes the company of Leopold Bloom, Stephen Dedalus and others. It seems you can never get far without passing a landmark that appears in the novel.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrating Bloomsday, With James Joyce (and Other Irish Writers)', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joyce, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T21:45:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_