hat is perhaps the natural result of a tech press anxious to say something, anything, to seem informed on a topic.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/microsoft-samsung-apple-secrecy/', 'snippet': 'There is something different about Microsoft’s event scheduled for Monday in Los Angeles, but also something very familiar: Secrecy. It creates buzz that is perhaps the natural result of a tech press anxious to say something, anything, to seem inf...', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is something different about Microsoft’s event scheduled for Monday in Los Angeles, but also something very familiar. The secrecy surrounding this particular product introduction feels a lot like Apple’s.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Microsoft and Samsung Try Out Apple’s Secret Sauce', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T22:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6576e1dc-71ca-599b-8a43-2b36f3f9bd0f', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6576e1dc-71ca-599b-8a43-2b36f3f9bd0f'}, {'abstract': 'A silent march planned for Sunday to protest the Police Department’s stop-and-frisk tactic was inspired by a 1917 march.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/15/a-history-of-making-messages-heard-silently/', 'snippet': 'A silent march planned for Sunday to protest the Police Department’s stop-and-frisk tactic was inspired by a 1917 march.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They marched down Fifth Avenue on that summer Saturday without saying a word. They chanted no chants, sang no protest songs. The only sounds were the disconcertingly mournful thuds of muffled drums — and, of course, the marchers’ footsteps on the hot pavement. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A History of Making Protest Messages Heard, Silently', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protest March on Sunday Is Inspired by the Profundity of Silence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jealous, Benjamin Todd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharpton, Al', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn for the Advancement of Colored People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (NYC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-15T22:57:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Barron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e860ab1b-24db-5d1f-a64e-7be81acd50de', 'word_count': 