ly.html', 'snippet': 'Books by Deborah Kenny, an education pioneer; Barry Farber, a conservative talk-radio host; and Neil Fabricant, a former grad school president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARENTS and principals trying to understand what makes successful New York City schools work ought to read Deborah Kenny’s “Born to Rise: A Story of Children and Teachers Reaching Their Highest Potential” (Harper, $25.99). Teachers don’t need to. They already know. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/nyregion/17BOOK/17BOOK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/nyregion/17BOOK/17BOOK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1535, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/nyregion/17BOOK/17BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/nyregion/17BOOK/17BOOK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/nyregion/17BOOK/17BOOK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Educator’s Recipe for School Success', 'kicker': 'Bookshelf', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Educator’s Recipe For School Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Deborah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 2