n by another man, and paid with his life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/nyregion/corey-capers-stabbing-victim-remembered-as-a-suspect-vanishes.html', 'snippet': 'A man came to the defense of a woman being beaten by another man, and paid with his life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A woman named Amy, 37, stood with her 3-year-old daughter parked on her hip on East Fifth Street in Alphabet City. “I was his fiancée,” she said. “We had wedding bands already.” And plans for Father’s Day. “We were all going to dress the same. Red shorts and striped, red-and-white polo shirts. From T. J. Maxx.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 817, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1634, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 188, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Dead Father Remembered by Many, and a Stabbing Suspect Known to Few', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Dead Father Remembered by Many, and a Stabbing Suspect Known to Few', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Knox, Carl', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capers, Corey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T00:51:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/794d896e-baf3-5387-ad67-bf93ffe9b3ff', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/794d896e-baf3-5387-ad67-bf93ffe9b3ff'}, {'abstract': 'Why is there an image of a housefly in some urinals at Kennedy Airport?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/nyregion/answers-to-questions-about-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Why is there an image of a housefly in some urinals at Kennedy Airport?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. On returning to Kennedy Airport from a trip abroad, I went through Terminal 4. There is something strange about the men’s rooms in that building. At the center of each urinal, toward the bottom, there is an image of a large black housefly. Is this someone’s idea of a joke? Please explain.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/nyregion/17fyi-fly/17fyi-fly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 408, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo'