9-gives-school-lunch-failing-grade.html', 'snippet': 'A food blog started by a primary schooler has helped galvanize a health movement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — On the first day Martha Payne, 9, reviewed her school lunch online, she also posted a picture of a small pizza, a cupcake, a smattering of sweet corn and a solitary reconstituted potato croquette. “I’m a growing kid and I need to concentrate all afternoon and I can’t do it on 1 croquette,” she wrote. “Do any of you think you could?” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/world/SCOTLAND/SCOTLAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 580, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/world/SCOTLAND/SCOTLAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 770, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/world/SCOTLAND/SCOTLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/16/world/SCOTLAND/SCOTLAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/world/SCOTLAND/SCOTLAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Girl, 9, Gives School Lunch Failing Grade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Girl, 9, Gives School Lunch Failing Grade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's