reatened after they scored five runs in the first inning against the Seawolves ace Tyler Johnson.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — After arriving in Omaha as the toast of the town, the Stony Brook Seawolves were routed by U.C.L.A. on Friday in the team’s inaugural appearance at the College World Series. The Bruins, the tournament’s No. 2 overall seed, beat the Seawolves, 9-1, at TD Ameritrade Park. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.C.L.A. Trounces Stony Brook in Series Opener', 'kicker': 'College World Series', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stony Brook Beaten', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York at Stony Brook', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College World Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T02:18:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian M. Ayers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23970ec2-ec36-5bb5-869b-b8a61de9aa38', 'word_count': 535, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23970ec2-ec36-5bb5-869b-b8a61de9aa38'}, {'abstract': 'In one of the few states with enough animals for a hunting season, an annual lottery drew 13,400 people who hoped to secure one of 275 permits for an October hunt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/us/new-hampshire-holds-lottery-for-moose-hunt.html', 'snippet': 'In one of the few states with enough animals for a hunting season, an annual lottery drew 13,4