e8f0b0-78c3-59d6-9477-42704f0ea978'}, {'abstract': 'At an annual conference, mayors said that despite Washington’s profound inaction they have managed to shrink deficits, increase property values and create new jobs in their cities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/us/politics/mayors-see-slight-gains-no-thanks-to-congress.html', 'snippet': 'At an annual conference, mayors said that despite Washington’s profound inaction they have managed to shrink deficits, increase property values and create new jobs in their cities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ORLANDO, Fla. — Three years after their cities were battered by recession, America’s mayors are exhaling — collectively — and saying the worst may be over.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayors See Slight Gains, No Thanks to Congress', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mayors See Slight Gains, No Thanks To Congress', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Kasim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Scott', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transportation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Conference of Mayors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T03:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'la