ans-prime-minister-orders-restart-of-2-nuclear-reactors.html', 'snippet': 'Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda’s order to restart the Ohi nuclear plant made it the nation’s first to go back on line since the crisis last year in Fukushima.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Brushing aside widespread public opposition to avoid feared electric power shortages, Prime Minister Yoshihiko Noda ordered the reactivation of two nuclear reactors at a plant in western Japan on Saturday, making it the nation’s first plant to go back online since the crisis last year in Fukushima.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Public Still Divided as 2 Reactors to Be Opened', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan Public Still Divided As 2 Reactors To Be Opened', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noda, Yoshihiko', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T10:02:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martin Fackler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fackler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/439244f0-c690-5299-9ba0-bb671f2d59af', 'word_count': 732, 'uri': 'nyt://article/439244f0-c690-5299-9ba0-bb671f2d59af'}, {'abstract': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/newswallah-bharat-edition-44/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of news from across India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jammu and Kashmir: The state police arrested five men in Kashmir on Thursday, accused of being operatives in the terror group Lashkar-e-Taiba, in connection with planting an explosive device on the outskirts of Srinagar last month, Hindustan Times reported. The police had foiled the bid, which they claim was aimed at security personnel, after receiving a tip off from a local, the newspaper reported. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newswallah: Bharat Edition', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prison Escapes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Railroads', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Taiba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Times of India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangalore (India)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karnataka (India)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kashmir and Jammu (India)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T10:55:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356704de-73bf-5ee4-a3b6-d3e854a282a5', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356704de-73bf-5ee4-a3b6-d3e854a282a5'}, {'abstract': 'The N.F.L. is giving fans the chance to pay to see the same game film that players and coaches review.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/n-f-l-fans-will-have-access-to-coaches-film/', 'snippet': 'The N.F.L. is giving fans the chance to pay to see the same game film that players and coaches review.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.F.L. is giving fans the chance to pay to see the same game film that players and coaches review. That should lead to better analysis, despite what critics like Charley Casserly said last year. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Fans Will Have Access to Coaches’ Film', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T11:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea13db00-7c67-56c5-87b6-19e8234eb744', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea13db00-7c67-56c5-87b6-19e8234eb744'}, {'abstract': 'Expecting to return from New York with celebratory trinkets and clothing representing a historic weekend, but instead returning with an empty suitcase and a very strong belief that it most definitely could have been.', 'web_url': 'https://therail.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/enough-expectations-to-fill-a-suitcase/', 'snippet': 'Expecting to return from New York with celebratory trinkets and clothing representing a historic weekend, but instead returning with an empty suitcase and a very strong belief that it most definitely could have been.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When one packs a suitcase for a trip, it is filled with things to accommodate your travel needs. One packs what he or she hopes is the appropriate clothing, hats, medicines and those special comfort items needed when traveling away from home. But there is something else intangible that also goes into the suitcase, and that is personal expectations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Suitcase Packed With Expectations, Stowed Away Until Next Year', 'kicker': 'The Rail', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Belmont Stakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "I'll Have Another (Race Horse)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reddam, J Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T11:18:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie June Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': 'June', 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfaf96ae-a97b-5a7c-80ef-a45285539896', 'word_count': 1378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfaf96ae-a97b-5a7c-80ef-a45285539896'}, {'abstract': 'Liu Yang was part of a three-person crew expected to complete the country’s first manned docking mission, an important step in an ambitious plan to build a Chinese space station by 2020.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/science/space/china-sends-3-astronauts-including-a-woman-into-space.html', 'snippet': 'Liu Yang was part of a three-person crew expected to complete the country’s first manned docking mission, an important step in an ambitious plan to build a Chinese space station by 2020.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — China sent a crew of three,