uro-gloom on Saturday to mark Bloomsday, an annual celebration of the life and work of James Joyce and of his most famous fictional character, Leopold Bloom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/blogs/joyce-celebration-rdv/joyce-celebration-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 608, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/16/blogs/joyce-celebration-rdv/joyce-celebration-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1187, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy Bloomsday! The World Celebrates James Joyce', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joyce, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dublin (Ireland)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ireland', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T12:53:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f47f3ab7-e1dc-5872-a457-c6e34509e44c', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f47f3ab7-e1dc-5872-a457-c6e34509e44c'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations’ decision to pause observers’ work was the most severe blow yet to a wobbly peace plan world powers had seen as the best chance to solve Syria’s deadly conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/world/middleeast/un-suspends-its-mission-in-syria-citing-violence.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations’ decision to pause observers’ work was the most severe blow yet to a wobbly peace plan world powers had seen as the best chance to solve Syria’s deadly conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The United Nations said Saturday that it was suspending its observer mission in Syria because of the escalating violence, the most severe blow yet to months of international efforts to negotiate a peace plan and prevent Syria’s descent into civil war. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/world/17syria-span/17syria-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 317, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/world/17syria-span/17syria-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 317}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/world/17syria-span/17syria-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/world/17syria-span/17syria-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1451, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/world/17syria-span/17syria-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/world/17syria-span/17syria-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb