 in the Khyber tribal region occurred at a bus stand and a nearby bakery in the town of Landi Kotal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/world/asia/car-bombing-in-pakistan-kills-24-people.html', 'snippet': 'The blasts in the Khyber tribal region occurred at a bus stand and a nearby bakery in the town of Landi Kotal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PESHAWAR, Pakistan — Two bombings killed at least 32 people on Saturday in the Khyber tribal region, according to a senior regional administration official and The Associated Press. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bombs in Pakistan Kill at Least 32', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bombs in Pakistan Kill at Least 32', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-i-Islam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Federally Administered Tribal Areas (Pakistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T14:56:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ismail Khan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ismail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0953791-f79b-5453-910e-486ee1e2afe7', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0953791-f79b-5453-910e-486ee1e2afe7'}, {'abstract': 'Europe’s crisis and the welfare state.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/death-throes/', 'snippet': 'Europe’s crisis and the welfare state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague David Brooks tells us that Republicans see the economic crisis as showing that the welfare state is in its “death throes”. And it’s true — that is what they think, or claim to think.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Throes', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T15:07:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1657d76-ef85-5e29-87bf-f18d574a2016', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1657d76-ef85-5e29-87bf-f18d574a2016'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney says perhaps Barack Obama should have spent some time running a state.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/romney-accidentally-puts-obama-in-govenors-office-but-goes-with-the-idea/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney says perhaps Barack Obama should have spent some time running a state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEATHERLY, Pa. — At an early morning stop on Saturday here in Weatherly — a town in a county in which President Obama barely eked out a victory four years ago — Mitt Romney had some backhanded advice for the president.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Accidentally Puts Obama in Governor’s Office, but Goes With the Idea', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T15:08:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46e9491d-ccfe-5f05-9398-bac453231691', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46e9491d-ccfe-5f05-9398-bac453231691'}, {'abstract': 'John W. Thompson describes his journey from sales rep at I.B.M. to chief executive of Symantec and now Virtual Instruments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/jobs/john-thompson-of-virtual-instruments-on-his-career.html', 'snippet': 'John W. Thompson describes his journey from sales rep at I.B.M. to chief executive of Symantec and now Virtual Instruments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I GREW up in West Palm Beach, Fla. My dad took me hunting, trapping and fishing when I was a kid. Years later, when I was working for I.B.M. in the Midwest, a customer invited me to go pheasant hunting in South Dakota. I haven’t missed a season there in 20 years. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/business/17-BOSS/17-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/business/17-BOSS/17-BOSS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2032, 'width': 1567, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/business/17-BOSS/17-BOSS-thumbStand