le want to turn Colorado National Monument into a national park. Others say that would just be a bother.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GRAND JUNCTION, Colo. — In 1906, a vagabond with an eye for beauty named John Otto fell in love with the unscarred land out here. After seeing the sandstone spires and hypnotic canyons that rise above this town, he made a decision: “I’m going to stay and build trails and promote this place,” he wrote, “because it should be a national park.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/JP-MONUMENT-1/JP-MONUMENT-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Disputing Whether a Treasure Needs a Name Upgrade', 'kicker': 'Grand Junction Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disputing Whether a Treasure Needs a Name Upgrade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Park Service', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Parks, Monuments and Seashores', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T15:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2acf5b4c-c372-58d9-9115-99b48ebf1552', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2acf5b4c-c372-58d9-9115-99b48ebf1552'}, {'abstract': 'Putting was the key as Jack Nicklaus beat Arnold Palmer in an 18-hole playoff to win the 1962 United States Open at Oakmont.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/sports/golf/50-years-ago-arnold-palmer-let-the-us-open-slip-away.html', 'snippet': 'Putting was the key as Jack Nicklaus beat Arnold Palmer in an 18-hole playoff to win the 1962 United States Open at Oakmont.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arnold Palmer couldn’t miss winning the 1962 United States Open. Two months earlier he had won the Masters for the third time in five years. He had won the 1960 Open with a final-round 65 and also the 1961 British Open. More popular than ever at age 32, the charismatic commander of Arnie’s Army made the cover of Newsweek with the caption “Arnold Palmer: Perfection Under Pressure.” In the cherrywood-paneled basement of his Latrobe, Pa., home a coffee table was inlaid with 24 gold medals, each representing a tournament he had won. But one space was empty.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/sports/anderson-reefer/anderson-reefer-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/sports/anderson-reefer/anderson-reefer-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/sports/anderson-reefer/anderson-reefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/sports/anderson-reefer/anderson-reefer-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/sports/anderson-reefer/anderson-reefer-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Palmer, One That Got Away', 'kicker': 'Sports of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Palmer, One That Got Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Arnold', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nicklaus, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T15:13:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', '