ists at the vanguard of last year’s revolution demoralized by the choice between two conservatives, journalists and bloggers reported a distinct lack of enthusiasm, and a low turnout of younger voters, in Saturday’s presidential election runoff.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/amid-tight-security-and-low-expectations-egypt-votes-again/', 'snippet': 'With many of the Egyptian activists at the vanguard of last year’s revolution demoralized by the choice between two conservatives, journalists and bloggers reported a distinct lack of enthusiasm, and a low turnout of younger voters, in Saturday’s ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — As my colleague David Kirkpatrick reports, voters went to the polls in Egypt on Saturday, starting two days of voting in the country’s presidential runoff election, which pits ousted President Hosni Mubarak’s former prime minister against an Islamist candidate from the Muslim Brotherhood.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Tight Security and Low Expectations, Egypt Votes Again', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T15:34:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6564e8c9-4fde-5c3d-8f51-17423c85689f', 'word_count': 354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6564e8c9-4fde-5c3d-8f51-17423c85689f'}, {'abstract': 'A police chief said Zamal Uddin was probably killed because of his reporting on the illegal drug trade.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/world/asia/journalist-is-killed-in-bangladesh.html', 'snippet': 'A police chief said Zamal Uddin was probably killed because of his reporting on the illegal drug trade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DHAKA, Bangladesh (AP) — A journalist hacked to death by unidentified assailants was probably killed because of his reporting on the illegal drug trade in southwestern Bangladesh, the police said Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Journalist Is Killed in Bangladesh', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Journalist Is Killed in Bangladesh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T15:39:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By THE ASSOCIATED PRESS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'THE ASSOCIATED PRESS'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1a23797-ae3a-54a2-8b94-303793d47c85', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1a23797-ae3a-54a2-8b94-303793d47c85'}, {'abstract': 'When you’re a dad, life sometimes tosses miracles ... like taking your son to the World Series and then passing a love of baseball to the next generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/sports/box-seats-best-seats-in-the-house-any-place-with-dad.html', 'snippet': 'When you’re a dad, life sometimes tosses miracles ... like taking your son to the World Series and then passing a love of baseball to the next generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you’re a dad, life sometimes tosses miracles. You have to be enough of a child to catch them.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/sports/father/fath