ness of the risks of exposure to the sun.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/30-seconds-with-johnny-bench/', 'snippet': 'After a bout with skin cancer, the Hall of Fame catcher aims to raise awareness of the risks of exposure to the sun.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johnny Bench played his way into the Hall of Fame with power hitting and defense during a 17-year-career as a catcher with the Cincinnati Reds. In addition to his 389 home runs and 1,376 runs batted in, Bench won 10 Gold Glove awards and led the National League three times in percentage of runners caught stealing. He had a .990 fielding percentage as a catcher. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '30 Seconds With Johnny Bench', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '30 Seconds With Johnny Bench: Spreading the Word About Sunscreen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bench, Johnny', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cincinnati Reds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T17:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Brescia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brescia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/291830ac-b809-5317-af74-e14bc4cbb027', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/291830ac-b809-5317-af74-e14bc4cbb027'}, {'abstract': 'The Chukchansi Indians recently pledged $1 million over five years to the linguistics department of California State University, Fresno.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/us/chukchansi-tribe-in-california-pushes-to-preserve-language.html', 'snippet': 'The Chukchansi Indians recently pledged $1 million over five years to the linguistics department of California State University, Fresno.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COARSEGOLD, Calif. — Inside a classroom of some 20 adults and children studying the language of their tribe, a university linguist pointed out that Chukchansi has no “r” sound and that two consonants never follow each other. The comments seemed to stir forgotten childhood memories in Holly Wyatt, 69, the only fluent speaker present, who was serving as a living reference book.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/17/us/TRIBE-1/TRIBE-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150,