gate Team', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watergate Affair', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T18:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e04b4064-58c0-5d11-9b6b-454a5164bf9d', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e04b4064-58c0-5d11-9b6b-454a5164bf9d'}, {'abstract': 'In his comments to the Faith and Freedom Coalition, Mitt Romney stuck with conservative positions popular with his audience, the loyal contingent of Republicans whose turnout will be crucial for him in November.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/romney-paints-himself-as-the-anti-obama/', 'snippet': 'In his comments to the Faith and Freedom Coalition, Mitt Romney stuck with conservative positions popular with his audience, the loyal contingent of Republicans whose turnout will be crucial for him in November.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Speaking by video from Pennsylvania to a crowd gathered at the Faith and Freedom Coalition conference here on Saturday, Mitt Romney presented himself as the antithesis of President Obama and his policies. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Paints Himself as the Anti-Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T18:58:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name':