556', 'word_count': 490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09054d83-4ae9-52dd-8471-24748c7df556'}, {'abstract': 'A textbook case.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/reagan-and-inflation/', 'snippet': 'A textbook case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hmm. I thought I might respond to something that has been coming up in comments and emails recently. I’ve been writing about how macroeconomic reality under Ronald Reagan didn’t actually match the myth, and many people are inevitably upset. And one of the things they tend to bring up is the hoary old myth that the 80s success in taming inflation was somehow a terrible shock and surprise to Keynesians, who had no explanation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reagan and Inflation', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T19:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26b767cf-3085-5842-bf37-4e754e1986a8', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26b767cf-3085-5842-bf37-4e754e1986a8'}, {'abstract': 'Egyptians lined up Saturday to pick the first president since the ouster of Hosni Mubarak, choosing between a stalwart of the old secular autocracy and a veteran of its Islamist opposition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/16/world/middleeast/20120617-EGYPT.html', 'snippet': 'Egyptians lined up Saturday to pick the first president since the ouster of Hosni Mubarak, choosing between a stalwart of the old secular autocracy and a veteran of its Islamist opposition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Egyptians lined up Saturday to pick the first president sin