'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adaobi Tricia Nwaubani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adaobi', 'middlename': 'Tricia', 'lastname': 'Nwaubani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee402d6a-d5a0-50dd-97c8-639f22e44824', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee402d6a-d5a0-50dd-97c8-639f22e44824'}, {'abstract': 'Of New York City’s summonses in 2011, most were dismissed or thrown out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/17/sunday-review/summonses-often-issued-mostly-tossed.html', 'snippet': 'Of New York City’s summonses in 2011, most were dismissed or thrown out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of New York City’s summonses in 2011, most were dismissed or thrown out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summonses Often Issued, Mostly Tossed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T20:38:43+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c4f6bc03-38c9-5fb3-92b0-637cb4fc8882', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c4f6bc03-38c9-5fb3-92b0-637cb4fc8882'}, {'abstract': 'The violations may be minor, like biking on the sidewalk, but there is nothing petty about the half-million summonses issued by New York police officers each year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/opinion/sunday/inside-the-warped-world-of-summons-court.html', 'snippet': 'The violations may be minor, like biking on the sidewalk, but there is nothing petty about the half-million summonses issued by New York police officers each year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Step into the dingy hallways of New York City summons court in Lower Manhattan and you are instantly struck by the racialized nature of this system. New York is a multiracial city, but judging from the faces in cramped courtrooms, one would think that whites scarcely ever commit the petty offenses that lead to the more than 500,000 summonses issued in the city every year.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the Warped World of Summons Court', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Sunday Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the Warped World Of Summons Court', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sweet, Robert W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dear, Noach', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T20:38:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2197c74f-d596-50af-9825-68e09e7215bb', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2197c74f-d596-50af-9825-68e09e7215bb'}, {'abstract': 'Kentucky has taken a significant step against the widespread doping of horses, but regulators across the country will need to do a lot more to change the industry’s cynical culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/opinion/sunday/stronger-medicine-for-what-ails-horse-racing.html', 'snippet': 'Kentucky has taken a significant step against the widespread doping of horses, but regulators across the country will need to do a lot more to change the industry’s cynical culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Regulators in Kentucky, the heart of the horse breeding industry, have taken a significant step against the widespread doping that is putting horses’ lives and the sport’s credibility at risk at racetracks across the nation. A diuretic drug routinely used on race days to shed water weight and boost horses’ performance will be banned under an overdue regulation adopted last week by the Kentucky Horse Racing Commission. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stronger Medicine for What Ails Horse Racing', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stronger Medicine for What Ails Horse Racing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Udall, Tom', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitfield, Ed', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Neill, Douglas F", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T20:38:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/899197fb-631f-55f9-9f3a-d9cdc9014c60', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/899197fb-631f-55f9-9f3a-d9cdc9014c60'}, {'abstract': 'New York’s laws on child sex abuse are weak, and so is Albany’s will to fix them. Lawmakers should bring the statute of limitations into line with the reality of late uncovering of abuse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/opinion/sunday/the-children-deserve-justice.html', 'snippet': 'New York’s laws on child sex abuse are weak, and so is Albany’s will to fix them. Lawmakers should bring the statute of limitations into line with the reality of late uncovering of abuse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There has been no shortage of child sex abuse scandals during the legislative session that is going into its final week in Albany — the Penn State case and the cover-up trial of Msgr. William Lynn in Pennsylvania and, closer to home, the abuse allegations at Syracuse University and the private Horace Mann School in New York. That makes it all the worse that lawmakers have done little to fix New York’s weak laws for protecting children from sexual predators and providing victims with justice.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Children Deserve Justice', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Children Deserve Justice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statutes of Limitations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuomo, Andrew M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Markey, Margaret', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Horace Mann School', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syracuse University', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T20:39:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/edf87cb8-dbcb-5ecc-adcc-0fee39818809', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edf87cb8-dbcb-5ecc-adcc-0fee39818809'}, {'abstract': 'Pandering to his right and Big Oil, Mitt Romney disavows his risk-taking, climate-conscious past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/opinion/sunday/energy-etch-a-sketch.html', 'snippet': 'Pandering to his right and Big Oil, Mitt Romney disavows his risk-taking, climate-conscious past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As governor of Massachusetts, Mitt Romney endorsed an aggressive program to reduce the state’s greenhouse gas emissions, pushed to close old coal-fired power plants and embraced wind and solar power. Then came his bids for the Republican presidential nomination, first in 2008 and now in 2012. On climate change as on other issues, he has transformed himself, bit by reactionary bit.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Energy Etch A Sketch', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Energy Etch A Sketch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, '