hletics and Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T21:12:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allen Barra', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c729d545-146b-597d-a031-96d4cd9ccee0', 'word_count': 690, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c729d545-146b-597d-a031-96d4cd9ccee0'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my column from Iran, about what I saw of the impact of economic sanctions there.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/readers-comment-on-iran-sanctions/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my column from Iran, about what I saw of the impact of economic sanctions there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column, based on my road trip across Iran, looks at economic sanctions there. Bottom line is that they are working pretty much as Washington wants them to: they are inflicting real pain, often on ordinary citizens, in ways that inflame discontent with the system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers Comment on Iran Sanctions', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T21:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7231ea7-85b4-5585-b809-916594101423', 'word_count': 223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7231ea7-85b4-5585-b809-916594101423'}, {'abstract': 'Kyle T. Dolan impersonates a “Fat Albert” character. Sort of.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/16/playable/', 'snippet': 'Kyle T. Dolan impersonates a “Fat Albert” character. Sort of.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Notepad Alert! There will be a Notepad that is worth reading in tomorrow’s (Monday’s) puzzle that says: “When this puzzle is done, the circled letters, reading from left to right and top to bottom, will reveal who wrote the seven songs in the theme.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Playable', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-16T22:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c8a6aa7-80a6-52bc-abbf-1faad8869d61', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c8a6aa7-80a6-52bc-abbf-1faad8869d61'}, {'abstract': 'Andy Pettitte was strong in his first start since turning 40, and a two-run double by Mark Teixeira in the 14th helped the Yankees stretch their winning streak to eight games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/sports/baseball/yankees-beat-nationals-in-14-innings.html', 'snippet': 'Andy Pettitte was strong in his first start since turning 40, and a two-run double by Mark Teixeira in the 14th helped the Yankees stretch their winning streak to eight games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Oh, the lengths the Yankees must go just to win a game without a home run.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge