n nursing, and the bridegroom is a health and science teacher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elizabeth Hadley Fisk, a daughter of Hadley Taylor Fisk of Sudbury, Mass., and Samuel Hoar Fisk of Keene Valley, N.Y., was married Saturday to Russell Warren Wells Jr., a son of Lea Ann Wells and Mr. Wells of Dallas. The Rev. Milton Dudley, a minister of the United Church of Christ, officiated at the home of the bride’s father and stepmother, Linda Chamberlaine Coe, in Keene Valley.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Elizabeth Fisk, Russell Wells Jr.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elizabeth Fisk, Russell Wells Jr.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-17T04:16:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/259aaf52-23c3-5437-8b8e-60cc2153f3dc', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/259aaf52-23c3-5437-8b8e-60cc2153f3dc'}, {'abstract': 'The couple married in New York and had a Lutheran ceremony in Phoenix.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/fashion/weddings/nicholas-butler-clark-olson-weddings.html', 'snippet': 'The couple married in New York and had a Lutheran ceremony in Phoenix.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nicholas Dale Butler and Clark David Olson were married Monday evening in New York in the apartment of the architects Billie Tsien and Tod Williams, acquaintances of the couple. The ceremony was led by Barbara S. Baron, who became a minister through Rose Ministries in order to officiate. On June 9, the couple had a Lutheran ceremony, led by the Rev. Sarah L. Stadler-Ammon, at the Arizona Biltmore resort in Phoenix.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_pa