ue': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T11:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thaddeus Rutkowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thaddeus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutkowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c75a696-f934-529b-9c8d-748b03464dfd', 'word_count': 991, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c75a696-f934-529b-9c8d-748b03464dfd'}, {'abstract': 'There once was a time when landing LaDainian Tomlinson on your fantasy football roster felt as if you had won the lottery.', 'web_url': 'https://fifthdown.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/tomlinsons-legacy-real-and-fantasy/', 'snippet': 'There once was a time when landing LaDainian Tomlinson on your fantasy football roster felt as if you had won the lottery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Links for your consideration:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tomlinson’s Legacy, Real and Fantasy', 'kicker': 'The Fifth Down', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tomlinson, Ladainian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Diego Chargers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T11:02:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Toni Monkovic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Toni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Monkovic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organiza