p closer on Monday to its £1.04 billion ($1.63 billion) takeover of Cable & Wireless Worldwide, after the largest investor in the British telecommunications company backed Vodafone’s bid.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investor Backs Vodafone’s $1.6 Billion Bid for Cable & Wireless', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vodafone Group Plc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T13:12:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/356edb03-2832-5661-8926-c27cb03b0806', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/356edb03-2832-5661-8926-c27cb03b0806'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: The large number of times a police tactic has been used doesn’t necessarily translate into victory. At the same time, statistics need to be considered in context.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/stopping-and-questioning-the-numbers/', 'snippet': 'The Day: The large number of times a police tactic has been used doesn’t necessarily translate into victory. At the same time, statistics need to be considered in context.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is wisdom to be gleaned from the torrent of emotions over the police practice commonly known as stop-and-frisk, it is that City Hall’s worship of statistics has distinct limitations. And if there is anyone who you’d think would have understood that point instinctively, it is the police commissioner, \xa0Raymond W. Kelly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stopping to Question the Numbers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Statistics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T13:17:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ab5372c-776c-5e16-841d-c4e1841de69d', 'word_count': 712, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ab5372c-776c-5e16-841d-c4e1841de69d'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Open and Game 3 of the N.B.A. finals were tough to watch. Ronaldo was much more fun.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/sports/dont-look-now.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Open and Game 3 of the N.B.A. finals were tough to watch. Ronaldo was much more fun.', 'lead_paragraph': "Championships do not come with a guarantee that they'll be worthy of framing. Often, in the slog of a drive for a title, many of a sport's fine artistic points are lost, their beauty obscured in the sheer effort it takes to win. Or, in the case of the United States Open golf championship or the N.B.A. finals, it gets buried in a cloud of fog and unrepentant fairways or drowned out by referees' whistles and bodies hitting the floor.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/sports/golf/19leadingpic/19leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy'