cle', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a10ba6c2-e55d-55a0-b351-6f63dad41644', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a10ba6c2-e55d-55a0-b351-6f63dad41644'}, {'abstract': 'One of the most bizarre shows of the weekend belonged to the design team Meadham Kirchhoff, presenting a collection on models who looked like strung-out addicts on highs of sugar, junk food, cigarettes or the really rough stuff, Internet pornography.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/in-london-the-ones-that-stand-out/', 'snippet': 'One of the most bizarre shows of the weekend belonged to the design team Meadham Kirchhoff, presenting a collection on models who looked like strung-out addicts on highs of sugar, junk food, cigarettes or the really rough stuff, Internet pornograp...', 'lead_paragraph': 'One peculiar thing about the London men’s collections taking place this weekend is that the coolest young designers, or at least the ones with the most buzz here, tend to show in what would seem to be the worst time slots. Jonathan Anderson, whose label J. W. Anderson has been on the hot list for men’s and women’s wear in recent seasons, showed at 9 a.m. on Sunday, on the last day of the men’s shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In London, the Ones That Stand Out', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T14:13:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier':