hing that I want to see happen.” For “Honey, the Baby Is Coming; Quick, Call the Photographer,” Elissa Gootman spoke to parents, photographers and doctors about the new “front lines” of documenting childhood: birth photographers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Professional Photographers in the Delivery Room', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T14:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23bfda9c-8e35-5dd2-a4c9-a8681825978e', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23bfda9c-8e35-5dd2-a4c9-a8681825978e'}, {'abstract': 'Researchers have found that ginseng can help in the relief of cancer-related fatigue, a side effect of radiation therapy and other treatments.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/really-ginseng-can-help-relieve-fatigue/', 'snippet': 'Researchers have found that ginseng can help in the relief of cancer-related fatigue, a side effect of radiation therapy and other treatments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE FACTS', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 529, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/12/21/health/21really/21really-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Really? Ginseng Can Help Relieve Fatigue', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Really? The Claim: Ginseng can help relieve fatigue.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chemotherapy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fatigue', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T14:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': "By Anahad O'Connor", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anahad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connor", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70f344e3-dc56-50c5-b135-68519f512bc1', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70f344e3-dc56-50c5-b135-68519f512bc1'}, {'abstract': 'Environmentalists appeal for tougher language that commits nations to concrete environmental goals.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/on-our-radar-the-negotiating-text-in-rio/', 'snippet': 'Environmentalists appeal for tougher language that commits nations to concrete environmental goals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Environmentalists complain that the negotiating text being readied for the Rio+20 environmental conference this week in Brazil is riddled with words like “support” and encourage” rather than “must” or “will,” the language of commitment; a coalition, meanwhile, organizes a “Twitterstorm” calling for an end to fossil-fuel subsidies. The conference opens on Wednesday. [W.W.F., endfossilfuelsubsidies.org]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: The Negotiating Text in Rio', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'ke