 at the London Palladium in June 2013, according to a news release. The ubiquitous Marc Shaiman and Scott Wittman, who co-wrote the lyrics for the Tony-winning musical “Hairspray” (Mr. Shaiman wrote the music) and created the music for the NBC series about Broadway, “Smash,” will be writing songs for the show.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Charlie and the Chocolate Factory,’ With ‘Hairspray’ Song Team, Plans London Opening', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Hairspray’ Team Needs Rhymes for ‘Wonka’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dahl, Roald', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greig, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mendes, Sam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaiman, Marc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wittman, Scott', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Neal Street Productions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warner Brothers', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T16:20:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9b5c151-6cc1-5e32-903c-4b63f9d2e3c3', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9b5c151-6cc1-5e32-903c-4b63f9d2e3c3'}, {'abstract': 'Out-takes from the interview that appeared in The One-Page Magazine, including thoughts on religion, gardening, and death.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/what-rodney-king-said-during-one-of-his-final-interviews/', 'snippet': 'Out-takes from the interview that appeared in The One-Page Magazine, including thoughts on religion, gardening, and death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since last November, when we introduced the The One-Page Magazine, I’ve interviewed more than 30 celebrities and cultural luminaries for a mini how-to column. (It’s our version of what would be the back page of a “multipage” magazine.) Dr. Phil told me how to break off an engagement nicely; Diahann Carroll divulged\xa0how to look great in your 70s; Fran Drescher spoke about how to stay friends with your ex.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Rodney King Said During One of His Final Interviews', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Rodney Glen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T16:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Spencer Bailey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Spencer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bailey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28e24fef-0c7e-5af3-a90c-75a9582221db', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28e24fef-0c7e-5af3-a90c-75a9582221db'}, {'abstract': 'Acute water shortage has plagued several parts of Delhi.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/image-of-the-day-june-18/', 'snippet': 'Acute water shortage has plagued several parts of Delhi.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: June 18', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name':