: 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'ContinuousNews', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'Emily B. Hager, Nikolia Apostolou, Channon Hodge and Ben Solomon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3947816e-566d-549b-b66e-9f612f0c3654', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3947816e-566d-549b-b66e-9f612f0c3654'}, {'abstract': 'Hoping to fill a gap left by the Communist Party’s war against traditions, Russians are improvising new rituals to mark life’s milestones, often to gaudy or ridiculous effect.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/for-weddings-and-a-funeral/', 'snippet': 'Hoping to fill a gap left by the Communist Party’s war against traditions, Russians are improvising new rituals to mark life’s milestones, often to gaudy or ridiculous effect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TBILISI, Georgia — It’s a modern marriage. A puppet show tells the couple’s love story in verse: while a young man narrates, five custom-made marionettes — the bride, the groom and their three children — bob about. The two people we’ve come to honor have to pick each other out of two line-ups of a dozen potential grooms and brides draped in bed sheets. Then emerges a young bearded man wearing a red cloak and a TV remote control around his neck. Placing battery-operated Christmas-tree lights on the couple’s heads, he pronounces them husband and wife to the applause of the 60 or so guests in attendance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Weddings and a Funeral', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cemeteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Masha Gessen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Masha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gessen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f85cd0ab-07b3-54c5-ba81-904231847e1e', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f85cd0ab-07b3-54c5-ba81-904231847e1e'}, {'abstract': 'Roberta Ridolfi’s London fashion week photo diary.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/photos-of-the-moment-christopher-raeburn/', 'snippet': 'Roberta Ridolfi’s London fashion week photo diary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Photos of The Moment | Christopher Raeburn', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'London Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:19:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Ridolfi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ridolfi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6180d2a-d3c9-5005-a628-4a8aa3fc8e6d', 'word_count': 28, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6180d2a-d3c9-5005-a628-4a8aa3fc8e6d'}, {'abstract': 'On “Meet the Press,” the senator called Citizens United “arrogant, uninformed, naïve.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/john-mccains-three-little-words/', 'snippet': 'On “Meet the Press,” the senator called Citizens United “arrogant, uninformed, naïve.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his 2010 State of the Union address, President Obama roundly criticized the Supreme Court’s Citizens United decision, arguing that it had “reversed a century of law.” That practically sounds like a hymn of praise compared to what Senator John McCain had to say on “Meet the Press” this weekend. He called Citizens United: “arrogant, uninformed, naïve.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'John McCain’s Three Little Words', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCain, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ebd6679-259d-5221-9c2f-190fff74226f', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ebd6679-259d-5221-9c2f-190fff74226f'}, {'abstract': 'For buying $168 (plus tax) worth of his new fragrance, 500 lucky fans received tickets for a show at the Apollo on Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/bieber-fever-comes-to-macys/', 'snippet': 'For buying $168 (plus tax) worth of his new fragrance, 500 lucky fans received tickets for a show at the Apollo on Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For hard-core Justin Bieber fans it was an opportunity not to be missed. The pop star put out the word over Twitter on Sunday that there were 500 tickets available for an unannounced show Monday night at the Apollo Theater. All one had to do to get two of them was to buy $168 (plus tax) worth of his new fragrance at Macy’s in Herald Square.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bieber Fever Comes to Macy’s', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whiff of Biebermania Envelops Macy’s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bieber, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'APOLLO THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HERALD SQUARE (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:21:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e0cd39d-99ed-5f2a-bb6f-aa8426ac1cea', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e0cd39d-99ed-5f2a-bb6f-aa8426ac1cea'}, {'abstract': 'The JPMorgan Chase chief executive, who will testify on Tuesday before the House Financial Services Committee, plans to stick to the script from his first appearance last week on Capitol Hill, with prepared remarks that are virtually identical.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/in-house-testimony-dimon-sticks-to-script/', 'snippet': 'The JPMorgan Chase chief executive, who will testify on Tuesday before the House Financial Services Committee, plans to stick to the script from his first appearance last week on Capitol Hill, with prepared remarks that are virtually identical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anyone hoping that Jamie Dimon‘s second round of prepared Congressional testimony will reveal the full story behind his bank’s multibillion-dollar trading loss — or any fresh details for that matter — is in for a disappointing read.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In House Testimony, Dimon Sticks to Script', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/986363f1-de2c-51b6-b9b2-ce80bbc1687b', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/986363f1-de2c-51b6-b9b2-ce80bbc1687b'}, {'abstract': 'Federal investigators are examining the power-window switches on the Toyota and Chevrolet vehicles after receiving reports of fires and short circuits.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/fires-prompt-intensified-investigations-of-1-4-million-toyotas-and-342000-chevy-trailblazers/', 'snippet': 'Federal investigators are examining the power-window switches on the Toyota and Chevrolet vehicles after receiving reports of fires and short circuits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has intensified investigations into whether 1.4 million Toyotas and almost 342,000 General Motors sport utility vehicles may have defective power-window switches that could lead to smoke and fire conditions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fires Prompt Intensified Investigations of 1.4 Million Toyotas and 342,000 Chevy TrailBlazers', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nissan Motor Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:37:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29ce69a3-e17a-5b36-afcc-4702ecc8e670', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29ce69a3-e17a-5b36-afcc-4702ecc8e670'}, {'abstract': 'People infected with H.I.V. have more heart attacks and have them earlier in life, researchers have found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/health/heart-attacks-are-much-more-frequent-in-hiv-patients.html', 'snippet': 'People infected with H.I.V. have more heart attacks and have them earlier in life, researchers have found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike Godfrey was 19 when he found out he had H.I.V.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19cardiac_cnd/19cardiac_cnd-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heart Trouble Early and Often in H.I.V. Patients', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heart Trouble Early and Often In H.I.V. Patients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholesterol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood Pressure', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the American College of Cardiology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:40:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c9b7a0b-72c2-53c2-afd1-531e2d2dac41', 'word_count': 1155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c9b7a0b-72c2-53c2-afd1-531e2d2dac41'}, {'abstract': 'The trillions of germs living in and around your body; the mysterious third voyage of a 15th-century explorer; and new findings on cardiac deaths among patients with H.I.V.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2012/06/19/science/19science_pod.html', 'snippet': 'The trillions of germs living in and around your body; the mysterious third voyage of a 15th-century explorer; and new findings on cardiac deaths among patients with H.I.V.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trillions of germs living in and around your body; the mysterious third voyage of a 15th-century explorer; and new findings on cardiac deaths among patients with H.I.V.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The trillions of germs living in and around your body; the mysterious third voyage of a 15th-century explorer; and new findings on cardiac deaths among patients with H.I.V.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:51:29+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/f977d491-e2ad-59ec-a094-7ca8a402dc77', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/f977d491-e2ad-59ec-a094-7ca8a402dc77'}, {'abstract': 'What does a 350,000-mirror gamble on solar power look like?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/17/magazine/a-bet-on-the-sun.html', 'snippet': 'What does a 350,000-mirror gamble on solar power look like?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Out in the Mojave Desert in California, a power plant that could eventually generate enough electricity for 140,000 homes hopes to get its moment in the sun soon. When the $2.2 billion solar thermal plant known as Ivanpah is completed — sometime next year, if all goes according to plan — nearly 350,000 mirrors on 3,600 acres will reflect light onto boilers. Steam will power turbines, which will generate electricity that flows to California homes. It will be the largest such plant in the world. These “solar workhorses of the desert,” says V. John White, an analyst in Sacramento and an advocate for renewable energy, “can produce a lot of high-quality energy in the way that other renewable energies can’t do. And there are only a handful of places on the planet that have solar radiation that good.” But some opponents have criticized the Obama administration for pushing solar projects that don’t pan out. The solar-panel maker Solyndra declared bankruptcy last year despite receiving $528 million in federally guaranteed loans, while BrightSource Energy, one of Ivanpah’s developers, has benefited from a similar $1.6 billion government loan. It’s expensive harnessing the sun. And the costs go beyond construction. BrightSource says that it has spent more than $56 million relocating desert tortoises. JULIE BOSMAN', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bet on the Sun', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bet on the Sun', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BrightSource Energy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:55:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac1cdb40-aebd-5013-a0aa-de632fc5d6cf', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac1cdb40-aebd-5013-a0aa-de632fc5d6cf'}, {'abstract': 'It’s becoming cool to say “Hook ‘Em Horns” on a golf course. The University of Texas men’s golf team recently won the N.C.A.A. title, and a current and future Longhorn both played well at the U.S. Open.', 'web_url': 'https://onpar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/at-the-u-s-open-the-look-of-a-longhorn-dynasty/', 'snippet': 'It’s becoming cool to say “Hook ‘Em Horns” on a golf course. The University of Texas men’s golf team recently won the N.C.A.A. title, and a current and future Longhorn both played well at the U.S. Open.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The University of Texas is becoming known for more than its football and basketball prowess, thanks to the recent success of its men’s golf team. The Longhorns just won the N.C.A.A. title, and can count on having two up-and-coming talents as part of their team for the next few years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Look of a Longhorn Dynasty at the U.S. Open', 'kicker': 'On Par', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Golf)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hossler, Beau', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spieth, Jordan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Texas at Austin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T17:58:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanne C. Gerstner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanne', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Gerstner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/585530f0-58a1-5ab5-92a9-927a1f081121', 'word_count': 498, 'uri': 'nyt://article/585530f0-58a1-5ab5-92a9-927a1f081121'}, {'abstract': 'A Bronx middle-school teacher who blogs about her experiences writes: "My students don’t have it easy. But every year I go to prom, and I see them at graduation.  They are happy, looking their best, feeling successful, cheering for themselves and for one another.  I see their parents snapping pictures of them, and hugging them, and smiling proudly.  And I realize that for many kids, that is a rare occasion." When some of the children can\'t afford prom and graduation, some people are happy to help, because  "feeling for one day that they have done something worth celebrating is a cause worth investing in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/18/too-poor-for-their-own-graduation/', 'snippet': 'A Bronx middle-school teacher who blogs about her experiences writes: "My students don’t have it easy. But every year I go to prom, and I see them at graduation.  They are happy, looking their best, feeling successful, cheering for themselves and ...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Poor for Their Own Graduation', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By LAURA KLEIN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KLEIN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f42cbdc-7911-5afe-a2e4-9abf24882bd0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f42cbdc-7911-5afe-a2e4-9abf24882bd0'}, {'abstract': 'In a trial, those on statins were significantly more likely than those on placebo to report that their energy level had declined.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/statin-drugs-cause-fatigue-in-some-people/', 'snippet': 'In a trial, those on statins were significantly more likely than those on placebo to report that their energy level had declined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many observational reports have suggested that statin drugs cause fatigue in some people, and now a randomized trial has found further evidence for the effect.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/11/health/well_risks/well_risks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 215, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption