g, smoking and using recreational drugs were not.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/boxers-or-briefs-choice-may-harm-fertility/', 'snippet': 'Manual work and some other modifiable behaviors were associated with abnormal semen in a study of British men who sought fertility help. Drinking, smoking and using recreational drugs were not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Drinking, smoking and using recreational drugs probably will not reduce a man’s fertility, a new study suggests — but working on a road crew might.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 214, 'width': 215, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/05/21/health/well_patterns/well_patterns-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Job May Affect Fertility, but a Beer May Not', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vital Signs | Patterns: Job May Affect Fertility, but a Beer May Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infertility', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lingerie and Underwear', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:03:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e91deb60-88ed-5748-84ba-54b497bbf566', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e91deb60-88ed-5748-84ba-54b497bbf566'}, {'abstract': 'Do you think magnet schools still matter? How important is integration as a goal for New York City’s schools?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/do-magnet-schools-still-matter/', 'snippet': 'Do you think magnet schools still matter? How important is integration as a goal for New York City’s schools?', 'lead_paragraph': 'As detailed in Sunday’s Metropolitan cover story, “Integrating a School, One Child at a Time,” four elementary schools in Brooklyn’s District 14 won a federal magnet grant in 2010 for approximately $1.5 million over three years to desegregate. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Magnet Schools Still Matter?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magnet Schools', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:04:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a42a604-a541-57e0-b673-ee2f96feabf1', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a42a604-a541-57e0-b673-ee2f96feabf1'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook has bought an Israeli start-up company called face.com that can scan images in real time and identify the people in them. Facebook has worked with the company for years, but now it needs to make more effort applying the technology to mobile devices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/facebook-acquires-israeli-facial-recognition-company/', 'snippet': 'Facebook has bought an Israeli start-up company called face.com that can scan images in real time and identify the people in them. Facebook has worked with the company for years, but now it needs to make more effort applying the technology to mobi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facebook, the largest repository of pictures anywhere and at any time in history, has acquired an Israeli company, called face.com, that makes facial recognition technology. Neither company disclosed the sale price nor the other terms of the deal.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facebook Acquires Israeli Facial Recognition Company', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:06:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78eed8b4-7ef0-5c5a-869d-95e2c75b025a', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78eed8b4-7ef0-5c5a-869d-95e2c75b025a'}, {'abstract': 'Even though there are thousands of people in New York City who work as doormen, only a few hundred are women. And the pace of change has been glacial.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/nyregion/doormen-and-building-superintendents-still-rarely-women-in-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'Even though there are thousands of people in New York City who work as doormen, only a few hundred are women. And the pace of change has been glacial.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Monique Catus stood at the entrance of an elegant Art Deco apartment building on East 51st Street one day this spring, with a smile on her face and pristine white gloves on her hands. A little girl trotted by, she later recounted, looked up at her, and then looked at her mother. She was confused.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/19appraisal/19appraisal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Women Are Still a Rarity in Building Service Jobs', 'kicker': 'The Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At the Door or on the Roof, Women Are Still a Rarity In Building Service Jobs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building Service Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doormen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peterson, Amy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nontraditional Employment for Women', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:18:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f425b30-887b-5072-ba13-0589d34ea5ea', 'word_count': 922, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f425b30-887b-5072-ba13-0589d34ea5ea'}, {'abstract': 'If a war goes badly, declare victory and get out. That seems to be the Morgan Stanley strategy for the Facebook I.P.O. debacle.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/morgan-stanley-declares-victory/', 'snippet': 'If a war goes badly, declare victory and get out. That seems to be the Morgan Stanley strategy for the Facebook I.P.O. debacle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Morgan Stanley, with Facebook egg all over its face, has adopted the strategy memorably advocated by Senator George Aiken in 1966: Declare victory, and get out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morgan Stanley Declares Victory', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorman, James P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandberg, Sheryl K', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerberg, Mark E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d9d9869-ddf1-5a17-9269-4abca10df6e9', 'word_