', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the third inning of the New York Gothams’ first game on Governors Island on Saturday, a batter hit a towering fly ball to shallow left field.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Bounce, You’re Out, at the Old Ball Game', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That One-Bounce Catch Meant the Batter Was Out, in 1864', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History (Academic Subject)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Governors Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T18:57:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Palmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Palmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95ba2326-588e-516e-ac38-9220d524c693', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95ba2326-588e-516e-ac38-9220d524c693'}, {'abstract': 'Sonos, which makes home audio equipment for listening to digital music, is raising $135 million from a group of investors that includes a couple of former Apple executives.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/sonos-gets-boost-from-former-apple-executives-other-investors/', 'snippet': 'Sonos, which makes home audio equipment for listening to digital music, is raising $135 million from a group of investors that includes a couple of former Apple executives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sonos is a company that sometimes gets compared to Apple because it designs the hardware and software for its products, a line of home audio equipment for listening to digital music. Now the company is raising money from a group of investors that includes a couple of former Apple executives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sonos Gets Boost From Former Apple Executives and Other Investors', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sonos Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17eede25-0796-5f52-82e9-233567d40211', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17eede25-0796-5f52-82e9-233567d40211'}, {'abstract': 'Large predators like coyotes and foxes that aren’t typically associated with Lyme disease transmission may have a big impact on the spread of the disease.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/predators-prey-and-lyme-disease/', 'snippet': 'Large predators like coyotes and foxes that aren’t typically associated with Lyme disease transmission may have a big impact on the spread of the disease.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deer ticks are aptly named, in a sense; a Northeastern deer can carry over 1,000 of these ticks on its body. But as far as humans are concerned, the ticks might be more relevantly called mouse ticks. That’s because white-footed mice and other small mammals, not deer, are now known by scientists to be major carriers of Lyme disease.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Predators, Prey and Lyme Disease', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'key