hether the reproductive hormone progesterone can reduce mortality and long-term disability if administered within hours of the injury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late one evening last December, 18-year-old Michelle Vaquero was crossing a busy street in San Jose, Calif., when a car slammed into her. She landed more than 30 feet away. An ambulance rushed her to Santa Clara Valley Medical Center, where doctors diagnosed traumatic brain injury. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19BRAI_SPAN/19BRAI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hormonal Remedy for Brain Injuries Is Explored', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Hormonal Remedy for Brain Injuries Is Explored', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institutes of Health', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hormones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traumatic Brain Injury', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:33:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tuller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tuller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/634aecdb-b4f7-59c5-a6a0-e5a8106f68b0', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/634aecdb-b4f7-59c5-a6a0-e5a8106f68b0'}, {'abstract': 'But the Camerkozy types prevailed.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/a-mythical-anniversary/', 'snippet': 'But the Camerkozy types prevailed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’re coming up on the second anniversary of my piece “Myths of Austerity“, in which I tried to knock down the simply insane conventional wisdom then gelling among Very Serious People. Intellectually it was, I think I can say without false modesty, a huge win; I (and those of like mind) have been right about everything. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mythical Anniversary', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:34:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b080b2f-3e2b-56c3-9a26-7b5c581145c0', 'word_count': 179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b080b2f-3e2b-56c3-9a26-7b5c581145c0'}, {'abstract': 'Prosecutors in Florida released audio recordings and transcripts of six phone conversations between George Zimmerman and his wife, Shellie, when he was in Seminole County jail in April.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/transcripts-of-conversations-between-zimmermans-are-released/', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors in Florida released audio recordings and transcripts of six phone conversations between George Zimmerman and his wife, Shellie, when he was in Seminole County jail in April.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recorded conversations from jail, George Zimmerman and his wife, Shellie, discussed how to move tens of thousands of dollars from the money that flowed into an online defense fund he set up to credit union accounts under her name and into his sister’s account, according to audio recordings of their conversations and court documents released in Florida on Monday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transcripts of Conversations Between Zimmermans Are Released', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, Shellie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:40:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f571355-bb23-54a1-aefb-e7a4ea1a3e2e', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f571355-bb23-54a1-aefb-e7a4ea1a3e2e'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Brantley on new plays by Ella Hickson (“Boys”) and the Belarus Free Theater (“Minsk, 2011″).', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/london-theater-journal-imagination-from-despair-in-edinburgh-and-minsk/', 'snippet': 'Ben Brantley on new plays by Ella Hickson (“Boys”) and the Belarus Free Theater (“Minsk, 2011″).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t bother telling the title characters of “Boys,” Ella Hickson’s play at the Soho Theater, to clean up their room. They’re beyond hope, in every sense of the phrase. In addition to the usual clutter of bottles, boxes and stolen street signs that passes for interior decoration among university students, fat bags of trash occupy a wall by the stove. In the tenants’ defense, allow me to note that they’re not just making excuses when they say they can’t do a thing about it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Imagination From Despair in Edinburgh and Minsk', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acker, Kathy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hickson, Ella', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belarus Free Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Edinburgh (Scotland)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:47:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/262115d1-c193-507a-9e55-c084104014ab', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/262115d1-c193-507a-9e55-c084104014ab'}, {'abstract': 'At its best, the food at Battersby is thoughtful, poised and occasionally revelatory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/dining/reviews/battersby-restaurant-thrives-on-smith-street-in-cobble-hill-brooklyn-hungry-city.html', 'snippet': 'At its best, the food at Battersby is thoughtful, poised and occasionally revelatory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IT is elbow to elbow at Battersby on a Saturday night, at tables barely wide enough for a game of checkers. “How am I supposed to talk to you?” a flummoxed swain whispers. Couples cleave to a wall; latecomers hunch at the bar. Outside it is Smith Street in Cobble Hill, a formerly insalubrious strip (weren’t they all?) that is now just a Marc Jacobs away from becoming Brooklyn’s Bleecker. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/dining/20HUNGRY2_SPAN/20HUNGRY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/dining/20HUNGRY2_SPAN/20HUNGRY2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/dining/20HUNGRY2_SPAN/20HUNGRY2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'cr