ith its strategic plan.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/nelson-peltz-takes-5-1-stake-in-lazard/', 'snippet': 'Nelson Peltz’s Trian Fund Management says it now owns a 5.1 percent stake in Lazard Ltd., stressing that it believes the investment bank is undervalued but on the right track with its strategic plan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nelson Peltz‘s Trian Fund Management said on Monday that it now owns a 5.1 percent stake in Lazard, stressing that it believes the investment bank is undervalued but on the right track with its strategic plan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nelson Peltz Takes 5.1% Stake in Lazard', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peltz, Nelson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lazard Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:54:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a3d6149-c74b-5c98-b884-0d6672cedc79', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a3d6149-c74b-5c98-b884-0d6672cedc79'}, {'abstract': 'As the rotation of Earth starts to slow, and days and nights lengthen, profound uncertainty seems the new normal for the world, as seen from the perspective of a girl coming of age in this novel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/books/the-age-of-miracles-by-karen-thompson-walker.html', 'snippet': 'As the rotation of Earth starts to slow, and days and nights lengthen, profound uncertainty seems the new normal for the world, as seen from the perspective of a girl coming of age in this novel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1954 Ray Bradbury story “All Summer in a Day,” Earthlings who have colonized Venus see the Sun shine only once every seven years, and then only for a couple of hours: The rest of the time it rains, and a little girl, who has recently arrived from Earth, is mocked by her schoolmates for describing her memories of what the Sun looked like from home. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/book/book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/book/book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1487, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/book/book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/book/book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 211, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Normalcy Grinds to a Halt', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Normalcy Grinds To a Halt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Age of Miracles (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Karen Thompson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T19:55:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d650c5a-50a1-5340-85d2-372794fd8ece', 'word_count': 1071, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d650c5a-50a1-5340-85d2-372794fd8ece'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court ruled that sales representatives for pharmaceutical companies did not qualify for overtime pay under federal law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/business/justices-Back-Drug-Industry-on-Overtime.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court ruled that sales representatives for pharmaceutical companies did not qualify for overtime pay under federal law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Representatives of pharmaceutical companies who visit doctors’ offices to promote their companies’ products are not entitled to overtime pay, the Supreme Court ruled on Monday in a 5-to-4 decision that broke along ideological lines. A contrary decision would have exposed the pharmaceutical industry to billions of dollars in potential liability.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/business/Bizcourt/Bizcourt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 870, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/business/Bizcourt/Bizcourt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1741, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Justic