y-of-digital/', 'snippet': 'For those of us who have switched to digital e-readers, the e-book shopping experience and reading on iPads and Kindles has zero nostalgia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past weekend, while visiting New York on a short work-related trip, I was\xa0reminded\xa0of how much I miss printed books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An E-Book Fan, Missing the Smell of Paper and Glue', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amazon Kindle', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Books and Readers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T20:08:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20358915-7c2e-56e6-af0d-d6bd0aedcc50', 'word_count': 465, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20358915-7c2e-56e6-af0d-d6bd0aedcc50'}, {'abstract': 'The GTM component car could outperform a C6 Corvette at a fraction of the cost of the C5 donor vehicle. Only trick: you’d have to build it yourself.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/factory-five-gen-2-gtm-wringing-small-miracles-from-the-corvette-parts-bin/', 'snippet': 'The GTM component car could outperform a C6 Corvette at a fraction of the cost of the C5 donor vehicle. Only trick: you’d have to build it yourself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cranberry bogs of southeastern Massachusetts are normally quite serene. But this area also happens to be the headquarters of Factory Five Racing, where I recently made a pilgrimage to drive the company’s second-generation GTM supercar. And once I was behind the wheel of the midengine, 420-horsepower GTM, the two-lane roads wending past the cranberry bogs were no longer quite so peaceful.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Factory Five Gen 2 GTM: Wringing Small Miracles From the Corvette Parts Bin', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T20:15:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ezra Dyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ezra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f88dac5-4d4f-5697-b08a-4c3b2fd05efb', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f88dac5-4d4f-5697-b08a-4c3b2fd05efb'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Kuo breaks down the album, “Da Mind of Traxman,” by Traxman, the Chicago ghetto-house and juke D.J.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/charting-traxman/', 'snippet': 'Andrew Kuo breaks down the album, “Da Mind of Traxman,” by Traxman, the Chicago ghetto-house and juke D.J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the world of dance music, Traxman is known as a longtime Chicago ghetto-house and juke D.J. who also helped develop the stripped-down, kick-drum-heavy footwork genre. His recent album, “Da Mind of Traxman,” out now on Planet Mu, is fast, playful, sample-heavy and chaotic. Traxman is playing June 23 at the Knitting Factory. The artist Andrew Kuo breaks it down, track by track.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charting Traxman', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T20:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Kuo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf9c7bec-a774-52ad-84a2-3bd2cfc242ab', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf9c7bec-a774-52ad-84a2-3bd2cfc242ab'}, {'abstract': 'The French company has bought 20 percent of Zoom Advertising, a small agency that comes with considerable symbolic significance, the company said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/technology/19iht-publicis19.html', 'snippet': 'The French company has bought 20 percent of Zoom Advertising, a small agency that comes with considerable symbolic significance, the company said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Publicis Groupe of France said Monday that it had acquired a stake in an advertising agency based in Ramallah, on the West Bank, in what it described as the first equity investment by any of the big Western marketing companies in the Palestinian territories.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Publicis Makes Advertising's First Foray Into Palestinian Territories", 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ad Giant Gets Share of Firm In West Bank', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WPP Group Plc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'g