', '_id': 'nyt://article/1889fb69-d9cc-5eab-bd0d-c1efe883f931', 'word_count': 255, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1889fb69-d9cc-5eab-bd0d-c1efe883f931'}, {'abstract': 'As we learn more about the trillions of microbes we carry around, some scientists want to be like wildlife managers — nurturing the good and weeding out the bad.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/science/studies-of-human-microbiome-yield-new-insights.html', 'snippet': 'As we learn more about the trillions of microbes we carry around, some scientists want to be like wildlife managers — nurturing the good and weeding out the bad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a century, doctors have waged war against bacteria, using antibiotics as their weapons. But that relationship is changing as scientists become more familiar with the 100 trillion microbes that call us home — collectively known as the microbiome.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19MICR/19MICR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 622, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19MICR/19MICR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1243, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19MICR/19MICR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19MICR/19MICR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/science/19MICR/19MICR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subTy