12/06/18/egypts-generals-hollow-out-its-presidency/', 'snippet': 'By stripping Egypt’s new president of many powers, are members of the ruling military council appointed by Hosni Mubarak setting him up to fail?', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — As my colleague David Kirkpatrick reports, the apparent victory of Mohamed Morsi, the Muslim Brotherhood’s candidate, in Egypt’s presidential election was complicated on Monday by legal maneuvers from the ruling military council which cast doubt on what power the office now holds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Generals Hollow Out Its Presidency', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shafik, Ahmed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Council of the Armed Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T21:27:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/748838b7-a926-580a-ac1d-d26b8b10e6eb', 'word_count': 839, 'uri': 'nyt://article/748838b7-a926-580a-ac1d-d26b8b10e6eb'}, {'abstract': 'Karl Ove Knausgaard’s “My Struggle,” just published in the United States, has caused a furor in Norway for its candid look at the author’s family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/books/a-debate-over-karl-ove-knausgaards-my-struggle.html', 'snippet': 'Karl Ove Knausgaard’s “My Struggle,” just published in the United States, has caused a furor in Norway for its candid look at the author’s family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until the recent publication of “My Struggle,” a 3,600-page work in six volumes, the career of the Norwegian writer Karl Ove Knausgaard had followed a fairly conventional trajectory: A young man besotted by the beauty of words, nature, music and painting writes a coming-of-age novel that earns him prizes and praise and then tries something more ambitious, which becomes an international best seller and wins more prizes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/KNAUSGAARD/KNAUSGAARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 710, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/KNAUSGAARD/KNAUSGAARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1420, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/KNAUSGAARD/KNAUSGAARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/KNAUSGAARD/KNAUSGAARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/arts/KNAUSGAARD/KNAUSGAARD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge'