ught to America as children.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Media and Obama’s Immigration Gambit', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-18T21:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71d7129b-3b9b-5a3b-ae4f-4823655359bf', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71d7129b-3b9b-5a3b-ae4f-4823655359bf'}, {'abstract': 'A neighborhood thick with hipsters, like East Nashville, is an indicator that good food is not far away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/20/dining/20120620-NASHVILLE.html', 'snippet': 'A neighborhood thick with hipsters, like East Nashville, is an indicator that good food is not far away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A neighborhood thick with hipsters, like East Nashville, is an indicator that good food is not far away.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/dining/20120620-NASHVILLE-slide-VZH5/20120620-NASHVILLE-slide-VZH5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/dining/20120620-NASHVILLE-slide-VZH5/20120620-NASHVILLE-slide-VZH5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/dining/20120620-NASHVILLE-slide