_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kimberly Seals Allers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kimberly', 'middlename': 'Seals', 'lastname': 'Allers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dd3a679-0215-53ec-bcc5-54948e808eb9', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dd3a679-0215-53ec-bcc5-54948e808eb9'}, {'abstract': 'Sales of new software licenses jumped, sending revenue higher for the quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/technology/oracles-results-surpass-analysts-estimates.html', 'snippet': 'Sales of new software licenses jumped, sending revenue higher for the quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO (AP) — Oracle reported financial results late Monday that exceeded Wall Street’s expectations and said it would buy back up to $10 billion of its shares. But the bigger surprise was the timing of the company’s announcement; the numbers were not expected to be released until Thursday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oracle’s Results Surpass Analysts’ Expectations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oracle’s Results Surpass Analysts’ Expectations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oracle Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T01:03:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By REUTERS', 'person': [], 'organization': 'REUTERS'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3813bc5a-b95a-5786-893a-c7585a05ac20', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3813bc5a-b95a-5786-893a-c7585a05ac20'}, {'abstract': 'If America wants democracy for Egyptians, it must stop supporting the military council.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/opinion/the-betrayal-of-egypts-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'If America wants democracy for Egyptians, it must stop supporting the military council.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CairoPreliminary election results show that the Muslim Brotherhood’s Mohamed Morsi is likely to become Egypt’s next president. But even if Mr. Morsi is declared the official winner later this week, Egypt’s first popular presidential election will not have been a democratic milestone.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Betrayal of Egypt’s Revolution', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Betrayal of Egypt’s Revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mubarak, Hosni', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Council of the Armed Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Aid', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T01:10:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sara Khorshid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khorshid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f75c35a7-b8cd-5884-8a6e-f72b1a691f3e', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f75c35a7-b8cd-5884-8a6e-f72b1a691f3e'}, {'abstract': 'Sales at physical electronics stores have declined an average of 2.6 percent a year in the last five years, while sales online have risen an average of 14.7 percent a year in that period.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/business/electronics-stores-struggle-to-adapt-to-changing-market.html', 'snippet': 'Sales at physical electronics stores have declined an average of 2.6 percent a year in the last five years, while sales online have risen an average of 14.7 percent a year in that period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as Best Buy insists it can get out of its current predicament, competitors are circling, as everyone tries to prove one point: that electronics stores can thrive.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/business/SHOP/SHOP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/19/business/SHOP/SHOP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/business/SHOP/SHOP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/business/SHOP/SHOP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Electronics Retailers Scramble to Adapt to Changing Market', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoping to Outlive Best Buy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electronics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Best BUY Company Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Behavior', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T01:11:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Clifford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clifford', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2932a387-699e-5705-aa32-cdb2c3b7f09f', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2932a387-699e-5705-aa32-cdb2c3b7f09f'}, {'abstract': 'Greece and Germany will face off Friday with a berth in the semifinals of Euro 2012 at stake. But the two teams met in an even more momentous game back in 1972.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/and-now-for-something-completely-different/', 'snippet': 'Greece and Germany will face off Friday with a berth in the semifinals of Euro 2012 at stake. But the two teams met in an even more momentous game back in 1972.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greece and Germany will face off Friday with a berth in the semifinals of Euro 2012 at stake. The two teams met in an even more momentous game back in 1972.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And Now for Something Completely Different', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARCHIMEDES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beckenbauer, Franz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T01:14:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca80c752-fbbe-52ce-a3bd-406f842e7aa6', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca80c752-fbbe-52ce-a3bd-406f842e7aa6'}, {'abstract': 'More on the issue of free speech vs. attacks on dignity, with guest columnist Jeremy Waldron and reader comments.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/hate-speech-and-free-speech-part-two/', 'snippet': 'More on the issue of free speech vs. attacks on dignity, with guest columnist Jeremy Waldron and reader comments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Readers of my column about Jeremy Waldron’s new book, “The Harm in Hate Speech,” wondered how the hate speech regulations Waldron calls for could be implemented, and wondered, too, whether key terms like “dignity” and “harm” could be defined in ways that would avoid the dangers of imprecision and the slippery slope. The editors and I have invited Professor Waldron to respond to these and other questions. One poster asked if I was reporting on Waldron’s arguments or endorsing them. I was endorsing them, as I have already (implicitly) done in “There’s No Such Thing as Free Speech … And It’s a Good Thing, Too” and other publications. — S.F.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hate Speech and Free Speech, Part Two', 'kicker': 'Stanley Fish', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T01:15:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Waldron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5309337b-cf96-5c3f-ae92-30d85354f58c', 'word_count': 1792, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5309337b-cf96-5c3f-ae92-30d85354f58c'}, {'abstract': 'Dharun Ravi, who was convicted of using a webcam to spy on his roommate, Tyler Clementi, is expected to be released Tuesday after serving 20 days in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/nyregion/officials-will-not-seek-to-deport-dharun-ravi-over-rutgers-case.html', 'snippet': 'Dharun Ravi, who was convicted of using a webcam to spy on his roommate, Tyler Clementi, is expected to be released Tuesday after serving 20 days in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Immigration officials said Monday that they would not try to deport Dharun Ravi, the Indian-born 20-year-old convicted in March of using a webcam to spy on his roommate having sex with another man in their dormitory at Rutgers University.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rutgers Case Will Not Spur Deportation, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rutgers Case Will Not Spur Deportation, Officials Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravi, Dharun', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hate Crimes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clementi, Tyler', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T01:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Zernike', 'perso