ijing — if they only knew — would help in his efforts to gain legal rights for farmers, the disabled and people forced into abortions or ster...', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGKOK — Even after years of detention, rough treatment and harassment in his rural village in China, Chen Guangcheng seemed to hold tight to the belief that Beijing was a shining city on a hill, a place where officials in the central government — if they only knew — would look favorably on his efforts to win legal rights for beleaguered plaintiffs over illegal land grabs and forced abortions. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/blogs/CGC-rdv/CGC-rdv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/blogs/CGC-rdv/CGC-rdv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1395, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Activist, Now in New York, Takes a Harder Look at Beijing', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T03:26:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/074c9859-06f9-5328-80d6-e4cfc2e7fcfe', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/074c9859-06f9-5328-80d6-e4cfc2e7fcfe'}, {'abstract': 'Asian immigrants have pushed the United States’ population of Asian descent to a record 18.2 million and helped make Asians the country’s fastest-growing racial group, a study says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/us/asians-surpass-hispanics-as-biggest-immigrant-wave.html', 'snippet': 'Asian immigrants have pushed the United States’ population of Asian descent to a record 18.2 million and helped make Asians the country’s fastest-growing racial group, a study says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asians have surpassed Hispanics as the largest wave of new immigrants to the United States, pushing the population of Asian descent to a record 18.2 million and helping to make Asians the fastest-growing racial group in the country, according to a study released Tuesday by the Pew Research Center. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Shift, Biggest Wave of Migrants Is Now Asian', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Shift, Biggest Wave Of Migrants Is Now Asian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T03:30:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Semple', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Semple', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8062d82e-de58-5d14-b13f-9f8f0701087e', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8062d82e-de58-5d14-b13f-9f8f0701087e'}, {'abstract': 'Asians have overtaken Hispanics as the largest stream of new immigrants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/19/us/asians-are-immigrations-new-face.html', 'snippet': 'Asians have overtaken Hispanics as the largest stream of new immigrants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Asians have overtaken Hispanics as the largest stream of new immigrants.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asians Are Immigrations New Face', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T03:34:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/00168258-a355-58fe-8e3d-abc5c15b25ca', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/00168258-a355-58fe-8e3d-abc5c15b25ca'}, {'abstract': 'If conservative evangelicals are serious about making common political cause with black Protestants, they must rethink their approach to America’s history and its modern-day problems.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/18/southern-baptist-convergence/', 'snippet': 'If conservative evangelicals are serious about making common political cause with black Protestants, they must rethink their approach to America’s history and its modern-day problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The secular media usually ignores the thousands of pastors, missionaries and church volunteers who gather every summer for the annual meeting of the Southern Baptist Convention. This year is different. Everyone from PBS to the Huffington Post is buzzing with anticipation — and not because they are awaiting the tedious discussion of committee reports and budgets necessary to manage the country’s largest evangelical denomination. The reason for all the excitement is this: the 2012 convention, which opens Tuesday in New Orleans, will elect a black man as president for the first time in Southern Baptist history. This is no small thing for a denomination that separated in 1845 from its northern brethren in order to defend the right of Southern slaveholders to serve as missionaries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Southern Baptist Convergence', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evangelical Movement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ministers (Protestant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Theological Seminary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Baptist Convention', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T03:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Molly Worthen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Molly', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Worthen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4db7d6af-7c37-5751-842d-df5dba4b3d66', 'word_count': 1908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4db7d6af-7c37-5751-842d-df5dba4b3d66'}, {'abstract': 'The English-speaking children of Mexicans returning because of deportations, tougher state laws and unemployment struggle to adjust, often going to schools that are not equipped to integrate them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/world/americas/american-born-children-struggle-to-adjust-in-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'The English-speaking children of Mexicans returning because of deportations, tougher state laws and unemployment struggle to adjust, often going to schools that are not equipped to integrate them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IZÚCAR DE MATAMOROS, Mexico — Jeffrey Isidoro sat near the door of his fifth-grade classroom here in central Mexico, staring outside through designer glasses that, like his Nike sneakers and Nike backpack, signaled a life lived almost entirely in the United States. His parents are at home in Mexico. Jeffrey is lost.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/world/IMMIGRATION_span/IMMIGRATION-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {