ogether with violent ones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/nyregion/at-a-new-jersey-halfway-house-a-volatile-mix-fuels-a-murder.html', 'snippet': 'As financial pressures grow, officials are using vast halfway houses as dumping grounds, The New York Times found. At Delaney Hall in Newark, low-level offenders are thrown together with violent ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWARK — Derek West Harris wore tailored pants, soft sweaters and shiny shoes. People called him D-Nice. His easygoing manner drew customers to his barber’s chair at Million Dollar Kutz in Newark, a shop where he was known as much for his conversation as for his trims. He chatted about religion, relationships and cars, which he loved.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/JP-UNLOCKED1/JP-UNLOCKED1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/JP-UNLOCKED1/JP-UNLOCKED1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1342, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/JP-UNLOCKED1/JP-UNLOCKED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/JP-UNLOCKED1/JP-UNLOCKED1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/19/nyregion/JP-UNLOCKED1/JP-UNLOCKED1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 101, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Penal Unit, a Volatile Mix Fuels a Murder', 'kicker': 'Unlocked | Part Three', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Penal Unit, A Volatile Mix Fuels a Murder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiVincenzo, Joseph N Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Education Centers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Essex County (NJ)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T03:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/402c0152-5599-5997-85b0-8af919e59411', 'word_count': 3223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/402c0152-5599-5997-85b0-8af919e59411'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government will seek the death penalty in the case of a man at the center of a legal custody battle between the State of Rhode Island and federal prosecutors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/us/rhode-island-death-penalty-sought-as-state-feared.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government will seek the death penalty in the case of a man at the center of a legal custody battle between the State of Rhode Island and federal prosecutors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government will seek the death penalty in the case of Jason W. Pleau, the man at the center of a legal custody battle between the State of Rhode Island and federal prosecutors. Gov. Lincoln Chafee had initially refused to hand over Mr. Pleau, who is accused of killing a gas station attendant during a robbery in 2010 in Woonsocket, R.I., to federal authorities, arguing that doing so could expose him to the death penalty, which Rhode Island does not have. A federal appeals court ordered the transfer last month. On Monday, federal prosecutors filed a notice of intent to seek a death sentence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rhode Island: Death Penalty Sought, as State Feared', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rhode Island: Death Penalty Sought, as State Feared', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pleau, Jason Wayne', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chafee, Lincoln', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhode Island', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T03:43:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9850960d-dbe3-5861-b986-1d69013287c9', 'word_count': 106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9850960d-dbe3-5861-b986-1d69013287c9'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets knuckleballer manhandled the Orioles and became the first pitcher to record back-to-back one-hitters since Dave Stieb in 1988.', 'web_url': 'https