was evident at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Which Wayne Rooney Will Return for England?', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rooney, Wayne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T04:30:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Ruthven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruthven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3218a8d5-5cf1-5645-be2b-28d52358a4ff', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3218a8d5-5cf1-5645-be2b-28d52358a4ff'}, {'abstract': 'Comments from the two countries’ foreign ministries follow a call by the presidents of the United States, Russia and France for a peaceful settlement to the 20-year conflict.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/world/europe/leaders-call-for-end-to-armenia-azerbaijan-war.html', 'snippet': 'Comments from the two countries’ foreign ministries follow a call by the presidents of the United States, Russia and France for a peaceful settlement to the 20-year conflict.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A day after the presidents of the United States, Russia and France issued a joint statement calling for a peaceful settlement to the more than 20-year war between Armenia and Azerbaijan over the disputed territory of Nagorno-Karabakh, the two enemies publicly blamed each other Tuesday for failing to resolve the conflict.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Armenia and Azerbaijan Blame Each Other for Protracted War', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Armenia and Azerbaijan Blame Each Other for Conflict', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARMENIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nagorno-Karabakh', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Azerbaijan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:16:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/392c516e-cd09-50ac-a206-b13ec066d8b2', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/392c516e-cd09-50ac-a206-b13ec066d8b2'}, {'abstract': 'An official’s comments on women’s shelters and a new national almanac’s estimates on Afghanistan’s ethnic breakdown have stirred tensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/world/asia/insurgents-strike-checkpoint-in-southern-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'An official’s comments on women’s shelters and a new national almanac’s estimates on Afghanistan’s ethnic breakdown have stirred tensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Events this week that raised questions on women’s rights and ethnic tensions have added to long-term concerns about Afghanistan after American-led forces withdraw in 2014 and new elections are held.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/world/AFGHANISTAN/AFGHANISTAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Worries About Women’s Rights and Ethnic Tensions Emerge in Afghanistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Worries About Women’s Rights and Ethnic Tensions Emerge in Afghanistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazaras (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:24:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d37da26a-51c8-553a-ab9a-ae278b9e1a3e', 'word_count': 989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d37da26a-51c8-553a-ab9a-ae278b9e1a3e'}, {'abstract': 'Upheavals in Ivory Coast, Libya, Somalia, Sudan and elsewhere drove 800,000 people to flee their countries and become refugees in 2011, the United Nations said Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/world/africa/800000-people-forced-to-flee-across-borders-in-2011-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'Upheavals in Ivory Coast, Libya, Somalia, Sudan and elsewhere drove 800,000 people to flee their countries and become refugees in 2011, the United Nations said Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Upheavals in Ivory Coast, Libya, Somalia, Sudan and elsewhere drove 800,000 people to flee their countries and become refugees in 2011, the highest number in 11 years, the United Nations said Monday in its annual report on the forcibly displaced. The office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees said that 4.3 million people in all were newly displaced last year, which includes those who stayed in their countries and those who fled. At the end of 2011, the report said, 42.5 million people were either refugees (15.2 million), internally displaced (26.4 million) or in the process of seeking asylum (895,000). The overall total was lower than the 2010 total of 43.7 million mainly because 3.2 million internally displaced people returned home, the report said. The number of people who fled their countries and became refugees last year was the highest in that category since 822,000 in 2000. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '800,000 People Forced to Flee Across Borders in 2011, Report Says', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | United Nations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '800,000 People Forced to Flee Across Borders in 2011, Report Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ivory Coast', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1146b99-7fb7-582f-af32-49fe5990b098', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1146b99-7fb7-582f-af32-49fe5990b098'}, {'abstract': 'A man wearing an explosives belt detonated it amid a group of Shiite mourners at a funeral in Diyala Province on Monday, killing at least 15 people and wounding more than 40, according to security officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/world/middleeast/iraq-bomber-attacks-funeral.html', 'snippet': 'A man wearing an explosives belt detonated it amid a group of Shiite mourners at a funeral in Diyala Province on Monday, killing at least 15 people and wounding more than 40, according to security officials.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A man wearing an explosives belt detonated it amid a group of Shiite mourners at a funeral in Diyala Province on Monday, killing at least 15 people and wounding more than 40, according to security officials. The attack came after days of strikes against mostly Shiite targets in a stepped-up campaign of sectarian violence carried out by the Sunni insurgent group Al Qaeda in Iraq. Over the past week nearly 150 Iraqis have been killed in attacks. Violence, largely sectarian in nature, has substantially increased after a period of relative calm following the withdrawal of the American military in December. The rising violence coincides with a political struggle involving Iraq’s three main factions — the Shiite majority, which controls the government, and the minority Kurds and Sunnis, who have called for a vote of no confidence against Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Bomber Attacks Funeral', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Bomber Attacks Funeral', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb52630-dec7-5c30-96bd-fda74643f70f', 'word_count': 146, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb52630-dec7-5c30-96bd-fda74643f70f'}, {'abstract': 'A Chinese spacecraft carrying three astronauts docked with an orbiting module on Monday, another first for the country as it strives to match American and Russian exploits in space.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/world/asia/china-spacecraft-docks-with-orbiting-module.html', 'snippet': 'A Chinese spacecraft carrying three astronauts docked with an orbiting module on Monday, another first for the country as it strives to match American and Russian exploits in space.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Chinese spacecraft carrying three astronauts docked with an orbiting module on Monday, another first for the country as it strives to match American and Russian exploits in space. The Shenzhou 9 capsule completed the maneuver with the Tiangong 1 module 213 miles above Earth. The astronauts will live and work in the module for several days as part of preparations for a permanent space station. The crew includes 33-year-old Liu Yang, an air force pilot and the first Chinese woman in space. The docking was a first for Chinese astronauts. In November 2011, the unmanned Shenzhou 8 successfully docked twice with Tiangong 1 by remote control. Monday’s docking also was completed by remote control from a ground base in China. A manual docking, to be carried out by one of the crew members, is scheduled for later in the mission. (AP)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Spacecraft Docks With Orbiting Module', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Spacecraft Docks With Orbiting Module', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Yang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilots', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:39:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e09f1a9-aa43-5dbc-9d99-a15400f83ba3', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e09f1a9-aa43-5dbc-9d99-a15400f83ba3'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/news-quiz-june-19-2012/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | June 19, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/011b38a3-a2b0-5567-83fc-14aaae29f59a', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/011b38a3-a2b0-5567-83fc-14aaae29f59a'}, {'abstract': 'Over the years, the focus of the censor board appears to have shifted from sex and violence to people’s “hurt sentiments.”', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/an-insiders-view-of-the-film-censor-board/', 'snippet': 'Over the years, the focus of the censor board appears to have shifted from sex and violence to people’s “hurt sentiments.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A housewife rolls in bed, mysteriously moaning all alone at night, unable to sleep. Her husband, an officer with the merchant navy, is always traveling for work. Her gawky young brother-in-law watches her every night from the bedroom door left open. In the morning, the housewife serves breakfast to her shy brother-in-law while they exchange uncomfortable glances. The same scenes get repeated for hours, only the moans keep getting louder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Insider’s View of the Film Censor Board', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deo, Abhinay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Imran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Akshay', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T05:59:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mayank Shekhar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mayank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shekhar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d4360b0-14f5-57a1-8ac2-305cbb8a0b29', 'word_count': 1523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d4360b0-14f5-57a1-8ac2-305cbb8a0b29'}, {'abstract': 'There is a culture of intolerance around us, says the chief executive officer of India’s film censor board.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/a-conversation-with-film-censor-board-chief-executive-pankaja-thakur/', 'snippet': 'There is a culture of intolerance around us, says the chief executive officer of India’s film censor board.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pankaja Thakur is the chief executive of the Central Board of Film Certification, commonly known as the Censor Board of India. The post of 