ou choose the best synonym for “anomaly”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'This question was written by Shannon Doyne. It comes from the television article “The Vampire Who Came Out in the Afternoon.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | English, June 19, 2012', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T08:29:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8c299f7-3d09-5dbd-996c-01dc769ea42b', 'word_count': 48, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8c299f7-3d09-5dbd-996c-01dc769ea42b'}, {'abstract': 'A second day of talks between Iran and six world powers began Tuesday, as negotiators sought to head off the danger of military confrontation over Tehran’s nuclear ambitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/world/middleeast/tense-iran-nuclear-talks-resume-in-moscow.html', 'snippet': 'A second day of talks between Iran and six world powers began Tuesday, as negotiators sought to head off the danger of military confrontation over Tehran’s nuclear ambitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Talks on Iran’s disputed nuclear program descended into mistrust and frustration in Moscow on Tuesday, casting doubt on whether the two sides can negotiate a way out of the escalating crisis.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/world/NUCLEAR-1/NUCLEAR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/world/NUCLEAR-1/NUCLEAR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank'