inal': 'By Ellen Barry and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76edbd33-7e51-587f-9dba-895482b82477', 'word_count': 1172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76edbd33-7e51-587f-9dba-895482b82477'}, {'abstract': '6 Q’s About the News | What Obama administration executive action was announced on June 15?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/a-new-policy-for-illegal-immigrants/', 'snippet': '6 Q’s About the News | What Obama administration executive action was announced on June 15?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Please note: Today’s edition of 6 Q’s focuses on the complex issue of immigration policy, and our questions are drawn from several sources. Those answers not found in the related article linked above can be found by clicking the link in the question.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Policy for Illegal Immigrants', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T08:56:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shannon Doyne and Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shannon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a1e1a3d-b9dc-5041-b123-bbdac7235c44', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a1e1a3d-b9dc-5041-b123-bbdac7235c44'}, {'abstract': 'The report on past job performance has become a driver of future job performance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/are-the-jobs-number-killing-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The report on past job performance has become a driver of future job performance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At precisely 8:30 a.m. on the first Friday of the month, thousands of people (including me) stare at a dull government Web site and hit refresh until they see the number: how many jobs were created or lost during the previous month. Then, with amazing speed, reports and analysis of the number are disseminated by newspapers, bank economists, independent analysts, investment newsletters and countless TV pundits. Within minutes, the national narrative is set. Either the economy is doing far worse (like last month) or far better (as in January) than anyone realized.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24economy/24economy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24economy/24economy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 534}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24economy/mag-24Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24economy/mag-24Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None