41e-8e9b-aefecd1f9263'}, {'abstract': 'The American drug store chain Walgreens has agreed to buy a 45 percent stake in Alliance Boots, the European pharmacy retailer, for $6.7 billion, in a deal that could allow Walgreens to take full control of Alliance Boots by 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/walgreens-to-take-45-stake-in-alliance-boots-for-6-7-billion/', 'snippet': 'The American drug store chain Walgreens has agreed to buy a 45 percent stake in Alliance Boots, the European pharmacy retailer, for $6.7 billion, in a deal that could allow Walgreens to take full control of Alliance Boots by 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:20 p.m. | Updated ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walgreen to Take Stake in Alliance Boots for $6.7 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Walgreen To Buy Stake In European Drug Chain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALLIANCE BOOTS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walgreen Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T11:42:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df7ba8dc-e44a-5831-830a-fe1ff818cec5', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df7ba8dc-e44a-5831-830a-fe1ff818cec5'}, {'abstract': 'If the names Monogram, Aurora and Revell instantly summon memories of “put tab A in slot B,” then you’ll recognize the design behind the iPhone covers from KitcaseUSA.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/an-iphone-case-some-assembly-required/', 'snippet': 'If the names Monogram, Aurora and Revell instantly summon memories of “put tab A in slot B,” then you’ll recognize the design behind the iPhone covers from KitcaseUSA.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the names Monogram, Aurora and Revell instantly summon memories of “put tab A in slot B,” then you’ll recognize the design behind the iPhone covers from KitcaseUSA.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An iPhone Case, Some Assembly Required', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Customized Case for iPhones, Some Assembly Required', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T11:50:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc361a10-f070-58b4-ab8f-c3ae780d073a', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc361a10-f070-58b4-ab8f-c3ae780d073a'}, {'abstract': 'If Mitt Romney moves closer to a lukewarm acquiescence of President Obama’s decision, he may be accused of flip-flopping. But candidates flip-flop when they conclude that the alternative might be more costly.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/what-obamas-immigration-decision-might-mean-for-2012/', 'snippet': 'If Mitt Romney moves closer to a lukewarm acquiescence of President Obama’s decision, he may be accused of flip-flopping. But candidates flip-flop when they conclude that the alternative might be more costly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even in an era where partisanship is on the rise, demographic changes exert a gravitational pull on policy and politics and are occasionally enough to overcome political divisions. What is more remarkable than President Obama’s decision on Friday to suspend deportations of some illegal immigrants is Republicans’ relatively passive reaction to it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Obama’s Immigration Decision Might Mean for 2012', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Hispanic Center', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T11:55:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d6e7ee9-4912-53a0-af9d-c8f15c07cdbb', 'word_count': 888, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d6e7ee9-4912-53a0-af9d-c8f15c07cdbb'}, {'abstract': 'A New Jersey family finds that a year in the Maine woods feels just right — allowing them to burrow deep, yet not lose ties with the outside.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/is-one-year-in-the-woods-enough-yes-just/', 'snippet': 'A New Jersey family finds that a year in the Maine woods feels just right — allowing them to burrow deep, yet not lose ties with the outside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moving our family from the New Jersey suburbs to the woods of Maine for a year was a big step. It took planning, perseverance and a willingness to deal with biting insects, no dishwasher, no coffeemaker, no microwave and doing laundry at the laundromat. (Thankfully, the laundromat doubles as the pub.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making the Most of a Year in the Woods', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T11:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Craig Leisher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Craig', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leisher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1de9b78a-2b5e-5bc0-a37c-5f87f8bad698', 'word_count': 707, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1de9b78a-2b5e-5bc0-a37c-5f87f8bad698'}, {'abstract': 'Hyphens can clarify a phrase and are sometimes crucial to the meaning. But if we sprinkle them heedlessly where they’re not called for, the effect is distracting at best and can be confusing.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/too-many-hyphens/', 'snippet': 'Hyphens can clarify a phrase and are sometimes crucial to the meaning. But if we sprinkle them heedlessly where they’re not called for, the effect is distracting at best and can be confusing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Notes from the newsroom on grammar, usage and style. (Some frequently asked questions are here.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Many Hyphens', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 