it and provide more services for children with special needs. This spring, they have been asking the Legislature for the authority to form coalitions, so they can pool resources that will help them fulfill their mandate. The bill seemed to be cruising along, but now the state teachers' union has thrown up a roadblock.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/19/charter-schools-face-opposition-to-plan-for-special-needs-children/', 'snippet': 'Charter schools are under increasing pressure to admit and provide more services for children with special needs. This spring, they have been asking the Legislature for the authority to form coalitions, so they can pool resources that will help th...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Charter Schools Face Opposition to Plan for Special Needs Children', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T12:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/211cf659-fe8d-5dee-a858-e284914fc92e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/211cf659-fe8d-5dee-a858-e284914fc92e'}, {'abstract': 'Many workers remain underpaid and underemployed, groups urge Facebook not to aim ads at preteens, missing the smell and feel of actual books and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/tuesday-reading-many-workers-remain-underpaid-and-underemployed/', 'snippet': 'Many workers remain underpaid and underemployed, groups urge Facebook not to aim ads at preteens, missing the smell and feel of actual books and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Many Workers Remain Underpaid and Underemployed', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T12:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60bcbe66-0c5f-5bde-924f-af5672d0a5a4', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60bcbe66-0c5f-5bde-924f-af5672d0a5a4'}, {'abstract': 'Crowding out versus solvency.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/interest-rates-varieties-of-error/', 'snippet': 'Crowding out versus solvency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote recently about how the failure of inflation to soar was one of the three key tests that classical economics, in all its forms, failed in this depression, while Keynesian economics succeeded. A second was the effect of austerity; Jared Bernstein points us to one of the many charts, this time from Jay Shambaugh, showing that euro experience looks awfully Keynesian:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Interest Rates: Varieties of Error', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T12:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1394b533-c983-52ad-b964-3fe68a8667a4', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1394b533-c983-52ad-b964-3fe68a8667a4'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, Square released software updates for Square Register, its iPad app that serves as a cash register for merchants. At the same time, it updated its Pay With Square app for customers with an iPhone or Android handset. The software upgrades will allow merchants to reward regular customers by applying discounts automatically when they return to the store.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/square-introduces-a-digital-loyalty-card/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, Square released software updates for Square Register, its iPad app that serves as a cash register for merchants. At the same time, it updated its Pay With Square app for customers with an iPhone or Android handset. The software upgrade...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Square, the mobile payments start-up, thinks it has come up with another good reason to buy things with a smartphone instead of cash or a credit card. Its apps now allow shoppers to carry around a digital loyalty card, a replacement for the cards that get punched — buy 10 coffees and get the next one free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Square Introduces a Digital Loyalty Card', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customer Loyalty Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Commerce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Square Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T13:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df1d9dcc-921c-5674-a81c-766c4c0180ca', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df1d9dcc-921c-5674-a81c-766c4c0180ca'}, {'abstract': 'In a film by The Selby, the chef Ignacio Mattos and his friends prepare a richly flavored meal at his home in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/edible-selby-ignacios-mostly-latin-lunch/', 'snippet': 'In a film by The Selby, the chef Ignacio Mattos and his friends prepare a richly flavored meal at his home in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a film by The Selby, the chef Ignacio Mattos (formerly of Isa and Il Buco) prepares a richly flavored (mostly) Latin lunch at his home in Brooklyn with his wife, Gabi Plater; their son, Paco Plater Noya; and their friends David Tanis (a New York Times contributor and the author, most recently, of “A Platter of Figs“), Fernando Aciar (owner of O Café) and Pam Yung (a former pastry chef at Isa). Click here to see what’s on the menu.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Edible Selby | Ignacio’s Mostly Latin Lunch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Selby, Todd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T13:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Todd Selby', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Todd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Selby', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8493e3c7-546f-