sonable.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DHAKA, Bangladesh — The Rohingyas of Myanmar would seem to be a most impolite people. They refuse to die. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bangladesh’s Right of Refusal', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rohingya (Ethnic Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T14:53:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Morrison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morrison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/102b5628-04cf-5475-9311-5bbb9205ebe6', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/102b5628-04cf-5475-9311-5bbb9205ebe6'}, {'abstract': 'Which boring Midwestern conservative will Mitt Romney pick as his running mate?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/its-v-p-mentioning-season-for-the-g-o-p/', 'snippet': 'Which boring Midwestern conservative will Mitt Romney pick as his running mate?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who will be Mitt Romney’s running mate? I can hardly wait to find out, and I’m sure you can’t, either. Lots of names are getting tossed around, with the background encouragement of Mr. Romney’s aides, who are trying hard to show that they’re doing a better job of vetting candidates than Republican nominees generally do.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s V.P. Mentioning Season for the G.O.P.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pawlenty, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Portman, Rob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T15:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60d5252e-7d56-5c34-ad6c-e618e4eb631c', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60d5252e-7d56-5c34-ad6c-e618e4eb631c'}, {'abstract': 'A Brooklyn public school that had leaking light fixtures will be moved to the top of the list of schools with PCB problems, and the city will replace its lighting very soon, city officials said last week. But some health and environmental experts say the timeline for light fixture removal from schools should be expedited citywide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/19/as-pcb-issue-lingers-removal-will-be-expedited-at-a-brooklyn-school/', 'snippet': 'A Brooklyn public school that had leaking light fixtures will be moved to the top of the list of schools with PCB problems, and the city will replace its lighting very soon, city officials said last week. But some health and environmental experts ...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As PCB Issue Lingers, Removal Will Be Expedited at a Brooklyn School  ', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], '