mendments unrelated to agriculture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/us/politics/amendments-trimmed-senate-moves-ahead-on-farm-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The farm bill, an effort to change the nation’s food and agriculture policy fundamentally, still includes several amendments unrelated to agriculture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Senate began voting Tuesday on a slimmed-down list of amendments to a farm bill that would set the nation’s food and agriculture policy for the next five years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stack of Farm Proposals Is Coming Up for Votes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stack of Farm Proposals Is Coming Up for Votes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T17:10:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Nixon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nixon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e4c3438-4e7f-5f5d-8395-801693c839fb', 'word_count': 669, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e4c3438-4e7f-5f5d-8395-801693c839fb'}, {'abstract': 'Mo Farah, who is the favorite to win gold medals in the 5,000 and 10,000 meters at the Olympics this summer, is a passionate fan of Arsenal and watches as many Euro 2012 games as he can.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/a-track-favorite-who-cant-get-enough-soccer/', 'snippet': 'Mo Farah, who is the favorite to win gold medals in the 5,000 and 10,000 meters at the Olympics this summer, is a passionate fan of Arsenal and watches as many Euro 2012 games as he can.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer’s Euro 2012 has had no shortage of stories about soccer fandom. Some of them have been good natured, others less so, but they’ve all given credence to the argument that more than any other sport soccer seems to bring out the fanatic in its supporters. As images from the fan zone in Warsaw, Poland, make clear, soccer fans are plentiful. And they can be found anywhere — even among Olympic hopefuls, such as Mo Farah, track and field’s world champion in the 5,000 meters and this year’s favorite to win the gold medal in both the 5,000 and the 10,000 meters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Track Favorite Who Can’t Get Enough Soccer', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Farah, Mo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Thierry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arsenal (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T17:13:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gendelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gendelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organi