s.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/amazonia-or-bust/', 'snippet': 'How Greater Ecuador became a tiny South American country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Babylon may well be glorified for its walls, Nineveh for its grandeur, Athens for its letters, and Constantinople for its empire, but Quito trumps them all: as the key of Christianity, and for having conquered a world; for to this city belongs the discovery of the great River of the Amazon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazonia or Bust!', 'kicker': 'Borderlines', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Geographical', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Union of South American Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T17:38:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86540436-35fd-5c3e-bb58-a85c9b3404b1', 'word_count': 2227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86540436-35fd-5c3e-bb58-a85c9b3404b1'}, {'abstract': 'Nervous and wide-eyed, Dorothy Sandusky testified, trying to repair her husband’s image after testimony that he sexually abused children in the Sanduskys’ home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/sports/ncaafootball/sandusky-defense-suggests-the-police-coached-accusers.html', 'snippet': 'Nervous and wide-eyed, Dorothy Sandusky testified, trying to repair her husband’s image after testimony that he sexually abused children in the Sanduskys’ home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BELLEFONTE, Pa. 