mpell discuss. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video: Microsoft’s New Tablet', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:01:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e32fb76-2e94-51fe-a920-a293f3787bcf', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e32fb76-2e94-51fe-a920-a293f3787bcf'}, {'abstract': 'Brett Picou, a teacher’s aide at P.S. 52 in Queens, still faces the possibility of dismissal or discipline from the Department of Education.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/teachers-aide-accused-of-sexual-misconduct-is-cleared-by-grand-jury/', 'snippet': 'Brett Picou, a teacher’s aide at P.S. 52 in Queens, still faces the possibility of dismissal or discipline from the Department of Education.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A teacher’s aide in New York City is caught between the justice system and the New York City Department of Education since a grand jury on Monday declined to indict him on child sexual abuse charges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Teacher’s Aide Accused of Sexual Misconduct Is Cleared by Grand Jury', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picou, Brett', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:03:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b49622de-c17b-511f-9e94-503db5302f0e', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b49622de-c17b-511f-9e94-503db5302f0e'}, {'abstract': 'Barry and Fran Weissler, veteran Broadway producers, are considering signing on as backers of Ms. Paulus’s revival of the 1972 musical “Pippin” that is scheduled to run this winter at the American Repertory Theater in Cambridge, Mass.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/diane-paulus-pippin-may-get-broadway-backers/', 'snippet': 'Barry and Fran Weissler, veteran Broadway producers, are considering signing on as backers of Ms. Paulus’s revival of the 1972 musical “Pippin” that is scheduled to run this winter at the American Repertory Theater in Cambridge, Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The next major theater project by Diane Paulus, the director of the Tony Award-winning musical “The Gershwins’ Porgy and Bess,” is already attracting Broadway attention. Barry and Fran Weissler, veteran Broadway producers, are considering signing on as backers of Ms. Paulus’s revival of the 1972 musical “Pippin” that is scheduled to run this winter at the American Repertory Theater in Cambridge, Mass., a spokesman for Mr. Weissler confirmed on Tuesday. While the spokesman, Clint Bond Jr., said any talk of a Broadway move for “Pippin” was premature, such a transfer would become a possibility if the Weisslers, who have produced musical revivals like the long-running “Chicago,” come on board and the show draws strong reviews in Cambridge, where it is scheduled to run Dec. 5-Jan. 20, 2013.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Diane Paulus ‘Pippin’ May Get Broadway Backers', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Pippin’ Revival Draws Broadway Interest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulus, Diane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weissler, Barry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weissler, Fran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN REPERTORY THEATER', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:23:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf3cd94-d426-51b5-9d0f-19a88ee78883', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf3cd94-d426-51b5-9d0f-19a88ee78883'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday morning, about 15,000 bees were blessed on the grounds at St. John the Divine Cathedral.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/the-blessing-of-the-bees/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday morning, about 15,000 bees were blessed on the grounds at St. John the Divine Cathedral.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday morning, witnesses to a ceremony at the Cathedral Church of St. John the Divine were encouraged to wear long sleeves, long pants and socks. The subjects of this holy event were about 15,000 honeybees that live on the church’s campus in Morningside Heights. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Blessing of the Bees', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Honey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cathedral Church of St John the Divine (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:29:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a106362-5371-5327-8db8-3224372104b9', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a106362-5371-5327-8db8-3224372104b9'}, {'abstract': 'The 62-year-old clarinetist and mandoplin player has long been a fixture on the New York City folk scene, having made a dozen LPs that explore a range of genres: bluegrass, klezmer, pop and jazz.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/andy-statman-a-brooklyn-virtuoso-receives-heritage-award/', 'snippet': 'The 62-year-old clarinetist and mandoplin player has long been a fixture on the New York City folk scene, having made a dozen LPs that explore a range of genres: bluegrass, klezmer, pop and jazz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andy Statman, the virtuoso clarinetist and mandolin player from Brooklyn, was awarded the National Endowment for the Arts Heritage Fellowship on Monday for his contributions to bluegrass and klezmer music, the organization announced on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Andy Statman, a Brooklyn Virtuoso, Receives Heritage Award', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bromberg, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dylan, Bob', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fleck, Bela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skaggs, Ricky', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Statman, Andy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Endowment for the Arts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:39:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinely Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinely', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c228d8e-cd39-5a2c-aee2-dba5b2c0cc7a', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c228d8e-cd39-5a2c-aee2-dba5b2c0cc7a'}, {'abstract': 'New York City officials announced in January that they were shutting Williamsburg Charter High School in Brooklyn because of concerns about its management, but court proceedings have stalled the efforts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/19/as-year-ends-students-at-williamsburg-charter-high-wonder-will-we-be-back/', 'snippet': 'New York City officials announced in January that they were shutting Williamsburg Charter High School in Brooklyn because of concerns about its management, but court proceedings have stalled the efforts.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fate of Charter School in Brooklyn Is Unclear', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By THEODORIC MEYER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Theodoric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'MEYER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6773c4ad-ee75-5fca-a627-da259267a275', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6773c4ad-ee75-5fca-a627-da259267a275'}, {'abstract': 'There’s something fussy about caring about shoes, so I looked into Justin Vernon’s magazine profile to see if there were any hints that he might be the fussy shoemaking type.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/that-bon-iver-singer-songwriter-dude-releases-a-shoe/', 'snippet': 'There’s something fussy about caring about shoes, so I looked into Justin Vernon’s magazine profile to see if there were any hints that he might be the fussy shoemaking type.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I just found out that Justin Vernon has “released” a shoe. There’s something fussy about caring about shoes, let alone designing one for sale when your living is made making music, so I went back to look at last year’s\xa0profile of Vernon in the magazine\xa0to see if there were any hints that he might be the fussy shoemaking type. Some of Vernon’s attributes: Songwriter since age 12. Religion major in college. Women’s studies minor. Tattoo on his chest of Wisconsin, where he grew up. Didn’t go hunting till he was 23. Maker of an album that “sounds like crying, deep primal purging.” Where he recorded that album: in his father’s hunting cabin in the woods. And so on.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Bon Iver Singer-Songwriter Dude Releases . . . a Shoe?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vernon, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bon Iver', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-19T19:42:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maya Lau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ma