10,000 coins of the 38,000 sold by the Hispanic Society this year have been lent long-term to the American Numismatic Society, keeping them available to the public and scholars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/arts/some-coins-sold-by-hispanic-society-go-to-numismatic-society.html', 'snippet': 'Some 10,000 coins of the 38,000 sold by the Hispanic Society this year have been lent long-term to the American Numismatic Society, keeping them available to the public and scholars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the financially struggling Hispanic Society of America decided to sell its collection of nearly 38,000 rare coins last year, that Upper Manhattan museum sought to allay fears that its cultural treasure would become inaccessible to scholars and the public by striving to find a public institution to buy it. None, however, was found to purchase the collection, valued at more than $25 million; the coins landed in private hands; and some of those scholars’ concerns are now being realized.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/HISPANIC/HISPANIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 987, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/HISPANIC/HISPANIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1973, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/HISPANIC/HISPANIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/HISPANIC/HISPANIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': No