en', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/767acdfe-24de-5c62-bd0f-afcf8776ef10', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/767acdfe-24de-5c62-bd0f-afcf8776ef10'}, {'abstract': 'The musicals “Fela!” and “Bring It On” have distinct pedigrees and histories, but are taking similar financial risks in making limited summer runs on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/theater/fela-and-bring-it-on-go-to-broadway-in-summer.html', 'snippet': 'The musicals “Fela!” and “Bring It On” have distinct pedigrees and histories, but are taking similar financial risks in making limited summer runs on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The height of summer and the dead of winter are the worst times to open a Broadway show, since too many theatergoers are distracted by vacations and weather. But the lure of empty New York theaters has led the producers of two multimillion-dollar touring musicals to bring them to town for limited engagements, starting in July, in hopes of earning short-term profits and adding Broadway cachet before sending the shows back on the road.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/FILLINS/FILLINS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1309, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/FILLINS/FILLINS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1564, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/arts/FILLINS/FILLINS-thumbStandard.jpg',