never had the Duke-Michigan conversation. Though it did come up that Battier, the erstwhile Blue Devil who grew up in a Detroit suburb, once accepted a pair of autographed sneakers from Howard when the latter was playing for the Wolverines as a member of the Fab Five.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1228, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YJPDRIBBLE2/YJPDRIBBLE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Split by Rivalry, United in Bid for a Ring', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble: N.B.A. Finals', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Split by Rivalry, United in Bid for a Ring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howard, Juwan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Battier, Shane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Michigan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T00:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46ef1e48-bf0e-5d1d-ab97-ab18913e3b4a', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46ef1e48-bf0e-5d1d-ab97-ab18913e3b4a'}, {'abstract': 'A second lawsuit was filed in federal court in Miami on Tuesday against the State of Florida over its search of voter rolls for noncitizens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/us/florida-state-is-sued-again-over-voter-purge.html', 'snippet': 'A second lawsuit was filed in federal court in Miami on Tuesday against the State of Florida over its search of voter rolls for noncitizens.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A second lawsuit was filed in federal court in Miami on Tuesday against the State of Florida over its search of voter rolls for noncitizens. Several civil and voters’ rights groups joined in the suit, which says the search violates the National Voting Rights Act and the National Voter Registration Act. The groups said the review discriminates against minorities and is prohibited within 90 days of an election. Florida has a primary in August. The state is also being sued by the Department of Justice. Earlier this year, the state sent names of 2,700 possible noncitizens to county election supervisors, who were advised to write those people, asking them to offer proof of citizenship or risk being dropped from the rolls. But the list, compiled by comparing voter rolls to a driver’s license databank and overwhelmingly singled out minorities, was found to be flawed. The state has asked the Department of Homeland Security to allow it to use an immigration database to verify the list, but the federal government has not done so. As a result, Florida is suing Homeland Security over access to the database. The civil rights groups say they hope their suit deters other states from conducting similar searches. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: State Is Sued Again Over Voter Purge ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: State Is Sued Again Over Voter Purge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T00:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2aa6d44b-5213-5e08-8659-7fea27128317', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2aa6d44b-5213-5e08-8659-7fea27128317'}, {'abstract': 'No country has the right to tell another people whom their leader should be, President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia said at the close of the Group of 20 meeting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/world/europe/putin-says-syrians-must-decide-assads-fate.html', 'snippet': 'No country has the right to tell another people whom their leader should be, President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia said at the close of the Group of 20 meeting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN JOSÉ DEL CABO, Mexico — President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia said Tuesday that the fate of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria should be left to the hands of the Syrians, saying that no one country has the right to tell another people whom their leader should be.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Putin Rules Out Intervention to Stop the Syrian Rebellion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putin Rules Out Intervention To Stop the Syrian Rebellion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Twenty', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T00:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helene Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1c3f072-059d-5ef5-8457-2c3df312efda', 'word_count': 319, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1c3f072-059d-5ef5-8457-2c3df312efda'}, {'abstract': 'The evidence is in: Immigrants have had a mostly positive impact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/opinion/the-beneficial-impact-of-immigrants.html', 'snippet': 'The evidence is in: Immigrants have had a mostly positive impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IMMIGRATION is in the headlines again, with President Obama’s decision last week to stop deporting young illegal immigrants who came to the United States as children, and the Supreme Court’s approaching decision on the constitutionality of Arizona’s crackdown on undocumented migrants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Shut the Golden Door', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don&#8217;t Shut the Golden Door', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T00:36:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John M. MacDonald and Robert J. Sampson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8293feda-c84b-55a2-b67b-f80babd2f813', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8293feda-c84b-55a2-b67b-f80babd2f813'}, {'abstract': 'There is something seriously lacking in the current campaigns from President Obama and Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/opinion/friedman-wasting-warren-buffett.html', 'snippet': 'There is something seriously lacking in the current campaigns from President Obama and Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Watching this campaign unfold reaffirms how much it would have benefitted from a serious, centrist third-party challenger. It would have been so clarifying to have an independent voice calling out Mitt Romney for running a campaign that consists of decrying the last three and a half years of the Obama presidency, while offering to reinstate the very same failed policies that made the eight years of George W. Bush a disaster that President Obama has spent most of his time cleaning up. And it would have been equally clarifying to have an independent challenger calling out Obama for failing to put a credible, specific economic plan on the table — at the scale of our problem — but relying instead on a campaign that amounts to a series of discrete appeals to each of the Democratic Party constituencies. It feels like a ground war with no air cover.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman