 '_id': 'nyt://article/2d4e3d60-74d9-5c1d-af37-48d00b4caf73', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d4e3d60-74d9-5c1d-af37-48d00b4caf73'}, {'abstract': 'More than 14,000 second graders have learned to swim with the Swim for Life program, which was conceived by the city’s departing parks commissioner, Adrian Benepe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/nyregion/parks-department-offers-swimming-lessons-for-second-graders.html', 'snippet': 'More than 14,000 second graders have learned to swim with the Swim for Life program, which was conceived by the city’s departing parks commissioner, Adrian Benepe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the first swim lessons, no one could pry Amahri’s arms from the neck of the instructor trying to coax her into the pool. It turns out that an 8-year-old girl, determined to keep her face dry, has the strength of a sumo wrestler. Perched near the instructor’s head, she could not complete the Blowing Bubbles in the Water portion of the curriculum, which followed Introductory Toe Wiggling.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/nyregion/ABOUT1/ABOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/nyregion/ABOUT1/ABOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/nyregion/ABOUT1/ABOUT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/nyregion/ABOUT1/ABOUT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1433, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', '