r.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/summer-sketches/', 'snippet': 'As summer officially begins, a short film for the season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I made “Summer Sketches” so I could keep some summer in my pocket. Come the dead of winter, when I play the film back on my phone, it will warm by sparking memories of bare feet in sand, warm breezes off bays, the smell of sun-tan lotion and chlorine, the kids turning amphibian for a day, and secret tan lines. The film is about water, too — being in it, on it, under it and next to it. Water is the most animated substance on the planet, and when I’m not drawing it or painting with it (watercolor) I often find myself photographing it. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Summer Sketches’', 'kicker': 'Jeff Scher', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T01:15:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Scher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f499945-b3f4-542d-b428-a890b953882a', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f499945-b3f4-542d-b428-a890b953882a'}, {'abstract': 'With the economy slowly expanding, state tax revenues have started to recover, but governors and legislatures are keeping a tight rein on spending.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/business/public-workers-face-continued-layoffs-and-recovery-is-hurt.html', 'snippet': 'With the economy slowly expanding, state tax revenues have started to recover, but governors and legislatures are keeping a tight rein on spending.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Companies have been slowly adding workers for more th