ord_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/156508df-9012-5064-98f0-5d942cf5d9b9'}, {'abstract': 'In which Alan Arbesfeld switches it up on us.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/spoon/', 'snippet': 'In which Alan Arbesfeld switches it up on us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Administrivial Notepad and Blog Maintenance Alert! There will be a Notepad in tomorrow’s puzzle (Thursday, June 21) which reads: “Parts of six answers have been entered in the grid for you.” Also, the blog maintenance work has been rescheduled, so the Wordplay post for this puzzle will be appearing at its regular time. For now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spoon Full of Sugar', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T02:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae589389-d639-5a52-b6e2-80ae2cb0e910', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae589389-d639-5a52-b6e2-80ae2cb0e910'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print for June 20, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/pageoneplus/corrections-june-20.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print for June 20, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 20', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T02:00:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/d78f1b39-cd15-5ab3-998a-cc2774b4decb', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d78f1b39-cd15-5ab3-998a-cc2774b4decb'}, {'abstract': 'Why is it that in the presidential election the challenger and the incumbent have reversed their traditional roles?', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/romney-the-cautious/', 'snippet': 'Why is it that in the presidential election the challenger and the incumbent have reversed their traditional roles?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney’s vigorous denial notwithstanding, yesterday’s report that his campaign isn’t even planning to vet Florida Senator Marco Rubio as a potential vice presidential pick was entirely consistent with the kind of campaign that Team Romney appears intent on running. Rubio has long been cited as one of the most exciting running mates available – someone who would add youth, charisma and diversity to a ticket lacking all three. But with youth comes inexperience and with excitement comes risk, and lately the Romney campaign seems to have decided that they can win this election without taking any substantial risks at all.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney the Cautious', 'kicker': 'Campaign Stops', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T02:03:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/557e4a2c-2ed2-5dc0-9037-d7b5c7a24e65', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/557e4a2c-2ed2-5dc0-9037-d7b5c7a24e65'}, {'abstract': 'Rupert Murdoch’s media conglomerate has agreed to acquire Consolidated Media Holdings. If approved, it would give News Corporation a stronger foothold in the lucrative pay television industry in Australia.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/19/news-corp-makes-2-billion-deal-to-acquire-australian-pay-tv-company/', 'snippet': 'Rupert Murdoch’s media conglomerate has agreed to acquire Consolidated Media Holdings. If approved, it would give News Corporation a stronger foothold in the lucrative pay television industry in Australia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a move that would give News Corporation a larger foothold in the lucrative pay TV business in Australia, Rupert Murdoch’s media conglomerate said it has agreed to pay roughly $2.2 billion to acquire Consolidated Media Holdings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corp. Makes $2 Billion Deal to Acquire Australian Pay TV Company', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Sky Broadcasting  Group (BSkyB)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foxtel', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 9, 'major':