day when the WikiLeaks founder Julian Assange wandered in on a sunlit afternoon, trailing a web of legal and diplomatic complications. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'WikiLeaks Founder Turns to Ecuador for Asylum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'WikiLeaks Founder Turns to Ecuador for Asylum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ecuador', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Rafael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asylum, Right of', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T02:16:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/addc5313-6fbc-5e3b-a7a8-30af54ba422f', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/addc5313-6fbc-5e3b-a7a8-30af54ba422f'}, {'abstract': 'The prosecutions result from leftover cases begun under President George W. Bush; proliferating e-mail and computer audit trails; and bipartisan support in Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/us/politics/accidental-path-to-record-leak-cases-under-obama.html', 'snippet': 'The prosecutions result from leftover cases begun under President George W. Bush; proliferating e-mail and computer audit trails; and bipartisan support in Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Under fire from Republicans who claim that the White House has leaked classified information to make him look tough, President Obama has pointed to his administration’s unmatched record in prosecuting leaks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 177, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 177}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 302, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/us/SECRETS-1/SECRETS-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Administration Took Accidental Path to Setting Record for Leak Cases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Administration Took Accidental Path to Setting Record for Leak Cases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T02:22:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Shane and Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66fcf4ef-626f-50aa-9054-aa850baea58d', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66fcf4ef-626f-50aa-9054-aa850baea58d'}, {'abstract': 'For the past 15 years, Sherry Von Riesen has tended to Olympic hopefuls as they cope with the pressures of everything from athletic aspirations to dating and family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/sports/olympics/playing-housemother-to-olympic-hopefuls.html', 'snippet': 'For the past 15 years, Sherry Von Riesen has tended to Olympic hopefuls as they cope with the pressures of everything from athletic aspirations to dating and family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLORADO SPRINGS — Athletes at the United States Olympic Training Center here have access to world-class trainers, coaches, physiologists, underwater cameras for the swimming pool, video replay for weight lifting and specialized massage boots for aching leg muscles. The best biomechanists in the world watch runners jog on gravity-defying $25,000 treadmills, and chefs prepare fresh, wholesome meals every day for some 170 resident athletes and coaches who train here. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/sports/YMOM1/YMOM1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Olympians’ Housemother', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Olympians’ Housemother', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'ke