re of Queens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/24/magazine/look-fort-tilden.html', 'snippet': 'Makeshift shelters and a quiet vibe on the southern shore of Queens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Makeshift shelters and a quiet vibe on the southern shore of Queens.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW/look-fort-tilden-slide-01YW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Which Way to the (Hidden) Beach?', 'kicker': 'Look', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fort Tilden (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T11:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b9392759-267d-5f54-ae73-cac24ddc5a4b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b9392759-267d-5f54-ae73-cac24ddc5a4b'}, {'abstract': 'A new type of investment pays real dividends for prevention programs that reduce crime, homelessness and other problems.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/the-promise-of-social-impact-bonds/', 'snippet': 'A new type of investment pays real dividends for prevention programs that reduce crime, homelessness and other problems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a government needs to invest in an expensive capital project — a new sewer system, bridge or highway — it issues bonds. Bonds raise upfront money from private sector investors, who are then paid back with interest from the tolls or charges the project will generate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Promise of Social Impact Bonds', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Impact Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T11:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e3b1128-46df-5512-9a0b-2d3c184ae51e', 'word_count': 1943, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e3b1128-46df-5512-9a0b-2d3c184ae51e'}, {'abstract': 'That’s the life of the small-business owner: you think you have made it to the next level, and then you realize that it’s not a particularly secure position and you need to open your wallet again to try to keep from falling back.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/figuring-out-a-better-way-to-train-employees/', 'snippet': 'That’s the life of the small-business owner: you think you have made it to the next level, and then you realize that it’s not a particularly secure position and you need to open your wallet again to try to keep from falling back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is the second of a two-part follow-up to my post on how I fire workers. In the first follow-up, I responded to commenters who had strong opinions on my employee manual. Now I’d like to address commenters who questioned my failure to train workers whom I had hired in the years before the crash in 2008. For instance, this comment:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Figuring Out a Better Way to Train Employees', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Productivity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vistage International Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dfa8201-4380-5d08-a5e0-2b17c838fc94', 'word_count': 1076, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dfa8201-4380-5d08-a5e0-2b17c838fc94'}, {'abstract': 'Can the cranky old coach lead Andy Murray to his breakthrough win at a Grand Slam tournament — and lift Wimbledon’s curse on British tennis players?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/can-ivan-lendl-lead-andy-murray-to-tennis-greatness.html', 'snippet': 'Can the cranky old coach lead Andy Murray to his breakthrough win at a Grand Slam tournament — and lift Wimbledon’s curse on British tennis players?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On New Year’s Eve, Andy Murray, a 25-year-old Scot and professional tennis player who has lost in the finals of three major championships and is currently on pace to end his fifth year in a row ranked No. 4 in the world, announced that he had hired Ivan Lendl as his new coach. His decision to offer employment to the mostly unloved, all-time-great Lendl made Murray’s desperate unhappiness with his also-ran status achingly public and set the tennis world abuzz, particularly in Britain, where Wimbledon starts next week and there hasn’t been a native-born male champion since 1936.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lendlmurray2/24lendlmurray2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1048, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lendlmurray2/24lendlmurray2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1048, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lendlmurray2/24lendlmurray2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lendlmurray2/24lendlmurray2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail