ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'iTunes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T11:38:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d16cd36b-0ca8-5c09-aef6-5cd2077610ef', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d16cd36b-0ca8-5c09-aef6-5cd2077610ef'}, {'abstract': 'The man, identified as Naamen Meziche, was close to members of the Hamburg, Germany, cell who carried out the attacks of Sept. 11, 2001, according to Western intelligence assessments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/world/asia/french-citizen-suspected-of-qaeda-links-arrested-in-pakistan.html', 'snippet': 'The man, identified as Naamen Meziche, was close to members of the Hamburg, Germany, cell who carried out the attacks of Sept. 11, 2001, according to Western intelligence assessments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Pakistani intelligence officials have detained a Frenchman of Algerian origin who is suspected of having links to a cell of Al Qaeda that carried out the attacks of Sept. 11, a senior Pakistani official said Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan Arrests Frenchman Suspected of Qaeda Links', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan Arrests Frenchman Suspected of Qaeda Links', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meziche, Naamen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T11:41:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fc5fcdb-a0dd-5587-9d0d-c356da7b0807', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fc5fcdb-a0dd-5587-9d0d-c356da7b0807'}, {'abstract': 'More than 50,000 people, including representatives of more than 120 countries, gather for a United Nations conference on sustainable development.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/on-our-radar-back-in-rio-20-years-later/', 'snippet': 'More than 50,000 people, including representatives of more than 120 countries, gather for a United Nations conference on sustainable development.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 50,000 people and representatives of more than 120 countries gather in Rio de Janeiro for the opening of the Rio+20 conference on sustainable development. Topics include the destruction of the rain forest, vanishing coral reefs, land grabs, the need for food security, clean water, the role of women in food production, safe drinking water, energy access, clogged transit systems, jobs and sustainable development as a way of fighting poverty. The conference marks the 20th anniversary of the 1992 Earth Summit in Rio. [The Miami Herald]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Back in Rio, 20 Years Later', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T11:46:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f53174d-1bfa-5aa8-a463-473cdacbbe76', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f53174d-1bfa-5aa8-a463-473cdacbbe76'}, {'abstract': 'The confusion over the health of Hosni Mubarak continued when his lawyer contradicted what he called false reports that the former president had nearly died.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/world/middleeast/official-silence-surrounds-mubaraks-condition-in-egypt-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'The confusion over the health of Hosni Mubarak continued when his lawyer contradicted what he called false reports that the former president had nearly died.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — A new sense of political intrigue compounded the confusion over the health of Hosni Mubarak on Wednesday when one of his lawyers contradicted what he called false reports in Egypt’s state-run media that the imprisoned former president had nearly died, insisting that Mr. Mubarak simply fell down in the prison bathroom.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/21egypt/21egypt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/21/world/21egypt/21egypt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/21egypt/21egypt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/21egypt/21egypt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'captio