 Care Act will mean for health insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the public sector, the pink slips keep coming. | What a verdict on the Affordable Care Act will mean for health insurance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/business/video-bdl-120620/video-bdl-120620-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/business/video-bdl-120620/video-bdl-120620-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/business/video-bdl-120620/video-bdl-120620-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/business/video-bdl-120620/video-bdl-120620-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Day Live | June 20, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T14:36:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop, Nadia Sussman, Pedro Rosado and Channon Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nadia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sussman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/a541e97d-ded4-57d7-9d98-9bd5b1f5389b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/a541e97d-ded4-57d7-9d98-9bd5b1f5389b'}, {'abstract': 'The artist, Ai Weiwei, is suing tax officials, and hundreds of his supporters showed up at the Chaoyang District Court in Beijing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/world/asia/supporters-take-up-chinese-artist-ai-weiwei-s-cause-at-court.html', 'snippet': 'The artist, Ai Weiwei, is suing tax officials, and hundreds of his supporters showed up at the Chaoyang District Court in Beijing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — If the Chinese authorities thought that barring the artist Ai Weiwei from the courtroom where his lawsuit against tax officials is being heard might tamp down public interest in the matter, they must be sorely disappointed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1492, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/world/asia/21beijing/21beijing-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Artist Is Barred From His Own Hearing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Artist Is Barred From His Own Hearing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T14:38:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72463890-e658-5cc1-8e99-f229d3e6ed27', 'word_count': 680, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72463890-e658-5cc1-8e99-f229d3e6ed27'}, {'abstract': 'In the novel “A Hologram for the King,” an American businessman hopes to close a deal in Saudi Arabia.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/waiting-for-the-king-dave-eggers-talks-about-his-new-novel/', 'snippet': 'In the novel “A Hologram for the King,” an American businessman hopes to close a deal in Saudi Arabia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Dave Eggers’s new novel, “A Hologram for the King” (McSweeney’s Books), a 54-year-old American businessman named Alan Clay travels to Saudi Arabia in hopes of selling holographic technology to the country. This depends on making a presentation to the king, who may or may not show up. In her review, Michiko Kakutani wrote: “Thanks to Mr. Eggers’s uncommon ability to access his characters’ emotions and channel their every mood, we are instantly immersed in Alan’s story, rooting for him somehow to win an audience with the king and turn his life around.” In a recent interview via e-mail, Mr. Eggers discussed his inspiration for the novel, his editing process, the people he met in Saudi Arabia and more. Below are excerpts from the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waiting for the King: Dave Eggers Talks About His New Novel', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eggers, Dave', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T14:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bb14552-71ed-55d3-8ead-64ca8a84a0e7', 'word_count': 1199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bb14552-71ed-55d3-8ead-64ca8a84a0e7'}, {'abstract': 'Analysts and producers expect demand for lithium, used extensively in batteries intended for E.V.’s, to double or triple in the next 10 years.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/wheelies-the-ionic-edition/', 'snippet': 'Analysts and producers expect demand for lithium, used extensively in batteries intended for E.V.’s, to double or triple in the next 10 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In which we bring you motoring news from around the Web:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wheelies: The Ionic Edition', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bentley Motors Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ferrari SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T14:58:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/023e1533-93f9-5ef2-8a43-2d18671746f9', 'word_count': 343, 'uri': 'nyt://article/023e1533-93f9-5ef2-8a43-2d18671746f9'}, {'abstract': 'Bonnie Christensen’s picture book tells the story of the man Albert Einstein called “the father of modern science.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/books/i-galileo-by-bonnie-christensen.html', 'snippet': 'Bonnie Christensen’s picture book tells the story of the man Albert Einstein called “the father of modern science.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Following up on her illustrated biographies for older readers (“Woody Guthrie,” “The Daring Nellie Bly,” “Django”), Bonnie Christensen dials\xa0back\xa0several\xa0centuries in “I, Galileo,” demonstrating once again how a well-conceived and executed picture book can deliver a serious story — in this case, of one of history’s great independent thinkers — in a beautiful, enriching way for those readers who’ve supposedly “moved on” to chapter books.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/books/20galileo-img2/20galileo-img2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 598, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/books/20galileo-img2/20galileo-img2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 598, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/books/20galileo-img2/20galileo-img2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/books/20galileo-img2/20galileo-img2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/books/20galileo-img2/20galileo-img2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Galileo Galilei, Observed', 'kicker': "Children's Books", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T14:58:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pamela Paul', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pamela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paul', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/470a57ed-6d4c-52c6-bc42-0570ee8b8549', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/470a57ed-6d4c-52c6-bc42-0570ee8b8549'}, {'abstract': 'Studies show that the Fed really can lower interest rates by purchasing large quantities of Treasury securities, mortgage-backed securities, or other kinds of securities.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/asset-purchases-work-at-least-a-little/', 'snippet': 'Studies show that the Fed really can lower interest rates by purchasing large quantities of Treasury securities, mortgage-backed securities, or other kinds of securities.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:26 p.m. | Updated  This seems like a good day for a reminder that asset purchases work. The Federal Reserve really can lower interest rates by purchasing large quantities of Treasury securities, mortgage-backed securities, or other kinds of securities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Asset Purchases Work, at Least a Little', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fe