kabout-620-people-free-airport-check-ins-and-a-new-fly-fishing-hole/', 'snippet': 'People-free airport check-ins, a fly-fishing hotspot and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Fly-Fishing Hotspot As Punta Allen, Mexico, has emerged as a fly-fishing destination, local lobstermen have been enlisted to serve as guides to where to find bonefish, tarpon and permit. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Walkabout — 6/20: People-Free Airport Check-Ins and a New Fly-Fishing Hole', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:23:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ccfc4f4-d37e-5ec6-a448-be56800d7fe8', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ccfc4f4-d37e-5ec6-a448-be56800d7fe8'}, {'abstract': 'During a House Veterans Affairs Committee hearing on the ever-growing backlog of disability compensation claims Tuesday, one lawmaker turned a normally staid policy meeting into a contentious affair.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/backlog-of-disability-claims-for-veterans-sends-democrat-on-a-tear/', 'snippet': 'During a House Veterans Affairs Committee hearing on the ever-growing backlog of disability compensation claims Tuesday, one lawmaker turned a normally staid policy meeting into a contentious affair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday, the House Veterans Affairs Committee held one of its perennial hearings on the ever-growing backlog of disability compensation claims pending before the Department of Veterans’ Affairs. The usual polite questioning of V.A. officials was expected, followed by the usual complex answers that few on the committee might be expected to comprehend. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Backlog of Disability Claims for Veterans Sends Democrat on a Tear', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:25:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Dao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19207384-f069-58c8-9214-3af683534002', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19207384-f069-58c8-9214-3af683534002'}, {'abstract': 'The A.U.’s unwillingness to arrest President Bashir of Sudan, who is wanted by the I.C.C., undermines its case that it is capable — and deserving — of taking charge of its own political destiny.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/an-african-answer-to-african-problems/', 'snippet': 'The A.U.’s unwillingness to arrest President Bashir of Sudan, who is wanted by the I.C.C., undermines its case that it is capable — and deserving — of taking charge of its own political destiny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — If only I could be a Malawian citizen for a day. Then I could brag that my country’s new leader, President Joyce Banda, is doing the right thing by warning Sudanese leader Omar al-Bashir that he’ll be arrested if he sets foot in Malawi. In honoring the arrest warrant that the International Criminal Court has issued against Bashir for crimes against humanity — and showing basic respect for human rights and international law — she stands virtually alone among African leaders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An African Answer to African Problems', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banda, Joyce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Omar Hassan Al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Malawi', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sudan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eusebius McKaiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eusebius', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKaiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3193848c-1d2d-5055-98ca-9ee294971832', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3193848c-1d2d-5055-98ca-9ee294971832'}, {'abstract': 'Local offices are being opened to make the probation process less disruptive and to connect clients to job opportunities, G.E.D. classes and other resources in their neighborhoods.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/for-probationers-moving-offices-closer-to-improve-results/', 'snippet': 'Local offices are being opened to make the probation process less disruptive and to connect clients to job opportunities, G.E.D. classes and other resources in their neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One recent hot Friday evening, 15 young men and women on probation filed into an unfurnished room in a former school in central Harlem, awaiting some kind of news. Probation officers set up fans and passed out drinks and chips.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Probationers, Moving Offices Closer to Improve Results', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiraldi, Vincent', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Probation Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'HARLEM (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:38:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hannah Miet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hannah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec367593-9ec7-5bbd-a6da-e92ca2e79a0e', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec367593-9ec7-5bbd-a6da-e92ca2e79a0e'}, {'abstract': 'Is a candy company that gives tours to children taking a risk if it does not hire criminals?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/making-sense-of-new-e-e-o-c-rules-on-hiring/', 'snippet': 'Is a candy company that gives tours to children taking a risk if it does not hire criminals?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Second chances come up often when you talk to business owners on the record about hiring people who have served time — the subject, indirectly, of a just-published Times story about the new rules from the Equal Employment Opportunity Commission that may limit using criminal records in hiring decisions. Joseph Dutra, who employs 23 people at Kimmie Candy Company in Reno, Nev., is willing to give somebody with a criminal history a second chance, provided the crime didn’t include violence or a sexual advance on a child. “We don’t have a blanket policy here, but we need to have people with good morals, who are compatible with the public that we bring in,” said Mr. Dutra, who added that groups of schoolchildren often tour the factory. “We’re trying to make this a fun little place where people can come and feel safe.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Sense of New E.E.O.C. Rules on Hiring', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Equal Employment Opportunity Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:42:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robb Mandelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mandelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/740594cb-b5a7-5169-9c18-385435b6d957', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/740594cb-b5a7-5169-9c18-385435b6d957'}, {'abstract': 'Accepting, slowly, a child’s decision to marry young and embrace a more religious life.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/when-a-daughter-marries-very-young/', 'snippet': 'Accepting, slowly, a child’s decision to marry young and embrace a more religious life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Admitted: This is among my personal fears as a parent. On Tablet, Evelyn Krieger, who describes herself as a “Modern Orthodox Jew,” writes about her daughter’s decision to marry very young, at 20, as part of her choice to follow a more rigorous religious path. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Daughter Marries (Very) Young', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:44:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19c4bef2-b4b5-5276-ae8c-92120a76e405', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19c4bef2-b4b5-5276-ae8c-92120a76e405'}, {'abstract': 'Under new rules presented to Parliament, companies listed in Britain would have to get majority support from shareholders for their executive compensation packages.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/in-britain-a-plan-to-give-shareholders-more-say-on-pay/', 'snippet': 'Under new rules presented to Parliament, companies listed in Britain would have to get majority support from shareholders for their executive compensation packages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Britain will make shareholder votes on executive pay binding next year as part of a set of measures announced by the government on Wednesday to rein in excessive remuneration.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Britain, a Plan to Give Shareholders More Say on Pay', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shareholder Votes on Pay To Be Binding in Britain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cable, Vince', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T15:45:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c16520c6-a84c-5073-b0a3-fd3ec1438246', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c16520c6-a84c-5073-b0a3-fd3ec1438246'}, {'abstract': 'It is the first time all four have toured together since 1985.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/jackson-brothers-start-a-tour/', 'snippet': 'It is the first time all four have toured together since 1985.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The four remaining members of the Jackson Five are starting a tour on Wednesday, just days before the third anniversary of their brother Michael’s death, The Associated Press reported.\xa0 The “Unity” tour will begin at Casino Rama in Ontario and will finish up on July 29 at a casino in Snoqualmie, Wash., hitting 14 other cities along the way. They will play the Apollo Theater in Harlem on June 28.\xa0\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times',