 teachable moment for a young team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a while — for almost the entire game Tuesday night, in fact — it looked as if Heat-Thunder was going to be a real series. But then LeBron James channeled Willis Reed, or a flu-stricken Michael Jordan, and now Miami is up, three games to one, and pretty much everyone is conceding the N.B.A. title to the talents in South Beach.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Countdown to a Coronation', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Countdown to a Coronation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:07:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Reddicliffe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reddicliffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ff67908-cb7c-5aa3-9e2c-2eb9f25e4890', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff67908-cb7c-5aa3-9e2c-2eb9f25e4890'}, {'abstract': 'The baking maven Dorie Grrenspan and her son, Joshua, will open cookie shops this summer at the Essex Street Market and La Marqueta.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/beurre-sel-cookies-coming-to-two-markets/', 'snippet': 'The baking maven Dorie Grrenspan and her son, Joshua, will open cookie shops this summer at the Essex Street Market and La Marqueta.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dorie Greenspan (right) who has written a shelf load of baking books, and has been running occasional pop-up cookie bakeries with her son, Joshua Greenspan, plan to open cookie shops called Beurre & Sel (butter and salt) in the Essex Street Market and in La Marqueta by late summer. The two will also have bakery space at La Marqueta, in East Harlem. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beurre & Sel Cookies Coming to Two Markets', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:20:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ca8cdf6-aff5-59e4-8a9a-11e480897ece', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ca8cdf6-aff5-59e4-8a9a-11e480897ece'}, {'abstract': 'Deutsche Bank said on Wednesday that it had failed to reach an agreement to sell its real estate investment business Guggenheim Partners, following an earlier announcement that talks had ended for other parts of the bank’s asset management unit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/deutsche-bank-ends-deal-talks-with-guggenheim-partners/', 'snippet': 'Deutsche Bank said on Wednesday that it had failed to reach an agreement to sell its real estate investment business Guggenheim Partners, following an earlier announcement that talks had ended for other parts of the bank’s asset management unit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Deutsche Bank said on Wednesday that it had failed to reach an agreement to sell part of its asset management business to Guggenheim Partners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank Ends Deal Talks With Guggenheim Partners', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'o