is seeking to become the first openly transgender athlete to make a United States Olympic team.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/transgender-athlete-looks-to-qualify-in-hammer-throw/', 'snippet': 'Keelin Godsey, 28, of North Adams, Mass., is seeking to become the first openly transgender athlete to make a United States Olympic team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keelin Godsey is one of 24 athletes scheduled to participate Thursday in the women’s hammer throw at the United States Olympic trials, but for Godsey, 28, of North Adams, Mass., there is much more than a spot in London at stake.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transgender Athlete Looks to Qualify in Hammer', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexual', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Godsey, Keelin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:29:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c3eb8dd-6cb6-5d78-93ab-df0015774db6', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c3eb8dd-6cb6-5d78-93ab-df0015774db6'}, {'abstract': 'Similar voices and terminology in the false reports of two boat sinkings have Coast Guard investigators trying to determine if the same man was involved in both..', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/coast-guard-trying-to-tie-sandy-hook-hoax-to-one-in-texas/', 'snippet': 'Similar voices and terminology in the false reports of two boat sinkings have Coast Guard investigators trying to determine if the same man was involved in both..', 'lead_paragraph': 'The vessel-in-distress calls, placed to the Coast Guard three weeks and half a continent apart, were strangely similar.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coast Guard Investigating if Hoaxes in New Jersey and Texas Are Linked', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coast Guard Investigating if Hoaxes in New Jersey and Texas Are Linked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hoaxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Coast Guard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Galveston (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:32:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/807c9e9a-773f-5829-bbd1-b4f65a825503', 'word_count': 541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/807c9e9a-773f-5829-bbd1-b4f65a825503'}, {'abstract': 'Campaign aides wanted to discuss what they called President Obama’s “record of failure on the economy.” Reporters wanted to know about Mr. Romney’s views on immigration. The conference call abruptly ended.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/speaking-of-the-economy-lets-talk-about-immigration/', 'snippet': 'Campaign aides wanted to discuss what they called President Obama’s “record of failure on the economy.” Reporters wanted to know about Mr. Romney’s views on immigration. The conference call abruptly ended.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s on the mind of a campaign’s message machine may not be the burning issue in journalists’ minds. When Mitt Romney’s campaign held a conference call with reporters on Wednesday morning to discuss what it called President Obama’s “record of failure on the economy,” the first three questions from reporters were about Mr. Romney’s views on immigration. Campaign press aides abruptly ended the conversation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Speaking of the Economy, Let’s Talk About Immigration', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b08b3861-bede-5e42-bf86-a33e8bc13589', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b08b3861-bede-5e42-bf86-a33e8bc13589'}, {'abstract': 'Iranian politicians and military commanders said Wednesday that their country would never relinquish what they called its nuclear rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/world/middleeast/iran-officials-assert-defiance-of-west-in-aftermath-of-nuclear-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Iranian politicians and military commanders said Wednesday that their country would never relinquish what they called its nuclear rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iranian politicians and military commanders said Wednesday that their country would never relinquish what they called its nuclear rights, a day after talks between Iran and world powers in Moscow failed to make substantive progress in the dispute over Iran’s uranium enrichment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran Officials Assert Defiance of West in Aftermath of Nuclear Talks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran Officials Assert Defiance of West in Aftermath of Nuclear Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jalili, Saeed', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65daae29-6483-5f9c-b43a-a7216a590aa0', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65daae29-6483-5f9c-b43a-a7216a590aa0'}, {'abstract': 'The Romney campaign contemplates playing blue collar identity politics with its veep pick.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/the-pawlenty-possibility/', 'snippet': 'The Romney campaign contemplates playing blue collar identity politics with its veep pick.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hard on the heels of the (swiftly denied, but totally plausible) report that Team Romney isn’t even vetting Marco Rubio as a potential running mate comes a Wall Street Journal report that Tim Pawlenty’s star is rising in Romneyland:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'h