e': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wurzelbacher, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d23323d-745b-596f-b86d-66f3e15e2891', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d23323d-745b-596f-b86d-66f3e15e2891'}, {'abstract': 'Carbon isotope analysis of residues from excavated pottery indicated that people 7,000 years ago in what is now Libya had milk and other dairy products as part of their diet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/science/in-african-pottery-evidence-of-ancient-dairy-farmers.html', 'snippet': 'Carbon isotope analysis of residues from excavated pottery indicated that people 7,000 years ago in what is now Libya had milk and other dairy products as part of their diet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prehistoric people in Saharan Africa had dairy farming operations 7,000 years ago, a new study reports — an insight revealed by their pottery. Researchers performed isotope analysis on samples drawn from excavated pottery, and were able to identify organic residues that originated from dairy fat.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26OBMILK3/26OBOX3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26OBMILK3/26OBOX3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26OBMILK3/26OBOX3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26OBMILK3/26OBOX3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26OBMILK3/26OBOX3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ancient Dairy Farmers Of the Green Sahara', 'kicker': 'Observatory', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ancient Dairy Farmers Of the Green Sahara', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHAEOLOGY', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ceramics and Pottery', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dairy Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTHROPOLOGY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:58:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c31b516-0e60-51cd-96c4-2ce45a59b581', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c31b516-0e60-51cd-96c4-2ce45a59b581'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama and several conservative groups are going head-to-head in a flurry of new attack ads, trading accusations over mishandled economic policies and inattention to the plight of struggling Americans.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/new-ads-trade-shots-on-the-economy/', 'snippet': 'President Obama and several conservative groups are going head-to-head in a flurry of new attack ads, trading accusations over mishandled economic policies and inattention to the plight of struggling Americans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama and several conservative groups are going head-to-head in a flurry of new attack ads, trading accusations over mishandled economic policies and inattention to the plight of struggling Americans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ads Trade Shots on the Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T17:58:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7864b48b-da1b-5aac-9c42-f8c3d70d4450', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7864b48b-da1b-5aac-9c42-f8c3d70d4450'}, {'abstract': 'The artist known for mishmashing her own brand of punk, haute glam and horror discusses her forthcoming projects.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/the-lowdown-kembra-pfahler/', 'snippet': 'The artist known for mishmashing her own brand of punk, haute glam and horror discusses her forthcoming projects.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Kembra Pfahler is best known for getting completely naked and then covering her svelte body in red paint, donning a three-tiered black wig, and speak-singing (sometimes roaring) along to the music of her band the Voluptuous Horror of Karen Black. It should be mentioned that despite what her penchant for public full-frontal might lead you to think, Pfahler is 50. She has been a star on the scene since the 1980s, mishmashing her own brand of punk, haute glam and horror. It is always a great thrill to find her and her band of body-painted troublemakers shaking up the status quo at self-important art events, as she straps bowling balls to her feet or stands on her head while a cohort cracks paint-filled eggs between her legs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Lowdown | Kembra Pfahler', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T18:02:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/affec6f3-4758-537d-8482-c6cf75d8f2df', 'word_count': 1280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/affec6f3-4758-537d-8482-c6cf75d8f2df'}, {'abstract': 'The European soccer championships had a rare off day in Poland and Ukraine, and tennis players tuned up for Wimbledon in Eastbourne, England.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/20/sports/20120620photoreplay.html', 'snippet': 'The European soccer championships had a rare off day in Poland and Ukraine, and tennis players tuned up for Wimbled