ntally fit for trial was supposed to be held Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A hearing to determine whether the man who confessed to killing Etan Patz is mentally fit to stand trial will be pushed back until Oct. 1, people briefed on the case said on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sanity Hearing Is Postponed for Man Who Said He Killed Etan Patz', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proceedings In Patz Case Are Postponed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T18:27:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russ Buettner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russ', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buettner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0347d2b6-6bae-5814-be21-0bd01f7892c9', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0347d2b6-6bae-5814-be21-0bd01f7892c9'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Brantley on “Sweeney Todd” and other London shows in which the on-stage death toll is unusually high.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/london-theater-journal-body-counts/', 'snippet': 'Ben Brantley on “Sweeney Todd” and other London shows in which the on-stage death toll is unusually high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the cannibal pie-maker Mrs. Lovett sings “times is hard” in the popular new revival of “Sweeney Todd” at the Adelphi Theater, the words reverberate more than usual. Played by a smashing Imelda Staunton as the ultimate avatar of British can-do resourcefulness, Mrs. Lovett inhabits a visual landscape guaranteed sure to set off alarm bells in London audiences. That’s in addition to the usual tensions that come from knowing that many throats will be cut before the evening’s end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul