ling “Imagine: How Creativity Works,” will continue blogging for the magazine despite several instances in which he recycled earlier work.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/lehrer-apologizes-for-recycling-work-while-new-yorker-says-it-wont-happen-again/', 'snippet': 'Jonah Lehrer, the author of the best-selling “Imagine: How Creativity Works,” will continue blogging for the magazine despite several instances in which he recycled earlier work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The science writer Jonah Lehrer, author of the runaway bestseller “Imagine: How Creativity Works,” has become the latest high-profile journalist to be caught up in a plagiarism scandal, with a counterintuitive twist that could come right out of his own books: The journalist he has been accused of borrowing from is himself.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lehrer Apologizes for Recycling Work, While New Yorker Says It Won’t Happen Again', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lehrer, Jonah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romenesko, Jim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houghton Mifflin Harcourt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T20:03:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71cfa3ff-a7ac-5f52-8423-a3867f29c5fe', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71cfa3ff-a7ac-5f52-8423-a3867f2