: 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/senate-move-to-reverse-mercury-rule-fails/', 'snippet': 'The vote was 46 to 53; only five Democrats crossed the aisle to support it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Senate resolution seeking to reverse federal regulations limiting emissions of mercury and other toxic substances from coal-burning power plants failed to win passage on Wednesday. The resolution, introduced by Senator James M. Inhofe, an Oklahoma Republican, won support from 46 senators; 53 voted against it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senate Move to Reverse Mercury Rule Fails', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Metals and Minerals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inhofe, James M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manchin, Joe III', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rockefeller, John D IV', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T20:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Berg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6756b90c-86aa-5331-94a0-f5dc02267d9e', 'word_count': 250, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6756b90c-86aa-5331-94a0-f5dc02267d9e'}, {'abstract': 'If camping didn’t take planning, more city dwellers would do it. The following Web sites will take the headache out of the process.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/the-campster-outdoorsy-web-sites/', 'snippet': 'If camping didn’t take planning, more city dwellers would do it. The following Web sites will take the headache out of the process.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If camping didn’t take planning, more city dwellers would do it. (How much easier to book that hotel room in the Hamptons.) But even the plushest of hotels can’t supply the recharging that comes from a night spent outdoors. The following Web sites will take the headache out of the planning and point the way to some of the best open-air spots near you.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Campster | Outdoorsy Web Sites', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camps and Camping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T20:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Thrope', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thrope', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://ar