ier souvenirs and royal memorabilia available in London. There were temporary tattoos of corgis, a solar-powered waving doll of Elizabeth and a gelatin mold in the shape of her face. What really seemed to upset people was a Jubilee “sick bag,” for those who overindulged in the festivities.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/fashion/21ROW/21zROW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/fashion/21ROW/21zROW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/fashion/21ROW/21ROW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/21/fashion/21ROW/21ROW-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/fashion/21ROW/21ROW-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long Live the Kitsch', 'kicker': 'Front Row', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Live The Kitsch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prince Henry of Wales', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elizabeth II, Queen of Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diamonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 