, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Plycraft', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cherner, Norman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cherner, Benjamin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-20T22:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caf4042f-62d5-5b79-9032-f7e0dd996962', 'word_count': 170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caf4042f-62d5-5b79-9032-f7e0dd996962'}, {'abstract': 'About 100 lots of works by the likes of Eileen Gray, Hella Jongerius and Ron Arad will be offered at auction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/garden/moss-plans-a-silent-auction-of-its-design-inventory.html', 'snippet': 'About 100 lots of works by the likes of Eileen Gray, Hella Jongerius and Ron Arad will be offered at auction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After closing its SoHo storefront earlier this year, the design shop Moss established itself in a smaller space in the garment district, trendsetting goods and all. “We have no way to display some of this stuff,” said Franklin Getchell, president and an owner of the entity now called Moss Bureau, which offers consulting services along with stylish tabletop objects, furniture and jewelry. “I’m trying to get us out of the inventory business.”', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Moss Goods for a Whisper', 'kicker': 'Currents | Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moss Goods for a Whisper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design an