vironmentalists approve of them, locavores can’t live without them, and the first lady has hitched her vegetable cart crusade to them. As health-giving as those bundles of mouthwatering leafy greens and crates of plump tomatoes are, the greatest social contribution of the farmers’ market may be its role as a delivery vehicle for putting dirt back into the American diet and in the process, reacquainting the human immune system with some “old friends.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/opinion/0621OPEDnassef/0621OPEDnassef-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/opinion/0621OPEDnassef/0621OPEDnassef-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/opinion/0621OPEDnassef/0621OPEDnassef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/21/opinion/0621OPEDnassef/0621OPEDnassef-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/opinion/0621OPEDnassef/0621OPEDnassef-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dirtying Up Our Diets', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dirtying Up Our Diets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autoimmune Diseases', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organic Foods and Products', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immune System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Farmers' Markets", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microbiology', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:05:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff D. Leach', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f78c5aca-945e-5dcc-a621-0f1c3ae67e2a', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f78c5aca-945e-5dcc-a621-0f1c3ae67e2a'}, {'abstract': 'The much vilified operator of the tsunami-hit nuclear power plant at Fukushima releases its final report on last year’s disaster, exonerating itself of any failure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/world/asia/tepco-operator-of-fukushima-exonerates-itself-in-report.html', 'snippet': 'The much vilified operator of the tsunami-hit nuclear power plant at Fukushima releases its final report on last year’s disaster, exonerating itself of any failure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — The much vilified operator of the tsunami-hit nuclear power plant at Fukushima released a report on Wednesday that said the company never hid information, never underplayed the extent of fuel meltdown and certainly never considered abandoning the ravaged site. It asserts that government interference in the disaster response created confusion and delays.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nuclear Operator in Japan Exonerates Itself in Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nuclear Operator in Japan Exonerates Itself in Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tokyo Electric Power Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fukushima Daiichi Nuclear Power Plant (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:05:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hiroko Tabuchi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiroko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tabuchi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9d42e76-a281-5b73-91fa-d50e387d8ed5', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9d42e76-a281-5b73-91fa-d50e387d8ed5'}, {'abstract': 'Former Senator George LeMieux of Florida will end his bid to return to the U.S. Senate, clearing the way for Representative Connie Mack to run as the Republican nominee.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/florida-republican-drops-bid-to-return-to-u-s-senate/', 'snippet': 'Former Senator George LeMieux of Florida will end his bid to return to the U.S. Senate, clearing the way for Representative Connie Mack to run as the Republican nominee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Senator George LeMieux of Florida will end his bid to return to the United States Senate, clearing the way for Representative Connie Mack to run as the Republican nominee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Republican Drops Bid to Return to U.S. Senate', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:08:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Berg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2605ac0b-5816-556a-8ca6-de057984ef4f', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2605ac0b-5816-556a-8ca6-de057984ef4f'}, {'abstract': 'A new campaign for Dramamine is directed at summer vacationers, focusing not on the suffering but on beautiful views from cars, planes and ships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/business/media/new-dramamine-ads-take-aim-at-summer-vacationers.html', 'snippet': 'A new campaign for Dramamine is directed at summer vacationers, focusing not on the suffering but on beautiful views from cars, planes and ships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR a product that treats motion sickness, Dramamine has itself barely moved in terms of marketing in recent years, with no national advertising campaigns since at least 2005, according to Prestige Brands, which purchased Dramamine from Johnson & Johnson last year. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/business/Adco/Adco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/business/Adco/Adco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Aiming for the Time and Place Right Before That Queasy Feeling', 'kicker': 'Advertising', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aiming for the Time and Place Right Before That Queasy Feeling', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Prestige Brands Holdings Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motion Sickness', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson & Johnson', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:10:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Adam Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a47a93a-b240-5d1f-872e-acd8d21af5ca', 'word_count': 897, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a47a93a-b240-5d1f-872e-acd8d21af5ca'}, {'abstract': 'The European Central Bank should gain the power to shut down insolvent banks, limit skyrocketing central bank credit, and make it clear to the euro zone that help from Frankfurt cannot go on forever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/opinion/the-european-central-bank-needs-more-power.html', 'snippet': 'The European Central Bank should gain the power to shut down insolvent banks, limit skyrocketing central bank credit, and make it clear to the euro zone that help from Frankfurt cannot go on forever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the world economy teeters again, pressure is mounting on central banks to reopen their spigots, make it even cheaper for companies and households to borrow money, and prop up commercial banks to prevent another financial crisis. On Wednesday, the Federal Reserve, which had already promised to keep short-term interest rates near zero until the end of 2014, extended its latest, modest strategy to keep long-term rates down, too.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Needs a Federal Reserve', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Europe Needs a Federal Reserve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bundesbank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:22:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Tornell and Frank Westermann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tornell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Westermann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd2f3afd-bf38-58a4-857f-985acb10cfd9', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd2f3afd-bf38-58a4-857f-985acb10cfd9'}, {'abstract': 'Remedy, a 34-year-old quarter horse and stalwart, used to rule his fellow horses, but not anymore. Is this a sign of the inevitable drawing near?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/opinion/one-last-lesson.html', 'snippet': 'Remedy, a 34-year-old quarter horse and stalwart, used to rule his fellow horses, but not anymore. Is this a sign of the inevitable drawing near?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early May, my neighbor and I moved my three horses across the gravel road to her summer pasture. Last year, it took a while before her animals — a thoroughbred and a mule — herded up with mine, but eventually they settled down into a single unit. This year, they did something unexpected. They ejected Remedy, my old quarter horse, from the herd. My neighbor put salve on his bites. And, when I went to check on him the next morning, I found him standing alone in the shallow creek, as if his feet were hot. His head was to the fence, and his tail to all the rest of the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Last Lesson', 'kicker': 'Editorial | The Rural Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Last Lesson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:33:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Verlyn Klinkenborg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Verlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klinkenborg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e64fea5-266b-58c8-b24a-2417bd38f3fe', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e64fea5-266b-58c8-b24a-2417bd38f3fe'}, {'abstract': 'Guidance from the Environmental Protection Agency on protecting all bodies of water has been a prisoner of election-year politics. President Obama should intervene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/opinion/where-are-the-clean-water-act-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Guidance from the Environmental Protection Agency on protecting all bodies of water has been a prisoner of election-year politics. President Obama should intervene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In April last year, the Environmental Protection Agency proposed badly needed policy “guidance” reminding the staff of the Army Corps of Engineers of their duty under the Clean Water Act to protect all bodies of water, large and small, from harmful development. The guidance was sent to the White House in February for final approval. There it has languished — another prisoner of election-year politics. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Are the Clean Water Rules?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Are the Clean Water Rules?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clean Water Act', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:36:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd24982b-dafa-5307-88d2-ea68b6635744', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd24982b-dafa-5307-88d2-ea68b6635744'}, {'abstract': 'The Bowl Championship Series commissioners will present a four-team seeded playoff format to university presidents next week for approval.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/sports/ncaafootball/bcs-commissioners-reach-consensus-on-4-team-playoff.html', 'snippet': 'The Bowl Championship Series commissioners will present a four-team seeded playoff format to university presidents next week for approval.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The expected became a reality Wednesday as college football’s leaders announced that they will move forward with a four-team seeded playoff to decide the sport’s champion starting in 2014. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'B.C.S. Commissioners Reach Consensus on 4-Team Playoff', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Commissioners Reach Consensus on a Playoff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowl Championship Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bowl Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:37:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Thamel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thamel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/18e8c31a-78ca-563e-a94d-f441ea25c2d1', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/18e8c31a-78ca-563e-a94d-f441ea25c2d1'}, {'abstract': 'After seven years, the amount of late fees skimmed from the Yonkers Public Library by a member of its staff totaled $163,582.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/nyregion/library-fines-add-up-to-jail-time-for-an-embezzling-employ