ng and forcibly prostituting a neighborhood woman for nearly a decade, said that prosecutors notified them on Wednesday that they were planning to drop all charges in the case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawyers Say Rape Case in Brooklyn Won’t Go On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prosecutor Is Said to Drop A Rape Case In Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brockett, Jamali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crooks, Damien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dula, Darrell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crown Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brockett, Jawara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hersh, Lauren', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T00:51:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Colin Moynihan and Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Colin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moynihan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d599c8d-d98e-508f-b58b-1b9790e88664', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d599c8d-d98e-508f-b58b-1b9790e88664'}, {'abstract': 'A move to muzzle a fund-raising banker may be seen as another setback for the president on Wall Street, where he is raising far less than he did in 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/201