ts-dies-at-91.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Neiman, who painted racetrack scenes and Olympic contests, depicted public life in gaudy colors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LeRoy Neiman, whose brilliantly colored, impressionistic sketches of sporting events and the international high life made him one of the most popular artists in the United States, died on Wednesday in Manhattan. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/arts/21neiman2_337/21neiman2_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 809, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/arts/21neiman2_337/21neiman2_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1617, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/arts/21neiman2_337/21neiman2_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/21/arts/21neiman2_337/21neiman2_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/arts/21neiman2_337/21neiman2_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'LeRoy Neiman Dies at 91; Artist of Bold Life and Bright Canvases', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bold Life and Bright Canvases', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neiman, LeRoy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T01:42:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Grimes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grimes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1ea4be2-8069-5c22-9ece-aef0b6b6be0f', 'word_count': 1330, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1ea4be2-8069-5c22-9ece-aef0b6b6be0f'}, {'abstract': 'The Travelers Championship has succeeded by developing relationships with the next generation of stars and providing them with sponsor exemptions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/sports/golf/travelers-championship-remains-proving-ground-for-young-players.html', 'snippet': 'The Travelers Championship has succeeded by developing relationships with the next generation of stars and providing them with sponsor exemptions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CROMWELL, Conn. — Webb Simpson, the newly crowned United States Open champion, has not forgotten the tournaments that gave him his start. In 2008, shortly after he turned pro following the N.C.A.A.’s golf championship, opportunity presented itself when he was given a sponsor’s exemption from the Travelers Championship here. Simpson made his second professional start — one of five he made as a pro that year — and tied for 37th, earning $25,800. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/sports/GOLF/GOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u