tics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear and Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/653b3121-d4ed-5c5e-9009-ac9bc70dc4a7', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/653b3121-d4ed-5c5e-9009-ac9bc70dc4a7'}, {'abstract': 'The two men called for the return of the exiled Dalai Lama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/world/asia/china-2-tibetans-set-themselves-on-fire-to-protest-beijings-rule.html', 'snippet': 'The two men called for the return of the exiled Dalai Lama.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Two Tibetans set themselves on fire on Wednesday to protest Chinese rule and to call for the return of the exiled Dalai Lama, according to a report by Radio Free Asia. The Tibetans were identified as Tenzin Khedup, 24, a former monk, and Ngawang Norphel, 22. The self-immolations occurred in the Yushu Prefecture of Qinghai, a Chinese province that is traditionally the northeastern Tibetan area of Amdo. The burnings occurred in the town of Dzatoe, known in Chinese as Zaduo. The report, which cited a monk in India who came from the Yushu area, said that Tenzin Khedup died at the scene and that Ngawang Norphel was badly burned. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: 2 Tibetans Set Themselves on Fire to Protest Beijing’s Rule', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: 2 Tibetans Set Themselves On Fire to Protest Beijing’s Rule', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalai Lama', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immolation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T02:08:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cdeb9fd-2b55-56f8-bd02-a435afebfa6f', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cdeb9fd-2b55-56f8-bd02-a435afebfa6f'}, {'abstract': 'A disabled 67-year-old Vietnam veteran who sells “I ♥ NY” merchandise from a table near Battery Park said on Wednesday that he and two other street vendors had been arrested.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/20/vendors-arrested-for-sale-of-counterfeit-t-shirts/', 'snippet': 'A disabled 67-year-old Vietnam veteran who sells “I ♥ NY” merchandise from a table near Battery Park said on Wednesday that he and two other street vendors had been arrested.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A disabled 67-year-old Vietnam veteran who sells “I ♥ NY” merchandise from a table near Battery Park said on Wednesday that he and two other street vendors had been arrested for selling counterfeit versions of the ubiquitous white T-shirts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Vendors Arrested for Sale of Counterfeit T-Shirts', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T02:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea63ea53-bbae-5b8a-b4bd-4e312c3aa39a', 'word_cou