nt overturned, and $69 million to ads supporting it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/health/policy/health-care-law-loses-ad-war.html', 'snippet': 'About $235 million has gone to advertisements attacking the law, which most Americans want overturned, and $69 million to ads supporting it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DOYLESTOWN, Pa. — Erika Losse is precisely the kind of person President Obama’s signature health care law is intended to help. She has no health insurance. She relies on her mother to buy her a yearly checkup as a Christmas gift, and she pays out of her own pocket for the rest of her medical care, including $1,250 for a recent ultrasound. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/us/21hate1/21hate1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 878, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/us/21hate1/21hate1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1756, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Distaste for Health Care Law Reflects Spending on Ads', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opinion of Health Care Law Reflects Ad Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Advertising', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T02:31:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'subsection_name': 'Money & Policy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename'