correspondents going on hazardous assignments to be trained adequately to face risks. It is unclear if any Indian news organization appears to be providing similar training; of the six news organizations in India that India Ink approached, two responded, and neither provides such training.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Primer on Best Practices for Journalistic Safety', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T06:55:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salil Tripathi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tripathi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce275bc4-3a83-533c-b60c-7ceaf5ce9829', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce275bc4-3a83-533c-b60c-7ceaf5ce9829'}, {'abstract': 'The release of results of two audits is expected to let Spain’s government begin bargaining with European officials over the terms of a bailout.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/business/global/daily-euro-zone-watch.html', 'snippet': 'The release of results of two audits is expected to let Spain’s government begin bargaining with European officials over the terms of a bailout.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — Spain’s increasingly fragile finances were on full display Thursday, with the government again having to pay high interest rates to sell its bonds, and audit reports indicating that the country will need as much as 62 billion euros, or $79 billion