': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/747af4e8-0146-5e43-ab8c-e7f186ed874c', 'word_count': 909, 'uri': 'nyt://article/747af4e8-0146-5e43-ab8c-e7f186ed874c'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Brennan would like to see a start-up culture that’s a rough analogue of the slow-food movement: intimate, deliberate and unhurried.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/in-detroit-the-green-garage-is-a-different-kind-of-incubator/', 'snippet': 'Tom Brennan would like to see a start-up culture that’s a rough analogue of the slow-food movement: intimate, deliberate and unhurried.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Built in 1920, the brick warehouse at 4444 Second Avenue in Detroit used to be a showroom for the city’s pride: Model T-based automobiles. Now it’s a metaphor for urban reinvention. Last fall, the building reopened as the Green Garage, a living laboratory and co-working space for the what its owners, Tom and Peggy Brennan, see as the future of Motown — triple-bottom-line sustainable enterprises that define success by social and environmental measures as well as by financial profit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Detroit, the Green Garage Is a Different Kind of Incubator', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T11:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Bruder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/484f167e-34aa-58ec-97e5-9dc0794caccc', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/484f167e-34aa-58ec-97e5-9dc0794caccc'}, {'abstract': 'Peaches, cherries, plums — poached, stewed, sautéed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/a-dozen-ways-to-serve-stone-fruit.html', 'snippet': 'Peaches, cherries, plums — poached, stewed, sautéed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stone fruit is summer in your hand. To me, there isn’t a better unmessed-with food than a good, ripe peach. Still, stone fruit can be fun to play around with, and a recipe for one kind is a recipe for almost all. Peaches, nectarines, apricots, plums, mangoes and cherries all respond similarly to sautéing, poaching, macerating, grilling, roasting and drying. And once cooked, stone fruit goes with just about everything.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '42', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24eat/24eat-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24eat/24eat-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24eat/24eat-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24eat/24eat-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24eat/24eat-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'image