hers in pursuit of rhinos or tigers in Nepal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Conservationists in Nepal will soon start using special drones as part of an effort to protect endangered species like rhinos and tigers. The pilotless aircraft can alert enforcement teams to the presence of poachers. [BBC]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: A Drone for Tracking Poachers', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T12:13:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/085b2478-99b4-56e2-a1e0-39355f87629f', 'word_count': 171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/085b2478-99b4-56e2-a1e0-39355f87629f'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/morning-take-out-510/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bosses Rein In Banker Who Golfs With Obama \xa0|\xa0 One of the biggest banks in the world wants the president’s favorite banker muzzled. The banker, Robert Wolf, a top UBS executive in New York, is among President Obama’s leading fund-raisers, building more than $500,000 for his re-election so far this year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T12:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization':