esident Asif Ali Zardari to be the next prime minister.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — Pakistan’s judiciary stepped up its assault on government authority on Thursday when a court, prompted by a military-run antidrug agency, issued an arrest warrant for a close ally of President Asif Ali Zardari, effectively blocking his nomination as the country’s next prime minister. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/pakistan/pakistan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan Court Orders Arrest of Presidential Ally in a Drug Inquiry', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pakistan Court Orders Arrest of Presidential Ally in a Drug Inquiry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iftikhar, Arsalan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilani, Yousaf Raza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shahabuddin, Makhdoom', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hussain, Malik Riaz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pakistan Peoples Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zardari, Asif Ali', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chaudhry, Iftikhar Muhammad', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T12:21:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/486f5d3f-4e63-565f-8c08-e27594d8bd6a', 'word_count': 709, 'uri': 'nyt://article/486f5d3f-4e63-565f-8c08-e27594d8bd6a'}, {'abstract': 'In seeking asylum from Ecuador is the founder of WikiLeaks finding clever, if flashy ways of exercising his rights, or is he trying to put himself above the law?', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/assange-the-drama-king/', 'snippet': 'In seeking asylum from Ecuador is the founder of WikiLeaks finding clever, if flashy ways of exercising his rights, or is he trying to put himself above the law?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WikiLeaks’ founder still has it. Julian Assange made headlines again this week by walking into the Ecuadorean Embassy in London requesting asylum. He is hoping to avoid extradition to Sweden (for questioning over alleged sexual abuse and rape) and perhaps ultimately the United States (where Assange believes he could face charges of treason and espionage).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Assange, the Drama King', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assange, Julian P', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Correa, Rafael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T12:23:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Politi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Politi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dac4975-d58e-5b6b-bf2b-4a7a4565df8f', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dac4975-d58e-5b6b-bf2b-4a7a4565df8f'}, {'abstract': 'The defense team for George Zimmerman, the suspect in the Trayvon Martin killing, has released documents and audio and video interviews with Mr. Zimmerman.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/documents-tell-zimmermans-side-in-martin-shooting.html', 'snippet': 'The defense team for George Zimmerman, the suspect in the Trayvon Martin killing, has released documents and audio and video interviews with Mr. Zimmerman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI — George Zimmerman was in a panic. A “suspicious” man he had been watching had jumped him in the rain. The man was pummeling him, slamming his head repeatedly into the pavement so it “felt like my head was going to explode,” Mr. Zimmerman told the police in newly released tapes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/22shooting-cnd/22shooting-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/us/22shooting-cnd/22shooting-cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/22shooting-cnd/22shooting-cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 508, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/22shooting-cnd/22shooting-cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 508,