lls.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/open-door-outlaws/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Many stores are violating a city ordinance by leaving their doors wide open, but the price they pay often is just improved sales and higher utility bills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Summer officially arrived on Wednesday at 7:09 p.m. Hours earlier, on a day so hot that the only things half-baked were the usual weather clichés, many shopkeepers in New York welcomed the season in traditional fashion:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Enjoying Air-Conditioned Sidewalks?  Thank the Lawbreakers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Conditioning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy Efficiency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Affairs Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T12:55:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e871437-b6a1-57b0-af8e-3139517753de', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e871437-b6a1-57b0-af8e-3139517753de'}, {'abstract': 'Company’s 30th season will also include plays by Rajiv Joseph and Jenny Schwartz.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/play-about-checkers-speech-to-kick-off-vineyard-theater-season/', 'snippet': 'Company’s 30th season will also include plays by Rajiv Joseph and Jenny Schwartz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New plays about Richard and Pat Nixon, a high school confrontation and older women looking at their futures will make up the Vineyard Theater’s 30th season, the Off Broadway company announced on Thursday. The Vineyard also announced that the new musical “The Landing,” with music by the Tony Award winner John Kander (“Cabaret,” “Chicago”) and lyrics and book by Greg Pierce (“Slowgirl”), will be produced in the fall of 2013. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Play About ‘Checkers’ Speech to Kick Off Vineyard Theater Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vineyard Theater Plans ‘Checkers’ Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Joseph, Rajiv', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Douglas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Jenny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vineyard Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T13:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25081c3d-e336-5000-bd05-f0d09c13a582', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25081c3d-e336-5000-bd05-f0d09c13a582'}, {'abstract': 'Here are 20 of summer’s must-reads to pack in your beach tote.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/fashion-books-for-summer-reading/', 'snippet': 'Here are 20 of summer’s must-reads to pack in your beach tote.', 'lead_parag