d', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Richard', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:08:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f279065-0ee6-57e5-9ee5-28ae963aa1f8', 'word_count': 998, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f279065-0ee6-57e5-9ee5-28ae963aa1f8'}, {'abstract': 'Crossroads GPS should reveal its list of donors. But transparency isn’t enough to fix the campaign finance system.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/disclosure-would-be-great-then-what/', 'snippet': 'Crossroads GPS should reveal its list of donors. But transparency isn’t enough to fix the campaign finance system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama’s lawyers have sent a letter to the Federal Election Commission complaining that Crossroads GPS, a partisan campaign committee that pretends to be a “social welfare” organization, is really a partisan campaign committee that pretends to be a “social welfare” organization.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disclosure Would Be Great. Then What?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rove, Karl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:10:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca934782-4382-5945-b7b6-51059ac5a69f', 'word_count': 422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca934782-4382-5945-b7b6-51059ac5a69f'}, {'abstract': 'Also, Julian Assange’s prospects at the Ecuadorian Embassy, new music services take on Pandora, and remembering LeRoy Neiman.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/the-breakfast-meeting-fox-friends-and-the-campaign-and-a-new-iphone-rival/', 'snippet': 'Also, Julian Assange’s prospects at the Ecuadorian Embassy, new music services take on Pandora, and remembering LeRoy Neiman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The morning show “Fox & Friends” has become the home of some of the most strident attacks on President Obama at Fox News, Jeremy W. Peters reports. It is also a reliably friendly landing spot for Mitt Romney, who has appeared as a guest 21 times in the last year. Fox News officials stress that the show falls under the network’s entertainment umbrella and does not pretend to be straight news, but, even so, Mr. Peters writes that “Fox & Friends” offers a test for the network and Mr. Obama’s reelection campaign:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: ‘Fox & Friends’ and the Campaign, and a New iPhone Rival', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70bdb378-3402-5201-8b86-bb313ebb8c9e', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70bdb378-3402-5201-8b86-bb313ebb8c9e'}, {'abstract': 'Another major power outage in Venezuela, another wild government response. Mismanagement and underinvestment didn’t cause the grid’s latest failure. A possum did.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/the-possum-ate-my-cable/', 'snippet': 'Another major power outage in Venezuela, another wild government response. Mismanagement and underinvestment didn’t cause the grid’s latest failure. A possum did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Venezuelans are pretty jaded about the news these days, and for good reason. Newspapers often read like a magic-realist novel: the president’s daughter redesigns national symbols on a whim; the government might mess with the time on your watch and the remains of independence-era heroes. But the bizarreness reached a new height this week when the Venezuelan government announced that the major blackout Ciudad Guayana had suffered the day before was to be blamed, not on years of mismanagement and underinvestment, but on a wily possum that had chewed through cables at a local substation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Possum Ate My Cable', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab13fc70-b3ee-55a2-928f-30dcce68ef56', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab13fc70-b3ee-55a2-928f-30dcce68ef56'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/what-were-reading-462/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Serious Eats: “Great bartenders are born, not made.” Do you have what it takes? Michael Neff (above) offers 20 rules for bartenders. See where you fit in, even if you weren’t born with a vest and sleeve garters. — Eric Asimov ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:14:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5dbe1531-95ec-53a0-bcae-d6b13b5528ab', 'word_count': 626, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5dbe1531-95ec-53a0-bcae-d6b13b5528ab'}, {'abstract': 'ESPN will show each round of Wimbledon live, a departure from tournament coverage that had been shown on NBC.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/espn-will-emphasize-live-coverage-of-wimbledon/', 'snippet': 'ESPN will show each round of Wimbledon live, a departure from tournament coverage that had been shown on NBC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The ESPN networks take over full coverage of Wimbledon for the first time next week, ending NBC’s 43-year partnership with the tournament, a switch that was motivated in part by the All-England Club’s frustration with NBC’s inability to consistently show live tennis.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ESPN Will Emphasize Live Coverage of Wimbledon', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'All England Lawn Tennis and Croquet Club', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ESPN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:17:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e6c343f1-ab0f-554b-ab19-8cffa62af4f8', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e6c343f1-ab0f-554b-ab19-8cffa62af4f8'}, {'abstract': 'Sportswriters brace for a world in which college football may get a playoff and LeBron James may get a championship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/sports/football-and-basketball-prepare-for-changeup-leading-off.html', 'snippet': 'Sportswriters brace for a world in which college football may get a playoff and LeBron James may get a championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seemed as if Wednesday existed in sports as a day to contemplate the future and how everything is going to change. It appears we are about to exit a world in which LeBron James has become the most vaunted athlete who has not won anything and enter one in which he has. College football moved with more finality out of the hated Bowl Championship Series era and into one with something resembling a playoff. That this all happened on the summer solstice might either prove to you that higher powers are fiddling with our fun and games, or prompt you to say, "It\'s summer for goodness\' sake, why is the N.B.A. still playing basketball?!"', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Football and Basketball Prepare for Changeup', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lundqvist, Henrik', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Malkin, Evgeni', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:28:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66e2e2ab-deec-58c8-b0dc-1bb58b04be27', 'word_count': 786, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66e2e2ab-deec-58c8-b0dc-1bb58b04be27'}, {'abstract': 'On Wall Street, stocks dropped about 2 percent after commodities prices fell and new data heightened concerns about a softening global economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'On Wall Street, stocks dropped about 2 percent after commodities prices fell and new data heightened concerns about a softening global economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Major stock indexes fell to their lowest levels of the week on Thursday, driven down by worries about global economic growth, troubled banks and falling oil prices.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/business/22markets-graphic/22markets-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 292, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/business/22markets-graphic/22markets-graphic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 292, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Markets Down Sharply on Economic News', 'kicker': 'Stocks & Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Markets Down Sharply on Economic News', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Labor Department (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1851c695-924e-5098-b571-4c533f29b4c5', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1851c695-924e-5098-b571-4c533f29b4c5'}, {'abstract': 'On finding ways to enrich children’s lives through a blend of digital and direct experience with nature.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/on-children-and-digital-depictions-of-nature/', 'snippet': 'On finding ways to enrich children’s lives through a blend of digital and direct experience with nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carol Kaesuk Yoon, who writes frequently for Science Times and in 2002 collaborated with me on a story about the growing human influence on that thing called “nature,” had a thought-provoking essay in the paper this week titled “Nature Follows a Path of Pixels Into Children’s Hearts.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Children and Digital Depictions of Nature', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Biology and Biochemistry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yoon, Carol Kaesuk', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:41:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2382baed-5090-5227-9865-612ca48ae10a', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2382baed-5090-5227-9865-612ca48ae10a'}, {'abstract': 'Day 2 of the summer’s first hot spell toppled a record for the date at Kennedy International Airport, but power use did not appear headed for record highs and Con Edison reported few customers without power. Please send us your weather-related observations.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/how-hot-is-it/', 'snippet': 'Day 2 of the summer’s first hot spell toppled a record for the date at Kennedy International Airport, but power use did not appear headed for record highs and Con Edison reported few customers without power. Please send us your weather-related obs...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:33 p.m. | Day 2 of Summer 2012’s opening blast brought more blistering heat and record-setting or record-breaking temperatures, though not in Central Park, weather forecasters said. Power consumption, although high, was short of record levels, utility officials said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Hot Is It?', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consolidated Edison Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Weather Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T14:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b234236-e2f0-553d-bda0-ac2658091270', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b234236-e2f0-553d-bda0-ac2658091270'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for one of Jerry Sandusky’s adopted children said Thursday that he had been abused by Sandusky, and had offered to testify in the case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/sports/ncaafootball/sandusky-judge-instructs-jury-before-closing-arguments.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for one of Jerry Sandusky’s adopted children said Thursday that he had been abused by Sandusky, and had offered to testify in the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BELLEFONTE, Pa. — Hours after a jury began deliberating the child sexual abuse charges against Jerry Sandusky, lawyers for one of his adopted children said Thursday that he had been abused by Sandusky and had offered to testify in the case.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1340, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/jp-sandusky/jp-sandusky-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType