: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6ae5c6f-22fa-5f88-85fd-4593a403a07a', 'word_count': 1309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6ae5c6f-22fa-5f88-85fd-4593a403a07a'}, {'abstract': 'Barring Congressional action, nearly every sector of government will be affected by the $1.2 trillion in cuts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/politics/pentagon-gets-attention-but-planned-cuts-range-far-and-wide.html', 'snippet': 'Barring Congressional action, nearly every sector of government will be affected by the $1.2 trillion in cuts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It is no secret here that come January, barring Congressional action, huge spending cuts will hit the Pentagon. Congressional Republicans, President Obama’s secretary of defense and military contractors have taken pains to denounce the planned reductions, which were scheduled as part of the resolution to the debt-ceiling crisis of last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/CONGRESS-1/CONGRESS-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pentagon Gets Attention, but Planned Spending Cuts Range Far and Wide', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pentagon Gets Attention, but Planned Spending Cuts Range Far and Wide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T15:42:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d94ca9ee-80b7-52e0-ae66-ed29cff3bdfa', 'word_count': 1055, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d94ca9ee-80b7-52e0-ae66-ed29cff3bdfa'}, {'abstract': 'The gases on which most air-conditioners run contribute enormously to global warming. But a new model developed in China relies on a hydrocarbon that is more environmentally friendly.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/my-air-conditioner-envy/', 'snippet': 'The gases on which most air-conditioners run contribute enormously to global warming. But a new model developed in China relies on a hydrocarbon that is more environmentally friendly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With scorching heat enveloping New York City this week, I’m suffering from air-conditioner envy. I want a model like the one I saw in April at the Terre Policy Center in Pune, India. But I can’t buy it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Air-Conditioner Envy', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T15:49:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6737cdac-6ff2-593a-b4a9-1a099e80b33f', 'word_count': 538, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6737cdac-6ff2-593a-b4a9-1a099e80b33f'}, {'abstract': 'A necropsy is planned to determine what killed the dolphin.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/dead-dolphin-found-at-chelsea-piers/', 'snippet': 'A necropsy is planned to determine what killed the dolphin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 6:40 p.m. | A dead dolphin was found Thursday morning in the Hudson River at Chelsea Piers. It was a common dolphin, said Kimberly Durham, a biologist with the Riverhead Foundation, the organization that removed the animal’s body from the marina. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dead Dolphin Found at Chelsea Piers', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dolphins and Porpoises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chelsea Piers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T15:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jillian Dunham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jillian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dunham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/075a7f22-b1fd-5640-9cdd-ac60605db23e', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/075a7f22-b1fd-5640-9cdd-ac60605db23e'}, {'abstract': 'One in seven homeless people have served in the military. This year, at 25, I became one of those homeless veterans.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/in-need-in-new-york/', 'snippet': 'One in seven homeless people have served in the military. This year, at 25, I became one of those homeless veterans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A native of Chicago’s South Side, I was raised in poverty. Several times my mother and I had to take refuge in other people’s homes, and sometimes in shelters. I thought that by joining the Navy at 18, I would get the training and education I needed to improve my life and help my family. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Need, in New York', 'kicker': 'Townies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T16:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/918d7785-2985-57be-b86f-b5059bc0c058', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/918d7785-2985-57be-b86f-b5059bc0c058'}, {'abstract': 'Superfund tours, flight diversions in Maine and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/morning-walkabout-621-flight-diversions-and-superfund-tours/', 'snippet': 'Superfund tours, flight diversions in Maine and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Touring a Different New York Mitch Waxman, who earns his living retouching photos, leads tours of Newton Creek, on the Brooklyn-Queens border, which was designated a Superfund site in 2010. (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Walkabout — 6/21: Flight Diversions and Superfund Tours', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T16:04:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff86bb64-206c-5910-823a-57d01f90fcfb', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff86bb64-206c-5910-823a-57d01f90fcfb'}, {'abstract': 'The justices declined to address whether the government still had the authority to regulate indecency on broadcast television, but excused two broadcasters from fines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/business/media/justices-reject-indecency-fines-on-narrow-grounds.html', 'snippet': 'The justices declined to address whether the government still had the authority to regulate indecency on broadcast television, but excused two broadcasters from fines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — \xa0 The Supreme Court on Thursday declined to address whether the government still has the authority to regulate indecency on broadcast television, but it ruled in favor of two broadcasters who had faced potential fines for programs featuring cursing and nudity on narrow grounds. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/business/BIZCOURT/BIZCOURT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 729, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/business/BIZCOURT/BIZCOURT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1459, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Rejects F.C.C. Fines for Indecency', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Now, 2 Networks Win Ruling On Decency', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T16:05:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cc8ca6d-4dd0-599f-b0ec-806059bcba74', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cc8ca6d-4dd0-599f-b0ec-806059bcba74'}, {'abstract': 'Last night, the SoHo-based sunglasses company celebrated its new collection with cocktails and a screening of a silent short film. Watch it here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/now-screening-warby-parkers-le-chat-cambrioleur/', 'snippet': 'Last night, the SoHo-based sunglasses company celebrated its new collection with cocktails and a screening of a silent short film. Watch it here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night at the Payne Whitney Mansion at the French Embassy in New York, the SoHo-based sunglasses company Warby Parker celebrated Les Auteurs, its new collection, with cocktails and a screening of the film “Le Chat Cambrioleur” (“The Cat Burglar”). Inspired by midcentury French cinema and shot true-to-form on 16 millimeter film, the silent short stars Martine Langatta (wearing the line’s Filmore frames) and Diego Ongaro (in the Winston style). “A lot of what made French films from this period stand out was that the plot was secondary to the attitudes of the characters and the style of the times,” said the brand’s co-founder Neil Blumenthal. “That’s very much the case with our piece.” Watch it here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Screening | Warby Parker’s ‘Le Chat Cambrioleur’', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T16:11:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ee8c63d-1e11-5fe0-b44e-8e5151f17fd5', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ee8c63d-1e11-5fe0-b44e-8e5151f17fd5'}, {'abstract': 'Inspired by midcentury French cinema and shot true-to-form on 16 millimeter film, the silent short stars Martine Langatta and Diego Ongaro sporting frames by Warby Parker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/t-magazine/100000001618100/the-cat-burglar.html', 'snippet': 'Inspired by midcentury French cinema and shot true-to-form on 16 millimeter film, the silent short stars Martine Langatta and Diego Ongaro sporting frames by Warby Parker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inspired by midcentury French cinema and shot true-to-form on 16 millimeter film, the silent short stars Martine Langatta and Diego Ongaro sporting frames by Warby Parker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/multimedia/video-tmag-warbyparker/video-tmag-warbyparker-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/20/multimedia/video-tmag-warbyparker/video-tmag-warbyparker-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/20/multimedia/video-tmag-warbyparker/video-tmag-warbyparker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/20/multimedia/video-tmag-warbyparker/video-tmag-warbyparker-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Cat Burglar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T16:13:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Warby Parker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Warby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Parker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/e62d2a74-6229-5b48-827e-614144b15661', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/e62d2a74-6229-5b48-827e-614144b15661'}, {'abstract': 'Will Democrats invoke the 14th amendment to protect the nation’s credit?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/the-debt-ceiling-escape-hatch/', 'snippet': 'Will Democrats invoke the 14th amendment to protect the nation’s credit?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, when House Republicans pushed the government to the point of default by threatening not to raise the debt limit, there was a lot of frantic talk about using the Constitution as an escape hatch. Because the 14th Amendment prohibits any action that raises doubt about the public debt, the theory went, President Obama could declare the ceiling unconstitutional and simply ignore the House’s threat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Debt Ceiling Escape Hatch', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T16:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Firestone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Firestone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bf2b25c-54f9-5ef4-8685-698dbceacae4', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bf2b25c-54f9-5ef4-8685-698dbceacae4'}, {'abstract': 'Kerry K. Killinger, the bank’s chief executive until his ouster in 2008, is taking issue with a new book about Washington Mutual.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/washington-mutuals-former-chief-takes-issue-with-books-portrayal/', 'snippet': 'Kerry K. Killinger, the bank’s chief executive until his ouster in 2008, is taking issue with a new book about Washington Mutual.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new book about Washington Mutual, “The Lost Bank” by Kirsten Grind, has been praised for its in-depth account of biggest bank failure in the nation’s history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Washington Mutual’s Former Chief Takes Issue With Book’s Portrayal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicke