b_date': '2012-06-21T17:19:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Mac William Bishop, Pedro Rosado and Channon Hodge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mac', 'middlename': 'William', 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Pedro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f648fa67-d2e1-5c5b-8abe-528f696221bb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f648fa67-d2e1-5c5b-8abe-528f696221bb'}, {'abstract': 'The 3-D animated film “Brave” has a female protagonist who finds independence outdoors and tradition indoors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/movies/brave-pixars-new-animated-film.html', 'snippet': 'The 3-D animated film “Brave” has a female protagonist who finds independence outdoors and tradition indoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The riotous mass of bouncy curls that crowns Merida, the free-to-be-me heroine of the new Pixar movie, “Brave,” is a marvel of computer imagineering. A rich orange-red the color of ripe persimmon, Merida’s hair doesn’t so much frame her pale, creamy face as incessantly threaten to engulf it, the thick tendrils and fuzzy whorls radiating outward like a sunburst. There’s so much beauty, so much untamed animation in this hair that it makes Merida look like a hothead, a rebel, the little princess who wouldn’t and didn’t. Then again, Rapunzel has a supernice head of hair too.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 249, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 249}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 785, 'width': 676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/0622wkdBRAVE/0622wkdBRAVE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 63, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Needs a Prince When Fun’s Afoot?', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Needs a Prince When Fun’s Afoot?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMATED FILMS', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pixar Animation Studios', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Brave (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:20:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af35ffca-aa23-56ba-843a-0cf0747044e6', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af35ffca-aa23-56ba-843a-0cf0747044e6'}, {'abstract': 'Timothy S. Durham, who owned and leased exotic cars, was convicted on Wednesday on 10 felony counts of fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/for-convicted-financier-a-farewell-to-bugatti-and-other-baubles/', 'snippet': 'Timothy S. Durham, who owned and leased exotic cars, was convicted on Wednesday on 10 felony counts of fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Timothy S. Durham once presided over an investment portfolio that included restaurants, bars and the National Lampoon constellation of media properties, as well as a dream garage of contemporary and classic sports cars. On Wednesday in Indianapolis, a jury found the financier guilty on 12 felony charges relating to fraud.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Convicted Financier, a Farewell to Bugatti and Other Baubles', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durham, Timothy S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bugatti Motors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indianapolis (Ind)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:27:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualif