fly crashed to earth on Thursday. Its site was unavailable for roughly an hour.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/twitters-site-suffers-some-downtime/', 'snippet': 'Just weeks after unveiling its new logo – a bird in flight – Twitter briefly crashed to earth on Thursday. Its site was unavailable for roughly an hour.', 'lead_paragraph': ' 5:21 p.m. | Updated Further explanation of the company, added at the bottom of the post. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Twitter’s Site Suffers Some Downtime', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Network Outages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:29:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/192be975-924d-5ded-80c5-c0b71296def5', 'word_count': 297, 'uri': 'nyt://article/192be975-924d-5ded-80c5-c0b71296def5'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. field hockey team finished eighth in Beijing in 2008, and have been preparing for strong competition in London.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/the-field-hockey-chronicles-strength-in-numbers/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. field hockey team finished eighth in Beijing in 2008, and have been preparing for strong competition in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michelle Kasold, a striker, has been a member of the U.S. field hockey team since 2006 and will compete in her first Olympics in London this summer. She will be writing regularly for the 2012 London Olympics blog. This is her first post.The 2012 Olympic Field Hockey Team by the Numbers', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Field Hockey Chronicles: Strength in Numbers', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2008)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pan American Games', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Kasold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd8a74df-4399-58b8-8404-13a677dd7244', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd8a74df-4399-58b8-8404-13a677dd7244'}, {'abstract': 'A photography exhibition at Brooklyn Bridge Park and plays at Morris-Jumel Mansion are two free or inexpensive distractions from the heat in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/photos-at-brooklyn-bridge-park-plays-at-morris-jumel.html', 'snippet': 'A photography exhibition at Brooklyn Bridge Park and plays at Morris-Jumel Mansion are two free or inexpensive distractions from the heat in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Miser was younger and needed the money, guarding one of the world’s greatest art collections in a majestic Fifth Avenue fortress didn’t seem like such a horrible prospect, even if the uniform sure wasn’t anyone’s idea of sexy. Summer weekends were tough, though. Long stretches were spent gazing out of available windows, neglecting priceless artifacts. Our holdings of works from Africa, Oceania and the Americas, for example, could have been greatly reduced thanks to the more prosaic distractions of Central Park in summer. Think about that next time you read of some daring art heist somewhere.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/SUBMISER/SUBMISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/SUBMISER/SUBMISER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1998, 'width': 1822, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/SUBMISER/SUBMISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/SUBMISER/SUBMISER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/SUBMISER/SUBMISER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Photoville Comes to Brooklyn Bridge Park', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Bridge Park (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca24672e-cc10-526d-bad9-9ae52a382d72', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca24672e-cc10-526d-bad9-9ae52a382d72'}, {'abstract': 'The Sonics left Seattle and became the Oklahoma City Thunder. Now, former fans find themselves rooting for the Miami Heat in the N.B.A. finals.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/a-jilted-city-finds-itself-enjoying-the-heat/', 'snippet': 'The Sonics left Seattle and became the Oklahoma City Thunder. Now, former fans find themselves rooting for the Miami Heat in the N.B.A. finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE – It was Wednesday, the day after the Miami Heat went up, three games to one, against the Oklahoma City Thunder in the N.B.A. finals. And all around this city, there was a good deal of satisfaction that the Thunder, the team that used to be known as the Seattle SuperSonics, was probably going to come up short in their quest to win a championship.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Jilted City Finds Itself Enjoying the Heat', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collison, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payton, Gary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle SuperSonics', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starbucks Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Seattle (Wash)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:42:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a276f75-0586-5a14-aefe-c7552e619f65', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a276f75-0586-5a14-aefe-c7552e619f65'}, {'abstract': 'He was named musician of the year for the second year in a row and winning best record and best tenor saxophonist to boot', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/sonny-rollins-is-big-winner-at-jazz-awards/', 'snippet': 'He was named musician of the year for the second year in a row and winning best record and best tenor saxophonist to boot', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sonny Rollins, the veteran saxophonist, was the big winner on Wednesday night at the annual Jazz Awards in New York, taking home three trophies. He was named musician of the year for the second year in a row and won for best record and best tenor saxophonist to boot.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sonny Rollins Is Big Winner at Jazz Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sonny Rollins Honored At Jazz Awards', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Anat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coleman, Ornette', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Iyer, Vijay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lovano, Joe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Ben', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Note', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WBGO', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:46:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a51ddb0-2096-5eb2-bf54-c95cce4b0280', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a51ddb0-2096-5eb2-bf54-c95cce4b0280'}, {'abstract': 'The downward spiral in Americans’ trust is not unique to government, though, and it’s also not terribly recent.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/losing-faith-in-american-institutions/', 'snippet': 'The downward spiral in Americans’ trust is not unique to government, though, and it’s also not terribly recent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Tyler Cowen (and then I) wrote about earlier this week, trust in government is declining.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Losing Faith in American Institutions', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:46:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/433715a0-ccfd-5ddf-b4ee-a5509a62b9dd', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/433715a0-ccfd-5ddf-b4ee-a5509a62b9dd'}, {'abstract': 'Mike Tyson will hardly be the first prizefighter to take to the stage after his athletic career is done.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/theater-talkback-boxers-on-broadway/', 'snippet': 'Mike Tyson will hardly be the first prizefighter to take to the stage after his athletic career is done.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ArtsBeat once again is inviting members of the theater world to contribute over the summer to the weekly Theater Talkback column, alternating with the critics Ben Brantley and Charles Isherwood. For the first guest post, Trav S. D., a historian of vaudeville, talks about the long bare-knuckles history shared between the boxing\xa0 ring and the stage. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Talkback: Boxers on Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Moonlighting Boxers’ History of Socko Box Office', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaMotta, Jake', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Spike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trav S D', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyson, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bowery (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trav S.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trav', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'D', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e6c5754-9eb5-5b4c-bd32-d55b757481f0', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e6c5754-9eb5-5b4c-bd32-d55b757481f0'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A. lockout deprived basketball fans of a fully functional regular season, but a riveting postseason has returned professional basketball to form.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/a-strong-finish-makes-up-for-a-strange-ride/', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A. lockout deprived basketball fans of a fully functional regular season, but a riveting postseason has returned professional basketball to form.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the Oklahoma City Thunder await their formal elimination from the postseason, the rest of us can only enjoy – and dread – the waning moments of another brilliant N.B.A. campaign. What began in a Christmas Day fervor has ended with a gift; an exhausting regular-season schedule was upstaged by riveting playoff theater, and has culminated in an unforgettable display of artistry and grandeur in the N.B.A. finals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Strong Finish Makes Up for a Strange Ride', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durant, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westbrook, Russell', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T17:52:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f5d63f2-7a6d-52c2-aed6-c9117a8e8e74', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f5d63f2-7a6d-52c2-aed6-c9117a8e8e74'}, {'abstract': 'Romney shifts on immigration. | The showdown over “Fast and Furious” poses political risks | Connecticut Republicans face off in a Senate race | Romney thanks donors with a personal touch.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/politics/100000001620259/timescast-politics-immigration-.html', 'snippet': 'Romney shifts on immigration. | The showdown over “Fast and Furious” poses political risks | Connecticut Republicans face off in a Senate race | Romney thanks donors with a personal touch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Romney shifts on immigration. | The showdown over “Fast and Furious” poses political risks | Connecticut Republicans face off in a Senate race | Romney thanks donors with a personal touch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/us/politics/video-pol-120621/video-pol-120621-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/21/us/politics/video-pol-120621/video-pol-120621-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/us/politics/video-pol-120621/video-pol-120621-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum