 made voluntarily, but it warned it could have to resort to firings if the unions reject the proposals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Air France said Thursday that it would eliminate more than 5,100 jobs, or 10 percent of its work force, by the end of next year, part of its efforts to return the company to profitability at a time of deepening economic gloom across Europe.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Air France Plans to Cut 10 Percent of Its Work Force', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Air France Plans to Cut 10 Percent of Its Work Force', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T18:13:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af33d2ec-f116-5529-adf0-e0427846590d', 'word_count': 704, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af33d2ec-f116-5529-adf0-e0427846590d'}, {'abstract': 'For Design Miami/Basel, Burstein created designs influenced by the shape of Swarovski’s classic Chaton-cut crystals.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/crystal-clear-eyal-burstein-for-swarovski/', 'snippet': 'For Design Miami/Basel, Burstein created designs influenced by the shape of Swarovski’s classic Chaton-cut crystals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to believe that Swarovski’s Crystal Palace program, in which contemporary designers imagine ever-newer uses for Swarovski crystals, is 10 years old. The years — and crystals, as interpreted by people like Toord Boontje, Zaha Hadid, Ron Arad and John Pawson — have flown by. But last week, Swarovski celebrated the program’s anniversary at Design Miami/Basel with Beta, an installation by the designer Eyal Burstein, of the Berlin studio Beta Tank, in which the crystals were conceptual rather than literal. Beta featured three concrete and metal chairs and a plexiglass bench, all of which were influenced by the shape of Swarovski’s classic Chaton-cut crystals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crystal Clear | Eyal Burstein for Swarovski', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T18:14:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pilar Viladas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pilar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Viladas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4595268f-f3f2-5c07-95b8-b2a2ef587f0f', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4595268f-f3f2-5c07-95b8-b2a2ef587f0f'}, {'abstract': 'What to do about neighbors who keep asking for favors, deciding between a family trip and a pet, and questions about gum-chewing and a malapropism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/fashion/how-to-say-no-to-the-neighbors.html', 'snippet': 'What to do about neighbors who keep asking for favors, deciding between a family trip and a pet, and questions about gum-chewing and a malapropism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently resigned from my job as an engineer to be at home more with my young children. When news got around, I started receiving requests for favors from neighbors (for baby-sitting, dealing with garbage bins, walking dogs). I didn’t mind at first, but now I’m being asked several times a week, often at the last minute and for much longer than originally requested (one hour turns to five). I feel like a lousy neighbor when I refuse, but even that hasn’t deterred the guilt-trippers. Any advice?J. C., Baltimore', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption':