York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/health/21Chen/21Chen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/health/21Chen/21Chen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1501, 'width': 1999, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/health/21Chen/21Chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/21/health/21Chen/21Chen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/21/health/21Chen/21Chen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Doctors Learn Empathy?', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T18:52:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pauline W. Chen, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pauline', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a68216a9-8d1f-5e38-8d76-231dccaf6a0c', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a68216a9-8d1f-5e38-8d76-231dccaf6a0c'}, {'abstract': 'Far more money has gone into attacking the A.C.A. than defending it. Maybe it’s not surprising that people neither understand it nor like it.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/health-care-propaganda/', 'snippet': 'Far more money has gone into attacking the A.C.A. than defending it. Maybe it’s not surprising that people neither understand it nor like it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Times’s Abby Goodnough reported today that right-wing groups have spent $235 million on ads attacking President Obama’s health-care law — and seem to have gotten their money’s worth. People hate the law, they don’t understand it, they think it’s something that will hurt, oppress and bankrupt them — even when it won’t.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care Confusion', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T19:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b000d77-9c0d-55b3-81f5-7d1da4ba959d', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b000d77-9c0d-55b3-81f5-7d1da4ba959d'}, {'abstract': 'Louis C. K. keeps stretching the possibilities of TV sitcoms with the third season of “Louie,” and Mike Birbiglia’s “Sleepwalk With Me” reaches movie screens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/television/louie-and-sleepwalk-with-me.html', 'snippet': 'Louis C. K. keeps stretching the possibilities of TV sitcoms with the third season of “Louie,” and Mike Birbiglia’s “Sleepwalk With Me” reaches movie screens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While “Seinfeld” was famously about nothing, last season “Louie” often seemed to be about everything, whether it was grappling with our country’s history of racism or the inexplicable torture of unrequited love. Yet what makes this FX show the best comedy on television — and its third season, which has its premiere on Thursday, the cultural event I am most excited about this summer — is how it manages to tackle big, complicated issues through a very small prism. The specificity of the New York stand-up comedy world that Louis C. K. presents on this show lets him explore universal themes without becoming abstract, overly cerebral or ever less than intensely funny. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Laughs From the Comic’s Perspective', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Comedy ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laughs From the Comic’s Perspective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'C K, Louis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Birbiglia, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T19:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efebca2b-55ae-5183-8326-75251cba5e36', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efebca2b-55ae-5183-8326-75251cba5e36'}, {'abstract': 'Moody’s Investors Service has begun notifying some big banks that their credit ratings may be cut as early as this afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/big-banks-brace-for-credit-rating-downgrades/', 'snippet': 'Moody’s Investors Service has begun notifying some big banks that their credit ratings may be cut as early as this afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Moody’s Investors Service has begun notifying some big banks that their credit ratings may get cut as early as this afternoon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Banks Brace for Credit Rating Downgrades', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Investors Service Inc", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T19:10:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susanne Craig, Peter Eavis and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c31a8a98-85e6-5a50-8e59-0d55ee2769bf', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c31a8a98-85e6-5a50-8e59-0d55ee2769bf'}, {'abstract': 'Louise Brooks, a popular actress of the early 20th century, left poison-tipped essays collected in “Lulu in Hollywood,” about the moviemaking machine that gave her a career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/books/lulu-in-hollywood-tales-from-louise-brooks.html', 'snippet': 'Louise Brooks, a popular actress of the early 20th century, left poison-tipped essays collected in “Lulu in Hollywood,” about the moviemaking machine that gave her a career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The energy source for Laura Moriarty’s new novel, “The Chaperone,” is its secondary character: Louise Brooks, at the age of 15. This book is really about the older woman enlisted to accompany Louise to New York from Wichita, Kan., during the summer of 1922. Louise was going to study dance. The woman’s job was to keep Louise on the path of virtue. As if. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22MASLIN/0622WKDMASLIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 773, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22MASLIN/0622WKDMASLIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1133, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22MASLIN/0622WKDMASLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22MASLIN/0622WKDMASLIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22MASLIN/0622WKDMASLIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 199, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blunt Memories of Celluloid Life', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Blunt Memories Of Celluloid Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brooks, Louise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T19:12:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Janet Maslin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Janet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maslin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a90a151a-1f20-5f10-9569-f988d1ee469f', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a90a151a-1f20-5f10-9569-f988d1ee469f'}, {'abstract': 'Currently co-host of the 2012 European Soccer Championship, Kiev has become a vibrant 21st-century city. But today’s attractions are just the beginning of the capital’s story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/travel/36-hours-in-kiev-ukraine.html', 'snippet': 'Currently co-host of the 2012 European Soccer Championship, Kiev has become a vibrant 21st-century city. But today’s attractions are just the beginning of the capital’s story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER seven decades of Soviet dominance, Kiev, the capital of Ukraine, has emerged as one of Europe’s most vibrant 21st-century cities. With a thriving contemporary art scene, a new generation of chefs taking innovative approaches to Ukrainian cuisine, and a delirious dance-til-dawn night life, Kiev — currently a co-host of the 2012 European Soccer Championship — is a weekend magnet for European and Russian fashionistas. But new cuisine and clubs are only the latest cultural attributes of a city that has more than its share of ancient catacombs, churches and monuments. Don’t let Kiev’s reputation as “the birthplace of the Slavs” conjure up stereotypes of Slavic dourness. For starters, the city looks as if it was painted like a Ukrainian Easter egg, with brightly colored buildings and gold domes glittering on the hills above the Dnieper River. And then there are the Kievans themselves — a resilient lot whose hearty sense of humor and a seemingly boundless hunger for fun are reflected in the city’s bustling cafes, thronged beaches and bars that never close.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24HOURS_SPAN/24HOU