 on forecasts from Moody’s Analytics, now shows a projected employment gain of only 125,000 in June, down from a projection of 150,000 last week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Darkening Jobs Picture', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T20:41:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Leonhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leonhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef7a6589-b1a3-5b91-920e-b09416757f69', 'word_count': 239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef7a6589-b1a3-5b91-920e-b09416757f69'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s Newport Folk Festival has some indie-rock additions in its lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/music/newport-folk-festival-2012.html', 'snippet': 'This year’s Newport Folk Festival has some indie-rock additions in its lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My last visit to the Newport Folk Festival was 10 years ago, when Bob Dylan made his long-awaited return, bringing a heavy dose of mystique and a fainter trace of closure. He hadn’t played Newport since 1965 — the year Dylan Went Electric, as lore would have it, raising the stakes for rock ’n’ roll artistry and planting a stake in the heart of the folk revival. Of course the rift was never really that simple, and the reunion was no act of penitence. In 2002 Mr. Dylan showed up in a fake beard and a cowboy suit and, backed by his whip-smart band, played a proud, locomotive set. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/22CHINEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/22CHINEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/0622WKDCHINEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/0622WKDCHINEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/22CHINEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/22CHINEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CHINEN_SPAN/22CHINEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Faces for a Familiar Festival', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Music', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Faces for a Familiar Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {