em without doing a lot of number-crunching.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tool for Selecting the Best Cash-Back Credit Card', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larson, Erik', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMPANY', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Capital One Financial Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:08:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b7ee2b4-28b0-5539-904b-3b54b572986a', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b7ee2b4-28b0-5539-904b-3b54b572986a'}, {'abstract': 'Ai Weiwei, whose probation followed his 81 days of detention last year, said he was still unable to leave the country because he was being investigated on other charges.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/world/asia/chinese-artist-ai-weiwei-ends-yearlong-probation.html', 'snippet': 'Ai Weiwei, whose probation followed his 81 days of detention last year, said he was still unable to leave the country because he was being investigated on other charges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — Ai Weiwei, the Chinese rebel artist, said Thursday that his one-year probation had ended but that the police had told him he could not leave China because of continuing investigations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22beijing_337/22beijing_337-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Dissident Artist Ends Yearlong Probation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese Dissident Artist Ends Year of Probation, but Is Still Under Scrutiny', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ai Weiwei', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:08:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d83f609a-5cb1-5490-983a-23254336deb3', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d83f609a-5cb1-5490-983a-23254336deb3'}, {'abstract': '“Modernist Art From India: Approaching Abstraction,” at the Rubin Museum, examines art of the 1960s and 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/design/modernist-art-from-india-approaching-abstraction-at-rubin.html', 'snippet': '“Modernist Art From India: Approaching Abstraction,” at the Rubin Museum, examines art of the 1960s and 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Approaching Abstraction,” at the Rubin Museum, tries to put an Eastern phenomenon in a Western box. It doesn’t always work, but there’s much to be learned from the effort. It helps to let go of the Euro-American idea that abstraction is purely a formal phenomenon; in Indian modernism it can also be a rupture in narrative. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22RUBIN1/22RUBIN1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22RUBIN1/22RUBIN1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1511, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22RUBIN1/22RUBIN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22RUBIN1/22RUBIN1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaving the Figure Behind', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Leaving the Figure Behind', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rubin Museum of Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:10:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/71fda35f-59d0-5190-8e96-26717337c6d1', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71fda35f-59d0-5190-8e96-26717337c6d1'}, {'abstract': 'An illustrator’s book proposal, lost after he died in World War II, will be auctioned; the town of Garryowen, Mont., along with some artifacts, is for sale; HistoryMiami will have an exhibition about the guayabera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/design/ravilious-book-proposal-a-town-and-custer-archive-for-sale.html', 'snippet': 'An illustrator’s book proposal, lost after he died in World War II, will be auctioned; the town of Garryowen, Mont., along with some artifacts, is for sale; HistoryMiami will have an exhibition about the guayabera.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 1940s proposal for a children’s picture book turned up a few months ago in forgotten files in London, after scholars had spent decades hunting for it as far away as Iceland. The illustrator Eric Ravilious was finishing the images when he was killed in a Royal Air Force plane crash in 1942, at 39.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ANTIQUES1/ANTIQUES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long-Missing Proposal Found Close to Home', 'kicker': 'Antiques', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long-Missing Proposal Found Close to Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eve M. Kahn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d0cab1a3-a20b-5a12-8d9a-8a703d2be135', 'word_count': 919, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d0cab1a3-a20b-5a12-8d9a-8a703d2be135'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s choice of two directors with technology and Internet experience reflects its commitment to pursuing digital opportunities.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/times-co-names-2-directors-including-joi-ito-internet-entrepreneur/', 'snippet': 'The company’s choice of two directors with technology and Internet experience reflects its commitment to pursuing digital opportunities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times Company, continuing its efforts to move forward in a more digitally focused news media industry, has added two members with extensive technology backgrounds to its board.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times Co. Names 2 Directors, Including Joi Ito, Internet Entrepreneur', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Times Names 2 With Broad Technology Experience to Its Board', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC SPORTS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'aQuantive Incorporated', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creative Commons', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Massachusetts Institute of Technology', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Company', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:13:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b0843f1-2956-5f9c-81ea-3d7c8885709a', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b0843f1-2956-5f9c-81ea-3d7c8885709a'}, {'abstract': 'Renzo Piano and his inspiring ideas of what it means to live and work in tall buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/the-shard-and-the-nyt-tower/', 'snippet': 'Renzo Piano and his inspiring ideas of what it means to live and work in tall buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Olympic Games are off and running on TV next month, viewers are sure to see lots of shots of the Shard, which topped out recently. That’s the new London tower above, in a picture taken by the photographer Chris Levine for the magazine earlier this year. (In that same “London” issue the novelist China Miéville provided a word-picture equivalent: “The spine of the Shard soars over South London accumulating glass as if it’s in solution, growing crystals.”) When, as the BBC notes, you’ve got the tallest building in Western Europe — somewhere in Eastern Europe something looms taller, I guess — you can expect it to be the focus of much attention.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shard and the NYT Tower', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buildings (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levine, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Piano, Renzo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dean Robinson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dean', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robinson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/530b633c-8e2b-5e8f-975b-f99fc4926dcb', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/530b633c-8e2b-5e8f-975b-f99fc4926dcb'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic’s “All-Mozart” is this season’s last subscription program, but the orchestra still has a number of summer performances scheduled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/music/new-york-philharmonics-all-mozart-at-avery-fisher-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic’s “All-Mozart” is this season’s last subscription program, but the orchestra still has a number of summer performances scheduled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last subscription program of the New York Philharmonic’s current season began Wednesday evening at Avery Fisher Hall, but it would be understandable if you had failed to notice it. Not to sell the program short — Alan Gilbert led as majestic a Mozart performance as anyone might want, with the kind of guests that would make cognoscenti sit up and take notice.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/FINALE1-ALT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/FINALE1-ALT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN/22ALTFINALE1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Season’s End, a Flourish and a Glimpse of What’s to Come', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Season’s End, a Flourish And a Glimpse of What’s to Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilbert, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mozart, Wolfgang Amadeus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ax, Emanuel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Avery Fisher Hall', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:16:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8eeabb76-b5f6-54e8-8ce0-50767f006bf3', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8eeabb76-b5f6-54e8-8ce0-50767f006bf3'}, {'abstract': '“Closer Than Ever,” a 1989 musical revue, gets a revival directed by one of its creators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/theater/reviews/closer-than-ever-a-york-theater-musical-revue.html', 'snippet': '“Closer Than Ever,” a 1989 musical revue, gets a revival directed by one of its creators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Step aside, all you apple-cheeked newspaper boys and American idiots, you little mermaids and littler orphans. The grown-ups have something to say. You may want to take some notes — and not just because you’ll be one of them soon enough. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CLOSER_SPAN/CLOSER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CLOSER_SPAN/CLOSER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CLOSER_SPAN/CLOSER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 997, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CLOSER_SPAN/CLOSER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1874, 'width': 1925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legac