vision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daniels, Jeff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:21:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/faf6e2bf-7160-56cb-8680-e48042ecbc03', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faf6e2bf-7160-56cb-8680-e48042ecbc03'}, {'abstract': 'The Cassatt String Quartet performed as pictures of the universe were projected above at the Hayden Planetarium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/music/cassatt-string-quartet-at-the-hayden-planetarium.html', 'snippet': 'The Cassatt String Quartet performed as pictures of the universe were projected above at the Hayden Planetarium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As throngs of musicians and listeners, professional and amateur, looked forward to Make Music New York — an annual daylong, citywide celebration of the summer solstice on Thursday — the Hayden Planetarium, with its proprietary interest in the phenomenon, stole a march on Wednesday evening. Part of the American Museum of Natural History, the planetarium presented “Summer Solstice,” a collaboration between the Cassatt String Quartet and Carter Emmart, the museum’s director of astrovisualization and the wizard behind the curtain of the Digital Universe, the museum’s compilation of data gathered from astronomical catalogs and other sources.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/22CASSATT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/22CASSATT_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/CASSATT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/CASSATT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/22CASSATT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/22CASSATT_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22CASSATT_SPAN/22CASSATT_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Look Up to the Heavens and Listen', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Look Up to the Heavens and Listen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Make Music New York (Festival)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN MUSEUM OF NATURAL HISTORY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hayden Planetarium', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cassatt String Quartet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:22:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/70948b1d-8a41-59fb-9998-8188c4fd5cb2', 'word_count': 458, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70948b1d-8a41-59fb-9998-8188c4fd5cb2'}, {'abstract': 'ABC’s all-out commitment to pushing “Jimmy Kimmel Live” during its coverage of the National Basketball Association finals paid off last week with the best ratings for the show in five years.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/kimmel-is-lifted-to-late-night-victory-by-n-b-a-tie-ins/', 'snippet': 'ABC’s all-out commitment to pushing “Jimmy Kimmel Live” during its coverage of the National Basketball Association finals paid off last week with the best ratings for the show in five years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC’s all-out commitment to pushing Jimmy Kimmel’s late-night show during its coverage of the N.B.A. finals paid off last week with the best ratings for the show in five years, and a first: Mr. Kimmel topped both Jay Leno and David Letterman in the most important late-night ratings category.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kimmel Is Lifted to Late-Night Victory by N.B.A. Tie-Ins', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmel, Jimmy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:25:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebf463e5-5da6-5604-82ef-fb8830ec8fc6', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebf463e5-5da6-5604-82ef-fb8830ec8fc6'}, {'abstract': 'The ruling applies across the European Union, and entitles workers sick during a vacation to more time off, underscoring the difficulties in changing labor practices that impede efforts to revive economies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/world/europe/europe-court-says-sick-workers-can-retake-vacations.html', 'snippet': 'The ruling applies across the European Union, and entitles workers sick during a vacation to more time off, underscoring the difficulties in changing labor practices that impede efforts to revive economies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — For most Europeans, almost nothing is more prized than their four to six weeks of guaranteed annual vacation leave. But it was not clear just how sacrosanct that time off was until Thursday, when Europe’s highest court ruled that workers who happened to get sick on vacation were legally entitled to take another vacation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Vacation and Sick? A Court Says Take Another', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Vacation And Sick? A Court Says Take Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:25:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Geitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Geitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d36e4f99-a7d8-5709-a5f8-94f3f1e1bc4a', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d36e4f99-a7d8-5709-a5f8-94f3f1e1bc4a'}, {'abstract': 'David Greilsammer, known for his inventive programs of piano works, will play one of the late-night concerts at the Mostly Mozart Festival. Wine included.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/music/david-greilsammer-at-the-mostly-mozart-festival.html', 'snippet': 'David Greilsammer, known for his inventive programs of piano works, will play one of the late-night concerts at the Mostly Mozart Festival. Wine included.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Little Night Music is the apt title for the Mostly Mozart Festival’s popular series of late-night programs in the Kaplan Penthouse at Lincoln Center. The success of this seemingly modest venture shows that it does not take much to freshen up the protocols of classical music and entice audiences. People sit at small round tables with complimentary wine, taking in starry views of the city. The programs begin at 10:30 and last about an hour. Audiences have relished the chance to hear a string quartet or a singer, a Baroque vocal group or a contemporary music ensemble, in this intimate, relaxed setting. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/22TOMMASINI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/22TOMMASINI_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/0622WKDTOMMASINI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/0622WKDTOMMASINI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/22TOMMASINI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/22TOMMASINI_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22TOMMASINI_SPAN/22TOMMASINI_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Late-Night Drinks With a Pianist', 'kicker': 'The Hot List', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Late-Night Drinks With a Pianist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greilsammer, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mostly Mozart Festival', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:28:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa8ab87a-7483-59d1-97d1-427adec1c83d', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa8ab87a-7483-59d1-97d1-427adec1c83d'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Philharmonic’s “Philharmonic 360” will use the Park Avenue Armory’s cavernous space to immerse the audience in several different orchestras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/music/new-york-philharmonics-philharmonic-360-at-the-armory.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Philharmonic’s “Philharmonic 360” will use the Park Avenue Armory’s cavernous space to immerse the audience in several different orchestras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a way, the New York Philharmonic’s “Philharmonic 360” program at the Park Avenue Armory is a classical music critic’s summer escapist fantasy: The orchestra, freed from the formal atmosphere and mediocre acoustics of Avery Fisher Hall, moves across town to the cavernous armory to present a program far quirkier and more adventurous than anything it does during the regular season.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22WKDKOZINN_SPAN/0622WKDKOZINN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name':