': 'Credit Agricole SA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group A.G', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC.', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Stanley', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Canada', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Societe Generale', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'UBS A.G', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:45:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Eavis and Susanne Craig', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eavis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Susanne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Craig', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33da6f1e-33ca-5248-a129-1ab282b104b0', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33da6f1e-33ca-5248-a129-1ab282b104b0'}, {'abstract': 'A kitchen-supply store in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, is opening an outlet in the Flatiron district.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/whisk-opens-another-cookware-shop/', 'snippet': 'A kitchen-supply store in Williamsburg, Brooklyn, is opening an outlet in the Flatiron district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When creativity hits, cooking often provides release. Take Natasha Amott, who decided four years ago that working with finance in the nonprofit sector did not inspire her. So she opened Whisk, a cookware store in Williamsburg, Brooklyn. On Friday, she’ll add a larger outlet in the Flatiron district that goes somewhat beyond the offerings in Brooklyn. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whisk Opens Another Cookware Shop', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Stuff: Cookie Cutters That Break the Mold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:45:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/753e622b-35ad-5730-9317-5aa76b78c1cb', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/753e622b-35ad-5730-9317-5aa76b78c1cb'}, {'abstract': '“Forbidden Broadway,” the satirical revue that kept theater vultures sated for nearly three decades before closing in Manhattan in 2009, is returning this summer with plenty to spoof.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/theater/forbidden-broadway-returns-in-august.html', 'snippet': '“Forbidden Broadway,” the satirical revue that kept theater vultures sated for nearly three decades before closing in Manhattan in 2009, is returning this summer with plenty to spoof.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hamminess, sloppiness, fatuity, inanity and, if we’re lucky, all-out insanity: such are the attributes that make a bad Broadway show so satisfying for people with a taste for turkey. In recent years mainstream New York theater certainly hasn’t been lacking in productions that embody those essential traits. And disaster cultists who train their sights on Broadway thank the New York theater for continuing to deliver such abundance. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1194, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1757, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22BRANTLEY/22BRANTLEY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 149, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back Onstage, and Showing No Mercy', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Theater', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back Onstage, and Showing No Mercy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALESSANDRINI, GERARD', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:49:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0fb61a9-cbb5-5af0-8603-6309865615ae', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0fb61a9-cbb5-5af0-8603-6309865615ae'}, {'abstract': '“Doctor Who” screenings at the Paley Center in Manhattan feature remastered episodes from this classic series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/television/doctor-who-screenings-at-paley-center-in-manhattan.html', 'snippet': '“Doctor Who” screenings at the Paley Center in Manhattan feature remastered episodes from this classic series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fans of the modern “Doctor Who” — the fast-paced, high-tech, hyper-verbal science-fiction series that will begin its seventh season later this year — most likely know that the show has a long, storied and intensely codified history, stretching back 49 years and nearly 800 episodes. But if they’re American, the odds are good that they’ve never seen the show’s earlier incarnation, which ran on the BBC from 1963 to 1989.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HALE/22HALE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1582, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HALE/22HALE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1326, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HALE/22HALE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HALE/22HALE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HALE/22HALE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 232, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time Machines, Always Cool', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time Machines, Always Cool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'British Broadcasting Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paley Center for Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:49:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Hale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46d34806-e7b3-5671-b40b-d189020a9395', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46d34806-e7b3-5671-b40b-d189020a9395'}, {'abstract': 'We asked 20 arts critics for The New York Times to share the one thing on, or inspired by, the cultural calendar that they most looked forward to.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/from-20-critics-a-ticket-to-summer.html', 'snippet': 'We asked 20 arts critics for The New York Times to share the one thing on, or inspired by, the cultural calendar that they most looked forward to.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUMMER sauntered in this week and it wants to play. What will make its desultory heart race, its toes tap, its synapses fire in the steamy idle hours that stretch ahead? What movie, what concert, what play, what book, what TV show, what dance, what high art or low comedy? We asked 20 arts critics for The New York Times to share the one thing on, or inspired by, the cultural calendar that they most looked forward to. Their answers — your guide to a summer of entertainment — are below.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HOT/22HOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1835, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HOT/22HOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1143, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HOT/22HOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HOT/22HOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22HOT/22HOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From 20 Critics, a Ticket to Summer', 'kicker': 'The Hot List', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From 20 Critics, A Ticket to Summer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:50:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a09b7df-2ecb-5842-9c76-de2aac4e4570', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a09b7df-2ecb-5842-9c76-de2aac4e4570'}, {'abstract': 'In a summer of theater riches, “DruidMurphy,” three plays by Tom Murphy produced by the Druid Theater Company for the Lincoln Center Festival, might be the season’s best.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/theater/druidmurphy-at-the-lincoln-center-festival.html', 'snippet': 'In a summer of theater riches, “DruidMurphy,” three plays by Tom Murphy produced by the Druid Theater Company for the Lincoln Center Festival, might be the season’s best.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Lincoln Center Festival’s rich roster of theater offerings this year includes a couple of promising star turns: a one-man “Macbeth” starring Alan Cumming, and Cate Blanchett portraying the languid, dissatisfied Yelena in “Uncle Vanya.” But the production I’m most looking forward to is “DruidMurphy,” a cycle of three plays by the contemporary Irish writer Tom Murphy, presented by the Druid Theater Company of Galway. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ISHERWOOD_SPAN/0622WKDISHERWOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ISHERWOOD_SPAN/0622WKDISHERWOOD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ISHERWOOD_SPAN/0622WKDISHERWOOD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ISHERWOOD_SP