n Secretariat flashed across the line in the 1973 Preakness Stakes, it seemed he had fallen a full second short of the Preakness record of 1:54. Or had he?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/sports/secretariat-rides-advances-in-technology-to-preakness-record.html', 'snippet': 'When Secretariat flashed across the line in the 1973 Preakness Stakes, it seemed he had fallen a full second short of the Preakness record of 1:54. Or had he?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secretariat, the racehorse synonymous in most people’s minds with thoroughbred greatness, broke many records in his career. The latest fell only this week. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/22racing2/22racing2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Secretariat, Faster Today Than in 1973', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Secretariat, a Record 39 Years After a Victory', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Triple Crown (Horse Racing)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Preakness Stakes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:52:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Mather', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mather', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b352118-9d4e-558e-b734-3109a8c140a8', 'word_count': 1201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b352118-9d4e-558e-b734-3109a8c140a8'}, {'abstract': 'The seclusion may be the biggest selling point of the Hamptons estate belonging to Robert Hurst, a former Goldman Sachs partner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/realestate/exclusive-65-million-property-on-sagg-pond.html', 'snippet': 'The seclusion may be the biggest selling point of the Hamptons estate belonging to Robert Hurst, a former Goldman Sachs partner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHAT could be better than a sprawling home in one of the Hamptons’ most exclusive enclaves on the banks of the tranquil Sagg Pond, with sweeping views of the ocean? What if that home sat on one of the largest parcels of privately owned land in the area — 33 acres to be exact — and was bordered by dozens of acres of protected land, ensuring privacy and pristine conditions in perpetuity?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN/24EXCLUSIVE1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '33 Acres of Privacy for $65 Million', 'kicker': 'Exclusive | Sagaponack, N.Y.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '33 Acres of Privacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sagaponack (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:53:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/365dad7d-9d7a-5e3b-ba0d-ea497d40cfc2', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/365dad7d-9d7a-5e3b-ba0d-ea497d40cfc2'}, {'abstract': 'Christian Marclay’s artwork that runs like clockwork, “The Clock,” will return to New York, this time at the David Rubenstein Atrium in Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/design/the-clock-by-christian-marclay-comes-to-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'Christian Marclay’s artwork that runs like clockwork, “The Clock,” will return to New York, this time at the David Rubenstein Atrium in Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer the city that never sleeps will have another glimpse of an artwork that doesn’t relent much either: “The Clock,” a spellbinding, time-telling 24-hour wonder of film and sound montage by Christian Marclay, the polymath composer, collagist, video artist and pioneer turntablist. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22SMITH2_SPAN/22SMITH2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22SMITH2_SPAN/22SMITH2_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22SMITH2_SPAN/22SMITH2_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg