b84b4a27', 'word_count': 423, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11b539a9-ffb7-5f2d-b98b-810cb84b4a27'}, {'abstract': 'The new government headed by Prime Minister Antonis Samaras plans on a four-year term, but it may struggle to last a fraction of that time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/world/europe/in-greece-a-tenuous-coalition-government-is-sworn-in.html', 'snippet': 'The new government headed by Prime Minister Antonis Samaras plans on a four-year term, but it may struggle to last a fraction of that time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Greece’s new coalition government, sworn in on Thursday, declared that its chief goals were “to tackle the crisis, pave the way for growth and revise the terms of the loan agreement without endangering the country’s European course and its position in the euro zone.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tenuous Coalition Government Takes Reins in Greece', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Greece, a Tenuous Coalition Government Takes the Reins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:53:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a2d98a5-3d0b-5513-bbd6-a55e945214f7', 'word_count': 671, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a2d98a5-3d0b-5513-bbd6-a55e945214f7'}, {'abstract': 'Review our online and sample sale picks of the week, and find some great markdowns.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/online-shopping-sale-picks/', 'snippet': 'Review our online and sample sale picks of the week, and find some great markdowns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Give your wallet a break this week and get ready to beat the Web shopping sharks for some great markdowns. Review our online and sample sale picks of the week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Sale Picks for June 21', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:53:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ana J. Calderone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ana', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Calderone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d10af96d-8881-5020-a9d9-d5b4b4d783df', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d10af96d-8881-5020-a9d9-d5b4b4d783df'}, {'abstract': 'Politics as performance art has a home base in Queens, where Immigrant Movement International continues its work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/design/immigrant-movement-international-in-queens.html', 'snippet': 'Politics as performance art has a home base in Queens, where Immigrant Movement International continues its work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Artists have always blurred the lines among art, life and politics. Joseph Beuys planted thousands of trees as ecological sculpture. Gordon Matta-Clark stockpiled useless slivers of Manhattan real estate to illustrate the absurdity of property ownership. The tradition continues in the work of the Cuban-born artist Tania Bruguera, who has created the equivalent of a full-time performance piece called the Immigrant Movement International in Corona, Queens.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/22COTTER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/22COTTER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/0622WKDCOTTER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/0622WKDCOTTER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/22COTTER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/22COTTER_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22COTTER_SPAN/22COTTER_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Politics as Performance, an Evolving Art', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Politics as Performance, an Evolving Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruguera, Tania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:56:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f59d18d6-097b-56c0-9b33-3c54c26c73cc', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f59d18d6-097b-56c0-9b33-3c54c26c73cc'}, {'abstract': '“Pictures From the Moon: Artists’ Holograms 1969-2008” at the New Museum looks at art in different dimensions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/design/pictures-from-the-moon-holograms-at-the-new-museum.html', 'snippet': '“Pictures From the Moon: Artists’ Holograms 1969-2008” at the New Museum looks at art in different dimensions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Holograms haven’t been cool for a long time. I’m old enough to remember when they were, at least to a 1980s kid raised on “Star Wars” and “Jem and the Holograms.” Somehow they’ve been left out of the great 3-D revival, confined to credit cards, scanners and other useful but dull items.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ROSENBERG/0622SUBROSENBERG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ROSENBERG/0622SUBROSENBERG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1560, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ROSENBERG/22ROSENBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ROSENBERG/22ROSENBERG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ROSENBERG/22ROSENBERG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 197, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Holograms Are Hopping Again', 'kicker': 'The Hot List | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Holograms Are Hopping Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:57:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3634c17b-274f-5168-bb74-4f3c5a97f5bf', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3634c17b-274f-5168-bb74-4f3c5a97f5bf'}, {'abstract': 'An assortment of noteworthy cultural events in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/spare-times-for-june-22-29.html', 'snippet': 'An assortment of noteworthy cultural events in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': ' LUMEN 2012 (Saturday) It wasn’t until February that Christopher Eamon, the curator of Lumen festival on Staten Island, knew that the mountains of salt weren’t going anywhere. This free festival, dedicated to video, interactive and performance art, is being held from 6 p.m. until midnight at the Atlantic Salt Company, which provides New York with road salt. This year’s mild winter meant the mounds didn’t budge. So Mr. Eamon and Melanie Cohn, executive director of the Council on the Arts and Humanities for Staten Island, the festival’s sponsor, decided to use the 150,000 tons of salt as a canvas. The biggest mound will serve as a screen for projections — Marco Brambilla’s re-creation of the lunar landing, and a neon salt digger courtesy of a Brooklyn artist, Jeanne Verdoux, who made the cut in a local open call. The others will be surrounded by performances and site-specific installations. “We’re going to shape the salt in various formations and do something like a salt Zen garden,” Mr. Eamon said via Skype on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spare Times for June 22-29', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spare Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Street Fairs and Festivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T21:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Mancuso', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mancuso', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e6059b-ccaa-5ebd-8c82-e4a3d629ab6d', 'word_count': 3098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e6059b-ccaa-5ebd-8c82-e4a3d629ab6d'}, {'abstract': 'Examples of how graphic novelists have illuminated our stories, especially when it wasn’t possible to use photographs.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/when-graphic-novelists-go-where-photographers-cant/', 'snippet': 'Examples of how graphic novelists have illuminated our stories, especially when it wasn’t possible to use photographs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes circumstance dictates how we treat our articles visually. Often, for example, photography is not practicable for reasons of danger or an inability to capture past events. We’re then forced to find a solution that not only depicts a sense of place but also helps tell the story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Graphic Novelists Go Where Photographers Can’t', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-21T22:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caleb Bennett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caleb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf3eb08-521a-5e4e-8968-a9ba7508358f', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf3eb08-521a-5e4e-8968-a9ba7508358f'}, {'abstract': 'Kenneth MacMillan’s “Romeo and Juliet” is the latest ballet in which three international ballerinas shared the same exciting role.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/arts/dance/ballet-theaters-romeo-and-juliet-at-metropolitan-opera.html', 'snippet': 'Kenneth MacMillan’s “Romeo and Juliet” is the latest ballet in which three international ballerinas shared the same exciting role.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Star quality: I don’t know what it is, but I’ve got it.” The words are Noël Coward’s and “Star Quality” is the title of the marvelous Coward show at the New York Public Library for the Performing Arts. It is also epitomized by three international ballerinas performing next door at Lincoln Center as part of American Ballet Theater’s current season. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/22ABT3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/22ABT3_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/ABT3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1434, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/22ABT3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/22ABT3_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/22ABT3_SPAN/22ABT3_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 105, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'ma