': 'It will soon be much safer to be a fish in Australia, now that the country is planning to turn nearly one-third of its coastal waters into the world’s largest network of marine preserves. The plan would restrict fishing and oil and gas drilling in a patchwork totaling 1.2 million square miles, including the Coral Sea and the Great Barrier Reef. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good News From Down Under', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good News From Down Under', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservation of Resources', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T00:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d275a32-98ae-55f3-957b-a6910e58faa1', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d275a32-98ae-55f3-957b-a6910e58faa1'}, {'abstract': 'The Spanish Supreme Court’s chief justice, Carlos Dívar, was accused by another judge of claiming vacations as business trips and using public money to pay for them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/world/europe/spains-chief-justice-divar-quits-over-trips.html', 'snippet': 'The Spanish Supreme Court’s chief justice, Carlos Dívar, was accused by another judge of claiming vacations as business trips and using