the workers’ smartphone to tell the home office where they are at all times. It may transform the efficiency of utility trucks and pizza delivery, but some see a danger of over ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Workplace hooky, a hallowed tradition that put so many salesmen into movie matinees between customer calls, is so Web 1.0.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/technology/22bits-maps/22bits-maps-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/technology/22bits-maps/22bits-maps-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 931, 'width': 1325, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Maps Where Your Workers Are', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Google, A Mapping App Tracks Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T00:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/433230de-f5d9-59e0-aa61-724115ce73a9', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/433230de-f5d9-59e0-aa61-724115ce73a9'}, {'abstract': 'Myanmar’s opposition leader, Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, urged British leaders to support moves toward openness in her country, in an address to Parliament on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/world/asia/britain-a-historic-address.html', 'snippet': 'Myanmar’s opposition leader, Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, urged British leaders to support moves toward openness in her country, in an address to Parliament on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Myanmar’s opposition leader, Daw Aung San Suu Kyi, urged British leaders to support moves toward openness in her country as she became the first person who was not a head of state to address Parliament on Thursday. Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi’s visit to Britain, where she once lived with her husband and children, was her first in more than two decades. She endured long periods of house arrest in Myanmar, or Burma, but refused to leave when she had the chance, fearing that she would be denied re-entry. “I am here in part to ask for practical help,” she said, addressing a hall packed with Britain’s political elite, “in support of the reforms which can bring better lives, greater opportunities, to the people of Burma who have been for so long deprived of their rights and their place in the world.” Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi, a Nobel laureate and now a lawmaker, also met with Prime Minister David Cameron. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain: A Historic Address', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain: A Historic Address', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aung San Suu Kyi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T00:40:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b79b16f-9915-58ad-86f5-5cb66f808b91', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b79b16f-9915-58ad-86f5-5cb66f808b91'}, {'abstract': 'The group of Keegan Bradley, Bubba Watson and Webb Simpson, who have won the three most recent majors, was the big draw in the first round of the Travelers Championship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/sports/golf/with-a-four-under-66-webb-simpson-keeps-smiling.html', 'snippet': 'The group of Keegan Bradley, Bubba Watson and Webb Simpson, who have won the three most recent majors, was the big draw in the first round of the Travelers Championship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CROMWELL, Conn. — The sound of cheers reverberated Thursday from the first tee at T.P.C. River Highlands, where they greeted the marquee group of Keegan Bradley, Bubba Watson and Webb Simpson as they began the first round of the Travelers Championship.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/y-golf/y-golf-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/y-golf/y-golf-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1843, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/y-golf/y-golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/y-golf/y-golf-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/sports/y-golf