hares began trading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nasdaq has blamed Facebook’s botched debut last month on flawed computers and “technical errors.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Facebook Seeks Answers, S.E.C. Investigates Exchanges', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finger-Pointing at Nasdaq', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greifeld, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NASDAQ OMX Group Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T01:12:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess, Evelyn M. Rusli and Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Evelyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/653647b6-7534-58a6-901a-2b025f08315f', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/653647b6-7534-58a6-901a-2b025f08315f'}, {'abstract': 'Federal prosecutors contend that Melissa G. King stole $40 million from the benefit plans that she ran for Local 147, whose members dig the city’s giant water and train tunnels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/nyregion/6-year-sentence-for-melissa-g-king-who-stole-millions-from-sandhog-union.html', 'snippet': 'Federal prosecutors contend that Melissa G. King stole $40 million from the benefit plans that she ran for Local 147, whose members dig the city’s giant water and train tunnels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By any measure, Melissa G. King lived an extraordinary life, one that far eclipsed her position administering benefit funds for the sandhogs’ union. She spent millions of dollars on herself, hiring a personal staff, buying expensive clothes and jewelry, and running up about $5 million in equestrian-related expenses, prosecutors have said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/nyregion/SANDHOGS-alt/SANDHOGS-alt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/nyregion/SANDHOGS-alt/SANDHOGS-alt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Six-Year Sentence in Theft of Millions in Union Funds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Six-Year Sentence in Theft Of Millions in Union Funds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Melissa G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embezzlement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T01:12:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Weiser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8efc9b99-0178-5102-9d08-a970fbb5d4c2', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8efc9b99-0178-5102-9d08-a970fbb5d4c2'}, {'abstract': 'As the threat of wildfires grows in the West, the fleet of planes used to fight them is aging and depleted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/fire-threat-up-as-vintage-air-arsenal-shrinks.html', 'snippet': 'As the threat of wildfires grows in the West, the fleet of planes used to fight them is aging and depleted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BROOMFIELD, Colo. — With a low roar, the 1954-vintage warplane barreled down the runway and heaved itself into the air, wobbling for a moment as its engines toiled to pull skyward. “They’re not exactly leaping off the runway,” said Paul Buxton-Carr, a Canadian pilot, as he watched the potbellied plane, designed to hunt submarines, climb toward its latest mission: dousing wildfires in the American West. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/subPLANES/subPLANES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/us/subPLANES/subPLANES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 275}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/subPLANES/subPLANES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/subPLANES/subPLANES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 937