would lead to “better safety for our communities.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/nyregion/new-jersey-democrats-call-for-greater-oversight-of-halfway-house-system.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers called for stricter oversight of the system of prisoner re-entry centers, saying new requirements would lead to “better safety for our communities.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Democrats in New Jersey’s Legislature called for stricter oversight of the state’s troubled system of halfway houses on Thursday, saying new disclosure requirements would lead to “better safety for our communities and the halfway house residents.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Seek New Reports on New Jersey Halfway Houses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democrats Seek New Reports On New Jersey Halfway Houses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Community Education Centers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T01:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Dolnick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dolnick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc13dce-e55c-524d-aa14-81e80cfc0cb6', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc13dce-e55c-524d-aa14-81e80cfc0cb6'}, {'abstract': 'At their convention, the Afscme delegates elevated the union’s secretary-treasurer, Lee Saunders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/business/union-defensive-after-wisconsin-vote-prepares-for-a-new-leader.html', 'snippet': 'At their convention, the Afscme delegates elevated the union’s secretary-treasurer, Lee Saunders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Nearly 3,000 delegates from the nation’s largest union of state and local government employees gathered here this week. Judging from the talk on the convention floor, one would hardly know that they had experienced a huge defeat this month in their effort to recall Wisconsin’s governor, or that they faced lawmakers and voters across the country who have grown increasingly unsympathetic to public sector workers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/business/LABOR/LABOR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/business/LABOR/LABOR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Union, on Heels of Wisconsin Recall Vote, Selects a New President', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Union, on Heels of Wisconsin Recall Vote, Selects a New President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collective Bargaining', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN FEDERATION OF STATE, COUNTY AND MUNICIPAL EMPLOYEES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donohue, Danny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saunders, Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T01:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b583f0c-f2b9-507b-a2c7-58069552f308', 'word_count': 1266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b583f0c-f2b9-507b-a2c7-58069552f308'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S.O.C. believed it was issuing a standard cease-and-desist order when it asked knitting enthusiasts to drop the name Ravelympics for a contest they planned to hold. The was when the wool began to fly.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/21/u-s-o-c-knits-a-controversy/', 'snippet': 'The U.S.O.C. believed it was issuing a standard cease-and-desist order when it asked knitting enthusiasts to drop the name Ravelympics for a contest they planned to hold. The was when the wool began to fly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Olympic Committee unintentionally offended thousands, if not millions, of people this week – and potentially dangerous people, too, considering they wield long, sharp sticks — when it sent a letter to a knitting Web site asking that it stop using the term ‘Ravelympics’ for a contest it planned to hold in conjunction with the London Olympics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S.O.C. Knits a Controversy', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'ra