pposition movement against President Mikheil Saakashvili. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Georgia: Satellite Dishes Seized', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Georgia: Satellite Dishes Seized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia (Georgian Republic)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saakashvili, Mikheil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ivanishvili, Bidzina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T03:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b2c9189-dc98-5950-9cc6-339a85593b2e', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b2c9189-dc98-5950-9cc6-339a85593b2e'}, {'abstract': 'The federal government has distributed at least $13.7 billion to date to various government and private groups as part of the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act, the federal health care law passed in 2010.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/22/business/where-the-money-has-gone.html', 'snippet': 'The federal government has distributed at least $13.7 billion to date to various government and private groups as part of the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act, the federal health care law passed in 2010.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The federal government has distributed at least $13.7 billion to date to various government and private groups as part of the Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act, the federal health care law passed in 2010.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where the Money Has Gone', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T03:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/bc86ad60-ac89-56bc-b5fc-e4f5f07953e0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/bc86ad60-ac89-56bc-b5fc-e4f5f07953e0'}, {'abstract': 'In parts of Texas, there is no enthusiasm for two-party politics, with some counties reporting no Democratic votes in the May primaries, and little participation in Republican counties, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/with-few-real-choices-some-just-sit-out-vote.html', 'snippet': 'In parts of Texas, there is no enthusiasm for two-party politics, with some counties reporting no Democratic votes in the May primaries, and little participation in Republican counties, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ross Ramsey, the managing editor of The Texas Tribune, writes a regular column for the Tribune.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Few Real Choices, Some Just Sit Out Vote', 'kicker': 'The Texas Tribune', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Few Real Choices, Some Just Sit Out Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value