yline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and Eric Lichtblau', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lichtblau', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4476b16a-da08-51ee-be90-e2069061186b', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4476b16a-da08-51ee-be90-e2069061186b'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Jeff Wentworth had been expected to face Elizabeth Ames Jones in a runoff after a three-way Republican primary, but Ms. Jones came in last.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/senator-jeff-wentworth-facing-dr-donna-campbell-in-runoff.html', 'snippet': 'Senator Jeff Wentworth had been expected to face Elizabeth Ames Jones in a runoff after a three-way Republican primary, but Ms. Jones came in last.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sleep is a precious commodity for Donna Campbell these days. Even as she seeks to unseat longtime State Senator Jeff Wentworth, Republican of San Antonio, much of her time is still devoted to her work as an emergency room physician. It is not unheard-of for Dr. Campbell to plow through a series of campaign events after finishing a shift at 6 a.m.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21A', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/22TTCampaign/22TTCampaign-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/us/22TTCampaign/22TTCampaign-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarg