gton adopted a go-slow approach to the brewing confrontation between the House and Attorney General Eric H. Holder Jr., worried that a blowup over the “Fast and Furious” scandal would detract from their central message of the 2012 campaign: jobs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Partisan Confrontation That Not All Wanted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Partisan Confrontation That Not All Wanted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Firearms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Privilege, Doctrine of', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T03:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab647773-52e2-5523-bb0a-414e625fd9a3', 'word_count': 988, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab647773-52e2-5523-bb0a-414e625fd9a3'}, {'abstract': 'A rise of up to 2 percent on one-year leases and 4 percent on two-year leases was approved despite opposition from tenant and owner representatives.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/nyregion/rent-increase-is-approved-for-nyc-rent-stabilized-apartments.html', 'snippet': 'A rise of up to 2 percent on one-year leases and 4 percent on two-year leases was approved despite opposition from tenant and owner representatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rent Guidelines Board voted on Thursday to approve a rise in rents on rent-stabilized apartments in New York City, authorizing increases of up to 2 percent on one-year leases and 4 percent on two-year leases.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Board Authorizes Rent Increases for Rent-Stabilized Apartments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Board Authorizes Rent Increases for Rent-Stabilized Apartments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rent Control and Stabilization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T03:32:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8c2867b-0199-5b4e-96a0-ecdcc61b411d', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8c2867b-0199-5b4e-96a0-ecdcc61b411d'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement contains billions in cuts, many to social service programs, and relies on voters approving a tax increase in the next election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/california-reaches-a-budget-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement contains billions in cuts, many to social service programs, and relies on voters approving a tax increase in the next election.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Just 10 days before the start of the new fiscal year, Gov. Jerry Brown and the Democratic-controlled Legislature reached a budget deal on Thursday to close a nearly $16 billion budget gap. The agreement came after days of negotiations, with legislative leaders reluctant to make the cuts that Governor Brown said were urgently needed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Approving Billions in Cuts to Social Services, California Reaches a Budget Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Approving Billions in Cuts to Social Services, California Reaches a Budget Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T03:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Medina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Medina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99f1c8b8-6527-56d7-8352-32979f4fcc9b', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99f1c8b8-6527-56d7-8352-32979f4fcc9b'}, {'abstract': 'The dismissal of Jasper’s first black police chief has touched off a feud that has dredged up bitter memories of the town’s not-so-distant past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/us/fired-jasper-tex-police-chief-is-at-center-of-divide.html', 'snippet': 'The dismissal of Jasper’s first black police chief has touched off a feud that has dredged up bitter memories of the town’s not-so-distant past.', 'lead_parag