': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22norway-span/22norway-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22norway-span/22norway-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22norway-span/22norway-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/world/22norway-span/22norway-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Trial’s End, Lawyers Say Norway Killer Is Not Insane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Trial’s End, Lawyers Say Norway Killer Is Not Insane', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breivik, Anders Behring', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norway', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T09:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Lewis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32ed8c56-ba79-55e9-8db5-46a689af2db4', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32ed8c56-ba79-55e9-8db5-46a689af2db4'}, {'abstract': 'Consciously using your mornings as something beyond a death march out the door can be a great way to give your family your best, rather than what’s left over.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/what-the-most-successful-parents-do-before-breakfast/', 'snippet': 'Consciously using your mornings as something beyond a death march out the door can be a great way to give your family your best, rather than what’s left over.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Years ago, when I was writing a book on time management, a first year legal associate who was the mother of a 2-year-old asked me to look at her schedule. She wanted to spend more time with her daughter during the week. The problem? She frequently had to work into the evening. She pushed back when she could, but as a new hire, she didn’t have much control over her hours, and she seldom got home long before her daughter went to bed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Most Successful Parents Do Before Breakfast', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Time', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T09:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Vanderkam', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vanderkam', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e3922ad-daf4-5880-9f40-3d0a87dc5b18', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e3922ad-daf4-5880-9f40-3d0a87dc5b18'}, {'abstract': 'The table tennis club in California, built by Indian immigrants, will send three Asian-Americans to represent the United States in the London Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/an-unlikely-incubator-of-olympic-talent/', 'snippet': 'The table tennis club in California, built by Indian immigrants, will send three Asian-Americans to represent the United States in the London Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The table tennis club was built by Indian immigrants who made their fortunes in Silicon Valley,” Somini Sengupta wrote in The New York Times. “Its coaches were imported from around the world.” And its star players were born to “immigrant parents from China and Taiwan,” Ms. Sengupta wrote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Unlikely Incubator of Olympic Talent', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T09:31:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc73dcbf-fa57-59f1-ba5e-9fd0b80a4a1a', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc73dcbf-fa57-59f1-ba5e-9fd0b80a4a1a'}, {'abstract': 'The Oslo Accords have done little other than dampen Palestinians’ will to resist the Israeli occupation. Now we endure our ordeal at checkpoints, as docile as too-well-mannered children.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/israeli-checkpoint-willies/', 'snippet': 'The Oslo Accords have done little other than dampen Palestinians’ will to resist the Israeli occupation. Now we endure our ordeal at checkpoints, as docile as too-well-mannered children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jabaa Checkpoint, West Bank — Every day, at hundreds of checkpoints throughout the West Bank, Palestinians are stopped and made to wait, often for a long while, before they are let through. Last week I was halted at the Jabaa checkpoint on my way from my home in Ramallah to dinner at a friend’s house in Bethlehem.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Checkpoint Jitters', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Checkpoint', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ramallah (West Bank)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T09:52:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raja Shehadeh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shehadeh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4eeb52c-8ff3-5584-98bb-ddb2b54c61a6', 'word_count': 688, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4eeb52c-8ff3-5584-98bb-ddb2b54c61a6'}, {'abstract': 'Several readers have offered to help the 16-year-old daughter of a sex worker, who aspires to be a doctor.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/how-to-help-aparna-and-girls-like-her/', 'snippet': 'Several readers have offered to help the 16-year-old daughter of a sex worker, who aspires to be a doctor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The India Ink article, “Meet Aparna, Mumbai’s Teenage Sex Educator,” inspired many among our readers to write and leave comments on the piece, asking how they could help Aparna to fulfill her dream of becoming a gynecologist.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Help Aparna and Girls Like Her', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T09:58:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neha Thirani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thirani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c30dff27-f187-51ad-bd52-983c77e5d40f', 'word_count': 393, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c30dff27-f187-51ad-bd52-983c77e5d40f'}, {'abstract': 'Hospitals are holding increasing numbers of elderly patients for “observation” without admitting them, a new report finds.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/in-the-hospital-but-not-really-a-patient/', 'snippet': 'Hospitals are holding increasing numbers of elderly patients for “observation” without admitting them, a new report finds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Labor Day weekend in 2009, Miriam Nyman, 83, arrived by ambulance at Rhode Island Hospital. She’d fallen, a result of a degenerative brain disorder, and broken her neck. She and her daughter, Tamar Lasky, waited in the emergency room for eight hours until finally, close to midnight, Dr. Lasky needed to go home to sleep.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Hospital, but Not Really a Patient', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fab717eb-68f5-5fe3-bb55-77032e0cece6', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fab717eb-68f5-5fe3-bb55-77032e0cece6'}, {'abstract': 'The lack of a clear legal consensus on the underlying issues of the health care act may pave the way for the Supreme Court to rule based on ideology, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/awaiting-the-supreme-courts-health-care-ruling/', 'snippet': 'The lack of a clear legal consensus on the underlying issues of the health care act may pave the way for the Supreme Court to rule based on ideology, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uwe E. Reinhardt is an economics professor at Princeton. He has some financial interests in the health care field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Awaiting the Supreme Court’s Health Care Ruling', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T10:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/84dc2b30-c50c-52f3-856f-f32e21389b21', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/84dc2b30-c50c-52f3-856f-f32e21389b21'}, {'abstract': 'The vehicles weigh 900 pounds less than their aluminum-body equivalents, a factor that is expected to reduce fuel consumption by 40 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/u-p-s-to-put-150-plastic-body-trucks-into-service/', 'snippet': 'The vehicles weigh 900 pounds less than their aluminum-body equivalents, a factor that is expected to reduce fuel consumption by 40 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a yearlong field test in five regions, United Parcel Service has ordered the production of 150 delivery trucks with bodies built of composite plastic panels. The company said that relative to the aluminum-bodied P70 package car, as the company’s equivalent vehicle is known, each plastic-body truck would lower fuel consumption by 40 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.P.S. Is to Put 150 Plastic-Body Trucks Into Service', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Parcel Service Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T10:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Motavalli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Motavalli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e22983e-dcf3-59c6-9519-fed0b1cb0d6a', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e22983e-dcf3-59c6-9519-fed0b1cb0d6a'}, {'abstract': 'Mitt Romney was more conciliatory toward illegal immigrants Thursday while addressing to Hispanic officials than he had been during the primary season.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/the-early-word-now-and-then/', 'snippet': 'Mitt Romney was more conciliatory toward illegal immigrants Thursday while addressing to Hispanic officials than he had been during the primary season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Today’s Times:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Early Word: Now and Then', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T10:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6d77abe-16af-5912-9ff1-d6ad33b2b4f9', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6d77abe-16af-5912-9ff1-d6ad33b2b4f9'}, {'abstract': 'In 1992, Andre Agassi finally showed all the doubters, himself included, that he truly did have the right Grand Slam stuff in what was supposed to be the wrong place: Wimbledon’s Centre Court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/sports/tennis/23iht-srwiagassi23.html', 'snippet': 'In 1992, Andre Agassi finally showed all the doubters, himself included, that he truly did have the right Grand Slam stuff in what was supposed to be the wrong place: Wimbledon’s Centre Court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Has it really been 20 years since Andre Agassi won Wimbledon, since he rose above the external critics and internal monologue with his long, faux-blond hair streaming out of the back of his cap?', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/