end of each week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our Summer Reading Contest is in its second week. We’ll post the winner from Week One on Monday, July 2.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Interested You Most in The Times This Week?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T11:02:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23833024-f978-507b-a121-12ab505d68f2', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23833024-f978-507b-a121-12ab505d68f2'}, {'abstract': 'Passersby share their thoughts on the environmental conference in Rio and whether such meetings can lead to meaningful policy changes.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/rio20-the-view-from-manhattan/', 'snippet': 'Passersby share their thoughts on the environmental conference in Rio and whether such meetings can lead to meaningful policy changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week we hit the streets of Manhattan to talk to the public about Rio+20, the three-day environmental conference that opened on Wednesday in Rio de Janeiro. We wanted to gauge public awareness of the event and solicit views on whether developing nations should pursue economic growth in an environmentally sustainable way. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rio+20: The View from Manhattan', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations',