c5-5a99-b6a1-9ed99049356d'}, {'abstract': 'Voters pay less attention to the presidential race in the summer, resulting in lots of varied results in individual polls.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/polls-shift-into-the-swings-of-summer/', 'snippet': 'Voters pay less attention to the presidential race in the summer, resulting in lots of varied results in individual polls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With summer here, accompanied by the heat, fireflies and the aromas of food on the grill, we can also expect volatility in the polls. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polls Shift Into the Swings of Summer', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg Business News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pew Research Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Quinnipiac University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:32:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allison Kopicki', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kopicki', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f18d38d3-5492-586b-b804-24d9f700352a', 'word_count': 452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f18d38d3-5492-586b-b804-24d9f700352a'}, {'abstract': 'Kate Summerscale looks at an early divorce case for insight into Victorian novels, health fads and views of marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/books/review/mrs-robinsons-disgrace-by-kate-summerscale.html', 'snippet': 'Kate Summerscale looks at an early divorce case for insight into Victorian novels, health fads and views of marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Nov. 15, 1850, 37-year-old Isabella Robinson went to a party in Edinburgh where she was introduced to Edward Lane. Later she noted in her diary that he was “handsome” and “fascinating,” the first of many entries describing her feelings for Lane, a married medical student 10 years her junior.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/books/review/0624-WULF/0624-WULF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/books/review/0624-WULF/0624-WULF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/books/review/0624-WULF/0624-WULF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/books/review/0624-WULF/0624-WULF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/books/review/0624-WULF/0624-WULF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/books/review/0624-WULF/0624-WULF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '