 None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/sports/23trout1/23trout1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/23/sports/23trout1/23trout1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/sports/23trout1/23trout1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mike Trout, the Angels’ Prodigy, Is Enjoying the Ride', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quick Feet, Quick Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trout, Mike', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Angels of Anaheim', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/307a5d9a-6a3f-52bf-8570-c7c89c13d83a', 'word_count': 1718, 'uri': 'nyt://article/307a5d9a-6a3f-52bf-8570-c7c89c13d83a'}, {'abstract': 'Don Draper and Christian Grey both represent an enduring archetype: the sexy, dashing and emotionally disconnected fortune hunter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/what-don-draper-and-christian-grey-have-in-common.html', 'snippet': 'Don Draper and Christian Grey both represent an enduring archetype: the sexy, dashing and emotionally disconnected fortune hunter.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You can have one girlfriend or three,” my divorced father once told me, offering advice, as usual, that only applied to him. “But never two. When two girlfriends find out about each other, you’ve got trouble.” Presumably two girlfriends would gouge each other’s eyes out, whereas three girlfriends might unpack a picnic lunch of tea sandwiches and cherry wine, lovingly braid one another’s hair and then fall asleep in the sun.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/mag-24Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 92, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/mag-24Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 92}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/mag-24Riff-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 158, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/mag-24Riff-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/24riff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/24riff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24riff/24riff-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '50 Shades of Mad Men', 'kicker': 'Riff', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘A Mean Daddy, a Supervillain, a Lothario and Gordon Gekko, All Rolled Into One’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Gatsby (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mad Men (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fifty Shades of Grey (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Havrilesky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Havrilesky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2756a9f7-cae6-5c0e-b02e-3eaf3a4548ef', 'word_count': 1875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2756a9f7-cae6-5c0e-b02e-3eaf3a4548ef'}, {'abstract': 'Lying, hiding, cheating.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/to-tell-or-not-to-tell.html', 'snippet': 'Lying, hiding, cheating.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My mother has been having memory issues for a number of years. Her neurologist has been telling her it is “mild dementia.” Her cognitive impairment and memory loss have worsened, and I recently met the neurologist without her. He told me that she has Alzheimer’s. He felt we should not yet tell my mother, as that diagnosis has been her greatest fear and it would be too devastating. He felt we could not tell my father unless we told my mother. I am uncomfortable keeping this terrible secret. Is it better to tell a loved one of the prognosis they fear, or is it more ethical to let them live in hopes that they have escaped it? NAME WITHHELD', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24ethicist/24ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24ethicist/24ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24ethicist/24ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24ethicist/24ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24ethicist/24ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Tell or Not to Tell', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Tell or Not to Tell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bible', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheating', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:43:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba9763c-16fb-5107-9343-f3db0ce21ab1', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba9763c-16fb-5107-9343-f3db0ce21ab1'}, {'abstract': 'How an attempt to bring democracy to the workplace spawned a billion-dollar industry and a metonym for drudgery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/who-made-that-cubicle.html', 'snippet': 'How an attempt to bring democracy to the workplace spawned a billion-dollar industry and a metonym for drudgery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine yourself in a typing pool in the early 1960s, amid the clack-clack-clack-PING of dozens of Smith-Coronas. You’re out in the open, like a factory worker, with nowhere to hide from the raking gaze of the boss.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/24wmt-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/24wmt-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/24wmt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/24wmt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24wmt/24wmt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That Cubicle?', 'kicker': 'Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? (Cubicle)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pagan Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pagan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7851da5-c0d9-507b-916e-36eb9e8df551', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7851da5-c0d9-507b-916e-36eb9e8df551'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/the-6-10-12-issue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PREP-SCHOOL PREDATORS', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 6.10.12 Issue', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The 6.10.12 Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:43:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c379ebe9-13ff-561d-816c-3b8bf01678eb', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c379ebe9-13ff-561d-816c-3b8bf01678eb'}, {'abstract': 'The birth-control advocate Sandra Fluke on Rush Limbaugh, hate speech and ‘feminist porn.’', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/sandra-flukes-rocky-path-to-feminist-superstardom.html', 'snippet': 'The birth-control advocate Sandra Fluke on Rush Limbaugh, hate speech and ‘feminist porn.’', 'lead_paragraph': 'After you testified before House Democrats in February about the limited contraceptive coverage in Georgetown University’s insurance plan, Rush Limbaugh referred to you as a “slut” on his radio show. He said you were “having so much sex” that you couldn’t afford all the birth-control pills you needed. Do you suppose he doesn’t understand how the pill works?  It does seem to make a case for comprehensive sex education, doesn’t it? Actually, what I’ve learned has less to do with Mr. Limbaugh specifically and more to do with a part of our population that has this view. Because frankly, you don’t go on national radio and talk for several days about something that no one wants to hear. There’s an audience for this type of sexist vitriol. There is real hate and sexism within our society that we have to do something about.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24talk/mag-24talk-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24talk/mag-24talk-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24talk/24talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24talk/24talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24talk/24talk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Lady of Contraception', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Lady of Contraception', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fluke, Sandra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Limbaugh, Rush', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T14:43:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Andrew Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Andrew', 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/7edc3acb-51bb-58cd-a274-8f45f2779b8d', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7edc3acb-51bb-58cd-a274-8f45f2779b8d'}, {'abstract': 'Forty years after my mother’s boyfriend gave her a stolen piece of Greek history, we’re giving it back.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/magazine/looted-for-love.html', 'snippet': 'Forty years after my mother’s boyfriend gave her a stolen piece of Greek history, we’re giving it back.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I grew up in the East Village, in New York City, surrounded by art. Most of it was contemporary, but there was one piece that was old — really old. It was a fragment of an ancient marble column, and we used it as a doorstop. I’d never seen marble like that outside of the Metropolitan Museum — marble that changed color with the time of day, almost as if it were blushing. After looking at the marble for 30 years, I finally asked where it was from.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lives/mag-24Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1012, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lives/mag-24Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1012, 'width': 724, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 210, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looted for Love', 'kicker': 'Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Looted for Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corinth (Gr