g theme has been “sustainable energy for all” — a push catalyzed by Secretary General Ban Ki-moon in a stump speech on energy poverty that he has delivered many times over the past year. The most effective lines in these speeches draw on his personal experience growing up with no electricity in post-war South Korea:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dispatches from Rio and Nepal: Knife Fights Over Firewood', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Energy and Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Himalayas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nepal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T15:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/727fab88-7662-5d84-8f6f-b43ec03fbed1', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/727fab88-7662-5d84-8f6f-b43ec03fbed1'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/weekend-fare-mermaids-and-gay-pride/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In conjunction with the 30th annual Mermaid Parade, the Coney Island Brewing Company, 12th Street and Surf Avenue, in Coney Island, Brooklyn, will offer tastings on Saturday starting at 2 p.m. of four new beers. One is Shmaltz Brewing’s Mermaid Pilsner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare: Mermaids and Gay Pride', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T15:05:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4be80bc6-83a2-5443-a6c7-31916640272e', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4be80bc6-83a2-5443-a6c7-31916640272e'}, {'abstract': 'Whitley’s boot stamping, guitar strumming and deep wails brought the schmoozing to a grinding, and welcome, halt at a recent performance at the Standard Hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/notes-from-the-underground-trixie-whitley/', 'snippet': 'Whitley’s boot stamping, guitar strumming and deep wails brought the schmoozing to a grinding, and welcome, halt at a recent performance at the Standard Hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had been warned to brace myself for the power of Trixie Whitley’s voice, but nothing could have prepared me for what came spilling out of the mouth of this diminutive blonde. Whitley’s vocals are nothing less than soaring, and the soul that pours forth from her is heart wrenching. Even in the stuffy reality that is an Art Forum/D.A.P. cocktail party at the top of the Standard Hotel, Whitley’s boot stamping, guitar strumming and deep wails brought the schmoozing to a grinding, and welcome, halt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Underground | Trixie Whitley', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T15:07:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By IO Tillett Wright', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Io', 'middlename': 'Tillett', 'lastname': 'Wright', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48c3974a-da74-5103-9168-e0f6589ff7f0', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48c3974a-da74-5103-9168-e0f6589ff7f0'}, {'abstract': 'The time has come for me, a longtime marriage advocate, to accept gay marriage and emphasize the good that it can do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/opinion/how-my-view-on-gay-marriage-changed.html', 'snippet': 'The time has come for me, a longtime marriage advocate, to accept gay marriage and emphasize the good that it can do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN my 2007 book, “The Future of Marriage,” and in my 2010 court testimony concerning Proposition 8, the California ballot initiative that defined marriage as between a man and a woman, I took a stand against gay marriage. But as a marriage advocate, the time has come for me to accept gay marriage and emphasize the good that it can do. I’d like to explain why.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How My View on Gay Marriage Changed', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How My View on Gay Marriage Changed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T15:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Blankenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlenam