aurant, and it’s only open for lunch. But if you make it there, be prepared to eat a lot, and pay only a little.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/travel/restaurant-report-restaurante-da-dona-liceia-in-arapei-brazil.html', 'snippet': 'You have to work to get to this farmhouse restaurant, and it’s only open for lunch. But if you make it there, be prepared to eat a lot, and pay only a little.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wealthiest guests travel to Liceia Franklin de Oliveira’s farmhouse restaurant by helicopter, landing amid the green hills outside Arapeí, Brazil, about 20 miles as the chopper flies from the resort town of Angra dos Reis. But you don’t need to be rich to afford the 70-real prix fixe lunch: that’s only $35 at 1.98 reais to the dollar. Plebeians will, however, need some time. By car it’s a two-hour, 110-mile drive from Rio de Janeiro, the last three miles of which are down a dirt road barely wide enough for a compact rental. (Ask for directions if you don’t see signs in town for the restaurant.)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24BITES2/24BITES2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24BITES2/24BITES2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24BITES2/24BITES2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/travel/24BITES2/24BITES2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb