and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ramsey, Dave', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T15:34:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melinda F. Emerson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melinda', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Emerson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8dc059f-1b78-5d21-97e4-46f34a41f0b4', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8dc059f-1b78-5d21-97e4-46f34a41f0b4'}, {'abstract': 'A selection of events.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/arts/june-24-30.html', 'snippet': 'A selection of events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AN early oratorio version of Paola Prestini’s multimedia opera, “OCEANIC VERSES,” was performed at New York City Opera’s Vox readings in 2011, and it left a mixed impression. But since then Ms. Prestini — an inventive composer whose style mixes the ancient and the up-to-date, the folk inspired and the artfully polished — has revamped the work, expanding it into a full opera, with a libretto by Donna Di Novelli and film by Ali Hossaini. The nonlinear story follows four characters — the Sailor, the Soldier, the Scholar and the Peasant — whose individual quests are linked by a search for a common past in the disappearing traditions of southern Italy. The characters have alter egos of sorts, film versions meant to represent their inner selves. The expanded work is having its New York premiere as part of the River to River Festival. The production is directed by Kevin Newbury, and Claudio Prima, Christopher Burchett, Helga Davis and Nancy Allen Lundy sing the principal roles, with Julian Wachner conducting Novus NY (the contemporary music ensemble of Trinity Wall Street), the Washington Chorus and the Brooklyn Youth Chorus. 7:30 p.m. Monday, Michael Schimmel Center for the Arts, 3 Spruce Street, Lower Manhattan, (212) 219-9401, rivertorivernyc.com; free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24GUIDE2_SPAN/24GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'June 24 — 30', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date':