despite years fronting his own band, the Frames — is now supporting his first solo album, “Rhythm and Repose.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/arts/music/glen-hansard-touring-behind-his-rhythm-and-repose.html', 'snippet': 'Glen Hansard — an international star after “Once,” despite years fronting his own band, the Frames — is now supporting his first solo album, “Rhythm and Repose.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE audience at Housing Works Bookstore Cafe in SoHo might well have expected Glen Hansard to open his recent show there with a song from “Once,” the Broadway show built around his songs that had won eight Tonys just two days earlier. Or maybe something from his first solo album, “Rhythm and Repose,” which was about to be released. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 697, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1393, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/arts/24HANSARD1_SPAN/24HANSARD1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 102, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Busker Is Now Back as a Solo', 'kicker': 'Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Busker Is Now Back As a Solo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansard, Glen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b714f59-3bb3-5d58-be43-b62df178974c', 'word_count': 1585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b714f59-3bb3-5d58-be43-b62df178974c'}, {'abstract': 'Jesse Curtis Morton was sentenced to 11 ½ years in prison on Friday, after pleading guilty in February to federal counts of conspiracy, communicating threats and using the Internet to intimidate.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/man-is-sentenced-for-threats-against-creators-of-south-park/', 'snippet': 'Jesse Curtis Morton was sentenced to 11 ½ years in prison on Friday, after pleading guilty in February to federal counts of conspiracy, communicating threats and using the Internet to intimidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man involved with a Web site that posted threatening messages about the creators of the Comedy Central series “South Park” was sentenced to 11½ years in prison on Friday, The Associated Press reported. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man Is Sentenced for Threats Against Creators of ‘South Park’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Man Sentenced for Threats to ‘South Park’ Creators', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Threats and Threatening Messages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Awlaki, Anwar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chesser, Zachary A', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Trey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Matt', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Gogh, Theo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59fd2f4a-8109-5020-ac44-686c74aa246b', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59fd2f4a-8109-5020-ac44-686c74aa246b'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Times film critics on “Brave,” “To Rome With Love,” and “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/movies/100000001622361/this-weeks-movies-june-22-2012.html', 'snippet': 'The New York Times film critics on “Brave,” “To Rome With Love,” and “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Times film critics on “Brave,” “To Rome With Love,” and “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/video-movies-06222012/video-movies-06222012-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/video-movies-06222012/video-movies-06222012-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/video-movies-06222012/video-movies-06222012-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/arts/video-movies-06222012/video-movies-06222012-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Movies | June 22, 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reviews', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:04:15+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'Natalia V. Osipova', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalia', 'middlename': 'V.', 'lastname': 'Osipova', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/3d229d68-ca7d-5c5e-b7ce-baa3831e5a13', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/3d229d68-ca7d-5c5e-b7ce-baa3831e5a13'}, {'abstract': 'Jolie’s deliberate, look-at-my-leg pose has taken hold of red carpets everywhere, from New York to Hollywood and Antibes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/look-of-the-moment-the-angelina-effect/', 'snippet': 'Jolie’s deliberate, look-at-my-leg pose has taken hold of red carpets everywhere, from New York to Hollywood and Antibes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Angelina Jolie’s leg stole the Academy Awards show this past February, the fashion police raged. Shocked and bemused, no one would have predicted at the time that the thigh-high slit in that Atelier Versace dress combined with Jolie’s deliberate, look-at-my-leg pose would start a red-carpet trend. But alas, the Angelina Effect has taken hold of red carpets everywhere, from New York to Hollywood and Antibes. A repeat offender, the model Anja Rubik took the look to new heights in an Anthony Vaccarello dress slit on the right for the Met Ball, and then in Roberto Cavalli at the Cannes Film Festival. “There is something so seductive about the movement of a dress with a high slit,” said Jason Wu, who designed the racy lace dress worn by the model Jessica Stam to the CFDA Awards earlier this month. “It definitely makes you look twice.” Also spotted at the CFDA Awards was the model Hilary Rhoda, in modernist Rebecca Minkoff. “Adding a slit to a long dress makes it feel less formal,” Minkoff said. “It’s a modern bombshell look.” That’s got legs, no doubt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Look of The Moment | The Angelina Effect', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:12:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29a8ad4f-0d8a-5a32-a098-c1c3b01dbf88', 'word_count': 194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29a8ad4f-0d8a-5a32-a098-c1c3b01dbf88'}, {'abstract': 'Techie-friendly ad campaigns, a T.S.A. gadget that doesn’t work and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/morning-walkabout-622-techie-friendly-ads-and-a-t-s-a-gadget-that-doesnt-work/', 'snippet': 'Techie-friendly ad campaigns, a T.S.A. gadget that doesn’t work and more in our daily capsule of travel news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ads and Apps Two techie-friendly ad campaigns: Crystal Cruises will let owners of iPhones with the Aurasma-augmented reality app use it to view videos that use the print ads as a jumping-off point. Air France has introduced a free iPhone app that lets passengers create personalized, location-based photo albums on their trips that can be shared on Facebook with friends and also with a network of Air France’s “Travel Bookers.”\xa0 (The New York Times)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Walkabout — 6/22: Techie-Friendly Ads and a T.S.A. Gadget That Doesn’t Work', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crystal Cruises', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tate Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c905b34-afe7-5fc7-9b5f-46b02418194b', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c905b34-afe7-5fc7-9b5f-46b02418194b'}, {'abstract': 'While Pakistan’s politicians, generals and judges play tug of war, each in the name of the people, no one is looking out for the country’s welfare.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/pakistans-politicians-are-playing-tug-of-war/', 'snippet': 'While Pakistan’s politicians, generals and judges play tug of war, each in the name of the people, no one is looking out for the country’s welfare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London — For as long as I can remember, the politics of Pakistan\xa0 have been discussed in binary terms: civil vs. military, democracy vs. dictatorship, good vs. evil. The ouster this week of Prime Minister Yousaf Raza Gilani on an order of the Supreme Court changes all that. Thanks to this “judicial coup,” as many in Pakistan are calling the move, the country is now in effect being run by a ménage-à-trois.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pakistan’s Ménage à Trois', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gilani, Yousaf Raza', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Pakistan People's Party", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Punjab (Pakistan)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:14:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb265baf-36cb-5359-b72c-dfb81bdb77fd', 'word_count': 518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb265baf-36cb-5359-b72c-dfb81bdb77fd'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Mourdock preacts to the Supreme Court’s health care ruling.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/whatever-happens-i-will-have-reacted-already/', 'snippet': 'Richard Mourdock preacts to the Supreme Court’s health care ruling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a politician responds to something another politician has not yet said, we call that a “prebuttal.” It’s a variant is the “presponse,” in which networks air the opposition party’s “response” to a State of the Union Address that was taped prior to delivery.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Whatever Happens, I Will Have Reacted Already', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mourdock, Richard E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0b7b839-9780-57ae-8858-069ca09e67e9', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0b7b839-9780-57ae-8858-069ca09e67e9'}, {'abstract': 'Video: This Week’s Movies', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/this-weeks-movies-june-22/', 'snippet': 'Video: This Week’s Movies', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s edition of This Week’s Movies, Manhola Dargis reviews the horror fantasy “Abraham Lincoln: Vampire Hunter” — a film with “such 