incentive?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week’s parental quandary was mine, or, at least, mine and a whole lot of other people’s. The problem? Children squabbling madly away in the car. I offered my solution in the video when I first posted it last week: I will give a Tic Tac to any child who can get through a car ride without poking, prodding or otherwise antagonizing a sibling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should You Bribe Children to Behave in the Car?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Road Trips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T16:55:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fb51bac-5639-542c-af78-3d4963244c99', 'word_count': 838, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fb51bac-5639-542c-af78-3d4963244c99'}, {'abstract': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott talk about summer rock festivals and “The Electric Daisy Carnival.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/arts/100000001621042/the-sweet-spot-june-22-2012.html', 'snippet': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott talk about summer rock festivals and “The Electric Daisy Carnival.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Carr and A. O. Scott talk about summer rock festivals and “The Electric Daisy Carnival.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i