tate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Constance Rosenblum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Constance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenblum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/afdc12a2-acb9-5fb5-9e0e-0db7e2a1f510', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/afdc12a2-acb9-5fb5-9e0e-0db7e2a1f510'}, {'abstract': 'The U.S. women’s soccer team recently spent two weeks training in Sweden and playing matches against the host country. Heather O’Reilly was happy with the team’s play and excited by Sweden’s enthusiasm for the game.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/the-soccer-chronicles-inspiration-in-sweden/', 'snippet': 'The U.S. women’s soccer team recently spent two weeks training in Sweden and playing matches against the host country. Heather O’Reilly was happy with the team’s play and excited by Sweden’s enthusiasm for the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heather O’Reilly, a midfielder on the U.S. women’s soccer team and a two-time gold medalist, will be writing regularly for the 2012 London Olympics blog. This is her second post.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Soccer Chronicles: Inspiration in Sweden', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's World Cup (Soccer)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Reilly, Heather", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sundhage, Pia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Breakers (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:22:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': "By Heather O'Reilly", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Reilly", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6cc3189-51b5-5017-a8a2-67b82393d044', 'word_count': 1025, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6cc3189-51b5-5017-a8a2-67b82393d044'}, {'abstract': 'In the absence of a binding accord, some are questioning whether global environmental meetings are worth the trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/on-our-radar-limping-toward-the-end-in-rio/', 'snippet': 'In the absence of a binding accord, some are questioning whether global environmental meetings are worth the trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although serious policy discussions have unfolded at the Rio+20 environmental conference in Brazil — along with plenty of theatrics — it will wrap up today without committing nations to any binding targets on sustainability. [The Washington Post]', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Our Radar: Limping Toward the End in Rio', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:24:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/444d1139-ca12-54c5-abb9-1260f3568d90', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/444d1139-ca12-54c5-abb9-1260f3568d90'}, {'abstract': 'The country, which is recovering from a banking crisis and recession, even had words of encouragement for Europeans: Things get better.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/business/global/iceland-plans-to-join-european-bloc-despite-economic-turmoil.html', 'snippet': 'The country, which is recovering from a banking crisis and recession, even had words of encouragement for Europeans: Things get better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Despite a sovereign debt crisis that threatens to tear the European Union apart, Iceland is speeding ahead on its bid to join the bloc and even delivered a pep talk Friday to those struggling to hold it together.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/business/Iceland/Iceland-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 835, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/business/Iceland/Iceland-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1670, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Iceland Plans to Join European Bloc Despite Economic Turmoil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iceland Eager to Join European Bloc Despite Turmoil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iceland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:27:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Geitner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Geitner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc469e27-9e93-53b3-a9bf-94b6910a82de', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc469e27-9e93-53b3-a9bf-94b6910a82de'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s Android 4.0 system offers a quick way to respond to a caller, without actually anwsering the phone.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/tip-of-the-week-texting-a-caller-back/', 'snippet': 'Google’s Android 4.0 system offers a quick way to respond to a caller, without actually anwsering the phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever been in a meeting or other quiet occasion where answering an incoming phone call is not an option? Smartphones running the Android 4.0 software (also known as Ice Cream Sandwich in Google’s dessert-themed nickname scheme) offer a convenient feature that lets you respond to the caller with a text message.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tip of the Week: Texting a Caller Back', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Google Phone', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:28:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.d. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2cec002-191c-5944-8c95-24cc4d298abc', 'word_count': 177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2cec002-191c-5944-8c95-24cc4d298abc'}, {'abstract': 'With New York’s economy seemingly recovering, condominium boards are growing more aggressive in cracking down on delinquent owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/realestate/condo-boards-take-a-stand-on-delinquencies.html', 'snippet': 'With New York’s economy seemingly recovering, condominium boards are growing more aggressive in cracking down on delinquent owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A SUCCESSFUL condominium depends, in large part, on owners’ paying their monthly fees promptly and in full. Delinquencies can mean less money for maintenance and amenities — and draw the ill will of fellow residents. While the sheer size of larger buildings can often blunt their impact on the budget, small buildings with a high number of delinquencies can be toxic for buyers and a millstone for sellers.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/24COVER_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 763, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/realestate/24COVER_SPAN/cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1525, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/realestate/