-06-22T17:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70821c41-a60b-523e-b53b-014175c45eab', 'word_count': 276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70821c41-a60b-523e-b53b-014175c45eab'}, {'abstract': 'PBS videos.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/making-sense-with-me-me-me/', 'snippet': 'PBS videos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, actually it’s Making Sense With Paul Solman, but currently it’s a lot of me me me; videos galore. Also some of Robin.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Sense With Me Me Me', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:43:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/092b02c9-4073-5ddb-8f82-808622b70c51', 'word_count': 23, 'uri': 'nyt://article/092b02c9-4073-5ddb-8f82-808622b70c51'}, {'abstract': 'A new online feature showcases all of the finalists and winners in the fiction category.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/down-memory-lane-with-the-national-book-awards-and-not-just-the-winners/', 'snippet': 'A new online feature showcases all of the finalists and winners in the fiction category.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Book Foundation has created an online exhibit to highlight notable American authors like Cynthia Propper Seton, Earl Thompson and Alan Saperstein. Oh, and Hemingway, Faulkner and Flannery O’Connor, too. They’re all among the 373 finalists for the National Book Award for Fiction since the honor was first issued in 1950.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Down Memory Lane With the National Book Awards (and Not Just the Winners)', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Famous and the Forgotten, on the Same Online Shelf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Book Awards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Book Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ac0b183-fead-5e6b-a5fd-097fa11bb0c2', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ac0b183-fead-5e6b-a5fd-097fa11bb0c2'}, {'abstract': 'The bride was surprised when she realized how well the bridegroom fit the vision she had for her life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/letty-brown-and-jan-novak-vows.html', 'snippet': 'The bride was surprised when she realized how well the bridegroom fit the vision she had for her life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN Letty Brown and Jan Novak were introduced by a mutual friend at a Japanese restaurant in Sacramento in 2008, her course seemed set. Dr. Brown, a botanist, was planning to depart for eastern Brazil, where she was to map an uncharted corner of the Atlantic Forest on a Fulbright scholarship.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/24VOWS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/24VOWS1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/subVOWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/subVOWS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/24VOWS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/24VOWS1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/fashion/weddings/24VOWS1_SPAN/24VOWS1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letty Brown and Jan Novak', 'kicker': 'Vows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letty Brown and Jan Novak', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vows (Times Column)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:45:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stacey Solie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stacey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Solie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0c52b26-4979-547c-8b29-52a2e15e0faa', 'word_count': 1258, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0c52b26-4979-547c-8b29-52a2e15e0faa'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists have been documenting what is left of the oil tanker Lightburne, which ran aground in 1939, and other local wrecks to help in the design of a $150 million exhibit at the New York Aquarium.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/planning-a-live-shark-exhibit-by-diving-through-wrecks/', 'snippet': 'Scientists have been documenting what is left of the oil tanker Lightburne, which ran aground in 1939, and other local wrecks to help in the design of a $150 million exhibit at the New York Aquarium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the evening of Feb. 10, 1939, the oil tanker Lightburne ran aground in dense fog on a shoal off Block Island, R.I. In lashing winds and pounding surf, the Coast Guard raced to the site and performed what The New York Times called “one of the most spectacular ship rescues in recent years,” saving all 35 crew members.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shipwreck as a Portal for an Aquarium Exhibit', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Shipwreck as a Portal for an Aquarium Exhibit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diving and Divers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shipwrecks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Aquarium', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wildlife Conservation Society', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Block Island (RI)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:47:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Olsen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1f54d3e-2335-5a3e-b17f-539bdb38c0dc', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1f54d3e-2335-5a3e-b17f-539bdb38c0dc'}, {'abstract': 'Live blogging the Euro 2012 quarterfinal between Germany and Greece in Gdansk, Poland.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/euro-2012-live-blogging-germany-vs-greece/', 'snippet': 'Live blogging the Euro 2012 quarterfinal between Germany and Greece in Gdansk, Poland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Germany Coach Joachim Löw made a number of changes to his starting lineup. Lukas Podolski, Lars Bender, Thomas Müller and Mario Gomez were out; Miroslav Klose, Marko Reus and Mesut Özil are in. Boateng returned to the defense, And there’s more. Perhaps only a team with the depth, and confidence of Germany could and would dare to make such wholesale changes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012 Highlights: Germany (4) vs. Greece (2)', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Low, Joachim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gdansk (Poland)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:48:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b927f99-d10b-5bda-a6f4-2e4e2bf7d93f', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b927f99-d10b-5bda-a6f4-2e4e2bf7d93f'}, {'abstract': 'This year’s N.B.A. title may be an extension of the LeBron James narrative, but Chris Bosh has has his own rightful claim to the Miami Heat’s triumph.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/chris-bosh-the-second-most-maligned-n-b-a-champion/', 'snippet': 'This year’s N.B.A. title may be an extension of the LeBron James narrative, but Chris Bosh has has his own rightful claim to the Miami Heat’s triumph.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This N.B.A. title — and all that comes with it — belongs to LeBron James, the player of unspeakable talent, unbelievable growth and the target of unprecedented criticism. But while his personal journey has become the narrative of an entire league, he shares the Heat’s scene with so many others. Dwyane Wade tabled injury and personal trial to compete for another title. Erik Spoelstra pushed the Heat into the future with his adaptive rotation. And Chris Bosh — the unbelievably strange target of a raging public’s remaining bile — thrived for Miami in a more crucial capacity than ever.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chris Bosh, the Second-Most Maligned N.B.A. Champion', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bosh, Chris', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:53:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c30fb3c2-9d88-5512-98ef-fbb60b6bc33f', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c30fb3c2-9d88-5512-98ef-fbb60b6bc33f'}, {'abstract': 'The leaders of Germany, France, Italy and Spain said they would use all means necessary to protect the common currency, but there is clear disagreement over what measures to take.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/world/europe/european-leaders-vow-to-defend-euro.html', 'snippet': 'The leaders of Germany, France, Italy and Spain said they would use all means necessary to protect the common currency, but there is clear disagreement over what measures to take.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — The leaders of the euro zone’s four largest economies vowed Friday to defend the common currency with all means necessary, trying to reassure jittery financial markets before yet another summit meeting of the European Union next week in Brussels. But clear disagreements remained on what those mechanisms ought to be. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaders Vow to Defend Euro, but Hint at Rifts on How', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'European Leaders’ Vow to Defend Euro Is Undercut by Discord Over Means', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:54:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo and Steven Erlanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erlanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/645df825-a837-58fd-9b71-07c902376424', 'word_count': 1105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/645df825-a837-58fd-9b71-07c902376424'}, {'abstract': 'A Marine relates his own struggle as he tries to heal battlefield wounds.', 'web_url': 'https://atwar.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/living-with-p-t-s-d-and-allowing-myself-to-get-help/', 'snippet': 'A Marine relates his own struggle as he tries to heal battlefield wounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An alarm clock chimes across a pitch-black room. I slowly rise. Standing in my bathroom, I brush my teeth and shave away yesterday’s stubble – part of every Marine’s mandatory morning routine. The person in the mirror seems somehow unfamiliar. Downstairs, the morning pot of coffee brews. I finally begin to wake. Leaving home, the roads are lined with beautiful farmland, backlit by a rising sun. Morning dew glinting off the fields gives way to a kaleidoscope of neon signs as I reach town. Pulling into the parking lot, I take a deep breath and step out of my truck.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Living With P.T.S.D. and Allowing Myself to Get Help', 'kicker': 'At War', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:55:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas James Brennan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'James', 'lastname': 'Brennan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/12c5ab40-566f-5fbf-b47a-8ff9196621bc', 'word_count': 2121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12c5ab40-566f-5fbf-b47a-8ff9196621bc'}, {'abstract': 'Bain Capital agreed on Friday to buy 50 percent of one of Japan’s biggest television shopping companies, in the latest move by the private equity firm in that country.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/bain-capital-buys-half-of-japanese-tv-shopping-company/', 'snippet': 'Bain Capital agreed on Friday to buy 50 percent of one of Japan’s biggest television shopping companies, in the latest move by the private equity firm in that country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bain Capital agreed on Friday to buy 50 percent of one of Japan’s biggest television shopping companies, in the latest move by the private equity firm in that country.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bain Capital Buys Half of TV Shopping Company in Japan', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Retailing: Bain Capital Buys a Stake In a Japanese TV Retailer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sumitomo Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T17:59:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92a8a1b5-bab9-5ed3-8fb6-d3399fa9117f', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92a8a1b5-bab9-5ed3-8fb6-d3399fa9117f'}, {'abstract': 'A Hamptons-style pop-up shop opens in the West Village.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/shelf-life-summer-at-karma/', 'snippet': 'A Hamptons-style pop-up shop opens in the West Village.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From its seashell-encrusted vessels and faux aged terra cotta flower pots to the hand-painted driftwood key chains and dip dyed towels, Summer is exactly the kind of home décor shop that you might expect to find on main street Sag Harbor or Amagansett. Only this three-week retail operation is in the West Village, in the storefront of Karma, Brendan Dugan’s design office/gallery/bookstore, and its proprietors, Aaron Aujla and Dylan Bailey, are not out-of-work Domino editors but the gainfully employed assistants to the artists Nate Lowman and Dan Colen, respectively. Aujla and Bailey, whose personal studio practices trade in mimicry and appropriation, spent untold hours studying and documenting virtually every home décor shop within about 100 miles, meticulously cataloging the tropes and tricks of visual branding and retail display — “Have you ever noticed that the dog bowl outside of the Thom Browne store up the street has a lemon wedge in it?” Aujla asks — and then set out to set up a shop of their own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shelf Life | Summer at Karma', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T18:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alix Browne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/645676a7-79cc-5747-bc43-096d3db56509', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/645676a7-79cc-5747-bc43-096d3db56509'}, {'abstract': 'After writing a short piece about the Microsoft Surface, and noting that the Apple iPad’s screen is difficult for long-form typing, I was on the receiving end of the ire of some Apple zealots.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/when-apple-fanboys-attack/', 'snippet': 'After writing a short piece about the Microsoft Surface, and noting that the Apple iPad’s screen is difficult for long-form typing, I was on the receiving end of the ire of some Apple zealots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So far this year I’ve only been called an “idiot” on two occasions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Zealots Attack', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPad', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'iPhone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Incorporated', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Microsoft Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T18:10:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4f7eef70-308e-5c52-b82f-1ab3085bf021', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4f7eef70-308e-5c52-b82f-1ab3085bf021'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Daragjati, who had bragged about falsely arresting a man last year, received a nine-month sentence for violating the man’s civil rights, and a four-year term for a separate extortion case..', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/ex-police-officer-sentenced-to-prison-for-false-arrest/', 'snippet': 'Michael Daragjati, who had bragged about falsely arresting a man last year, received a nine-month sentence for violating the man’s civil rights, and a four-year term for a separate extortion case..', 'lead_paragraph': 'A former New York police officer who used a racial slur while bragging about falsely arresting a black man last year was sentenced on Friday to nine months in prison for violating the man’s civil rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Officer Gets 9-Month Term in Racially Tainted False Arrest', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Officer Gets 9-Month Sentence Over Racially Tainted Fals