litics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7121646-0aa4-5340-b801-238876c1de2f', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7121646-0aa4-5340-b801-238876c1de2f'}, {'abstract': 'In what amounted to the general election campaign’s first immigration debate, President Obama told a Latino audience that had heard from Mitt Romney that they should not trust Mr. Romney’s shifting rhetoric.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/obama-assails-republicans-over-immigration-policy/', 'snippet': 'In what amounted to the general election campaign’s first immigration debate, President Obama told a Latino audience that had heard from Mitt Romney that they should not trust Mr. Romney’s shifting rhetoric.', 'lead_paragraph': '9:14 p.m. | Updated  A revised version of this post is available here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Florida, Obama Assails Republicans Over Immigration Policy', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T19:33:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a8f93b9-6251-552d-93c5-ff8109035208', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a8f93b9-6251-552d-93c5-ff8109035208'}, {'abstract': 'Reality and our perception of it are incommensurate to a far greater degree than is commonly believed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/opinion/sunday/your-brain-on-a-magic-trick.html', 'snippet': 'Reality and our perception of it are incommensurate to a far greater degree than is commonly believed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PINCH a coin at its edge between the thumb and first fingers of your right hand and begin to place it in your left palm, without letting go. Begin to close the fingers of the left hand. The instant the coin is out of sight, extend the last three digits of your right hand and secretly retract the coin. Make a fist with your left — as if holding the coin — as your right hand palms the coin and drops to the side. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/opinion/24graymatter_img/24graymatter_img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/opinion/24graymatter_img/24graymatter_img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/opinion/24graymatter_img/24graymatter_img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/opinion/24graymatter_img/24graymatter_img-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/opinion/24graymatter_img/24graymatter_img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/opinion/24graymatter_img/24graymatter_img-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidt