source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democrats Mock Scott Brown’s Claim of Secret Meetings with Royalty', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Scott P', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T22:25:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3493bc54-51ee-5510-8706-13a2d2966945', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3493bc54-51ee-5510-8706-13a2d2966945'}, {'abstract': 'The XKR-S is spectacular to behold, and with 550 supercharged V-8 horsepower and a top speed of 186 miles per hour, it can be considered the explosive cap to the long-running XK lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/reviewing-the-jaguar-xkr-s/', 'snippet': 'The XKR-S is spectacular to behold, and with 550 supercharged V-8 horsepower and a top speed of 186 miles per hour, it can be considered the explosive cap to the long-running XK lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Sunday’s Automobiles section, Lawrence Ulrich reviews the 2012 Jaguar XKR-S, a limited-edition, range-topping coupe and convertible from an automaker that currently forgoes the entry-level luxury buyer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviewing the Jaguar XKR-S', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jaguar Land Rover', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T22:27:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cd60514-4715-570b-a065-18183b1a316c', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cd60514-4715-570b-a065-18183b1a316c'}, {'abstract': 'As Egyptians wait for the official results of last weekend’s presidential election, rumors and conspiracy theories are spreading through the country’s news sources.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/on-egyptian-news-sites-shocking-breaking-news-that-might-not-be-true/', 'snippet': 'As Egyptians wait for the official results of last weekend’s presidential election, rumors and conspiracy theories are spreading through the country’s news sources.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Saturday 6:56 a.m. CAIRO — As my colleague David Kirkpatrick reports, tensions escalated in Egypt on Friday as the country’s presidential election commission continued to delay the publication of official results, five days after the polls closed and the votes were counted in public. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Egyptian News Sites, ‘Shocking, Breaking News’ That Might Not Be True', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shafik, Ahmed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T22:34:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42f414e7-d815-5b20-ba02-06162025352a', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42f414e7-d815-5b20-ba02-06162025352a'}, {'abstract': 'The blues-rock duo of Patrick Carney and Dan Auerbach claim that the two companies used elements of their hits songs without permission.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/the-black-keys-sue-home-depot-and-pizza-hut/', 'snippet': 'The blues-rock duo of Patrick Carney and Dan Auerbach claim that the two companies used elements of their hits songs without permission.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Black Keys have sued both the Home Depot and Pizza Hut for copyright infringement, saying that the companies used musical elements from the band’s recent hits without permission in commercials, The Associated Press reported.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Black Keys Sue Home Depot and Pizza Hut', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headli