k area.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/devils-to-host-next-years-draft/', 'snippet': 'For the first time, the N.H.L. will bring its annual draft to the New York area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PITTSBURGH — The Devils will host to the 2013 entry draft, the N.H.L. announced Friday. It will be the first time the league has held the draft in the New York area.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Devils to Host Next Year’s Draft', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prudential Center (Newark)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Jersey Devils', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Flyers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T22:41:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89827c6c-69fa-5900-9513-0c62fc093cdf', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89827c6c-69fa-5900-9513-0c62fc093cdf'}, {'abstract': 'With exquisite timing, a heat wave arrived on the first day of summer, and stylish New Yorkers didn’t miss a beat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/fashion/100000001622785/bill-cunningham-sizzle.html', 'snippet': 'With exquisite timing, a heat wave arrived on the first day of summer, and stylish New Yorkers didn’t miss a beat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With exquisite timing, a heat wave arrived on the first day of summer, and stylish New Yorkers didn’t miss a beat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/fashion/video-0624billcunningham/video-0624billcunningham-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/22/fashion/video-0624billcunningham/video-0624billcunningham-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/22/fashion/video-0624billcunningham/video-0624billcunningham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/22/fashion/video-0624billcunningham/video-0624billcunningham-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Sizzle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T22:44:11+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/0443085b-f61d-58c8-82f0-f63672f0cfce', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/0443085b-f61d-58c8-82f0-f63672f0cfce'}, {'abstract': 'LeRoy Neiman tackled subjects that the serious art world chose to ignore, but not with a depth that would have made them matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/arts/design/leroy-neiman-and-the-serious-art-world.html', 'snippet': 'LeRoy Neiman tackled subjects that the serious art world chose to ignore, but not with a depth that would have made them matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was in graduate school in the mid-’70s, trying to learn how to paint, a useful, shorthand criticism for a certain kind of creation was, “It looks like a LeRoy Neiman.” A reasonably sophisticated art student knew what that meant, and it was not a compliment. It referred to the splashy, garish, instantly recognizable style of illustration, a formulaic mix of impressionism, expressionism and realism, that Mr. Neiman used to make himself one of the most famous artists in America. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/arts/NEIMAN/NEIMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 667, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/arts/NEIMAN/NEIMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1335, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/arts/NEIMAN/NEIMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/23/arts/NEIMAN/NEIMAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/arts/NEIMAN/NEIMAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Achieving Fame Without a Legacy', 'kicker': 'An Appraisal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fame Without a Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neiman, LeRoy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T22:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae40a95f-38f4-5af4-a116-63984e55bab4', 'word_count': 910, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae40a95f-38f4-5af4-a116-63984e55bab4'}, {'abstract': 'Judge Kelleher helped change tennis by leading efforts to admit professionals into major tournaments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/sports/tennis/robert-j-kelleher-judge-and-tennis-official-dies-at-99.html', 'snippet': 'Judge Kelleher helped change tennis by leading efforts to admit professionals into major tournaments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robert J. Kelleher, a federal judge and former tennis champion who helped transform tennis in the United States by spearheading an effort to admit professionals into major tournaments, died Wednesday at his home in Los Angeles. He was 99. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/sports/tennis/23kelleher-tennis/23kelleher-tennis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/sports/tennis/23kelleher-tennis/23kelleher-tennis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1654, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'