 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevrolet Division of General Motors Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Highway Traffic Safety Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T23:12:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Schultz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schultz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1afdf93-1aaf-596e-a367-34090c7fe67c', 'word_count': 434, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1afdf93-1aaf-596e-a367-34090c7fe67c'}, {'abstract': 'Working with seasonal and mostly local ingredients, with an emphasis on vegetables and fish, the chef at Thirty Acres serves up unconventional dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/nyregion/a-review-of-thirty-acres-in-jersey-city.html', 'snippet': 'Working with seasonal and mostly local ingredients, with an emphasis on vegetables and fish, the chef at Thirty Acres serves up unconventional dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST when I thought I had experienced almost everything the restaurant scene had to offer, I walked into a renovated pizzeria in Jersey City and ordered a spicy barbecued squid salad. The pickled pearl onions, jalapeño peppers and fresh, bright cilantro seemed to pop in my mouth, to set off intensifying waves of flavor. Here was a kind of cuisine I had never tasted in New Jersey.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINENJ2/24DINENJ2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Innovations, Both Raw and Cooked', 'kicker': 'New Jersey Dining | Jersey City', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Innovations, Both Raw and Cooked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Thirty Acres (Jersey City, NJ, Restaurant)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pemoulie, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T23:15:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fran Schumer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fran', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schumer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a43e7ec0-302b-5934-b569-68f208a6d036', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a43e7ec0-302b-5934-b569-68f208a6d036'}, {'abstract': 'At Ssambap Korean B.B.Q. in Stony Brook, diners can cook thin slices of raw meat on gas grills at their tables, or have them barbecued in the kitchen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/nyregion/a-review-of-ssambap-korean-bbq-in-stony-brook.html', 'snippet': 'At Ssambap Korean B.B.Q. in Stony Brook, diners can cook thin slices of raw meat on gas grills at their tables, or have them barbecued in the kitchen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOREAN barbecue is a refreshing change of pace from the big slabs of smoked or slow-cooked meat featured in American styles. At Ssambap Korean B.B.Q. in Stony Brook, for instance, diners cook thin slices of raw meat on gas grills at their tables, then take the cooked morsels of meat and enfold them in a romaine leaf, possibly adding some bean paste, scallions and sliced radishes from among the condiments on the table. The resulting lettuce-wrapped package is a ssam; add rice to the mix and you have a ssambap.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINELI3/24DINELI-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINELI3/24DINELI-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1182, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINELI3/24DINELI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINELI3/24DINELI3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'