ure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b94fc03-44ee-5cc0-a03e-578dcfdf0253', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b94fc03-44ee-5cc0-a03e-578dcfdf0253'}, {'abstract': 'Cedar Street Grill, in Dobbs Ferry, is the kind of place every town should have, but few do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/nyregion/a-review-of-cedar-street-grill-in-dobbs-ferry.html', 'snippet': 'Cedar Street Grill, in Dobbs Ferry, is the kind of place every town should have, but few do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It wasn’t clear, at first, what the relationships were. Three handsome guys in their 20s were sitting at one of Cedar Street Grill’s prime window tables, talking and trading hats and goofing around. Friends? Roommates? But as the meal proceeded, it was revealed by the diners’ body language: The middle-age man and woman sitting with them were their parents, and the three were brothers, probably just back from college.', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINEWE2/24DINEWE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINEWE2/24DINEWE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24DINEWE2/24DINEWE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'sub