d_paragraph': 'Walking home in Astoria, Queens, one night this month, Daniel Rutkowski, 52, noticed a darkened stretch of sidewalk and looked up to see that the streetlight was out. He pulled out his cellphone and dialed, and said to the person on the other end, by way of introduction, “Here is my number,” rattling off a confidential identification code. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/nyregion/CRIMESCENE1/CRIMESCENE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Far From a Shooting in Florida, an Increase in Block Watchers', 'kicker': 'Crime Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Far From a Shooting in Florida, An Increase in Block Watchers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volunteers and Community Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-22T23:47:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c12a597e-1a41-5a51-b149-eeb791bbb02f', 'word_count': 798, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c12a597e-1a41-5a51-b149-eeb791bbb02f'}, {'abstract': 'The Westport Country Playhouse puts on a moving production of the play “The Year of Magical Thinking,” which Joan Didion adapted from her memoir of dealing with the death of her husband.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/nyregion/a-review-of-the-year-of-magical-thinking-at-the-westport-country-playhouse.html', 'snippet': 'The Westport Country Playhouse puts on a moving production of the play “The Year of Magical Thinking,” which Joan Didion adapted from her memoir of dealing with the death of her husband.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I first read Joan Didion’s book “The Year of Magical Thinking,” in 2005, the observation I remembered best was about shoes. Ms. Didion, newly widowed, reasoned that she could not give away her husband’s shoes because he would need them when he came back. After seeing the Westport Country Playhouse’s moving, elegiac production of the play that Ms. Didion adapted from that book, the line that echoes in my head is “You’re safe. I’m here.” ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSCT1_SPAN/24ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSCT1_SPAN/24ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSCT1_SPAN/24ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name'