k': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T00:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a0e34c2-6aed-5dd2-a1c7-782604c22d38', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a0e34c2-6aed-5dd2-a1c7-782604c22d38'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Hairston has been a pleasant surprise for the Mets and their manager, Terry Collins, and the journeyman outfielder now expects to play against left-handers.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/hairston-embraces-his-bigger-if-still-limited-role/', 'snippet': 'Scott Hairston has been a pleasant surprise for the Mets and their manager, Terry Collins, and the journeyman outfielder now expects to play against left-handers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ronny Cedeno, in his first game since May 26 after going on the diabled list with a strained left calf, was starting and batting second Friday night aganst the Yankees. Kirk Nieuwenhuis, the starting center fielder and usual leadoff man, was on the bench, as was the regular starting catcher, Josh Thole, and second baseman Daniel Murphy, who badly needed at-bats to shake a 2-for-21 slump. Manager Terry Collins felt he had no choice. A left-handed pitcher was on the mound.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hairston Embraces His Bigger, If Still Limited, Role', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Left-Handedness', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'nam