ttps://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/us/mississippis-only-abortion-clinic-is-at-risk-as-new-law-nears.html', 'snippet': 'The physicians who do the majority of the work at the Jackson Women’s Health Organization do not currently meet a new requirement that goes into effect on July 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JACKSON, Miss. — It was only recently that Dr. Willie Parker began flying down here from Washington, heading to work at a vaultlike building that sits unassumingly on a busy thoroughfare. On his way in, he may pass Prof. Matt Friedeman, standing on the sidewalk with a Bible and a handful of pamphlets, having made the four-minute drive from his home as he has done once a week for years.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/JP-ABORTION/JP-ABORTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/23/us/JP-ABORTION/JP-ABORTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/JP-ABORTION/JP-ABORTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/JP-ABORTION/JP-ABORTION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1327, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mississippi’s Only Abortion Clinic at Risk as Law Nears', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mississippi’s Only Abortion Clinic Is at Risk as New Law Draws Near', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Jackson Women's Health Organization", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T01:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/380c34f8-8447-5c4c-9d0c-7e76325850f8', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/380c34f8-8447-5c4c-9d0c-7e76325850f8'}, {'abstract': 'The fast-food restaurant chain made big news this week in going public. Here is why private equity firms keep feasting on burgers and fries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/opinion/nocera-burger-king-the-cash-cow.html', 'snippet': 'The fast-food restaurant chain made big news this week in going public. Here is why private equity firms keep feasting on burgers and fries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this week, a well-known company went public in a complicated transaction that involved a handful of Wall Street sharpies and a mysterious investment vehicle called a SPAC. The company was Burger King. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,