 was a Broadway hit in the 1960s, is being staged at the John Drew Theater in East Hampton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Soon after “Luv” became a huge hit on Broadway in 1964, Murray Schisgal, its author, was asked in an interview to explain the title. The “emotion of love has been perverted and misused to such an extent that it can only be defined by using another word,” he answered in part. “L-u-v is the perversion of l-o-v-e.”', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/nyregion/24ARTSLI1_SPAN/24ARTSLI1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Skewed Take on Love in the ’60s', 'kicker': 'Arts | Long Island', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Skewed Take on Love in the ’60s', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Hampton (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'John Drew Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanton, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schisgal, Murray', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Price, Lonny', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T01:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aileen Jacobson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aileen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1aec971-e992-5647-a22f-386af7e2ba91', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1aec971-e992-5647-a22f-386af7e2ba91'}, {'abstract': 'Aerial surveillance shed some new light on a mission that showed intensifying American involvement in counternarcotics operations in Central America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/world/americas/video-adds-to-mystery-of-drug-mission-in-honduras.html', 'snippet': 'Aerial surveillance shed some new light on a mission that showed intensifying American involvement in counternarcotics operations in Central America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Aerial surveillance video of a fatal shootout during a counternarcotics mission in Honduras last month shows a long, dugout-style boat ramming a smaller canoe carrying Honduran and American agents — and a seized cocaine shipment — followed by a brief but furious round of gunfire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/world/drugs/drugs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/world/drugs/drugs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Adds to Honduran Drug Raid Mystery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Video Adds to Honduran Drug Raid Mystery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Customs and Border Protection (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Drug Enforcement Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T01:46:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker and Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a9b002a-a12d-5425-b7fa-98780afd23fb', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a9b002a-a12d-5425-b7fa-98780afd23fb'}, {'abstract': 'The guests on “The New York Times Close Up” this weekend include The Times’s David W. Chen, Michael Powell and Clyde Haberman. Also appearing, Representative Charles B. Rangel and Michael Long.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/the-week-in-pictures-for-june-22/', 'snippet': 'The guests on “The New York Times Close Up” this weekend include The Times’s David W. Chen, Michael Powell and Clyde Haberman. Also appearing, Representative Charles B. Rangel and Michael Long.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is a slide show of photographs from the past week in New York City and the region. Subjects include Nik Wallenda’s tightrope walk across Niagara Falls, the first hot spell of summer and a rock slide in the Palisades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Week in Pictures for June 22', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallenda, Nik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niagara Falls (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Palisades (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T01:49:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19bac4e0-6b10-58f8-b92b-d28f69604fe8', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19bac4e0-6b10-58f8-b92b-d28f69604fe8'}, {'abstract': 'Germany and others edge toward a plan for job-creating projects, and not a moment too soon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/opinion/a-small-stimulus-for-europe.html', 'snippet': 'Germany and others edge toward a plan for job-creating projects, and not a moment too soon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the conclusion of the meeting of leaders from the Group of 20 largest economies early this week, participants said they were united in their efforts to promote growth and jobs. But no one was sure whether Angela Merkel, Germany’s chancellor and a champion of budget austerity, was ready to drop her opposition to more government spending to ease Europe’s debt crisis. Her agreement on Friday to a stimulus package worth up to 130 billion euros is a welcome sign that she might come around after all.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Small Stimulus for Europe', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Small Stimulus for Europe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Twenty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T01:52:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/8955052c-2f0c-5a7c-b1f2-6a3e6cd6a229', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8955052c-2f0c-5a7c-b1f2-6a3e6cd6a229'}, {'abstract': 'A Catholic university’s lawyer says the union that adjunct professors want to organize there presents a conflict between church and state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/education/for-professors-at-duquesne-university-union-fight-transcends-religion.html', 'snippet': 'A Catholic university’s lawyer says the union that adjunct professors want to organize there presents a conflict between church and state.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Union busting is a mortal sin,” the Catholic Scholars for Worker Justice said in a 2010 statement on the indispensable role of unions. And while the church hierarchy has never quite put it that way, workers’ right to unionize is an issue on which church teachings are pretty clear.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/23/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/23/us/BELIEFS/BELIEFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Duquesne Professors, a Union Fight That Transcends Religion', 'kicker': 'Beliefs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_