of Rob Hennigan as the general manager of the Orlando Magic, Emerson now boasts two of the more powerful individuals in the league.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON – Situated in the heart of the city’s theater district, Emerson College boasts a list of notable alumni that includes the longtime Hollywood figures Jay Leno, Norman Lear and Henry Winkler.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Emerson College Makes Splash in N.B.A.', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Presti, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Magic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T03:09:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter May', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'May', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b42b473-57cf-5c4f-9bec-e3dbc6a345b9', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b42b473-57cf-5c4f-9bec-e3dbc6a345b9'}, {'abstract': 'Game 5 of the N.B.A. finals, which the Miami Heat won, 121-106, drew the most viewers of the series. Miami won the series, four games to one.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/22/game-5-draws-highest-average-audience-of-series/', 'snippet': 'Game 5 of the N.B.A. finals, which the Miami Heat won, 121-106, drew the most viewers of the series. Miami won the series, four games to one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miami Heat won the N.B.A. title Thursday night, but even after being blown out in Game 5, the Oklahoma City Thu