ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T15:56:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/946c6ef0-3e07-58c0-959f-2f5dd098a93d', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/946c6ef0-3e07-58c0-959f-2f5dd098a93d'}, {'abstract': 'A whirlpool of solving fun from the puzzle master Will Shortz.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/variety-spiral/', 'snippet': 'A whirlpool of solving fun from the puzzle master Will Shortz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SECOND SUNDAY PUZZLE — You don’t need me for this. Honestly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Spiral', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T16:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3653dad1-d7e4-55c2-98c1-067f54af5510', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3653dad1-d7e4-55c2-98c1-067f54af5510'}, {'abstract': 'Ciudad Juárez became infamous for attacks beginning in the 1990s that left hundreds of women dead, but as international attention moved on, the killings have continued.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/world/americas/wave-of-violence-swallows-more-women-in-juarez-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'Ciudad Juárez became infamous for attacks beginning in the 1990s that left hundreds of women dead, but as international attention moved on, the killings have continued.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CIUDAD JUÁREZ, Mexico — First, there were just a few bones and body parts, found in a valley beyond the sprawl of this wild city. At least four women had been killed and dumped, the authorities said. Then, in the same area, investigators made another discovery early this year: a dozen more dead women and girls. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JUAREZ/JUAREZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wave of Violence Swallows More Women in Juárez', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wave of Violence Swallows More Women in Juárez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ciudad Juarez (Mexico)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T16:05:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Cave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b180bd6f-100b-5eca-93be-c8ab0f1d9ebf', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b180bd6f-100b-5eca-93be-c8ab0f1d9ebf'}, {'abstract': 'The plan to trademark Linsanity formed quickly inside Jeremy Lin’s legal and marketing team and started with filing a claim to the United States Patent and Trademark Office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/sports/basketball/jeremy-lin-has-linsanity-trademarked.html', 'snippet': 'The plan to trademark Linsanity formed quickly inside Jeremy Lin’s legal and marketing team and started with filing a claim to the United States Patent and Trademark Office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By Feb. 13, Jeremy Lin was five games into transforming the Knicks. He was the point guard they craved, the player whose court vision, zippy passing and double-figure scoring brought unexpected joy to Madison Square Garden. Fro