'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e66da45-6084-5a25-b410-67e691794c04', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e66da45-6084-5a25-b410-67e691794c04'}, {'abstract': 'The new government aims to revoke certain taxes, suspend planned layoffs in the bloated public sector and extend by two years the deadline for imposing additional austerity measures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/world/europe/greek-coalition-outlines-plan-to-renegotiate-loan-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The new government aims to revoke certain taxes, suspend planned layoffs in the bloated public sector and extend by two years the deadline for imposing additional austerity measures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATHENS — Two days before Greece’s international creditors return to Athens to begin talks on keeping the nearly bankrupt country solvent, the new coalition government on Saturday highlighted the main points it plans to renegotiate with lenders, aiming to revoke certain taxes, suspend planned layoffs in the bloated public sector and extend by two years the deadline for imposing additional austerity measures. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Coalition Outlines Plan to Renegotiate Loan Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greek Coalition Outlines Plan to Renegotiate Loan Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T17:03:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25630c56-70c5-5126-92e0-a5592305beb6', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25630c56-70c5-5126-92e0-a5592305beb6'}, {'abstract': 'Three top American decathletes set their sights on glory in London, but the defending gold medalist, Bryan Clay, faltered at the Olympic trials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/sports/olympics/us-olympic-trials-a-triple-threat-in-decathlon.html', 'snippet': 'Three top American decathletes set their sights on glory in London, but the defending gold medalist, Bryan Clay, faltered at the Olympic trials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — Twenty years and some 2,000 miles removed from the most memorable duel (and startling stumble) in United States decathlon history, a serendipitous twist of timing appeared to have left the sport on the cusp of another American renaissance. The Olympic trials here were supposed to be the send-off. There was the veteran Bryan Clay, 32, hoping to defend his gold medal from Beijing; there was the defending world champion, Trey Hardee, 28, squarely in his prime; and there was the phenom Ashton Eaton, who at 24 may already be the best of the group. American dominance in London seemed almost assured.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/24decathlon/24decathlon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330,