'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T17:12:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0255e040-6f88-5835-9679-5124a20fecc9', 'word_count': 1663, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0255e040-6f88-5835-9679-5124a20fecc9'}, {'abstract': 'Coverage and live analysis of the Euro 2012 quarterfinal between Spain and France in Donetsk, Ukraine.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/coverage-and-live-analysis-spain-vs-france/', 'snippet': 'Coverage and live analysis of the Euro 2012 quarterfinal between Spain and France in Donetsk, Ukraine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Midfielder Xabi Alonso scored two goals in his 100th appearance for Spain, giving the defending World Cup and European champions a 2-0 victory over France on Saturday in a Euro 2012 quarterfinal in Donetsk, Ukraine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012 Quarterfinals: Spain 2, France 0', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UEFA European Football Championship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T17:18:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Das', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Das', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a57d9ce-9bd3-59dd-ac98-dae969880fc9', 'word_count': 2675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a57d9ce-9bd3-59dd-ac98-dae969880fc9'}, {'abstract': 'While consumers tend to think of Apple’s headquarters as the company’s heart and soul, a majority of its workers in the United States are hourly wage earners selling iPhones and MacBooks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/business/apple-store-workers-loyal-but-short-on-pay.html', 'snippet': 'While consumers tend to think of Apple’s headquarters as the company’s heart and soul, a majority of its workers in the United States are hourly wage earners selling iPhones and MacBooks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, during his best three-month stretch, Jordan Golson sold about $750,000 worth of computers and gadgets at the Apple Store in Salem, N.H. It was a performance that might have called for a bottle of Champagne — if that were a luxury Mr. Golson could have afforded. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/apple/apple-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/apple/apple-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1186, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/apple/apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/business/apple/apple-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/apple/apple-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_n