ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institutional Revolutionary Party (Mexico)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Cartels', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena Nieto, Enrique', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calderon, Felipe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez Obrador, Andres Manuel', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:07:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jo Tuckman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tuckman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee8e5211-168b-573a-8664-492c639ce7ba', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee8e5211-168b-573a-8664-492c639ce7ba'}, {'abstract': 'Aleksei L. Kudrin, the former minister of finance, warned at a news conference that Russia was in danger of falling into a recession.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/world/europe/former-russian-finance-minister-warns-of-recession.html', 'snippet': 'Aleksei L. Kudrin, the former minister of finance, warned at a news conference that Russia was in danger of falling into a recession.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG, Russia — President Vladimir V. Putin was all swagger last week at the annual economic forum here, effectively wagging a finger at Europe over its fiscal problems and keeping the chief executives of some of the world’s most powerful oil companies waiting for hours in a hallway until he finally met with them. In the forum’s keynote address, Mr. Putin boasted of Russia’s relatively low debt burden, balanced budget and “fiscal discipline.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Former Russian Minister Warns of Economic Ebb', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Russian Minister Warns of Economic Ebb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kudrin, Aleksei L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:11:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer and David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ac8fbf3-066b-5e9e-a002-54547195c7e5', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ac8fbf3-066b-5e9e-a002-54547195c7e5'}, {'abstract': 'With its rigid, doctrinaire approach and refusal to work with any politician who ever disagrees with it, the organization is putting its federal funding at risk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/opinion/sunday/planned-parenthoods-self-destructive-behavior.html', 'snippet': 'With its rigid, doctrinaire approach and refusal to work with any politician who ever disagrees with it, the organization is putting its federal funding at risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PLANNED PARENTHOOD has a large target on its back. At no time in the organization’s history has it faced such a concerted Congressional challenge to its agenda. But most worrisome is the organization’s shrinking number of defenders, and Planned Parenthood has only itself to blame. It has adopted a strategy driven by blind partisanship, electing to burn bridges instead of building them. That strategy is damaging, and possibly imperiling, its mission.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Planned Parenthood’s Self-Destructive Behavior', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Planned Parenthood’s Self-Destructive Behavior', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dold, Robert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Collins, Susan M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:16:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/46c825a9-1bcc-55fb-a822-7444d90dd7b2', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46c825a9-1bcc-55fb-a822-7444d90dd7b2'}, {'abstract': 'For enlightening summer reading, students should pick up nonfiction that tells them about the world as it actually is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/opinion/sunday/how-to-choose-summer-reading-for-students.html', 'snippet': 'For enlightening summer reading, students should pick up nonfiction that tells them about the world as it actually is.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BECAUSE I am a middle school reading enrichment teacher, parents and colleagues often ask my advice about summer assignments. My automatic reply echoes a hit song from the ’70s, “any love is good lovin’.” I tell them blithely that any reading is good reading, while I think to myself, we’ll take whatever we can get.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sunday-review/24READING/24READING-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sunday-review/24READING/24READING-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sunday-review/24READING/24READING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/sunday-review/24READING/24READING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sunday-review/24READING/24READING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 1