/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Information for Us, or for the Enemy?', 'kicker': 'Letters to the Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Information for Us, or for the Enemy?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:42:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/827bccb0-ac81-53f3-8da5-545c67efcc24', 'word_count': 961, 'uri': 'nyt://article/827bccb0-ac81-53f3-8da5-545c67efcc24'}, {'abstract': 'With the possible exception of a euro zone meltdown, the housing market remains the largest threat to economic recovery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/opinion/sunday/housing-still-depressed-after-all-these-years.html', 'snippet': 'With the possible exception of a euro zone meltdown, the housing market remains the largest threat to economic recovery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Europe suffering under self-destructive austerity and the United States facing its own prospect of punishing budget cuts, it is easy to forget that the housing bust has been the biggest drag on the economy over the past five years. Even with recent housing market improvements, sales and construction are still at very low levels, while prices are still falling in most areas. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Still Depressed, After All These Years', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Still Depressed, After All These Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeowner Affordability and Stability Plan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menendez, Robert', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/290e8eba-80b7-546c-8f33-87f6ffc17703', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/290e8eba-80b7-546c-8f33-87f6ffc17703'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Adelson is writing the biggest political checks in history to Republicans to advance his personal, ideological and financial agenda, which is at odds with the nation’s needs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/opinion/sunday/what-sheldon-adelson-wants.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Adelson is writing the biggest political checks in history to Republicans to advance his personal, ideological and financial agenda, which is at odds with the nation’s needs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No American is dedicating as much of his money to defeat President Obama as Sheldon Adelson, the casino magnate who also happens to have made more money in the last three years than any other American. He is the perfect illustration of the squalid state of political money, spending sums greater than any political donation in history to advance his personal, ideological and financial agenda, which is wildly at odds with the nation’s needs.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Sheldon Adelson Wants', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Sheldon Adelson Wants', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adelson, Sheldon G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Las Vegas Sands Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crossroads Grassroots Policy Strategies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:48:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ccdadd-64d3-5f1d-b937-489046291045', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ccdadd-64d3-5f1d-b937-489046291045'}, {'abstract': 'Federal taxpayers have spent almost $250 million on a new federal prison for women in Aliceville that should never have been built.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/opinion/sunday/alabamas-white-elephant.html', 'snippet': 'Federal taxpayers have spent almost $250 million on a new federal prison for women in Aliceville that should never have been built.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Federal taxpayers have spent almost $250 million on a new federal prison for women in Aliceville, Ala., that should never have been built. The prison is almost completed and, within a year or so, is scheduled to house around 1,500 secure prisoners as well as 250 minimum-security inmates — or about one of every eight women in federal prison. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama’s White Elephant', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alabama’s White Elephant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Aliceville (Ala)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shelby, Richard C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Prisons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T20:51:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editoria