ename': None, 'lastname': 'Manbo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Muller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d65ff2b-7847-5ef7-83de-f444b9e76932', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d65ff2b-7847-5ef7-83de-f444b9e76932'}, {'abstract': 'In Europe, policy makers focus on ailing banks and high bond yields, while China and the United States display signs of economic slowdowns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/your-money/investors-muddle-through-mire-of-uncertainty.html', 'snippet': 'In Europe, policy makers focus on ailing banks and high bond yields, while China and the United States display signs of economic slowdowns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN Europe, the obsessive concern of policy makers shifted from Greece to Spain, with its ailing banks and brutally high bond yields. In China and in the United States, there were signs of economic slowdowns. And for investors nearly everywhere, it was difficult to muster much confidence.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-STRA/24-STRA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 648, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-STRA/24-STRA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1295, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Investors Muddle Through Mire of Uncertainty', 'kicker': 'Strategies', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investors Muddle Through Mire of Uncertainty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Barclays PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HSBC Holdings PLC', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T21:48:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Sommer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sommer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c41162b3-d226-5eb9-8b1b-5dae951fb710', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c41162b3-d226-5eb9-8b1b-5dae951fb710'}, {'abstract': 'Lenders need to write down the amounts owed by homeowners, but the different stakeholders have been unable to agree on how to do this, though they share common interests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/business/economy/real-estates-collective-action-problem.html', 'snippet': 'Lenders need to write down the amounts owed by homeowners, but the different stakeholders have been unable to agree on how to do this, though they share common interests.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IMAGINE that you are watching an outdoor theater production while sitting on the grass. You have difficulty seeing, so you prop yourself up on your knees. Soon everyone behind you does the same. Eventually, most people are kneeling or standing, yet they are less comfortable than they were before and have no better view. Everyone should sit down, and everyone knows it, but no one does.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-VIEW/24-VIEW-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-VIEW/24-VIEW-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reviving Real Estate Requires Collective Action', 'kicker': 'Economic View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviving Real Estate Requires Collective Action', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geanakoplos, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hockett, Robert C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koniak, Susan P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T21:50:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert J. Shiller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Shiller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66490b79-4099-52cd-95