ars ago, in front of my 300 colleagues at LRN, I ripped up our organizational chart and proclaimed that none of us would report to a boss anymore. From that point on, we would all “report” to our company mission. Literally. No one would experience life at LRN as someone else’s subordinate. In short, we would strive to become a self-governing company.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-PRE/24-PRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-PRE/24-PRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1683, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-PRE/24-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-PRE/24-PRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-PRE/24-PRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letting the Mission Govern a Company', 'kicker': 'Preoccupations', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Letting The Mission Govern A Company', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LRN Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seidman, Dov', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T21:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dov Seidman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dov', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seidman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8fab5b8-39f7-51bd-ab54-1d270fd5c7da', 'word_count': 724, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8fab5b8-39f7-51bd-ab54-1d270fd5c7da'}, {'abstract': 'An important message from Liz Gorski.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/element-surprise/', 'snippet': 'An important message from Liz Gorski.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — Oh my. I’m blushing right now because I did not get this theme at first, and now that I’ve figured it out (with some help from a friend) I’m in awe. All I needed was a smack upside the back of the head, which loosened up the brain bits that still remember my high school chemistry. Element of surprise, indeed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Element of Surprise', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T22:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/509e10e1-c0ac-5724-9bff-fcbe47e6d11b', 'word_count': 358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/509e10e1-c0ac-5724-9bff-fcbe47e6d11b'}, {'abstract': 'The president of the franchise store division of United Parcel Service says one lesson he learned early was to give people a chance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/jobs/stuart-k-mathis-of-ups-talks-about-his-career.html', 'snippet': 'The president of the franchise store division of United Parcel Service says one lesson he learned early was to give people a chance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS born in Hattiesburg, Miss. When I was 5 years old my parents moved to Georgia, to begin new teaching jobs.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-BOSS/24-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-BOSS/24-BOSS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1780, 'width': 1373, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-BOSS/24-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-BOSS/24-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/business/24-BOSS/24-BOSS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lessons of Early Hardship', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lessons of Early Hardship', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathis, Stuart K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dominos Pizza Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Un