: 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/56a44c2f-514f-55ab-8f89-9b0ef1819b05', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56a44c2f-514f-55ab-8f89-9b0ef1819b05'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my Iran columns, and the video that accompanies them.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/reader-comments-on-iran-2/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my Iran columns, and the video that accompanies them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column is my last from my Iran road trip, and it’s accompanied by a terrific video made by a Times video journalist, Adam Ellick, who accompanied me. I am still somewhat surprised and awed that Iran not only gave us visas but also allowed us to travel across the country unescorted. After all, Bahrain — our ally! — doesn’t even give me a visa, because of my human rights reporting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reader Comments on Iran', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-23T23:54:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c714b33a-8f52-5915-bca5-6f53fdcfddc1', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c714b33a-8f52-5915-bca5-6f53fdcfddc1'}, {'abstract': 'Early confidence in the law’s constitutionality, based on Supreme Court precedents, proved to be a miscalculation that put the White House on the defensive as its legal strategy evolved over the last two years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/us/past-denials-of-vulnerability-raise-health-act-what-ifs.html', 'snippet': 'Early confidence in the law’s constitutionality, based on Supreme Court precedents, proved to be a miscalculation that put the White House on the defensive as its legal strategy evolved over the last two years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With the Supreme Court likely to render judgment on President Obama’s health care law this week, the White House and Congress find themselves in a position that many advocates of the legislation once considered almost unimaginable.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/us/CARE-1/CARE-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/us/CARE-1/CARE-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supporters Slow to Grasp Health Law’s Legal Risks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supporters Slow to Grasp Health Law’s Legal Risks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verrilli, Donald B Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katyal, Neal K', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interstate Commerce', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 's