ct': 'Jason Bay said he feels “astronomically better” since experiencing dizziness, headaches and shoulder soreness in the days after crashing into an outfield wall on June 15.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/23/mets-bay-feeling-much-better-after-concussion/', 'snippet': 'Jason Bay said he feels “astronomically better” since experiencing dizziness, headaches and shoulder soreness in the days after crashing into an outfield wall on June 15.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets’ clubhouse was all laughs before Saturday’s game against the Yankees. That was chiefly because of Little Jerry Seinfeld, a chicken that Tim Byrdak let loose inside as a gag a day earlier, which players say has brought good luck and humor to Citi Field. Left out of the shenanigans was Jason Bay, who addressed the serious subject matter of the concussion that\xa0 landed him on the disabled list.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets’ Bay Feeling Much Better', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bay, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T01:35:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hunter Atkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hunter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Atkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4183856-7813-5565-b303-bd96282fe1df', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4183856-7813-5565-b303-bd96282fe1df'}, {'abstract': 'After a bitter 149-day lockout that consumed the summer and fall, the N.B.A. exceeded expectations in every area this season, from revenue to ratings to attendance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/sports/basketball/after-bad-start-nba-season-finishes-on-high-note.html', 'snippet': 'After a bitter 149-day lockout that consumed the summer and fall, the N.B.A. exceeded expectations in every area this season, from revenue to ratings to attendance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the music blared and the confetti spilled Thursday night in Miami, two transcendent figures met at midcourt, shared an embrace and some parting words — a poetic coda to a season that almost wasn’t, an inspiring vision for the future.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 606, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1212, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/sports/BECK/BECK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Bad Start, N.B.A. Season Finishes with Inspiring Vision', 'kicker': 'On Pro Basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Bad Start, N.B.A. Season Finishes with Inspiring Vision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Westbrook, Russell', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Durant, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Heat', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lockouts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T01:35:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Howard Beck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Howard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b45c2300-161d-53c9-96b4-f57a44f8e1e6', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b45c2300-161d-53c9-96b4-f57a44f8e1e6'}, {'abstract': 'The Arizona Wildcats changed stadiums and wound up hosting an N.C.A.A. regional. Now they are in the College World Series finals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/sports/baseball/move-to-new-park-helped-arizona-on-road-to-college-world-series.html', 'snippet': 'The Arizona Wildcats changed stadiums and wound up hosting an N.C.A.A. regional. Now they are in the College World Series finals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — Baseball fans in Tucson revere Hi Corbett Field nearly as much as Bostonians do Fenway Park. The memories transcend generations. The Hall of Famers Bob Feller, Willie Mays and Ted Williams played at Hi Corbett during its 46 years as the spring training home of the Cleveland Indians, and part of the 1989 film “Major League” was filmed there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Move to a New (Old) Park Helped Arizona on Road to College World Series', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Move to a New (Old) Park Helped Arizona on Road to C.W.S.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College World Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Arizona', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T02:21:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ad23779-8825-51e4-8eb5-ecf0bb4a0823', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ad23779-8825-51e4-8eb5-ecf0bb4a0823'}, {'abstract': 'Magnus Carlsen eked out a victory at the Tal Memorial tournament in Moscow after five players were tied for first with two rounds to go.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/crosswords/chess/chess-carlsen-wins-tal-memorial-tournament.html', 'snippet': 'Magnus Carlsen eked out a victory at the Tal Memorial tournament in Moscow after five players were tied for first with two rounds to go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Tal Memorial tournament in Moscow was a nail-biter: five of the 10 players were tied for the lead with two rounds to go.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'World’s No. 1 Needs Help to Prevail in Moscow', 'kicker': 'Chess', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World’s No. 1 Needs Help To Prevail in Moscow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aronian, Levon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carlsen, Magnus', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McShane, Luke', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T02:32:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47567848-9fcc-5511-b0a5-6a1dfb76fd7d', 'word_count': 457, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47567848-9fcc-5511-b0a5-6a1dfb76fd7d'}, {'abstract': 'Two jihadis in Libya represent opposing directions for Islamists, democracy or militancy with Taliban-style rule, and for the moment, democracy appears to have the upper hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/world/africa/libya-jihadis-offer-2-paths-democracy-or-militancy.html', 'snippet': 'Two jihadis in Libya represent opposing directions for Islamists, democracy or militancy with Taliban-style rule, and for the moment, democracy appears to have the upper hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DARNAH, Libya — Abdul-Hakim al-Hasadi first took up arms nearly 20 years ago to try to bring Islamic law to Libya. He studied under the Taliban in Afghanistan, and during last year’s uprising he led a local militia council here in a city famous as a cradle of Islamic jihad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/24/world/JIHADI/JIHADI-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya Democracy Clashes With Fervor for Jihad', 'kicker': 'The New Islamists', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya Democracy Clashes With Fervor for Jihad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belhaj, Abdul Hakim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Qumu, Abu Sufian Ibrahim Ahmed Hamuda bin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T02:50:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By David D. Kirkpatrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59e50355-5182-57e7-9025-f00b6e04a3e2', 'word_count': 1310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59e50355-5182-57e7-9025-f00b6e04a3e2'}, {'abstract': 'The Philadelphia Flyers acquired defenseman Luke Schenn from the Toronto Maple Leafs for forward James van Riemsdyk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/sports/flyers-acquire-defenseman-luke-schenn-from-maple-leafs.html', 'snippet': 'The Philadelphia Flyers acquired defenseman Luke Schenn from the Toronto Maple Leafs for forward James van Riemsdyk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Philadelphia Flyers acquired defenseman Luke Schenn from the Toronto Maple Leafs for forward James van Riemsdyk. Schenn, 22, who has 14 goals and 61 assists in four seasons, should help replace the void created by the loss of Chris Pronger, who is unlikely to return because of postconcussion symptoms. Van Riemsdyk, also 22, has 47 goals and 52 assists for 99 points in three seasons. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_