es and was also awarded an Emmy for directing. Bill Geddie, the executive producer of “The View” on ABC, received a lifetime achievement award. But ABC didn’t come out on top in the morning show category: NBC’s “Today” show bested “Good Morning America” for the fourth year in a row.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daytime Emmy for ‘Regis and Kelly’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daytime Emmy For ‘Regis and Kelly’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Philbin, Regis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soap Operas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Live With Regis and Kelly (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T21:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb9b0f11-a5ce-58f4-896a-51923b07c68e', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb9b0f11-a5ce-58f4-896a-51923b07c68e'}, {'abstract': 'Jennifer Hudson is set to join a fellow “American Idol” runner-up, Katharine McPhee, for a guest stint on NBC’s musical drama “Smash,” the network has announced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/arts/television/jennifer-hudson-to-appear-on-smash.html', 'snippet': 'Jennifer Hudson is set to join a fellow “American Idol” runner-up, Katharine McPhee, for a guest stint on NBC’s musical drama “Smash,” the network has announced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Hudson is set to join a fellow “American Idol” runner-up, Katharine McPhee, for a guest stint on NBC’s musical drama “Smash,” the network has announced. Ms. Hudson, left, who has won an Academy Award, a Golden Globe and a Grammy, will portray a Tony-winning Broadway star for a multi-episode arc, starting with the Season 2 premiere. The second season is expected to begin early next year, though no date has been set. The premiere of “Smash” drew 11.4 million viewers in February, but the show attracted just 6 million for its season finale in May.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jennifer Hudson to Appear on ‘Smash’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jennifer Hudson To Appear on ‘Smash’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hudson, Jennifer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T21:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4183755-a4b8-5f49-b8f3-6cf09df7cfc4', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4183755-a4b8-5f49-b8f3-6cf09df7cfc4'}, {'abstract': 'Milan', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/24/fashion/runway-mens/moncler-spring-2013-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'Milan', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milan', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i