en and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T21:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/307eac5d-ec65-5db6-bb83-7abf50ef17d7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/307eac5d-ec65-5db6-bb83-7abf50ef17d7'}, {'abstract': 'The Mark Morris Dance Group performed sacred and secular works at a New Haven festival.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/arts/dance/mark-morris-dance-groups-gloria-and-jesu-meine-freude.html', 'snippet': 'The Mark Morris Dance Group performed sacred and secular works at a New Haven festival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — Titters spread through the Shubert Theater here on Friday, when the Mark Morris Dance Group performed as part of the International Festival of Arts & Ideas. Mr. Morris has created many comic works, but none of those were on this program. Of the three dances presented, all set to live Baroque or classical music, two were overtly and sincerely religious. The laughter was the uncomfortable kind. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/MORRIS/MORRIS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When Sacred Themes Arrive Wrapped in Unlikely Packages', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Sacred Themes Arrive Wrapped in Unlikely Packages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morris, Mark, Dance Group', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T21:22:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/788af629-e428-5292-bd26-285778272ba4', 'word_count': 637, 'uri': 'nyt://article/788af629-e428-5292-bd26-285778272ba4'}, {'abstract': '“L’Olympiade,” a little-known opera by Vivaldi, is presented by Garsington Opera on an estate in the English countryside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/arts/music/garsington-operas-olympiade-by-vivaldi-in-england.html', 'snippet': '“L’Olympiade,” a little-known opera by Vivaldi, is presented by Garsington Opera on an estate in the English countryside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HIGH WYCOMBE, England — It is hard to imagine a more idyllic outdoor setting for an opera production than Wormsley, the splendid country estate in the Chiltern Hills northwest of London. For the second summer this is the home of Garsington Opera, founded in 1989. Productions are presented in a commodious, airy and well-equipped open-air pavilion seating 600 comfortably, with a large stage, a sizable orchestra pit and see-through soft plastic walls offering views of the bucolic surroundings. It is equally hard to imagine a more appropriate work for Garsington to be presenting right now than Vivaldi’s musically rich and charming opera “L’Olimpiade,” set in ancient Olympia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/25VIVALDI/25VIVALDI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 626, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/25VIVALDI/25VIVALDI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1252, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/25VIVALDI/25VIVALDI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/25VIVALDI/25VIVALDI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/25VIVALDI/25VIVALDI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', '