tasteful, but the real-life medical cases the episodes describe certainly make you feel the frustration and terror of an attack by an unknown enemy. The program, “Diagnosis: Dead or Alive,” which has its premiere Monday night, explores medical mysteries through re-enactments and commentaries from the families and doctors who experienced them. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/diagnosis/diagnosis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/diagnosis/diagnosis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 1876, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/diagnosis/diagnosis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/diagnosis/diagnosis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/arts/diagnosis/diagnosis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Medical Guessing Game, With Life as the Ultimate Prize', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Medical Guessing Game, With Life as the Ultimate Prize', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Discovery Channel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T21:57:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/edd8f6e5-dee9-5064-a624-4ed4ac749260', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edd8f6e5-dee9-5064-a624-4ed4ac749260'}, {'abstract': 'Nancy Kavanaugh rushes us through her puzzle.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/furious/', 'snippet': 'Nancy Kavanaugh rushes us through her puzzle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — True story: When I was pregnant with The Boy, there was a point where the pregnancy hormones and resulting brain fog turned me into the worst driver in the history of driving. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Fast, Too Furious', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T22:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48f4d991-a153-5032-942c-61877d105f45', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48f4d991-a153-5032-942c-61877d105f45'}, {'abstract': 'With one child in college and one graduating, the author finds herself in need of a new label.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/with-grown-kids-what-am-i-besides-mom/', 'snippet': 'With one child in college and one graduating, the author finds herself in need of a new label.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As I was driving down the Long Island Expressway, my friend, an aspiring cinematographer, was filming me from the passenger seat. She asked me to give her one word that best identified me. I fought like crazy to stop myself from saying it. I spewed forth lawyerly equivocation, harking back to my days as a litigator, but out it came: “Mom.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Grown Children, What Am I Besides ‘Mom’?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-24T22:00:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Risa Doherty', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Risa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doherty', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707aec77-11fb-5d0a-b4bf-bd395aef952c', 'word_count': 694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707aec77-11fb-5d0a-b4bf-bd395aef952c'}, {'abstract': 'Alessandro Diamanti scored the decisive penalty kick to give Italy a shootout win over England and a spot in the semifinals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/sports/soccer/euro-2012-italy-secures-spot-in-semifinals-on-penalty-kicks.html', 'snippet': 'Alessandro Diamanti scored the decisive penalty kick to give Italy a shootout win over England and a spot in the semifinals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/25goal2/25goal2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/25goal2/25g