eer best with a 62 and won the Travelers Championship by one stroke.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/sports/golf/at-travelers-leishman-gets-first-pga-tour-win.html', 'snippet': 'Marc Leishman, who was six strokes off the pace at the start of the day, matched a career best with a 62 and won the Travelers Championship by one stroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CROMWELL, Conn. — Ever since the Australian golfer Marc Leishman won the Warrnambool Club championship at age 13, he had dreamed of victory on the PGA Tour. But not even Leishman could have imagined he would shoot an eight-under-par 62 to rally from a six-shot deficit at the start of the final round and then wait more than two hours to earn his first tour title, by one stroke.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 873, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1745, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YGOLF/YGOLF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At Travelers, Leishman Gets First PGA Tour Win', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Rally and Some Help, Getting First Tour Win', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Golf', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, Charley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leishman, Marc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Bubba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T00:35:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Golf', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Schupak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schupak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb1c7784-21a9-5110-b787-0e8b5bc28222', 'word_count': 846, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb1c7784-21a9-5110-b787-0e8b5bc28222'}, {'abstract': 'In Europe and America, those who have the power to contain the crisis refuse to act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/opinion/krugman-the-great-abdication.html', 'snippet': 'In Europe and America, those who have the power to contain the crisis refuse to act.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among economists who know their history, the mere mention of certain years evokes shivers. For example, three years ago Christina Romer, then the head of President Obama’s Council of Economic Advisers, warned politicians not to re-enact 1937 — the year F.D.R. shifted, far too soon, from fiscal stimulus to austerity, plunging the recovering economy back into recession. Unfortunately, this advice was ignored.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xla