wers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:02:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Goldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c245abf0-79f9-52bf-8204-7d54324c77a0', 'word_count': 1206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c245abf0-79f9-52bf-8204-7d54324c77a0'}, {'abstract': 'A fire began in a security X-ray machine causing smoke to billow through a Delta terminal and leading to the brief evacuation of about 600 people.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/small-fire-at-la-guardia-prompts-evacuation/', 'snippet': 'A fire began in a security X-ray machine causing smoke to billow through a Delta terminal and leading to the brief evacuation of about 600 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hundreds of people were briefly evacuated from a Delta terminal at La Guardia Airport on Sunday evening as firefighters responded to a small electrical fire at one of the security stations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Small Fire at La Guardia Prompts Evacuation', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fire Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LaGuardia Airport (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:03:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6c6eb7e-bf38-5a82-984e-9a9f0512ff1c', 'word_count': 165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6c6eb7e-bf38-5a82-984e-9a9f0512ff1c'}, {'abstract': 'Entering Sunday night’s game against the Mets, the Yankees had won 12 of 17 games against National League opponents this season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/sports/baseball/yankees-feast-on-interleague-opponents.html', 'snippet': 'Entering Sunday night’s game against the Mets, the Yankees had won 12 of 17 games against National League opponents this season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When interleague play began in May, the Yankees were only two games over .500 and were in fourth place, four and a half games out of the American League East lead. Since then they have fattened up on the National League, winning 12 of their 17 interleague games going into Sunday’s finale against the Mets, and have used the N.L. to greatly improve their outlook.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YYANKEES/YYANKEES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YYANKEES/YYANKEES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1867, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Yankees Have Feasted on National League Foes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Yankees Have Feasted on the National League', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Girardi, Joe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swisher, Nick', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21d7c0fa-a3a8-5e7f-8ef5-fae46b0d18ec', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21d7c0fa-a3a8-5e7f-8ef5-fae46b0d18ec'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate is rightly demanding a full accounting of the damage from next year’s brutal sequester.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/opinion/lift-the-veil-on-the-spending-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'The Senate is rightly demanding a full accounting of the damage from next year’s brutal sequester.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pentagon’s powerful Republican friends in Congress are griping about a required $500 billion cut to the military budget over nine years beginning in January. It would “hollow our military,” said Speaker John Boehner. It’s a “national disgrace,” said Representative Howard McKeon, chairman of the Armed Services Committee.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lift the Veil on the Spending Cuts', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lift the Veil on the Spending Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:10:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac3bb8cd-81c8-5d5c-bc0b-6823e168a74a', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac3bb8cd-81c8-5d5c-bc0b-6823e168a74a'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery Numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/nyregion/lottery-numbers-for-new-york-new-jersey-and-connecticut.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery Numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut', 'lead_paragraph': 'June 24, 2012', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lottery Numbers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lottery Numbers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:11:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f4f4077-8ca2-5caf-9831-17b57bd7b625', 'word_count': 195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f4f4077-8ca2-5caf-9831-17b57bd7b625'}, {'abstract': 'The Random House audiobooks division, which began at Mr. Schulte’s suggestion in 1985, is now the largest in the market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/business/anthony-m-schulte-publishing-executive-dies-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'The Random House audiobooks division, which began at Mr. Schulte’s suggestion in 1985, is now the largest in the market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anthony M. Schulte, a publishing executive who was an early proponent of audiobooks and among the first to tap the ready-made audience for books written by trusted television personalities like Alistair Cooke, Carl Sagan and Walter Cronkite, died on June 17 in a swimming accident in Maine. He was 82. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/business/schulte-obit/schulte-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/business/schulte-obit/schulte-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/business/schulte-obit/schulte-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/business/schulte-obit/schulte-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/business/schulte-obit/schulte-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anthony Schulte, Publisher and Early Audiobook Proponent, Dies at 82', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Anthony Schulte, 82, Publisher And Early Audiobook Booster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schulte, Anthony M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Random House', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audiobooks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:12:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd86b4bb-7562-5dce-b7f4-fb11e9996936', 'word_count': 784, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd86b4bb-7562-5dce-b7f4-fb11e9996936'}, {'abstract': 'The bill cuts environmental programs too much, gives food stamps a needless hit and does not alter the program’s bias toward big farmers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/opinion/a-mediocre-farm-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The bill cuts environmental programs too much, gives food stamps a needless hit and does not alter the program’s bias toward big farmers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The farm bill approved by the Senate last week makes significant changes in existing farm programs, some for the better. But it takes a disproportionate whack from environmental programs, needlessly trims food stamps and does not fundamentally alter the program’s bias toward relatively well-off growers of big crops like corn, wheat and soybeans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mediocre Farm Bill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mediocre Farm Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crop Controls and Subsidies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Farm Bill (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc7c2819-2a3a-5030-b0d9-d720da07ca98', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc7c2819-2a3a-5030-b0d9-d720da07ca98'}, {'abstract': 'Advocates of a law allowing same-sex marriage think it has a good chance of passing, but history is against them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/us/politics/second-time-around-hope-for-gay-marriage-in-maine.html', 'snippet': 'Advocates of a law allowing same-sex marriage think it has a good chance of passing, but history is against them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AUGUSTA, Me. — Three years after voters in Maine rejected same-sex marriage, they will consider the matter again in November. This time, advocates say they have reason for optimism.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit':