a, is being revised to conform with the rigorous new standards proposed by the National Governors Association, along with state school superintendents. New York State and New York City will have to do more to prepare people for an exam that could help them get a leg up in the job market.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Try Finding a Job Without a G.E.D.', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Try Finding a Job Without a G.E.D.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'General Educational Development Test (GED)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:24:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/77f1c9a1-0dee-5c11-81bd-e590b4c488b5', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77f1c9a1-0dee-5c11-81bd-e590b4c488b5'}, {'abstract': 'In the coming months Fandango will focus more on improving its nonticketing offerings, including better use of content from its corporate sibling, Universal Pictures.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/fandango-adds-msn-to-its-ticket-sales-portals/', 'snippet': 'In the coming months Fandango will focus more on improving its nonticketing offerings, including better use of content from its corporate sibling, Universal Pictures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — It’s starting to look as if the movie ticketing war in the United States has been won, with MSN’s switch to Fandango as the latest evidenc