rural areas, likely to close.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Congress approved a $445 million advance appropriation for the Corporation for Public Broadcasting in December, the corporation, which administers funds given to public broadcasters, was directed to investigate an important question: Could public television and radio survive without federal funds?', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Federal Funds Called Vital for Many Public Stations', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Federal Funds Called Vital For Many Public Stations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corp for Public Broadcasting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/061b4911-2578-54b2-8c92-a7413d66d912', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/061b4911-2578-54b2-8c92-a7413d66d912'}, {'abstract': 'Many governmental entities across the nation are looking at new money-raising strategies to keep from cutting services.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/us/cities-consider-selling-ads-as-economic-lifelines.html', 'snippet': 'Many governmental entities across the nation are looking at new money-raising strategies to keep from cutting se