nyt://article/47a59ebf-c865-58fa-bcc8-b4b7c3c6485b'}, {'abstract': 'Sanya Richards-Ross, recovering from health problems in recent years, ran the fastest time in the event this year and earned a spot on the Olympic team.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/24/healthy-and-happy-richards-ross-ties-trials-record-in-400/', 'snippet': 'Sanya Richards-Ross, recovering from health problems in recent years, ran the fastest time in the event this year and earned a spot on the Olympic team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — Sanya Richards-Ross is back with a vengeance. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Healthy and Happy, Richards-Ross Ties Trials Record in 400', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richards, Sanya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:58:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0c8b097-1b52-54c1-b7a8-608629b0d801', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0c8b097-1b52-54c1-b7a8-608629b0d801'}, {'abstract': 'The Yankees haven’t had much experience against R. A. Dickey and his knuckleball, but they said they would not change their routines heading into Sunday night’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/sports/baseball/facing-knuckleball-of-mets-dickey-yankees-have-no-fear.html', 'snippet': 'The Yankees haven’t had much experience against R. A. Dickey and his knuckleball, but they said they would not change their routines heading into Sunday night’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing Nick Swisher saw Sunday morning when he woke up and turned on the television, he said, was Mets starter R. A. Dickey giving an interview about the pitch that has transformed him into a sensation.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YKNUCKLER/YKNUCKLER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YKNUCKLER/YKNUCKLER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YKNUCKLER/YKNUCKLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YKNUCKLER/YKNUCKLER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/sports/YKNUCKLER/YKNUCKLER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knuckleball Is Unfamiliar, but Yankees Keep Routine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knuckleball Is Unfamiliar, But Yankees Keep Routine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dickey, R A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wakefield, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T01:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d202fda2-4e20-5b22-af8d-0dd9bd462662', 'word_count': 730, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d202fda2-4e20-5b22-af8d-0dd9bd462662'}, {'abstract': 'The Folger Shakespeare Library editions will be available in e-book format for the first time beginning Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/books/folger-shakespeares-in-e-book-format.html', 'snippet': 'The Folger Shakespeare Library editions will be available in e-book format for the first time beginning Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Folger Shakespeare Library editions will be available in e-book format for the first time beginning Monday. Known as one of the most popular and accessible editions of Shakespeare’s works, they feature scene summaries and notes and are frequently used in schools. Simon & Schuster said it collaborated with the Folger Shakespeare Library to create the e-books. The e-books, including “Hamlet,” “Julius Caesar” and “The Merchant of Venice,” will be sold for $5.99 each. “Shakespeare’s plays are one of the true landmarks in English writing, and the Folger editions have always served to make accessible, authoritative editions of the plays available to a broad sweep of the reading and playgoing public,” Michael Witmore, the director of the Folger Shakespeare Library, said in a statement. “The arrival of Folger Editions as e-books extends the reach of this invaluable series even further.”', 'print_section':