 in the case revealed an exceptionally garrulous and jocular bench.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court’s momentous decision on the fate of President Obama’s health care law is expected Thursday, and it is likely to be dry, sober, weighty and self-conscious about its place in constitutional history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/sub-26bar/sub-26bar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/sub-26bar/sub-26bar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look Back at Court’s Arguments on Health Care, Laugh Count Included', 'kicker': 'Sidebar', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reviewing the Health Care Arguments, Laugh Count Included', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Texas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T13:12:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d0e6175-486c-5a3a-a897-001176ff702d', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d0e6175-486c-5a3a-a897-001176ff702d'}, {'abstract': 'Abu Jindal, one of the many pseudonyms of the man suspected to be a key planner of the Mumbai terror attacks has been arrested, Indian home minister said.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/police-arrests-key-suspect-in-the-mumbai-terror-attack/', 'snippet': 'Abu Jindal, one of the many pseudonyms of the man suspected to be a key planner of the Mumbai terror attacks has been arrested, Indian home minister said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The police in New Delhi have arrested a man suspected of being one of the planners of the 2008 militant attacks in Mumbai that killed more than 160 people, the government said Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Arrest Key Suspect in the Mumbai Terror Attack', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Taiba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T13:21:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1efbc17c-cb71-5ff8-84d2-848d7feb135d', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1efbc17c-cb71-5ff8-84d2-848d7feb135d'}, {'abstract': 'Also, the Vatican hires a Fox News correspondent as a senior communications adviser, and a Web site that focuses on the Unites States Supreme Court gears up for a big week.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/the-breakfast-meeting-ads-ads-everywhere-and-what-ratings-are-best/', 'snippet': 'Also, the Vatican hires a Fox News correspondent as a senior communications adviser, and a Web site that focuses on the Unites States Supreme Court gears up for a big week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Local governments, transit systems and school districts have been offering up advertising and sponsorship deals that encroach on basic services and equipment, including ads on school buses, sponsorship of subway stations, or (temporary) ads on fire hydrants and manhole covers, Michael Cooper writes. The deals — like one being considered in Baltimore to allow advertisements on fire trucks — seemingly serve a need for each side. Cash-strapped cities averse to raising taxes can help pay the bills with the revenue from sponsorship deals. (By renaming its Bus Rapid Transit system the HealthLine, Cleveland received $6.25 million over 25 years.) And, Mr. Cooper writes, advertisers can “try to reach consumers who have grown more adept at tuning out commercials, whether with remote controls or digital video recorders.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Ads, Ads Everywhere, and What Ratings Are Best?', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T13:22:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b9adc88-712b-568a-a056-1bb9a29e86c8', 'word_count': 492, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b9adc88-712b-568a-a056-1bb9a29e86c8'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: Is there a point at which an uncommonly long prison sentence strays past justice and stumbles into the realm of vengeance against a loathed defendant?', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/taking-a-second-look-at-an-ex-officers-75-year-sentence/', 'snippet': 'The Day: Is there a point at which an uncommonly long prison sentence strays past justice and stumbles into the realm of vengeance against a loathed defendant?', 'lead_paragraph': 'If a contest were held for the most despised man in New York, Michael Pena would be a strong contender. “Despicable” doesn’t begin to describe what he did.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Taking a Second Look at an Ex-Officer’s 75-Year Sentence', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pena, Michael V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T13:22:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e3601a3-325c-518e-8613-c2c345e29a07', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e3601a3-325c-518e-8613-c2c345e29a07'}, {'abstract': 'The next tour will be the last for the electronic dance music trio, but a live album is said to be in the works.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/swedish-house-mafias-pulsating-tour-to-come-to-an-end/', 'snippet': 'The next tour will be the last for the electronic dance music trio, but a live album is said to be in the works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The glowsticks are dimming and the beat will be slowing for Swedish House Mafia. The trio, whose thumping house tracks quickly entranced millions of neon-clad, pulsing fans of electronic dance music, announced on Saturday that it will stop touring.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Swedish House Mafia’s Pulsating Tour to Come to an End', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Swedish House Mafia To Stop Touring', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Axwell', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swedish House Mafia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T13:34:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11cf5dbb-b4c8-5890-8768-11117eb4732b', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11cf5dbb-b4c8-5890-8768-11117eb4732b'}, {'abstract': 'Milan', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/25/fashion/runway-mens/gucci-spring-2013-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'Milan', 'lead_paragraph': 'Milan', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/fashion/runway/gucci_mws13app-slide-XLQ4/gucci_mws13app-slide-XLQ4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/25/fashion/runway/gucci_mws13app-slide-XLQ4/gucci_mws13app-slide-XLQ4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'capti