ins of their staff, and says virtual work environments might be designed to make us even more trusting and productive.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/will-oxytocin-keep-the-virtual-office-humming/', 'snippet': 'Paul Zak is a neuroeconomist, studying how a chemical called oxytocin elicits trust, empathy and better workplace cooperation. He has identified ways managers can produce this chemical in the brains of their staff, and says virtual work environmen...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even as technology blows companies apart, can the people in them work better together?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/blogs/oxytocin/oxytocin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 328, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/25/blogs/oxytocin/oxytocin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 328, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Will Oxytocin Keep the Virtual Office Humming?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cloud Computing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oxytocin (Hormone)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T14:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Quentin Hardy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a346e9a-c7b8-5ad2-8db7-6f1b9b3da18c', 'word_count': 576, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a346e9a-c7b8-5ad2-8db7-6f1b9b3da18c'}, {'abstract': 'The host of “Jeopardy!” is expected to be back at work when production for the show’s 29th season begins next month.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/alex-trebek-suffers-mild-heart-attack/', 'snippet': 'The host of “Jeopardy!” is expected to be back at work when production for the show’s 29th season begins next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Alex Trebek, the “Jeopardy!” host and burglar-foiler, had a mild heart attack on Saturday. He was admitted to Cedars-Sinai Medical Center in Los Angeles, according to Paula Askanas, a spokeswoman for Sony Television, which distributes the game show. “Trebek is in good spirits and is currently under observation and undergoing further testing,” Sony said in a statement on Sunday. “He is expected to fully recover and be back at Jeopardy! when production begins taping in July for the new season, the show’s 29th.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alex Trebek Suffers Mild Heart Attack', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Alex Trebek Has Heart Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trebek, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T14:17:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a86517f-21d7-5356-988e-f5521b440109', 'word_count': 115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a86517f-21d7-5356-9