thought they were and filming when they thought they weren’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During a drive back from a shoot last week for the PBS series I’m hosting, “NOVA ScienceNow,” I was telling the story of one cameraman I worked with, earlier in my career, who found himself in that classic nightmare: He discovered that he hadn’t been filming when he thought he was, and was filming when he thought he wasn’t. He’d somehow gotten out of cycle with his Record button. (The new season of the show will have six episodes, one hour each; they begin in October.) ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even Video Pros Make Mistakes', 'kicker': 'Pogue&#039;s Posts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Camcorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T14:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Pogue', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogue', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8246cce2-0eeb-53cc-940c-b273338ee5e6', 'word_count': 466, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8246cce2-0eeb-53cc-940c-b273338ee5e6'}, {'abstract': 'N.Y. See: It was a dark and stormy morning.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/west-72nd-street-looking-east-723-a-m/', 'snippet': 'N.Y. See: It was a dark and stormy morning.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'West 72nd Street, Looking East, 7:23 A.M.', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T14:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Th