tors who got back all the cash they had invested with Bernard L. Madoff before his December 2008 arrest.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/top-court-declines-to-review-madoff-payout-plan/', 'snippet': 'Without comment, the Supreme Court declined to hear an appeal from lawyers for investors who got back all the cash they had invested with Bernard L. Madoff before his December 2008 arrest.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:25 p.m. | Updated The Supreme Court said on Monday that it would not hear a dispute over how the claims of investors in Bernard L. Madoff’s huge Ponzi scheme should be calculated, a decision that could speed up payouts to the victims of the fraud.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Declines to Hear Madoff Dispute', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Declines To Hear Madoff Dispute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ponzi and Pyramid Schemes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madoff, Bernard L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picard, Irving H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities Investor Protection Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:02:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Lattman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lattman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6cdd3aa-3c35-5188-9a0e-73312ca243ae', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6cdd3aa-3c35-5188-9a0e-73312ca243ae'}, {'abstract': 'The police in New Delhi have arrested a man suspected of instructing attackers as they carried out a siege that left more than 160 people dead.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/world/asia/suspected-planner-of-mumbai-attack-arrested-in-india.html', 'snippet': 'The police in New Delhi have arrested a man suspected of instructing attackers as they carried out a siege that left more than 160 people dead.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The police in New Delhi have arrested a man suspected of being one of the planners of the 2008 attacks in Mumbai that killed more than 160 people, the government said Monday. The police did not provide the suspect’s name, referring to him only by the alias Abu Jindal. Indian news media reports have identified him as Sayeed Zabiudeen Ansari. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Indian Police Arrest Suspect in 2008 Mumbai Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indian Police Arrest Suspect in 2008 Mumbai Attack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lashkar-e-Taiba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:03:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb64d513-c189-5e4f-bd5e-7ec8cefe29c1', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb64d513-c189-5e4f-bd5e-7ec8cefe29c1'}, {'abstract': 'A new book offers ideas on improving neighborhoods for the aging from experts in finance, technology, architecture — and, yes, politics.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/aging-a-collective-response/', 'snippet': 'A new book offers ideas on improving neighborhoods for the aging from experts in finance, technology, architecture — and, yes, politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the things I appreciate about the new book “Independent for Life: Homes and Neighborhoods for an Aging America” is the sheer amount of information it collects in one handsomely designed paperback.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aging: A Collective Response', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:09:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6051dcca-b7f0-565e-96a9-10823d2f0e6c', 'word_count': 410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6051dcca-b7f0-565e-96a9-10823d2f0e6c'}, {'abstract': 'Jeff Koons’s “Split-rocker” has popped up again this summer. This time it’s in Basel, in one of three exhibitions of the prolific American artist’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/in-europe-its-a-jeff-koons-summer/', 'snippet': 'Jeff Koons’s “Split-rocker” has popped up again this summer. This time it’s in Basel, in one of three exhibitions of the prolific American artist’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, a room full of Hoover vacuum cleaners and shampoo polishers can be beautiful! The curators at Fondation Beyeler in Basel, Switzerland, have used tricks of light and space to stage its first exhibition of the American artist Jeff Koons’s work, writes Elisabeth Hopkins in the IHT’s Global Arts Guide. A riot of colors, ideas and symbols, the work is are arranged in three sections: the Hoovers (‘The New’’), the ‘‘Banality’’ sculptures, each of them according to Mr. Koons, a ‘‘metaphor for the viewer’s cultural guilt and shame,’’ and ‘‘Celebration,’’ a mix of paintings and balloon sculptures (dog, tulips, a heart). “Split-rocker,” a massive floral sculpture first assembled in Avignon in 2000 and, notoriously, at Versailles in 2008, is blooming now in the foundation’s park. www.fondationbeyeler.ch', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Europe, It’s a Jeff Koons Summer', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koons, Jeff', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Basel (Switzerland)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:19:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By The International Herald Tribune', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The International Herald Tribune'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/745baf13-802d-5ead-b0da-ee3ee912ff77', 'word_count': 254, 'uri': 'nyt://article/745baf13-802d-5ead-b0da-ee3ee912ff77'}, {'abstract': 'Phillip Kirschen-Clark is leaving after the restaurant decided to make major changes to its offerings.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/chef-departs-demi-monde/', 'snippet': 'Phillip Kirschen-Clark is leaving after the restaurant decided to make major changes to its offerings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Phillip Kirschen-Clark, above, the chef who attracted attention at Vandaag, which he left last summer and which recently closed, has now left Demi Monde, a bar and lounge with a chef’s table in the Financial District that opened in mid-May. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chef Departs Demi Monde', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirschen-Clark, Phillip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Demi Monde (Manhattan, NY, Bar)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:19:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7862b29b-f480-5823-87fc-070d89104a8f', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7862b29b-f480-5823-87fc-070d89104a8f'}, {'abstract': 'A dead heat in the women’s 100 meters at the Olympic trials has raised a question — who gets to go to the Games? — that no one seems able to answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/sports/leading-off-no-way-to-run-an-olympic-trial.html', 'snippet': 'A dead heat in the women’s 100 meters at the Olympic trials has raised a question — who gets to go to the Games? — that no one seems able to answer.', 'lead_paragraph': "The easiest old joke among the five-ring set is that the only amateurs left in the Olympics are the people running them. This theme pops up reliably at every Games, so we have to hand it to USA Track and Field for getting a jump on things and accomplishing this a month before the Olympics even start. In the first weekend of its Olympic trials, a dead heat for third place in the women's 100 means one of the marquee spots in the Olympics might be decided by a coin flip, or Allyson Felix or Jeneba Tarmoh could gracefully bow out for the good of making this seeming like less of a circus. The fact that those are two of the top three options hanging over the scenario two days after the race tells you pretty much everything you need to know about this enterprise. And these options were stumbled upon by USA Track and Field about a day and a half ago.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/sports/olympics/26leadingpic/26leadingpic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/sports/olympics/26leadingpic/26leadingpic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1589, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/sports/olympics/26leadingpic/26leadingpic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/26/sports/olympics/26leadingpic/26leadingpic-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/sports/olympics/26leadingpic/26leadingpic-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Way to Run an Olympic Trial', 'kicker': 'Leading Off', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Track and Field', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania State University', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merritt, LaShawn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sandusky, Jerry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Marion', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hodgson, Roy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gatlin, Justin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Youkilis, Kevin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Felix, Allyson', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:30:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Zinser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4304e74-75f7-53b4-bf18-035bccca54d8', 'word_count': 789, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4304e74-75f7-53b4-bf18-035bccca54d8'}, {'abstract': 'Fire at a revered shrine sparked off anti-India protests in Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/image-of-the-day-june-25/', 'snippet': 'Fire at a revered shrine sparked off anti-India protests in Srinagar, Jammu and Kashmir.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Image of the Day: June 25', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5da908b6-d373-5536-9cd5-c39bb6786082', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5da908b6-d373-5536-9cd5-c39bb6786082'}, {'abstract': 'Reese Hoffa is an Olympic shot putter. He also is amazingly adept with a Rubik’s cube.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/master-of-the-shot-put-and-the-cube/', 'snippet': 'Reese Hoffa is an Olympic shot putter. He also is amazingly adept with a Rubik’s cube.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — On Sunday, after fending off a number of competitors, shot-putter Reese Hoffa made the U.S. Olympic team for a third time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Master of the Shot Put, and the Cube', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shot Put', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffa, Reese', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:32:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a92f1c39-822c-5f77-a6d7-6fa0c78e7b7e', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a92f1c39-822c-5f77-a6d7-6fa0c78e7b7e'}, {'abstract': 'The complex has an oyster bar, an outdoor terrace and a duplex restaurant indoors.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/toy-a-new-diversion-in-the-gansevoort-hotel/', 'snippet': 'The complex has an oyster bar, an outdoor terrace and a duplex restaurant indoors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Toy, an ambitious, multifaceted restaurant, opens on Monday, replacing Tanuki Tavern and Carte Blanche in the Gansevoort chain’s hotel in the meatpacking district. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toy, a New Diversion in the Gansevoort Hotel', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beers, Jeffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hotel Gansevoort (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toy (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Meatpacking District (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:36:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a01da69-c13a-5045-8061-5d39170392ce', 'word_count': 94, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a01da69-c13a-5045-8061-5d39170392ce'}, {'abstract': 'Danny DeVito and Richard Griffiths reveal the raw hostility at the core of Neil Simon’s “Sunshine Boys.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/london-theater-journal-sunshine-in-different-sizes/', 'snippet': 'Danny DeVito and Richard Griffiths reveal the raw hostility at the core of Neil Simon’s “Sunshine Boys.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Willie Clark, the great vaudeville comedian, has a carved-in-stone list of things that are funny. Words that have “k” sounds, for instance, like pickle and cake and cucumber. Might I add to that list the image of a tufted Danny DeVito in striped pajamas and a sports jacket?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: ‘Sunshine’ in Different Sizes', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Mutt and a Jeff, Together Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeVito, Danny', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Griffiths, Richard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orton, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharrock, Thea', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:40:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c6dc7ac-2d7b-5783-8d2d-017a1b805a76', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c6dc7ac-2d7b-5783-8d2d-017a1b805a76'}, {'abstract': 'A rare bronze bust of Auguste Rodin, made by his disciple and lover Camille Claudel, has been recovered by the French police more than a decade after it was stolen from a museum, The Telegraph reported.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/stolen-bust-of-rodin-by-camille-claudel-recovered-in-france/', 'snippet': 'A rare bronze bust of Auguste Rodin, made by his disciple and lover Camille Claudel, has been recovered by the French police more than a decade after it was stolen from a museum, The Telegraph reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rare bronze bust of Auguste Rodin, made by his disciple and lover Camille Claudel, has been recovered by French police more than a decade after it was stolen from a museum, The Telegraph reported. The bust, which was taken from the Museum of Art and Archeology in Guéret in central France in 1999, was discovered in the van of an antiques dealer who had been under surveillance in connection with recent thefts in the Lyon region, and who was arrested on Tuesday with another man. The bust, one of about 50 sculptures made by Claudel, is estimated to be worth between about $600,000 and $1.2 million, according to Agence France-Presse. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stolen Bust of Rodin by Camille Claudel Recovered in France', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stolen Bust of Rodin Is Recovered in France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rodin, Auguste', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:40:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0e1c731-752b-50ef-8f98-7efac39fda36', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0e1c731-752b-50ef-8f98-7efac39fda36'}, {'abstract': 'Thinking of a Wii or an Xbox with Kinect in the hopes of getting your kids off the couch? Think again.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/exergames-dont-make-children-more-fit/', 'snippet': 'Thinking of a Wii or an Xbox with Kinect in the hopes of getting your kids off the couch? Think again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thinking of a Wii or an Xbox with Kinect to get your children off the couch? Think again: new research reported in The New York Times’s Business section shows that even children who have access to only the most active games aren’t more active over all. The kids may get off the couch at first, but once their initial interest in the games wanes, they seem to go back to more sedentary pursuits. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Exergames’ Don’t Make Children Fitter', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer and Video Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:46:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14ae53dd-fc78-5217-ac75-ee0ea88693d4', 'word_count': 75, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14ae53dd-fc78-5217-ac75-ee0ea88693d4'}, {'abstract': 'In voting not to take another look at its blockbuster 2010 Citizens United ruling, the court reversed a Montana Supreme Court decision not to follow it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/us/supreme-court-declines-to-revisit-citizens-united.html', 'snippet': 'In voting not to take another look at its blockbuster 2010 Citizens United ruling, the court reversed a Montana Supreme Court decision not to follow it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In a brief unsigned decision, the Supreme Court on Monday declined to have another look at its blockbuster 2010 campaign finance decision, Citizens United v. Federal Election Commission. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/26citizen/26citizen-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Court Declines to Revisit Its Citizens United Decision', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Declines to Revisit Its Citizens United Decision', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Supreme Courts (State)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:47:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10e1d15b-3d4b-5c76-bf26-0fadad2a82f7', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10e1d15b-3d4b-5c76-bf26-0fadad2a82f7'}, {'abstract': 'Diego de Giorgi is set to become the co-head of global corporate and investment banking for Europe at Bank of America.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/goldman-executive-to-join-bank-of-america/', 'snippet': 'Diego de Giorgi is set to become the co-head of global corporate and investment banking for Europe at Bank of America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Diego de Giorgi, a senior Goldman Sachs executive, is leaving the firm to take a top position at Bank of America Merrill Lynch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Goldman Executive to Join Bank of America', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:50:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/977ecd11-c139-54bd-bd6d-afd3d63bab18', 'word_count': 208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/977ecd11-c139-54bd-bd6d-afd3d63bab18'}, {'abstract': 'Refusing to fix a massive market failure.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/deleveraging-and-the-depression-gang/', 'snippet': 'Refusing to fix a massive market failure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bank for International Settlements has just come out with a report emphasizing the “limits to monetary policy”, which is apparently being taken seriously. I guess I’d start from the observation that the BIS has already embraced liquidationism, the idea that all this suffering is good for us and that trying to mitigate the pain would somehow be a bad thing. Now they’re just trying to come up with additional arguments for doing nothing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deleveraging and the Depression Gang', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:50:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d0caea5-c3ed-51e5-b835-b6c49e1558f0', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d0caea5-c3ed-51e5-b835-b6c49e1558f0'}, {'abstract': 'Ease is a word used too seldom in fashion. It takes particular assurance to do as Frida Giannini, the Gucci designer, did in her lively show for spring 2013 which, by modifying the sartorial grammar of Mediterranean summer dressing.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/at-gucci-assuredly-made-in-italy/', 'snippet': 'Ease is a word used too seldom in fashion. It takes particular assurance to do as Frida Giannini, the Gucci designer, did in her lively show for spring 2013 which, by modifying the sartorial grammar of Mediterranean summer dressing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Inevitably all conversation here these days turns to the floundering Euro zone economy. Even fans rooting for the underdog in the European cup match pitting Germany against Greece over the weekend were secretly relieved when the German team won. Everyone knows that in the larger sense Germany controls the ball.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Gucci, Assuredly ‘Made in Italy’', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giannini, Frida', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T15:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Guy Trebay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Guy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trebay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c984c03-4d84-5743-b6ec-572be81a6584', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c984c03-4d84-5743-b6ec-572be81a6584'}, {'abstract': "June 25, 2012 - David Segal on Apple's retail army.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001626958/business-day-live-apple-stores.html', 'sni