o', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosado', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Olsen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/f9068f9e-c05e-5c0c-b823-21a29aae4a91', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/f9068f9e-c05e-5c0c-b823-21a29aae4a91'}, {'abstract': 'What’s next in this series: f4e, s9, se5en?', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/numberplay-se5en/', 'snippet': 'What’s next in this series: f4e, s9, se5en?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Numberplay, the weeklong game of collaboration and discovery that also happens to be about math. If you’re new to the game, give it a try by leaving a comment at the end of this post. You don’t have to solve the problem; hunches are good. So are wild conjectures. At Numberplay, the standard answer is just the beginning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: se5en', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cryptography, Codes and Ciphers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T16:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/652817bf-853e-506e-b02d-063bc376a1c7', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/652817bf-853e-506e-b02d-063bc376a1c7'}, {'abstract': 'Cubed, soaked in milk and mixed with seasonal fruit or vegetables, yesterday’s loaf takes on a whole new identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/health/nutrition/sweet-and-savory-bread-puddings.html', 'snippet': 'Cubed, soaked in milk and mixed with seasonal fruit or vegetables, yesterday’s loaf takes on a whole new identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I used to bake bread every week, but in recent years I’ve gotten out of the habit. The main reason is that I don’t eat as much as I used to, and I kept finding myself with stale bread on my hands. But I reminded myself this week how much I like bread puddings, both savory and sweet, so I may get back into the habit, as they’re such an easy and delicious destination for stale bread.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/26/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/25recipehealth/25recipehealth-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/25r