 or language.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/justice-dept-to-monitor-elections-in-queens-and-orange-county/', 'snippet': 'The department did not say why it would monitor polling places in Queens, but the Voting Rights Act prohibits discrimination in the voting process on the basis of race, color or language.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department will send federal officials to observe Congressional primary elections on Tuesday in Queens and the Hudson Valley, the department announced on Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justice Dept. to Monitor Elections in Queens and Orange County', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Rights Act (1965)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillibrand, Kirsten E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayworth, Nan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River Valley (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T17:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f56b285-dfa6-5bca-be2f-f90603a3b43b', 'word_count': 174, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f56b285-dfa6-5bca-be2f-f90603a3b43b'}, {'abstract': 'Mörel, a self-professed bibliophile, is the antithesis of the typical bottom-line-observant publisher.', 'web_url': 'https://tmaga