Wimbledon but has to play top-seeded Novak Djokovic in the second.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/harrison-survives-gets-djokovic-next/', 'snippet': 'American Ryan Harrison won his first round match at Wimbledon but has to play top-seeded Novak Djokovic in the second.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Ryan Harrison rallied from a first-set lapse to defeat Lu Yen-Hsun of Taiwan, 4-6, 6-3, 6-4, 6-2, in the first round of Wimbledon Monday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harrison Survives, Gets Djokovic Next', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lu, Yen-Hsun', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T20:27:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30010011-6551-55f2-b904-d214b4e4d990', 'word_count': 477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30010011-6551-55f2-b904-d214b4e4d990'}, {'abstract': 'A “Casablanca” statuette is put up for auction, something the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences frowns on.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/casablanca-directors-oscar-goes-on-the-block/', 'snippet': 'A “Casablanca” statuette is put up for auction, something the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences frowns on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Round up the usual entertainment memorabilia collectors: The 1943 best director Oscar for “Casablanca” is on the auction block, the latest in a slew of little gold men from Hollywood’s Golden Age to come up for sale.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Casablanca’ Director’s Oscar Goes on the Block', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Casablanca’ Oscar On the Auction Block', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welles, Orson', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T20:28:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d3c9fe6-7ec1-565d-a197-8fe40e19054c', 'word_count': 235, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d3c9fe6-7ec1-565d-a197-8fe40e19054c'}, {'abstract': 'In the final Principal\'s Office interview of the 2011-12 school year, Jill Hoder, principal of P.S. 161 Arthur Ashe School in Queens, said data helps the school personalize the learning experience for its diverse student body and in inclusion classes that accommodate a special-needs population of 13 percent. "The mission and the motto in this building is that we take public education personally. What you do or what you need to learn is gravely different from what the person next to you needs to learn."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/25/jill-hoder-take-public-education-personally/', 'snippet': "In the final Principal's Office interview of the 2011-12 school year, Jill Hoder, principal of P.S. 161 Arthur Ashe School in Queens, said data helps the school personalize the learning experience for its diverse student body and in inclusion clas...", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jill Hoder: Take Public Education Personally ', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T20:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By HITEN SAMTANI', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hiten', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'SAMTANI', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2cd1610-1dc1-5c56-9621-673b922e506b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2cd1610-1dc1-5c56-9621-673b922e506b'}, {'abstract': 'For high-level executives who lose their positions, gone are the days of flying overseas or hopping from one American city to another, often in the front of the plane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/business/dealing-with-travel-downgrades.html', 'snippet': 'For high-level executives who lose their positions, gone are the days of flying overseas or hopping from one American city to another, often in the front of the plane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a credit union chief executive, James L. Van Arsdale used to travel frequently to big conferences and to meetings with clients. Now, more than four years after he led the acquisition of the credit union, he is an insurance agent with Mass Mutual, offering people financial advice and dealing with a life of fewer perks. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/business/26former-web/26former-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,