 show @facebook.com addresses. The company argues that this was not a change to the site’s privacy settings, just a “visual setting change.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/facebook-changes-e-mail-settings-without-user-consent/', 'snippet': 'Facebook has changed people’s e-mail address settings on the site to automatically show @facebook.com addresses. The company argues that this was not a change to the site’s privacy settings, just a “visual setting change.”', 'lead_paragraph': '10:55 a.m. | Updated Clarifying the language between Facebook and the F.T.C.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Like It or Not, Facebook Changes E-Mail Settings', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T21:22:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/422e613a-593b-57a2-8891-62d463ce7870', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/422e613a-593b-57a2-8891-62d463ce7870'}, {'abstract': 'On Site Opera, a new company, made its debut with Shostakovich’s “Tale of the Silly Baby Mouse” at the Bronx Zoo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/arts/music/shostakovichs-tale-of-the-silly-baby-mouse-at-bronx-zoo.html', 'snippet': 'On Site Opera, a new company, made its debut with Shostakovich’s “Tale of the Silly Baby Mouse” at the Bronx Zoo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now and then you witness a debut so happy and so rich with potential that you can’t wait to share the news. In the case of On Site Opera, a fledgling company that mounted its inaugural production on Saturday afternoon, it seems especially vital to spread the word, since few cognoscenti were on hand to witness its opening splash. True to the troupe’s mission of presenting operas in unconventional settings, the performance took place on the Asia Plaza Stage at the Bronx Zoo.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1261, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/TALES/TALES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Troupe Chooses Bronx Zoo for a Debut', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Troupe Chooses Bronx Zoo For a Debut', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shostakovich, Dmitri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Zoo Wildlife Conservation Park', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'On Site Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T21:28:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/231e669a-5240-516a-b801-ed3029eb66b4', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/231e669a-5240-516a-b801-ed3029eb66b4'}, {'abstract': 'Dagmar Spain/Dance Imprints performed two pieces, “Await ...” and “Yellow Is Not Gold,” at Danspace Project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/arts/dance/dagmar-spain-dance-imprints-at-danspace-project.html', 'snippet': 'Dagmar Spain/Dance Imprints performed two pieces, “Await ...” and “Yellow Is Not Gold,” at Danspace Project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the two works presented by Dagmar Spain and her company, Dance Imprints, at Danspace Project from Thursday through Saturday, the best performance was given by Alec Dana. For the first few minutes of the first piece, Mr. Dana, an elegant older gentleman, sat silent and dignified as he was berated by the actor Iorgo Papoutsas. After that Mr. Dana left, never to appear again. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/dagmar/dagmar-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/arts/dagmar/dagmar-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wandering and Waiting for the Unknown', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wandering and Waiting For the Unknown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dance Imprints', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Spain, Dagmar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T21:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3eafd208-37a5-5468-a8c6-8b732bb8132c', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3eafd208-37a5-5468-a8c6-8b732bb8132c'}, {'abstract': 'In “Motel Cherry,” a new play by Peggy Stafford, a group of travelers congregate in a dumpy roadside motel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/theater/reviews/motel-cherry-by-peggy-stafford-at-here-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'In “Motel Cherry,” a new play by Peggy Stafford, a group of travelers congregate in a dumpy roadside motel.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Functional is all I’m looking for.” So announces the hustling copier salesman, Mark (Mike Shapiro), about his modest expectations for overnight accommodations. It’s a low bar, but sorry, mister, you’ve checked into the wrong establishment.', 'print_section': 'C', 'pr