stname': 'La Rocco', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/25fdeb01-64af-5dd3-8c3b-d6856701edf8', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25fdeb01-64af-5dd3-8c3b-d6856701edf8'}, {'abstract': 'Ernests Gulbis defeated Tomas Berdych at Wimbledon on Monday with an effective second serve.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/how-gulbis-defeated-berdych-his-second-serve/', 'snippet': 'Ernests Gulbis defeated Tomas Berdych at Wimbledon on Monday with an effective second serve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ernests Gulbis edged sixth-seeded Tomas Berdych of the Czech Republic in three straight tiebreakers at Wimbledon on Monday, in a clash of two of the biggest hitters on the tour. Gulbis played boldly, hitting an astonishing 62 winners while committing only 33 unforced errors. The talented Latvian kept Berdych off balance with big serving and returning. Berdych, normally a power player who dominates points with his serve and forehand, was in the unusual position of having to react to Gulbis throughout the match. He managed only 30 winners (13 of which were aces) and had 27 unforced errors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Gulbis Defeated Berdych: His Second Serve', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berdych, Tomas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gulbis, Ernests', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T21:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': Non