the news anchor Will McAvoy in “The Newsroom” as the embodiment of venality, superficiality and intellectual laziness, rather than its noble opponent, he may have come up with something closer to the Canadian sa...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night was the debut of “The Newsroom,” the anticipated and by-now widely dissected new HBO series from Aaron Sorkin. It’s intended, in large part, as a critique of the news industry —\xa0its venality, its superficiality and its overall intellectual laziness. All of which is exposed by Will McAvoy (played by Jeff Daniels), a mad-as-hell-and-not-taking-it-anymore news anchor who decides he can do better —\xa0and an example of a stock Sorkin character type that The New Yorker’s TV critic Emily Nussbaum calls “The Great Man,” a character “who is theoretically flawed, but really a primal truth-teller whom everyone should follow (or date).”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before ‘The Newsroom,’ There Was ‘The Newsroom’', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorkin, Aaron', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T22:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Sternbergh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sternbergh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d471c500-06c7-553f-82d6-219c67e6bbb5', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d471c500-06c7-553f-82d6-219c67e6bbb5'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t be a victim to unpredictable summer weather. Here’s an alternative to chunky rain boots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/25/fashion/25JellySandals.html',