'WASHINGTON — Intelligence officials will face the possibility of additional scrutiny by lie detector tests and a recently established inspector general under new rules intended to deter and detect leaking to news organizations, James R. Clapper Jr., the director of national intelligence, announced Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Intelligence Chief Announces New Rules to Curb Leaks', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Rules Set To Curb Leaks And Ensnare The Leakers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapper, James R Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inspectors General', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-25T22:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2991600a-21b1-555e-ace1-41c7ec2ed442', 'word_count': 777, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2991600a-21b1-555e-ace1-41c7ec2ed442'}, {'abstract': 'New research on the H5N1 virus suggests that it could evolve to be transmitted between mammals, but the process of such a mutation remains mysterious.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/science/the-evolution-of-bird-flu-and-the-race-to-keep-up.html', 'snippet': 'New research on the H5N1 virus suggests that it could evolve to be transmitted between mammals, but the process of such a mutation remains mysterious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On May 20, a 10-year-old girl in rural Cambodia got a fever. Five days later, she was admitted to a hospital, and after two days of intensive care she was dead. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/science/26FLU_SPAN/26FLU-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Evolution of Bird Flu, and the Race to Keep Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Evolution of Bird Flu, And the Race to Keep Up', 'name'