f headlines. It is an e-mail from the Chicago Police Department listing the crimes that were committed during the night that just ended. By 7 a.m., he is calling Garry F. McCarthy, the police superintendent. That is unlikely to be their final conversation of the day, or even of the morning. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/jpCHICAGO1/jpCHICAGO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/us/jpCHICAGO1/jpCHICAGO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rate of Killings Rises 38 Percent in Chicago in 2012', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rate of Killings Rises 38 Percent In Chicago In ’12', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T03:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monica Davey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cfbc0d6-6886-5ab1-ba73-5f58aeff80a8', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cfbc0d6-6886-5ab1-ba73-5f58aeff80a8'}, {'abstract': 'Mardy Fish will skip the London Olympics and play an ATP tour event in Washington, a decision he said had nothing to do with his health problems this year.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/25/fish-with-emotional-loss-in-2004-will-remain-away-from-the-olympics/', 'snippet': 'Mardy Fish will skip the London Olympics and play an ATP tour event in Washington, a decision he said had nothing to do with his health problems this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The lure of the Olympics is particularly powerful at Wimbledon this year. Three weeks after the tournament ends, the predominantly all-white clothing rule will be waived and most of the world’s best tennis players will return for the Olympic tournament on the grass they know so well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fish, With Emotional Loss in 2004, Will Remain Away From the Olympics', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T03:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93c85923-bd61-540c-9df7-bc0115bc6bcf', 'word_count': 556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93c85923-bd61-540c-9df7-bc0115bc6bcf'}, {'abstract': 'As the economy has improved, so have the fortunes of Senator Orrin Hatch as he seeks to fen