}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vollmer, Dana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T04:05:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d6dbe95-f813-571b-a6d2-a93e0b0339fb', 'word_count': 322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d6dbe95-f813-571b-a6d2-a93e0b0339fb'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese man who published photographs online of his wife and their dead fetus — government officials forced her to submit to an abortion at seven months — has gone missing after being tracked by security officials and thugs, according to his sister.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/father-in-china-abortion-scandal-is-said-to-be-missing/', 'snippet': 'The Chinese man who published photographs online of his wife and their dead fetus — government officials forced her to submit to an abortion at seven months — has gone missing after being tracked by security officials and thugs, according to his s...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Update, 3:58 p.m. Tuesday, E.S.T.: Deng Jiyuan called his sister, Deng Jicai, on Tuesday afternoon to report that he was safe, Ms. Deng told Edward Wong of The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Father in Chinese Forced-Abortion Scandal Is Said to Be Missing', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fines (Penalties)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio Free Asia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sina Weibo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'South China Morning Post Limited', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T04:11:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95ee19d8-bf56-5993-9e70-08eec18563bf', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95ee19d8-bf56-5993-9e70-08eec18563bf'}, {'abstract': 'State-mandated mediation between the City of Stockton and its creditors was set to expire at midnight on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/us/california-bankruptcy-looms-for-city-at-end-of-mediation.html', 'snippet': 'State-mandated mediation between the City of Stockton and its creditors was set to expire at midnight on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'State-mandated mediation between the City of Stockton and its creditors was set to expire at midnight on Monday, moving the Central Valley community one step closer to becoming the largest city in the country to go bankrupt. If the 90-day mediation fails, the City Council is set to vote Tuesday evening on a new budget to cover a $26 million deficit in case of bankruptcy. City officials would then have until July 1 to officially file for bankruptcy protection. Once a booming bedroom community for San Francisco Bay Area commuters, the city was hard hit by falling housing prices, enduring one of the highest foreclosure rates in the country. Since 2009, the city has cut some $90 million from its budget, including deep cutbacks to municipal staff, police and fire departments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Bankruptcy Looms for City at End of Mediation', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Bankruptcy Looms For City at End of Mediation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stockton (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T04:16:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0937f321-b6f4-5ad6-b44c-f2666bd297bb', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0937f321-b6f4-5ad6-b44c-f2666bd297bb'}, {'abstract': 'Lawyers for James (Whitey) Bulger won a four-month delay in his trial and told a judge that a deal between their client and the government renders him immune from prosecution.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/us/massachusetts-bulger-trial-delayed.html', 'snippet': 'Lawyers for James (Whitey) Bulger won a four-month delay in his trial and told a judge that a deal between their client and the government renders him immune from prosecution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers for James (Whitey) Bulger on Monday won a four-month delay in his trial and told a judge that a deal between their client and the government renders him immune from prosecution, and that they will seek to have charges against Mr. Bulger dropped. Mr. Bulger, who prosecutors said acted as an F.B.I. informer while playing a leading role in Boston’s crime underworld, faces charges including 19 murders at a trial now scheduled to begin March 4, 2013. His lawyers said they need more time to prepare his defense. Mr. Bulger was captured last summer in Santa Monica, Calif., after spending 16 years in hiding with his girlfriend, Catherine Greig, who was recently sentenced to eight years in prison on charges of harboring a fugitive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Massachusetts: Bulger Trial Delayed', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Massachusetts: Bulger Trial Delayed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fugitives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bulger, James J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greig, Catherine Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T04:19:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb18fb2b-8283-5136-9151-255fa807aa3c', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb18fb2b-8283-5136-9151-255fa807aa3c'}, {'abstract': 'The lawyer for George Zimmerman argued on Monday that his client should be granted bond for a second time as he awaits trial on murder charges in the shooting death of Trayvon Martin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/us/florida-zimmerman-seeks-another-chance-at-freedom-on-bond.html', 'snippet': 'The lawyer for George Zimmerman argued on Monday that his client should be granted bond for a second time as he awaits trial on murder charges in the shooting death of Trayvon Martin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lawyer for George Zimmerman argued on Monday that his client should be granted bond for a second time as he awaits trial on murder charges in the shooting death of Trayvon Martin. In a motion filed with the Seminole County Circuit Court, the lawyer, Mark O’Mara, said his client is not a flight risk and takes responsibility for his role in not alerting the judge about tens of thousands of dollars in donations made to an online fund that he had set up before his first bond hearing in April. Bail was revoked for Mr. Zimmerman on June 1 after prosecutors told the court that he and his wife, Shellie Zimmerman, 25, had misled the court about their finances and had spoken to each other in code about the estimated $125,000 in donations. The second bond hearing is scheduled for Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida: Zimmerman Seeks Another Chance at Freedom on Bond', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida: Zimmerman Seeks Another Chance at Freedom On Bond', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Mara, Mark M", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T04:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/889d8b23-649c-5656-be30-cefb87d7d7f2', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/889d8b23-649c-5656-be30-cefb87d7d7f2'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Lochte broke out a pair of Adidas high-top “star-spangled” sneakers that he helped design after winning the 400-meter individual medley at the Olympic trials Monday night.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/after-a-victory-lochte-steps-out-in-style/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Lochte broke out a pair of Adidas high-top “star-spangled” sneakers that he helped design after winning the 400-meter individual medley at the Olympic trials Monday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — After winning the 400-meter individual medley at the Olympic trials Monday night, Ryan Lochte broke out a pair of Adidas high-top “star-spangled” sneakers that he helped design. The right shoe is blue with white stars. The left one is white with red horizontal stripe. Both have wings, as if he is an All-American Hermes. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Victory, Lochte Steps Out in Style', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T04:23:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1024a7ca-6a3c-5083-b1e8-5d78656e78c8', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1024a7ca-6a3c-5083-b1e8-5d78656e78c8'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Education is issuing data on Tuesday showing that 5 percent of career-training programs failed all three requirements of the department’s new gainful-employment regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/us/5-percent-of-job-programs-fail-test-on-graduates-success.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Education is issuing data on Tuesday showing that 5 percent of career-training programs failed all three requirements of the department’s new gainful-employment regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Education is issuing data on Tuesday showing that 5 percent of career-training programs — all of them at for-profit institutions — failed all three requirements of the department’s new gainful-employment regulations. Under the new rules, intended to protect students from taking on high debt for worthless job credentials, at least 35 percent of graduates must be repaying their loans, and the typical graduate’s estimated annual loan payments must not exceed 12 percent of earnings, or 30 percent of discretionary income. Starting next fall, schools that fail all three tests for three of four consecutive years will lose their access to federal aid. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '5 Percent of Job Programs Fail Test on Graduates’ Success', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '5 Percent of Job Programs Fail Test On Graduates’ Success', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 1, 'major':