get dance has ended, and the City Council and Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg have waltzed to a deal for $68.5 billion that includes no tax increases, no firehouse closings, no widespread layoffs of teachers or others — and, in fact,...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New City Budget Restores Money for Day Care and After-School Programs', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T12:20:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aad2a9a7-f9a3-52fc-8d6a-b682a9b4a8ee', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aad2a9a7-f9a3-52fc-8d6a-b682a9b4a8ee'}, {'abstract': 'In his memoir “Yes, Chef,” Marcus Samuelsson writes about his background, the hard work that led to his success, and the frustrating lack of exalted black chefs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/books/yes-chef-by-marcus-samuelsson.html', 'snippet': 'In his memoir “Yes, Chef,” Marcus Samuelsson writes about his background, the hard work that led to his success, and the frustrating lack of exalted black chefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The universal rule of kitchen work, Marcus Samuelsson says in his crisp new memoir, “Yes, Chef,” goes as follows: “Stay invisible unless you’re going to shine.” That rule applies to writers too, especially to those who would write food memoirs. Because you like to put things in your mouth does not mean you have a story to tell. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/books/27book-img2/27book-img2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 827, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/books/27book-img2/27book-img2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1655, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/books/27book-img2/27book-img2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/27/books/27book-img2/27book-img2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/books/27book-img2/27book-img2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Life Spent in Sugar and Spice', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Life Spent In Sugar And Spice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samuelsson, Marcus', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T12:37:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb2c4ebc-18c9-5a20-905a-4c76ba82a679', 'word_count': 1176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb2c4ebc-18c9-5a20-905a-4c76ba82a679'}, {'abstract': 'Zynga hopes to impress Wall Street and game players with new games at an event Tuesday, and emerging media companies are filling the gaps left by contracting Western newspapers and broadcasters.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/the-breakfast-meeting-dividing-news-corp-and-quoting-men-about-women/', 'snippet': 'Zynga hopes to impress Wall Street and game players with new games at an event Tuesday, and emerging media companies are filling the gaps left by contracting Western newspapers and broadcasters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation is considering splitting itself in two, DealBook reported early Tuesday morning, with the publishing businesses — including The Wall Street Journal, The Times of London, The New York Post and the HarperCollins book business — separated from its entertainment assets like the Fox movie studio and TV networks. The change, which was long opposed by Rupert Murdoch, wouldn’t be expected to affect the Murdoch family’s control of both sets of assets, DealBook reported, but would please investors who are looking for a clean break from the phone-hacking scandals related to the News Corporation newspapers in Britain.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Dividing News Corp.? And Quoting Men About Women', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Zynga Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04044858-eec8-51d1-8506-5031c001cde3', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04044858-eec8-51d1-8506-5031c001cde3'}, {'abstract': 'SideCar allows people to use their private cars as taxis, while giving riders a cheaper alternative to other car-for-hire services. The question of its legality and whether it will need to be regulated looms over the business. Nevertheless, the company has attracted financing. It introduced its service in San Francisco on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/a-new-ride-sharing-service-turns-private-cars-into-taxis/', 'snippet': 'SideCar allows people to use their private cars as taxis, while giving riders a cheaper alternative to other car-for-hire services. The question of its legality and whether it will need to be regulated looms over the business. Nevertheless, the co...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Technology start-ups continue to chip away at the idea that everyone should own a car or two. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/technology/26bits-sidecar2/26bits-sidecar2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/26/technology/26bits-sidecar2/26bits-sidecar2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1412, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Ride-Sharing Service Turns Private Cars Into Taxis', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:00:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Brustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e2fdcad-af33-5f23-8f72-688ccd18cbb0', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e2fdcad-af33-5f23-8f72-688ccd18cbb0'}, {'abstract': 'Vuitton is celebrating all things French with the launch of three new jewelry collections, all inspired by three of the City of Light’s most iconic locations.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/the-get-louis-vuittons-orangerie-des-tuileries-brooch/', 'snippet': 'Vuitton is celebrating all things French with the launch of three new jewelry collections, all inspired by three of the City of Light’s most iconic locations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louis Vuitton is celebrating all things French just before Bastille Day (July 14), opening its first fine jewelry and watchmaking boutique on July 3 on the renowned Place Vendôme in Paris. To mark the occasion, Lorenz Bäumer, the artistic director of haute joaillerie for Vuitton, has designed three new collections inspired by three of the City of Light’s most iconic locations: the Place de la Concorde, the Champs Élysées and the Tuileries. Here, the Orangerie des Tuileries brooch features two flowers lifted from LV’s near-synonymous logo, one made of tsavorite and diamonds, and a larger one with a blue tanzanite gemstone in the center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Get | Louis Vuitton’s Orangerie des Tuileries Brooch', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsea Zalopany', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zalopany', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d511d6b1-8d69-52b4-a540-b1460b9b0137', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d511d6b1-8d69-52b4-a540-b1460b9b0137'}, {'abstract': 'Some parents say they have far more visibility into their children’s lives in the digital age than their parents had into theirs, as a new study finds that teenagers are leery of too much parental vigilance.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/can-gadgets-bring-you-closer-to-your-children/', 'snippet': 'Some parents say they have far more visibility into their children’s lives in the digital age than their parents had into theirs, as a new study finds that teenagers are leery of too much parental vigilance.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Can you know your children as well as your parents knew you? Or in the digital age, can you know them better? ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Gadgets Bring You Closer to Your Children?', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:10:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/202dd70d-08e0-5179-8511-4b9f42dea38b', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/202dd70d-08e0-5179-8511-4b9f42dea38b'}, {'abstract': 'With doctors expressing concern about the future of Jared Sullinger’s back, the Ohio State forward has fallen from lottery pick to not even being invited to attend Thursday’s N.B.A. draft.', 'web_url': 'https://offthedribble.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/in-a-draft-lacking-drama-sullingers-stock-plummets/', 'snippet': 'With doctors expressing concern about the future of Jared Sullinger’s back, the Ohio State forward has fallen from lottery pick to not even being invited to attend Thursday’s N.B.A. draft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jared Sullinger insists he is not injured. He participated in the pre-draft combine and worked out for various teams in the leadup to Thursday’s N.B.A. draft. Yet the player who was projected as a top-five pick out of Ohio State just a year ago was red-flagged as a future injury concern by doctors who have examined his back, leading to a precipitous fall in his draft ranking.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Draft Lacking Drama, Sullinger’s Stock Plummets', 'kicker': 'Off the Dribble', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Red Flag Is Raised, And Sullinger’s Standing Falls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melo, Fab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullinger, Jared', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:20:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce1ab3c8-046b-531b-8a9f-3e7a14cf5031', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce1ab3c8-046b-531b-8a9f-3e7a14cf5031'}, {'abstract': 'Immigration activists hoping that the U.S. Supreme Court would strike down a controversial Arizona law were generally heartened by the court’s ruling on Monday. But supporters of the law, known as S.B. 1070, also celebrated, saying a core provision of the legislation had been upheld.', 'web_url': 'https://rendezvous.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/for-hispanics-a-court-decision-wont-root-out-profiling/', 'snippet': 'Immigration activists hoping that the U.S. Supreme Court would strike down a controversial Arizona law were generally heartened by the court’s ruling on Monday. But supporters of the law, known as S.B. 1070, also celebrated, saying a core provisio...', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — For millions of Latinos who sought to get rid of Arizona’s infamous and draconian immigration law, the U.S. Supreme Court’s ruling on Monday brought some relief — but not a full reprieve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Hispanics, A Court Decision Won’t Root Out Profiling', 'kicker': 'IHT Rendezvous', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arizona Immigration Law (SB 1070)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigrants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brewer, Jan', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:21:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Luisita Lopez Torregrosa', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Luisita', 'middlename': 'Lopez', 'lastname': 'Torregrosa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e77e185d-1773-5700-955c-de9d027ec176', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e77e185d-1773-5700-955c-de9d027ec176'}, {'abstract': 'In another sign of growing ties between the countries, an annual award created by billionaires will honor people who attribute their achievement to Jewish values.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/world/europe/russians-establish-1-million-jewish-prize-with-israel.html', 'snippet': 'In another sign of growing ties between the countries, an annual award created by billionaires will honor people who attribute their achievement to Jewish values.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — A charity founded by Russian Jewish billionaires is establishing a $1 million annual award for excellence in virtually any field, to honor those people who attribute their success to Jewish values. The prize will be administered in partnership with the Israeli government, highlighting the strong ties between Israel and Russia. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russians Join Israel to Start Jewish Prize of $1 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russians Join Israel to Start Jewish Prize Of $1 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:26:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7ab7ec4-f892-50a2-8fbd-8a10cd0a9e85', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7ab7ec4-f892-50a2-8fbd-8a10cd0a9e85'}, {'abstract': 'John Isner, Donald Young and Venus Williams all lost in the first round at Wimbledon–and all three will play for the U.S. at the London Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/at-wimbledon-disappointing-results-for-u-s-olympians/', 'snippet': 'John Isner, Donald Young and Venus Williams all lost in the first round at Wimbledon–and all three will play for the U.S. at the London Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — The United States Tennis Association must be hoping that its squad announced Tuesday for the London Olympics will fare better at the All England Club next month than it has so far at Wimbledon. Representing the men in singles will be John Isner, Andy Roddick, Donald Young and Ryan Harrison. Roddick is scheduled to play later Tuesday, but of the other three Americans only Harrison won his first-round match. Isner and Roddick will team in doubles, as will Bob and Mike Bryan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Wimbledon, Disappointing Results for U.S. Olympians', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isner, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lepchenko, Varvara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McHale, Christina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raymond, Lisa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Venus', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Donald', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:26:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Shpigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shpigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fa55e00-ba6b-5339-9921-cb15877c1904', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fa55e00-ba6b-5339-9921-cb15877c1904'}, {'abstract': 'Fighting acid reflux may bring other risks, tools to control your child’s technology, finding a sustainable running stride and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/tuesday-reading-fighting-acid-reflux-may-bring-other-risks/', 'snippet': 'Fighting acid reflux may bring other risks, tools to control your child’s technology, finding a sustainable running stride and other consumer-focused news from The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A variety of consumer-focused articles appears daily in The New York Times and on our blogs. Each weekday morning, we gather them together here so you can quickly scan the news that could hit you in your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tuesday Reading: Fighting Acid Reflux May Bring Other Risks', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:31:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1c2ba49-9c2d-5685-9889-bf97bdef1ec1', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1c2ba49-9c2d-5685-9889-bf97bdef1ec1'}, {'abstract': 'The Day: On this Primary Day, considerable attention is focused on the fortunes of Representative Charles B. Rangel. But there’s another race that may say more about this city.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/on-primary-day-closely-watching-two-races/', 'snippet': 'The Day: On this Primary Day, considerable attention is focused on the fortunes of Representative Charles B. Rangel. But there’s another race that may say more about this city.', 'lead_paragraph': ' By the hundreds of thousands, New Yorkers will not vote in primaries being held on Tuesday in Congressional districts. We’re very good at not voting in this city. Our approach to polling stations is similar to what Lawrence Peter Berra, the catcher in the wry, once said about ballparks, something to the effect that if people don’t want to go, nothing can stop them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Primary Day, Closely Watching Two Races', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barron, Charles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rangel, Charles B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:32:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd929c65-d5a7-549a-94eb-7f38c2b9bf4b', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd929c65-d5a7-549a-94eb-7f38c2b9bf4b'}, {'abstract': 'We’re presenting workshops this week on The Times and the Common Core Standards. Here are some of the things we’ll be saying, and links we’ll be sharing.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/engaging-nonfiction-the-times-the-common-core-and-a-question-for-you/', 'snippet': 'We’re presenting workshops this week on The Times and the Common Core Standards. Here are some of the things we’ll be saying, and