k Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Coney Island Kernels', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T13:57:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victor Washkevich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victor', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Washkevich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f478aaab-d9a3-5cd6-973f-f532ddaf9760', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f478aaab-d9a3-5cd6-973f-f532ddaf9760'}, {'abstract': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/what-were-reading-465/', 'snippet': 'A collection of links from the reporters and editors of the Dining section.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ham Independence: An Iowa-based maker of excellent prosciutto, La Quercia, wants Americans to declare independence from foreign hams. Herb Eckhouse is on tour, promoting “Life, Liberty, and the Prosciutto of Happiness.” — Julia Moskin', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Reading', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T14:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb3dc3a9-07fa-5480-8946-cd90c40ea02b', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb3dc3a9-07fa-5480-8946-cd90c40ea02b'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Lochte looks very ready to take on Michael Phelps for swimming supremacy. a first-round exit by Venus Williams at Wimbledon raises questions about her future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/sports/olympics/leading-off-swimming-rivalry-intensifies-a-tennis-career-in-doubt.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan Lochte looks very ready to take on Michael Phelps for swimming supremacy. a first-round exit by Venus Williams at Wimbledon raises questions about her future.', 'lead_paragraph': "Swimming threw its first splash of pool water into the Olympic season Monday with the first day of the United States Olympic trials, which means from now until the last wall is touched in August, it is officially Ryan Lochte vs. Michael Phelps season. If this is not a season you are ready for, NBC's brain programmers will be at your door shortly. This is the great rivalry of the coming Games, an epic clash of titans, the tale of the superstar coming into his own (Lochte) trying to unseat swimming's Superman (Phelps). Knowing that, you can now put NBC on mute for two months, because it will do little but fill your head with that theme. Dramatic overkill, after all, is that fourth Olympic principle after higher, faster, stronger.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/sports/leading-off/leading-off-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/27/sports/leading-off/leading-off-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/sports/leading-off/leading-off-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp