://article/be95eeab-1fdc-570c-b0a3-cad11dc3754a', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be95eeab-1fdc-570c-b0a3-cad11dc3754a'}, {'abstract': 'How does Las Vegas’s 40 million annual visitors decide where to spend their money? Restaurant critic Al Mancini is here to help. Ask him anything about the mix of food, entertainment, and money that is the Las Vegas restaurant scene.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/al-mancini-las-vegas-restaurant-critic-is-answering-questions/', 'snippet': 'How does Las Vegas’s 40 million annual visitors decide where to spend their money? Restaurant critic Al Mancini is here to help. Ask him anything about the mix of food, entertainment, and money that is the Las Vegas restaurant scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Al Mancini is a conspicuous character in a city full of them — Las Vegas, where he is a restaurant critic and journalist. From graduating from Brooklyn Law School, to tending bar at CBGB’s Pizza in the East Village, to writing reviews of strip clubs, he has followed an unorthodox path to the luxurious dining rooms he now frequents. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Al Mancini, Las Vegas Restaurant Critic, Is Answering Questions', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Las Vegas (Nev)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T15:53:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62a75be7-1a1d-5e0a-824a-bf7a4eb7ad6a', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62a75be7-1a1d-5e0a-824a-bf7a4eb7ad6a'}, {'abstract': '“Viva Forever!” is the idea of Judy Craymer, who produced “Mamma Mia!,” based on the music of Abba, which opened in London in 1999 and is still running there.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/spice-girls-reunite-to-announce-a-musical/', 'snippet': '“Viva Forever!” is the idea of Judy Craymer, who produced “Mamma Mia!,” based on the music of Abba, which opened in London in 1999 and is still running there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty years ago they were mere wannabes, but now there is going to be a stage musical based on their music and their careers. The Spice Girls, symbols of bubbly mid-’90s dance pop, reunited briefly in London on Tuesday for the announcement of “Viva Forever!,” which is scheduled to open there at the end of the year; according to its creators, it will address the “bitter reality of fame.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spice Girls Reunite to Announce a Musical', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Spice Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T15:55:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2287375d-6d3b-52c3-9ada-e0bef74d605f', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2287375d-6d3b-52c3-9ada-e0bef74d605f'}, {'abstract': 'The attack is the latest iteration of President Obama’s attempts to demonize Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/obama-ad-attacks-romney-as-outsourcer-in-chi