lead_paragraph': '“The Glass House,” the reality show that was the subject of a bitter legal dispute between ABC and CBS — which went in ABC’s favor — has quickly earned mostly disfavor with viewers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Glass House’ Ratings Sink; CW Ratings Approach Rock Bottom', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CW Television Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T17:05:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9c1a6df-8ea5-5246-9182-b715fbd12b4e', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9c1a6df-8ea5-5246-9182-b715fbd12b4e'}, {'abstract': 'The Herbfarm Restaurant seems like precisely the kind of small business that should benefit from the Affordable Care Act’s tax credits.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/a-small-restaurant-gets-a-big-hike-in-health-premiums-and-misses-the-tax-credit/', 'snippet': 'The Herbfarm Restaurant seems like precisely the kind of small business that should benefit from the Affordable Care Act’s tax credits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With this post, The Agenda returns to our occasional series on how small companies are coping with providing health insurance. We’re going to Woodinville, Wash., about a half hour north of Seattle, and The Herbfarm Restaurant. The Herbfarm, which grows many of its own ingredients in its garden and 