 less likely to be liquidated when the going gets tough, according to a study by Moody’s Investors Service. The author writes that private equity does more to save jobs at struggling companies than other type...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Farley is a partner in the corporate practice of Paul Hastings and is based in the firm’s New York office. His practice centers on representing some of the world’s leading commercial and investment banks in leveraged buyout financing, recapitalization and refinancing. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Tough Times, Private Equity Saves Jobs', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T18:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Farley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Farley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78fa7a75-1151-5d0d-abc5-6ec351f7575e', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78fa7a75-1151-5d0d-abc5-6ec351f7575e'}, {'abstract': 'Louis C.K. is bypassing services like Ticketmaster and offering tickets to his next tour for a flat $45 through his own Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/louis-c-k-gets-into-the-ticket-selling-business/', 'snippet': 'Louis C.K. is bypassing services like Ticketmaster and offering tickets to his next tour for a flat $45 through his own Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At this point in his booming career, Louis C.K. could fill theaters by charging B