348-53ea-9a95-f8f107b4f95c', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96b7af7c-c348-53ea-9a95-f8f107b4f95c'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, Twitter, General Electric, Google and eBay announced a new initiative called “Girls Who Code.” By creating a mentoring and teaching program, they hope to increase the number of young women who become programmers and engineers.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/tech-companies-announce-girls-who-code-initiative/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, Twitter, General Electric, Google and eBay announced a new initiative called “Girls Who Code.” By creating a mentoring and teaching program, they hope to increase the number of young women who become programmers and engineers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s no secret that programmers who work at start-ups are predominantly men. This is evident on all corners of the Internet: from the naming of some products — which can sometimes “make women cringe”\xa0—\xa0to the endless stream of “top 100″ lists that are often 95 percent men.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tech Companies Announce ‘Girls Who Code’ Initiative', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saujani, Reshma', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'eBay Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1667261-3f22-59f0-9925-b785b5990fdf', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1667261-3f22-59f0-9925-b785b5990fdf'}, {'abstract': 'An IVF anniversary and the bioethical landscape of today.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/the-wisdom-of-a-moral-panic/', 'snippet': 'An IVF anniversary and the bioethical landscape of today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a piece pegged to the death of the first woman to conceive through in vitro fertilization, the Atlantic’s Megan Garber looks back\xa0on what she calls “the IVF panic” that accompanied the technology’s 1970s emergence:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wisdom of a Moral Panic', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:30:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec114849-7d00-5d77-8da6-81eaa7db75c4', 'word_count': 613, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec114849-7d00-5d77-8da6-81eaa7db75c4'}, {'abstract': 'The clubby restaurant’s managing partner said it may reopen within a week.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/waverly-inn-is-closed-after-fire/', 'snippet': 'The clubby restaurant’s managing partner said it may reopen within a week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Waverly Inn and Garden is closed, after a fire in the basement early Monday evening. The clubby restaurant in Greenwich Village is likely to reopen within a week, said Emil Varda, the managing partner in the restaurant, which is also owned by Graydon Carter, the editor-in-chief of Vanity Fair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Waverly Inn Is Closed After Fire', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Graydon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich Village (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:36:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55c32da1-8d40-5c07-9b0d-3efcc5323f2d', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55c32da1-8d40-5c07-9b0d-3efcc5323f2d'}, {'abstract': 'What’s the right level of parental supervision for a child with a life online?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/following-your-children-online-how-much-is-too-much/', 'snippet': 'What’s the right level of parental supervision for a child with a life online?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I get a pitch from a P.R. person to cover some form of child-monitoring/Internet safety app, tool or device almost every day. Internet safety, however you define it, is both big business and a huge parental concern — and judging from the 230-plus comments so far on “Big Brother? No, It’s Parents” in The Times today, we’re not nearly done with\xa0 talking about how software can, and whether it should, help us monitor our children’s lives online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Following Your Children Online: How Much Is Too Much?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:36:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By KJ DELL'ANTONIA", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "DELL'ANTONIA", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/339191ec-a7fe-5e46-a2b7-064d474d3bbc', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/339191ec-a7fe-5e46-a2b7-064d474d3bbc'}, {'abstract': '“The Ahh Factor,” by Bruce Graham, and works by A. R Gurney and Neil LaBute highlight six plays about dealing with disabilities in “More of Our Parts,” at the Clurman Theater.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/theater/reviews/more-of-our-parts-six-short-plays-at-clurman-theater.html', 'snippet': '“The Ahh Factor,” by Bruce Graham, and works by A. R Gurney and Neil LaBute highlight six plays about dealing with disabilities in “More of Our Parts,” at the Clurman Theater.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are world premieres by famous playwrights in “More of Our Parts” at the Clurman Theater, among them works by the lord of the WASPs, A. R. Gurney, and the king of emotional brutality, Neil LaBute. Yet the wittiest script among these six short one-act plays about life with disabilities comes from a relative unknown, Bruce Graham, the Philadelphia playwright who did “Any Given Monday.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/SUB-MORE/SUB-MORE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/SUB-MORE/SUB-MORE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1913, 'width': 1465, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/SUB-MORE/SUB-MORE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/SUB-MORE/SUB-MORE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/SUB-MORE/SUB-MORE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiptoeing Past the Deaf', 'kicker': 'Theater Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tiptoeing Past the Deaf', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disabilities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sweet, Jeffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaBute, Neil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schambelan, Ike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Theater Breaking Through Barriers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gurney, A R', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brunstetter, Bekah', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'subsection_name': 'Theater Reviews', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f9cf054-b0f2-501a-9c55-48021528fd9b', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f9cf054-b0f2-501a-9c55-48021528fd9b'}, {'abstract': 'Ratings for the network’s prime-time shows plunged by 40 percent from a year ago; it was the network’s worst-ever performance in a second quarter.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/without-news-cnn-is-without-viewers/', 'snippet': 'Ratings for the network’s prime-time shows plunged by 40 percent from a year ago; it was the network’s worst-ever performance in a second quarter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The news for CNN has been bad for a long time, but it got especially bad in the second quarter of this year. Ratings for the network’s prime-time shows plunged by 40 percent from a year ago, and the network’s performance was its worst ever for a second quarter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Without News, CNN Is Without Viewers', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:43:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44a49e3f-346d-5bbc-b4f1-fd50cdb278fe', 'word_count': 456, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44a49e3f-346d-5bbc-b4f1-fd50cdb278fe'}, {'abstract': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel must know that dissolving the currency would cost Germany much more than maintaining it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/business/economy/why-germany-will-pay-up-to-save-the-euro.html', 'snippet': 'Chancellor Angela Merkel must know that dissolving the currency would cost Germany much more than maintaining it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To go by the pronouncements coming out of Germany over the last couple of weeks, you might naturally conclude that the euro is toast. Speaking before Parliament, Chancellor Angela Merkel broadly rejected “counterproductive” proposals to pool Europe’s resources to help floundering Mediterranean nations. Germany’s “strength is not infinite,” she stressed. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/02/29/business/eduardo-porter/eduardo-porter-thumbLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Germany Will Pay Up to Save the Euro', 'kicker': 'Economic Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany Will Pay Up To Save Euro', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euro (Currency)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:47:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eduardo Porter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eduardo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Porter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/caac1c61-fb8e-5aa0-aeff-f0784b5ae252', 'word_count': 1453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/caac1c61-fb8e-5aa0-aeff-f0784b5ae252'}, {'abstract': 'A study pokes holes in supply-side economic theory.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/no-income-tax-no-boost/', 'snippet': 'A study pokes holes in supply-side economic theory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past February, Oklahoma Governor Mary Fallin announced a plan to phase out her state’s income tax over ten years. “We’re going to have the most pro-growth tax system in the region,” she said, according to The Wall Street Journal. \xa0Lawmakers in Kansas and Missouri have also pushed to eliminate their state income taxes this year—convinced, like Ms. Fallin and like the majority of the Republican Party since the 1980s, that the best way to grow is to cut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Income Tax? No Boost.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fallin, Mary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:52:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/457e141f-85cc-5c77-a769-837af5578649', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/457e141f-85cc-5c77-a769-837af5578649'}, {'abstract': 'A children’s media researcher says the benefits of digital entertainment are often overlooked. Readers are invited to respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/opinion/invitation-to-a-dialogue-play-in-a-digital-age.html', 'snippet': 'A children’s media researcher says the benefits of digital entertainment are often overlooked. Readers are invited to respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/opinion/27ldialogue-img/27ldialogue-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 555, 'subType': 'jumbo'