er says it’s up to the Spurs and their doctors to decide whether he will play in the Olympics for France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.B.A.’s current relationship with international basketball competition is, in a word, complex.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Parker’s Injury Leaves Olympic Fate in Hands of Spurs', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Tony', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:55:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rob Mahoney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mahoney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4afe12f2-c7a4-5b2e-b776-36937ec67f97', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4afe12f2-c7a4-5b2e-b776-36937ec67f97'}, {'abstract': 'An exit strategy for disaffected Catholics who don’t have centuries to wait for reform.', 'web_url': 'https://keller.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/catholics-continued/', 'snippet': 'An exit strategy for disaffected Catholics who don’t have centuries to wait for reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My last column discussed an exit strategy for disaffected Catholics. The proposition was that Catholics who want a church more bighearted on issues like the role of women and the acceptance of gay love should consider looking elsewhere, because today’s Catholic hierarchy is stuck in a deep rut. The reaction was unusually plentiful and heartfelt, but it rolled in while I was on vacation with my family, mostly unplugged. This is an attempt to reckon with some of the feelings I seem to have aroused. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Catholics, Continued', 'kicker': 'Bill Keller', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T19:57:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df9058f6-6839-50de-8a9c-5c8b85626762', 'word_count': 1220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df9058f6-6839-50de-8a9c-5c8b85626762'}, {'abstract': 'Breaking down the News Corporation might show that both parts of the media conglomerate — its vast entertainment holdings and its smaller publishing arm — could yield a significant jump in shareholder value.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/valuing-a-news-corp-breakup/', 'snippet': 'Breaking down the News Corporation might show that both parts of the media conglomerate — its vast entertainment holdings and its smaller publishing arm — could yield a significant jump in shareholder value.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wall Street, it’s called the “Murdoch discount.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Valuing a News Corp. Breakup', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'pr