lled by two other major radio companies, the Cox Media Group and Emmis Communications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How does the biggest radio company in the country become bigger online? By inviting hundreds of competitors to join its aggregator app.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Notes: Clear Channel Signs Rivals’ Stations to Its App', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clear Channel Communications Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emmis Communications Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:11:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f60c2775-1773-5138-aed0-0ff92b298c33', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f60c2775-1773-5138-aed0-0ff92b298c33'}, {'abstract': 'The speech by Mohammad-Reza Rahimi, who blamed Judaism’s holiest book, the Talmud, for causing the global spread of illegal drugs, seemed bound to further isolate Iran just days before new sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/world/middleeast/irans-vice-president-rahimi-makes-anti-semitic-speech.html', 'snippet': 'The speech by Mohammad-Reza Rahimi, who blamed Judaism’s holiest book, the Talmud, for causing the global spread of illegal drugs, seemed bound to further isolate Iran just days before new sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran’s vice president delivered a baldly anti-Semitic speech on Tuesday at an international antidrug conference here, saying that the Talmud, a central text of Judaism, was responsible for the spread of illegal drugs around the world.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Vice President Makes Anti-Semitic Speech at Forum', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran’s Vice President Makes Anti-Semitic Speech at Forum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Talmud', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rahimi, Mohammad-Reza', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:11:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa93448a-e35e-598a-969a-fa96b27f9e92', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa93448a-e35e-598a-969a-fa96b27f9e92'}, {'abstract': 'About 1,000 jobs will be lost when the drug giant closes its Nutley, N.J., site.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/business/roche-to-shut-down-former-us-headquarters-after-83-years.html', 'snippet': 'About 1,000 jobs will be lost when the drug giant closes its Nutley, N.J., site.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roche, the Swiss pharmaceutical company, said Tuesday that it would shut down its site in Nutley, N.J., which served as its American headquarters for 80 years, in an effort to cut costs. About 1,000 jobs would be lost, the company said. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/business/Roche/Roche-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/business/Roche/Roche-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2012, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/business/Roche/Roche-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Roche to Shut Former U.S. Headquarters', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Roche to Shut Former U.S. Headquarters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roche Holding A G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:16:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cbbb635-10bf-5a15-b3b2-397350f0c284', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cbbb635-10bf-5a15-b3b2-397350f0c284'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Andy Ricker, owner of an acclaimed cluster of casual Thai eating and drinking places in Portland, Ore., expands his reach to a new restaurant, Pok Pok Ny.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/dining/reviews/pok-pok-ny-brooklyn-restaurant-review.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Andy Ricker, owner of an acclaimed cluster of casual Thai eating and drinking places in Portland, Ore., expands his reach to a new restaurant, Pok Pok Ny.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT first I didn’t notice the green chile paste at the center of the plate. I was in the backyard of a new Thai restaurant in Brooklyn called Pok Pok Ny (rhymes with “rock rock fly”), enjoying a deep communion with a grilled sausage that seemed to be everything anyone could want on a summer night. The sausage was rough-hewed and reddish, with little studs of melting pork fat and traces of galangal and white pepper that were flowery and spicy at the same time. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/dining/27REST1_SPAN/27REST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/27/dining/27REST1_SPAN/27REST1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/dining/27REST1_SPAN/27REST1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/dining/27REST1_SPAN/27REST1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/dining/27REST1_SPAN/27REST1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'w