/06/26/a-mock-trial-over-genocide-meant-to-help-students-face-history/', 'snippet': 'On a recent Wednesday morning, at the Bronx Hall of Justice, Augustin Bizimungu, the former Rwandan army chief, was being grilled by a prosecutor over his role in the Rwandan genocide. Luckily for him, the stakes at this second trial were much low...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Mock Trial Over Genocide, Meant to Help Students Face History', 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:40:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By DANIEL KRIEGER', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'KRIEGER', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1d31b71-1927-5a08-a261-e2d7dee19330', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1d31b71-1927-5a08-a261-e2d7dee19330'}, {'abstract': 'The Landmarks Preservation Commission added 190 buildings to an Upper West Side Historic District, established a historic district in Crown Heights and named three Lower Manhattan buildings as landmarks.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/hundreds-of-buildings-gain-landmark-protection/', 'snippet': 'The Landmarks Preservation Commission added 190 buildings to an Upper West Side Historic District, established a historic district in Crown Heights and named three Lower Manhattan buildings as landmarks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Landmarks Preservation Commission closed its last meeting of the 2012 fiscal year with the addition of 190 buildings to the Riverside-West End Historic District on the Upper West Side, the designation of a new historic district in Crown Heights and the naming of three buildings in Lower Manhattan as landmarks.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Than 200 Buildings Gain Landmark Protection', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bowery Mission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Landmarks Preservation Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Crown Heights (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:44:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Edwards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Edwards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/927b3a19-9f3d-5c1e-9607-c8001850dccd', 'word_count': 317, 'uri': 'nyt://article/927b3a19-9f3d-5c1e-9607-c8001850dccd'}, {'abstract': 'Facing a torrent of criticism, the school’s trustees made a stunning turnabout Tuesday, voting to reinstate President Teresa A. Sullivan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/education/university-of-virginia-reinstates-ousted-president.html', 'snippet': 'Facing a torrent of criticism, the school’s trustees made a stunning turnabout Tuesday, voting to reinstate President Teresa A. Sullivan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHARLOTTESVILLE, Va. — Facing a torrent of criticism, the University of Virginia trustees made a stunning turnabout on Tuesday, voting unanimously to reinstate the president they had forced to resign over concerns that the university was not adapting fast enough to financial and technological pressures.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', '