'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:46:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d825fb66-3d96-5a70-9ff6-d44393c3851a', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d825fb66-3d96-5a70-9ff6-d44393c3851a'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan Lochte decided not to swim in the 100-meter backstroke at the Olympics in London.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/lochte-wont-compete-in-100-meter-backstroke-at-olympics/', 'snippet': 'Ryan Lochte decided not to swim in the 100-meter backstroke at the Olympics in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA – Ryan Lochte finished third in the 100-meter backstroke at the 2008 United States Olympic trials, missing a berth on the Beijing-bound team by one place. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lochte Won’t Compete in 100-Meter Backstroke at Olympics', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grevers, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:49:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc9f7bad-eacb-5452-929f-e14f28624a4b', 'word_count': 187, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc9f7bad-eacb-5452-929f-e14f28624a4b'}, {'abstract': '“Beasts of the Southern Wild,” a passionate and unruly explosion of Americana, winks at skepticism, laughs at sober analysis and stares down criticism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/movies/beasts-of-the-southern-wild-directed-by-benh-zeitlin.html', 'snippet': '“Beasts of the Southern Wild,” a passionate and unruly explosion of Americana, winks at skepticism, laughs at sober analysis and stares down criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hushpuppy, the 6-year-old heroine of “Beasts of the Southern Wild,” has a smile to charm fish out of the water and a scowl so fierce it can stop monsters in their tracks. The movie, a passionate and unruly explosion of Americana, directed by Benh Zeitlin, winks at skepticism, laughs at sober analysis and stares down criticism. Made on a shoestring by a resourceful New Orleans-based collective, it is animated by the same spirit of freedom it sets out to celebrate. If, as the Fourth of July approaches, you find yourself craving an antidote to anger and cynicism, a bracing reminder of the meaning of independence, and a helping of homegrown art to go with your hamburgers and watermelon, then this may be just what you need.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s the Man of This Swamp', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She’s the Man of This Swamp', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zeitlin, Benh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beasts of the Southern Wild (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallis, Quvenzhane', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Dwight', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T20:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7c84517-93b8-533a-85b6-623cd160e5c4', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7c84517-93b8-533a-85b6-623cd160e5c4'}, {'abstract': 'The Department of Defense recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/us/us-military-deaths-in-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'The Department of Defense recently confirmed the deaths of the following Americans who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Department of Defense has identified 2,007 American service members who have died as a part of the Afghan war and related operations. It confirmed the deaths of the following Americans recently: ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Names of the Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Names of the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:04:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b15a625-9ee1-5fa6-8cbe-71b3496bed72', 'word_count': 105, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b15a625-9ee1-5fa6-8cbe-71b3496bed72'}, {'abstract': 'Microsoft, tablets, and the theory of the firm.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/the-hart-of-the-matter/', 'snippet': 'Microsoft, tablets, and the theory of the firm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'And now for something completely different: I haven’t seen anyone point this out, but the very interesting Times story on why Microsoft is building its own tablet was a perfect illustration of Oliver Hart’s theory of the firm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hart of the Matter', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:06:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c17514aa-5303-554a-b5ab-1048eae71528', 'word_count': 213, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c17514aa-5303-554a-b5ab-1048eae71528'}, {'abstract': 'The importance of not going too fast.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/deleveraging-monetary-policy-and-fiscal-policy-a-further-note/', 'snippet': 'The importance of not going too fast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I wrote the other day about the nature of our depression, and how Very Serious People seem determined to block all useful responses — all in the name of sound policy, of course. While I’m at it, however, I realized that thinking about the depression this way may offer a better, or at least different, answer to the question that originally inspired both my Sam and Janet post and my work with Gauti Eggertsson: How can the answer to a crisis brought on by too much debt be more debt?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deleveraging, Monetary Policy, and Fiscal Policy: A Further Note', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:07:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe41c2fc-4157-5eb1-82a7-fbf2ae91d0ed', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe41c2fc-4157-5eb1-82a7-fbf2ae91d0ed'}, {'abstract': 'An ordered end to the institute’s international focus ignites concerns that its collaborations with American arts institutions could be in jeopardy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/romanian-cultural-institutes-new-mandate-draws-protests-in-europe-and-u-s/', 'snippet': 'An ordered end to the institute’s international focus ignites concerns that its collaborations with American arts institutions could be in jeopardy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past five years or so, the Romanian Cultural Institute has become an important force in global cultural exchanges, promoting writers, artists and especially the critically acclaimed cinema movement known as the Romanian New Wave. But the coalition government that recently came to power in Romania has ordered an end to that international focus as it tightens its political control over the institute, actions that have set off protests among arts groups throughout Europe and the United States.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romanian Cultural Institute’s New Mandate Draws Protests in Europe and United States', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romanians Rein In Arts Institute', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:08:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb845856-9a57-5229-a10c-a814c86428cf', 'word_count': 975, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb845856-9a57-5229-a10c-a814c86428cf'}, {'abstract': 'Facebook says its tweaks to the settings for the display of people’s e-mail addresses was not a “privacy” change but rather a “visibility setting” change. Some people might disagree with that interpretation.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/for-facebook-visibility-is-not-privacy-while-others-disagree/', 'snippet': 'Facebook says its tweaks to the settings for the display of people’s e-mail addresses was not a “privacy” change but rather a “visibility setting” change. Some people might disagree with that interpretation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I called Facebook on Monday to ask why the company had changed the settings  for the display of people’s e-mail addresses without their permission, potentially violating users’ privacy, I was told that the swap was not a “privacy” change, but rather a “visibility setting” change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Facebook, the Semantics of Visibility vs. Privacy', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:09:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d2f7635-349a-5f5a-be7f-540c96bcc2aa', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d2f7635-349a-5f5a-be7f-540c96bcc2aa'}, {'abstract': 'Berlioz’s “Troyens” has both inspired and confounded some of the best directors in the field, and David McVicar’s production uses updated imagery to tell the story.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/arts/music/les-troyens-at-the-royal-opera-house-in-london.html', 'snippet': 'Berlioz’s “Troyens” has both inspired and confounded some of the best directors in the field, and David McVicar’s production uses updated imagery to tell the story.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A lot was riding on the new production of Berlioz’s epic opera “Les Troyens” that opened at the Royal Opera, Covent Garden, on Monday night. This staging by the director David McVicar is a co-production with the Vienna State Opera, Teatro Alla Scala in Milan and the San Francisco Opera. The Royal Opera’s “Troyens” is also a major event in the London 2012 Festival, and it will be shown in movie theaters worldwide in November.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/troyens/troyens-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/troyens/troyens-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/arts/troyens/troyens-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 