'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thai Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ricker, Andy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pok Pok Ny (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:50:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61be1ff3-da60-5fd7-9e59-ba60a6c6ab17', 'word_count': 1226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61be1ff3-da60-5fd7-9e59-ba60a6c6ab17'}, {'abstract': 'Grigor Dimitrov, whose nickname is “Baby Fed,” showed new maturity in his upset of Kevin Anderson at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/in-dmitrov-winning-echoes-of-federer/', 'snippet': 'Grigor Dimitrov, whose nickname is “Baby Fed,” showed new maturity in his upset of Kevin Anderson at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rapidly improving Bulgarian Grigor Dimitrov, nicknamed Baby Fed by tennis observers, made a telling comment in his news conference after his upset win over 32nd-seeded Kevin Anderson. When asked about comparisons between his game and Roger Federer’s, Dimitrov, while acknowledging the “great compliment,” gave an honest assessment of his game: “I’ve not got to the second week of a Grand Slam yet and have not won an ATP event or reached the top 20 … I need to progress a lot and can’t cut any corners.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Dimitrov, Winning Echoes of Federer', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Kevin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Federer, Roger', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Assn of Tennis Professionals', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:50:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c2b3a80-58e7-54f0-8566-14b13664687b', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c2b3a80-58e7-54f0-8566-14b13664687b'}, {'abstract': 'TV ratings for the four quarterfinals at the championships were up 31 percent on ESPN.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/euro-2012-espn-scores-big-ratings/', 'snippet': 'TV ratings for the four quarterfinals at the championships were up 31 percent on ESPN.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly three million people hunkered down last Sunday to watch on ESPN as Italy eliminated England in a penalty-kick shootout in a quarterfinal match in Kiev, Ukraine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Euro 2012: ESPN Scores Big Ratings', 'kicker': 'Goal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-26T21:54:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1634372f-0516-5086-9bfd-bec2c531323b', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1634372f-0516-5086-9bfd-bec2c531323b'}, {'abstract': 'In a little over two hours on Tuesday night, Sotheby’s managed to sell $108 million worth of contemporary art, another testament to the breadth and depth of interest in works by well-known names like Basquiat, Bacon, Twombly and Warhol.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/sothebys-contemporary-sale-makes-108-million/', 'snippet': 'In a little over two hours on Tuesday night, Sotheby’s managed to sell $108 million worth of contemporary art, another testament to the breadth and depth of interest in works by well-known names like Basquiat, Bacon, Twombly and Warhol.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In a little over two hours on Tuesday night, Sotheby’s managed to sell $108 million worth of contemporary art, another testament to the breadth and depth of interest in works by well-known names like Basquiat, Bacon, Twombly and Warhol. The auction house had packed the sale with 79 paintings, sculptures, drawings and prints, mostly by artists who have brought top prices in recent seasons. But while the salesroom was filled with an international crowd of dealers and collectors, the evening could best be described as more solid than exciting. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sotheby’s Contemporary Sale Makes $108 Million', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Damien', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Richter, Gerhard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 6, 'ma