e': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74ce5725-a9c0-5cf4-8aab-8d44bd062a02', 'word_count': 1578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74ce5725-a9c0-5cf4-8aab-8d44bd062a02'}, {'abstract': 'The Federal Reserve and the European Central Bank cannot wait for politicians to boost the slowing global economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/opinion/time-for-bankers-to-intervene.html', 'snippet': 'The Federal Reserve and the European Central Bank cannot wait for politicians to boost the slowing global economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Bernanke, the chairman of the Federal Reserve, and Mario Draghi, the president of the European Central Bank, have both argued correctly that the slowing global economy requires decisive action by political leaders. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Time for Bankers to Intervene', 'kicker': 'Editorial ', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time for Bankers to Intervene', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Draghi, Mario', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Monetary Union', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T01:17:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7ba97e3-040d-5d87-94b7-dabdbbb74c04', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7ba97e3-040d-5d87-94b7-dabdbbb74c04'}, {'abstract': 'One of the peculiarities of New York City is the proximity of our geographical past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/opinion/the-old-neighborhood.html', 'snippet': 'One of the peculiarities of New York City is the proximity of our geographical past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’ve lived for long in New York City, chances are you’ve lived in several different places. On the map of where we dwell now is also where we used to dwell, just across the park, a borough away, a few subway stops farther north or south. That is one of the peculiarities of this city — the proximity of our geographical past. Some people move from Ohio to Oregon. We move from 93rd to 13th, from Alphabet City to Carroll Gardens, all over town. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Old Neighborhood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T01:19:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fc607e4-0d88-5e0f-89af-b522fea392f3', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fc607e4-0d88-5e0f-89af-b522fea392f3'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Schul