com/2012/06/26/in-rizzo-cubs-hope-they-have-a-player-to-build-around/', 'snippet': 'First baseman Anthony Rizzo was called up Monday night from Class AAA Iowa, making his debut with the Cubs in the No. 3 spot in the batting order against the Mets.', 'lead_paragraph': '12:06 a.m. | Updated CHICAGO — Wrigley Field, the Friendly Confines, has been glum this year. The Cubs are a major league-worst 25-48, taking their lumps as Theo Epstein’s new regime promises a future of “sustained success.” Tuesday, though, the cloud of despair was lifted — at least for one day — to reveal, perhaps, a hint of that future. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rizzo, Cubs Hope They Have a Player to Build Around', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T02:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2849e9c5-d79e-5b9e-9729-3057edf5d155', 'word_count': 616, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2849e9c5-d79e-5b9e-9729-3057edf5d155'}, {'abstract': 'DuPont, which introduced a herbicide linked to the deaths of thousands of trees, said requests for compensation are running into the hundreds of millions of dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/us/dupont-says-claims-over-herbicide-hit-the-millions.html', 'snippet': 'DuPont, which introduced a herbicide linked to the deaths of thousands of trees, said requests for compensation are running into the hundreds of millions of dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DuPont, which introduced a herbicide last year that was later linked to the deaths of  thousands of trees, has begun processing claims for compensation that are running into the hundreds of millions of dollars, company officials said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/subHERBICIDE/subHERBICIDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 921, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/subHERBICIDE/subHERBICIDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1916, 'width': 1724, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/subHERBICIDE/subHERBICIDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/27/us/subHERBICIDE/subHERBICIDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/subHERBICIDE/subHERBICIDE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'DuPont Says Claims Over Herbicide Are Rising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'DuPont Says Claims Over Herbicide Are Rising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trees and Shrubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lawns', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defoliants and Herbicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DuPont Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T02:56:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8571cab9-4d49-5f94-b7d2-831b6628a57c', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8571cab9-4d49-5f94-b7d2-831b6628a57c'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Bootsma, 18, set a girls 17-18 national age-group record of 59.10 seconds. It lasted less than five minutes. In the next heat, the 17-year-old Missy Franklin swam a 59.06.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/in-the-womens-100-back-a-record-is-set-and-quickly-eclipsed/', 'snippet': 'Rachel Bootsma, 18, set a girls 17-18 national age-group record of 59.10 seconds. It lasted less than five minutes. In the next heat, the 17-year-old Missy Franklin swam a 59.06.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — In the first semifinal heat of the women’s 100-meter backstroke, Rachel Bootsma, 18, set a girls’ 17-18 national age-group record of 59.10 seconds. It lasted less than five minutes. In the next heat, the 17-year-old Missy Franklin swam a 59.06.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Women’s 100 Backstroke, a Record Is Set and Quickly Eclipsed', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coughlin, Natalie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Franklin, Missy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T02:58:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78c48156-778e-51f8-889a-fb98708c679d', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78c48156-778e-51f8-889a-fb98708c679d'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 27, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/pageoneplus/corrections-june-27.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 27, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: June 27', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T03:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95a2b83d-9a7e-55be-bdd3-3d3d10c2a0de', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95a2b83d-9a7e-55be-bdd3-3d3d10c2a0de'}, {'abstract': 'The attorney general of New York is investigating contributions to tax-exempt groups that are heavily involved in political campaigns, focusing on the U.S. Chamber of Commerce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/us/politics/new-york-attorney-general-enters-campaign-finance-fray.html', 'snippet': 'The attorney general of New York is investigating contributions to tax-exempt groups that are heavily involved in political campaigns, focusing on the U.S. Chamber of Commerce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Attorney General Eric T. Schneiderman of New York has begun investigating contributions to tax-exempt groups that are heavily involved in political campaigns, focusing on a case involving the U.S. Chamber of Commerce, which has been one of the largest outside groups seeking to influence recent elections but is not required to disclose its donors. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inquiry Looks Into a Shield for Donors in Elections', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inquiry Looks Into a Shield For Donors In Elections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Chamber of Commerce', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Chamber Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Starr Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T03:01:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/537208c0-973e-52e7-92e7-e6f8d4165e35', 'word_count': 880, 'uri': 'nyt://article/537208c0-973e-52e7-92e7-e6f8d4165e35'}, {'abstract': 'A report finds that the chairman of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission did not overstep his authority in response to the Fukushima Daiichi meltdown last year in Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/us/investigation-finds-no-violations-by-nuclear-head.html', 'snippet': 'A report finds that the chairman of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission did not overstep his authority in response to the Fukushima Daiichi meltdown last year in Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A report by the inspector general of the Nuclear Regulatory Commission, released Tuesday, has found that the commission’s chairman did not exceed his authority in directing his agency’s response to the Fukushima Daiichi meltdown last year in Japan, despite his colleagues’ complaints over his management. The chairman, Gregory B. Jaczko, has said he will resign as soon as a successor is sworn in, probably next week. The inspector general has investigated a variety of actions, but the new report does not find any clear violations. It said Dr. Jaczko had broken with past practice by seeking to change the recommendations of the commission staff, and that he limited staff communications with the other four commissioners in a way that “was inconsistent with the commissioners’ expectations.” His behavior was “not supportive of an open and collaborative work environment,” the report said. Dr. Jaczko denied any wrongdoing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investigation Finds No Violations by Nuclear Head', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investigation Finds No Violations By Nuclear Head', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Japan Earthquake and Tsunami (2011)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Regulatory Commission', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaczko, Gregory B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T03:13:45+0000', 'documen