ary challenge from a Tea Party-backed insurgent candidate on Tuesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/us/politics/hatch-overcomes-challenge-in-republican-primary-in-utah.html', 'snippet': 'The six-term Republican fended off a primary challenge from a Tea Party-backed insurgent candidate on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALT LAKE CITY — Senator Orrin G. Hatch, a six-term Utah Republican, fended off a primary challenge from a Tea Party-backed insurgent candidate on Tuesday, a result that showed the power of money, organization and incumbency to overcome grass-roots anger at the Washington establishment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/us/UTAH/UTAH-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hatch Overcomes Challenge in Republican Primary in Utah', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hatch Overcomes Challenge in Republican Primary in Utah', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Primaries and Caucuses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liljenquist, Daniel R', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T03:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b34f8373-7925-588b-8a9b-03699f50258b', 'word_count': 566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b34f8373-7925-588b-8a9b-03699f50258b'}, {'abstract': 'No matter how they feel about Obamacare, conservatives should welcome the left’s rejection of activist judges.', 'web_url': 'https://campaignstops.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/26/the-liberal-embrace-of-judicial-restraint/', 'snippet': 'No matter how they feel about Obamacare, conservatives should welcome the left’s rejection of activist judges.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a great pleasure, in this week when the entire political world is hanging on the Supreme Court’s health care ruling, to welcome so many liberals to a cause