], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af226283-2251-5994-84e8-4c4e29c4c1e7', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af226283-2251-5994-84e8-4c4e29c4c1e7'}, {'abstract': 'MultiFunding has introduced a system that grades every bank in the country on its small-business lending. Not everyone approves.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/which-banks-really-want-to-lend-to-small-businesses/', 'snippet': 'MultiFunding has introduced a system that grades every bank in the country on its small-business lending. Not everyone approves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On any given day at MultiFunding, I talk with a dozen or so bankers. As we work together to close loans, they demand precise information as they try to reach lending decisions. After all, precise information is what banking is all about.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grading Banks on Their Small-Business Lending', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Sun', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank of America Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Financial Services Roundtable', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huffington Post', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T11:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ami Kassar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ami', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kassar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dcde4c8-fcf6-5299-b5cf-3eb2aa771822', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dcde4c8-fcf6-5299-b5cf-3eb2aa771822'}, {'abstract': 'In this week’s links: Sartre’s problem with intellectuals, an algorithmic map of philosophical influence, and a copy of Aristotle’s works (its medieval, and it’s got pictures) on display.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/stone-links-a-constellation-of-philosophers/', 'snippet': 'In this week’s links: Sartre’s problem with intellectuals, an algorithmic map of philosophical influence, and a copy of Aristotle’s works (its medieval, and it’s got pictures) on display.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is an intriguing map of philosophical space at the statistics blog Drunks and Lampposts, drawn in terms of the field’s leading lights. The map looks much like a chart of the heavens, but lines of influence are what define the size and position of each node. The raw data was culled from the “influenced by” section for the pages of all the philosophers listed in Wikipedia — using an algorithm. The images are startling, and the map does seem to give many of the big thinkers what seems to be intuitively the right size and location (though one does notice Descartes’ “star” must be too small relative to his influence). But it is unclear how effective the algorithm is at saying something meaningful about the history of philosophy and, correlatively, the history of ideas. One also wonders what a similar map drawing on the data in, say, The Stanford Encylopedia of Philosophy, would look like. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stone Links: A Constellation of Philosophers', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Review of Books', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T11:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark de Silva', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Silva', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44586824-bf47-5a25-850b-6be25cc02d46', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44586824-bf47-5a25-850b-6be25cc02d46'}, {'abstract': 'Glencore International’s planned combination with Xstrata faces a new obstacle after Qatar Holding, which owns a large stake in Xstrata, asked for the bid to be increased.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/glencores-deal-for-xstrata-under-threat/', 'snippet': 'Glencore International’s planned combination with Xstrata faces a new obstacle after Qatar Holding, which owns a large stake in Xstrata, asked for the bid to be increased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Glencore International’s $24 billion deal with Xstrata is under threat after Qatar Holding asked Glencore to increase its bid amid mounting opposition to executive pay arrangements.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Glencore’s $24 Billion Deal for Xstrata Under Threat', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T11:14:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 