 Werewolf” features a female of the species trying to rescue her son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glen Duncan’s novel “The Last Werewolf” was narrated by a 200-year-old man/wolf named Jake Marlowe. Jake’s creepy condition forced him to eat a human being every month or perish, but otherwise he was a charming fellow. In The New York Times Book Review, Justin Cronin said the book “plays out in splendid good fun, bouncing from one James Bondian locale to another, bon mot to bon mot, the text saturated with literary and cultural references.” Mr. Duncan’s new book is a sequel, “Talulla Rising,” about a female werewolf desperate to rescue her newborn son from a pack of vampires. In a recent interview via e-mail, Mr. Duncan discussed his relationship to the paranormal, the appeal of unsympathetic characters and why psychotherapy is not for him. Below are excerpts from the conversation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Werewolves, Vampires, Shrinks and Other Terrors: Glen Duncan Talks About ‘Talulla Rising’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Word With: Glen Duncan: Writing a Werewolf Myth, and Making It His Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duncan, Glen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T14:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5139b6f4-285a-59cc-93b2-250d024813b5', 'word_count': 1132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5139b6f4-285a-59cc-93b2-250d024813b5'}, {'abstract': 'For the second straight year, no women were chosen for the Hockey Hall of Fame. A possible reason: No women were on the selection committee.', 'web_url': 'https://slapshot.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/no-women-for-the-hall-again/', 'snippet': 'For the second straight year, no women were chosen for the Hockey Hall of Fame. A possible reason: No women were on the selection committee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tuesday’s Hockey Hall of Fame election in Toronto sent four very worthy former players to the induction ceremonies next November: Joe Sakic, Mats Sundin, Adam Oates and Pavel Bure.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Women for the Hall. Again.', 'kicker': 'Slap Shot', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bye, Karyn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Granato, Cammi', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Angela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hockey Hall of Fame', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T14:58:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1b220a8-0e2c-529f-b53c-9db80eb83891', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1b220a8-0e2c-529f-b53c-9db80eb83891'}, {'abstract': 'Wickr, a new smartphone app, secures text messages, photos and videos using military-grade encryption and never stored. The service camouflages user names and other identifiable information, such as a smartphone’s identification number, by appending several random digits to each value, then mashing them up with a mathematical algorithm, a process security experts refer to as “salting” and “hashing.”', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/an-app-that-encrypts-shreds-hashes-and-salts/', 'snippet': 'Wickr, a new smartphone app, secures text messages, photos and videos using military-grade encryption and never stored. The service camouflages user names and other identifiable information, such as a smartphone’s identification number, by appendi...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to mobile apps and social networks, the devil, increasingly, is in the default settings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/blogs/wickr/wickr-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 320, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/blogs/wickr/wickr-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 320, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An App That Encrypts, Shreds, Hashes and Salts', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T14:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://a