n and threatening to spit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: A ‘Henry V’ That Doesn’t Take Sides', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dromgoole, Dominic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shakespeare, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Shakespeare's Globe Theater", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T15:15:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35ccc73f-ea0d-5e5c-8d13-5278e31cbee1', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35ccc73f-ea0d-5e5c-8d13-5278e31cbee1'}, {'abstract': 'The sale fetched the second-highest price ever paid for a Lincoln-signed proclamation.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/copy-of-emancipation-proclamation-sells-for-nearly-2-1-million/', 'snippet': 'The sale fetched the second-highest price ever paid for a Lincoln-signed proclamation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rare copy of the Emancipation Proclamation, the document signed by President Abraham Lincoln during the Civil War that freed tens of thousands of slaves and laid the foundation for the end of slavery, sold for $2.085 million at auction in New York City on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Copy of Emancipation Proclamation Sells for Nearly $2.1 Million', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Copy of Proclamation Fetches $2.1 Million', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emancipation Proclamation (1863)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Robert Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carlyle Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T15:18:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7379b9a6-c46c-519c-a0c8-5e6037e83659', 'word_count': 444, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7379b9a6-c46c-519c-a0c8-5e6037e83659'}, {'abstract': 'Politicians and economic regulators implicated in Spain’s economic meltdown have rebranded themselves as exponents of financial responsibility. This is rhetorical bait and switch.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/the-survivors-of-spains-rush-to-ruin/', 'snippet': 'Politicians and economic regulators implicated in Spain’s economic meltdown have rebranded themselves as exponents of financial responsibility. This is rhetorical bait and switch.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — While international observers gawked over the size of the Spanish-bank bailout announced on Monday, the indignados were calling for justicia para rato, literally “a moment of justice.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Survivors of Spain’s Rush to Ruin', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major