': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67672761-5daa-5e31-9247-3a49f0de5211', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67672761-5daa-5e31-9247-3a49f0de5211'}, {'abstract': 'The novelist, screenwriter and director, who died Tuesday, was a passionate foodie.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/nora-ephron-never-forgot-the-food/', 'snippet': 'The novelist, screenwriter and director, who died Tuesday, was a passionate foodie.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The writer Nora Ephron, who died Tuesday night, wore many hats, all of them jauntily. She was a screenwriter, feminist, journalist, humorist and passionate (but absolutely unsnobbish) foodie, long before the term existed. Even when she wore those other hats and became a Big Hollywood Screenwriter, for food lovers, she was always one of us, endlessly entertained by restaurants, cooking, cookbooks, the whole crazy salad of foodie life. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nora Ephron Never Forgot the Food', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ephron, Nora', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T16:30:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Moskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25f45650-f1e6-5232-8f5c-30facfee35a3', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25f45650-f1e6-5232-8f5c-30facfee35a3'}, {'abstract': 'Philipp Humm, chief executive of T-Mobile USA, has resigned from his position, said Deutsche Telekom, the company that owns the carrier. The company said he planned to pursue a new career and spend more time with his family in Europe.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/head-of-t-mobile-usa-resigns/', 'snippet': 'Philipp Humm, chief executive of T-Mobile USA, has resigned from his position, said Deutsche Telekom, the company that owns the carrier. The company said he planned to pursue a new career and spend more time with his family in Europe.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Philipp Humm, chief executive of T-Mobile USA, has resigned from his position, Deutsche Telekom, the company that owns the carrier, said on Wednesday. The company said he planned to pursue a new career and spend more time with his family in Europe. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Head of T-Mobile USA Resigns', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Humm, Philipp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T-Mobile', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T16:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dacf8647-cc82-547c-a140-cb0651ab94d1', 'word_count': 99, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dacf8647-cc82-547c-a140-cb0651ab94d1'}, {'abstract': 'Iran, the strongest regional ally of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria, and Saudi Arabia, a prominent supporter of Mr. Assad’s enemies, will be absent from a meeting in Geneva on Saturday to revive a paralyzed peace plan for Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/world/middleeast/annan-to-convene-group-on-syria-minus-iran-and-saudi-arabia.html', 'snippet': 'Iran, the strongest regional ally of President Bashar al-Assad of Syria, and Saudi Arabia, a prominent supporter of Mr. Assad’s enemies, will be absent from a meeting in Geneva on Saturday to revive a paralyzed peace plan for Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Kofi Annan, the special Syria representative from the United Nations and the Arab League whose paralyzed peace plan is in danger of collapse, announced in a statement on Wednesday that he was convening an “action group” meeting of influential countries here on Saturday in an effort to revive the plan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Talks Won’t Include the Saudis or Iranians', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria Talks Won’t Include The Saudis Or Iranians', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANNAN, KOFI', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T16:33:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce and Rick Gladsto