.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/budget-woes-prompt-cuts-at-seattle-opera/', 'snippet': 'Beginning in 2004, the company will present four operas instead of five.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Seattle Opera says an anticipated $1 million budget shortfall this season will mean cuts in salaries and staff and a reshaping of its programming, with a four-opera season instead of five beginning in 2014. Opera company officials said in a press release issued Tuesday night after a board meeting that a difficult economy, along with a drop in subscription sales and major donations, have contributed to its fiscal woes. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Budget Woes Prompt Cuts at Seattle Opera', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuts at Seattle Opera', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Seattle Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T17:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71431c5d-06bd-5288-8527-f03b1b095aef', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71431c5d-06bd-5288-8527-f03b1b095aef'}, {'abstract': 'What we’re reading (and watching) now, from coverage of the men’s shows in Milan to a behind-the-scenes video on Carine Roitfeld’s new magazine.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/fashion-news-were-reading-now-9/', 'snippet': 'What we’re reading (and watching) now, from coverage of the men’s shows in Milan to a behind-the-scenes video on Carine Roitfeld’s new magazine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Catch up on what’s going on with the men in Milan. Here is complete coverage of Milan Fashion Week Spring 2013.Go backstage in Milan with T Magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion News We’re Reading Now', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T17:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86382a95-c593-538b-b7ec-fee3635ad4a3', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86382a95-c593-538b-b7ec-fee3635ad4a3'}, {'abstract': 'Australopithecus sediba apparently lived on a diet of leaves, fruits, wood and bark, scientists report, while other hominins in Africa mainly consumed grasses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/science/australopithecus-sediba-preferred-forest-foods-fossil-teeth-suggest.html', 'snippet': 'Australopithecus sediba apparently lived on a diet of leaves, fruits, wood and bark, scientists report, while other hominins in Africa mainly consumed grasses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost two million years after their last meals, two members of a prehuman species in southern Africa left traces in their teeth of what they had eaten then, as well as over a lifetime of foraging. Scientists were surprised to find that these hominins apparently lived almost exclusively on a diet of leaves, fruits, wood and bark.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/science/28diet1/28diet1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 680, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo'