ured left ankle.', 'lead_paragraph': '3:40 p.m. | Updated Andy Pettitte, who at 40 has been as dependable as any Yankees starter this season, fractured his left ankle in a game against the Cleveland Indians on Wednesday and will be out for at least six weeks, the Yankees said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Injured Pettitte Will Be Out at Least Six Weeks', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T19:06:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed17b4e9-d63c-531a-b180-39c3b73c144e', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed17b4e9-d63c-531a-b180-39c3b73c144e'}, {'abstract': '“Orphans” is best remembered in New York as a critically acclaimed hit Off Broadway in 1985, starring John Mahoney (“Frasier”) as Harold and Terry Kinney and Kevin Anderson as the brothers, Treat and Phillip.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/alec-baldwin-returning-to-broadway-in-spring-2013/', 'snippet': '“Orphans” is best remembered in New York as a critically acclaimed hit Off Broadway in 1985, starring John Mahoney (“Frasier”) as Harold and Terry Kinney and Kevin Anderson as the brothers, Treat and Phillip.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After seven seasons playing the charismatic, controlling network executive  Jack Donaghy on the NBC comedy “30 Rock,” Alec Baldwin will return to Broadway in spring 2013 in a much darker show – but in a role that is no less charismatic or controlling. Mr. Baldwin will portray Harold, a mobster who is kidnapped and held by two troubled brothers in Lyle Kessler’s 1983 drama “Orphans,” the show’s producers said on Wednesday. The play will be directed by the Tony Award winner Daniel Sullivan (“The Columnist,” “Proof”), who is also staging a Broadway revival of “Glengarry Glen Ross” this fall.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alec Baldwin Returning to Broadway in Spring 2013', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Broadway Return For Alec Baldwin', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, Alec', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Daniel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Steppenwolf Theatre Co', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T19:06:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe2835df-4869-5680-8287-43ac3c17ac50', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe2835df-4869-5680-8287-43ac3c17ac50'}, {'abstract': 'Service speed remains one of the game’s talking points, but it also remains one of the least reliable measures of excellence, in part because huge servers do not necessarily make great players.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/sports/tennis/28iht-serve28.html', 'snippet': 'Service speed remains one of the game’s tal