251-b96b-5669-b784-c2d6cfcfe927'}, {'abstract': 'A claim by the Syrian government that armed rebels executed journalists working for a pro-government channel provoked debate about whether reporters whose work aides the autocratic government might be considered legitimate targets.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/attack-on-pro-assad-television-studio-raises-questions-on-rules-of-war/', 'snippet': 'A claim by the Syrian government that armed rebels executed journalists working for a pro-government channel provoked debate about whether reporters whose work aides the autocratic government might be considered legitimate targets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — As my colleagues Rod Nordland, Nick Cumming-Bruce and Alan Cowell report, Syria said Wednesday that rebels stormed a pro-government television station in a Damascus suburb, killing journalists and blowing up the station, in a predawn raid. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack on Pro-Assad Television Studio Raises Questions on Rules of War', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Propaganda', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Free Syrian Army', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North Atlantic Treaty Organization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2