'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a10ca1f3-a697-5f05-87c9-e9b69ad3af76', 'word_count': 1291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a10ca1f3-a697-5f05-87c9-e9b69ad3af76'}, {'abstract': 'With his second-round defeat on Wednesday, Philipp Petzschner has now blown two-set leads in all four Grand Slam tournaments.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/maybe-petzschner-cant-deal-with-success/', 'snippet': 'With his second-round defeat on Wednesday, Philipp Petzschner has now blown two-set leads in all four Grand Slam tournaments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men’s tennis is experiencing an age of unprecedented record-setting and players who are able to play equally well on all surfaces, making the present into what some are calling a golden age for the sport. While the surefire Hall of Famers Rafael Nadal, Roger Federer and Novak Djokovic contend for a Grand Slam, Philipp Petzschner of Germany made his own sort of history at Wimbledon on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Maybe Petzschner Can’t Deal With Success', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petzschner, Philipp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T22:16:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/802865c5-a8e8-58b0-a262-b92c104b3adf', 'word_count': 625, 'uri': 'nyt://article/802865c5-a8e8-58b0-a262-b92c104b3adf'}, {'abstract': 'In overriding the governor’s veto, the state legislature makes New Hampshire the latest state to require that voters present a picture ID to vote.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/27/n-h-approves-voter-id-law/', 'snippet': 'In overriding the governor’s veto, the state legislature makes New Hampshire the latest state to require that voters present a picture ID to vote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New Hampshire legislature on Wednesday overrode Gov. John Lynch’s veto of a voter ID bill, making it the latest state to require that voters present photo identification at the polls. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.H. Approves Voter ID Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T22:18:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c2071c7-1c9d-51d0-8d00-0527ce5b210a', 'word_count': 316, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c2071c7-1c9d-51d0-8d00-0527ce5b210a'}, {'abstract': 'Colin Davis conducted the London Symphony Orchestra in the Berlioz Requiem at St. Paul’s Cathedral in London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/arts/music/colin-davis-conducts-the-berlioz-requiem-at-st-pauls.html', 'snippet': 'Colin Davis conducted the London Symphony Orchestra in the Berlioz Requiem at St. Paul’s Cathedral in London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A cathedral can be a terribly reverberant place to hear music, especially symphonic works. But there is a rich heritage of pieces that were conceived for the resonant acoustics and spatial dimensions of a large church, like the sacred music Monteverdi and Gabrieli wrote for St. Mark’s Basilica in Venice, music that gloried in placing groups of singers, strings and brasses in lofts and alcoves to produce exhilarating antiphonal effects.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/arts/requiem/requiem-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 866, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/arts/requiem/requiem-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1732, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/arts/requiem/requiem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/28/arts/requiem/requiem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/arts/requiem/requiem-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Soaring Requiem to Fill St. Paul’s', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Soaring Requie