GY', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-27T23:23:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Penelope Green', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Penelope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Green', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bd1032f-71c1-5131-b2f2-e5d84b8e7bf8', 'word_count': 894, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bd1032f-71c1-5131-b2f2-e5d84b8e7bf8'}, {'abstract': 'A designer nostalgic for his childhood creates hand-painted tops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/garden/a-designer-nostalgic-for-his-childhood-creates-hand-painted-tops.html', 'snippet': 'A designer nostalgic for his childhood creates hand-painted tops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the Pakistani designer Tahir Mahmood, 43, moved to Toronto five years ago, he vowed to give his son, Efan, who was 4 at the time, the pleasure of two pastimes Mr. Mahmood had enjoyed growing up in Lahore. Kite flying was easy, but playing with spinning tops proved trickier. Mr. Mahmood had trouble finding wooden tops. “So I designed this set for my kids,” he said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/garden/28GOODS/28GOODS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1140, 'width': 825, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/garden/28GOODS/28GOODS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1140, 'width': 825, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/g