t://article/1e3f1bad-d71c-5492-b0db-a95d59e7ccec', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e3f1bad-d71c-5492-b0db-a95d59e7ccec'}, {'abstract': 'Three women frustrated with the gender imbalance in math and science build a wired dollhouse called Roominate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/garden/roominate-a-dollhouse-wired-to-teach-girls-science.html', 'snippet': 'Three women frustrated with the gender imbalance in math and science build a wired dollhouse called Roominate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, educators have debated how to get more women into math and science careers. Alice Brooks, Bettina Chen and Jennifer Kessler, who met as master’s students at Stanford, have come up with a novel solution: a dollhouse with circuit boards. The women were frustrated by the gender imbalance in their classes, Ms. Brooks said, and realized “we could trace the initial spark for our interest in math and science to the toys that we played with.” (Her dad gave her a saw instead of a Barbie.)', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/garden/28KIDS_SPAN/28KIDS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/28/garden/28KIDS_SPAN/28KIDS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/garden/28KIDS_SPAN/28KIDS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/garden/28KIDS_SPAN/28KIDS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbna