umbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/business/TABLET-1340835433087/TABLET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Google Sees the Promise in Hardware', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Google Sees Promise On the Hardware Side', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tablet Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T00:43:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth and Nick Bilton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlroth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44af3dea-712e-5491-a98a-633c6254dc55', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44af3dea-712e-5491-a98a-633c6254dc55'}, {'abstract': 'The whole world is going to remember Nora Ephron for her writing and movies. A rather hefty chunk of the world is going to remember her as a dear friend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/opinion/nora-ephron-the-best-mailgirl-ever.html', 'snippet': 'The whole world is going to remember Nora Ephron for her writing and movies. A rather hefty chunk of the world is going to remember her as a dear friend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Nora Ephron graduated from college in 1962, she applied for a job as a writer at Newsweek, was told women weren’t allowed to be writers there, and settled for mailgirl. I used that story as a kind of centerpiece in a book I wrote about American women because it reminded me of one of those old movies about a Broadway musical with pompous stars played by actors you’ve never heard of, plus Judy Garland in the back of the chorus. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Best Mailgirl Ever', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Best Mailgirl Ever', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ephron, Nora', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Friendship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T00:44:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b69700c-0913-5ff3-811b-fa6fb53a09ba', 'word_count': 842, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b69700c-0913-5ff3-811b-fa6fb53a09ba'}, {'abstract': 'The three defendants were accused of hazing a sophomore, George Desdunes, whose blood alcohol content was 0.356 percent when he died after a fraternity induction ritual last year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/nyregion/ex-cornell-students-acquitted-of-hazing-in-death-of-fraternity-member.html', 'snippet': 'The three defendants were accused of hazing a sophomore, George Desdunes, whose blood alcohol content was 0.356 percent when he died after a fraternity induction ritual last year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three former Cornell University undergraduates have been found not guilty of hazing a sophomore who died during a fraternity ritual last year, in a case that drew attention to dangerous behavior among American college students. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Students Acquitted of Hazing in Cornell Death', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Former Students Acquitted Of Hazing in Cornell Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'su