'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7eb80e65-c042-57b1-a1ed-aaacf0adabba', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7eb80e65-c042-57b1-a1ed-aaacf0adabba'}, {'abstract': 'Bain Capital’s investments in companies that outsourced jobs used as a weapon against Mitt Romney.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/outsourcing-becomes-toxic-in-u-s-presidential-campaign/', 'snippet': 'Bain Capital’s investments in companies that outsourced jobs used as a weapon against Mitt Romney.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Outsourcing has never been a popular term in the Western countries that lose jobs to emerging markets, but it has become positively toxic in the current United States presidential campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Outsourcing Becomes Toxic in U.S. Presidential Campaign', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outsourcing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bain Capital', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Post', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T04:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Timmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Timmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/880b58cc-bafa-518b-bb81-f726125cd7e1', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/880b58cc-bafa-518b-bb81-f726125cd7e1'}, {'abstract': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau said more homeowners were taking out reverse mortgages at their first opportunity, often without fully understanding the loans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/business/economy/report-highlights-a-rise-in-reverse-mortgages.html', 'snippet': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau said more homeowners were taking out reverse mortgages at their first opportunity, often without fully understanding the loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — As baby boomers edge toward retirement, they are beginning to transform yet another slice of the financial industry: the market for reverse mortgages, a type of loan in which older homeowners borrow against the value of their house.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Report Highlights a Rise in Reverse Mortgages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Report Highlights a Rise In Reverse Mortgages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T04:12:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07d8560e-44f4-5f8d-8b19-fec5c7791cc9', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07d8560e-44f4-5f8d-8b19-fec5c7791cc9'}, {'abstract': 'Acute myeloid leukemia, which took the life of Nora Ephron on Tuesday, is an uncommon disease that accounts for only about 1 percent of cancer deaths in the United States.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/science/nora-ephrons-leukemia-was-an-uncommon-and-complicated-type.html', 'snippet': 'Acute myeloid leukemia, which took the life of Nora Ephron on Tuesday, is an uncommon disease that accounts for only about 1 percent of cancer deaths in the United States.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The illness that claimed the life of Nora Ephron is an uncommon type of leukemia for which there are few treatments, medical experts said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/EPHRON/EPHRON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/EPHRON/EPHRON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1299, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/EPHRON/EPHRON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/28/us/EPHRON/EPHRON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/EPHRON/EPHRON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ephron’s Leukemia Was Uncommon and Complicated', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ephron’s Leukemia Was Uncommon and Complicated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ephron, Nora', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leukemia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T04:14:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e7eea66-2f69-5a05-9459-51cd3f073ba2', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e7eea66-2f69-5a05-9459-51cd3f073ba2'}, {'abstract': 'Would Annie Chandler join Matt Grevers on the Olympic team before joining him in matrimony? She left nothing in the pool in her race, she said, but she came up short.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/for-a-swim-couple-one-stays-one-goes/', 'snippet': 'Would Annie Chandler join Matt Grevers on the Olympic team before joining him in matrimony? She left nothing in the pool in her race, she said, but she came up short.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — Ten minutes before Annie Chandler was due on the blocks for the 100-meter breaststroke final, she interrupted her prerace reverie to watch her fiancé, Matt Grevers, race for an Olympic berth in the 100-meter backstroke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Swim Couple, One Stays, One Goes', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berens, Ricky', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chandler, Annie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grevers, Matt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soni, Rebecca', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T04:21:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1def3810-c353-54b1-9d0b-a27d6ed4aeae', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1def3810-c353-54b1-9d0b-a27d6ed4aeae'}, {'abstract': 'Under a consumer protection settlement filed Wednesday, QuinStreet Inc. will turn over its GIBill.com Web site to the Department of Veterans Affairs and pay $2.5 million to the states involved.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/education/kentucky-settlement-is-reached-over-site-that-focused-on-veterans-college-benefits.html', 'snippet': 'Under a consumer protection settlement filed Wednesday, QuinStreet Inc. will turn over its GIBill.com Web site to the Department of Veterans Affairs and pay $2.5 million to the states involved.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Under a consumer protection settlement with 20 state attorneys general filed Wednesday in Frankfort, QuinStreet Inc. will turn over its GIBill.com Web site to the Department of Veterans Affairs and pay $2.5 million to the states involved. Attorney General Jack Conway of Kentucky, who announced the settlement, led a multistate investigation into the Web site, which was aimed at veterans for their education benefits, falsely giving the appearance that it was operated or endorsed by the government. Veterans have been the targets of aggressive recruiting by for-profit colleges, which are required to get at least 10 percent of their revenues from sources other than federal student loan or Pell grants. A loophole provides that veterans’ benefits count toward that 10 percent. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kentucky: Settlement Is Reached Over Site That Focused on Veterans’ College Benefits', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kentucky: Settlement Is Reached Over Site That Focused On Veterans’ College Benefits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'QuinStreet Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T04:33:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b8a5c4d-87c4-5fa6-a7c9-607cc43e17a7', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b8a5c4d-87c4-5fa6-a7c9-607cc43e17a7'}, {'abstract': 'On Wednesday night, Breeja Larson, 20, became an Olympian with a victory in the 100-meter breaststroke.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/a-newcomer-is-making-her-own-waves/', 'snippet': 'On Wednesday night, Breeja Larson, 20, became an Olympian with a victory in the 100-meter breaststroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — As a first-time competitor at the Olympic trials, Breeja Larson faced a quandary. Should she act as if she had been here before or go ahead and try to get the autographs of all her favorite swimming stars?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Newcomer Is Making Her Own Waves', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larson, Breeja', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T04:38:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04285f6f-f81b-566b-915e-13bc372be36a', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04285f6f-f81b-566b-915e-13bc372be36a'}, {'abstract': 'The State Legislature on Wednesday overrode a veto by Gov. John Lynch of a bill concerning both identification for voters and partial-birth abortion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/us/new-hampshire-lawmakers-override-vetoes-on-voting-and-abortion-bills.html', 'snippet': 'The State Legislature on Wednesday overrode a veto by Gov. John Lynch of a bill concerning both identification for voters and partial-birth abortion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The State Legislature on Wednesday overrode a veto by Gov. John Lynch of a bill requiring that individuals present a valid form of identification or sign an affidavit in order to vote. The list of acceptable forms of identifications will be narrowed in September 2013 to exclude student identification cards, and those who sign affidavits will be required to be photographed. The Legislature also overrode Mr. Lynch’s veto of a ban on the procedure known as partial-birth abortion. Overall, the state’s House and Senate overrode 6 of 13 vetoes on Wednesday; a veto on the House’s redistricting plan was overridden in March.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/BRFS/BRFS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 416, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/BRFS/BRFS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 416, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/BRFS/BRFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/28/us/BRFS/BRFS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/BRFS/BRFS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hampshire: Lawmakers Override Vetoes on Voting and Abortion Bills', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | New England', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Hampshire: Lawmakers Override Vetoes On Voting and Abortion Bills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, John H', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Hampshire', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'p