head of a meeting in Geneva on Saturday at which a proposal for a Syrian national unity cabinet that includes opposition figures could be put forward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/middleeast/russia-says-syria-transition-needed-but-cannot-be-imposed.html', 'snippet': 'The comments came ahead of a meeting in Geneva on Saturday at which a proposal for a Syrian national unity cabinet that includes opposition figures could be put forward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia’s foreign minister, Sergey V. Lavrov, said on Thursday that Syria needed a period of political transition but reiterated Moscow’s resistance to any plan being imposed by the international community.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Says Transition Is Needed in Syria but Cannot Be Imposed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia Says Transition Is Needed in Syria but Cannot Be Imposed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lavrov, Sergey V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T10:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry, Nick Cumming-Bruce and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c86cc7c8-6441-54e1-bf62-2a9621287406', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c86cc7c8-6441-54e1-bf62-2a9621287406'}, {'abstract': '“Absalom, Absalom!” was written more than 75 years ago, yet it remains the most serious attempt by any white writer to deal with the madness of race in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/magazine/how-william-faulkner-tackled-race-and-freed-the-south-from-itself.html', 'snippet': '“Absalom, Absalom!” was written more than 75 years ago, yet it remains the most serious attempt by any white writer to deal with the madness of race in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A poll of well over a hundred writers and critics, taken a few years back by Oxford American magazine, named William Faulkner’s “Absalom, Absalom!” the “greatest Southern novel ever written,” by a decisive margin — and the poll was conducted while looking back on a century in which a disproportionate number of the best American books were Southern — so to say that this novel requires no introduction is just to speak plainly.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/magazine/01riff/mag-01Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/01/magazine/01riff/mag-01Riff-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/magazine/01riff/mag-01Riff-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 478, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/magazine/01riff/mag-0