urces of Canada, the latest in a wave of energy deals. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Petronas to Buy Progress Energy for $5.35 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Petronas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T11:51:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/658335b9-24dd-5ac7-9210-c48eba8ca23c', 'word_count': 225, 'uri': 'nyt://article/658335b9-24dd-5ac7-9210-c48eba8ca23c'}, {'abstract': 'After a vote by the board of directors Wednesday night, the company confirmed it would spin off its newspaper unit as a separate company.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/news-corporations-big-move-murdoch-informs-the-staff/', 'snippet': 'After a vote by the board of directors Wednesday night, the company confirmed it would spin off its newspaper unit as a separate company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'News Corporation announced Thursday morning that it would spin off its publishing division from its entertainment unit and create two separate, publicly traded companies. Here is the memo Rupert Murdoch, News Corporation’s chairman and chief executive, sent to the company’s employees.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Corporation’s Big Move: Murdoch Informs the Staff', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carey, Chase', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sun, The (British Newspaper)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T11:51:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editors', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editors'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/01a47938-8d3c-56bb-a8eb-3a710b702c6a', 'word_count': 1067, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01a47938-8d3c-56bb-a8eb-3a710b702c6a'}, {'abstract': 'Instead of going to great lengths to delay or avoid vaccination, as some American parents do, mothers in the developing world struggle to get to clinics and to get the required vaccinations.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/when-parents-fear-vaccines/', 'snippet': 'Instead of going to great lengths to delay or avoid vaccination, as some American parents do, mothers in the developing world struggle to get to clinics and to get the required vaccinations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to argue with the premise that in the United States, some parents take lightly their ability to vaccinate children against childhood diseases. Recent studies suggest that as many as 21 percent of parents in the U.S. are delaying or refusing some or all of the recommended early childhood vaccines. Schools in some areas — educated, upper-middle-class regions — have startlingly low vaccination rates: in one Washington State county, 72 percent of kindergartners and 89 percent of sixth graders are either not compliant with or exempt from vaccination requirements for school entry, and at a Bay Area Waldorf school I wrote about last year, only 23 percent of the incoming kindergarten class had been fully vaccinated.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking, and Resisting, Vaccines', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/000f0b93-0a06-517a-95c9-2f0e89347f2a', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/000f0b93-0a06-517a-95c9-2f0e89347f2a'}, {'abstract': 'In Seth MacFarlane’s film “Ted,” a toy bear comes to life and turns out to have a filthy mouth and a taste for weed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/movies/ted-by-seth-macfarlane-with-mark-wahlberg-and-mila-kunis.html', 'snippet': 'In Seth MacFarlane’s film “Ted,” a toy bear comes to life and turns out to have a filthy mouth and a taste for weed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is really only one joke in “Ted” — a toy bear comes to life and turns out to have a filthy mouth and a taste for weed — but the movie’s attempts at humor can nonetheless be sorted into a few distinct categories. There are jokes that are funny only because a stuffed bear says them, jokes that are not funny even though a stuffed bear says them and jokes that may or may not be funny because of Mark Wahlberg. Mila Kunis is also in the movie, but she can’t be funny because she’s a girl, and her job is to be amused, tolerant and pretty.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/movies/ted-span/ted-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], '