9f62-c19b9f4e5514'}, {'abstract': "Jean-Bernard Lévy, under whose leadership the company's stock price has languished, has been criticized for not having a vision for the media conglomerate.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/business/global/chief-of-vivendi-set-to-resign.html', 'snippet': "Jean-Bernard Lévy, under whose leadership the company's stock price has languished, has been criticized for not having a vision for the media conglomerate.", 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Jean-Bernard Lévy stepped down as chief executive of Vivendi, the French media and telecommunications conglomerate, on Thursday after losing a boardroom battle over strategy. The move prompted speculation about a possible breakup of the company. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/business/Vivendi/Vivendi-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/business/Vivendi/Vivendi-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1954, 'width': 1407, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Chief of Vivendi Resigns After Strategy Dispute', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disputing Strategy, Vivendi’s Chief Quits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vivendi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levy, Jean-Bernard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Activision Blizzard Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T14:55:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Global Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Pfanner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pfanner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6febf372-06fb-5491-8dcc-2ed0c026a02d', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6febf372-06fb-5491-8dcc-2ed0c026a02d'}, {'abstract': 'The Westminster Abbey Choir has long been a symbol of the Church of England’s separation from the Roman Catholic Church.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/sistine-chapel-choir-to-sing-with-westminster-abbey-choir/', 'snippet': 'The Westminster Abbey Choir has long been a symbol of the Church of England’s separation from the Roman Catholic Church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time since its founding more than 500 years ago, the Sistine Chapel Choir will sing as a single chorus with another choir. But not just any group of voices: the Westminster Abbey Choir, a much older body that, at least since the16th century, has been a symbol of the Church of England’s separation from the Roman Catholic Church.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sistine Chapel Choir to Sing With Westminster Abbey Choir', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Church of England', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T14:58:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sectio