n the U.S.A., by Google; and more turbulence for Philip Falcone, a once high-flying investor.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Business Day Live: Google’s Route to ‘Made in the U.S.’', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T15:13:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dealbook', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dealbook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/338df68e-835f-5ab0-ba95-c4277fe1f8cc', 'word_count': 27, 'uri': 'nyt://article/338df68e-835f-5ab0-ba95-c4277fe1f8cc'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey won’t go to war with Syria over that downed jet, if only because that would tip the domestic balance of power back toward the military.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/turkey-and-syria-are-nowhere-near-war/', 'snippet': 'Turkey won’t go to war with Syria over that downed jet, if only because that would tip the domestic balance of power back toward the military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL – Having been introduced to international diplomacy by the Marx Brothers in “Duck Soup,” I cannot but view Turkey’s current crisis with Syria with unease. In that 1933 film, Groucho (aka Rufus T. Firefly) swaps finely tuned insults with the ambassador of Sylvania until he famously cries: “This means war!” When the ambassador pleads that he will do anything to avoid conflict, Firefly replies: “I’ve already paid a month’s rent on the battlefield.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Too Important to Be Left to the Generals', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 