ness Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vinod Sreeharsha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vinod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sreeharsha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c21065d-c51f-56f1-b166-738a05e170e5', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c21065d-c51f-56f1-b166-738a05e170e5'}, {'abstract': 'Both President Obama and Mitt Romney looked for advantages in the health care ruling to use in their presidential campaigns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/us/politics/republicans-press-on-with-health-law-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'Both President Obama and Mitt Romney looked for advantages in the health care ruling to use in their presidential campaigns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Mitt Romney and other Republicans who oppose the health care law are looking ahead to one remaining avenue of appeal: the ballot box in November.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/politics/0728romney4/0728romney4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Vowing to Take Battle Over Health Care Law Into November', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'G.O.P. Vowing To Take Battle Into November', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T17:05:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Zeleny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zeleny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/70c78038-c239-5d13-956c-a14b8628dc87', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70c78038-c239-5d13-956c-a14b8628dc87'}, {'abstract': 'Fire officials said cooler and lighter winds should allow them to gain more control over the Waldo Canyon Fire burning around Colorado Springs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/us/furious-wildfire-in-colorado-leaves-destruction-in-its-wake.html', 'snippet': 'Fire officials said cooler and lighter winds should allow them to gain more control over the Waldo Canyon Fire burning around Colorado Springs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLORADO SPRINGS — Helped by cooler temperatures and lighter winds, fire officials said Thursday morning that they hoped to gain more control over the Waldo Canyon Fire burning around Colorado Springs. Wind and heat had earlier fueled the furious wildfire burning in the foothills around Colorado’s second-largest city, first roaring past containment lines and forcing tens of thousands of residents to flee, chased by billowing smoke, blowing ash and fear that their homes might burn to the ground. At a news conference Thursday morning, officials said 5 percent of the fire was contained, though they expected that number to grow significantly by the end of the day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Conditions Improve Slightly in Fighting Colorado Wildfires', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conditions Improve Slightly in Fighting Colorado Wildfires', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forest and Brush Fires', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Western States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T17:07:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Frosch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frosch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d49a7ab0-2b07-54b5-8b2b-0bc1b8b7d475', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d49a7ab0-2b07-54b5-8b2b-0bc1b8b7d475'}, {'abstract': 'A victory for Obama on health care should indeed benefit him politically.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/in-health-ruling-relief-for-obama-but-a-blow-to-conventional-wisdom/', 'snippet': 'A victory for Obama on health care should indeed benefit him politically.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s 5-to-4 decision on Thursday to uphold most of President Obama’s health care law represents a hurdle cleared for Mr. Obama. He had been at risk of seeing his most ambitious policy initiative — and most expensive, in terms of the political capital it required — neutered oroverturned by the court.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Health Ruling, Relief for Obama but a Blow to Conventional Wisdom', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T17:08:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Silver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8db3a31e-778d-553b-b768-d88ab9008229', 'word_count': 1004, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8db3a31e-778d-553b-b768-d88ab9008229'}, {'abstract': '“Dow Jones is a very viable company and The Wall Street Journal is a very viable newspaper,” Rupert Murdoch said in a phone interview with The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/in-a-morning-media-blitz-murdoch-defends-his-newspaper-assets/', 'snippet': '“Dow Jones is a very viable company and The Wall Street Journal is a very viable newspaper,” Rupert Murdoch said in a phone interview with The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rupert Murdoch went on a rare publicity blitz on Thursday to defend News Corporation’s decision to split the company’s newspapers from its entertainment assets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Morning Media Blitz, Murdoch Defends His Newspaper Assets', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newspapers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dow Jones & Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T17:10:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, '