ltimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'London Theater Journal: Meeting the Faces in the Crowd', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leigh, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:30:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb998956-f2f7-5dac-ba88-7d5dc31a3329', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb998956-f2f7-5dac-ba88-7d5dc31a3329'}, {'abstract': 'On Tuesday, The New York Times Magazine defeated The New Yorker, beginning this year’s softball season in romping fashion.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/theres-no-crying-in-media-league-softball/', 'snippet': 'On Tuesday, The New York Times Magazine defeated The New Yorker, beginning this year’s softball season in romping fashion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our story begins one steamy evening last August, on the fertile lowlands of Central Park’s public fields, as dusk settled and the promise of the Tap a Keg summoned, and The New York Times Magazine’s ragtag softball team’s once-commanding lead against its archrival, The New Yorker, evaporated in the game’s final inning. As the sun set, what once appeared a sure win ended in a tie. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s No Crying in Media-League Softball', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Softball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Yorker', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:46:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Kelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db015a4e-c9aa-5d4d-b864-9b97c4c4dbb8', 'word_count': 911, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db015a4e-c9aa-5d4d-b864-9b97c4c4dbb8'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Greenberg is blogging via satellite as he travels down the Stuyahok River in search of sockeye salmon, which number 40 million this time of year.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/chasing-the-sockeye-salmon-migration/', 'snippet': 'Paul Greenberg is blogging via satellite as he travels down the Stuyahok River in search of sockeye salmon, which number 40 million this time of year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In early summer, the biggest run of wild salmon left in the world reaches its peak.\xa0The sockeye salmon migration of Bristol Bay, Alaska, can number more than 40 million fish; the resulting fishing industry is worth more than $400 million.\xa0The award-winning author (and Times contributor) Paul Greenberg, author of the New York Times bestseller “Four Fish,” is blogging via satellite as he travels down the Stuyahok River with the Alaska guide and longtime outdoorsman Mark Rutherford. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chasing the Sockeye Salmon Migration', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Commercial', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salmon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bristol Bay (Alaska)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:49:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c46171b-dfe8-5d39-a109-eff33ca5a115', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c46171b-dfe8-5d39-a109-eff33ca5a115'}, {'abstract': 'The utility will purchase all of the electricity produced by new medium-size projects over the life of a 20-year contract.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/with-feed-in-financing-modest-solar-projects-for-long-island/', 'snippet': 'The utility will purchase all of the electricity produced by new medium-size projects over the life of a 20-year contract.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Long Island Power Authority approved a new program on Thursday to encourage developers to build medium-scale solar projects using a financing mechanism, the feed-in tariff, that has resulted in both booms and busts overseas. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Feed-In Financing, Modest Solar Projects  for Long Island', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diane Cardwell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cardwell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82257aff-b364-5d55-98c8-e4edab5b622b', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82257aff-b364-5d55-98c8-e4edab5b622b'}, {'abstract': 'After a ski injury, doctors weren’t sure Jack Brown would swim again. At the Olympic trials on Thursday, he tied for 12th place in the preliminaries of the 200-meter breaststroke.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/brown-finishes-12th-and-couldnt-be-happier/', 'snippet': 'After a ski injury, doctors weren’t sure Jack Brown would swim again. At the Olympic trials on Thursday, he tied for 12th place in the preliminaries of the 200-meter breaststroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — Jack Brown tied for 12th in the preliminaries of the 200-meter breaststroke on Thursday. Never mind the chance to make his first United States Olympic team, Brown had much to be proud about in advancing to the semifinals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brown Finishes 12th, and Couldn’t Be Happier', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Jack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hansen, Brendan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:51:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca79f856-8b9a-582b-bb1e-991b049f86bb', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca79f856-8b9a-582b-bb1e-991b049f86bb'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s fourth-largest city, nestled in one of the country’s top food and wine regions, offers a diverse menu, from slow strolls and Slow Food to classic cafes and classic cars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/travel/36-hours-in-turin-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Italy’s fourth-largest city, nestled in one of the country’s top food and wine regions, offers a diverse menu, from slow strolls and Slow Food to classic cafes and classic cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHEN it comes to urban reputations, being home to the Shroud of Turin and the headquarters of Fiat isn’t a lot to coast on. But Turin, Italy’s fourth-largest city, also has the elegant cafe culture of Trieste by day and the vibrant aperitivo scene of Milan by night, all while being nestled in Piedmont, arguably the finest food and wine region in Italy. Recently, the city inaugurated a stadium for the popular Juventus soccer club and reopened a pair of stellar museums highlighting the city’s multifaceted importance throughout Italy’s history. Turin, it seems, is revving its engine.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 208, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 208}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 355, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN/01HOURS_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Turin, Italy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Turin, Italy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turin (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:52:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ingrid K. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ingrid', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eae4c41f-a7f8-5a98-9392-417d59320c1e', 'word_count': 1429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eae4c41f-a7f8-5a98-9392-417d59320c1e'}, {'abstract': 'Where Italy stretches toward France, walk among palaces and visit a giant temple to food.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/07/01/travel/01TURIN.html', 'snippet': 'Where Italy stretches toward France, walk among palaces and visit a giant temple to food.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Where Italy stretches toward France, walk among palaces and visit a giant temple to food.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01TURIN-slide-D5OY/01TURIN-slide-D5OY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01TURIN-slide-D5OY/01TURIN-slide-D5OY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01TURIN-slide-D5OY/01TURIN-slide-D5OY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01TURIN-slide-D5OY/01TURIN-slide-D5OY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/travel/01TURIN-slide-D5OY/01TURIN-slide-D5OY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Touring Turin, Italy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turin (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:54:17+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c2ef2067-9353-5a0f-a59e-2619ce580252', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c2ef2067-9353-5a0f-a59e-2619ce580252'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Schimmel, one of the most respected authorities on postwar Los Angeles art, is leaving the Museum of Contemporary Art.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/chief-curator-to-leave-museum-of-contemporary-art-los-angeles/', 'snippet': 'Paul Schimmel, one of the most respected authorities on postwar Los Angeles art, is leaving the Museum of Contemporary Art.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Paul Schimmel, the chief curator at the Museum of Contemporary Art, Los Angeles, and one of the most respected authorities on postwar Los Angeles art, is leaving the museum, according to its board.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chief Curator to Leave Museum of Contemporary Art, Los Angeles', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chief Curator to Leave Los Angeles Museum', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suspensions, Dismissals and Resignations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deitch, Jeffrey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T18:55:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03b6a8d0-13a9-5016-8912-5475df26fe58', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03b6a8d0-13a9-5016-8912-5475df26fe58'}, {'abstract': 'One of two genocide charges against the former wartime leader, Radovan Karadzic, were dropped, but he will still stand trial for war crimes in The Hague.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/europe/ex-bosnian-serb-leader-karadzic-to-face-war-crimes-trial.html', 'snippet': 'One of two genocide charges against the former wartime leader, Radovan Karadzic, were dropped, but he will still stand trial for war crimes in The Hague.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Radovan Karadzic, the former Bosnian Serb psychiatrist who became a nationalist wartime leader, has failed in his bid to get his war crimes trial in The Hague halted and have all charges thrown out for lack of sufficient evidence. But the United Nations judges hearing his case have dropped one of the two counts of genocide against him, the court announced Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/world/europe/29hague/29hague-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 820, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/world/europe/29hague/29hague-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1640, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/world/europe/29hague/29hague-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/29/world/europe/29hague/29hague-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/world/europe/29hague/29hague-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'su