2', 'word_count': 433, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c96780a9-11a8-5431-a536-e2af1bddf8c2'}, {'abstract': 'Set to Symphony No. 9 by Dmitri Shostakovich, the ballet, which will have its world premiere on Oct. 18, will be the first of three new one-act ballets by Alexei Ratmansky to Shostakovich.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/a-new-ratmansky-work-to-debut-at-american-ballet-theaters-fall-city-center-season/', 'snippet': 'Set to Symphony No. 9 by Dmitri Shostakovich, the ballet, which will have its world premiere on Oct. 18, will be the first of three new one-act ballets by Alexei Ratmansky to Shostakovich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Ballet Theater’s 2012 fall season at New York City Center, which runs from Oct. 16 to 20, will include the premiere of a new work by Alexei Ratmansky, the company’s artist in residence, Ballet Theater said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Ratmansky Work to Have Debut at American Ballet Theater’s Fall City Center Season', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Ratmansky Work Bound for City Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ratmansky, Alexei', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shostakovich, Dmitri', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T19:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf40faaf-e0c0-5fc8-8862-eee5e0def99f', 'word_count': 219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf40faaf-e0c0-5fc8-8862-eee5e0def99f'}, {'abstract': 'Tennis officials and broadcasters face a challenge of the highest order when pronouncing the names of players from Argentina to Uzbekistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/sports/tennis/wimbledon-2012-putting-twisted-tongue-to-names-of-globalized-tennis.html', 'snippet': 'Tennis officials and broadcasters face a challenge of the highest order when pronouncing the names of players from Argentina to Uzbekistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — If there are times when tennis officials and announcers warrant some sympathy, then the first few days of a major tournament like Wimbledon would be one of them. Hundreds of matches in singles and doubles featuring players from Argentina to Uzbekistan are a linguistic gantlet of the highest order. On the women’s side alone, there were first-round contests between Scheepers and Shvedova, Gajdosova and Zaniewska, and Foretz Gacon and Niculescu. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/tennis/29names-pic/29names-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/tennis/29names-pic/29names-pic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/tennis/29names-pic/29names-pic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/tennis/29names-pic/29names-pic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1100, 'width': 1600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'