samian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c83bb8a-812e-51c5-bac2-b357eecaa507', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c83bb8a-812e-51c5-bac2-b357eecaa507'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court largely let the health care overhaul stand, upholding the individual mandate and limiting the Medicaid provision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/28/us/how-the-justices-ruled-on-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court largely let the health care overhaul stand, upholding the individual mandate and limiting the Medicaid provision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court largely let the health care overhaul stand, upholding the individual mandate and limiting the Medicaid provision.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Justices Ruled on the Health Care Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/18ac19a8-330a-556d-a0df-732b166a359e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/18ac19a8-330a-556d-a0df-732b166a359e'}, {'abstract': 'Accounts differ on why The Province in Vancouver, British Columbia, pulled an animated parody of an Enbridge ad from its Web site.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/political-cartoon-taking-aim-at-pipeline-company-is-pulled/', 'snippet': 'Accounts differ on why The Province in Vancouver, British Columbia, pulled an animated parody of an Enbridge ad from its Web site.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Cartoon Taking Aim at Pipeline Company Is Pulled', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cartoons and Cartoonists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Enbridge Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:02:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8a7ce4-cdd9-532f-ac34-687810c7616b', 'word_count': 638, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8a7ce4-cdd9-532f-ac34-687810c7616b'}, {'abstract': 'The automaker’s international losses will triple in the second quarter, primarily because of flagging European demand, the company’s chief financial officer said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/business/ford-sees-overseas-losses-triple-this-quarter.html', 'snippet': 'The automaker’s international losses will triple in the second quarter, primarily because of flagging European demand, the company’s chief financial officer said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEARBORN, Mich. — Europe’s economic woes are taking a much bigger bite out of the profits of Ford Motor, which until now has largely avoided the hefty losses that have dragged down the profits of many of its rivals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/business/Ford/Ford-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 313, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/29/business/Ford/Ford-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 313}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/business/Ford/Ford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/business/Ford/Ford-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ford Motor, Citing Europe’s Woes, Says Foreign Losses to Triple in Quarter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ford Motor, Citing Europe’s Woes, Says Foreign Losses to Triple in Quarter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ford Motor Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:03:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Vlasic', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vlasic', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/21e3e7ea-d5cd-5c5e-b379-a914a419c62c', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21e3e7ea-d5cd-5c5e-b379-a914a419c62c'}, {'abstract': 'Securities fraud charges filed against Philip Falcone and his firm, Harbinger Capital Partners, are a warning that hedge funds can now expect the same scrutiny that Wall Street banks and brokerage firms receive.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/in-case-against-philip-falcone-a-warning-to-others/', 'snippet': 'Securities fraud charges filed against Philip Falcone and his firm, Harbinger Capital Partners, are a warning that hedge funds can now expect the same scrutiny that Wall Street banks and brokerage firms receive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hedge fund managers have long flown underneath the radar, doing pretty much as they pleased with little oversight from the Securities and Exchange Commission. Securities fraud charges filed against Philip Falcone and his firm, Harbinger Capital Partners, are a warning that funds can now expect the same scrutiny that Wall Street banks and brokerage firms receive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Case Against Philip Falcone, a Warning to Others', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falcone, Philip A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harbinger Capital Partners', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c43aedf-ed57-5216-8ae7-3d5d01fb8550', 'word_count': 1156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c43aedf-ed57-5216-8ae7-3d5d01fb8550'}, {'abstract': 'Hyper about health care.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/double-scotch-time/', 'snippet': 'Hyper about health care.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yes, I’m on vacation. And I’ve tried not to think about Scotus, even though I was campaigning for universal health care long before it was fashionable. But I did have a feeling of dread in the pit of my stomach this morning, all the same.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Double Scotch Time', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1316614-0e9e-5c0d-92b2-4566754c0315', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1316614-0e9e-5c0d-92b2-4566754c0315'}, {'abstract': 'In response to the Supreme Court’s health care ruling, the candidate ran through his usual talking points.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/romneys-call-to-arms/', 'snippet': 'In response to the Supreme Court’s health care ruling, the candidate ran through his usual talking points.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mitt Romney looked a little shaken when he faced the cameras this morning to comment on the Supreme Court’s decision upholding the Affordable Care Act. Having thrown out his preferred speech thanking the court for rejecting the law, he didn’t seem to have much of a backup other than a call to arms for conservative voters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Call to Arms', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'pers