e who thought that monitoring would damage the trust between parents and their children, and those who feel that the Internet raises new chal...', 'lead_paragraph': ' In Tuesday’s New York Times, Somini Sengupta wrote about software and services that let parents keep tabs on their children’s activities online. The article sparked a spirited conversation among Times readers, who were largely split into two camps: those who think monitoring will damage the trust between parents and their children, and those who feel that the Internet raises new challenges that require new tools. Here is a sampling of what people are saying. (Some of these comments are excerpts from longer passages.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers React to Surveillance Software for Parents', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:13:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8d3d51d-c115-5e86-a175-87a62bf1f3b2', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8d3d51d-c115-5e86-a175-87a62bf1f3b2'}, {'abstract': 'Money market funds can claim net asset values of $1 a share, without reserves and with an implicit government guarantee, but the Securities and Exchange Commission could change that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/business/money-market-funds-and-their-allies-resist-new-rules.html', 'snippet': 'Money market funds can claim net asset values of $