act': 'A round-up of Times coverage that discusses what President Obama’s health care law means for consumers.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/what-the-health-care-ruling-means-for-you/', 'snippet': 'A round-up of Times coverage that discusses what President Obama’s health care law means for consumers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the Supreme Court has upheld most of President Obama’s \xa0health care law, you may be looking for a little refresher on what it all means for you and your wallet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Health Care Ruling Means for You', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:20:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db534f49-9439-5fb7-b8a6-c3cda7e657eb', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db534f49-9439-5fb7-b8a6-c3cda7e657eb'}, {'abstract': 'Al Buehler, a retired Olympic and Duke University track coach, was recognized for his contributions to the sport.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/lifetime-achievement-award-for-a-throwback-coach/', 'snippet': 'Al Buehler, a retired Olympic and Duke University track coach, was recognized for his contributions to the sport.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — In the stands here is Al Buehler, a retired Olympic and Duke University track coach known for his wide-brimmed hat and long career. On Wednesday night, Buehler took center stage and received a lifetime achievement award from USA Track and Field, the national governing body for the sport. He is also the subject of a documentary film and a book coming out this summer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lifetime Achievement Award for a Throwback Coach', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Duke University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:22:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecdfc273-7d0d-5434-b2c5-085dbd529547', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecdfc273-7d0d-5434-b2c5-085dbd529547'}, {'abstract': 'The play, “Lucky Guy,” is about the journalist Mike McAlary, who wrote about cops, crime and police department scandals in the 1980s and ‘90s.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/producer-says-he-still-intends-to-bring-ephron-play-to-broadway/', 'snippet': 'The play, “Lucky Guy,” is about the journalist Mike McAlary, who wrote about cops, crime and police department scandals in the 1980s and ‘90s.', 'lead_paragraph': ' One of the theater producers aiming Nora Ephron’s new play “Lucky Guy” for Broadway confirmed on Thursday that he is going forward with the show, a bio-drama about the New York newspaper columnist Mike McAlary. Ms. Ephron, a celebrated humorist and Oscar-nominated screenwriter, died on Tuesday at the age of 71 from pneumonia brought on by acute myeloid leukemia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Producer Says He Still Intends to Bring Ephron Play to Broadway', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ephron Play Goes On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callender, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ephron, Nora', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hanks, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McAlary, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfe, George C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:26:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09d821de-5f1e-5ab1-a6b5-ff4387d0571d', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09d821de-5f1e-5ab1-a6b5-ff4387d0571d'}, {'abstract': 'A mash-up of advice from the people who know YouTube best: the amateurs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/magazine/100000001634876/how-to-be-a-youtube-celebrity.html', 'snippet': 'A mash-up of advice from the people who know YouTube best: the amateurs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A mash-up of advice from the people who know YouTube best: the amateurs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credi