plications of the rulings, and BuzzFeed’s Ben Smith recaps the day’s discussion on social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Leonhardt discusses the details of the Supreme Court’s ruling on President Obama’s health care law, Jim Rutenberg analyzes the political implications of the rulings and BuzzFeed’s Ben Smith recaps the social media’s discussion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'TimesCast Politics: Health Care Decision', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:41:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf9d01e4-a789-570b-95aa-3ea276d8a507', 'word_count': 35, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf9d01e4-a789-570b-95aa-3ea276d8a507'}, {'abstract': 'The introduction of 3-D TV has been a bumpy one; people just don’t seem to care all that much about it. But development of a glasses-less 3-D technology, and more subtle use of the 3-D effect , may help speed its adoption.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/less-may-be-more-for-3-d-tv/', 'snippet': 'The introduction of 3-D TV has been a bumpy one; people just don’t seem to care all that much about it. But development of a glasses-less 3-D technology, and more subtle use of the 3-D effect , may help speed its adoption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'StreamTV NetworksThis is precisely what is wrong with the marketing of 3-D TV.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/technology/personaltech/27bits-3Dtv/27bits-3Dtv-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 571, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/27/technology/personaltech/27bits-3Dtv/27bits-3Dtv-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 394, 'width': 571, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Less May Be More for 3-D TV', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three-Dimensional Devices and Effects', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LG Electronics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Samsung Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TOSHIBA Corporation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:42:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Grobart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grobart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42ec0251-0d8b-5f01-92c1-99d7f09fa2f6', 'word_count': 699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42ec0251-0d8b-5f01-92c1-99d7f09fa2f6'}, {'abstract': 'The dancer Shantala Shivalingappa offers a diverse four-piece program at the Joyce Theater this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/arts/dance/shantala-shivalingappa-at-joyce-theater.html', 'snippet': 'The dancer Shantala Shivalingappa offers a diverse four-piece program at the Joyce Theater this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At several points in her hourlong solo recital at the Joyce Theater this week, Shantala Shivalingappa keeps her back to the audience while continuing to dance. One such sequence occurs in the third of her four dances, “Shift,” which she choreographed. Those in the audience who are acquainted with Indian dance may recognize some gestures and phrases: the hand, held out with fingers splayed like an open fan, is moved in an arc sideways, and the eyes, torso and legs all follow it. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29SHANTALA/29SHANTALA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1002, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29SHANTALA/29SHANTALA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2003, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29SHANTALA/29SHANTALA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29SHANTALA/29SHANTALA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29SHANTALA/29SHANTALA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stylish Deconstruction, in a Flow of Movement and Stillness', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stylish Deconstruction, in a Flow of Movement and Stillness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reviews', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:46:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5641468c-b83b-569e-979e-4983b50f24ac', 'word_count': 763, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5641468c-b83b-569e-979e-4983b50f24ac'}, {'abstract': 'The Philadelphia Orchestra had endured years of declining ticket sales and donations, resulting in mounting losses and bankruptcy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/bankruptcy-court-gives-blessing-to-philadelphia-orchestra-reorganization/', 'snippet': 'The Philadelphia Orchestra had endured years of declining ticket sales and donations, resulting in mounting losses and bankruptcy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Philadelphia Orchestra, which filed for bankruptcy last year, jolting the classical music world, announced on Thursday that its reorganization plan had been approved by a federal bankruptcy court and that it expects to emerge from Chapter 11 by the end of July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bankruptcy Court Gives Blessing to Philadelphia Orchestra Reorganization', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philadelphia Orchestra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T20:50:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a40a628e-832a-5e5b-bd7f-768043b1be47', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a40a628e-832a-5e5b-bd7f-768043b1be47'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Auldon Clark’s Manhattan Chamber Orchestra continued its emphasis on American composers — and its 25th anniversary celebration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/arts/music/manhattan-chamber-orchestra-at-symphony-space.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Auldon Clark’s Manhattan Chamber Orchestra continued its emphasis on American composers — and its 25th anniversary celebration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Auldon Clark’s Manhattan Chamber Orchestra can be counted on to present entertaining programs of accessible contemporary works, with occasional glances at the repertory’s quirky mavericks to keep the programs fresh, and an emphasis on American composers. But you never know quite what form the ensemble will take until its players file out on stage. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29CHAMBER_SPAN/29CHAMBER_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29CHAMBER_SPAN/29CHAMBER_SPAN-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/29CHAMBER_SPAN/29CHAMBER_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u