d in a cave are 2,000 to 3,000 years older than examples found elsewhere, and probably came from simple concave vessels used for cooking food, archaeologists say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/03/science/oldest-known-pottery-found-in-china.html', 'snippet': 'Pottery fragments found in a cave are 2,000 to 3,000 years older than examples found elsewhere, and probably came from simple concave vessels used for cooking food, archaeologists say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fragments of ancient pottery found in southern China turn out to date back 20,000 years, making them the world’s oldest known pottery — 2,000 to 3,000 years older than examples found in East Asia and elsewhere. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/03/science/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN/03OBOX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 252, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/03/science/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN/03OBOX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 252}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/03/science/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN/03OBOX1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/03/science/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN/03OBOX1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 861, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/03/science/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/03/science/03OBPOTTERY1_SPAN/03OBPOTTERY1