on': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2fb2368-c435-5f8a-b2fc-a74dff53b24a', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2fb2368-c435-5f8a-b2fc-a74dff53b24a'}, {'abstract': 'Now in its 11th year, the New York Asian Film Festival offers more than 50 films from 10 countries encompassing some of the world’s most vital film industries.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/movies/new-york-asian-film-festival-at-walter-reade-theater.html', 'snippet': 'Now in its 11th year, the New York Asian Film Festival offers more than 50 films from 10 countries encompassing some of the world’s most vital film industries.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The King of Pigs,” an animated feature by the South Korean director Yeun Sang-ho, is a poisoned-memory play: two men who appear to be in their 30s meet for the first time in years and spend the rest of the film reminiscing about their youth. One is miserable over his stalled career as a writer, the other has failed in business and, in rage and despair, murdered his wife. The root of their malaise, they agree, is no mystery: it’s middle school.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/FESTIVAL_SPAN/FESTIVAL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/FESTIVAL_SPAN/FESTIVAL_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/FESTIVAL_SPAN/FESTIVAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/arts/FESTIVAL_SPAN/FESTIVAL-superJumbo.