ate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Gray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1621189f-94e5-532d-a148-f46f3b9e7c48', 'word_count': 834, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1621189f-94e5-532d-a148-f46f3b9e7c48'}, {'abstract': 'A roundup of new books featuring work by van Gogh, Ryan McGinley, Robert Longo, Thelma Herzl and the “other Audubon.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/books/books-by-ryan-mcginley-robert-longo-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'A roundup of new books featuring work by van Gogh, Ryan McGinley, Robert Longo, Thelma Herzl and the “other Audubon.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The savviest piece of advice I got as a rookie reporter-photographer came my first week on the job at The Exeter News-Letter in New Hampshire. The picture editor told me, “If you think you’re close, get closer.” Words to brand on your brain, maybe even your retinas, if you’re being paid to see, especially when laying bare the natural world.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/books/20120629-PAPER-slide-55HX/20120629-PAPER-slide-55HX-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/29/books/20120629-PAPER-slide-55HX/20120629-PAPER-slide-55HX-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/books/20120629-PAPER-slide-55HX/20120629-PAPER-slide-55HX-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'capti