e, 'lastname': 'Jennings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/077b4855-4d0d-56cb-b50f-3bbacbf5a7d4', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/077b4855-4d0d-56cb-b50f-3bbacbf5a7d4'}, {'abstract': 'Exhibitions at Snug Harbor Cultural Center: “Treasures of Sailors” and “Shopping Bag Intricacies.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/arts/design/treasures-of-sailors-at-snug-harbor-cultural-center.html', 'snippet': 'Exhibitions at Snug Harbor Cultural Center: “Treasures of Sailors” and “Shopping Bag Intricacies.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Snug Harbor Cultural Center, a bucolic spread of historic architecture on the north shore of Staten Island that includes a botanical garden and children’s museum, began life in the early 19th century as a retirement home for sailors. Tucked in Building D, one of the glorious Greek Revival structures on the grounds, is the Noble Maritime Collection, among the city’s distinctive and relatively unsung cultural institutions. On Sunday afternoon it will host a free reception for its exhibition “Treasures of Sailors’ Snug Harbor.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gems From the Sea', 'kicker': 'Weekend Miser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Snug Harbor Cultural Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morgan Library & Museum', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T22:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'fi