Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican National Committee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-28T23:16:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bca515b-ae4f-50b6-b1d8-6e6ae0e95a68', 'word_count': 486, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bca515b-ae4f-50b6-b1d8-6e6ae0e95a68'}, {'abstract': 'Members of United Nations agencies and Doctors Without Borders have been held by the Burmese government in an area where sectarian violence erupted this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/asia/humanitarian-workers-detained-in-myanmar.html', 'snippet': 'Members of United Nations agencies and Doctors Without Borders have been held by the Burmese government in an area where sectarian violence erupted this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — The United Nations and several humanitarian agencies that operate in Myanmar said Thursday that a number of their staff members had been detained by the government in a part of the country where sectarian violence erupted this month, and that they were trying to secure their release. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aid Workers Detained in Myanmar', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aid Workers Detained in Myanmar', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Doctors Without Borders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 4, 'majo