 survey of nearly 2,000 retired officers found that the manipulation of crime reports — downgrading crimes to lesser offenses and discouraging victims from filing complaints to make crime statistics look better — has long been part of the culture of the New York Police Department. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Crime Report Manipulation Is Common Among New York Police, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Crime Report Manipulation Is Common Among New York Police, Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eterno, John A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality and Misconduct', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falsification of Data', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverman, Eli B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T00:21:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendy Ruderman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruderman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ade2cb8-5656-5308-9043-39e886e47bc8', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ade2cb8-5656-5308-9043-39e886e47bc8'}, {'abstract': 'Review our online and sample sale picks of the week, and find some great markdowns.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/online-sale-picks-for-june-28/', 'snippet': 'Review our online and sample sale picks of the week, and find some great markdowns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barneys.com Acne’s colored jeans, VPL lingerie and other designer goodies all up to 60 percent off.When: Ongoing', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Sale Picks for June 28', 'kicker': 'On the Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T00:25:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ana J. Calderone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ana', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Calderone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0984733c-6da5-57b1-a41e-fbecf375e29b', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0984733c-6da5-57b1-a41e-fbecf375e29b'}, {'abstract': 'The fractured left fibula that Andy Pettitte sustained will keep him sidelined for at least two months.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/pettittes-earliest-return-is-aug-28/', 'snippet': 'The fractured left fibula that Andy Pettitte sustained will keep him sidelined for at least two months.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Placed on the 60-day disabled list Thursday with a fractured left fibula, Andy Pettitte won’t be eligible to return until Aug. 28. He hadn’t expected to miss the rest of his summer when a sharp grounder struck him on Wednesday. His shins had taken plenty of hits before, and he told himself that the pain seemed tolerable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pettitte’s Earliest Return Is Aug. 28', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pettitte, Andy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T00:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b1da1c1-76d0-57e2-a4a5-ca3f5875e4b9', 'word_count': 347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b1da1c1-76d0-57e2-a4a5-ca3f5875e4b9'}, {'abstract': 'William Leer won the second heat of the men’s 1,500 meters with a time of 3:40.79. And he did it sporting a serious, serious mustache.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/man-and-mustache-advance-at-trials/', 'snippet': 'William Leer won the second heat of the men’s 1,500 meters with a time of 3:40.79. And he did it sporting a serious, serious mustache.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EUGENE, Ore. — Is facial hair making a comeback in track?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Man and Mustache Advance at Trials', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T00:44:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Pilon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pilon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36db75dd-03c0-58b7-9519-e526ec033c66', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36db75dd-03c0-58b7-9519-e526ec033c66'}, {'abstract': 'In upholding President Obama’s health care plan, the chief justice made two incompatible arguments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/opinion/a-confused-opinion.html', 'snippet': 'In upholding President Obama’s health care plan, the chief justice made two incompatible arguments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE stunner yesterday was that Chief Justice John G. Roberts Jr., joined by the Supreme Court’s four most liberal justices, wrote the majority opinion that upheld the individual mandate in President Obama’s signature Affordable Care Act, which requires Americans to obtain health insurance or pay a penalty. In an ironic twist, the chief justice simultaneously accepted the conservative argument that Congress’s power to regulate interstate commerce did not include the power to regulate economic inactivity, like a decision not to purchase health care. The court ruled 5 to 4 on that point, with the chief justice joined by the court’s four other conservative justices.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Confused Opinion', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Confused Opinion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interstate Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T00:46:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Epstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Epstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a4f004f-7a33-5d79-8a1a-b87bdb0a0d2a', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a4f004f-7a33-5d79-8a1a-b87bdb0a0d2a'}, {'abstract': 'Last-minute waivers will spare China and Singapore from potentially onerous financial penalties required under a strict American law on Iran sanctions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/us-exempts-china-and-singapore-from-sanctions-on-iranian-oil.html', 'snippet': 'Last-minute waivers will spare China and Singapore from potentially onerous financial penalties required under a strict American law on Iran sanctions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Acting at the last minute, the Obama administration on Thursday spared China and Singapore from potentially onerous financial penalties required under a strict American law on Iran sanctions, saying that both countries had earned an exemption by significantly reducing their purchases of Iranian crude oil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Exempts Singapore and China on Iran Oil', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Exempts Singapore And China On Iran Oil', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran'