ge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Modesty and Audacity', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Modesty And Audacity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interstate Commerce', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T00:58:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/86dc3b88-211a-5b92-83c2-a91d1ec23d23', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86dc3b88-211a-5b92-83c2-a91d1ec23d23'}, {'abstract': 'Russell Martin’s sore back acted up, and he was held out of the Yankees’ lineup in Thursday night’s game.', 'web_url': 'https://bats.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/martin-out-of-lineup-again/', 'snippet': 'Russell Martin’s sore back acted up, and he was held out of the Yankees’ lineup in Thursday night’s game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russell Martin’s sore back acted up again on Thursday and he was left out of the starting lineup for the Yankees game against the Chicago White Sox. Chris Stewart returned behind the plate.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Martin Out of Lineup Again', 'kicker': 'Bats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Russell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T01:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Waldstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waldstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/115614e9-c26d-5f25-8a05-ffc5f6ecf6ea', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/115614e9-c26d-5f25-8a05-ffc5f6ecf6ea'}, {'abstract': 'Following the Supreme Court’s decision on health care, Mitt Romney has no choice but to run against himself.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/romneys-supreme-burden/', 'snippet': 'Following the Supreme Court’s decision on health care, Mitt Romney has no choice but to run against himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congratulations to Mitt Romney! His signature contribution to American life, devising a health plan that became a model for the only major Western democracy without medical care for nearly all of its citizens, has been upheld. If Romney accomplishes nothing else in life, he will go down in history as the man who first proved, in the laboratory of Massachusetts, where he once governed, that an individual mandate could work.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney’s Supreme Burden', 'kicker': 'Timothy Egan', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T01:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/008d9b69-8638-583e-9e4d-da74ea85e423', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/008d9b69-8638-583e-9e4d-da74ea85e423'}, {'abstract': 'Cummings, a 12-season N.B.A. veteran, spent four seasons with the Knicks, averaging double-digit scoring in two of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/sports/basketball/pat-cummings-rugged-nba-forward-dies-at-55.html', 'snippet': 'Cummings, a 12-season N.B.A. veteran, spent four seasons with the Knicks, averaging double-digit scoring in two of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pat Cummings, who played 12 seasons in the N.B.A., including four seasons at power forward with the Knicks in the 1980s, was found dead on Tuesday at an apartment in Greenwich Village. He was 55.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/CUMMINGS-obit/CUMMINGS-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 874, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/CUMMINGS-obit/CUMMINGS-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1748, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/sports/CUMMINGS-obit/CUMMINGS-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum