for the food industry.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/HUNTS/HUNTS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/HUNTS/HUNTS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/HUNTS/HUNTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/HUNTS/HUNTS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/HUNTS/HUNTS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Food Company Deepens Roots in the Bronx, but Reception Is Mixed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Food Company Deepens Roots in Bronx, But Reception Is Mixed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FreshDirect', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Chefs' Warehouse", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hunts Point (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T01:05:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49d1f398-50d5-50c9-a19b-4a224013f0bb', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49d1f398-50d5-50c9-a19b-4a224013f0bb'}, {'abstract': 'As the giant McCarren Pool in north Brooklyn deteriorated — amid arguments, some racially tinged, over its future — the neighborhood changed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/nyregion/mccarren-pool-in-brooklyn-reopens-after-28-years.html', 'snippet': 'As the giant McCarren Pool in north Brooklyn deteriorated — amid arguments, some racially tinged, over its future — the neighborhood changed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 28 years, McCarren Pool sat empty on the Williamsburg-Greenpoint border in Brooklyn, its enormous basin growing cracks and sprouting weeds. One by one, the 10 other public pools that opened in New York City during the scorching summer of 1936 were revamped, but not McCarren. A generation of Brooklyn children learned of its invigorating charms only from their parents who had swum there when they were children.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/POOL/POOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/POOL/POOL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/nyregion/POOL/POOL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024,