le', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neal K. Katyal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neal', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Katyal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4be610a-b706-5a57-8ed1-69609ae2852e', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4be610a-b706-5a57-8ed1-69609ae2852e'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday upheld most of President Obama’s health care overhaul law, saying it was authorized by Congress’s power to levy taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/28/us/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday upheld most of President Obama’s health care overhaul law, saying it was authorized by Congress’s power to levy taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court on Thursday upheld most of President Obama’s health care overhaul law, saying it was authorized by Congress’s power to levy taxes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/28/us/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/28/us/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5/20120629_SCOTUS_HTML-slide-93I5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Upholds Health Care Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T01:53:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/1d684d34-41e5-5f4b-8f84-5ef163f16aef', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/1d684d34-41e5-5f4b-8f84-5ef163f16aef'}, {'abstract': 'A Greek man died on Thursday after falling from the Acropolis, the capital’s most prominent landmark, in what appeared to be the latest suicide linked to Greece’s economic hardship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/europe/greece-man-dies-after-fall-from-acropolis.html', 'snippet': 'A Greek man died on Thursday after falling from the Acropolis, the capital’s most prominent landmark, in what appeared to be the latest suicide linked to Greece’s economic hardship.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Greek man died on Thursday after falling from the Acropolis, the capital’s most prominent landmark, in what appeared to be the latest suicide linked to Greece’s economic hardship. A police spokeswoman confirmed that a man in his 40s jumped from the slopes of the hill at about 9 a.m. He was taken to a hospital but died of head injuries a few hours later. The man, who according to Greek media was a bank worker, reportedly fell on the marble bleachers of the ancient Theater of Dionysus, on the southern slopes of the Acropolis Hill, the site of the ancient Parthenon monument. Visitors and guards at the site, Greece’s foremost tourist attraction, said they heard a cry before seeing the man fall into the theater. Local media said the man had reported for work on Thursday at a branch of ATEbank, a state-owned agricultural lender with serious liquidity problems, but left for a break soon after. Suicides have sharply risen in recent months, most of them attributed to financial problems stemming from Greece’s economic crisis. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: Man Dies After Fall From Acropolis', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Man Dies After Fall From Acropolis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T01:55:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/790f511a-c61c-5d56-8077-92cedadeed05', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/790f511a-c61c-5d56-8077-92cedadeed05'}, {'abstract': 'Start your solving weekend with Patrick Berry.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/28/chew-on/', 'snippet': 'Start your solving weekend with Patrick Berry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRIDAY’S PUZZLE — Not bad for a Patrick Berry outing. Not his best, and I will admit that I cringed when I filled in the DESEX/SEXTET crossing. Sure, etymologically the two words are very different so it’s allowable, but it’s just not what I would expect from a Berry byline. There was no heart-grabbing, “Oh, my goodness, I can’t believe he pulled that off!” moment. Maybe I’ve become spoiled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Something to Chew On', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T02:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee939c55-e453-5505-96b1-6c1c1b2047ec', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee939c55-e453-5505-96b1-6c1c1b2047ec'}, {'abstract': 'A Shanghai dairy company announced Thursday that it was recalling a batch of milk that had been contaminated with lye.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/asia/china-tainted-milk-recalled.html', 'snippet': 'A Shanghai dairy company announced Thursday that it was recalling a batch of milk that had been contaminated with lye.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Shanghai dairy company announced Thursday that it was recalling a batch of milk that had been contaminated with lye, a chemical used to clean pipes, according to a message posted on the company’s Web site and a report by Xinhua, the state news agency. The company, Guangming Dairy Group, said it was recalling 300 cartons of tainted milk produced Monday. The Web site said that the milk had been tainted during routine maintenance, and that the company would compensate customers. Contaminated food is a constant issue in China, and many Chinese have been especially vigilant about tainted milk since a 2008 scandal that exposed a common practice in which a toxic chemical, melamine, was added to milk. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China: Tainted Milk Recalled', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Tainted Milk Recalled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Contamination and Poisoning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milk', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T02:01:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ad6873d-7aa1-589b-89d5-86109c129333', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ad6873d-7aa1-589b-89d5-86109c129333'}, {'abstract': 'The two cable news networks initially reported that the Supreme Court had struck down the health care law’s individual mandate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/us/cnn-and-foxs-supreme-court-mistake.html', 'snippet': 'The two cable news networks initially reported that the Supreme Court had struck down the health care law’s individual mandate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The national news media mostly got it right on Thursday in reporting the Supreme Court’s decision to uphold President Obama’s health care overhaul. But the cable news networks CNN and Fox News Channel initially got it wrong, causing consternation behind the scenes. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/us/29cnn1/29cnn1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 609, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/us/29cnn1/29cnn1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1218, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'CNN and Fox Trip Up in Rush to Get the News on the Air', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'CNN and Fox Trip Up in Rush to Get the News on the Air', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T02:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d892ec21-7f99-5cd8-94a5-ba85932dacb2', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d892ec21-7f99-5cd8-94a5-ba85932dacb2'}, {'abstract': 'The Palestinian Islamic group Hamas said Thursday that one of its members had been killed in Damascus, Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/middleeast/syria-hamas-member-killed.html', 'snippet': 'The Palestinian Islamic group Hamas said Thursday that one of its members had been killed in Damascus, Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Palestinian Islamic group Hamas said Thursday that one of its members had been killed in Damascus, Syria. The group did not immediately blame Israel for the death of the man, Kamal Husni Ghanaja, saying it was still investigating. Israel has long fought a shadow war with Hamas, which runs Gaza and advocates armed resistance against Israel. But some Israelis and Palestinians have noted that President Bashar al-Assad of Syria, who is trying to crush an armed uprising, also had a score to settle with Hamas. Hamas has refused to back Mr. Assad and abandoned its longtime base in Damascus a few months ago. Israel Hasson, an Israeli lawmaker and former security official, said that Mr. Ghanaja was responsible for supplying weapons to Hamas. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria: Hamas Member Killed', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Hamas Member Killed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T02:03:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabel Kershner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kershner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6702ec34-ee4b-55bb-9abf-a56345a0137e', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6702ec34-ee4b-55bb-9abf-a56345a0137e'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court ruling upholding Obamacare certainly is a big victory for the president, all right, but the real winners are people like you.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/opinion/the-real-winners.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court ruling upholding Obamacare certainly is a big victory for the president, all right, but the real winners are people like you.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So the Supreme Court — defying many expectations — upheld the Affordable Care Act, a k a Obamacare. There will, no doubt, be many headlines declaring this a big victory for President Obama, which it is. But the real winners are ordinary Americans — people like you. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_