le': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e2a701d-5c13-53cd-a761-0a2f099a2e41', 'word_count': 822, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e2a701d-5c13-53cd-a761-0a2f099a2e41'}, {'abstract': 'A court on Thursday sentenced a former oil minister and a business associate of former President Hosni Mubarak to 15 years in prison for corruption and squandering public funds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/world/middleeast/egypt-ex-official-sentenced.html', 'snippet': 'A court on Thursday sentenced a former oil minister and a business associate of former President Hosni Mubarak to 15 years in prison for corruption and squandering public funds.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A court on Thursday sentenced a former oil minister and a business associate of former President Hosni Mubarak to 15 years in prison for corruption and squandering public funds in the sale of natural gas to Israel. In addition to the former oil minister, Sameh Fahmy, above, five other officials of the ministry and the state-run natural gas company were also sentenced to prison for 3 to 10 years. The businessman, Hussein Salem, was tried in absentia; he is awaiting extradition from Spain. He was among the founders of a company that won a lucrative no-bid contract to act as a middleman in the gas deal. The state news agency said the group was fined a total of $2.3 billion. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/world/brief-fahmy/brief-fahmy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 669, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/world/brief-fahmy/brief-fahmy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1339, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo',