, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69c9af68-3305-5e72-bd9b-c207c2cc3ed2', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69c9af68-3305-5e72-bd9b-c207c2cc3ed2'}, {'abstract': 'The best of readers’ suggestions to put the Indian economy back on track.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/the-winner-of-the-india-ink-finance-minister-contest/', 'snippet': 'The best of readers’ suggestions to put the Indian economy back on track.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, India Ink invited you to submit your “application” to be the next finance minister of India. Well, the entries are in, and we at India Ink have been sifting through what you sent us. You may read all of them in the “Comments” section at the end of the original article.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Announcing … the Winner of India Ink’s Finance Minister Contest', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mukherjee, Pranab', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivek Dehejia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dehejia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06acaa6c-702b-57c0-a785-8f498c2b98f6', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06acaa6c-702b-57c0-a785-8f498c2b98f6'}, {'abstract': 'The quickie impeachment of Paraguay’s president last week suggests that the lines between a coup and a legitimate transfer of power are getting blurry.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/was-the-impeachment-of-paraguays-president-a-coup/', 'snippet': 'The quickie impeachment of Paraguay’s president last week suggests that the lines between a coup and a legitimate transfer of power are getting blurry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTREAL — Judging a change in government in Latin America used to be simple: either tanks were rolling down the street it was a coup and that was bad, or there’d been an election and it was democracy and that was good. No more. These days, the lines between a coup and a legitimate transfer of power are getting a lot blurrier. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s in a Coup?', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impeachment', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lugo Mendez, Fernando', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paraguay', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:19:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francisco Toro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francisco', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29402398-3cf2-5672-9296-1d0a6e2196da', 'word_count': 708, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29402398-3cf2-5672-9296-1d0a6e2196da'}, {'abstract': 'The young Americans Christina McHale and Sloane Stephens face key tests on Friday at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/matches-to-watch-day-5/', 'snippet': 'The young Americans Christina McHale and Sloane Stephens face key tests on Friday at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the fourth straight day, there are leftover matches from the previous day. One of Tuesday’s matches to watch, the second-round encounter between Sam Querrey and Milos Raonic, was halted because of darkness with the two knotted at one-set all and 3-3 in the third. They have just resumed on No. 1 Court. Here’s a fresh slate of five new matches to watch on Friday. Players’ seeds are in parentheses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matches to Watch: Day 5', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Djokovic, Novak', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stepanek, Radek', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:20:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fad46ee1-7005-52f4-bbb2-a1eb9bb72d3f', 'word_count': 856, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fad46ee1-7005-52f4-bbb2-a1eb9bb72d3f'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/morning-take-out-516/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the DealBook newsletter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOP STORIES ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Take-Out', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce340885-baf8-5d83-a975-f945d9297abf', 'word_count': 2566, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce340885-baf8-5d83-a975-f945d9297abf'}, {'abstract': 'The old-fashioned chore board has been reborn as an iPhone app called ChoreMonster. It assigns children tasks, tracks their completion via e-mails to parents, and gives children points, which can be applied to rewards of the parent’s choosing.', 'web_url': 'https://gadgetwise.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/an-app-that-prompts-children-to-do-their-chores/', 'snippet': 'The old-fashioned chore board has been reborn as an iPhone app called ChoreMonster. It assigns children tasks, tracks their completion via e-mails to parents, and gives children points, which can be applied to rewards of the parent’s choosing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a preteen I was fascinated with a neighbor’s chore board. I recall a rotating wheel, color coding and a list of household assignments. It showed who was to do what task that week, and it had a points system that led to rewards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An App That Prompts Children to Do Their Chores', 'kicker': 'Gadgetwise', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:30:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roy Furchgott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Furchgott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64751fdd-ab0b-5f80-8324-d15400ccb7c1', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64751fdd-ab0b-5f80-8324-d15400ccb7c1'}, {'abstract': 'Companies that aren’t successful yet in mobile could take some tips from Gilt Groupe. The New York-based start-up, best known for selling designer clothing, expects 40 percent of its revenue on the July 4th holiday to come from its iPhone and iPad apps, says the company’s chief executive.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/gilt-groupe-mobile/', 'snippet': 'Companies that aren’t successful yet in mobile could take some tips from Gilt Groupe. The New York-based start-up, best known for selling designer clothing, expects 40 percent of its revenue on the July 4th holiday to come from its iPhone and iPad...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Companies that aren’t successful yet in mobile (like Facebook) could take some tips from Gilt Groupe. The New York-based start-up, best known for selling designer clothing, expects 40 percent of its revenue on the July 4th holiday to come from its iPhone and iPad apps, says the company’s chief executive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/technology/29bits-gilt/29bits-gilt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/technology/29bits-gilt/29bits-gilt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 960, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gilt Groupe’s Recipe for Success in Mobile', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gilt Groupe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:37:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40d01f87-e608-510c-a28b-d10139a64fb9', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40d01f87-e608-510c-a28b-d10139a64fb9'}, {'abstract': "One of the many big changes coming to the city schools next year is the revamping of the special education program, which calls for more inclusion classrooms, with special education classes reserved for only the most severely disabled students. Now comes word that the city is creating a hot line so that parents can easily reach education officials if they have questions or problems with their child's placement or services that can't be addressed by the school.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/schoolbook/2012/06/29/questions-on-special-ed-theres-a-hotline-for-that/', 'snippet': 'One of the many big changes coming to the city schools next year is the revamping of the special education program, which calls for more inclusion classrooms, with special education classes reserved for only the most severely disabled students. No...', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Questions on Special Ed? There's a Hot Line for That", 'kicker': 'SchoolBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T12:40:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By MARY ANN GIORDANO', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Ann', 'lastname': 'GIORDANO', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00792229-4f02-5954-8f1e-a148a0be5b2f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00792229-4f02-5954-8f1e-a148a0be5b2f'}, {'abstract': 'Our columnist interviews George Howell, who continues to revolutionize how coffee is traded, roasted and prepared nearly 40 years after getting into the business.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/ristretto-the-old-guard-is-new-again/', 'snippet': 'Our columnist interviews George Howell, who continues to revolutionize how coffee is traded, roasted and prepared nearly 40 years after getting into the business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the old guard is also the avant-garde. Richard Serra still has his edge, ditto Patti Smith — the two artists surfaced in the 1970s, flirted with mainstream success and seem more comfortable hanging out at the fringe of the establishment than taking a seat at the table.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ristretto | The Old Guard Is New Again', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Strand', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strand', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/289e2e8a-72e8-5e4b-9b73-1fc963dfe550', 'word_count': 1553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/289e2e8a-72e8-5e4b-9b73-1fc963dfe550'}, {'abstract': 'The Swiss financial giant moved to calm investors’ fears on Friday by announcing it expected to report a second-quarter profit.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/credit-suisse-expects-profit-in-second-quarter/', 'snippet': 'The Swiss financial giant moved to calm investors’ fears on Friday by announcing it expected to report a second-quarter profit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – Credit Suisse moved to calm investors’ fears on Friday by announcing it expected to report a second-quarter profit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Suisse Expects Profit in Second Quarter', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Credit Suisse Group A.G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3e23086-c346-5a19-9b39-47c5d03d4b7a', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3e23086-c346-5a19-9b39-47c5d03d4b7a'}, {'abstract': 'The $2.2 billion deal will give Sony control over a huge catalog — from “Over the Rainbow” to songs by Amy Winehouse.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/passing-final-hurdle-sonys-deal-for-emi-publishing-is-approved-by-u-s/', 'snippet': 'The $2.2 billion deal will give Sony control over a huge catalog — from “Over the Rainbow” to songs by Amy Winehouse.', 'lead_paragraph': '7:38 p.m. | Updated An investor group led by Sony closed its $2.2 billion acquisition of EMI Music Publishing on Friday, creating a giant force in music publishing, the unglamorous but lucrative side of the music business that deals with songwriting rights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sony Closes Its Acquisition of EMI Music Publishing', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Group PLC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'EMI Music Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SONY/ATV Music Publishing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:08:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/532a4bf8-7515-5678-bd86-b941bbe5beaa', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/532a4bf8-751