 [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lester, Kenneth R Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Mara, Mark M", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, Shellie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:36:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6de76fb4-e5cf-509d-a7ad-f134557efe9a', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6de76fb4-e5cf-509d-a7ad-f134557efe9a'}, {'abstract': 'Also, Rupert Murdoch defends his newspaper holdings, and Twitter bests Google and Facebook in mobile ad sales.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/the-breakfast-meeting-rush-to-report-health-care-ruling-and-as-the-anchor-turns/', 'snippet': 'Also, Rupert Murdoch defends his newspaper holdings, and Twitter bests Google and Facebook in mobile ad sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the day of a historic Supreme Court ruling on the health care law, two cable news outlets — CNN and Fox News Channel — briefly made themselves the story, Brian Stelter writes. In trying to synthesize a complicated ruling, both reported that the court had struck down the law’s individual mandate, when in fact, in a 5-to-4 vote, the court had upheld the mandate as a tax; at CNN, the mistake lingered for six minutes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Breakfast Meeting: Rush to Report Health Care Ruling, and ‘As the Anchor Turns’', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curry, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg Business News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fox News Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wall Street Journal', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:38:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a00d6ce-4e6a-5058-9868-3ae4f34204c7', 'word_count': 435, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a00d6ce-4e6a-5058-9868-3ae4f34204c7'}, {'abstract': 'Stocks on Wall Street surged after European leaders agreed to use bailout funds to recapitalize struggling banks directly. Euro zone shares closed ahead 5 percent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/business/daily-stock-market-activity.html', 'snippet': 'Stocks on Wall Street surged after European leaders agreed to use bailout funds to recapitalize struggling banks directly. Euro zone shares closed ahead 5 percent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was the relief rally that beleaguered investors were waiting for as a new plan to tackle the European banking crisis sent stock markets in many countries to their best day of the year on Friday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/business/Markets/Markets-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/business/Markets/Markets-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1405, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Markets Cheer Europe’s Bailout Plan', 'kicker': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Markets Cheer Europe’s Bailout Plan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Popper and Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Popper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0936d51-85a2-53f6-9012-1fbd17e49660', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0936d51-85a2-53f6-9012-1fbd17e49660'}, {'abstract': 'Invoking academic freedom, officials say they plan no inquiry into a new university institute that critics say distorted the safety record of fracking.', 'web_url': 'https://green.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/university-will-not-investigate-fracking-institute/', 'snippet': 'Invoking academic freedom, officials say they plan no inquiry into a new university institute that critics say distorted the safety record of fracking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The State University of New York at Buffalo has rebuffed calls for an investigation of the work of a new institute it founded that is devoted to the study of shale gas drilling, saying it is defending the freedom of faculty members to conduct research.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'University Will Not Investigate Fracking Institute', 'kicker': 'Green', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drilling and Boring', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Natural Gas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State University of New York at Buffalo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Marcellus Shale', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T13:55:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mireya Navarro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mireya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Navarro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2926136c-9fc0-5937-be79-963611ef24d9', 'word_count': 623, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2926136c-9fc0-5937-be79-963611ef24d9'}, {'abstract': 'Posting about a personal loss online makes people — both the poster and the readers — uncomfortable. No one wants to see morbid thoughts and ruminations about death sandwiched between cheery updates about last night’s party and celebrity chatter. Why does the social Web seem limited to a few emotions?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/digital-diary-talking-about-death-online/', 'snippet': 'Posting about a personal loss online makes people — both the poster and the readers — uncomfortable. No one wants to see morbid thoughts and ruminations about death sandwiched between cheery updates about last night’s party and celebrity chatter. ...', 'lead_paragraph': ' Here’s a shortlist of the things I post about on the Internet on any given day of the week: the latest Rihanna remix, excerpts from interesting bits of writing around the Web, GIFs that made me crack up at my desk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Digital Diary: Talking About Death Online', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grief (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T14:00:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jenna Wortham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jenna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wortham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/036825ac-8c18-5de9-b108-74256170ac98', 'word_count': 863, 'uri': 'nyt://article/036825ac-8c18-5de9-b108-74256170ac98'}, {'abstract': 'The miseries of millions of Pakistanis trying to cope with repeated power outages are testament to the corruption and ineptitude of the Pakistani government.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/when-the-lights-go-out-in-pakistan/', 'snippet': 'The miseries of millions of Pakistanis trying to cope with repeated power outages are testament to the corruption and ineptitude of the Pakistani government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARACHI — For the first time in his 25 years of cleaning homes in Karachi’s posh residential neighborhoods, Ijaz Bashir has to break his own rules: he asks his employers for an advance on his salary. Owing to prolonged power outages, food supplies are rotting in his warm fridge. Pakistan faces a shortfall of 5,733 megawatts — out of a nationwide requirement of approximately 19,000 megawatts — and power cuts for up to 20 hours a day are common. “It’s my own fault,” Ijaz says. “I should have remembered not to buy perishable items in bulk.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When the Lights Go Out', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Outages and Blackouts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashraf, Raja Pervez', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T14:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Huma Yusuf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Huma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yusuf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/040d0130-da3d-5230-bae3-43584cfc5f5d', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/040d0130-da3d-5230-bae3-43584cfc5f5d'}, {'abstract': 'Paris', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2012/06/29/fashion/runway-mens/junya-watanabe-spring-2013-menswear.html', 'snippet': 'Paris', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris', 'sourc