t leave the average child who enjoys a pickup basketball game but is far from Olympic material?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/your-money/redefining-success-and-celebrating-the-unremarkable.html', 'snippet': 'Many of us define success as being extraordinary, but where does that leave the average child who enjoys a pickup basketball game but is far from Olympic material?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’VE been thinking a lot about the ordinary and extraordinary lately. All year, my sons’ school newsletters were filled with stories about students winning prizes for university-level scientific research, stellar musical accomplishments and statewide athletic laurels. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/30/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Redefining Success and Celebrating the Ordinary', 'kicker': 'Shortcuts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Redefining Success And Celebrating the Ordinary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T15:31:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alina Tugend', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tugend', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ddc4ccb-0123-5314-9aea-cf3af4684a97', 'word_count': 1363, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ddc4ccb-0123-5314-9aea-cf3af4684a97'}, {'abstract': 'Minority residents in Georgia have increased dramatically, but there’s been a mass exodus of white Southerners from the Democratic Party, fueling a Republican ascendance.', 'web_url': 'https://fivethirtyeight.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/presidential-geography-georgia/', 'snippet': 'Minority residents in Georgia have increased dramatically, but there’s been a mass exodus of white Southerners from the Democratic Party, fueling a Republican ascendance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today we continue our Presidential Geography series, a one-by-one examination of the economic and demographic peculiarities that drive the politics in all 50 states and the District of Columbia. Today’s stop: Georgia, the Peach State. FiveThirtyEight spoke with Merle Black, a professor of politics and government at Emory University, and Charles S. Bullock III, a professor of political science at the University of Georgia.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Presidential Geography: Georgia', 'kicker': 'FiveThirtyEight', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T15:32:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Micah Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Micah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8076f99-2c21-54a0-88ea-969820ee0d7d', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8076f99-2c21-54a0-88ea-969820ee0d7d'}, {'abstract': 'After his career was interrupted by a third major knee injury, the Mets’ Daniel Murphy found a way to untether his identity from the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/sports/baseball/finding-a-balance-despite-injuries-position-changes-and-a-slump.html', 'snippet': 'After his career was interrupted by a third major knee injury, the Mets’ Daniel Murphy found a way to untether his identity from the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — There is an image of Daniel Murphy, shaped slowly over the length of his professional baseball career, as a man unsettled.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30murphy1/30murphy1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 711, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30murphy1/30murphy1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1423, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30murphy1/30murphy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30murphy1/30murphy1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30mu