 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d6466fa-2132-50e7-999f-ee4c414ecb55', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d6466fa-2132-50e7-999f-ee4c414ecb55'}, {'abstract': 'In a match that was suspended because of darkness, Sam Querrey defeated Milos Raonic at Wimbledon.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/in-the-light-of-day-querrey-defeats-raonic/', 'snippet': 'In a match that was suspended because of darkness, Sam Querrey defeated Milos Raonic at Wimbledon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — In a hard-serving battle stalled by darkness, Sam Querrey of the United States surged back from a first-set stumble and defeated Milos Raonic of Canada, 6-7 (3), 7-6 (7), 7-6 (8), 6-4, on Friday in the second round of the 2012 Wimbledon Championships.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Light of Day, Querrey Defeats Raonic', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Querrey, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raonic, Milos', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T15:54:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca26536b-ae4d-5803-83a7-d83066b78ee2', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca26536b-ae4d-5803-83a7-d83066b78ee2'}, {'abstract': 'Recent Italian government reports “show that domestic demand is weak in Italy and is unlikely to improve substantially any time soon.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/business/economy/in-italy-consumer-confidence-reaches-record-low.html', 'snippet': 'Recent Italian government reports “show that domestic demand is weak in Italy and is unlikely to improve substantially any time soon.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS their recession deepens, Italians appear to be more worried about the future than they have been in decades, and they are responding by closing their purses and wallets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Italians, Their Confidence at a Record Low, Sharply Cut Their Spending', 'kicker': 'Off the Charts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Italians, Their Confidence at a Record Low, Sharply Cut Their Spending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Confidence (Economic Indicator)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T15:57:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Floyd Norris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Floyd', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Norris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d896df11-5d40-5d30-9841-d0a7bed54f90', 'word_count': 534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d896df11-5d40-5d30-9841-d0a7bed54f90'}, {'abstract': 'Bucks readers offer their opinions on classes that teach teenagers about spending, saving and investments.', 'web_url': 'https://bucks.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/an-early-education-in-finance/', 'snippet': 'Bucks readers offer their opinions on classes that teach teenagers about spending, saving and investments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paul Sullivan’s Wealth Matters column this week is about a program, Investing in Girls, that aims to open up finance as a possible career path for teenage girls. The program, run by a nonprofit group, pairs girls in the program with woman who are working in finance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Early Education in Finance', 'kicker': 'Bucks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T15:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bucks Editors', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bucks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Editors', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7baed882-f2ea-5a14-8423-4f9928595c75', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7baed882-f2ea-5a14-8423-4f9928595c75'}, {'abstract': 'Economic conditions are weakening across the board in Italy', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/29/business/economy/fear-rises-in-italy.html', 'snippet': 'Economic conditions are weakening across the board in Italy', 'lead_paragraph': 'Economic conditions are weakening across the board in Italy', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear Rises in Italy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Confidence (Economic Indicator)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T15:58:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/181739f6-96f3-5bb2-ae7a-14c0869fa212', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/181739f6-96f3-5bb2-ae7a-14c0869fa212'}, {'abstract': 'Beach volleyball will be in the middle of history at the Olympics in London this summer (and the sand is local).', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/know-that-venue-beach-volleyball-at-the-horse-guards-parade/', 'snippet': 'Beach volleyball will be in the middle of history at the Olympics in London this summer (and the sand is local).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those at a beach volleyball match at the London Olympics this summer will find themselves seated smack dab in the middle of history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Know That Venue: Beach Volleyball at the Horse Guards Parade', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beach Volleyball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:00:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5161c05c-b539-5a13-be9f-b50ccfd82fce', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5161c05c-b539-5a13-be9f-b50ccfd82fce'}, {'abstract': 'The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences this week decreed that the Oscar for makeup will henceforth be called the “makeup and hairstyling award.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/and-the-oscar-goes-to-the-bouffant/', 'snippet': 'The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences this week decreed that the Oscar for makeup will henceforth be called the “makeup and hairstyling award.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'It gives Hollywood hairstylists only a whisker of added industry respect, but there is celebrating nonetheless in the celebrity blow-out and bun-knotting world: The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences this week decreed that the Oscar for makeup will henceforth be called the “makeup and hairstyling award.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'And the Oscar Goes to…the Bouffant!', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibson, Ted', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ACADEMY OF MOTION PICTURE ARTS AND SCIENCES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:03:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brooks Barnes and Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a9e5b2e-dcfb-52f3-a950-9cdd7c581fab', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a9e5b2e-dcfb-52f3-a950-9cdd7c581fab'}, {'abstract': 'Geoffrey C. Ward’s great-grandfather, who ran a pyramid scheme, was the Bernie Madoff of the 1880s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/books/review/a-disposition-to-be-rich-by-geoffrey-c-ward.html', 'snippet': 'Geoffrey C. Ward’s great-grandfather, who ran a pyramid scheme, was the Bernie Madoff of the 1880s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of Americans loved Ulysses S. Grant, but, as so often with love, the relationship can be hard to understand from the outside. Grant did not woo the public. A rumpled man, he seemed shorter than he was. When he opened his mouth, cigars and whiskey went in, but few words came out. His critics, then and now, have disagreed over whether he should be condemned primarily as a brute of a general or a dupe of a president. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/books/review/01STILES/01STILES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1004, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/books/review/01STILES/01STILES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2009, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/books/review/01STILES/01STILES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/books/review/01STILES/01STILES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/books/review/01STILES/01STILES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dreams of Prosperity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dreams of Prosperity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ward, Ferdinand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ward, Geoffrey C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:06:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By T. J. Stiles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'T.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Stiles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0093a88f-b14f-5215-a332-fb37c6e14dd5', 'word_count': 1256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0093a88f-b14f-5215-a332-fb37c6e14dd5'}, {'abstract': 'Small buses and vans stitching together some of New York’s Chinese neighborhoods now have competition from some large buses whose operators were shut down by federal officials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/nyregion/after-shutdown-buses-shake-up-chinatown-network.html', 'snippet': 'Small buses and vans stitching together some of New York’s Chinese neighborhoods now have competition from some large buses whose operators were shut down by federal officials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Six large, white tour buses rolled up last Sunday morning looking as if they were bound for a casino, and, in fact, some of them bore the faded logos of Atlantic City casinos. But the buses that appeared on this particular block in Queens for the first time were not picking up gamblers. They were loading passengers in Chinatown in Flushing who were traveling to Chinatown in Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/30busses-span/30busses-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headli