ect', 'value': 'Hamburgers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:25:54+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'David Frank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/acd102fd-7b4c-5ba3-9c24-c27616c40728', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/acd102fd-7b4c-5ba3-9c24-c27616c40728'}, {'abstract': 'Times film critics on “People Like Us,” “Ted” and “Magic Mike.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/this-weeks-movies-june-29/', 'snippet': 'Times film critics on “People Like Us,” “Ted” and “Magic Mike.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In today’s edition of This Week’s Movies, our critics look at three Hollywood movies that are neither sequels nor based on a comic book. Stephen Holden offers his thoughts on the drama “People Like Us,” starring Chris Pine and Elizabeth Banks. A. O. Scott weighs in on “Seth MacFarlane’s comedy “Ted,”, about a toy bear who comes to life and turns out to have a filthy mouth. And Manohla Dargis offers a revealing and positive review of “Magic Mike,” Steven Soderbergh’s film starring Channing Tatum as a male stripper. Full reviews for these and all of this week’s movies can be found here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'This Week’s Movies: June 29', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banks, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'MacFarlane, Seth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pine, Chris', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soderbergh, Steven', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tatum, Channing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7406799-9cce-5b4e-95a2-55bd0ea0d88d', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7406799-9cce-5b4e-95a2-55bd0ea0d88d'}, {'abstract': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/weekend-fare-98/', 'snippet': 'Food-related events around New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rotating cast of food trucks will be parked each day from 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. through Labor Day at the New York Public Library, West 40th Street at Fifth Avenue, as part of the exhibition “Lunch Hour NYC.” ’Wichcraft, which has two carts at the library, will promote the exhibit Friday by offering free samples of its peanut butter and jelly sandwiches in the Stephen A. Schwarzman Building on the first floor in Astor Court. The triple-decker sandwiches will be sold for $3 while the exhibition is on display.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Fare', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Independence Day (US) (July 4)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bao Ong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bao', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b12ca1f-ae7d-5ea6-b3a0-06387aade8d1', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b12ca1f-ae7d-5ea6-b3a0-06387aade8d1'}, {'abstract': 'Although Brian Baker lost several years of his professional tennis career to injury, he is handling his recent success in a grounded manner that reflects not only maturity but strong character as well.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/after-years-of-injury-a-strong-character-emerges/', 'snippet': 'Although Brian Baker lost several years of his professional tennis career to injury, he is handling his recent success in a grounded manner that reflects not only maturity but strong character as well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday morning I ran into Alex Zotov, a former Davis Cup player for Belarus. He played college tennis at Vanderbilt University, where I coach the women’s team, and we started talking about Brian Baker. A year ago Zotov and Baker were playing in the Middle Tennessee Tennis League.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Years of Injury, a Strong Character Emerges', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:32:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ce9aa9b-22ee-56e6-86fd-a181b1eae744', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ce9aa9b-22ee-56e6-86fd-a181b1eae744'}, {'abstract': 'The two automakers signed a memorandum on Friday that would have the automakers co-develop a sports car as well as share hybrid and diesel technologies.', 'web_url': 'https://wheels.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/bmw-and-toyota-sign-agreement-to-collaborate-on-new-products-and-technologies/', 'snippet': 'The two automakers signed a memorandum on Friday that would have the automakers co-develop a sports car as well as share hybrid and diesel technologies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As vehicle manufacturers seek less expensive ways to produce desirable products and meet ever more stringent corporate fuel economy standards, teamwork is a recurring theme. On Friday, BMW Group and the Toyota Motor Corporation announced a collaborative effort aimed at developing new products and advanced-powertrain technologies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BMW and Toyota Sign Agreement to Collaborate on New Products and Technologies', 'kicker': 'Wheels', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reithofer, Norbert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toyoda, Akio', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bayerische Motorenwerke AG', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Toyota Motor Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:33:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Stenquist', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stenquist', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/16bec83f-9629-5981-b11a-44a381fc03f7', 'word_count': 409, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16bec83f-9629-5981-b11a-44a381fc03f7'}, {'abstract': 'On Twitter, gymnasts provide a glimpse of what it is like to compete for a spot on the U.S. Olympic team.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/18-moments-elite-gymnasts-behind-the-scenes/', 'snippet': 'On Twitter, gymnasts provide a glimpse of what it is like to compete for a spot on the U.S. Olympic team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes social media can feel like a giant, all-encompassing scrapbook your great aunt is forcing you to flip through — again. But if that book were pared down, there would be be some real gems. If you take away the noise of a thousand hash tags and the cacophony of fans, you’re left with a glimmer of what it is like for elite gymnasts competing for a spot on the Olympic team.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '18 Moments: Elite Gymnasts, Behind the Scenes', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Jose (Calif)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:33:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Samantha Storey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Samantha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Storey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d384acff-165e-5bc0-96d8-bf9cd09fe188', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d384acff-165e-5bc0-96d8-bf9cd09fe188'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Jackson’s four older brothers — Jermaine, Marlon, Tito and Jackie — performed a show that balanced carefully between respect and exploitation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/arts/music/review-the-jacksons-pay-homage-at-the-apollo.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Jackson’s four older brothers — Jermaine, Marlon, Tito and Jackie — performed a show that balanced carefully between respect and exploitation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was no avoiding thoughts of Michael Jackson when the Jacksons — his four older brothers, Jermaine, Marlon, Tito and Jackie — brought their Unity Tour to the Apollo Theater on Thursday night. Just over three years after Michael Jackson’s death, it was a show that treaded carefully between respect and exploitation. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/30jacksons-1/30jacksons-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/30jacksons-1/30jacksons-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/30jacksons-1/30jacksons-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/30jacksons-1/30jacksons-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/30jacksons-1/30jacksons-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'he