, an individual’s responsibility for the welfare of others, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uwe E. Reinhardt is an economics professor at Princeton. He has some financial interests in the health care field.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Care: Solidarity vs. Rugged Individualism', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libertarianism (US Politics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:36:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Uwe E. Reinhardt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Uwe', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Reinhardt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/623920ee-998f-56fe-b49b-c60e2e1942b7', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/623920ee-998f-56fe-b49b-c60e2e1942b7'}, {'abstract': 'The South African was hoping to become the first amputee runner to compete in the Olympics, which could still happen if he is selected for his nation’s 4x400 relay team.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/sports/olympics/oscar-pistorius-fails-to-meet-qualifying-time-for-olympics.html', 'snippet': 'The South African was hoping to become the first amputee runner to compete in the Olympics, which could still happen if he is selected for his nation’s 4x400 relay team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oscar Pistorius, trying to become the first amputee runner to compete in the Olympics, failed to meet the qualifying time for the 400 meters and now must hope to be selected for South Africa’s 4x400 relay team. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30pistorius1/30pistorius1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 761, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30pistorius1/30pistorius1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1522, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30pistorius1/30pistorius1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30pistorius1/30pistorius1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/sports/30pistorius1/30pistorius1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oscar Pistorius Fails to Meet Qualifying Time for Olympics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pistorius Fails to Meet Qualifying Time', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pistorius, Oscar', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fbcfd31-2e31-5831-aa91-039de0a43b6c', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fbcfd31-2e31-5831-aa91-039de0a43b6c'}, {'abstract': 'The chivito is now considered the ultimate Uruguayan snack, offered on menus all over the country and even in Argentina.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/04/dining/small-steak-sandwiches-that-satisfy-city-kitchen.html', 'snippet': 'The chivito is now considered the ultimate Uruguayan snack, offered on menus all over the country and even in Argentina.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the story goes, an Argentine lady on vacation walked into a beach-side restaurant in Punta del Este, Uruguay, and requested a sandwich, specifying it be made with chivito, grilled baby goat, the kind she could get back home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 856, 'width': 1286, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/04/dining/04KITCH1_SPAN/04KITCH1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 100, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Uruguay, a Sandwich to Rival the Reuben', 'kicker': 'City Kitchen', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Uruguay, a Sandwich to Rival the Reuben', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sandwiches', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beef', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uruguay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:45:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f54ea459-d2fa-53f2-b3c2-1b0c0e357ac3', 'word_count': 411, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f54ea459-d2fa-53f2-b3c2-1b0c0e357ac3'}, {'abstract': 'The programming is to begin in September with the inauguration of Dartmouth’s new arts district.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/yo-yo-ma-and-alvin-ailey-part-of-dartmouths-culture-celebration/', 'snippet': 'The programming is to begin in September with the inauguration of Dartmouth’s new arts district.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Yo-Yo Ma, John Lithgow, Alvin Ailey American Dance Theater and the Jazz at Lincoln Center Orchestra are among the artists to be featured in Dartmouth College’s special celebration of culture for the 2012-13 academic year, the New Hampshire college announced Friday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yo-Yo Ma and Alvin Ailey Part of Dartmouth’s Culture Celebration', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jarmusch, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lithgow, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ma, Yo-Yo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da594022-94d6-5c51-b16a-cc4b2f911fef', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da594022-94d6-5c51-b16a-cc4b2f911fef'}, {'abstract': 'The national snack of Uruguay is simple to prepare.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/its-like-a-burger-but-perhaps-even-gasp-better/', 'snippet': 'The national snack of Uruguay is simple to prepare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re in the mood to grill, why not make a chivito, the summery steak sandwich featured in this week’s City Kitchen column? Just as easy to make as a hamburger, but arguably better, it’s the iconic national snack of Uruguay. Essentially a chivito is a somewhat overstuffed affair with a thin slice of grilled beef on a roll, layered with burger-type accompaniments, and extras, like cheese, roasted peppers, grilled onions, egg, ham or bacon. But the best versions are small and restrained, or at least that’s the way I like them. (There are gargantuan chivitos as well, but I’d rather eat two little ones.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Like a Burger, but Perhaps (Gasp!) Even Better', 'kicker': 'Diner&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beef', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grilling (Cooking)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sandwiches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Uruguay', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:49:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Tanis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa8e786-329d-52bc-875d-7b2ac84f4642', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa8e786-329d-52bc-875d-7b2ac84f4642'}, {'abstract': 'June 29, 2012 - Winning the battle, but losing the war with health care ruling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000001636762/business-day-live-health-care-ruling.html', 'snippet': 'June 29, 2012 - Winning the battle, but losing the war with health care ruling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'June 29, 2012 - Winning the battle, but losing the war with health care ruling.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/business/video-bdl-120629-stewart/video-bdl-120629-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width