fe0-13a18c3afe15'}, {'abstract': 'Forget the “art” of film-making. The real money is in promotion, distribution and merchandise.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/what-a-pile-of-star-wars-figurines-has-to-do-with-smart-movie-making/', 'snippet': 'Forget the “art” of film-making. The real money is in promotion, distribution and merchandise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week in the magazine, Adam Davidson ponders how the film industry actually makes money. In their perfect world, studios could predict what moviegoers want. In reality, they’re stumped. A vast majority of movies fail to break even. So how have studios managed to make a steady profit, even as they churn out a steady stream of flops? Davidson writes that “they have found ways to, as they say, monetize the ancillary stream by selling pay-TV and overseas rights, creating tie-in video games, amusement-park rides and so forth.” Forget the art of making movies. The true artistry is in promotion, distribution and merchandise. Here are a few blockbusters that changed the way studios make money.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What a Pile of Star Wars Figurines Has to Do With Smart Movie-Making', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davidson, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Kedmey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kedmey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f678bec-dee6-5ae2-9813-c36b472054fc', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f678bec-dee6-5ae2-9813-c36b472054fc'}, {'abstract': 'The Olympic swimmer was riveted to the television during the Masters, which Bubba Watson in a sudden-death playoff.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/phelps-gives-a-tip-of-the-golf-cap-to-watson/', 'snippet': 'The Olympic swimmer was riveted to the television during the Masters, which Bubba Watson in a sudden-death playoff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA – Through the magic of Twitter’s direct messaging, Michael Phelps has traded cellphone numbers with the golfer Bubba Watson. If he could, he’d happily trade sports. Phelps, who took up golf after his record eight-gold-medal performance at the 2008 Olympics, said: “I love watching him. I try to hit the ball really far, but he just crushes it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Phelps Gives a Tip of the Golf Cap to Watson', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Masters Golf Tournament', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watson, Bubba', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:51:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb2d11bd-f5a7-5ef1-8184-082dd5f96d10', 'word_count': 296, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb2d11bd-f5a7-5ef1-8184-082dd5f96d10'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Nikki R. Haley, a Republican, had been accused of lobbying on behalf of businesses while she was a state representative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/us/gov-nikki-haley-cleared-in-ethics-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Nikki R. Haley, a Republican, had been accused of lobbying on behalf of businesses while she was a state representative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLUMBIA, S.C. — Gov. Nikki R. Haley was cleared of wrongdoing on Friday by state lawmakers who investigated assertions that she had violated ethics rules when she was a state representative by lobbying on behalf of two businesses she worked for. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ethics Inquiry Exonerates Governor In Lobbying', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ethics Inquiry Exonerates Governor In Lobbying', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Carolina', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haley, Nikki R', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:52:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robbie Brown', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brown', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78249798-6f03-5bd8-ad1e-bddcfc07904c', 'word_count': 667, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78249798-6f03-5bd8-ad1e-bddcfc07904c'}, {'abstract': 'Tyler Perry is back with Madea, a little less sassy in this film, as she shelters a witness in a Ponzi scheme.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/movies/tyler-perrys-madeas-witness-protection-opens.html', 'snippet': 'Tyler Perry is back with Madea, a little less sassy in this film, as she shelters a witness in a Ponzi scheme.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyler Perry has his Madea character on a leash in the latest movie in that franchise, “Tyler Perry’s Madea’s Witness Protection,” a comedy that’s too late to the Ponzi-scheme party to be topical, and not outrageous enough to take advantage of its own setups.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/movies/tyler-inline/tyler-inline-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/movies/tyler-inline/tyler-inline-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1365, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/movies/tyler-inline/tyler-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/29/movies/tyler-inline/tyler-inline-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/29/movies/tyler-inline/tyler-inline-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Woman No One Wants to Tangle With', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Woman No One Wants to Tangle With', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T16:54:16+0000',