ider an appeal by the agency over the 2004 Super Bowl halftime show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Friday refused to consider an appeal by the Federal Communications Commission of an appeals court ruling that overturned the agency’s fine against CBS for its broadcasting a fleeting image of Janet Jackson’s breast during the 2004 Super Bowl halftime show.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Rejects F.C.C. Appeal in Janet Jackson Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Rejects F.C.C. Appeal in Janet Jackson Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indecency, Obscenity and Profanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T17:16:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John H. Cushman Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'H.', 'lastname': 'Cushman', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cee4a5b-27f2-59b5-ac65-6072f80e5acd', 'word_count': 261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cee4a5b-27f2-59b5-ac65-6072f80e5acd'}, {'abstract': 'At this shop, opening Wednesday, the humble snack takes a sophisticated turn.', 'web_url': 'https://dinersjournal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/populence-has-popcorn-for-all-seasons/', 'snippet': 'At this shop, opening Wednesday, the humble snack takes a sophisticated turn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Maggie Paulus, who p