atwoman” issues is No. 1 on the hardcover list.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At No. 1 on our hardcover list this week is Vol. 1 of “Batwoman,” which reprints the first six issues of the continuing series. Like every other mainstream title from DC, “Batwoman” was part of the “New 52,” an overhaul of the company’s characters to spruce them up for a new generation. In September, my colleague Adam Kepler and I reviewed the first issue. Having read the first arc, my impression of the book is very much the same: The artwork by J.H. Williams III, who writes the series with W. Haden Blackman, is simply stunning. The richly detailed drawings and exciting page designs cause my eyes to linger far longer than they do on most comics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graphic Books Best Sellers: ‘Batwoman’ Ascends to the Top', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graphic Novels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T18:15:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7fd84a95-60e4-5d87-8572-271153298f5c', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7fd84a95-60e4-5d87-8572-271153298f5c'}, {'abstract': 'With Americans’ appetites subject to an array of dietary restrictions, balancing one guest’s requirements for gluten free with another’s for meatless can be a juggling act.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/fashion/rsvp-ps-no-gluten-fat-or-soy-please.html', 'snippet': 'With Americans’ appetites subject to an array of 