 and publishing businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wall Street has cheered Rupert Murdoch’s decision to separate News Corporation’s underperforming newspapers from its lucrative entertainment assets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even if News Corp. Divides, the Murdochs’ Control Is Undiluted', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murdoch, Rupert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T18:25:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8edbd419-0c69-5d43-acbd-3fb59292e92c', 'word_count': 329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8edbd419-0c69-5d43-acbd-3fb59292e92c'}, {'abstract': 'The N.B.A. draft showed that it can be a risky proposition for players with lottery-pick potential— like Perry Jones III — to put off going pro even for just one year.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/when-staying-in-school-is-a-bad-move/', 'snippet': 'The N.B.A. draft showed that it can be a risky proposition for players with lottery-pick potential— like Perry Jones III — to put off going pro even for just one year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last night’s N.B.A. draft showed that it is probably not a good idea for players with lottery-pick potential to stay in school. The traditional argument for turning pro as soon as possible has long been: What if a significant injury occurs while a player is (ostensibly) competing for free in in the N.C.A.A., and he never gets the big N.B.A. payday? But the case of Perry Jones III, the Baylor star and subject of my cover article in the magazine on March 8, 2011, raises another question: What if the nagging doubts raised by a promising player in Year 1 of college solidify, in Year 2, into conventional wisdom?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Staying in School Is a Bad Move', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Perry III', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T18:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Sokolove', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sokolove', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cff2b77-38c8-53ae-89de-1be1f321066f', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cff2b77-38c8-53ae-89de-1be1f321066f'}, {'abstract': 'The extended deal, along with an agreement by ABC to continue the broadcast in the United States through 2020, secures a lucrative arrangement for the academy.', 'web_url': 'https://mediadecoder.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/disney-media-unit-to-distribute-oscar-telecast-abroad-through-2020/', 'snippet': 'The extended deal, along with an agreement by ABC to continue the broadcast in the United States through 2020, secures a lucrative arrangement for the academy.', '