, 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/style/01RUSSIANS_SPAN/01RUSSIANS_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Czarinas Are Back', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Czarinas Are Back', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gazinskaya, Vika', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Couture (Fashion)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ziourova, Anya', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perminova, Elena', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duma, Miroslava', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sergeenko, Ulyana', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T20:02:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/817ab498-6cd7-5448-a88f-d3d22c1bef00', 'word_count': 1514, 'uri': 'nyt://article/817ab498-6cd7-5448-a88f-d3d22c1bef00'}, {'abstract': 'Paul Greenberg is blogging via satellite as he travels down the Stuyahok River in search of sockeye salmon, which number 40 million this time of year.', 'web_url': 'https://bittman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/rainbow-trout-both-rare-and-ubiquitous/', 'snippet': 'Paul Greenberg is blogging via satellite as he travels down the Stuyahok River in search of sockeye salmon, which number 40 million this time of year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late June and early July mark the peak of the biggest run of wild salmon left in the world. The sockeye salmon migration of Bristol Bay, Alaska, can number more than 40 million fish, and the commercial fishing industry in the region is worth more than $400 million. During this peak salmon period, Paul Greenberg, author of the New York Times bestseller “Four Fish,” will be blogging remotely via satellite as he travels down the Stuyahok River with the Alaska outfitter Mark Rutherford. This year’s fishing trip is particularly relevant. At present the Environmental Protection Agency is weighing whether to prevent the permitting of a 10 billion-ton copper and gold mine in this remote sensitive area, something many fishermen fear could spell the end of this magnificent run. —Mark Bittman', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rainbow Trout, Both Rare and Ubiquitous', 'kicker': 'Mark Bittman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trout', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenberg, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blue Ocean Institute', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monterey Bay Aquarium', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bristol Bay (Alaska)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T20:05:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original':