ame': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/41b1cdbc-9659-58f1-92f3-b32377c793cc', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/41b1cdbc-9659-58f1-92f3-b32377c793cc'}, {'abstract': 'H J Lim, a YouTube phenomenon advancing rapidly in the classical world, recorded the complete Beethoven piano sonatas at 24.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/arts/music/h-j-lim-classical-pianist-and-youtube-phenomenon.html', 'snippet': 'H J Lim, a YouTube phenomenon advancing rapidly in the classical world, recorded the complete Beethoven piano sonatas at 24.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JUST as actors traditionally portray King Lear later in their careers, pianists usually wait to record Beethoven’s complete piano sonatas. Offering the 32 works at 24 is a bold move, but the Korean pianist H J Lim, who performed the complete cycle in Paris in 2010, felt ready. She demonstrates her mettle with a set of distinctive, passionate interpretations, which landed at No. 1 on Billboard’s classical chart shortly after EMI Classics released them on iTunes in May. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 595, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/arts/01SNAPSHOT/01SNAPSHOT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Following Bliss With Beethoven', 'kicker': 'Snapshot | H J Lim', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Following Bliss With Beethoven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lim, H J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T20:48:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/512fca87-e968-500c-a706-c21256238151', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/512fca87-e968-500c-a706-c21256238151'}, {'abstract': 'Mustard, ketchup and pickles from your own kitchen put the supermarket varieties to shame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/04/dining/homemade-ketchup-mustard-and-pickles-a-good-appetite.html', 'snippet': 'Mustard, ketchup and pickles from your own kitchen put the supermarket varieties to shame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M no slouch when it comes to D.I.Y.-ing it. I confit my own tomatoes every August. I make ricotta, batch up habanero sauce, simmer jams and marmalades and put up homemade maraschino cherries. Once I even churned butter, though that was really an accident involving overbeaten whipped cream.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'