t-at-200-backstroke-medal/', 'snippet': 'Matt Grevers decided the 100-meter freestyle was the way to go after encountering difficult scheduling questions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA – Matt Grevers, who nearly set a world record in the 100-meter backstroke earlier this week, is capable of winning an Olympic medal in the 200-meter backstroke at next month’s London Games. That’s not the issue. He knows it. His coach knows it. No doubt Ryosuke Irie of Japan, another strong medal contender, knows it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grevers Passes on Shot at 200 Backstroke Medal', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grevers, Matt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Omaha (Neb)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T20:55:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/36980110-fc18-5d56-bcb5-15cc4e3e1ab0', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36980110-fc18-5d56-bcb5-15cc4e3e1ab0'}, {'abstract': 'This week’s job-creation projections from Moody’s Analytics continue to point to a close presidential election, and come with indications of midyear weakness.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/soft-patch-on-jobs-with-election-on-horizon/', 'snippet': 'This week’s job-creation projections from Moody’s Analytics continue to point to a close presidential election, and come with indications of midyear weakness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the unemployment report for June due in one week, and the general election a bit more than four months away, the job indicators for the pre-election season remain fragile, according to the latest weekly analysis from Moody’s Analytics. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Soft Patch’ on Jobs, With Election on Horizon', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Moody's Corporation", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T20:57:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By ECONOMIX EDITORS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Economix', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'EDITORS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4be72189-d3ca-5ef7-b65d-708af8426221', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4be72189-d3ca-5ef7-b65d-708af8426221'}, {'abstract': 'Everybody complains about the traffic, but no one does anything about it. That may finally be changing as new technology to track cars becomes more widely used.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/automobiles/in-traffic-next-time-use-an-app