ifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50b300f7-547a-56a8-acec-11fbc12fd80d', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50b300f7-547a-56a8-acec-11fbc12fd80d'}, {'abstract': 'Morphoses performs the premiere of “Within (Labyrinth Within),” paired with a 2010 dance film, at Jacob’s Pillow.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/arts/dance/morphoses-performing-at-jacobs-pillow.html', 'snippet': 'Morphoses performs the premiere of “Within (Labyrinth Within),” paired with a 2010 dance film, at Jacob’s Pillow.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BECKET, Mass. — No one can accuse Morphoses of false advertising. Founded in 2007 by Lourdes Lopez and Christopher Wheeldon, this contemporary ballet company reinvented itself following Mr. Wheeldon’s departure in 2010, shifting from a structure with a permanent artistic director to a rotating system. Ms. Lopez stayed, but choreographers and dancers came in, project by project. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MORPHOSES/MORPHOSES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MORPHOSES/MORPHOSES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MORPHOSES/MORPHOSES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MORPHOSES/MORPHOSES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1307, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb