aragraph': ' Before Facebook, Twitter, Google — even before the Web — there was The Well, an online discussion community founded in Northern California in 1985 that became home to the early denizens of what used to be called cyberspace. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Well, a Pioneering Online Community, Is for Sale Again', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Networking (Internet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T22:04:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/deea2f4c-9e7b-5443-a173-24cb31cf9f39', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/deea2f4c-9e7b-5443-a173-24cb31cf9f39'}, {'abstract': 'European leaders went a surprising distance toward restoring confidence in the shared currency, moving toward tighter economic integration and easing pressure on Spain and Italy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/world/europe/european-leaders-move-toward-deals-for-spain-and-italy.html', 'snippet': 'European leaders went a surprising distance toward restoring confidence in the shared currency, moving toward tighter economic integration and easing pressure on Spain and Italy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — European leaders went a surprising distance on Friday toward restoring confidence in the euro, taking a significant step toward economic integration and easing market pressure on Spain and Italy, as what appeared to be a new coalition of forces pushed Germany to bend.', 'print_s