starts to unfold a flag, play a flute or merely glance at a wristwatch. Then, before any of them utters a sound, they are dragged out of sight by a troop of stocking-capped men.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/MINSK-JP-1/MINSK-JP-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Cities on the Verge of Devouring Themselves', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Cities on the Verge of Devouring Themselves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Belarus Free Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ridley, Philip', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T22:09:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Brantley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brantley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8333bf16-c8ff-517c-ad44-75dfcd8bf631', 'word_count': 1104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8333bf16-c8ff-517c-ad44-75dfcd8bf631'}, {'abstract': 'In a move that puzzles book dealers, Dawn Powell’s biographer, Tim Page, is offering her 43 journals to bidders via the Internet, with a minimum bid of $500,000.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/books/auctioning-dawn-powells-diaries-on-the-web.html', 'snippet': 'In a move that puzzles book dealers, Dawn Powell’s biographer, Tim Page, is offering her 43 journals to bidders via the Internet, with a minimum bid of $500,000.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If it weren’t for Tim Page, the diaries of Dawn Powell wouldn’t be worth much. Mr. Page, a Pulitzer Prize-winning former music critic at The Washington Post (and before that a frequent contributor to The New York Times), has pretty much single-handedly engineered a revival of interest in Powell, a New York novelist greatly admired by critics like Gore Vidal and Edmund Wilson, but whose career, even during her lifetime, was always in need of a jump start. When she died in 1965, most of her 15 novels were out of print. She was buried in a potter’s field.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre