s endemic to contemporary art, like sampling, appropriating and remaking older artworks. ', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 330, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 330}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1402, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSNJ2_SPAN/01ARTSNJ2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Inspiration in a Borrowed Past', 'kicker': 'Arts | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Inspiration In a Borrowed Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montclair (NJ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Montclair Art Museum', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-29T23:22:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Martha Schwendener', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/75b925f0-a43d-500b-b8ce-84d3e68e8763', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/75b925f0-a43d-500b-b8ce-84d3e68e8763'}, {'abstract': 'Cherylyn Lavagnino Dance presented a new work with interlocked choreography for 11 dancers at Danspace Project.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/arts/dance/cherylyn-lavagnino-dance-at-danspace-project.html', 'snippet': 'Cherylyn Lavagnino Dance presented a new work with interlocked choreography for 11 dancers at Danspace Project.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cherylyn Lavagnino’s new “Triptych” has many fine ingredients. For the dance’s outer segments, American Virtuosi, an ensemble of Baroque specialists (including two countertenors) led by Kenneth Hamrick at the harpsichord, plays Couperin and Biber. In between, taped music by the composer Scott Killian provides both contrast and continuity. And throughout, 11 skilled dancers keep the stage aswirl with elegant, complex patterns.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/LAVAGNINO/LAVAGNINO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/06/30/arts/LAVAGNINO/LAVAGNINO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'captio