ve gone from backdrops of death to sunny, idyllic spots to imperiled expanses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/opinion/life-and-death-of-the-beach.html', 'snippet': 'Beaches have gone from backdrops of death to sunny, idyllic spots to imperiled expanses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANY of us have childhood memories of the beach. For members of the baby boom generation, who grew up in the golden age of American beach culture, those images are typically idyllic: pure, clean sands, peaceful, paradisiacal. I myself was born a bit earlier, and my own recollections of the beach — at Atlantic City on the Jersey Shore during World War II — are quite different. I remember a wreck-littered, oil-stained strand that bore witness to the dangers lurking just offshore.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Life and Death of the Beach', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Life and Death of The Beach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melville, Herman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coastal Areas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebald, W G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Theroux, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T01:00:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John R. Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gillis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bebbf9d-6d08-5e93-9c27-14c68b28887c', 'word_count': 801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bebbf9d-6d08-5e93-9c27-14c68b28887c'}, {'abstract': 'Serena Williams and Andy Roddick are at the top of the bill as the tournament heads into its first weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/matches-to-watch-day-6/', 'snippet': 'Serena Williams and Andy Roddick are at the top of the bill as the tournament heads into its first weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the first time since we started spotlighting matches, we have no carryovers into the next day of play. Here are five fresh picks for Saturday to refill your clean plate. Players’ seeds are in parentheses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Matches to Watch: Day 6', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'del Potro, Juan Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferrer, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fish, Mardy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roddick, Andy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Venus', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zheng Jie', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T01:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Rothenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rothenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fff5e44-fe20-5198-9683-e04900785a1d', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fff5e44-fe20-5198-9683-e04900785a1d'}, {'abstract': 'The Maverick Concerts in Woodstock this summer will study a shortlist of French masters through an eclectic mix of classical and jazz-inflected performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/nyregion/french-classics-and-jazz-at-woodstocks-maverick-concerts.html', 'snippet': 'The Maverick Concerts in Woodstock this summer will study a shortlist of French masters through an eclectic mix of classical and jazz-inflected performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS its name suggests, Maverick Concerts does not offer a conventionally grand stage. Set in a romantic, barnlike theater amid 100 acres of tall trees and farmland in Woodstock, its charm is largely rustic, and the theater, while lovingly restored, is lacking in some state-of-the-art technology and space — it seats just 230 people indoors and, weather permitting, another 150 on benches outside. In fact, to hear Alexander Platt, the concerts’ music director, tell it, the summer festival is a modest affair. As he prepared recently for Maverick’s 97th season, on the theme of a “Tour de France,” Mr. Platt sought to play down any suggestion that he would offer an extensive survey of the French musical literature. ', 'print_section': 'WE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSWE1/01ARTSWE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSWE1/01ARTSWE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01ARTSWE1/01ARTSWE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subT