 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/world/middleeast/irans-un-envoy-denouncing-sanctions-says-nuclear-talks-are-at-critical-point.html', 'snippet': 'Iran’s ambassador to the United Nations has denounced sanctions against his country, saying that negotiations over its disputed nuclear program have reached a “critical point.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Iran’s ambassador to the United Nations said Friday that negotiations with the big powers over the disputed Iranian nuclear program had reached a “critical point,” implicitly raising the possibility of failure, because of the new regimen of harsh economic sanctions that have just been imposed on his country by the United States and European Union.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iranian Says Nuclear Talks Have Reached ‘Critical Point’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iranian Says Nuclear Talks Have Reached ‘Critical Point’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T01:13:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0da2d6a4-917d-5867-845d-25b4668a2b28', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0da2d6a4-917d-5867-845d-25b4668a2b28'}, {'abstract': 'Books on the evolution of police corruption in New York, and a guide through Woody Guthrie’s haunts in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/nyregion/books-on-police-corruption-and-woody-guthries-haunts-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'Books on the evolution of police corruption in New York, and a guide through Woody Guthrie’s haunts in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN 1970, Mayor John V. Lindsay appointed Whitman Knapp to lead an investigation into the Police Department. Prompted by articles in The New York Times about the whistle-blower Frank Serpico, the commission set out to uncover proof not only of serious crimes committed by an “incorrigible few” (the so-called meat eaters) but also of a widespread culture of bribery among “grass eaters” who indulged in “everyday graft.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01BOOK1_SPAN/01BOOK1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01BOOK1_SPAN/01BOOK1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01BOOK1_SPAN/01BOOK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag