'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/dream-to-nightmare/', 'snippet': 'All baseball careers come to an end, but there’s nothing worse than the promising one that never really gets started.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The College World Series wrapped up on Monday and the Arizona Wildcats were crowned college baseball’s national champions. Despite the elite talent of the participants in the series, many of the graduating seniors will move on to new lives without baseball. Only a select few can make a profession out of the game, and they will have a new set of expectations for themselves — and from their future baseball employers — once they sign on that dotted line.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dream to Nightmare', 'kicker': 'Doug Glanville', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Sports)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Brien', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T01:15:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doug Glanville', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doug', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glanville', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c400c9fe-452a-5d07-916d-401d3d98475e', 'word_count': 1159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c400c9fe-452a-5d07-916d-401d3d98475e'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 30, 2012.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/pageoneplus/corrections-june-30.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on June 30, 2012.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section':