 {'abstract': 'Insurgents attacked three villages in the Kamdesh district of Nuristan Province near the Pakistan border on Friday, Afghan officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/world/asia/afghanistan-insurgents-kill-10-in-attacks-on-villages.html', 'snippet': 'Insurgents attacked three villages in the Kamdesh district of Nuristan Province near the Pakistan border on Friday, Afghan officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Insurgents attacked three villages in the Kamdesh district of Nuristan Province near the Pakistan border on Friday, killing six Afghan security officials and four civilians, Afghan officials said. The fighting lasted for more than 12 hours, and more than 50 houses were destroyed, said Shams Rahman, a border police battalion commander in Nuristan. He said more than a hundred insurgents had stormed the area. A large explosion set off by insurgents outside the district governor’s house killed the district governor’s wife, he said. NATO said that it provided some air support for Afghan security forces involved in the fighting. Coalition ground forces, led by the United States, have withdrawn from the remote province in eastern Afghanistan. In 2009, insurgents attacked two American bases in the Kamdesh district, killing eight Americans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghanistan: Insurgents Kill 10 in Attacks on Villages', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghanistan: Insurgents Kill 10 in Attacks on Villages', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nuristan Province (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T02:03:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/c88baba0-a955-50e2-9571-302fb02aa888', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c88baba0-a955-50e2-9571-302fb02aa888'}, {'abstract': 'Three Texans expressed cautious hope that the health care overhaul upheld by the Supreme Court would bring them much needed help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2012/06/30/us/30texas.html', 'snippet': 'Three Texans expressed cautious hope that the health care overhaul upheld by the Supreme Court would bring them much needed help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three Texans expressed cautious hope that the health care overhaul upheld by the Supreme Court would bring them much needed help.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Voices of the Struggling in Texas', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T02:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/93813387-c0c3-5b1b-9613-a8482f568d32', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/93813387-c0c3-5b1b-9613-a8482f568d32'}, {'abstract': 'A reader inquires about a mob shooting at a Coney Island restaurant that might have involved Lucky Luciano.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/nyregion/answer-to-a-question-about-a-mobsters-death-in-coney-island.html', 'snippet': 'A reader inquires about a mob shooting at a Coney Island restaurant that might have involved Lucky Luciano.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I’d like some information about the killing of Joe Masseria, the mob leader also known as the Boss, in 1931. All I’ve heard is that the shooting took place in Scarpato’s Coney Island Restaurant and that Lucky Luciano was supposed to have been there.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1595, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 193, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Coney Island’s Big Hit', 'kicker': 'F.Y.I.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coney Island’s Big Hit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Masseria, Giuseppe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'CONEY ISLAND (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T02:04:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Pollak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/25c6129e-f9d0-5be1-92da-ccb7a1238eae', 'word_count': 461, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25c6129e-f9d0-5be1-92da-ccb7a1238eae'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Brennan, a police officer who was shot in the head in January, was promoted to sergeant Friday in a ceremony at Police Headquarters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/nyregion/kevin-brennan-officer-shot-in-brooklyn-promoted-to-sergeant.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Brennan, a police officer who was shot in the head in January, was promoted to sergeant Friday in a ceremony at Police Headquarters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just five months ago, Officer Kevin Brennan lay on an operating table in a Manhattan hospital. He had been shot, point-blank, in the head. Trauma surgeons carefully removed a bullet from the base of his skull. Pumped with morphine, he later drifted in and out of consciousness, as his family maintained a vigil, not knowing if he would live to see his 6-week-old baby grow up. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/06/30/nyregion/SHOT/SHOT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0,