ename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3ef90e5-aca9-5e1d-a98a-493fa74e4450', 'word_count': 577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3ef90e5-aca9-5e1d-a98a-493fa74e4450'}, {'abstract': 'A rain delay and a decision to come out firing in the fifth set paved the way for Lukas Rosol’s victory over Rafael Nadal, one of the greatest upsets in Wimbledon history.', 'web_url': 'https://straightsets.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/rosol-brought-warriors-spirit-into-fifth-set-vs-nadal/', 'snippet': 'A rain delay and a decision to come out firing in the fifth set paved the way for Lukas Rosol’s victory over Rafael Nadal, one of the greatest upsets in Wimbledon history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lukas Rosol looked out of sorts at the end of the fourth set, as Rafael Nadal clearly had the momentum after breaking Rosol’s serve to even the match at two sets all. Securing the all-important second break meant that Nadal would serve to start the fifth set, which gave him the advantage of serving to go ahead in the score rather than serving to tie the score.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosol Brought Warrior’s Spirit Into Fifth Set vs. Nadal', 'kicker': 'Straight Sets', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wimbledon Tennis Tournament', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dosedel, Slava', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nadal, Rafael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosol, Lukas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T03:45:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88647d57-dd66-5110-ae91-31dee323cbf4', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88647d57-dd66-5110-ae91-31dee323cbf4'}, {'abstract': 'After getting into the 100-meter freestyle final when Ryan Lochte scratched, Jason Lezak finished sixth and talked as if he had just made the Olympic team. But that isn’t guaranteed.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/29/100-freestyle-wraps-up-but-relay-isnt-settled/', 'snippet': 'After getting into the 100-meter freestyle final when Ryan Lochte scratched, Jason Lezak finished sixth and talked as if he had just made the Olympic team. But that isn’t guaranteed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — As exciting as the 100-meter freestyle finish was at the Olympic trials on Friday night, it was only the start. Now it could get really interesting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '100 Freestyle Wraps Up, but Relay Isn’t Settled', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lezak, Jason', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T03:56:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d17a00e-0a1c-5bca-b105-1ddf9d29105f', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d17a00e-0a1c-5bca-b105-1ddf9d29105f'}, {'abstract': 'Tour organizers have said they want to highlight the intermediary mountain stages this year, not just the spectacular summits in the Alps and the French Pyrénées.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/sports/cycling/six-stages-to-watch-at-the-tour-de-france.html', 'snippet': 'Tour organizers have said they want to highlight the intermediary mountain stages this year, not just the spectacular summits in the Alps and the French Pyrénées.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Avid Tour de France fans may be disappointed: this year’s race will not feature famed mountain climbs like L’Alpe d’Huez or Mont Ventoux. Tour organizers have said they want to highlight the intermediary mountain stages this year, not just the spectacular summits in the Alps and the French Pyrénées. For the first time since 2007, there are also three individual time trials — totaling more than 100 kilometers, or 62 miles, of solo racing — which will serve to heighten the yellow jersey drama as well.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Six Stages to Watch at the Tour de France', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tour de France (Bicycle Race)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bicycles and Bicycling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T03:57:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Cycling', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f72ff1bd-42bd-5797-8fa1-646d9b924c03', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f72ff1bd-42bd-5797-8fa1-646d9b924c03'}, {'abstract': 'With less than an hour between races, Ryan Lochte had the fastest semifinals times in the 200-meter individual medley and the 200-meter backstroke.', 'web_url': 'https://london2012.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/in-difficult-double-lochte-bests-all-comers/', 'snippet': 'With less than an hour between races, Ryan Lochte had the fastest semifinals times in the 200-meter individual medley and the 200-meter backstroke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OMAHA — Michael Phelps’s birthday is Saturday, and Ryan Lochte was asked what he planned to give him for a gift. He smiled and said, “I’ll have to think about it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Difficult Double, Lochte Bests All Comers', 'kicker': '2012 London Olympics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clary, Tyler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lochte, Ryan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phelps, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T04:03:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Karen Crouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Karen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Crouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a8326c5-9d7c-558e-a82e-5d077556026d', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a8326c5-9d7c-558e-a82e-5d077556026d'}, {'abstract': 'The spotlight has been fixed firmly on Bradley Wiggins and Cadel Evans as Tour favorites, but several of the world’s top cyclists will vie for the yellow jersey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/sports/cycling/riders-to-watch-at-the-tour-de-fran