ld champion in the all-around, came one step closer to clinching a spot on the United States Olympic gymnastics team on Friday, finishing first in the all-around of the first day of Olympic Trials in San Jose, Calif. With 61.70 points, she leads the second-place Gabby Douglas by 0.30 points.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wieber Leads at Olympic Gymnastics Trials', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Gymnastics', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wieber Leads at U.S. Trials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wieber, Jordyn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T04:15:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a9574cd-08bd-5b1a-96e0-b0a50cc5b7d1', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a9574cd-08bd-5b1a-96e0-b0a50cc5b7d1'}, {'abstract': 'The European Championships did away with the third-place match after the 1980 tournament, meaning we won’t see Portugal vs. Germany on Saturday. Would you have watched?', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/would-you-watch-a-third-place-game/', 'snippet': 'The European Championships did away with the third-place match after the 1980 tournament, meaning we won’t see Portugal vs. Germany on Saturday. Would you have watched?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first two weeks of a major soccer tournament can be two of the best weeks of a fan’s year. (Wives of those fans, like mine, not