tps://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/sports/tennis/wimbledon-tennis-2012.html', 'snippet': 'Yaroslava Shvedova, ranked 65th in the world, won a Golden Set, putting the ball into play 44 times without losing a point, in her victory over 10th-seeded Sara Errani.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WIMBLEDON, England — Imagine a pitcher in baseball retiring all 27 batters and then not learning he had thrown a perfect game until he had reached the clubhouse. That is what happened Saturday to Yaroslava Shvedova, who played a flawless set of tennis, the best by a woman in at least 44 years, and did not even realize it.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/tennis/01tennis-1/01tennis-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 764, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/tennis/01tennis-1/01tennis-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1527, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/tennis/01tennis-1/01tennis-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/tennis/01tennis-1/01tennis-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/tennis/01tennis-1/01tennis-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perfect Set Is No Myth in the Women’s Third Round at Wimbledon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head