: 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/syrian-video-activists-plan-news-broadcasts-to-offer-an-alternative-to-state-media/', 'snippet': 'In an interview with The Lede in Cairo, the Syrian activist Rami Jarrah, a/k/a Alexander Page, described ambitious plans to expand his Activists News Association by starting an Internet radio station and live video broadcasts from rebel-held terri...', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — In an interview this week at his home here in the Egyptian capital, the British-Syrian activist Rami Jarrah described ambitious plans to create an Internet news network, with radio broadcasts and live video streams of daily life inside rebel-held territory, to offer an alternative to Syria’s state-controlled media.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syrian Video Activists Plan News Broadcasts to Offer an Alternative to State Media', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assad, Bashar al-', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Damascus (Syria)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T16:37:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef9e3511-742f-516d-8a66-77b09a32367c', 'word_count': 489, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef9e3511-742f-516d-8a66-77b09a32367c'}, {'abstract': 'Mark Prior, a successful starter with the Chicago Cubs until injuries disabled him in 2006, is pitching for the Pawtucket Red Sox in an attempt to resurrect his career as a short reliever.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/sports/baseball/pitcher-mark-prior-still-trying-to-return-to-majors.html', 'snippet': 'Mark Prior, a successful starter with the Chicago Cubs until injuries disabled him in 2006, is pitching for the Pawtucket Red Sox in an attempt to resurrect his career as a short reliever.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PAWTUCKET, R.I. — The last time Mark Prior pitched in the major leagues, for the Chicago Cubs on Aug. 10, 2006, he had no children. Now he has three. They have some grasp of what their father does for a living, which has never changed. Prior was a ballplayer then, and he has never stopped thinking of himself that way. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/prior/prior-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 715, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/prior/prior-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1429, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/prior/prior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/prior/prior-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/prior/prior-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '6 Years Later, Still Striving to Get Back to the Majors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nearly Six Years Later, Still Striving To Return to the Major Leagues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prior, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pawtucket Red Sox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T16:38:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5316b020-1899-51f6-adbb-cbb69623bd7b', 'word_count': 1416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5316b020-1899-51f6-adbb-cbb69623bd7b'}, {'abstract': 'An unnamed donor and supporter of Mitt Romney has purchased space on the jerseys of F.C. New York to spread the message of the presumptive Republican candidate for president.', 'web_url': 'https://goal.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/f-c-new-york-likes-mitt/', 'snippet': 'An unnamed donor and supporter of Mitt Romney has purchased space on the jerseys of F.C. New York to spread the message of the presumptive Republican candidate for president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Someone, somewhere just loves their soccer and the presumptive Republican presidential candidate Mitt Romney.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'F.C. New York Likes Mitt', 'k