, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T19:31:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6cf4ec35-ad3c-597d-b7f3-2094cbcd8708', 'word_count': 1194, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6cf4ec35-ad3c-597d-b7f3-2094cbcd8708'}, {'abstract': 'Yes, the Internet offers many distractions, but sometimes they can make us more efficient for the long haul.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/technology/when-internet-distractions-make-us-more-efficient.html', 'snippet': 'Yes, the Internet offers many distractions, but sometimes they can make us more efficient for the long haul.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE Internet is a rabbit hole of distraction. It’s easy to wind up knee-deep in paparazzi photos of Beyonce’s new baby when you intended only to answer a few e-mails. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/1-BITS/1-BITS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/1-BITS/1-BITS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/1-BITS/1-BITS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/business/1-BITS/1-BITS-thumbStandard.jp