journey from selling sandwiches in Colombia to leading tech businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I WAS born and raised in Bogotá, Colombia. We fled when I was 15 after my cousin was kidnapped during turmoil in Colombia in the early 1990s. I came home from school one day, and my parents said we had to pack our bags and leave home the next morning.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/01-BOSS/01-BOSS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/01-BOSS/01-BOSS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1146, 'width': 884, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/01-BOSS/01-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/business/01-BOSS/01-BOSS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/business/01-BOSS/01-BOSS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Dot-Com to Dot-Co', 'kicker': 'The Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Dot-Com to Dot-Co', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calle, Juan Diego', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Domain Names (Internet)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Straat Investments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '.CO Internet SAS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T19:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Job Market', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juan Diego Calle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juan', 'middlename': 'Diego', 'lastname': 'Calle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa5980c5-6d98-534f-9552-39eb0042d64b', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa5980c5-6d98-534f-9552-39eb0042d64b'}, {'abstract': 'A TARP, sort of, but then what?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2012/06/30/what-did-the-eu-summit-accomplish/', 'snippet': 'A TARP, sort of, but then what?', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, the summit was clearly an upside surprise: in effect, the Latin bloc forced Merkel to bend, at least slightly. But was it good enough?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Did the EU Summit Accomplish?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T19:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17fc99ab-fb30-5c6e-9db2-f1411387ebbb', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17fc99ab-fb30-5c6e-9db2-f1411387ebbb'}, {'abstract': 'Italy’s Mario Balotelli plays with an uncontrolled fire, at times injuring foes and confounding his coaches. But he also lights up the field.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/sports/soccer/mario-balotelli-one-of-soccers-most-gifted-and-eccentric-players.html', 'snippet': 'Italy’s Mario Balotelli plays with an uncontrolled fire, at times injuring foes and confounding his coaches. But he also lights up the field.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KIEV, Ukraine — The long diagonal pass floated across midfield, its accuracy all the more remarkable for its distance. Waiting with impeccable timing was Mario Balotelli of Italy, one of soccer’s most gifted and eccentric players. He sprinted past the German defense and turned to meet the ball, nimbly switching directions, backpedaling with the gliding agility of a man on skates.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/YJPSOCCER/YJPSOCCER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/YJPSOCCER/YJPSOCCER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1546, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/YJPSOCCER/YJPSOCCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/YJPSOCCER/YJPSOCCER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/YJPSOCCER/YJPSOCCER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 113, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Short-Fused and Explosive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kic