-9639-01d236dd9de4', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/659bcfb6-0900-58c7-9639-01d236dd9de4'}, {'abstract': 'The European project needs a grand unifying ideal — or it will fail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/opinion/sunday/wheres-charlemagne-when-we-need-him.html', 'snippet': 'The European project needs a grand unifying ideal — or it will fail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WRITING some 50 years ago, Archduke Otto Hapsburg, the last pretender to the crowns of Austria and Hungary, warned that economic cooperation alone would not satisfy the peoples of Europe and that European unification could not succeed unless it was imbued with an abstract principle. Only something as mystical, he wrote, as the Holy Roman Empire could give people hope, a sense of religious renewal and combat the pernicious effects of local interest, chauvinism, xenophobia and racism. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Europe/01Europe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Europe/01Europe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Europe/01Europe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Europe/01Europe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Europe/01Europe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Where’s Charlemagne When We Need Him?', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where’s Charlemagne When We Need Him?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Charlemagne, Emperor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Latin Language', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T20:13:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Istvan Deak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Istvan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a42ed236-2bf6-5801-a094-5b92e1d45aa4', 'word_count': 948, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a42ed236-2bf6-5801-a094-5b92e1d45aa4'}, {'abstract': 'With certain adjustments — and ground rules — working mothers can handle positions of power and family responsibilities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/sunday-review/working-mothers-at-the-top.html', 'snippet': 'With certain adjustments — and ground rules — working mothers can handle positions of power and family responsibilities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FOR years the debate about working motherhood has swung between two poles — the sunny optimism of having it all and the judgmental gloom of the finger-waggers. Now we are in another paroxysm of angst, prompted by a provocative article by Anne-Marie Slaughter in The Atlantic about the impossibility of combining working motherhood with jobs at the pinnacle of power. Yes, her article focuses on the elite. But she raises troubling questions about whether mothers with children at home can wield sustained power in American society — power that some might use to improve the lot of less privileged women.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Women/01Women-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Women/01Women-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1850, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Women/01Women-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Women/01Women-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01Women/01Women-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 192, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'To Have (It All) and Have Not', 'kicker': 'Dispatch', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Have (It All) and Have Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slaughter, Anne-Marie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T20:22:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Chira', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chira', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a66fe59-21df-516d-8c8a-5dd4a2bbbded', 'word_count': 1259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a66fe59-21df-516d-8c8a-5dd4a2bbbded'}, {'abstract': 'She devoted herself to expanding women’s rights to control their own bodies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/world/joan-dunlop-dies-at-78-fought-for-womens-health-rights.html', 'snippet': 'She devoted herself to expanding women’s rights to control their own bodies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Joan Dunlop, a global leader in addressing women’s issues who helped prod the United Nations to define a woman’s right to say no to sex as an essential human right, died on Friday at her home in Lakeville, Conn. She was 78.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/world/01DUNLOP-obit/dog-DUNLOP-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/world/01DUNLOP-obit/dog-DUNLOP-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1176, 'width': 1636, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/world/01DUNLOP-obit/dog-DUNLOP-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thu