aph': 'COLCHAGUA VALLEY, Chile — Up norte, the N.B.A. playoffs are over. The Stanley Cup has been passed around. Baseball is at midseason. And here, as usual, it’s rodeo time.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/dog-rodeo-5/dog-rodeo-5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 653, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/dog-rodeo-5/dog-rodeo-5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1228, 'width': 1926, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/dog-rodeo-5/dog-rodeo-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/dog-rodeo-5/dog-rodeo-5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sports/dog-rodeo-5/dog-rodeo-5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Chile, Rodeo Rules the Land', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Chile, Rodeo Rules the Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rodeos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cowboys and Cowgirls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cattle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T21:30:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerald Eskenazi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerald', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eskenazi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6c2017a-e4a4-5dae-bd73-5491b87c9e3f', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6c2017a-e4a4-5dae-bd73-5491b87c9e3f'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t fault President’s Obama’s legislative style. His conciliatory approach to corporations is the wise course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/opinion/sunday/how-liberals-win.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t fault President’s Obama’s legislative style. His conciliatory approach to corporations is the wise course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PRESIDENT OBAMA has endured much criticism of his legislative skills from his fellow progressives. His conciliatory approach has been compared unfavorably with Franklin D. Roosevelt’s gleeful pugnacity and Lyndon B. Johnson’s relentless arm-twisting. His willingness to strike deals with corporations has been tagged “business as usual.” Many progressives, frustrated over the past three years, have concluded that the political system is fundamentally broken because corporate power has been allowed to suffocate popular liberal policies.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/07/01/sunday-review/01SUBLIBERALS/01SUBLIBERALS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Liberals Win', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Liberals Win', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reform and Reorganization', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roosevelt, Franklin Delano', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2012-06-30T21:33:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Scher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Scher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ffec29-fb31-5560-adf5-83a3da43384a', 'word_count': 1180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ffec29-fb31-5560-adf5-83a3da43384a'}, {'abstract': 'A needed program shows how Times articles have been edited.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2012/07/01/opinion/sunday/article-changes-are-shown-in-a-tool-created-by-outsiders.html', 'snippet': 'A needed program shows how Times articles have been edited.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE NEW YORK TIMES is the closest thing we have in this country to a “newspaper of record.” A year ago I suggested that the paper should do a better job, therefore, of maintaining a record of the articles it publishes. Because of the swift changes wrought by the Internet, I observed, Times articles drift out into digital space in multiple versions. Some articles disappear altogether.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2010/08/11/opinion/brisbane/brisbane-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':